CORE_SUTRAS = [
    "Sūtra 1.1.1: vruddhiraadaich (वृद्धिरादैच्) — आ, ऐ and औ are called वृद्धि।",
    "Sūtra 1.1.2: adengunah (अदेङ् गुणः) — अ, ए and ओ are called गुण।",
    "Sūtra 1.1.3: ikogunavruddhee (इको गुणवृद्धी) — In the absence of any special role whenever गुण or वृद्धि is enjoined about any expression by using the terms गुण or वृद्धि, it is to be understood to come in the room of the इक् (इ, उ, ऋ, लृ) of that expression.",
    "Sūtra 1.1.4: nadhaatulopaardhadhaatuke (न धातुलोप आर्धधातुके) — The गुण and वृद्धि substitutions which otherwise would have presented themselves do not take place, when such an आर्धधातुक [[3.4.114]] affix follows, which causes a portion of the root to be elided.",
    "Sūtra 1.1.5: kngiticha (क्ङिति च) — And that, which otherwise would have caused गुण or वृद्धि, does not do so, when it has an indicatory क् , ग् , ङ्।",
    "Sūtra 1.1.6: deedheeveveetaam (दीधीवेवीटाम्) — The गुण and वृद्धि substitutions which otherwise would have presented themselves do not however come, in the place of the vowels of दिधि 'to shine' and वेवि 'to go', and of the augment called इट् ।",
    "Sūtra 1.1.7: halonantaraasamyogah (हलोऽनन्तराः संयोगः) — Consonants unseparated by a vowel are called conjunct consonants.",
    "Sūtra 1.1.8: mukhanaasikaavachanonunaasikah (मुखनासिकावचनोऽनुनासिकः) — That which is pronounced by the nose along with the mouth is called अनुनासिक or nasal.",
    "Sūtra 1.1.9: tulyaasyaprayatnamsavarnam (तुल्यास्यप्रयत्नं सवर्णम्) — Those whose place of utterance and effort are equal are called सवर्ण or homogeneous letters.",
    "Sūtra 1.1.10: naajjhalau (नाज्झलौ) — There is however no homogeneity between vowels and consonants, though their place and effort be equal.",
    "Sūtra 1.1.11: eedoodeddvivachanampragruhyam (ईदूदेद्द्विवचनं प्रगृह्यम्) — A dual case affix ending in ई or ऊ or ए is called प्रगृह्य , or excepted vowels which do not admit सन्धि or conjugation.",
    "Sūtra 1.1.12: adasomaat (अदसो मात्) — The same letters after the म् of the pronoun अदस् are प्रगृह्य।",
    "Sūtra 1.1.13: she (शे) — The affix शे (the Vedic substitute of the case-affixes) is a प्रगृह्य।",
    "Sūtra 1.1.14: nipaatekaajanaang (निपात एकाजनाङ्) — A particle [[1.4.56]] consisting of a single vowel, with the exception of the particle आङ् is प्रगृह्य।",
    "Sūtra 1.1.15: ot (ओत्) — The final ओ of a particle is a प्रगृह्य।",
    "Sūtra 1.1.16: sambuddhaushaakalyasyetaavanaarshe (सम्बुद्धौ शाकल्यस्येतावनार्षे) — The final ओ of a vocative singular [[2.3.49]] before the word इति according to शाकल्य , in a secular or non-vedic literature is a प्रगृह्य।",
    "Sūtra 1.1.17: unyah (उञः) — The particle ऊञ् before इति , according to शाकल्य is a प्रगृह्य।",
    "Sūtra 1.1.18: oon (ऊँ) — The particle ऊँ replaces उञ in non-vedic literature and it is a प्रगृह्य in the opinion of शाकल्य।",
    "Sūtra 1.1.19: eedootauchasaptamyarthe (ईदूतौ च सप्तम्यर्थे) — The final ई and ऊ of words giving the sense of the locative case are प्रगृह्य।",
    "Sūtra 1.1.20: daadhaaghvadaap (दाधा घ्वदाप्) — The words having the form of दा 'to give' and धा 'to place' are called घु।",
    "Sūtra 1.1.21: aadyantavadekasmin (आद्यन्तवदेकस्मिन्) — An operation should be performed on a single letter, as upon an initial or upon a final.",
    "Sūtra 1.1.22: taraptamapaughah (तरप्तमपौ घः) — The affixes तरप् and तमप् ae called घ।",
    "Sūtra 1.1.23: bahuganavatudatisamkhyaa (बहुगणवतुडति संख्या) — The words बहु 'many' , गण 'class' and the words ending in the affix वतु -- यद्तदेतेभ्यः परिमाणे वतुप् [[5.2.39]] and डति -- किमः संख्यापरिमाणे डति च [[5.2.41]] are called numerals (संख्या).",
    "Sūtra 1.1.24: shnaantaashat (ष्णान्ता षट्) — The संख्या-s having ष or न as their final are called षट्।",
    "Sūtra 1.1.25: daticha (डति च) — And the संख्या-s ending with the affix डति are called षट्।",
    "Sūtra 1.1.26: ktaktavatoonishthaa (क्तक्तवतू निष्ठा) — The affixes क्त and क्तवतु are called निष्ठा।",
    "Sūtra 1.1.27: sarvaadeenisarvanaamaani (सर्वादीनि सर्वनामानि) — The words सर्व 'all' and the rest are called सर्वनाम or pronouns.",
    "Sūtra 1.1.28: vibhaashaadiksamaasebahuvreehau (विभाषा दिक्समासे बहुव्रीहौ) — The above words are optionally सर्वनाम when they occur in a बहुव्रीही compound signifying direction -- दिङ्नामान्यन्तराले [[2.2.26]].",
    "Sūtra 1.1.29: nabahuvreehau (न बहुव्रीहौ) — The words सर्व etc. are not सर्वनाम when they occur in a बहुव्रीही compound.",
    "Sūtra 1.1.30: truteeyaasamaase (तृतीयासमासे) — In the Instrumental Determinative Compounds the words सर्व etc. are not सर्वनाम।",
    "Sūtra 1.1.31: dvandvecha (द्वन्द्वे च) — And in Collective Compound -- दिङ्नामान्यन्तराले [[2.2.26]], the words सर्व etc. are not सर्वनाम।",
    "Sūtra 1.1.32: vibhaashaajasi (विभाषा जसि) — Their द्वन्द compounds are optionally सर्वनाम when the nominative plural termination जस् follows.",
    "Sūtra 1.1.33: prathamacharamatayaalpaardhakatipayanemaashcha (प्रथमचरमतयाल्पार्धकतिपयनेमाश्च) — And also the words प्रथम 'first', चरम 'last', words with the affix तय -- संख्याया अवयवे तयप् [[5.2.42]], अल्प 'few', अर्ध 'half', कतिपय 'some' and नेम 'half' are optionally सर्वनाम , before the Nominative Plural termination. ",
    "Sūtra 1.1.34: poorvaparaavaradakshinottaraaparaadharaani (पूर्वपरावरदक्षिणोत्तरापराधराणि व्यवस्थायामसंज्ञायाम्) — The words पूर्व 'prior', पर 'after', अवर 'posterior', दक्षिण 'south', उत्तर 'north', अपर 'other', अधर 'inferior', when they discriminate relative position, not when they are appellatives, are optionally सर्वनाम before the affix जस्।",
    "Sūtra 1.1.35: svamadnyaatidhanaakhyaayaam (स्वमज्ञातिधनाख्यायाम्) — The word स्व 'own', when it does not mean a kinsman or property is optionally सर्वनाम before the affix जस्।",
    "Sūtra 1.1.36: antarambahiryogopasamvyaanayoh (अन्तरं बहिर्योगोपसंव्यानयोः) — The word अन्तर always being a सर्वनाम , when meaning 'outer' or 'lower garment', is optionally so before the affix जस्।",
    "Sūtra 1.1.37: svaraadinipaatamavyayam (स्वरादिनिपातमव्ययम्) — The words स्वर् 'heaven' etc. and the particles -- निपात एकाजनाङ् [[1.4.56]], are called अव्यय or indeclinables.",
    "Sūtra 1.1.38: taddhitashchaasarvavibhaktih (तद्धितश्चासर्वविभक्तिः) — And the words ending in तद्धित or secondary affixes -- तद्धिताः [[4.1.76]], which are not declined in all the cases are also अव्यय or indeclinables.",
    "Sūtra 1.1.39: krunmejantah (कृन्मेजन्तः) — The words formed by those कृत् or primary affixes -- कृदतिङ् [[3.1.93]], which end with a म् or in a ए , ओ , ऐ and औ are also अव्यय or indeclinables.",
    "Sūtra 1.1.40: ktvaatosunkasunah (क्त्वातोसुन्कसुनः) — The words ending in क्त्व , तोसुन् -- भावलक्षणे स्थेण्कृञ्वदिचरिहुतमिजनिभ्यस्तोसुन् [[3.4.16]], and कसुन् are अव्यय or indeclinables.",
    "Sūtra 1.1.41: avyayeebhaavashcha (अव्ययीभावश्च) — The compound called अव्ययीभाव is also अव्यय or indeclinable.",
    "Sūtra 1.1.42: shisarvanaamasthaanam (शि सर्वनामस्थानम्) — The affix शि [[7.1.20]] is called सर्वनामस्थान।",
    "Sūtra 1.1.43: sudanapumsakasya (सुडनपुंसकस्य) — The first five case affixes comprised in the प्रत्यहार सुट् (i.e. the three case-terminations of the Nominative, and the singular and dual of the Accusative) are also called सर्वनामस्थान , except the case-affixes of the neuter gender.",
    "Sūtra 1.1.44: navetivibhaashaa (न वेति विभाषा) — May or may not' is called विभाषा or option.",
    "Sūtra 1.1.45: igyanahasamprasaaranam (इग्यणः सम्प्रसारणम्) — The इक् vowels which replace the semi-vowels यण् are called सम्प्रसारण।",
    "Sūtra 1.1.46: aadyantautakitau (आद्यन्तौ टकितौ) — Of whatsoever the augments enunciated are distinguished by an indicatory ट् or क् , they precede or follow it accordingly.",
    "Sūtra 1.1.47: midachontyaatparah (मिदचोऽन्त्यात्परः) — The augment that has an indicatory म् comes after the last among the vowels and becomes the final position of that which it augments.",
    "Sūtra 1.1.48: echigghrasvaadeshe (एच इग्घ्रस्वादेशे) — Of एच् vowels, इक् is the substitute, when short is to be substituted.",
    "Sūtra 1.1.49: shashtheesthaaneyogaa (षष्ठी स्थानेयोगा) — The force of the genitive case in a sūtra is that of the phrase 'in the place of', when no special rules qualify the sense of Genitive 6th-Case. ",
    "Sūtra 1.1.50: sthaanentaratamah (स्थानेऽन्तरतमः) — When a common term is obtained as a substitute, the likest of its significates to that in the place of which it comes, is the actual substitute.",
    "Sūtra 1.1.51: uranraparah (उरण् रपरः) — When a letter of अण् प्रत्यहार comes as a substitute for ऋ it is always followed by र्।",
    "Sūtra 1.1.52: alontyasya (अलोऽन्त्यस्य) — The substitute takes the place of only the final letter (of that which is denoted by a term exhibited in the Genitive 6th-Case.",
    "Sūtra 1.1.53: ngichcha (ङिच्च) — And the substitute which is indicatory ङ् (even though it consists of more than one letter) takes the place of the final letter only of the original expression.",
    "Sūtra 1.1.54: aadehaparasya (आदेः परस्य) — That which is enjoined to come in the room of what follows is to be understood as coming in the room only of the first letter thereof.",
    "Sūtra 1.1.55: anekaalshitsarvasya (अनेकाल्शित्सर्वस्य) — A substitute consisting of more than one letter and a substitute having an indicatory श् take the place of the whole of the original expression exhibited in the Genitive 6th-Case.",
    "Sūtra 1.1.56: sthaanivadaadeshonalvidhau (स्थानिवदादेशोऽनल्विधौ) — A substitute (आदेश) is like the former occupant (स्थानी) but not in the case of a rule the occasion for the operation of which is furnished by the letters of the original term.",
    "Sūtra 1.1.57: achahaparasminpoorvavidhau (अचः परस्मिन् पूर्वविधौ) — A substitute in the room of a vowel caused by something that follows, should be regarded as that whose place it takes when a rule would else take effect on what stands anterior to the original vowel.",
    "Sūtra 1.1.58: napadaantadvirvachanavareyalopasvarasavarnaanusvaaradeerghajashcharvidhishu (न पदान्तद्विर्वचनवरेयलोपस्वरसवर्णानुस्वारदीर्घजश्चर्विधिषु) — Not so, in rules relating to the finals of words, to the doubling of letters, to the affixing of वरच् , to the elision of य , to accent, to homogenous letters, to अनुस्वर , to the lengthening of vowels and to the substitution of जस् and चर् characters.",
    "Sūtra 1.1.59: dvirvachanechi (द्विर्वचनेऽचि) — Before an affix having an initial vowel, which causes reduplication, the substitute which takes the place of a vowel is like the original vowel even in form, only for the purpose of reduplication and no further.",
    "Sūtra 1.1.60: adarshanamlopah (अदर्शनं लोपः) — The substitution of a blank (लोप) signifies disappearance.",
    "Sūtra 1.1.61: pratyayasyalukshlulupah (प्रत्ययस्य लुक्श्लुलुपः) — The disappearance of an affix when it is caused by the words लुक् , श्लु or लुप् are designated by those terms respectively.",
    "Sūtra 1.1.62: pratyayalopepratyayalakshanam (प्रत्ययलोपे प्रत्ययलक्षणम्) — When elision of an affix has taken place (लोप), the affix still exerts its influence and the operations dependant upon it, take place as if it were present.",
    "Sūtra 1.1.63: nalumataanggasya (न लुमताङ्गस्य) — Of the base (अङ्ग), whose affix has been elided by the use of the three words containing लु , the operations dependant on it do not take place, regarding such base.",
    "Sūtra 1.1.64: achontyaaditi (अचोऽन्त्यादि टि) — The final portion of a word, beginning with the last among the vowels in the word, is called टि।",
    "Sūtra 1.1.65: alontyaatpoorvupadhaa (अलोऽन्त्यात् पूर्व उपधा) — The letter immediately preceding the last letter of a word is called penultimate (उपधा).",
    "Sūtra 1.1.66: tasminnitinirdishtepoorvasya (तस्मिन्निति निर्दिष्टे पूर्वस्य) — When a term is exhibited in the seventh case in these sūtras, the operation directed, is to be understood as effecting the state of what immediately precedes the which the term denotes.",
    "Sūtra 1.1.67: tasmaadityuttarasya (तस्मादित्युत्तरस्य) — An operation caused by the exhibition of a term in the Ablative 5th case, is to be understood to enjoin the substitution of something in the room of that which immediately follows the word denoted by the term.",
    "Sūtra 1.1.68: svamroopamshabdasyaashabdasamjnyaa (स्वं रूपं शब्दस्याशब्दसंज्ञा) — In this Grammar, when an operation is directed with regard to a word, the individual form of the word possessing meaning is to be understood, except with regard to a word which is a definition.",
    "Sūtra 1.1.69: anuditsavarnasyachaapratyayah (अणुदित् सवर्णस्य चाप्रत्ययः) — The letters of the प्रत्याहार अण् i.e. the vowels and semi-vowels and a term having उ for its indicatory letter, refer to their own form as well as to their homogeneous letters, except when they are used as प्रत्यय-s or affixes.",
    "Sūtra 1.1.70: taparastatkaalasya (तपरस्तत्कालस्य) — The letter which has त् after or before it, besides referring to its own form, refers to those homogeneous letters which have the some prosodial length or time.",
    "Sūtra 1.1.71: aadirantyenasahetaa (आदिरन्त्येन सहेता) — An initial letter, with a final इत् letter as a final, is the name of itself and of the intervening letters.",
    "Sūtra 1.1.72: yenavidhistadantasya (येन विधिस्तदन्तस्य) — An injunction which is made with regard to a particular attribute, applies to words having that attribute at their end as well as to that attribute itself.",
    "Sūtra 1.1.73: vruddhiryasyaachaamaadistadvruddham (वृद्धिर्यस्याचामादिस्तद् वृद्धम्) — That word, among the vowels of which the first is a वृद्धि , is called वृद्धम्। ",
    "Sūtra 1.1.74: tyadaadeenicha (त्यदादीनि च) — The words त्यद् etc. are called वृद्धम्।",
    "Sūtra 1.1.75: engpraachaamdeshe (एङ् प्राचां देशे) — A word that has the letters ए and ओ as the first among its vowels, gets also the designation of वृद्धम्।",
    "Sūtra 1.2.1: gaangkutaadibhyonyninngit (गाङ्कुटादिभ्योऽञ्णिन्ङित्) —  All affixes after the verb गाङ् 'to study' and the verb कुट् 'to be crooked' and the rest, are as if they had an indicatory ङ् (ङित्), except those affixes which have an indicatory ञ् (ञित्) or ण् (णित्).",
    "Sūtra 1.2.2: vijait (विज इट्) —  An affix which begins with the augment इट् -- आर्धधातुकस्येड् वलादेः [[7.2.35]], is ङित् after the root विज् 'to fear, to move'.",
    "Sūtra 1.2.3: vibhaashornoh (विभाषोर्णोः) —  After the verb ऊर्ण 'to cover', the affix beginning with the augment इट् is regarded optionally like ङित्।",
    "Sūtra 1.2.4: saarvadhaatukamapit (सार्वधातुकमपित्) —  A सार्वधातुक -- तिङ्शित्सार्वधातुकम् [[3.4.113]], affix not having an indicatory ङित्।",
    "Sūtra 1.2.5: asamyogaallitkit (असंयोगाल्लिट् कित्) —  The affixes of लिट् (Perfect Tense) not coming after a conjunct consonant, are as if they had an indicatory क् (कित्).",
    "Sūtra 1.2.6: eendhibhavatibhyaamcha (इन्धिभवतिभ्यां च) —  The लिट् (Perfect Tense) affixes after the roots इन्धि 'to kindle' and भू 'to become' are also कित्।",
    "Sūtra 1.2.7: mrudamrudagudhakushaklishavadavasahaktvaa (मृडमृदगुधकुषक्लिशवदवसः क्त्वा) —  The affix क्त्वा is कित् after मृड् 'to be gracious', मृद् 'to squeeze', गुध् 'to wrap up', कुष् 'to tear', क्लिश् 'to suffer', वद् 'to speak' and वस् 'to dwell'.",
    "Sūtra 1.2.8: rudavidamushagrahisvapiprachchhahasanshcha (रुदविदमुषग्रहिस्वपिप्रच्छः सँश्च) — The affixes क्त्वा and सन् [[3.1.7]] are कित् after रुद् 'to weep', विद् 'to know', मुष् 'to steal', गृह् 'to seize', स्वप् 'to sleep' and प्रच्छ् 'to ask'. ",
    "Sūtra 1.2.9: ikojhal (इको झल्) — The affix सन् beginning with a letter of the प्रत्यहार झल् is like कित् after the verbs ending in इक् vowels.",
    "Sūtra 1.2.10: halantaachcha (हलन्ताच्च) —  And after a root ending in a consonant and preceded by a vowel of the प्रत्यहार इक् , the affix सन् beginning with a झल् consonant, is like कित् ।",
    "Sūtra 1.2.11: lingsichaavaatmanepadeshu (लिङ्सिचावात्मनेपदेषु) —  After roots ending in a consonant, that adjoins a vowel of इक् प्रत्यहार , the substitutes of the -- विधिनिमन्त्रणामन्त्रण अधीष्टसम्प्रश्नप्रार्थनेषु लिङ् [[3.3.161]] and सिच् -- च्लेः सिच् [[3.1.44]], when they begin with a consonant of झल् प्रत्यहार , are कित् when the आत्मनेपद affixes follow.",
    "Sūtra 1.2.12: ushcha (उश्च) —  And after the verbs ending in ऋ , the substitutes of लिङ् and the affix सिच् , are कित् , when they begin with झल् and the आत्मनेपद affixes follow.",
    "Sūtra 1.2.13: vaagamah (वा गमः) — Optionally after the verb गम् , the लिङ् and the सिच् beginning with झल् consonants, in the आत्मनेपद , are कित्।",
    "Sūtra 1.2.14: hanahasich (हनः सिच्) — The सिच् आत्मनेपद affixes are कित् after the root हन् 'to kill'.",
    "Sūtra 1.2.15: yamogandhane (यमो गन्धने) — The affix सिच् before आत्मनेपद affixes is कित् after the verb यम् when meaning 'to divulge'.",
    "Sūtra 1.2.16: vibhaashopayamane (विभाषोपयमने) — The affix सिच् before आत्मनेपद affixes is कित् optionally when यम् means 'to expose'.",
    "Sūtra 1.2.17: sthaaghvorichcha (स्था घ्वोरिच्च) — The affix सिच् before आत्मनेपद affixes is कित् after स्था 'to stand' and घु मृषस्तितिक्षायाम् [[1.2.20]] verbs, and these verbs change their आ into इ before these terminations.",
    "Sūtra 1.2.18: naktvaaset (न क्त्वा सेट्) —  The affix क्त्वा when it takes the augment इट् (i.e. when it is सेट्) is not कित् ।",
    "Sūtra 1.2.19: nishthaasheengsvidimidikshvididhrushah (निष्ठा शीङ्स्विदिमिदिक्ष्विदिधृषः) —  The सेट् निष्ठा affixes are not कित् after the verbs शीङ् 'to lie down', स्विद् 'to sweat', मिद् 'to melt', क्ष्विद् 'to be unctuous', and दृश् 'to offend'.",
    "Sūtra 1.2.20: mrushastitikshaayaam (मृषस्तितिक्षायाम्) —  The सेट् निष्ठा affix is not कित् after the verb मृष् 'to forbear'.",
    "Sūtra 1.2.21: udupadhaadbhaavaadikarmanoranyatarasyaam (उदुपधाद्भावादिकर्मणोरन्यतरस्याम्) —  The सेट् निष्ठा affix is optionally not कित् after the verbs with a penultimate उ if used impersonally or denoting the beginning of action.",
    "Sūtra 1.2.22: poongahaktvaacha (पूङः क्त्वा च) —  The सेट् निष्ठा affix and the सेट् क्त्वा are not कित् after the verb पुङ् 'to purify'.",
    "Sūtra 1.2.23: nopadhaatthaphaantaadvaa (नोपधात्थफान्ताद्वा) —  The सेट् क्त्वा is optionally कित् after the verbs having a penultimate न् ending in a थ् and फ्।",
    "Sūtra 1.2.24: vanychilunychyrutashcha (वञ्चिलुञ्च्यृतश्च) —  The सेट् क्त्वा is optionally कित् after the verbs वञ्च् 'to cheat', लुञ्च् 'to pluck' and ऋत् 'to dare or abhor'.",
    "Sūtra 1.2.25: trushimrushikrushehakaashyapasya (तृषिमृषिकृशेः काश्यपस्य) — The सेट् क्त्वा is optionally कित् , according to the opinion of ऋषि काश्यप after the verbs तृष् 'to be thirsty', मृष् 'to sprinkle' and कृश् 'to become lean'.",
    "Sūtra 1.2.26: ralovyupadhaaddhalaadehasamshcha (रलो व्युपधाद्धलादेः संश्च) —  After a verb which begins in a consonant and ends in a letter of रल् प्रत्यहार and has as its penultimate इ or ई and उ or ऊ , the क्त्वा and सन् affixes are optionally कित् ।",
    "Sūtra 1.2.27: ookaalojjhrasvadeerghaplutah (ऊकालोऽज्झ्रस्वदीर्घप्लुतः) —  A vowel whose time is that of short उ , ऊ and the prolated ऊ , is called respectively ह्रस्व short, दीर्घ long and प्लुत prolated.",
    "Sūtra 1.2.28: achashcha (अचश्च) —  The short, long and prolated, when enunciated as such, by using these terms, are to be understood to come in the place of vowels only.",
    "Sūtra 1.2.29: uchchairudaattah (उच्चैरुदात्तः) —  The vowel that is perceived as having a high tone is called उदात्त or acutely accented.",
    "Sūtra 1.2.30: neechairanudaattah (नीचैरनुदात्तः) — The vowel that is perceived as having a low tone is called अनुदात्तः or gravely accented",
    "Sūtra 1.2.31: samaahaarahasvaritah (समाहारः स्वरितः) — The vowel that has the combination of अनुदात्त and उदात्त tones is said to be स्वरित or circumflexly accented.",
    "Sūtra 1.2.32: tasyaaditudaattamardhahrasvam (तस्यादित उदात्तमर्धह्रस्वम्) — Of it (स्वरित-s) the first portion is उदात्त , to the extent of a half measure, or prosodial length.",
    "Sūtra 1.2.33: ekashrutidooraatsambuddhau (एकश्रुति दूरात् सम्बुद्धौ) — In addressing a person from a distance the tone is called एकश्रुति or monotony.",
    "Sūtra 1.2.34: yajnyakarmanyajapanyoongkhasaamasu (यज्ञकर्मण्यजपन्यूङ्खसामसु) — In sacrificial works there is Monotony, except in जप (silent repetition of a formula), न्यूङ्ख vowels (16 sorts of ओम्) and the साम Vedas.",
    "Sūtra 1.2.35: uchchaistaraamvaavashatkaarah (उच्चैस्तरां वा वषट्कारः) — The pronunciation of the word वषट् , may optionally be by raising the voice (acutely accented), or it may be pronounced with monotony.",
    "Sūtra 1.2.36: vibhaashaachhandasi (विभाषा छन्दसि) — The monotony is optional in the recitation of the Vedas or they may be recited with accents.",
    "Sūtra 1.2.37: nasubrahmanyaayaamsvaritasyatoodaattah (न सुब्रह्मण्यायां स्वरितस्य तूदात्तः) — There should be no Monotony in the recitation of the सब्रह्मण्य hymns and in those hymns, the vowels, that would otherwise have taken the स्वरित accent, take the उदात्त accent instead.",
    "Sūtra 1.2.38: devabrahmanoranudaattah (देवब्रह्मणोरनुदात्तः) — The words देवा and ब्राह्मण in those hymns have अनुदात्त accent.",
    "Sūtra 1.2.39: svaritaatsamhitaayaamanudaattaanaam (स्वरितात् संहितायामनुदात्तानाम्) — The Monotony takes the place of the अनुदात्त vowels which follow the स्वरित vowels, in close proximity (संहिता).",
    "Sūtra 1.2.40: udaattasvaritaparasyasannatarah (उदात्तस्वरितपरस्य सन्नतरः) — The accent called सन्नतर is substituted in the room of an अनुदात्त vowel, which has an उदात्त or स्वरित vowel following it.",
    "Sūtra 1.2.41: apruktekaalpratyayah (अपृक्त एकाल् प्रत्ययः) — An affix consisting of a single letter is called अपृक्त।",
    "Sūtra 1.2.42: tatpurushahasamaanaadhikaranahakarmadhaarayah (तत्पुरुषः समानाधिकरणः कर्मधारयः) — A तत्-पुरुष compound, the case of each member is the same, is called कर्मधारय or Appositional Determinative compound.",
    "Sūtra 1.2.43: prathamaanirdishtamsamaasupasarjanam (प्रथमानिर्दिष्टं समास उपसर्जनम्) — In (this book, in the sūtras relating to) compound, the word that is exhibited in the Nominative -1st case, is called उपसर्जन or the secondary word.",
    "Sūtra 1.2.44: ekavibhaktichaapoorvanipaate (एकविभक्ति चापूर्वनिपाते) — A word which is one fixed case, (while the word compounded with it may vary its case) is also उपसर्जन , except for the purposes of the the rule which requires the उपसर्जन to stand first in a compound.",
    "Sūtra 1.2.45: arthavadadhaaturapratyayahapraatipadikam (अर्थवदधातुरप्रत्ययः प्रातिपदिकम्) — A significant form of a word, not being a verbal root (धातु), or an affix (प्रत्यय) is called a प्रातिपदिक or crude-form.",
    "Sūtra 1.2.46: kruttaddhitasamaasaashcha (कृत्तद्धितसमासाश्च) — The forms ending कृत् affixes or तद्धित affixes, or compound are also called प्रातिपदिक।",
    "Sūtra 1.2.47: hrasvonapumsakepraatipadikasya (ह्रस्वो नपुंसके प्रातिपदिकस्य) — The short vowel is substituted in the neuter, for the final vowel, of a प्रातिपदिक।",
    "Sūtra 1.2.48: gostriyorupasarjanasya (गोस्त्रियोरुपसर्जनस्य) — A short vowel is the substitute of प्रातिपदिक which ends with the word गो 'a cow' and of that which ends with what has as its termination a feminine affix, when regarded as उपसर्जन।",
    "Sūtra 1.2.49: luktaddhitaluki (लुक् तद्धितलुकि) — When a तद्धित affix is elided by the word लुक् there takes place the elision by लुक् of feminine affix of the उपसर्जन।",
    "Sūtra 1.2.50: idgonyaah (इद्गोण्याः) — The short is substituted in the place of गोणी , when the तद्धित affix is elided by लुक्।",
    "Sūtra 1.2.51: lupiyuktavadvyaktivachane (लुपि युक्तवद्व्यक्तिवचने) — When a तद्धित affix is elided by using the word लुप् , then the gender and number (of the derivative word) agree with those of the original word.",
    "Sūtra 1.2.52: visheshanaanaamchaajaateh (विशेषणानां चाजातेः) — And of adjectives (the gender and number are the same as of the word formed by लुप् elision of the तद्धित and which they qualify) so far as the जाति (or kind of species) is concerned, (or when not expressing जाति).",
    "Sūtra 1.2.53: tadashishyamsamjnyaapramaanatvaat (तदशिष्यं संज्ञाप्रमाणत्वात्) — This (concord or gender and number, of primitive and derivative nouns, and of attributes and substantives need not be taught (or approved), because it has the authority of संज्ञा (conventional term or idiom).",
    "Sūtra 1.2.54: lubyogaaprakhyaanaat (लुब्योगाप्रख्यानात्) — The sūtras declaring लुप् elision need not also be taught, because of the non-currency of the etymological meaning of the words supposed to be formed by लुप् elision.",
    "Sūtra 1.2.55: yogapramaanechatadabhaavedarshanamsyaat (योगप्रमाणे च तदभावेऽदर्शनं स्यात्) — And if the etymological meaning 'be held authoritative', then when such meaning is absent, the word also should vanish.",
    "Sūtra 1.2.56: pradhaanapratyayaarthavachanamarthasyaanyapramaanatvaat (प्रधानप्रत्ययार्थवचनमर्थस्यान्यप्रमाणत्वात्) — (Nor need be taught) the rule relating to the dependance of the meaning of a word on the principal (प्रधान in a compound) or on the affix (प्रत्यय) because the authority of the meaning (of a word, compound or derivative) consists in something else.",
    "Sūtra 1.2.57: kaalopasarjanechatulyam (कालोपसर्जने च तुल्यम्) — And a rule fixing the meaning of Tense (काल) and उपसर्जन (sequence) is equally (unnecessary, and need not be taught).",
    "Sūtra 1.2.58: jaatyaakhyaayaamekasminbahuvachanamanyatarasyaam (जात्याख्यायामेकस्मिन् बहुवचनमन्यतरस्याम्) — In (a common) name (expressive of) class, in denoting the singular, the plural is optionally used.",
    "Sūtra 1.2.59: asmadodvaayoshcha (अस्मदो द्वयोश्च) — The plural of the pronoun अस्मद् 'I', is used optionally, though the sense requires a singular or a dual number.",
    "Sūtra 1.2.60: phalguneeproshthapadaanaamchanakshatre (फल्गुनीप्रोष्ठपदानां च नक्षत्रे) — And the dual of फाल्गुनी and प्रष्ठपदा , when signifying asterisms, (also connotes optionally plural).",
    "Sūtra 1.2.61: chhandasipunarvasvorekavachanam (छन्दसि पुनर्वस्वोरेकवचनम्) — In the Vedas, the two stars, पुनर्वासू , may optionally be singular, (and connote a dual).",
    "Sūtra 1.2.62: vishaakhayoshcha (विशाखयोश्च) — In the Vedas, the two stars विशाखा may optionally be in the singular number.",
    "Sūtra 1.2.63: tishyapunarvasvornakshatradvamdvebahuvachanasyadvivachanamnityam (तिष्यपुनर्वस्वोर्नक्षत्रद्वन्द्वे बहुवचनस्य द्विवचनं नित्यम्) — In the द्वन्द compounds of the stars तिष्व and पुनर्वसू , the dual constantly comes in place of the plural.",
    "Sūtra 1.2.64: saroopaanaamekasheshekavibhaktau (सरूपाणामेकशेष एकविभक्तौ) — Of the words having the same form and all in the same one case-termination, the last one is only retained.",
    "Sūtra 1.2.65: vruddhoyoonaatallakshanashchedevavisheshah (वृद्धो यूना तल्लक्षणश्चेदेव विशेषः) — The वृद्ध (or patronymic गोत्र word becomes एकशेष and is retained, when compounded) with a patronymic word युवन् , provided that the specific difference in form between them be in their signs (affix) only.",
    "Sūtra 1.2.66: streepumvachcha (स्त्री पुंवच्च) — And so also a feminine word, ending with a वृद्ध affix, when similarly spoken along with the same word but which ends with a युवन् affix, is only retained and it is treated like a masculine.",
    "Sūtra 1.2.67: pumaanstriyaa (पुमान् स्त्रिया) — A word in the masculine gender, similarly spoken along with the same word, but ending with the feminine affix, becomes एकशेष and the latter is dropped.",
    "Sūtra 1.2.68: bhraatruputrausvasruduhitrubhyaam (भ्रातृपुत्रौ स्वसृदुहितृभ्याम्) — The words भ्रातृ 'brother' and पुत्र 'son', when spoken of along with स्वसृ 'sister' and दुहितृ 'daughter' respectively are only retained and the latter are dropped.",
    "Sūtra 1.2.69: napumsakamanapumsakenaikavachchaasyaanyatarasyaam (नपुंसकमनपुंसकेनैकवच्चास्यान्यतरस्याम्) — A neuter noun, which has the same form, only differing in affix, is optionally retained and the other is dropped and it is like a singular number.",
    "Sūtra 1.2.70: pitaamaatraa (पिता मात्रा) — The word पितृ 'father' is optionally only retained when spoken of along with मातृ 'mother'.",
    "Sūtra 1.2.71: shvashurahashvashrvaa (श्वशुरः श्वश्र्वा) — The word श्वशुर 'father-in-law', is optionally only retained, when spoken of along with श्वशुरू 'mother-in-law'.",
    "Sūtra 1.2.72: tyadaadeenisarvairnityam (त्यदादीनि सर्वैर्नित्यम्) — The pronouns त्यद् etc. when spoken of along with any other noun, (pronoun other than त्यद् etc.) are always retained as एकशेष (to the exclusion of others).",
    "Sūtra 1.2.73: graamyapashusamgheshuataruneshustree (ग्राम्यपशुसंघेष्वतरुणेषु स्त्री) — The feminine noun is only retained when denoting a collection of domestic animals, not being young.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.1: bhoovaadayodhaatavah (भूवादयो धातवः) — The words beginning with भू 'to become' and denoting action, are called धातु or verbal roots.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.2: upadesheajanunaasikait (उपदेशेऽजनुनासिक इत्) — The nasalised vowels are इत् in उपदेश or original enunciation.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.3: halantyam (हलन्त्यम्) — In उपदेश , the final consonant of roots etc. is इत्।",
    "Sūtra 1.3.4: navibhaktautusmaah (न विभक्तौ तुस्माः) — The final dental consonants and the final स् and म् are not इत् , in affixes called विभक्ति or inflective affixes.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.5: aadirnyitudavah (आदिर्ञिटुडवः) — The initial ञि , टु , डु are इत्।",
    "Sūtra 1.3.6: shahapratyayasya (षः प्रत्ययस्य) — The initial ष् of an affix is indicatory.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.7: chutoo (चुटू) — The initial palatals and linguals of an affix are indicatory.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.8: lashakvataddhite (लशक्वतद्धिते) — The initial ल् and श् and the gutturals of all affixes, except , तद्धित are indicatory.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.9: tasyalopah (तस्य लोपः) — Of this, (namely of that which has been called इत् ), there is elision.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.10: yathaasamkhyamanudeshahasamaanaam (यथासंख्यमनुदेशः समानाम्) — When a rule involves the case of equal numbers of substitutes and of things for which these are to be substituted, their mutual correspondence or assignment of each to each, is according to the order of enumeration.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.11: svaritenaadhikaarah (स्वरितेनाधिकारः) — In these aphorisms, when a word is marked with a स्वरित accent, by that an अधिकार or a governing rule is to be understood.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.12: anudaattangitaatmanepadam (अनुदात्तङित आत्मनेपदम्) — After a root which has an indicatory अनुदात्त vowel (अनुदात्तेत्) or an indicatory ङ् (ङित्), the affixes are those of the आत्मनेपद।",
    "Sūtra 1.3.13: bhaavakarmmanoh (भावकर्मणोः) — An आत्मनेपद affix is the substitute of the affix ल [[3.4.69]] when it denotes the action of the verb or the object of the verb.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.14: kartarikarmmavyatihaare (कर्तरि कर्मव्यतिहारे) — In denoting the agent, when reciprocity of action is to be expressed, the affixes of the आत्मनेपद are employed.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.15: nagatihimsaarthebhyah (न गतिहिंसार्थेभ्यः) — After verbs having the sense of 'motion', or 'injury', when expressing interchange of action, the आत्मनेपद affixes are used.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.16: itaretaraanyonyopapadaachcha (इतरेतरान्योन्योपपदाच्च) — And after the verbs which take the words इतरेतर 'each other' and अन्योन्य 'one another', as उपपद (or dependant qualifying words), the affixes of आत्मनेपद are not used, though reciprocity of action be denoted.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.17: nervishah (नेर्विशः) — After the verb विश् 'to enter', when preceded by the preposition नि, the आत्मनेपद affixes are employed",
    "Sūtra 1.3.18: parivyavebhyahakriyah (परिव्यवेभ्यः क्रियः) — After the verb क्री 'to purchase', when preceded by परि , वि or अव , the आत्मनेपद affix is employed, even when the fruit of the action does not accrue to the agent.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.19: viparaabhyaamjeh (विपराभ्यां जेः) — After the verb जि 'to conquer', preceded by वि or परा , the आत्मनेपद affix is employed.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.20: aangodonaasyaviharane (आङो दोऽनास्यविहरणे) — After the verb दा 'to give', preceded by अङ् , and when not meaning 'to open the mouth', the आत्मनेपद affix is used, even when the fruit of the action does not accrue to the agent.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.21: kreedonusamparibhyashcha (क्रीडोऽनुसम्परिभ्यश्च) — After the verb क्रीड 'to play', preceded by अनु , सम् , or परि as well as आङ्, the आत्मनेपद affix is used.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.22: samavapravibhyahasthah (समवप्रविभ्यः स्थः) — After the verb स्था 'to stand', preceded by सम् , अव , प्र , वि , the आत्मनेपद affix is used.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.23: prakaashanastheyaakhyayoshcha (प्रकाशनस्थेयाख्ययोश्च) — After the verb स्था 'when meaning to indicate one's intentions to another', or 'to make an award as an arbitrator', the आत्मनेपद affix is employed.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.24: udonoorddhvakarmani (उदोऽनूर्ध्वकर्मणि) — After the verb स्था 'to stand', preceded by उत् , when not meaning 'to get up or rise', as from a seat; the आत्मनेपद affix is used.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.25: upaanmantrakarane (उपान्मन्त्रकरणे) — After the verb स्था 'to stand', preceded by उप , when meaning 'to adore', the आत्मनेपद affix is used.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.26: akarmakaachcha (अकर्मकाच्च) — After the verb स्था 'to stand', preceded by उप , when meaning 'to adore', the आत्मनेपद affix is used.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.27: udvibhyaamtapah (उद्विभ्यां तपः) — After the word तप 'to shine', when used intransitively and preceded by उत् or वि the आत्मनेपद affix is used.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.28: aangoyamahanah (आङो यमहनः) — After the verb यम् 'to stop' and हन् 'to injure', when used intransitively and preceded by अन् , the आत्मनेपद affix is used.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.29: samogamyruchchhiprachchhisvaratyartishruvidibhyah (समो गम्यृच्छिप्रच्छिस्वरत्यर्तिश्रुविदिभ्यः) — After the verbs गम् 'to go', ऋच्छ् 'to become hard', प्रच्छ् 'to ask', स्वर् 'to find fault', ऋ 'to go', श्रु 'to hear' and विद् 'to know', when used intransitively and preceded by सम् , the आत्मनेपद affix is used.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.30: nisamupavibhyohvah (निसमुपविभ्यो ह्वः) — After the verbs ह्वे 'to call', preceded by नि , सम् , उप and वि , the आत्मनेपद is used, even, when the fruit of the action does not accrue to the agent.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.31: sparddhaayaamaangah (स्पर्द्धायामाङः) — After the verbs ह्वे 'to call', when meaning 'to challenge' and preceded by अङ् , the आत्मनेपद is used, even, when the fruit of the action does not accrue to the agent.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.32: gandhanaavakshepanasevanasaahasikyapratiyatnaprakathanopayogeshukrunyah (गन्धनावक्षेपणसेवनसाहसिक्यप्रतियत्नप्रकथनोपयोगेषु कृञः) — After the verb कृ when meaning 'to divulge', 'to revile', 'to serve', 'to use violence', 'to cause change', 'to recite' and 'to do an act tending to effect a desired purpose', the आत्मनेपद is used, even when the fruit of the action does not accrue to the agent.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.33: adhehaprasahane (अधेः प्रसहने) — After the verb कृ preceded by अधि , when the sense is that of 'overcoming or defeat', the आत्मनेपद is used, even when the fruit of the action does not accrue to the agent.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.34: vehashabdakarmanah (वेः शब्दकर्मणः) — After the verb कृ preceded by वि , even when the fruit of the action does not accrue to the agent, and when the sense is that of 'making sound' (literally having 'sound' for its object), the आत्मनेपद affix is used.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.35: akarmakaachcha (अकर्मकाच्च) — After the verb कृ preceded by वि , when used intransitively, the आत्मनेपद is used.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.36: sammaananotsanyjanaachaaryakaranajnyaanabhrutivigananavyayeshuniyah (सम्माननोत्सञ्जनाचार्यकरणज्ञानभृतिविगणनव्ययेषु नियः) — After the verb नी 'to lead', when used in the sense of 'to guide so as to render the person guided worthy', 'to lift up', 'make one a spiritual guide', 'to determine the true sense', 'to employ on wages', 'to pay debt' and 'to give as in charity', even when the fruit of the action does not accrue to the agent, the आत्मनेपद is used.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.37: kartrusthechaashareerekarmani (कर्तृस्थे चाशरीरे कर्मणि) — After the verb नी , when it governs an incorporeal object in the agent, as its object, the आत्मनेपद is used.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.38: vruttisargataayaneshukramah (वृत्तिसर्गतायनेषु क्रमः) — After the verb क्रम् 'to move', when used in the senses of 'continuity', 'energy' and 'development', the आत्मनेपद is used.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.39: upaparaabhyaam (उपपराभ्याम्) — After the verb क्रम् , preceded by उप and पर , when used in the senses of 'continuity', 'energy' and 'development', the आत्मनेपद is used.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.40: aangudgamane (आङ उद्गमने) — After the verb क्रम् , preceded by an अङ् , the आत्मनेपद is used,when in the sense of 'the rising of a luminary'.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.41: vehpaadaviharane (वेः पादविहरणे) — After the verb क्रम् preceded by वि , the आत्मनेपद is used, when in the sense of 'placing of foot-steps'.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.42: propaabhyaamsamarthaabhyaam (प्रोपाभ्यां समर्थाभ्याम्) — After the verb क्रम् preceded by वि , the आत्मनेपद is used when it is preceded by प्र and उप , both conveying the same sense; viz. that of 'beginning an action'.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.43: anupasargaadvaa (अनुपसर्गाद्वा) — After the verb क्रम् the आत्मनेपद is optionally used, when it is not preceded by any preposition.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.44: apahnavejnyah (अपह्नवे ज्ञः) — After the verb ज्ञ , when used in the sense of 'denying', the आत्मनेपद is used.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.45: akarmakaachcha (अकर्मकाच्च) — And when used intransitively after the verb ज्ञ , the आत्मनेपद is used, when the fruit of the action does not accrue to the agent.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.46: sampratibhyaamanaadhyaane (सम्प्रतिभ्यामनाध्याने) — After the verb ज्ञ , preceded by सम् and प्रति , the आत्मनेपद is used, when Not Used in the sense of 'remembering with regret'.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.47: bhaasanopasambhaashaajnyaanayatnavimatyupamantraneshuvadah (भासनोपसम्भाषाज्ञानयत्नविमत्युपमन्त्रणेषु वदः) — After the verb वद् , the आत्मनेपद is used, when used in the senses of 'showing brilliance, or proficiency in', pacifying', 'knowledge', 'effort', 'difference of opinion' and 'flattering'.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.48: vyaktavaachaamsamuchchaarane (व्यक्तवाचां समुच्चारणे) — After the verb वद् , the आत्मनेपद is used, when used in the sense of 'speaking articulately in a similar manner'.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.49: anorakarmakaat (अनोरकर्मकात्) — After the verb वद् , preceded by अनु when it is intransitively used, the आत्मनेपद is used, when the sense is that of 'speaking articulately in a similar manner'.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.50: vibhaashaavipralaape (विभाषा विप्रलापे) — After the verb वद् , the आत्मनेपद is used optionally, when the sense is that of 'contradicting with each other'.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.51: avaadgrah (अवाद्ग्रः) — After the verb गॄ 'to swallow', when preceded by अव, the आत्मनेपद is used.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.52: samahapratijnyaane (समः प्रतिज्ञाने) — After the verb गॄ 'to swallow', when preceded by सम् , the आत्मनेपद affix is used in the sense of 'promising'.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.53: udashcharahasakarmakaat (उदश्चरः सकर्मकात्) — After the verb चर् 'to walk' preceded by उत् , when used intransitively, the आत्मनेपद is used.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.54: samastruteeyaayuktaat (समस्तृतीयायुक्तात्) — After the verb चर् 'to walk' preceded by सम् , and when connected with a noun in the Instrumental - 3rd Case, the आत्मनेपद is used.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.55: daanashchasaachechchaturthyarthe (दाणश्च सा चेच्चतुर्थ्यर्थे) — And after the verb दा 'to give', preceded by सम् , and connected with a noun in the Instrumental - 3rd Case, the आत्मनेपद affix is used, provided this Instrumental Case has the sense of the Dative - 4th Case.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.56: upaadyamahasvakarane (उपाद्यमः स्वकरणे) — After the verb यम् 'to give', preceded by उप , when used in the sense of 'espousing', the आत्मनेपद is used.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.57: jnyaashrusmrudrushaamsanah (ज्ञाश्रुस्मृदृशां सनः) — After the Desideratives formed by the affix सन् , of the verbs ज्ञा 'to know', श्रु 'to hear', स्मृ 'to remember' and दृश् 'to see', the आत्मनेपद is used.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.58: naanorjnyah (नानोर्ज्ञः) — After the Desiderative of ज्ञा 'to know' when preceded by अनु , the आत्मनेपद affix is Not used.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.59: pratyaangbhyaamshruvah (प्रत्याङ्भ्यां श्रुवः) — After the Desideratives of श्रु 'to hear', when preceded by प्रत and आङ् , the आत्मनेपद affix is Not used.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.60: shadehashitah (शदेः शितः) — After the verb शद् 'to decay', when it has one of the affixes with an indicatory श् (शित्) the आत्मनेपद is used.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.61: mriyaterlunglingoshcha (म्रियतेर्लुङ्लिङोश्च) — After the verb मृ 'to die', when it has one of the affixes having an indicatory श् , as well as when it takes the affixes लुङ् (Aorist [[3.2.110]]) and लिङ् (Benedictive [[3.3.159]]), the आत्मनेपद is used.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.62: poorvavatsanah (पूर्ववत् सनः) — The verb which is आत्मनेपदि in its primitive form before taking of the affix सन् , will also be आत्मनेपदि when it ends in the affix सन्। in other words; after a Desiderative verb, आत्मनेपद is used, if it would have been used after the primitive verb.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.63: aampratyayavatkrunyonuprayogasya (आम्प्रत्ययवत् कृञोऽनुप्रयोगस्य) — Like the verb that takes the affix आम् , if the verb be conjugated with the आत्मनेपद terminations, so of the verb कृ when subjoined thereto as an auxiliary, the terminations are of the आत्मनेपद , even when the fruit of the action does not accrue to the agent.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.64: propaabhyaamyujerayajnyapaatreshu (प्रोपाभ्यां युजेरयज्ञपात्रेषु) — After the verb युज् 'to join', the आत्मनेपद is used, when it is preceded by प्र and उप except with reference to sacrificial vessels even when the fruit of the action does not accrue to the agent.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.65: samahakshnuvah (समः क्ष्णुवः) — After the verb क्षणु 'to sharpen', preceded by सम् , the आत्मनेपद is used.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.66: bhujonavane (भुजोऽनवने) — After the verb भुज् , the आत्मनेपद is used, except in the sense of protecting.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.67: neranauyatkarmanauchetsakartaanaadhyaane (णेरणौ यत्कर्म णौ चेत् स कर्ताऽनाध्याने) — After a verb ending in the affix णि (causal) the आत्मनेपद is used, provided that when the object in the non-णि or non-causal sense becomes the agent in the causal; and when it does not mean 'to remember with regret', even when the fruit of the action does not accrue to the agent.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.68: bheesmyorhetubhaye (भीस्म्योर्हेतुभये) — After the causatives of the verbs भी 'to fear' and स्मि 'to wonder' even when the fruit of the action does not accrue to the agent the आत्मनेपद is employed, when the fear is produced directly by the causative agent.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.69: grudhivanychyohapralambhane (गृधिवञ्च्योः प्रलम्भने) — After the causatives of the verbs गृध 'to covet' and वञ्च 'to go' the आत्मनेपद is used in the sense of 'deceiving' even though the fruit of the action does not accrue to the agent.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.70: liyahasammaananashaaleeneekaranayoshcha (लियः सम्माननशालीनीकरणयोश्च) — After the causative of the verb लि 'to melt or stick', the आत्मनेपद is employed, when used in the sense of showing respect, subduing and deceiving, even though the fruit of action does not accrue to the agent.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.71: mithyopapadaatkrunyobhyaase (मिथ्योपपदात् कृञोऽभ्यासे) — After the causative of the verb कृ , the आत्मनेपद is used, when it has the word मिथ्या 'incorrect', as an उपपद or dependent word and is used in the sense of 'repeated wrong utterance', even when the fruit of action does not accrue no the agent.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.72: svaritanyitahakartrabhipraayekriyaaphale (स्वरितञितः कर्त्रभिप्राये क्रियाफले) — After the verb marked with a स्वरित or which has an indicatory ञित् , the terminations of the आत्मनेपद are used, when the fruit of the action accrues to the agent.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.73: apaadvadah (अपाद्वदः) — After the verb वद् 'to tell', preceded by अप , when the fruit of the action accrues to the agent, the terminations are of the आत्मनेपद।",
    "Sūtra 1.3.74: nichashcha (णिचश्च) — After a verb ending in the affix णि (causal) when the fruit of the action accrues to the agent, the आत्मनेपद is used.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.75: samudaangbhyoyamogranthe (समुदाङ्भ्यो यमोऽग्रन्थे) — After the verb यम् 'to strive', preceded by सम् , उत् and आङ् , when it does not refer to a book, the आत्मनेपद is used, when the fruit of the action accrues to the agent.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.76: anupasargaajjnyah (अनुपसर्गाज्ज्ञः) — After the verb ज्ञा , when not preceded by any उपसर्ग , the terminations are of the आत्मनेपद , when the fruit of the action accrues to the agent.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.77: vibhaashopapadenaprateeyamaane (विभाषोपपदेन प्रतीयमाने) — The आत्मनेपद is optionally used, when the fact of the fruit of the action accruing to the agent is indicted by an उपपदग i.e. by a word used along with the verb.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.78: sheshaatkartariparasmaipadam (शेषात् कर्तरि परस्मैपदम्) — After the rest i.e. all those verbs not falling under any one of the previous provisions, the terminations of the परस्मैपद are used, in marking the agent i.e. in the active voice.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.79: anuparaabhyaamkrunyah (अनुपराभ्यां कृञः) — After the verb कृ 'to make' preceded by the अनु and पर , परस्मैपद is used, even the fruit of the action goes to the agent and when the sense is that of 'divulging' etc.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.80: abhipratyatibhyahakshipah (अभिप्रत्यतिभ्यः क्षिपः) — After the verb क्षिप् 'to throw', coming after अभि , प्रति and अति , परस्मैपद is used, even though the fruit of the action goes to the agent",
    "Sūtra 1.3.81: praadvahah (प्राद्वहः) — After the verb वह् 'to bear', coming after प्र , परस्मैपद is used, even though the fruit of the action accrues to the the agent.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.82: parermrushah (परेर्मृषः) — After the verb मृष् 'to bear', preceded by परि , परस्मैपद is used when the fruit of the action accrues to the agent.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.83: vyaangparibhyoramah (व्याङ्परिभ्यो रमः) — After the verb रम् 'to sport', preceded by वि and आङ् , परस्मैपद is used.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.84: upaachcha (उपाच्च) — And also after उप , the verb रम् takes the affixes of the परस्मैपद।",
    "Sūtra 1.3.85: vibhaashaakarmakaat (विभाषाऽकर्मकात्) — After the verb रम् 'to sport', preceded by उप , परस्मैपद is optionally used, when employed intransitively.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.86: budhayudhanashajanengprudrusrubhyoneh (बुधयुधनशजनेङ्प्रुद्रुस्रुभ्यो णेः) — After the verbs बुध् 'to know', युध् 'to fight', नश् 'to destroy', जन 'to be born', एङ् 'to go', प्रु 'to move', द्रु 'to run' and स्रु 'to flow', ending in the affix णे (i.e. when used in the causative), परस्मैपद is used, even when the fruit of the action goes to the agent.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.87: nigaranachalanaarthebhyah (निगरणचलनार्थेभ्यश्च) — And after the causatives of verbs which have no sense of the 'eating or swallowing' and 'shaking or moving' परस्मैपद is used, even when the fruit of the action goes to the agent.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.88: anaavakarmakaachchittavatkartrukaat (अणावकर्मकाच्चित्तवत्कर्तृकात्) — The affixes of the परस्मैपद are used after the causal of that verb, which in its non-causal state was intransitive and had a being endowed with reason for its agent, even when the fruit of the action accrues to the agent.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.89: napaadamyaangyamaangyasaparimuharuchinrutivadavasah (न पादम्याङ्यमाङ्यसपरिमुहरुचिनृतिवदवसः) — But the affixes of the परस्मैपद are not used after the causals of the verbs पा 'to drink', दम् 'to tame', आयम् 'to extend', आयस् 'to exert oneself', परिमुह 'to be bewildered', रुच् 'to shine' नृत् 'to dance', वद् 'to speak' and वस् 'to dwell'.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.90: vaakyashah (वा क्यषः) — The affixes of the परस्मैपद are used optionally after the denominative verbs ending in the affix क्यष।",
    "Sūtra 1.3.91: dyudbhyolungi (द्युद्भ्यो लुङि) — After the verbs द्युत् 'to shine' etc., the terminations of the परस्मैपद are optionally employed, when the affixes of लुण् (Aorist) follow.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.92: vrudbhyahasyasanoh (वृद्भ्यः स्यसनोः) — After the verbs वृत् 'to exist' etc., परस्मैपद is optionally used when the affixes स्य (Future and conditional) and सन् (Desiderative) follow.",
    "Sūtra 1.3.93: lutichakapah (लुटि च कॢपः) — After the verb क्लिप् 'to be fit', परस्मैपद is optionally used, when लुट् (1st Future) is affixed, as well as when स्य and सन् are affixed.",
    "Sūtra 1.4.1: aakadaaraadekaasamjnyaa (आ कडारादेका संज्ञा) — From this सूत्र up the the aphorism कडाराः कर्मधारये [[2.2.38]] only one name of each thing named is to be understood.",
    "Sūtra 1.4.2: vipratishedheparamkaaryam (विप्रतिषेधे परं कार्यम्) — When rules of equal force prohibit each other then the last in the order herein given is to take effect.",
    "Sūtra 1.4.3: yoostryaakhyaunadee (यू स्त्र्याख्यौ नदी) — Word-forms ending in long ई and ऊ being names of females called नदी।",
    "Sūtra 1.4.4: neyanguvangsthaanaavastree (नेयङुवङ्स्थानावस्त्री) — Feminine words ending in ई and ऊ which admit the substitute इयङ् and उवङ् [[6.1.77]] are not called नदी ; except the word स्त्री (which is called नदी not withstanding its substituting इयङ्).",
    "Sūtra 1.4.5: vaami (वाऽऽमि) — Feminine words ending in ई and ऊ though admitting इयङ् and उवङ् [[6.1.77]] substitutes, are optionally termed नदी when the affix अम् (Genitive Plural) follows, but not so the word स्त्री , which is always नदी।",
    "Sūtra 1.4.6: ngitihrasvashcha (ङिति ह्रस्वश्च) — When a case-affix having an indicatory ङ् (ङित्) follows, then feminine words ending in short इ and उ are optionally termed नदी , as well as feminine nouns in long ई and ऊ which admit इयङ् and उवङ् ; but not so the word स्त्री which is always नदी।",
    "Sūtra 1.4.7: sheshoghyasakhi (शेषो घ्यसखि) — The rest of the words that end in short इ and उ are घि with the exception of the word सखि।",
    "Sūtra 1.4.8: patihasamaaseva (पतिः समास एव) — The word पति is called घि only when it is in a compound.",
    "Sūtra 1.4.9: shashtheeyuktashchhandasivaa (षष्ठीयुक्तश्छन्दसि वा) — The word पति when used in connection with a noun ending in the 6th or genitive case, is घि , optionally, in the छन्दस् (Veda).",
    "Sūtra 1.4.10: hrasvamlaghu (ह्रस्वं लघु) — A short vowel is called लघु 'light'.",
    "Sūtra 1.4.11: samyogeguru (संयोगे गुरु) — When a conjunct consonant follows a short vowel is termed गुरु 'heavy'.",
    "Sūtra 1.4.12: deerghamcha (दीर्घं च) — And a long vowel is also called गुरु 'heavy'.",
    "Sūtra 1.4.13: yasmaatpratyayavidhistadaadipratyayenggam (यस्मात् प्रत्ययविधिस्तदादि प्रत्ययेऽङ्गम्) — After whatsoever there is an affix enjoined, whether verbal or crude-form, that which begins therewith in the form in which it appears when the affix follows it, is called an अङ्ग 'Inflective base'.",
    "Sūtra 1.4.14: suptingantampadam (सुप्तिङन्तं पदम्) — That which ends in सुप् 'case-affix' [[4.1.2]] or तिङ् [[3.4.78]] (tense-affix), is called पद or inflected word.",
    "Sūtra 1.4.15: nahakye (नः क्ये) — The word-form ending in न् , is called पद when क्य follows (i.e. the affixes क्यच् , क्यङ् and क्यष्।",
    "Sūtra 1.4.16: siticha (सिति च) — When an affix having an indicatory स् follows then that which precedes it is called पद।",
    "Sūtra 1.4.17: svaadishvasarvanaamasthaane (स्वादिष्वसर्वनामस्थाने) — When the affixes beginning with a सु [[4.1.2]] and ending in कप् [[5.4.151]] follow, not being सर्वनामस्थान [[1.1.43]] then that which precedes is called पद।",
    "Sūtra 1.4.18: yachibham (यचि भम्) — And when an affix with an initial य् or an initial vowel, being one of the affixes, beginning with सु and ending in क् , follows, not being सर्वनामस्थान , then what precedes, is called भ।",
    "Sūtra 1.4.19: tasaumatvarthe (तसौ मत्वर्थे) — The word-form ending in त् or in स् is called भ when an affix with the force of मतुप् 'whose is it' or 'in whom it is' [[5.2.94]], follows.",
    "Sūtra 1.4.20: ayasmayaadeenichchhandasi (अयस्मयादीनि च्छन्दसि) — Words like अयस्मय etc. are valid forms in the छन्दस्।",
    "Sūtra 1.4.21: bahushubahuvachanam (बहुषु बहुवचनम्) — In expressing multeity, a Plural case affix is employed.",
    "Sūtra 1.4.22: dvyekayordvivachanaikavachane (द्व्येकयोर्द्विवचनैकवचने) — The dual and singular case-affixes are employed severally in the sense of duality and unity.",
    "Sūtra 1.4.23: kaarake (कारके) — The phrase कारक (meaning 'in the special relation to a word expressing an action') is to be understood in the following aphorisms.",
    "Sūtra 1.4.24: dhruvamapaayepaadaanam (ध्रुवमपायेऽपादानम्) — A noun whose relation to an action is that of a fixed point from which departure takes place is called अपादान or Ablation.",
    "Sūtra 1.4.25: bheetraarthaanaambhayahetuh (भीत्रार्थानां भयहेतुः) — In case of words implying 'fear' and 'protection from danger' that from which the danger of fear proceeds is called अपादान कारक।",
    "Sūtra 1.4.26: paraajerasodhah (पराजेरसोढः) — In the case of the verb पराजि 'to be tired or weary of', that which becomes unbearable, is called अपादान कारक।",
    "Sūtra 1.4.27: vaaranaarthaanaameepsitah (वारणार्थानामीप्सितः) — In case of verbs having the sense of 'preventing, the desired object from which one is prevented or warded off', is called Ablation or अपदान कारक।",
    "Sūtra 1.4.28: antarddhauyenaadarshanamichchhati (अन्तर्द्धौ येनादर्शनमिच्छति) — When concealment is indicated, the person whose sight one wishes to avoid, is called अपादान कारक।",
    "Sūtra 1.4.29: aakhyaatopayoge (आख्यातोपयोगे) — The noun denoting the teacher is called Ablation or अपादान , in relation to the action signifying formal teaching.",
    "Sūtra 1.4.30: janikartuhaprakrutih (जनिकर्तुः प्रकृतिः) — The prime cause of the agent of the verb जन् 'to be born', is called अपादान।",
    "Sūtra 1.4.31: bhuvahaprabhavah (भुवः प्रभवः) — The source of the agent of the verb भू 'to become' is called अपादान।",
    "Sūtra 1.4.32: karmanaayamabhipraitisasampradaanam (कर्मणा यमभिप्रैति स सम्प्रदानम्) — The person whom one wishes to connect with the object of giving, is called सम्प्रदान or recipient.",
    "Sūtra 1.4.33: ruchyarthaanaampreeyamaanah (रुच्यर्थानां प्रीयमाणः) — In case of verbs having the signification of the root रुच् 'to like', the person or thing that is pleased or satisfied, is called सम्प्रदान or recipient.",
    "Sūtra 1.4.34: shlaaghahnungsthaashapaamjnyeepsyamaanah (श्लाघह्नुङ्स्थाशपां ज्ञीप्स्यमानः) — In case of verbs श्लाघ् 'to praise', ह्नु 'to take away', स्था 'to stand', शप् 'to curse', the person whom it is intended to inform of or persuade by, these actions, is called सम्प्रदान।",
    "Sūtra 1.4.35: dhaareruttamarnah (धारेरुत्तमर्णः) — In the case of the verb धारि 'to owe', the creditor is called सम्प्रदान।",
    "Sūtra 1.4.36: spruhereepsitah (स्पृहेरीप्सितः) — In the case of the verb स्पृह् 'to desire', the thing desired is called सम्प्रदान कारक।",
    "Sūtra 1.4.37: krudhadruhershyaasooyaarthaanaamyampratikopah (क्रुधद्रुहेर्ष्याऽसूयार्थानां यं प्रति कोपः) — In the case of the verbs having the sense of क्रद्ध् 'to be angry', द्रुह् 'to injure', ईर्ष्या 'to envy', असूया 'to detract', the person against whom the feeling of anger etc. is directed is called सम्प्रदान।",
    "Sūtra 1.4.38: krudhadruhorupasrushtayohakarma (क्रुधद्रुहोरुपसृष्टयोः कर्म) — But in the case of the verbs क्रुद्ध् and द्रुह् , when preceded by prepositions, the person against whom the feeling of anger etc. is directed is called कर्म कारक or object.",
    "Sūtra 1.4.39: raadhikshyoryasyaviprashnah (राधीक्ष्योर्यस्य विप्रश्नः) — In the case of the verbs राध् 'to propitiate' and ईक्ष् 'to look to', the person about whose good or bad fortune questions are asked is called सम्प्रदान।",
    "Sūtra 1.4.40: pratyaangbhyaamshruvahapoorvasyakartaa (प्रत्याङ्भ्यां श्रुवः पूर्वस्य कर्ता) — In the case of the verb श्रु preceded by the prepositions प्रति and अङ् and meaning 'to promise', the person to whom promise is made (literally: the person who as the agent of the former verb) is called सम्प्रदान।",
    "Sūtra 1.4.41: anupratigrunashcha (अनुप्रतिगृणश्च) — In the case of the verb गृ preceded by अनु and प्रति and meaning 'to encourage by repeating', the person who was the agent of the prior action, which is repeated, is called सम्प्रदान।",
    "Sūtra 1.4.42: saadhakatamamkaranam (साधकतमं करणम्) — That which is especially auxiliary in the accomplishment of the action is called Instrument or करण कारक।",
    "Sūtra 1.4.43: divahakarmacha (दिवः कर्म च) — That which is especially auxiliary in the accomplishment of the action, of the verb दिव् 'to play' is called कर्म - object, as well as करण।",
    "Sūtra 1.4.44: parikrayanesampradaanamanyatarasyaam (परिक्रयणे सम्प्रदानमन्यतरस्याम्) — In the case of hiring on wages, that which is especially auxiliary in the accomplishment of the action of the verb परिक्री 'employing on stipulated wages', is optionally called सम्प्रदान or recipient.",
    "Sūtra 1.4.45: aadhaarodhikaranam (आधारोऽधिकरणम्) — That which is related to the action as the site where the action is performed by reason of the agent or the object being in that place is called अधिकरण or location.",
    "Sūtra 1.4.46: adhisheengsthaasaamkarma (अधिशीङ्स्थाऽऽसां कर्म) — That which is the site of the verbs शीङ् 'to lie down', स्था 'to stand', आस् 'to sit', when preceded by the preposition अधि , is however called कर्म कारक or object.",
    "Sūtra 1.4.47: abhinivishashcha (अभिनिविशश्च) — That which is the site of the verb अभिनिविश् 'to enter', is also called कर्म कारक।",
    "Sūtra 1.4.48: upaanvadhyaangvasah (उपान्वध्याङ्वसः) — That which is the site of the verb वस् 'to dwell', when preceded by उप , अनु , and आङ् is called कर्म कारक।",
    "Sūtra 1.4.49: kartureepsitatamamkarma (कर्तुरीप्सिततमं कर्म) — That which is intended should be most effected by the act of the agent is called the object or कर्म।",
    "Sūtra 1.4.50: tathaayuktamchaanipseetam (तथायुक्तं चानीप्सितम्) — If that which is not intended to be most affected by the act becomes however similarly connected with the action it also is called कर्म।",
    "Sūtra 1.4.51: akathitamcha (अकथितं च) — And if that कारक which is not spoken of as coming under any of the special relations of Ablation etc., is also called कर्म।",
    "Sūtra 1.4.52: gatibuddhipratyavasaanaarthashabdakarmaakarmakaanaamanikartaa (गतिबुद्धिप्रत्यवसानार्थशब्दकर्माकर्मकाणामणि कर्ता स णौ) — Of the verbs having the sense of 'motion', 'knowledge or information' and 'eating' and of verbs that have some literary work for their object and of intransitive verbs, that which was the agent of the verb in its primitive (non-णि or non-causal state), is called the कर्म or object, in its causative state (when the verb takes the affix णि).",
    "Sūtra 1.4.53: hrukroranyatarasyaam (हृक्रोरन्यतरस्याम्) — The agent of the verb in its non-णि (primitive) form in the case of हृ 'to lose' and कृ 'to make', is optionally called कर्म or object when these verbs take the affix.",
    "Sūtra 1.4.54: svatantrahakartaa (स्वतन्त्रः कर्ता) — Whatever the speaker chooses as the independent, principal and absolute source of action is called कर्ता or agent.",
    "Sūtra 1.4.55: tatprayojakohetushcha (तत्प्रयोजको हेतुश्च) — That which is the mover thereof, i.e. of the independent source of action, is called हेतु or cause, as well as कर्ता or agent.",
    "Sūtra 1.4.56: praagreeshvaraannipaataah (प्राग्रीश्वरान्निपाताः) — From this point forward up to the aphorism अधिरीश्वरे [[1.4.97]], all that we shall say is to be understood to have the name of निपात or Particles.",
    "Sūtra 1.4.57: chaadayosattve (चादयोऽसत्त्वे) — The word च 'and' etc. are called निपात or Particles, when they do not signify substances.",
    "Sūtra 1.4.58: praadayah (प्रादयः) — The words प्र etc. are called निपात when not signifying substances.",
    "Sūtra 1.4.59: upasargaahakriyaayoge (उपसर्गाः क्रियायोगे) — The words प्र etc. get the designation of उपसर्ग or prepositions, when in composition with a verb.",
    "Sūtra 1.4.60: gatishcha (गतिश्च) — The words प्र etc. are called also गति when in composition with a verb.",
    "Sūtra 1.4.61: ooryaadichvidaachashcha (ऊर्यादिच्विडाचश्च) — The words उरी 'assent' etc. and those that end with च्वि [[5.4.50]] and those that end with डाच् [[5.4.57]] (when in composition with the verb भू , कृ or अस् ) are called गति।",
    "Sūtra 1.4.62: anukaranamchaanitiparam (अनुकरणं चानितिपरम्) — A word imitative of sounds is also called गति when it is not followed by the word इति।",
    "Sūtra 1.4.63: aadaraanaadarayohasadasatee (आदरानादरयोः सदसती) — The words सत् and असत् when in composition with a verb is called गति , when used in the sense of 'respect or love' and 'disrespect or indifference'.",
    "Sūtra 1.4.64: bhooshanelam (भूषणेऽलम्) — The word अलम् when in composition with a verb is called गति , when used in the sense of 'ornament'.",
    "Sūtra 1.4.65: antaraparigrahe (अन्तरपरिग्रहे) — The word अन्तर् is called गति , when used in the sense of 'non-accepting', when in composition with a verb.",
    "Sūtra 1.4.66: kanemanaseeshraddhaaprateeghaate (कणेमनसी श्रद्धाप्रतीघाते) — The words कणे and मनस् are गति when in composition with a verb and used in the sense of 'reaction by satiation'.",
    "Sūtra 1.4.67: purovyayam (पुरोऽव्ययम्) — The word पुरः 'in front of', when indeclinable and in composition with a verb, is called गति।",
    "Sūtra 1.4.68: astamcha (अस्तं च) — And the indeclinable word अस्तम् 'at home' is called गति , when in composition with a verb.",
    "Sūtra 1.4.69: achchhagatyarthavadeshu (अच्छ गत्यर्थवदेषु) — The indeclinable word अच्छ 'before in the presence of' is called गति , when used in the composition with verbs denoting 'motion' or with the verb वद् 'to speak'.",
    "Sūtra 1.4.70: adonupadeshe (अदोऽनुपदेशे) — The word अदस् 'that' is called गति when in composition with a verb and not implying a direction to another.",
    "Sūtra 1.4.71: tirontarddhau (तिरोऽन्तर्द्धौ) — The word तिरस् when used in the sense of 'disappearance' is called गति when in composition with a verb.",
    "Sūtra 1.4.72: vibhaashaakrunyi (विभाषा कृञि) — The word तिरस् 'disappearance' is optionally called गति when the verb कृ follows.",
    "Sūtra 1.4.73: upaajenvaaje (उपाजेऽन्वाजे) — The words उपाजे and अनवाजे both meaning 'supporting or assisting the weak', are optionally called गति when used along with the verb कृ।",
    "Sūtra 1.4.74: saakshaatprabhruteenicha (साक्षात्प्रभृतीनि च) — The words साक्षात् 'in the presence of' etc. are optionally called गति when used along with the verb कृ।",
    "Sūtra 1.4.75: anatyaadhaanurasimanasee (अनत्याधान उरसिमनसी) — The word उर्सि 'in the breast' and मनसि 'in the mind' ae optionally called गति when the verb कृ follows, provided that they are not used in the sense of 'placing'.",
    "Sūtra 1.4.76: madhyepadenivachanecha (मध्ये पदे निवचने च) — And the words मध्ये 'in the middle', पदे 'in the foot' and निवचने 'speechless' are optionally called गति , when कृ follows, the sense not being of placing.",
    "Sūtra 1.4.77: nityamhastepaanaavupayamane (नित्यं हस्ते पाणावुपयमने) — The word हस्ते 'in the hand', पाणौ 'in the hand' are always necessarily called गति when used with the verb कृ in the sense of 'marriage'.",
    "Sūtra 1.4.78: praadhvambandhane (प्राध्वं बन्धने) — The indeclinable word प्रध्वम् followed by the verb कृ , is always called गति when in used in the sense of 'binding'.",
    "Sūtra 1.4.79: jeevikopanishadaavaupamye (जीविकोपनिषदावौपम्ये) — The words जीविका and उपनिषद् followed by the verb कृ are called गति when used in the sense of 'likeness and resemblance'.",
    "Sūtra 1.4.80: tepraagdhaatoh (ते प्राग्धातोः) — The particles called गति and उपसर्ग are to be employed before the verbal roots (i.e. to say that they are prefixes).",
    "Sūtra 1.4.81: chhandasiparepi (छन्दसि परेऽपि) — In the छन्दस् (Veda) these गति and उपसर्ग are employed indifferently after the verbal root, as well as before it.",
    "Sūtra 1.4.82: vyavahitaashcha (व्यवहिताश्च) — In the छन्दस् (Veda) these गति and उपसर्ग are also seen separated from the verb by intervening words.",
    "Sūtra 1.4.83: karmapravachaneeyaah (कर्मप्रवचनीयाः) — From this point as far as aphorism [[1.4.97]] treated of, are to be understood as having the name of कर्म-प्रवचनीय।",
    "Sūtra 1.4.84: anurlakshane (अनुर्लक्षणे) — The word अनु , when it denotes a sign, is called कर्म-प्रवचनीय।",
    "Sūtra 1.4.85: truteeyaarthe (तृतीयार्थे) — The word अनु , कर्म-प्रवचनीय when it has the force of the 3rd case.",
    "Sūtra 1.4.86: heene (हीने) — The word अनु , कर्म-प्रवचनीय when it is used in the sense of 'inferior or subordinate to'.",
    "Sūtra 1.4.87: upodhikecha (उपोऽधिके च) — The word उप when it means 'superior' or 'inferior to' is कर्म-प्रवचनीय।",
    "Sūtra 1.4.88: apapareevarjane (अपपरी वर्जने) — The words अप and परि are कर्म-प्रवचनीय when meaning 'exclusion'.",
    "Sūtra 1.4.89: aangmaryaadaavachane (आङ् मर्यादावचने) — The word आङ् 'as far as', is कर्म-प्रवचनीय when it expresses limit (e.g. when it means 'as far as inclusive of' or 'as far as exclusive of').",
    "Sūtra 1.4.90: lakshanetthambhootaakhyaanabhaagaveepsaasupratiparyanavah (लक्षणेत्थम्भूताख्यानभागवीप्सासु प्रतिपर्यनवः) — The words प्रति , परि and अनु are कर्म-प्रवचनीय when used in the sense of 'sign' ('in the direction of') , 'mere statement of circumstances' ('as regards'), 'division', 'share of' and 'pervasion', severally.",
    "Sūtra 1.4.91: abhirabhaage (अभिरभागे) — The word अभि is कर्म-प्रवचनीय when used in the above senses of 'in the direction of', 'as regards', and 'each severally', but not when it means 'division', 'share of'.",
    "Sūtra 1.4.92: pratihapratinidhipratidaanayoh (प्रतिः प्रतिनिधिप्रतिदानयोः) — The word प्रति is कर्म -प्रवचनीय when used in the sense of representative ('representative of') or exchange ('in exchange for').",
    "Sūtra 1.4.93: adhipareeanarthakau (अधिपरी अनर्थकौ) — The words अधि and परि are कर्म-प्रवचनीय when used as mere expletives.",
    "Sūtra 1.4.94: suhapoojaayaam (सुः पूजायाम्) — The word सु is कर्म-प्रवचनीय when used in the sense of respect, (when it means 'excellently').",
    "Sūtra 1.4.95: atiratikramanecha (अतिरतिक्रमणे च) — The word अति in the sense of super-abundance ('excessively') and 'excellently' is कर्म-प्रवचनीय।",
    "Sūtra 1.4.96: apihapadaarthasambhaavanaanvavasargagarhaasamuchchayeshu (अपिः पदार्थसम्भावनान्ववसर्गगर्हासमुच्चयेषु) — The word अपि is कर्म-प्रवचनीय when it implies, the sense of word 'understood' ('somewhat') or 'possibility' (e.g. 'even' in the sense of such a great person), or permission to do as one likes, ('if you like'), or censure ('even' in the sense of what is disgraceful); or collection ('and').",
    "Sūtra 1.4.97: adhireeshvare (अधिरीश्वरे) — The words अधि is कर्म-प्रवचनीय when used in the sense of 'lord' ('being as a lord' or 'having as a lord')",
    "Sūtra 1.4.98: vibhaashaakrunyi (विभाषा कृञि) — The words अधि is optionally कर्म-प्रवचनीय when the verb कृ follows.",
    "Sūtra 1.4.99: lahaparasmaipadam (लः परस्मैपदम्) — The substitutes of ल are called परस्मैपद।",
    "Sūtra 1.4.100: tangaanaavaatmanepadam (तङानावात्मनेपदम्) — The nine affixes comprised under the प्रत्याहार - तङ् and the two ending in आन (शानच् and कानच्), which are substitutes of ल are called आत्मनेपद।",
    "Sūtra 1.4.101: tingastreenitreeniprathamamadhyamottamaah (तिङस्त्रीणि त्रीणि प्रथममध्यमोत्तमाः) — The three triads in both the sets परस्मैपद and आत्मनेपद , of conjugational affixes (comprised under the general name तिङ् , a प्रत्यहार formed of the first and last of them, viz. तिप् and महिङ्) are called, in order, Lowest - 3rd Person of European Grammar, Middle -2nd Person, and Highest -1st Person.",
    "Sūtra 1.4.102: taanyekavachanadvivachanabahuvachanaanyekashah (तान्येकवचनद्विवचनबहुवचनान्येकशः) — These three triads of conjugational affixes, which have received the name of Lowest etc. are called (as regard the three expressions in each triad) severally 'the expression for one' (singular), 'the expression for two' (dual) and 'the expression for many' (plural).",
    "Sūtra 1.4.103: supah (सुपः) — Of सुप् (which is a प्रत्याहार formed of सु the first of the case affixes and the final प् of the last of them), the expressions in each successive set of the three, are also severally called singular, dual and plural.",
    "Sūtra 1.4.104: vibhaktishcha (विभक्तिश्च) — The triads of conjugational affixes and case affixes are also called विभक्ति or Inflective affixes.",
    "Sūtra 1.4.105: yushmadyupapadesamaanaadhikaranesthaaninyapimadhyamah (युष्मद्युपपदे समानाधिकरणे स्थानिन्यपि मध्यमः) — When the pronoun युष्मद् 'thou' understood, and also when the same expressed, is the attendant word in the agreement with the verb, then there is the verbal termination called the middle (2nd person).",
    "Sūtra 1.4.106: prahaasechamanyopapademanyateruttamekavachcha (प्रहासे च मन्योपपदे मन्यतेरुत्तम एकवच्च) — When joke is implied with reference to an action, the verb denoting it is used in the 2nd person; provided that the word मन्य 'to think' is the attendant word (उपपद) of such verb and of the verb मन्य itself, the affix must be of the 1st person and singular number.",
    "Sūtra 1.4.107: asmadyuttamah (अस्मद्युत्तमः) — When the pronoun अस्मद् 'I', understood and also when expressed, is the attendant word in agreement with the verb, then there is the verbal termination called the Highest or 1st person.",
    "Sūtra 1.4.108: shesheprathamah (शेषे प्रथमः) — In the other cases, viz. where 'thou' or 'I' are not the attendant words in agreement with the verb, there is the verbal termination called the Lowest (3rd person).",
    "Sūtra 1.4.109: parassannikarshahasamhitaa (परः सन्निकर्षः संहिता) — The closest proximity of letters, there being the intervention of half a मात्रा or prosodial length between them, is called contact or संहिता।",
    "Sūtra 1.4.110: viraamovasaanam (विरामोऽवसानम्) — The cessation or the absence of succeeding letters is called pause or अवसान।",
    "Sūtra 2.1.1: samarthahapadavidhih (समर्थः पदविधिः) — A rule which relates to complete words (and not to the roots out of which the words are constructed) is to be understood to apply only to those words the senses of which are connected.",
    "Sūtra 2.1.2: subaamantriteparaanggavatsvare (सुबामन्त्रिते पराङ्गवत् स्वरे) — A word ending in सुप् or a case-affix, when followed by a word in the Vocative Case, is regarded as if it was the अङ्ग or component part of such subsequent vocative word, when a rule relating to accent is to be applied.",
    "Sūtra 2.1.3: praakkadaaraatsamaasah (प्राक् कडारात् समासः) — From this point up to the aphorism कडाराः कर्मधारये [[2.2.38]], all the terms that we shall say, describe will get the designation of समास or compound",
    "Sūtra 2.1.4: sahasupaa (सह सुपा) — The words सह सुपा meaning 'with a word ending in a case-affix', are to be understood in each of the succeeding aphorisms.",
    "Sūtra 2.1.5: avyayeebhaavah (अव्ययीभावः) — From this point forward whatever we shall describe will get the name अव्ययीभाव समास or adverbial compound.",
    "Sūtra 2.1.6: avyayamvibhaktisameepasamruddhivyruddhyarthaabhaavaatyayaasampratishabdapraadurbhaavapashchaadyathaanupoorvyayaugapadyasaadrushyasampattisaakalyaantavachaneshu (अव्ययं विभक्तिसमीपसमृद्धिव्यृद्ध्यर्थाभावात्ययासम्प्रतिशब्दप्रादुर्भावपश्चाद्यथानुपूर्व्ययौगपद्यसादृश्यसम्पत्तिसाकल्यान्तवचनेषु) — An अव्यय - indeclinable, used with the sense of an inflective-affix (विभक्ति) or of near to, or prosperity, or diversity, or absence of the thing, or departure, or not now, or the production of some sound, or after, or according to, or order of arrangement, or totality, or termination, is invariably compounded with a word ending in a case-affix which is connected with it in sense and the compound so formed is called अव्ययीभाव।",
    "Sūtra 2.1.7: yathaasaadruye (यथासादृश्ये) — The indeclinable word यथा when it does not signify 'likeness' is invariably compounded with a word ending in a case-affix which is in construction with it and the compound is called अव्ययीभाव समास।",
    "Sūtra 2.1.8: yaavadavadhaarane (यावदवधारणे) — The indeclinable word यावत् when it signifies limitation, is invariably compounded with a word ending in a case-affix which is in construction with it, and the compound so formed is called अव्ययीभाव।",
    "Sūtra 2.1.9: suppratinaamaatraarthe (सुप्प्रतिना मात्रार्थे) — A word ending in a case-affix is compounded with the indeclinable word प्रति , when meaning 'a little' and the compound so formed is called अव्ययीभाव।",
    "Sūtra 2.1.10: akshashalaakaasamkhyaahaparinaa (अक्षशलाकासंख्याः परिणा) — The words अक्ष 'a die for playing with', शलाका 'an ivory piece used in gambling' and सङ्खया 'numerals' are compounded with the word परि and the compound so formed is called अव्ययीभाव।",
    "Sūtra 2.1.11: vibhaashaa (विभाषा) — The word विभाषा or option governs all succeeding sūtras.",
    "Sūtra 2.1.12: apaparibahiranychavahapanychamyaa (अपपरिबहिरञ्चवः पञ्चम्या) — The words अप , परि , बहिल् and indeclinables ending in अञ्चु may optionally be compounded with a word ending in the 5th case affix and the compound so formed will be अव्ययीभाव ।",
    "Sūtra 2.1.13: aangmaryaadaabhividhyoh (आङ् मर्यादाभिविध्योः) — The word आङ् when signifying limit exclusive or limit inclusive, may optionally be compounded with a word ending in the 5th case and the compound so formed is called अव्ययीभाव।",
    "Sūtra 2.1.14: lakshanenaabhiprateeaabhimukhye (लक्षणेनाभिप्रती आभिमुख्ये) — The words अभि and प्रति when implying direction (towards), are optionally compounded with a word ending in a case-affix denoting the limit, or the goal which regulates or marks the direction and the resulting compound is अव्ययीभाव।",
    "Sūtra 2.1.15: anuryatsamayaa (अनुर्यत्समया) — The word अनु 'near to' is optionally compounded with that word, nearness to which is indicated by the particle and the resulting compound is अव्ययीभाव।",
    "Sūtra 2.1.16: yasyachaayaamah (यस्य चायामः) — The word अनु 'alongside of' is optionally compounded with the word indicative of that whose length the particle expresses and compound so formed is called अव्ययीभाव।",
    "Sūtra 2.1.17: tishthadguprabhruteenicha (तिष्ठद्गुप्रभृतीनि च) — And the words तिष्ठद्गु 'at the time when the cows stand to be milked', etc. are अव्ययीभाव compounds.",
    "Sūtra 2.1.18: paaremadhyeshashthyaavaa (पारे मध्ये षष्ठ्या वा) — The words पार 'across' and मध्य 'middle' may optionally be compounded with a word ending in the 6th-Case-affix, when they take forms परे and मध्ये and the compound so formed is अव्ययीभाव।",
    "Sūtra 2.1.19: samkhyaavamshyena (संख्या वंश्येन) — A numeral (संख्या) may be compounded with a word denoting 'one belonging to a family' and the resulting compound is अव्ययीभाव ।",
    "Sūtra 2.1.20: nadeebhishcha (नदीभिश्च) — A numeral (संख्या) may be compounded with the names of 'rivers' and the resulting compound is अव्ययीभाव denoting an aggregate.",
    "Sūtra 2.1.21: anyapadaarthechasamjnyaayaam (अन्यपदार्थे च संज्ञायाम्) — A word ending in a case-affix is compounded with words denoting the names of rivers, when the compound word denotes a thing other than that expressed by the terms of the compound and is an appellative, the compound so formed being an अव्ययीभाव ।",
    "Sūtra 2.1.22: tatpurushah (तत्पुरुषः) — From this sūtra as far as sūtra [[2.2.23]], the word तत्-पुरुष is governing word, and is understood in all the following sūtras.",
    "Sūtra 2.1.23: dvigushcha (द्विगुश्च) — And the compound called द्विगु (Numeral Determinative Compound) is all called तत्-पुरुष ।",
    "Sūtra 2.1.24: dviteeyaashritaateetapatitagataatyastapraaptaapannaih (द्वितीया श्रितातीतपतितगतात्यस्तप्राप्तापन्नैः) — A word ending in a 2nd case-affix is compounded with the words श्रित 'who had recourse to', अतीत 'gone by', पतित 'who has fallen upon', गत 'who has gone to', अत्यस्त 'who has passed', प्राप्त 'who has obtained' and अपान्न 'who has reached' and the resulting compound is called तत्-पुरुष ।",
    "Sūtra 2.1.25: svayamktena (स्वयं क्तेन) — The indeclinable word स्वयम् 'oneself' is compounded with a word ending in the affix क्त and the resulting compound is तत्-पुरुष ।",
    "Sūtra 2.1.26: khatvaakshepe (खट्वा क्षेपे) — The word खट्वा in the Accusative -2nd case is compounded with a word ending in the affix क्त , when censure is implied and the compound so formed is तत्-पुरुष ।",
    "Sūtra 2.1.27: saami (सामि) — The indeclinable word सामि 'half' is compounded with a word ending in the affix क्त and the resulting compound is तत्-पुरुष ।",
    "Sūtra 2.1.28: kaalaah (कालाः) — The words denoting time, being in the Accusative -2nd case, are optionally compounded with a word ending in the affix क्त and the resulting compound is तत्-पुरुष।",
    "Sūtra 2.1.29: atyantasamyogecha (अत्यन्तसंयोगे च) — Words denoting time being in the Accusative -2nd case, are optionally compounded with a word ending in a case-affix, when used in the sense of complete connection throughout with the time (i.e. duration of time) and the resulting compound is तत्-पुरुष।",
    "Sūtra 2.1.30: truteeyaatatkrutaarthenagunavachanena (तृतीया तत्कृतार्थेन गुणवचनेन) — A word ending with the Instrumental -3rd case-affix is optionally compounded with what denotes quality, the quality being that which is instrumentally caused by the thing signified by what ends with the 3rd case-affix and with the word अर्थ 'wealth' and the resulting compound is तत्-पुरुष ।",
    "Sūtra 2.1.31: poorvasadrushasamonaarthakalahanipunamishrashlakshnaih (पूर्वसदृशसमोनार्थकलहनिपुणमिश्रश्लक्ष्णैः) — A word ending in Instrumental -3rd case-affix is compounded with the words पूर्व 'prior', सदृश 'like', सम 'similar', अनर्थ 'words having the sense of less', कलह 'quarrel', निपुण 'proficient', मिश्र 'mixed' and श्लक्षण 'polished sleek', and the resulting compound is तत्-पुरुष ।",
    "Sūtra 2.1.32: kartrukaranekrutaabahulam (कर्तृकरणे कृता बहुलम्) — A word ending with the Instrumental -3rd case-affix, when it denotes the agent or instrument -- [[2.3.18]], is compounded diversely with what ends with a कृत् affix and the resulting compound is तत्-पुरुष ।",
    "Sūtra 2.1.33: krutyairadhikaarthavachane (कृत्यैरधिकार्थवचने) — A word ending with the Instrumental -3rd case-affix when it denotes the agent or the Instrument, is compounded optionally with a word ending in a कृत्य affix, when exaggerated statement (whether of praise or of censure) is implied and the resulting compound is तत्-पुरुष ।",
    "Sūtra 2.1.34: annenavyanyjanam (अन्नेन व्यञ्जनम्) — A word ending with the Instrumental -3rd case-affix and denoting a condiment, is optionally compounded with a word ending in a case-affix, signifying food and the resulting compound is तत्-पुरुष ।",
    "Sūtra 2.1.35: bhakshyenamishreekaranam (भक्ष्येण मिश्रीकरणम्) — A word ending with the Instrumental -3rd case-affix and denoting a relish giving or refining ingredient, is compounded with a word meaning, victuals and the resulting compound is तत्-पुरुष ।",
    "Sūtra 2.1.36: chaturtheetadarthaarthabalihitasukharakshitaih (चतुर्थी तदर्थार्थबलिहितसुखरक्षितैः) — A word ending with the Dative -4th case is compounded with what denotes that which is for the purpose of what ends with the Dative -4th case and so too with the words अर्थ 'on account of', बलि 'a sacrifice', हित 'salutary', सुख 'pleasure' and रक्षित 'kept' and the resulting compound is तत्-पुरुष ।",
    "Sūtra 2.1.37: panychameebhayena (पञ्चमी भयेन) — A word ending with the Ablative -5th case-affix is optionally compounded with the word भय 'fear' and the resulting compound is तत्-पुरुष ।",
    "Sūtra 2.1.38: apetaapodhamuktapatitaapatrastairalpashah (अपेतापोढमुक्तपतितापत्रस्तैरल्पशः) — A word ending with the Ablative -5th case-affix is compounded with the words अपेत 'gone away', अपोध 'carried away', मुक्त 'freed', पतित 'fallen', अपत्रस्त 'afraid of', when the event takes place in a gradual manner and the resulting compound is तत्-पुरुष ।",
    "Sūtra 2.1.39: stokaantikadooraarthakruchchhraaniktena (स्तोकान्तिकदूरार्थकृच्छ्राणि क्तेन) — Words with a sense of स्तोक 'a little', अन्तिक 'near', दूर 'far' and कृच्छ्र 'penance', ending in the Ablative -5th case are compounded with what ends in क्त and the resulting compound is तत्-पुरुष ।",
    "Sūtra 2.1.40: saptameeshaundaih (सप्तमी शौण्डैः) — A word ending in the Locative -7th-case-affix is compounded with the words शौण्ड 'skilled' etc. and the resulting compound is तत्-पुरुष ।",
    "Sūtra 2.1.41: siddhashushkapakvabandhaishcha (सिद्धशुष्कपक्वबन्धैश्च) — A word ending with the Locative -7th-case-affix is compounded with the words सिद्ध 'perfected', शुष्क 'dried', पक्व 'cooked', and बन्ध 'bound' and the resulting compound is तत्-पुरुष । ",
    "Sūtra 2.1.42: dhvaangkshenakshepe (ध्वाङ्क्षेण क्षेपे) — A word ending in the Locative -7th-case-affix is compounded with the words ध्वाङ्क्ष 'a crow' and synonyms of crow when contempt is implied and the resulting compound is तत्-पुरुष ।",
    "Sūtra 2.1.43: krutyairrune (कृत्यैर्ऋणे) — A word ending with the Locative -7th-case-affix is compounded with words ending with कृत्य-affix (a Future Passive Participle) and the resulting compound is तत्-पुरुष ।",
    "Sūtra 2.1.44: sanjnaayaam (संज्ञायाम्) — A word ending with the Locative -7th-case-affix is invariably compounded with a word ending in a case-affix, when the compound thus formed is used as an appellative and the resulting compound is तत्-पुरुष ।",
    "Sūtra 2.1.45: ktenaahoraatraavayavaah (क्तेनाहोरात्रावयवाः) — The names of divisions of day or night ending with Locative -7th-case-affix are compounded with words ending with affix क्त and the resulting compound is तत्-पुरुष ।",
    "Sūtra 2.1.46: tatra (तत्र) — The word तत्र 'there' which is a word ending with Locative -7th-case-affix सप्तम्यास्त्रल् [[5.3.10]], is compounded with a word ending in क्त and the resulting compound is तत्-पुरुष ।",
    "Sūtra 2.1.47: kshepe (क्षेपे) — The word ending in Locative -7th-case-affix is compounded with a word ending with the affix क्त when 'censure' is implied and the resulting compound is तत्-पुरुष ।",
    "Sūtra 2.1.48: paatresamitaadayashcha (पात्रेसमितादयश्च) — The words like पात्रे-सम्मित 'a dish-companion' (a parasite) etc. are तत्-पुरुष compounds when contempt is implied.",
    "Sūtra 2.1.49: poorvakaalaikasarvajaratpuraananavakevalaahasamaanaadhikaranena (पूर्वकालैकसर्वजरत्पुराणनवकेवलाः समानाधिकरणेन) — A case-inflected word denoting an action which naturally precedes in time (पूर्वकाल) and the words एक 'one', सर्व 'all' जरत 'old', पुराण 'ancient', नव 'new', and केवल 'only' are compounded with their co-relative case-inflected words which are in the same case with them and the resulting compound is तत्-पुरुष ।",
    "Sūtra 2.1.50: diksamkhyesamjnyaayaam (दिक्संख्ये संज्ञायाम्) — The words expressing a point of the compass or a number (संख्या ) enter into composition with the word correlated to them by being in the same case, when the sense of the compound is that of an appellative and the resulting compound is तत्-पुरुष ।",
    "Sūtra 2.1.51: taddhitaarthottarapadasamaahaarecha (तद्धितार्थोत्तरपदसमाहारे च) — In a case where the sense is that of a तद्धित-affix or when an additional member comes after the compound or when an aggregate is to be expressed, then a word signifying a point of the compass or a number, enters into composition with a case-inflected word which is in agreement with it by being in the same case and the resulting compound is तत्-पुरुष ।",
    "Sūtra 2.1.52: samkhyaapoorvodviguh (संख्यापूर्वो द्विगुः) — In a case where the sense is that of a तद्धित-affix or when an additional member comes after the compound or when an aggregate is to be expressed, the compound, the first member of which is numeral, is called द्विगु (Numeral Determinative Compound).",
    "Sūtra 2.1.53: kutsitaanikutsanaih (कुत्सितानि कुत्सनैः) — Case-inflected words expressing vileness are compounded with case-inflected words, expressing contempt and the resulting compound is तत्-पुरुष ।",
    "Sūtra 2.1.54: paapaanakekutsitaih (पापाणके कुत्सितैः) — The case-inflected words पाप 'sin' and अणक 'insignificant' are compounded with words expressive of vileness and the resulting compound is तत्-पुरुष ।",
    "Sūtra 2.1.55: upamaanaanisaamaanyavachanaih (उपमानानि सामान्यवचनैः) — Case-inflected words denoting objects of comparison are compounded with words denoting what is likened to them, by reason of the latter possessing qualities in common with the former and the resulting compound is तत्-पुरुष ।",
    "Sūtra 2.1.56: upamitamvyaaghraadibhihasaamaanyaaprayoge (उपमितं व्याघ्रादिभिः सामान्याप्रयोगे) — A case-inflected word denoting subject of comparison is compounded with the words व्याघ्र 'tiger' etc., the latter being the standard of comparison and in construction with the former and the resulting compound is तत्-पुरुष ; provided that any word expressing the common characteristic (सामान्य) as explained above, is not used.",
    "Sūtra 2.1.57: visheshanamvisheshyenabahulam (विशेषणं विशेष्येण बहुलम्) — A case-inflected word denoting the qualifier (the Adjective), is compounded diversely with a case-inflected word denoting the thing thereby qualified, (the Substantive), the latter being in agreement (same case) with the former and the resulting compound is तत्-पुरुष ।",
    "Sūtra 2.1.58: poorvaaparaprathamacharamajaghanyasamaanamadhyamadhyamaveeraashcha (पूर्वापरप्रथमचरमजघन्यसमानमध्यमध्यमवीराश्च) — A case-inflected words पूर्व 'prior', अपर 'other', प्रथम 'first', चरम 'last', जघन्य 'hindmost', समान 'equal', मध्य 'middle', मध्यम 'middle', and वीर 'hero' are compounded with words ending with a case-affix and which are in agreement (same case) with them and the resulting compound is तत्-पुरुष ।",
    "Sūtra 2.1.59: shrenyaadayahakrutaadibhih (श्रेण्यादयः कृतादिभिः) — The case-inflected words श्रेणी 'class' etc. are compounded with words कृत् 'made' etc. which are in agreement (same case), with them and the resulting compound is तत्-पुरुष ।",
    "Sūtra 2.1.60: ktenananyvishishtenaanany (क्तेन नञ्विशिष्टेनानञ्) — A word ending with the affix क्त and not having the negative augment नञ् is compounded with the same word ending with the affix क्त but which is distinguished from the former, by having the augment नञ् and the resulting compound is तत्-पुरुष ।",
    "Sūtra 2.1.61: sanmahatparamottamotkrushtaahapoojyamaanaih (सन्महत्परमोत्तमोत्कृष्टाः पूज्यमानैः) — The words सत् 'good, महत् 'great', परम 'highest', उत्तम 'best' and उत्कृष्ट 'excellent' are compounded with the words denoting the person deserving the respect and the resulting compound is तत्-पुरुष ।",
    "Sūtra 2.1.62: vrundaarakanaagakunyjaraihapoojyamaanam (वृन्दारकनागकुञ्जरैः पूज्यमानम्) — A case-inflected word denoting object deserving of respect is compounded with the words वृन्दारक 'eminent', नाग 'serpent or elephant', कुञ्जर 'elephant' and the resulting compound is तत्-पुरुष ।",
    "Sūtra 2.1.63: katarakatamaujaatipariprashne (कतरकतमौ जातिपरिप्रश्ने) — The words कतर 'which or who of two', and कतम 'which or who of many', when used in asking questions about the genus or class, are compounded with the other case-inflected words with which they are in construction and the resulting compound is तत्-पुरुष ।",
    "Sūtra 2.1.64: kimkshepe (किं क्षेपे) — The word किम् 'what', when implying 'contempt' is compounded with a word ending in case-affix and the resulting compound is तत्-पुरुष ।",
    "Sūtra 2.1.65: potaayuvatistokakatipayagrushtidhenuvashaavehatbashkayaneepravaktrushrotriyaadhyaapakadhoortairjaatih (पोटायुवतिस्तोककतिपयगृष्टिधेनुवशावेहत्बष्कयणीप्रवक्तृश्रोत्रियाध्यापकधूर्तैर्जातिः) — A case-inflected word denoting a genus (जाति) is compounded with the words पोटा 'a hermaphrodite', युवति 'a young female', स्तोक 'a little', कतिपय 'a few', गृष्टि 'a cow which has had only one calf', धेनु 'milch cow', वशा 'a barren female', वेहद् 'a cow that miscarries', बष्कयणी 'a cow that has a full-grown calf', प्रवक्तृ 'an expounder', श्रोत्रिय 'a learned ब्राह्मण ', अध्यापक 'a teacher' and धूर्त 'a cunning fellow' and the resulting compound is तत्-पुरुष ।",
    "Sūtra 2.1.66: prashamsaavachanaishcha (प्रशंसावचनैश्च) — A case-inflected word denoting a genus (जाति) is compounded with a word denoting praise and the resulting compound is तत्-पुरुष ।",
    "Sūtra 2.1.67: yuvaakhalatipalitavalinajarateebhih (युवा खलतिपलितवलिनजरतीभिः) — The word युवा 'young' is compounded with the words खलति 'bald headed', पलित 'grey-haired', वलिन 'wrinkled', जरति 'decayed', when they are in agreement (same case) and the resulting compound is तत्-पुरुष ।",
    "Sūtra 2.1.68: krutyatulyaakhyaaajaatyaa (कृत्यतुल्याख्या अजात्या) — Words ending with कृत् -affix and the word तुल्य 'equal' and its synonyms are compounded with words which do not denote genus (जाति) being in the same case with them and the resulting compound is तत्-पुरुष ।",
    "Sūtra 2.1.69: varnovarnena (वर्णो वर्णेन) — A case-inflected word denoting 'colour' is compounded with another case-inflected word which is in agreement with the former and also denotes colour and the resulting compound is तत्-पुरुष ।",
    "Sūtra 2.1.70: kumaarahashramanaadibhih (कुमारः श्रमणादिभिः) — The word कुमार 'a boy' is compounded with co-ordinate words श्रमण 'an ascetic' etc. and the resulting compound is तत्-पुरुष ।",
    "Sūtra 2.1.71: chatushpaadogarbhinyaa (चतुष्पादो गर्भिण्या) — A case-inflected word denoting a quadruped is compounded with the co-ordinate word गर्भिणी and the resulting compound is तत्-पुरुष ।",
    "Sūtra 2.1.72: mayooravyamsakaadayashcha (मयूरव्यंसकादयश्च) — And the words मयूर-व्यंसका 'cunning like a peacock' etc. are तत्-पुरुष compounds.",
    "Sūtra 2.2.1: poorvaaparaadharottaramekadeshinaikaadhikarane (पूर्वापराधरोत्तरमेकदेशिनैकाधिकरणे) — The words पूर्व 'front', अपर 'near', अधर 'lower', उत्तर 'upper', are compounded when in construction with a word signifying a thing that has parts, provided that the thing having parts is distinguished numerically by unity; and the compound is तत्-पुरुष।",
    "Sūtra 2.2.2: ardhamnapumsakam (अर्धं नपुंसकम्) — The word अर्द्ध when it signifies exactly equal parts i.e. halves, is always neuter and is compounded with a word signifying a thing that has parts, provided that the thing halved is numerically one; and the compound is तत्-पुरुष।",
    "Sūtra 2.2.3: dviteeyatruteeyachaturthaturyaanyanyatarasyaam (द्वितीयतृतीयचतुर्थतुर्याण्यन्यतरस्याम्) — The words द्वितीय 'second', तृतीय 'third', चतुर्थ 'fourth', तुर्य 'fourth', are optionally compounded with that word which signifies a thing that has parts, provided that the thing having parts is distinguished numerically by unity. The compound so formed is called तत्-पुरुष।",
    "Sūtra 2.2.4: praaptaapannechadviteeyayaa (प्राप्तापन्ने च द्वितीयया) — The words प्राप्त 'obtained', and आपन्न 'obtained' are optionally compounded with words ending in a Second Case-affix and form तत्-पुरुष compound.",
    "Sūtra 2.2.5: kaalaahaparimaaninaa (कालाः परिमाणिना) — Words denoting time are compounded when in construction, with words denoting the object whose duration is measured by the time, and the compound is तत्-पुरुष।",
    "Sūtra 2.2.6: nany (नञ्) — The negative word नञ् is compounded with a case-inflected word with which it is in construction, and the compound is तत्-पुरुष।",
    "Sūtra 2.2.7: eeshadakrutaa (ईषदकृता) — The word ईषत् 'a little' is compounded with a case-inflected word which does not end with a कृत् affix and the compound is तत्-पुरुष।",
    "Sūtra 2.2.8: shashthee (षष्ठी) — A word ending with a sixth case-affix is compounded with a case-inflected word with which it is in construction and the compound is तत्-पुरुष।",
    "Sūtra 2.2.9: yaajakaadibhishcha (याजकादिभिश्च) — A word ending with a sixth case-affix is compounded with the word याजक 'sacrificer' etc. and the compound is तत्-पुरुष।",
    "Sūtra 2.2.10: nanirdhaarane (न निर्धारणे) — A word in the genitive case is not compounded with another, when the force of the sixth case-affix is that of specification (निर्धारण).",
    "Sūtra 2.2.11: pooranagunasuhitaarthasadavyayatavyasamaanaadhikaranena (पूरणगुणसुहितार्थसदव्ययतव्यसमानाधिकरणेन) — A word ending in a sixth case-affix is not compounded with a word having the sense of an ordinal, an attribute, or satisfaction, or with a participle ending in the suffix सत् 3.2127, or an indeclinable, or ending with the affix तव्य , or with a word denoting the same object (i.e. when they are in apposition).",
    "Sūtra 2.2.12: ktenachapoojaayaam (क्तेन च पूजायाम्) — A word ending with sixth case-affix is not compounded with a word ending with the affix क्त , when the force of क्त is to denote 'respect' etc.",
    "Sūtra 2.2.13: adhikaranavaachinaacha (अधिकरणवाचिना च) — A word ending with a sixth case-affix is not compounded with a word ending with the affix क्त , when the force of the latter is to denote 'locality' in which something happened",
    "Sūtra 2.2.14: karmmanicha (कर्मणि च) — A word ending with a sixth case-affix is not compounded with another, when the force of the genitive is that of the accusative.",
    "Sūtra 2.2.15: trujakaabhyaamkartari (तृजकाभ्यां कर्तरि) — A word ending with a sixth case-affix is not compounded with a word ending with त्रिच् or अक , when the force of the genitive case is that of an agent.",
    "Sūtra 2.2.16: karttaricha (कर्तरि  च) — A word ending with a sixth case-affix is not compounded with a word ending with त्रिच् or अक affix when the force of these latter affixes is that of an agent.",
    "Sūtra 2.2.17: nityamkreedaajeevikayoh (नित्यं क्रीडाजीविकयोः) — A word ending with a sixth case-affix is invariably compounded with a word ending with अक , when these affixes denote a sport or livelihood; and the compound is तत्-पुरुष।",
    "Sūtra 2.2.18: kugatipraadayah (कुगतिप्रादयः) — The indeclinable word कु 'bad' , the particles called गति and the prepositions प्र etc. are invariably compounded with other words with which they are in construction and the resulting compound is तत्-पुरुष।",
    "Sūtra 2.2.19: upapadamating (उपपदमतिङ्) — An उपपद of attendant word तत्रोपपदं सप्तमीस्थम् [[3.1.92]] which does not end with a tense-affix [[3.4.78]] is invariably compounded with that with which it is in construction. The compound thus formed is तत्-पुरुष।",
    "Sūtra 2.2.20: amaivaavyayena (अमैवाव्ययेन) — When an उपपद is compounded with an indeclinable, then it is compounded only with those अव्ययs which end in the affix अम्।",
    "Sūtra 2.2.21: truteeyaaprabhruteenyanyatarasyaam (तृतीयाप्रभृतीन्यन्यतरस्याम्) — An उपपद ending in third case-affix [[3.4.47]] etc. is compounded optionally with an indeclinable formed by the affix अम् and the compound is तत्-पुरुष।",
    "Sūtra 2.2.22: ktvaacha (क्त्वा च) — An उपपद ending in third case-affix or any other of the remaining four cases, is optionally compounded with a word ending with the affix क्तवा and the compound is तत्-पुरुष।",
    "Sūtra 2.2.23: sheshobahuvreehih (शेषो बहुव्रीहिः) — The remaining compound is called बहुव्रीही।",
    "Sūtra 2.2.24: anekamanyapadaarthe (अनेकमन्यपदार्थे) — Two or more words, ending in any case-affix, form compound, denoting another new thing, not connoted by those words individually and the compound is called बहुव्रीही।",
    "Sūtra 2.2.25: samkhyayaavyayaasannaadooraadhikasamkhyaahasamkhyeye (संख्ययाऽव्ययासन्नादूराधिकसंख्याः संख्येये) — indeclinable words and the words आसन्न 'near', अदूर 'near', अधिक 'more' and the words called संख्या (Numerals) are compounded with another संख्या word, when the sense is that of a numeral or संख्या। The compound is बहुव्रीही।",
    "Sūtra 2.2.26: dingnaamaanyantaraale (दिङ्नामान्यन्तराले) — Words which are the names of the points of the compass are compounded, when the compound signifies the intermediate point and the compound so formed is बहुव्रीही।",
    "Sūtra 2.2.27: tatratenedamitisaroope (तत्र तेनेदमिति सरूपे) — Two homonymous words (both being in the locative case or both being in the instrumental case) are compounded, the sense being 'this happens therein or with that'. The compound so formed is बहुव्रीही।",
    "Sūtra 2.2.28: tenasahetitulyayoge (तेन सहेति तुल्ययोगे) — The word सह 'together' is compounded with a word ending with the third case-affix and the compound is बहुव्रीही ; provided that, the companion and the person accompanied are equally effected by any action or thing, in the same manner.",
    "Sūtra 2.2.29: chaarthedvamdvah (चार्थे द्वन्द्वः) — When a set of several words ending with case-affixes stands in a relation expressable by 'and' the set is made into a compound and the compound so formed is called द्वन्द्व।",
    "Sūtra 2.2.30: upasarjanampoorvam (उपसर्जनं पूर्वम्) — The उपसर्जन [[1.2.43]] is to be placed first in a compound.",
    "Sūtra 2.2.31: raajadantaadishuparam (राजदन्तादिषु परम्) — The उपसर्जन is to be put last in the words राजदन्त etc.",
    "Sūtra 2.2.32: dvamdveghi (द्वन्द्वे घि) — In a द्वन्द्व compound, let a word called घि [[1.4.7]], stand first.",
    "Sūtra 2.2.33: ajaadyadantam (अजाद्यदन्तम्) — In a द्वन्द्व compound, let a what begins with a vowel and ends with a short अ be placed first.",
    "Sūtra 2.2.34: alpaachtaram (अल्पाच्तरम्) — In a द्वन्द्व compound, that word-form which has fewer vowels, is to be placed first.",
    "Sūtra 2.2.35: saptameevisheshanebahuvreehau (सप्तमीविशेषणे बहुव्रीहौ) — A word with the seventh case-affix and an epithet are to be placed first in the बहुव्रीही compound.",
    "Sūtra 2.2.36: nishthaa (निष्ठा) — What ends with a निष्ठा [[1.1.26]] shall stand first in a बहुव्रीही compound.",
    "Sūtra 2.2.37: vaahitaagnyaadishu (वाहिताग्न्यादिषु) — In the compounds अहिताग्नि and the like, the निष्ठा-formed word may optionally be placed first.",
    "Sūtra 2.2.38: kadaaraahakarmadharaaye (कडाराः कर्मधारये) — The words कडाराः and the like, are optionally placed first in the कर्मधार्य।",
    "Sūtra 2.3.1: anabhihite (अनभिहिते) — The word अनभिहिते meaning 'not being specified' is to be understood as the governing word.",
    "Sūtra 2.3.2: karmanidviteeyaa (कर्मणि द्वितीया) — When the object is not denoted by the termination of the verb i.e. when the verb does not agree with it, the 2nd case-affix is attached to the word.",
    "Sūtra 2.3.3: truteeyaachahoshchhandasi (तृतीया च होश्छन्दसि) — In the छन्दस् (Veda), the object of the verb हु 'to sacrifice' takes the affix of the 3rd case and of the 2nd case as well.",
    "Sūtra 2.3.4: antaraantarenayukte (अन्तराऽन्तरेण युक्ते) — A word joined with (or governed by) the word अन्तरा or अन्तरेण takes the second case-affix.",
    "Sūtra 2.3.5: kaalaadhvanoratyantasamyoge (कालाध्वनोरत्यन्तसंयोगे) — After a word denoting time, or length, the affix of the 2nd case is used, when denoting a full duration.",
    "Sūtra 2.3.6: apavargetruteeyaa (अपवर्गे तृतीया) — The 3rd case-affix is used after the words denoting the duration of time or place, when the accomplishment of the desired object is meant to be expressed.",
    "Sūtra 2.3.7: saptameepanychamyaukaarakamadhye (सप्तमीपञ्चम्यौ कारकमध्ये) — A noun denoting time or place gets the affix of the 7th or the 5th case when the sense applied is that the time or space is the interval between one action and another (or implies an interval of time and space between कारक-s.",
    "Sūtra 2.3.8: karmapravachaneeyayuktedviteeyaa (कर्मप्रवचनीययुक्ते द्वितीया) — The 2nd case-affix is employed after a word which is joined with a कर्मप्रवचनीयाः [[1.4.83]].",
    "Sūtra 2.3.9: yasmaadadhikamyasyacheshvaravachanamtatrasaptamee (यस्मादधिकं यस्य चेश्वरवचनं तत्र सप्तमी) — Where a word is governed by a कर्मप्रवचनीयाः [[1.4.83]] in the sense of 'more than' उपोऽधिके च [[1.4.87]] or 'lord of' अधिरीश्वरे [[1.4.97]] there the 7th case-affix (locative) is used.",
    "Sūtra 2.3.10: panychameeapaangparibhih (पञ्चम्यपाङ्परिभिः) — The 5th case-affix (Ablative) is used when a word is governed by the following कर्मप्रवचनीयाः [[1.4.83]] i.e. अप , आङ् and परि।",
    "Sūtra 2.3.11: pratinidhipratidaanechayasmaat (प्रतिनिधिप्रतिदाने च यस्मात्) — The 5th case-affix (Ablative) is used after whatsoever is governed by a कर्मप्रवचनीयाः [[1.4.83]] in the sense of 'substitute' or 'exchange' -- प्रतिः प्रतिनिधिप्रतिदानयोः [[1.4.92]].",
    "Sūtra 2.3.12: gatyarthakarmanidviteeyaachaturthyaucheshtaayaamanadhvani (गत्यर्थकर्मणि द्वितीयाचतुर्थ्यौ चेष्टायामनध्वनि) — In the case of roots implying motion, the place which the motion is directed takes the affix of the 2nd (Accusative) or the 4th (Dative) case in denoting the 'object', when physical motion is meant and the object is not a word expressing 'road'.",
    "Sūtra 2.3.13: chaturtheesampradaane (चतुर्थी सम्प्रदाने) — In denoting the सम्प्रदान-कारक -- कर्मणा यमभिप्रैति स सम्प्रदानम् [[1.4.32]], the 4th case-affix of the Dative is used after the noun.",
    "Sūtra 2.3.14: kriyaarthopapadasyachakarmanisthaaninah (क्रियार्थोपपदस्य च कर्मणि स्थानिनः) — The 4th case-affix is employed in denoting the object (कर्म) of that verb, which is suppressed (स्थानी) in a sentence and which has in construction (उपपद) there-with another verb, denoting an action, performed for the sake of the future action -- तुमुन्ण्वुलौ क्रियायां क्रियार्थायाम्[[3.3.10]]. In other words, when the sense of an infinitive of purpose formed by तुमुन् and ण्वुल् -- [[3.3.10]], is suppressed in a sentence, the object of this infinitive is put in the Dative -- 4th case.",
    "Sūtra 2.3.15: tumarthaachchabhaavavachanaat (तुमर्थाच्च भाववचनात्) — The 4th case-affix is used after a crude-form which ends in an affix denoting 'condition' (abstract noun -- भाववचनाश्च [[3.3.11]]) and having the force of the affix तुम् (or Infinitive or purpose).",
    "Sūtra 2.3.16: namahasvastisvaahaasvadhaalamvashadyogaachcha (नमःस्वस्तिस्वाहास्वधालम्वषड्योगाच्च) — The 4th case-affix is used in conjunction with the words नमः 'salutation', स्वस्ति 'peace', स्वाहा , स्वधा (terms used in offering oblations to Gods and पित्रि-s, respectively), अलम् , 'a match for', 'sufficient for' and वषट् , a term for oblation.",
    "Sūtra 2.3.17: manyakarmanyanaadarevibhaashaapraanishu (मन्यकर्मण्यनादरे विभाषाऽप्राणिषु) — In denoting the indirect object, which is not an animal, of the verb मन्य 'to think', the Dative -- 4th case is optionally used, when contempt is to be shown.",
    "Sūtra 2.3.18: kartrukaranayostruteeyaa (कर्तृकरणयोस्तृतीया) — In denoting the agent -- स्वतन्त्रः कर्ता [[1.4.54]], or the instrument -- साधकतमं करणम् [[1.4.42]], the 3rd case is used.",
    "Sūtra 2.3.19: sahayuktepradhaane (सहयुक्तेऽप्रधाने) — When the word सह 'with', is joined to a word the latter takes the 3rd case, when the sense is that the word in the 3rd case is not the principal but the accompaniment of the principal thing.",
    "Sūtra 2.3.20: yenaanggavikaarah (येनाङ्गविकारः) — By whatsoever limb, being defective, is pointed out the defect of the person after that the 3rd case-affix is used.",
    "Sūtra 2.3.21: itthambhootalakshane (इत्थंभूतलक्षणे) — Any mark or attribute, by which is indicated the existence of a particular state or condition, is put in the 3rd case to express this relation.",
    "Sūtra 2.3.22: samjnyonyatarasyaamkarmani (संज्ञोऽन्यतरस्यां कर्मणि) — After the verb सम्-ज्ञः , the 3rd case-affix is optionally used in denoting the object.",
    "Sūtra 2.3.23: hetau (हेतौ) — When the word denotes 'cause' it takes the 3rd case-affix.",
    "Sūtra 2.3.24: akartaryrunepanychamee (अकर्तर्यृणे पञ्चमी) — A word implying 'debt', considered as a 'cause' but not as कर्तृ or agent, takes the 5th case-affix.",
    "Sūtra 2.3.25: vibhaashaagunestriyaam (विभाषा गुणेऽस्त्रियाम्) — The 5th case-affix is used optionally when the noun expresses an attribute, being the cause of an action and not being of the feminine gender.",
    "Sūtra 2.3.26: shashtheehetuprayoge (षष्ठी हेतुप्रयोगे) — The 6th-Case-affix is used after a noun implying the cause of an action, when the word हेतु is used along with such a word.",
    "Sūtra 2.3.27: sarvanaamnastruteeyaacha (सर्वनाम्नस्तृतीया च) — After a सर्वनामस्थान -- सर्वादीनि सर्वनामानि [[1.1.27]], when it signifies the cause of an action and the word हेतु is used with it, the 3rd case-affix is used, as well as the 6th.",
    "Sūtra 2.3.28: apaadaanepanychamee (अपादाने पञ्चमी) — When the अपादान कारक -- ध्रुवमपायेऽपादानम् [[1.4.24]], is denoted, the 5th case-affix is used.",
    "Sūtra 2.3.29: anyaaraaditararttedikshabdaanychoottarapadaajaahiyukte (अन्यारादितरर्तेदिक्छब्दाञ्चूत्तरपदाजाहियुक्ते) — When a noun is joined with words meaning 'other than' or with आरात् 'near or remote', or इतर 'different from' or ऋते 'without', or words indicative of 'directions' (used also with reference to the time corresponding to them) or with words having अञ्चु 'to bend' as the last member of the compound and expressive of direction, or with words ending with the affix आच् -- दक्षिणादाच् [[5.3.36]] or आहि -- आहि च दूरे [[5.3.37]], the 5th case-affix is used.",
    "Sūtra 2.3.30: shashthyatasarthapratyayena (षष्ठ्यतसर्थप्रत्ययेन) — The 6th-Case-affix is used when used in connection with words ending with affixes having the sense of the affix अतसुच -- दक्षिणोत्तराभ्यामतसुच् [[5.3.28]].",
    "Sūtra 2.3.31: enapaadviteeyaa (एनपा द्वितीया) — With a word ending with the affix एनाप् -- एनबन्यतरस्यामदूरेऽपञ्चम्याः [[5.3.35]], the 2nd case-affix is used, as well as the 6th.",
    "Sūtra 2.3.32: pruthagvinaanaanaabhistruteeyaanyatarasyaam (पृथग्विनानानाभिस्तृतीयाऽन्यतरस्याम्) — When joined with the words पृथक् 'without', विना 'without' and नाना 'without', the 3rd case-affix is used, optionally (as well as the 5th and the 2nd).",
    "Sūtra 2.3.33: karanechastokaalpakruchchhrakatipayasyaasattvavachanasya (करणे च स्तोकाल्पकृच्छ्रकतिपयस्यासत्त्ववचनस्य) — When expressing an instrument-कारक, optionally after the words स्तोक 'little', अल्प 'little', कृच्छ्र 'difficulty' and कतिपय 'some', the 5th case-affix is used, when they do not denote material objects.",
    "Sūtra 2.3.34: dooraantikaarthaihashashthyanyatarasyaam (दूरान्तिकार्थैः षष्ठ्यन्यतरस्याम्) — When in conjunction with words having the sense of दूर 'distant' and अन्तिक 'near', the 6th-Case-affix is optionally used.",
    "Sūtra 2.3.35: dooraantikaarthebhyodviteeyaacha (दूरान्तिकार्थेभ्यो द्वितीया च) — After the words दूर 'distant' and अन्तिक 'near', the 2nd case-affix is used as well as the 5th and the 3rd.",
    "Sūtra 2.3.36: saptamyadhikaranecha (सप्तम्यधिकरणे च) — The 7th case-affix is used when the sense is that of location -- आधारोऽधिकरणम् [[1.4.45]], as well as after the words meaning 'distant' and 'near'.",
    "Sūtra 2.3.37: yasyachabhaavenabhaavalakshanam (यस्य च भावेन भावलक्षणम्) — By the action (भाव) of whatsoever, the time of another action is indicated, that takes the 7th case-affix.",
    "Sūtra 2.3.38: shashtheechaanaadare (षष्ठी चानादरे) — The 6th-Case-affix is used (as well as the 7th), when disregard is to be shown after that by whose action the time of another action is indicated.",
    "Sūtra 2.3.39: svaameeshvaraadhipatidaayaadasaakshipratibhooprasootaishcha (स्वामीश्वराधिपतिदायादसाक्षिप्रतिभूप्रसूतैश्च) — The 6th and the 7th case-affixes are used after words when they are joined with स्वामिन् 'master', ईश्वर 'lord', अधिपति 'ruler', दायाद 'an heir', साक्षिन् 'witness', प्रतिभू 'a surety' and प्रसूत 'begotten'.",
    "Sūtra 2.3.40: aayuktakushalaabhyaamchaasevaayaam (आयुक्तकुशलाभ्यां चासेवायाम्) — In conjunction with the words आयुक्त 'engaged', and कुशल 'skilful', when meaning entire absorption in an engagement, the 6th and the 7th case-affixes are used after a word.",
    "Sūtra 2.3.41: yatashchanirdhaaranam (यतश्च निर्धारणम्) — The 6th and the 7th case-affixes are used after those words from which specification is made, (as of an individual from the whole class).",
    "Sūtra 2.3.42: panychameevibhakte (पञ्चमी विभक्ते) — The 5th case-affix is used when the thing specified is different or divided from (and not included in) that from which specification is intended.",
    "Sūtra 2.3.43: saadhunipunaabhyaamarchaayaamsaptamyaprateh (साधुनिपुणाभ्यामर्चायां सप्तम्यप्रतेः) — In conjunction with the words साधु 'good' and निपुण 'skilful' when they denote respect, the 7th case-affix is used, provided that the word प्रति is not used.",
    "Sūtra 2.3.44: prasitotsukaabhyaamtruteeyaacha (प्रसितोत्सुकाभ्यां तृतीया च) — In conjunction with the words प्रसिक्त and उत्सुक 'greatly desirous of', the 3rd case-affix is used after the word, as well as the 7th.",
    "Sūtra 2.3.45: nakshatrechalupi (नक्षत्रे च लुपि) — When an affix declaring the time of an Asterism is elided by लुप् -- लुबविशेषे [[4.2.4]], the 7th and the 3rd case-affixes are used after the word, whose affix is also elided.",
    "Sūtra 2.3.46: praatipadikaarthalinggaparimaanavachanamaatreprathamaa (प्रातिपदिकार्थलिङ्गपरिमाणवचनमात्रे प्रथमा) — Where the sense is that of the Nominal-stem -- अर्थवदधातुरप्रत्ययः प्रातिपदिकम् [[1.2.45]], or of gender only, or measure only or number only, the 1st case-affix is used.",
    "Sūtra 2.3.47: sambodhanecha (सम्बोधने च) — And when the sense is that of addressing, the 1st case-affix is used.",
    "Sūtra 2.3.48: saamantritam (सामन्त्रितम्) — The word ending with the 1st case-affix, in the sense of addressing, is called आमन्त्रित or Vocative.",
    "Sūtra 2.3.49: ekavachanamsambuddhih (एकवचनं संबुद्धिः) — In the case of Vocative, the singular number of the 1st case-affix is called स्मबुद्धि।",
    "Sūtra 2.3.50: shashtheesheshe (षष्ठी शेषे) — The 6th-Case-affix is used in the remaining cases, that is to say, where there is a sense, such as the relation between property and its owner etc. different from that of a word related to a verb and from that of a Nominal-stem.",
    "Sūtra 2.3.51: jnyovidarthasyakarane (ज्ञोऽविदर्थस्य करणे) — Of the verb ज्ञा , when not used in the sense 'to know', the instrument takes the 6th-Case-affix.",
    "Sūtra 2.3.52: adheegarthadayeshaamkarmani (अधीगर्थदयेशां कर्मणि) — Of the verbs having the sense of 'remembering', (अधिक्), and of दय 'to give', 'to pity', 'to protect', 'to move' and of ईश 'to rule or be master of', the object takes the 6th-Case-affix.",
    "Sūtra 2.3.53: krunyahapratiyatne (कृञः प्रतियत्ने) — The object of the verb कृ takes the 6th-Case-affix, when it means 'to impart a new quality or virtue' -- गन्धनावक्षेपणसेवनसाहसिक्यप्रतियत्नप्रकथनोपयोगेषु कृञः [[1.3.32]].",
    "Sūtra 2.3.54: rujaarthaanaambhaavavachanaanaamajvareh (रुजार्थानां भाववचनानामज्वरेः) — The object of verbs having the sense of रुज् 'to afflict', with the exception of the Causative verb ज्वरय 'to be feverish', takes the 6th-Case-affix, when the verb expresses a condition (i.e. when the subject is an Abstract noun).",
    "Sūtra 2.3.55: aashishinaathah (आशिषि नाथः) — Of the verb नाथ् when meaning 'to bless', the object takes the 6th-Case-affix.",
    "Sūtra 2.3.56: jaasiniprahananaatakraathapishaamhimsaayaam (जासिनिप्रहणनाटक्राथपिषां हिंसायाम्) — The object of the verbs जासि 'to strike', 'to hurt', हन् 'to strike' preceded by नि and ग्र , नाट् 'to injure', क्राथ and पिष when they mean 'to injure', takes the 6th-Case-affix.",
    "Sūtra 2.3.57: vyavahrupanohasamarthayoh (व्यवहृपणोः समर्थयोः) — The object of the verbs व्यवहृ and पण् when they ae synonymous, that is when they mean 'dealing in sale and purchase transactions' or 'staking in gambling' takes the 6th-Case-affix.",
    "Sūtra 2.3.58: divastadarthasya (दिवस्तदर्थस्य) — The object of the verb दिव् when having the above-mentioned sense of 'dealing' or 'stalking', takes the 6th-Case.",
    "Sūtra 2.3.59: vibhaashopasarge (विभाषोपसर्गे) — The object of the verb दिव् when having the above-mentioned sense of 'dealing' or 'stalking', optionally takes the 6th-Case, when preceded by an उपसर्ग (preposition).",
    "Sūtra 2.3.60: dviteeyaabraahmane (द्वितीया ब्राह्मणे) — The object of the verb दिव् when having the above-mentioned sense of 'dealing' or 'stalking', takes the 2nd case, in the ब्राह्मण literature.",
    "Sūtra 2.3.61: preshyabruvorhavishodevataasampradaane (प्रेष्यब्रुवोर्हविषो देवतासम्प्रदाने) — The object of the verb प्रेष्य and ब्रूहि (imperative singular of दिवादि verb, meaning 'send' and 'utter') denoting sacrificial food, takes the 6th-Case-affix, when making offerings to deity is meant or when deity is the recipient.",
    "Sūtra 2.3.62: chaturthyarthebahulamchhandasi (चतुर्थ्यर्थे बहुलं छन्दसि) — In the छन्दस् the 6th-Case-affix is used diversely with the force of the 4th case-affix.",
    "Sūtra 2.3.63: yajeshchakarane (यजेश्च करणे) — The 6th-Case-affix is diversely used in the छन्दस् in denoting the instrument of the verb यज् 'to sacrifice'.",
    "Sūtra 2.3.64: krutvorthaprayogekaaledhikarane (कृत्वोऽर्थप्रयोगे कालेऽधिकरणे) — The 6th-Case-affix is used in denoting location (अधिकरण) after a word denoting time (काल) when used along with a word ending with an affix having the sense of कृत्वसुच् -- संख्यायाः क्रियाऽभ्यावृत्तिगणने कृत्वसुच् [[5.4.17]] 'so many times'.",
    "Sūtra 2.3.65: kartrukarmanohakruti (कर्तृकर्मणोः कृति) — The 6th-Case-affix is used after a word, in denoting the agent and the object, when used along with a word ending with a कृत्-affix --कृदतिङ् [[3.1.93]].",
    "Sūtra 2.3.66: ubhayapraaptaukarmani (उभयप्राप्तौ कर्मणि) — When the agent and the object of the action denoted by the words formed by कृत्-affixes, are both used in a sentence, in the object only, the 6th-Case-affix is employed and not in the agent (the object is put in the Genitive 6th-Case and not the Agent).",
    "Sūtra 2.3.67: ktasyachavartamaane (क्तस्य च वर्तमाने) — The past participle ending in क्त when used in the sense of the present tense, -- ञीतः क्तः [[3.2.187]] and -- मतिबुद्धिपूजार्थेभ्यश्च [[3.2.188]] , is used with the Genitive 6th-Case.",
    "Sūtra 2.3.68: adhikaranavaachinashcha (अधिकरणवाचिनश्च) — The past participle ending in क्त is used with the Genitive 6th-Case, when the former expresses location -- क्तोऽधिकरणे च ध्रौव्यगतिप्रत्यवसानार्थेभ्यः [[3.4.76]].",
    "Sūtra 2.3.69: nalokaavyayanishthaakhalarthatrunaam (न लोकाव्ययनिष्ठाखलर्थतृनाम्) — The 6th-Case-affix is not used the express the agent or the object, when the word is governed by an Active Participle ending in the affix ल , or उ , or उक or an indeclinable, or by a Past Participle in the क्त and क्तवतु or by a word ending in an affix having the sense of खल् or by a Noun of agency formed by तृन्।",
    "Sūtra 2.3.70: akenorbhavishyadaadhamarnyayoh (अकेनोर्भविष्यदाधमर्ण्ययोः) — The 6th-Case-affix is not used when the word is governed by a verbal noun in अक denoting futurity, or in a इन् denoting 'futurity and indebtedness'.",
    "Sūtra 2.3.71: krutyaanaamkartarivaa (कृत्यानां कर्तरि वा) — The 6th-Case-affix is optionally used in denoting the agent, (but not the object), when the word is governed by a Future Passive Participle (कृत्य).",
    "Sūtra 2.3.72: tulyaarthairatulopamaabhyaamtruteeyaanyatarasyaam (तुल्यार्थैरतुलोपमाभ्यां तृतीयाऽन्यतरस्याम्) — The 3rd or the 6th-Case-affix may optionally be employed, when the word is joined with another word meaning 'like to or resemblance', excepting तुला and उपना।",
    "Sūtra 2.3.73: chaturtheechaashishyaayushyamadrabhadrakushalasukhaarthahitaih (चतुर्थी चाशिष्यायुष्यमद्रभद्रकुशलसुखार्थहितैः) — The 4th as well as the 6th-Case-affix may be used, when blessing is intended in connection with the words आयुष 'long life', मद्र 'joy', भद्र 'good fortune', कुशल 'welfare', सुख 'happiness', अर्थ 'prosperity' and हित 'good'.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.1: dvigurekavachanam (द्विगुरेकवचनम्) —  All affixes after the verb गाङ् 'to study' and the verb कुट् 'to be crooked' and the rest, are as if they had an indicatory ङ् (ङित्), except those affixes which have an indicatory ञ् (ञित्) or ण् (णित्).",
    "Sūtra 2.4.2: dvamdvashchapraanitooryasenaanggaanaam (द्वन्द्वश्च प्राणितूर्यसेनाङ्गानाम्) —  An affix which begins with the augment इट् -- आर्धधातुकस्येड् वलादेः [[7.2.35]], is ङित् after the root विज् 'to fear, to move'.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.3: anuvaadecharanaanaam (अनुवादे चरणानाम्) — A द्वन्द compound or words signifying persons belonging to the different Vedic-schools, when the sense is that of repetition is singular.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.4: adhvaryukraturanapumsakam (अध्वर्युक्रतुरनपुंसकम्) — A द्वन्द compound of words denoting क्रतु (sacrifices) ordained by यजुर् (अध्वर्यु) Veda, is singular, provided they are never used in the neuter gender",
    "Sūtra 2.4.5: adhyayanatoviprakrushtaakhyaanaam (अध्ययनतोऽविप्रकृष्टाख्यानाम्) — A द्वन्द compound of words denoting (persons who have studied) subjects, which in their order of study are not remote from each other, is singular.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.6: jaatirapraaninaam (जातिरप्राणिनाम्) — A द्वन्द compound of words signifying जाति (genus) which are not the names of living beings, is singular.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.7: vishishtalinggonadeedeshograamaah (विशिष्टलिङ्गो नदी देशोऽग्रामाः) — A द्वन्द compound of words of different genders, denoting names of rivers and countries, but not of towns, is singular.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.8: kshudrajantavah (क्षुद्रजन्तवः) — A द्वन्द compound of words signifying small animals, is singular.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.9: yeshaamchavirodhahashaashvatikah (येषां च विरोधः शाश्वतिकः) — A द्वन्द compound of words signifying those animals only among whom there is permanent enmity i.e. natural and eternal antipathy or quarrel, is singular.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.10: shoodraanaamaniravasitaanaam (शूद्राणामनिरवसितानाम्) — A द्वन्द compound of words denoting those classes of शुद्रा-s who have not been expelled from the communion of higher classes, is singular.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.11: gavaashvaprabhruteenicha (गवाश्वप्रभृतीनि च) — The word गवाश and others are also द्वन्द compounds which take the singular number.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.12: vibhaashaavrukshamrugatrunadhaanyavyanyjanapashushakunyashvavadavapoorvaaparaadharottaraanaam (विभाषा वृक्षमृगतृणधान्यव्यञ्जनपशुशकुन्यश्ववडवपूर्वापराधरोत्तराणाम्) — A द्वन्द compound of words being the names of trees, wild animals, grass, corn, condiment, domestic beasts and birds and the compounds अश्व-वडव , पूर्व-पर and अधरोत्तर , are optionally singular.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.13: vipratishiddhamchaanadhikaranavaachi (विप्रतिषिद्धं चानधिकरणवाचि) — A द्वन्द compound of words of contrary significations, but not being the names of concrete substances.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.14: nadadhipayaadeeni (न दधिपयआदीनि) — The द्वन्द compounds like दधिपय etc. are not singular.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.15: adhikaranaitaavattvecha (अधिकरणैतावत्त्वे च) — A द्वन्द compound denoting a fixed number (एकत्व) of concrete things (अधिकरण) is not singular.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.16: vibhaashaasameepe (विभाषा समीपे) — A द्वन्द compound denoting an approximate number of concrete substances, is optionally singular.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.17: sanapumsakam (स नपुंसकम्) — It, namely the द्विगु or द्वन्द compound, with regard to which singular number has been ordained by the above rules, is always neuter gender.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.18: avyayeebhaavashcha (अव्ययीभावश्च) — An अव्ययीभाव -- अव्ययं विभक्तिसमीपसमृद्धिव्यृद्ध्यर्थाभावात्ययासम्प्रतिशब्दप्रादुर्भावपश्चाद्यथाऽऽनुपूर्व्ययौगपद्यसादृश्यसम्पत्तिसाकल्यान्तवचनेषु [[2.1.6]], compound is also neuter gender. ",
    "Sūtra 2.4.19: tatpurushonanykarmadhaarayah (तत्पुरुषोऽनञ् कर्मधारयः) — A तत्-पुरुष compound, with the exception of that which is formed by the particle नञ् , and or the कर्मधारय compound, becomes neuter gender, in the cases explained in the following sūtras.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.20: samjnyaayaamkanthosheenareshu (संज्ञायां कन्थोशीनरेषु) — When denoting an appellative, a तत्-पुरुष compound ending with the word कन्था 'town', is neuter in gender, provided that it is the name of a town situated in a country of the उशीनर-s.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.21: upajnyopakramamtadaadyaachikhyaasaayaam (उपज्ञोपक्रमं तदाद्याचिख्यासायाम्) — A तत्-पुरुष compound ending with the words उपज्ञा 'invention' and उपक्रम 'commencement' is neuter in gender, when it is intended to express the starting point of a work which is first invented or commenced.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.22: chhaayaabaahulye (छाया बाहुल्ये) — A तत्-पुरुष compound ending with the word छाया 'shadow' in neuter in gender when the sense is that of profuseness of the thing indicated by the first term.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.23: sabhaaraajaamanushyapoorvaa (सभा राजामनुष्यपूर्वा) — A तत्-पुरुष compound ending with the word सभा 'court' is neuter, provided that it is preceded by (a word synonymous with) the word राजा or by a word denoting a non-human-being. ",
    "Sūtra 2.4.24: ashaalaacha (अशाला च) — A तत्-पुरुष compound ending with the word सभा 'court', when it does not mean a house but means concourse, is neuter.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.25: vibhaashaasenaasuraachhaayaashaalaanishaanaam (विभाषा सेनासुराच्छायाशालानिशानाम्) — A तत्-पुरुष compound ending with the words सेना 'army', सुरा 'wine', छाया 'shadow', शाला 'house' and निशा 'night', is optionally neuter, with the exception of that which is formed by the particle नञ् -- नञ् [[2.2.6]], and the कर्मधारय compound.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.26: paravallinggamdvandvatatpurushayoh (परवल्लिङ्गं द्वन्द्वतत्पुरुषयोः) — The gender of द्वन्द compound or तत्-पुरुष compound is like that of the last word in it.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.27: poorvavadashvavadavau (पूर्ववदश्ववडवौ) — The gender of the compound of the word अश्व 'horse' and वडव 'a mare', is like that of the first word in it.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.28: hemantashishiraavahoraatrechachchhandasi (हेमन्तशिशिरावहोरात्रे च च्छन्दसि) — Of the compounds हेमन्त-शिशिरौ and अहोरात्रे , the gender is like that of the first word, in the छन्दस् ।",
    "Sūtra 2.4.29: raatraahnaahaahapumsi (रात्राह्नाहाः पुंसि) — The द्वन्द and तत्-पुरुष compound ending with the words रात्र and अह्न are spoken of in masculine.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.30: apathamnapumsakam (अपथं नपुंसकम्) — The तत्-पुरुष word अपथम् 'a bad road', is neuter.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.31: ardharchaahapumsicha (अर्धर्चाः पुंसि च) — The words अर्धर्च etc. are spoken of in masculine and neuter.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.32: idamonvaadesheshanudaattastruteeyaadau (इदमोऽन्वादेशेऽशनुदात्तस्तृतीयादौ) — In the room of इदम् 'this', in the case of its re-employment in a subsequent member of the same sentence and referring to the same thing (अन्वादेश) there is the substitution of अश् which is अनुदात्त (gravely accented), when the Instrumental -3rd case-affix and the rest follow.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.33: etadastratasostratasauchaanudaattau (एतदस्त्रतसोस्त्रतसौ चानुदात्तौ) — In the room of एतद् in the case of re-employment there is the substitution of the gravely accented अश् when the affixes त्र -- सप्तम्यास्त्रल् [[5.3.10]] and तस् -- पञ्चम्यास्तसिल् [[5.3.7]] follow, and the affixes त्र and तद् are अनुदात्त (gravely accented) also.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.34: dviteeyaataussvenah (द्वितीयाटौस्स्वेनः) — When an affix of the Accusative -2nd case or टा - Instrumental -3rd case singular or ओश् Locative -7th-case dual follows, एन् which is अनुदात्त is the substitute of इदम् and its re-employment.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.35: aarddhadhaatuke (आर्धधातुके) — The clause 'when the affix is आर्धधातुक is understood in the following sūtras up to sūtra [[2.4.58]].",
    "Sūtra 2.4.36: adojagdhirlyaptikiti (अदो जग्धिर्ल्यप्ति किति) — The word जग्धि is the substitute of अद् 'to eat', when the affix ल्यप् -- समासेऽनञ्पूर्वे क्त्वो ल्यप् [[7.1.37]] or an आर्धधातुक कित् affix beginning with a त follows.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.37: lungsanorghasa (लुङ्सनोर्घसॢ) — When लुङ् (Aorist) or सन् (Desiderative) follows घसॢ is the substitute of अद् 'to eat'.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.38: ghanyaposhcha (घञपोश्च) — And when the affix घञ् and अप् follow घसॢ is the substitute of अद्।",
    "Sūtra 2.4.39: bahulamchhandasi (बहुलं छन्दसि) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas), घसॢ is diversely substituted for अद्।",
    "Sūtra 2.4.40: lityanyatarasyaam (लिट्यन्यतरस्याम्) — When लिट् (Perfect Tense) follows घसॢ is optionally the substitute of अद्।",
    "Sūtra 2.4.41: venyovayih (वेञो वयिः) — When लिट् (Perfect Tense) follows, वयि is optionally the substitute follows of वेञ् 'to weave'.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.42: hanovadhalingi (हनो वध लिङि) — बध् is the substitute of हन् 'to kill' when the आर्धधातुक लिङ् (Benedictive) follows.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.43: lungicha (लुङि च) — And when लुङ् (Aorist) follows वध is the substitute of हन्।",
    "Sūtra 2.4.44: aatmanepadeshvanyatarasyaam (आत्मनेपदेष्वन्यतरस्याम्) — When आत्मनेपद affixes follow, वध् is optionally the substitute of हन् in the लुङ् (Aorist).",
    "Sūtra 2.4.45: inogaalungi (इणो गा लुङि) — गा is the substitute of the root इण् when लुङ् (Aorist) follows.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.46: naugamirabodhane (णौ गमिरबोधने) — When the affix णि (causal follows, गामि is the substitute of इण् when the sense is not that of 'informing' but that of 'going'.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.47: sanicha (सनि च) — And when सन् (Desiderative) follows, गमि is the substitute of ण् when the sense is not that of 'informing'.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.48: ingashcha (इङश्च) — And of इङ् 'to study', गमि is the substitute when सन् follows.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.49: gaangliti (गाङ् लिटि) — गाम् is the substitute of इङ् when लिट् (Perfect Tense) follows.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.50: vibhaashaalunglrungoh (विभाषा लुङ्लृङोः) — गाङ् is optionally the substitute of इङ् when लुङ् (Aorist) and ऌङ् (Conditional Future) follow.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.51: nauchasanshchangoh (णौ च संश्चङोः) — गाङ् is optionally the substitute of इङ् is the causative णि , when that causative takes the affix सन् (Desiderative) and चन् (Aorist).",
    "Sūtra 2.4.52: asterbhooh (अस्तेर्भूः) — भू is the substitute of the verb अस् 'to be' when an आर्धधातुक affix is to be applied.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.53: bruvovachih (ब्रुवो वचिः) — वचि is the substitute of ब्रू 'to speak' when any आर्धधातुक affix is to be supplied.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.54: chakshingahakhyaany (चक्षिङः ख्याञ्) — ख्याञ् is the substitute of चक्षिङ् 'to perceive, to tell', when any आर्धधातुक affix is to be applied.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.55: vaaliti (वा लिटि) — ख्याञ् is optionally the substitute of चक्षिङ् when लिट् (Perfect Tense) follows.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.56: ajervyaghanyapoh (अजेर्व्यघञपोः) — वी is the substitute of the verb अज् 'to drive', 'to lead', when an आर्धधातुक affix follows, with the exception of the affixes घञ् -- भावे [[3.3.18]] and अप् -- समुदोरजः पशुषु [[3.3.69]].",
    "Sūtra 2.4.57: vaayau (वा यौ) — वी is optionally the substitute of अज् when the affix -- अनद्यतने लुट् [[3.3.15]] etc. follows.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.58: nyakshatriyaarshanyitoyooniluganinyoh (ण्यक्षत्रियार्षञितो यूनि लुगणिञोः) — After a word ending with the गोत्र affix ण्य -- कुर्वादिभ्यो ण्यः [[4.1.151]] and after a गोत्र word denoting the descendant of a क्षत्रिय or a ऋषि 'seer' and after a word ending with a गोत्र affix having an indicatory ञ् , the affix ञ् , the affix अण् and इञ् employed in the forming युवन् -- जीवति तु वंश्ये युवा [[4.1.163]], descendants, are elided by the substitution of लुक्।",
    "Sūtra 2.4.59: pailaadibhyashcha (पैलादिभ्यश्च) — And after the words पैल etc. there is the लुक् elision of the युवन् affix.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.60: inyahapraachaam (इञः प्राचाम्) — After a word ending in the गोत्र affix -- [[4.1.95]], there is elision of लुक् of the युवन् affix, when the गोत्र of the people called प्राच्य 'Eastern' is denoted.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.61: nataulvalibhyah (न तौल्वलिभ्यः) — After the words तौल्वलि and the rest, there is no लुक् elision of the युवन् affix.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.62: tadraajasyabahushutenaivaastriyaam (तद्राजस्य बहुषु तेनैवास्त्रियाम्) — There is लुक् elision of तद्राज -- ते तद्राजाः [[4.1.174]], affix, when the word is used in the plural number, provided that the plural number is taken by the base itself and not by its standing as a compound epithet dependent upon another word and provided that the base is not used in the feminine.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.63: yaskaadibhyogotre (यस्कादिभ्यो गोत्रे) — After the word यस्क etc. there is the लुक् elision of the गोत्र affix when the word of itself and not as part of a compound epithet dependent on another word, takes the plural; but not in the feminine.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.64: yanyanyoshcha (यञञोश्च) — And there is लुक् elision of the गोत्र affix यञ् -- गर्गादिभ्यो यञ् [[4.1.105]] and अञ् -- अनृष्यानन्तर्ये बिदादिभ्योऽञ् [[4.1.104]], when the word of itself and not as part of a compound epithet dependent on another, takes the plural, but not in the feminine.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.65: atribhrugukutsavasishthagotamaanggirobhyashcha (अत्रिभृगुकुत्सवसिष्ठगोतमाङ्गिरोभ्यश्च) — After the words अत्रि , भृगु , कुत्स , वशिष्ठ , गोतम , अङ्गिरस , there is elision of the गोत्र affix, when the word takes the plural, but not in the feminine.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.66: bahvachahinyahapraachyabharateshu (बह्वचः इञः प्राच्यभरतेषु) — And there is लुक् elision of the गोत्र affix इञ् -- गोत्राद्यून्यस्त्रियाम् [[4.1.95]] after a word containing many vowels (a poly-syllabic word) which denotes the गोत्र of the people called प्राच्य and भरत when the word takes the plural.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.67: nagopavanaadibhyah (न गोपवनादिभ्यः) — After the words गोपवन etc. there is not लुक् elision of the गोत्र affix, when the word takes the plural.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.68: tikakitavaadibhyodvamdve (तिककितवादिभ्यो द्वन्द्वे) — After the words तिक , कितब etc. when used as द्वन्द compound, there is the लुक् elision of the गोत्र affixes when the compound word takes the plural.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.69: upakaadibhyonyatarasyaamadvamdve (उपकादिभ्योऽन्यतरस्यामद्वन्द्वे) — After the words उपक etc. there is optionally लुक् elision of the गोत्र affix when the words take the plural whether they enter into द्वन्द compound or are used separately.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.70: aagastyakaundinyayoragastikundinach (आगस्त्यकौण्डिन्ययोरगस्तिकुण्डिनच्) — There is लुक् elision of the गोत्र affixes अण् and यञ् of the words अगस्त्य , and कौणडिन्य , when they take the plural and the words अगस्ति and कण्डिनच् are the substitutes of the bases so remaining after the elision.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.71: supodhaatupraatipadikayoh (सुपो धातुप्रातिपदिकयोः) — There is लुक् elision of the case-affix of a word when it gets the name of धातु 'root' or is of a crude form.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.72: adiprabhrutibhyahashapah (अदिप्रभृतिभ्यः शपः) — After the verb अद् 'to eat' and the rest there is लुक् elision of the विकरण शप् -- कर्तरि शप् [[3.1.68]].",
    "Sūtra 2.4.73: bahulamchhandasi (बहुलं छन्दसि) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas) there is diversely the लुक् elision of the विकरण शप् -- कर्तरि शप् [[3.1.68]].",
    "Sūtra 2.4.74: yangochicha (यङोऽचि च) — And there is diversely the लुक् elision of यङ् -- धातोरेकाचो हलादेः क्रियासमभिहारे यङ् [[3.1.22]], when the affix अच् -- नन्दिग्रहिपचादिभ्यो ल्युणिन्यचः [[3.1.134]], follows.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.75: juhotyaadibhyahashluh (जुहोत्यादिभ्यः श्लुः) — After the verbs हू 'to sacrifice' and others there is श्लु elision of the विकरण शप् -- कर्तरि शप् [[3.1.68]].",
    "Sūtra 2.4.76: bahulamchhandasi (बहुलं छन्दसि) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas) there is elision of the शप् diversely.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.77: gaatisthaaghupaabhoobhyahasichahaparasmaipadeshu (गातिस्थाघुपाभूभ्यः सिचः परस्मैपदेषु) — There is लुक् elision of the affix सिच् -- च्लेः सिच् [[3.1.44]] in the परस्मैपद after the verbs गा 'to go', स्था 'to stand', the verbs called घु मृषस्तितिक्षायाम् [[1.2.20]], पा 'to drink' and भू 'to be'.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.78: vibhaashaaghraadhetshaachchhaasah (विभाषा घ्राधेट्शाच्छासः) — After the verbs घ्रा 'to smell', धेट् 'to drink', शा (शो) 'to pare' छा (छो) 'to cut' and सा (सो) 'to destroy' there is optionally the elision of सिच् when the परस्मैपद terminations are used.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.79: tanaadibhyastathaasoh (तनादिभ्यस्तथासोः) — After the verbs तन् 'to expand' and others there is optionally the लुक् elision of सिच् when the आत्मनेपद affixes त and थास् of the 2nd Person follow.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.80: mantreghasahvaranashavrudahaadvruchkrugamijanibhyoleh (मन्त्रे घसह्वरणशवृदहाद्वृच्कृगमिजनिभ्यो लेः) — In the मन्त्र portion of the Vedas there is लुक् elision of the sign of the Aorist (& लिट् -Perfect Tense) after the verbs घस् 'to eat', हूर् 'to be crooked', णश् 'to destroy', वृ 'to choose, to cover', दह् 'to burn', verbs ending in long आ , वृच् 'to avoid', कृ 'to make', गमि 'to go' and जनि 'to be produced'.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.81: aamah (आमः) — There is लुक् elision in the room of that tense-affix (लि) which comes after आम् of the लिट् (Perfect Tense).",
    "Sūtra 2.4.82: avyayaadaapsupah (अव्ययादाप्सुपः) — There is लुक् elision of आप् (the feminine termination) and सुप् (the case-affixes) after an अव्यय or indeclinable.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.83: naavyayeebhaavaadatomtvapanychamyaah (नाव्ययीभावादतोऽम्त्वपञ्चम्याः) — There is not लुक् elision of the case-affix after an अव्ययीभाव compound that ends in आ ; आम् is the substitute of its case-affix es, but not when it is the 5th case-affix.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.84: truteeyaasaptamyorbahulam (तृतीयासप्तम्योर्बहुलम्) — The change to अम् of the Instrumental -3rd case and Locative -7th-case-affixes coming after an अव्ययीभाव compound that ends in अ , occurs diversely.",
    "Sūtra 2.4.85: lutahaprathamasyadaaraurasah (लुटः प्रथमस्य डारौरसः) — डा , रौ and रस् are substituted respectively in the room of the three-affixes of the 3rd Person of लुट् (First Future), both in the परस्मैपद and आत्मनेपद। ",
    "Sūtra 3.1.1: pratyayah (प्रत्ययः) — An affix.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.2: parashcha (परश्च) — And subsequent.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.3: aadyudaattashcha (आद्युदात्तश्च) — That which is called an affix has an acute accent on its first syllable.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.4: anudattausuppitau (अनुदात्तौ सुप्पितौ) — The case-affix es (सुप्) and the affixes having an indicatory प (पित्) are अनुदात्त।",
    "Sūtra 3.1.5: guptijkidbhyahasan (गुप्तिज्किद्भ्यः सन्) — After the verbs गुप् , तिज् and कित् comes the affix सन्।",
    "Sūtra 3.1.6: maanbadhadaanshaanbhyodeerghashchaabhyaasasya (मान्बधदान्शान्भ्यो दीर्घश्चाभ्यासस्य) — The affix सन् comes after the verbs मान 'to honour', बध् 'to bind', दान् 'to cut', and शान् 'to whet', and long ई is the substitute of इ -- सन्यतः [[7.4.79]] of the re-duplicate -- पूर्वोऽभ्यासः [[6.1.4]] syllable.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.7: dhaatohakarmanahasamaanakartrukaadichchhaayaamvaa (धातोः कर्मणः समानकर्तृकादिच्छायां वा) — The affix is optionally attached, in the sense of 'wishing' after a root expressing the object wished and having the same agent of the action as the wisher thereof.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.8: supaatmanahakyach (सुप आत्मनः क्यच्) — The affix क्यच् is optionally employed, in the sense of wishing after a word ending in a case-affix expressing the object wished as connected with the wisher itself.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.9: kaamyachcha (काम्यच्च) — And the affix काम्यच् is also used in the sense of 'wishing' after a word ending in a case-affix, expressing the object wished as connected with the wisher's self.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.10: upamaanaadaachaare (उपमानादाचारे) — The affix क्यच् is optionally employed, in the sense of treatment after a word ending in a case-affix denoting the object of comparison.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.11: kartuhakyangsalopashcha (कर्तुः क्यङ् सलोपश्च) — The affix क्यङ् is optionally used in the sense of 'behaving' after a word ending in a case-affix denoting the object of comparison of the agent and there is लोप (elision) of the final स of the noun if it ends in a स।",
    "Sūtra 3.1.12: bhrushaadibhyobhuvyachverlopashchahalah (भृशादिभ्यो भुव्यच्वेर्लोपश्च हलः) — The affix क्यङ् in the sense of becoming what the thing previously was not, is used after the crude forms भृश् etc. which do not end with the affix च्वि -- अभूततद्भावे कृभ्वस्तियोगे सम्पद्यकर्तरि च्विः [[5.4.50]], and there is लोप (elision) of the final consonant of these words, if they end in a consonant.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.13: lohitaadidaajbhyahakyash (लोहितादिडाज्भ्यः क्यष्) — The affix क्यष् in the sense of becoming what the thing previously was not, is used after the words लोहित etc. and after those that end with the affix डाच् -- अव्यक्तानुकरणाद्द्व्यजवरार्धादनितौ डाच् [[5.4.57]], when these words do not take the affix च्वि -- अव्यक्तानुकरणाद्द्व्यजवरार्धादनितौ डाच् [[5.4.57]].",
    "Sūtra 3.1.14: kashtaayakramane (कष्टाय क्रमणे) — The affix क्यङ् in the sense of exerting in the dishonesty, is employed after the word कष्ट 'mischief' when the latter has the 4th case-affix in construction.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.15: karmanaharomanthatapobhyaamvarticharoh (कर्मणो रोमन्थतपोभ्यां वर्तिचरोः) — The affix क्यङ् is used after the words रोमन्य 'ruminating' and तपस 'austerity', when they are used as the objects of the action of repeating and performing respectively.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.16: baashposhmaabhyaamudvamane (बाष्पोष्मभ्यामुद्वमने) — The affix क्यङ् is used in the sense of ejecting after the words वाष्प 'vapour' and ऊष्म 'heat' as the object of the action.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.17: shabdavairakalahaabhrakanvameghebhyahakarane (शब्दवैरकलहाभ्रकण्वमेघेभ्यः करणे) — The affix क्यङ् , in the sense of 'making', comes after these words, as the object of the action, viz. शब्द 'sound', वैर 'hostility', कलह 'strife', अभ्र 'cloud', कण्व 'sin' and मेध 'cloud'.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.18: sukhaadibhyahakartruvedanaayaam (सुखादिभ्यः कर्तृवेदनायाम्) — The affix क्यङ् in the sense of 'feeling', comes after the words सुख 'pleasure' etc. when the pleasure etc. belong to the agent as feels thereof.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.19: namovarivashchitrangahakyach (नमोवरिवश्चित्रङः क्यच्) — The affix in the sense of 'making', comes after these words, as the object of the action, viz. नमस् 'adoration', वरिवस् 'honour', चित्र 'wonder'.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.20: puchchhabhaandacheevaraanning (पुच्छभाण्डचीवराण्णिङ्) — The affix णिङ् , in the sense of making, comes after these words as the object of the action, viz. पुच्छ 'tail', भाण्ड 'pot' and चीवर 'rag'.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.21: mundamishrashlakshnalavanavratavastrahalakalakrutatoostebhyo nich (मुण्डमिश्रश्लक्ष्णलवणव्रतवस्त्रहलकलकृततूस्तेभ्यो णिच्) — The affix णिच् , in the sense of 'making' comes after these words as the object of action viz. मुण्ड 'shaving', मिश्र 'mixture', श्लक्ष्ण 'soft', लवण 'salt', व्रत 'vow', वस्त्र 'dress', हल 'plough', कल 'strife', कृत 'done' and तूस्त 'matter hair'.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.22: dhaatorekaachohalaadehakriyaasamabhihaareyang (धातोरेकाचो हलादेः क्रियासमभिहारे यङ्) — The affix वङ् , in the sense of repetition of the act, comes after a root, having a single vowel and beginning with a consonant.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.23: nityamkautilyegatau (नित्यं कौटिल्ये गतौ) — The affix वङ् invariably comes in the sense of 'crookedness' after a simple verb expressing motion.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.24: lupasadacharajapajabhadahadashagrubhyobhaavagarhaayaam (लुपसदचरजपजभदहदशगॄभ्यो भावगर्हायाम्) — The affix वङ् when it is intended to convey the sense of contempt (गर्हा) in respect of the sense of the root (भाव) comes always after the following roots - लुप् 'to cut off', सद् 'to sit', चर् 'to walk', जप् 'to mutter silently any sacred formula', जभ 'to gape or yawn', दह् 'to burn', दश् 'to bite' and गृ 'to swallow'.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.25: satyaapapaasharoopaveenaatoolashlokasenaalomatvachavarmavarnachoornachuraadibhyonich (सत्यापपाशरूपवीणातूलश्लोकसेनालोमत्वचवर्मवर्णचूर्णचुरादिभ्यो णिच्) — The affix णिच् is used after these words - सत्य 'truth' (which then takes the form of सत्याप as exhibited in the sūtra), पाश 'a fetter', रूप 'form', वीणा 'a lute', तूल 'cotton', श्लोक 'celebration', सेना 'army', लोम 'the hair of the body', त्वच 'skin', वर्म 'mail', वर्ण 'celebration', चूर्ण 'powder' and the verb of the चुरादि class.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.26: hetumaticha (हेतुमति च) — The affix णिच् is used after a root, when the operation of a causer is to be expressed.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.27: kandvaadibhyoyak (कण्ड्वादिभ्यो यक्) — The affix यक् is used after the roots कण्डु 'to itch' etc.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.28: gupoodhoopavichchhipanipanibhyaayah (गुपूधूपविच्छिपणिपनिभ्य आयः) — The affix आय comes after गुपू 'to protect', धूप 'to heat', विच्छ 'to approach', पण 'to contract or praise' and पन 'to praise'.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.29: rutereeyang (ऋतेरीयङ्) — The affix ईयङ् comes after the sūtra root ऋति 'to reproach'.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.30: kamerning (कमेर्णिङ्) — The affix णिङ् comes after the root कम 'to desire'.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.31: aayaadayaardhaddhaatukevaa (आयादय आर्धधातुके वा) — The affixes आय and those that follow it i.e. आय , ईयङ् and णिङ् are optionally added, when it is desired to express one's self with an आर्धधातुक affix.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.32: sanaadyantaadhaatavah (सनाद्यन्ता धातवः) — All the roots ending with the affixes सन् and others are called धातु ।",
    "Sūtra 3.1.33: syataaseelrulutoh (स्यतासी लृलुटोः) — When ऌ and लुट् follow, then स्य and तासि are respectively the affixes of a verbal root",
    "Sūtra 3.1.34: sibbahulamleti (सिब्बहुलं लेटि) — सिप् is diversely the affix of a verbal root when लेट् follows.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.35: kaaspratyayaadaamamantreliti (कास्प्रत्ययादाममन्त्रे लिटि) — आम् is the affix of the verb कास् 'to cough' and of those roots that are formed by affixes i.e. the derivative verbs, when लिट् (Perfect Tense) follows, in the मन्त्र।",
    "Sūtra 3.1.36: ijaadeshchagurumatonruchchhah (इजादेश्च गुरुमतोऽनृच्छः) — The affix आम् is used when लिट् (Perfect Tense) follows after a root beginning with a letter of इच् प्रत्यहार and having a heavy vowel, excepting the root ऋच्छ 'to go'.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.37: dayaayaasashcha (दयायासश्च) — After the words दय 'to give', 'to go' and 'to protect', अय 'to go' and आस 'to sit', there is the affix आम् when लिट् (Perfect Tense) follows.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.38: ushavidajaagrubhyonyatarasyaam (उषविदजागृभ्योऽन्यतरस्याम्) — The affix आम् is optionally used after these - उष् 'to burn', विद् 'to know' and जागृ 'to wake', when लिट् (Perfect Tense) follows.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.39: bheehreebhruhuvaamshluvachcha (भीह्रीभृहुवां श्लुवच्च) — आम् is optionally affixed when लिट् (Perfect Tense) follows after these verbs - भी 'to fear', ह्री 'to be ashamed', भृ 'to nourish', हु 'to sacrifice' and when आम् is affixed, the effect is as if there were श्लु elision and the roots belonged to ह्वादि class.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.40: krunychaanuprayujyateliti (कृञ् चानुप्रयुज्यते लिटि) — After a verb which ends with आम् , the verb कृ 'to do', is annexed when लिट् (Perfect Tense) follows.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.41: vidaangkurvantvityanyatarasyaam (विदाङ्कुर्वन्त्वित्यन्यतरस्याम्) — The form विदाङ्कुर्वन्तु is optionally employed as an irregular form.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.42: abhyutsaadayaamprajanayaamchikayaamramayaamakah paavayamkruyaadvidaamkranniti chandasi (अभ्युत्सादयांप्रजनयांचिकयांरमयामकः पावयांक्रियाद्विदामक्रन्निति च्छन्दसि) — The forms अभ्युत्सादयामकः प्रजनयामकः चिकयामकः रमयामकः पावयांक्रियाद् विदामक्रन् are irregularly formed in the छन्दस् (Vedas).",
    "Sūtra 3.1.43: chlilungi (च्लि लुङि) — When लुङ् (Aorist) follows, the affix च्लि is added to the verbal root.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.44: chlehasich (च्लेः सिच्) — Of च्लि , सिच् is the substitute.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.45: shaligupadhaadanitahaksah (शल इगुपधादनिटः क्सः) — After a verb that ends in a शल consonant and has an इक् vowel for its penultimate letter and does not take इट् -- एकाच उपदेशेऽनुदात्तात् [[7.2.10]], क्स is the substitute of च्लि।",
    "Sūtra 3.1.46: shlishaalinggane (श्लिष आलिङ्गने) — क्स is the substitute of च्लि after the verb श्लिष , when used in the sense of 'embracing'.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.47: nadrushah (न दृशः) — क्स is not the substitute of च्लि after the verb दृश् 'to see'.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.48: nishridrusrubhyahakartarichang (णिश्रिद्रुस्रुभ्यः कर्तरि चङ्) — After a root which ends in the णि -- पुच्छभाण्डचीवराण्णिङ् [[3.1.20]], -- मुण्डमिश्रश्लक्ष्णलवणव्रतवस्त्रहलकलकृततूस्तेभ्यो णिच् [[3.1.21]], -- च्लेः सिच् [[3.1.44]] etc. and after the verb श्रि 'to serve', द्रु 'to run', and स्रु 'to drop', चङ् is the substitute of च्लि , when लुङ् (Aorist) follows signifying an agent.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.49: vibhaashaadhetshvyoh (विभाषा धेट्श्व्योः) — After the roots धे 'to suck' and श्वि 'to grow', चङ् is optionally the substitute of च्लि , when लुङ् (Aorist) follows signifying an agent.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.50: gupeshchhandasi (गुपेश्छन्दसि) — After the verb गुप् 'to protect', चङ् is optionally the substitute of च्लि in the छन्दस् (Vedas).",
    "Sūtra 3.1.51: nonayatidhvanayatyelayatyardayatibhyah (नोनयतिध्वनयत्येलयत्यर्दयतिभ्यः) — After the causatives of the verbs ऊन 'to decrease', ध्वन 'to sound', इल् 'to send' and अर्द 'to go or to beg' चङ् is not the substitute of च्लि in the छन्दस् (Vedas).",
    "Sūtra 3.1.52: asyativaktikhyaatibhyahang (अस्यतिवक्तिख्यातिभ्योऽङ्) — After the verbs अस् 'to throw', वच् 'to speak' and ख्या 'to speak', अङ् is the substitute of च्लि , when लुङ् (Aorist) follows signifying an agent.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.53: lipisichihvashcha (लिपिसिचिह्वश्च) — After the verbs लिप् 'to paint', सिच् 'to sprinkle' and ह्वे 'to call', अङ् is the substitute of च्लि when लुङ् (Aorist) follows signifying the agent.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.54: aatmanepadeshvanyatarasyaam (आत्मनेपदेष्वन्यतरस्याम्) — After the verbs लिप् , सिच् and ह्वे अङ् is optionally the substitute of च्लि when the affixes of the आत्मनेपद follow.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.55: pushaadidyutaadyaditahaparasmaipadeshu (पुषादिद्युताद्यॢदितः परस्मैपदेषु) — अङ् is the substitute of च्लि after the verbs पुष् 'to nourish' and the rest; द्युत् 'to shine' and the rest; and the verbs having an indicatory ऌ , when the affixes of the परस्मैपद follow.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.56: sarttishaastyartibhyashcha (सर्त्तिशास्त्यर्तिभ्यश्च) — After the words सृ 'to go', शास् 'to order' and ऋ 'to go', अङ् is the substitute of च्लि in the परस्मैपद as well as the आत्मनेपद ।",
    "Sūtra 3.1.57: iritovaa (इरितो वा) — अङ् is optionally the substitute of च्लि after that root which has an indicatory इर् , when the परस्मैपद terminations are used.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.58: jrustambhumruchumluchugruchugluchuglunychushvibhyashcha (जॄस्तम्भुम्रुचुम्लुचुग्रुचुग्लुचुग्लुञ्चुश्विभ्यश्च) — And, optionally अङ् is the substitute of च्लि after the verbs जॄ 'to stiffen', स्रुच् & स्लुच् 'to go', मुच् & ग्लुच् 'to steal', ग्लुञ्च् 'to go' and श्वि 'to grow' when the terminations of the परस्मैपद are used.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.59: krumrudruruhibhyashchhandasi (कृमृदृरुहिभ्यश्छन्दसि) — After the words कृ 'to do', मृ 'to die', दॄ (9P) 'to tear' and रुह 'to rise', अङ् is the substitute of च्लि when used in छन्दस् (Vedas).",
    "Sūtra 3.1.60: chintepadah (चिण् ते पदः) — चिण् is the substitute of च्लि after the verb पद् 'to go' when the affix त follows.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.61: deepajanabudhapooritaayipyaayibhyonyatarasyaam (दीपजनबुधपूरितायिप्यायिभ्योऽन्यतरस्याम्) — चिण् is optionally the substitute of च्लि , when त - 3rd Person Singular of आत्मनेपद follows after the verbs दीप् 'to shine', जन् 'to be produced', बुध् 'to teach or know', पूर् 'to be full', ताय् 'to extend or protect' and प्याय 'to smell'.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.62: achahakarmakartari (अचः कर्मकर्तरि) — चिण् is optionally the substitute of च्लि , when त - 3rd Person Singular of आत्मनेपद follows after a root which ends with a vowel and when the object itself is spoken of as the agent.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.63: duhashcha (दुहश्च) — चिण् is optionally the substitute of च्लि after the verb दुह् 'to milk', when it is used reflexively and when त follows.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.64: narudhah (न रुधः) — चिण् is not the substitute of च्लि after the verb रुध् 'to obstruct' when used in the reflexive sense in the 3rd Person Singular of आत्मनेपद ।",
    "Sūtra 3.1.65: taponutaapecha (तपोऽनुतापे च) — चिण् is not the substitute of च्लि after the verb तप् 'to suffer' when used reflexively and when the sense of experiencing remorse.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.66: chinbhaavakarmanoh (चिण् भावकर्मणोः) — चिण् is the substitute of च्लि when त -3rd Person Singular आत्मनेपद follows, denoting the action (भाव) or the object कर्म्म।",
    "Sūtra 3.1.67: saarvadhaatukeyak (सार्वधातुके यक्) — The affix यक् comes after a root when a सार्वधातुक -- तिङ्शित्सार्वधातुकम् [[3.4.113]], follows, denoting the action or the object.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.68: kartarishap (कर्तरि शप्) — The affix शप् comes after a root when a सार्वधातुक follows, signifies the agent.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.69: divaadibhyahashyan (दिवादिभ्यः श्यन्) — The affix श्यन् comes after a root of the दिवादि class when a सार्वधातुक affix denoting the agent follows.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.70: vaabhraashabhlaashabhramukramuklamutrasitrutilashah (वा भ्राशभ्लाशभ्रमुक्रमुक्लमुत्रसित्रुटिलषः) — The affix श्यन् optionally used in the active voice after the verbs - भ्राश् 'to shine', भ्लाश् 'to shine', भ्रम् 'to whirl', क्रम् 'to walk', क्लम् 'to be sad', त्रस् 'to fear', त्रुट् 'to cut' and लष् 'to desire'.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.71: yasonupasargaat (यसोऽनुपसर्गात्) — The affix श्यन् is optionally used after the verb यस् 'to strive' when it is used without a preposition and when a सार्वधातुक affix denoting an agent, follows. ",
    "Sūtra 3.1.72: samyasashcha (संयसश्च) — The affix श्यन् is optionally used after the verb यस् 'to strive' when it is preceded by the preposition सम् and when a सार्वधातुक affix denoting an agent, follows. ",
    "Sūtra 3.1.73: svaadibhyahashnuh (स्वादिभ्यः श्नुः) — The affix श्नु comes after the roots of स्वादि class when a सार्वधातुक affix denoting an agent follows.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.74: shruvahashrucha (श्रुवः शृ च) — And शृ is the substitute of श्नु and there is the affix श्नु after it, when a सार्वधातुक affix denoting an agent follows.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.75: akshonyatarasyaam (अक्षोऽन्यतरस्याम्) — The affix श्यन् is optionally used after the root अक्ष् 'to pervade' when it is preceded by the preposition सम् and when a सार्वधातुक affix denoting an agent, follows. ",
    "Sūtra 3.1.76: tanookaranetakshah (तनूकरणे तक्षः) — The affix श्यन् is optionally used after the root अक्ष् 'to bore or hew' when it is preceded by the preposition सम् and when a सार्वधातुक affix denoting an agent, follows. ",
    "Sūtra 3.1.77: tudaadibhyahashah (तुदादिभ्यः शः) — The affix श is used after the roots of तुदादि class, in denoting the agent when a सार्वधातुक affix follows.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.78: rudhaadibhyahashnam (रुधादिभ्यः श्नम्) — The affix श्नम् comes after the roots of the रुधादिगणः (7th Conjugation), in denoting an agent when a सार्वधातुक affix follows.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.79: tanaadikrunybhyuh (तनादिकृञ्भ्य उः) — The affix उ comes after the roots of the तनादिगणः (8th Conjugation) and after the verb कृ 'to make', when a सार्वधातुक affix follows, signifying the agent.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.80: dhinvikrunvyoracha (धिन्विकृण्व्योर च) — The affix उ comes after the roots धिन्व 'to please' and कृणिव 'to hurt', when a सार्वधातुक affix denoting the agent follows and in these verbs अ is the final substitute of the final इ।",
    "Sūtra 3.1.81: kryaadibhyahashnaa (क्र्यादिभ्यः श्ना) — The affix श्ना comes after the roots of the क्र्यादिगणः (9th Conjugation) when a सार्वधातुक affix follows denoting the agent.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.82: stambhustumbhuskambhuskumbhuskunybhyahashnushcha (स्तन्भुस्तुन्भुस्कन्भुस्कुन्भुस्कुञ्भ्यः श्नुश्च) — And there is the affix श्ना after स्तम्भ , स्तुम्भ , स्कम्भ or स्कुम्भ 'to hinder', to be dull or insensible' 'to support' and स्कु 'to go by leaps', as well as the affix श्नु , when a सार्वधातुक affix follows, in denoting the agent. (Note: The first 4 धातु are not found in the धातुपाठ and are found in the sūtras, and hence called सौत्र धातु ।)",
    "Sūtra 3.1.83: halahashnahashaanajjhau (हलः श्नः शानज्झौ) — The affix शानच् is the substitute of श्ना after a root ending with a consonant, when हि follows.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.84: chhandasishaayajapi (छन्दसि शायजपि) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas), शायच् is also the substitute of श्ना after the roots ending in consonants, when हि follows.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.85: vyatyayobahulam (व्यत्ययो बहुलम्) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas) there is diversely an interchange of the various विकरण-as शप् etc. which have been previously ordained under special circumstances.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.86: lingyaashishyang (लिङ्याशिष्यङ्) — The affix अङ् is used in the छन्दस् (Vedas) when the affixes of the आशीर्लिङ् (Benedictive) follow.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.87: karmavatkarmanaatulyakriyah (कर्मवत् कर्मणा तुल्यक्रियः) — The ल denoting the agent, when the action affecting the agent is similar to the action which affects the object, is treated as if it were a ल denoting the object.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.88: tapastapahakarmakasyaiva (तपस्तपःकर्मकस्यैव) — The agent of the verb तप् 'to heat', becomes similar to the object, only when the object is the word तपस् itself.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.89: naduhasnunamaamyakchinau (न दुहस्नुनमां यक्चिणौ) — The affix यक् -- सार्वधातुके यक् [[3.1.67]],and चिण् -- अचः कर्मकर्तरि [[3.1.62]] are not used in the reflexive voice of the verbs दुह् 'to milk', स्नु 'to fall in drops' and नम् 'to bow.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.90: kushirajohapraachaamshyanparasmaipadamcha (कुषिरजोः प्राचां श्यन् परस्मैपदं च) — The affix श्यन् comes after the roots कुष् 'to pull' and रञ्ज 'to colour' in the reflexive voice, according to the opinion of Eastern Grammarians and these verbs take the affixes of परस्मैपद ।",
    "Sūtra 3.1.91: dhaatoh (धातोः) — As far as the end of the Third Chapter reckoning from the present sūtra, the affixes treated of are to be understood as coming after some verbal root. (Note: This is an अधिकार सूत्र। All these verbal affixes are broadly classified as कृत् and कृत्य affixes)",
    "Sūtra 3.1.92: tatropapadamsaptameestham (तत्रोपपदं सप्तमीस्थम्) — In the Third Chapter of Grammar, referring to verbal roots, the word implied in a term exhibited in the Locative -7th-case, is called उपपद or dependant word.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.93: krudating (कृदतिङ्) — In this portion of the sūtras in which there is a reference to verbal roots, any affix except तिङ् - tense affixes, is called कृत् ।",
    "Sūtra 3.1.94: vaasaroopostriyaam (वाऽसरूपोऽस्त्रियाम्) — In this portion of the sūtras, in which there is reference to verbal roots, an affix which is calculated to debar a general one, not being of the same form, optionally debars it; but not so in the case of feminine affixes -- स्त्रियां क्तिन् [[3.3.94]].",
    "Sūtra 3.1.95: krutyaahapraangnvulah (कृत्याः) — From this sūtra up to ण्वुल्तृचौ [[3.1.133]] all the affixes treated will get the name कृत्य।",
    "Sūtra 3.1.96: tavyattavyaaneeyarah (तव्यत्तव्यानीयरः) — The affixes तव्यत् , तव्य and अनीयर् come after the verbal roots.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.97: achoyat (अचो यत्) — The affix यत् comes after a root that ends in a vowel.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.98: poradupadhaat (पोरदुपधात्) — The affix यत् comes after a root which ends in a labial letter preceded by a short अ।",
    "Sūtra 3.1.99: shakisahoshcha (शकिसहोश्च) — The affix यत् comes after roots शकॢ 'to be able' and सह 'to bear'.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.100: gadamadacharayamashchaanupasarge (गदमदचरयमश्चानुपसर्गे) — The affix यत् comes after roots गद् 'to eat', मद् 'to be mad', चर् 'to go, to eat' and यम् 'to restrain', when these roots do not take any preposition.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.101: avadyapanyavaryaagarhyapanitavyaanirodheshu (अवद्यपण्यवर्या गर्ह्यपणितव्यानिरोधेषु) — The words अवद्य , पण्य , वर्या are irregularly formed, having the sense of 'condemnable', saleable' and unobstructable', respectively.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.102: vahyamkaranam (वह्यं करणम्) — The word वह्यं is irregularly formed when the meaning of the word is an instrument of carrying.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.103: aryahasvaamivaishyayoh (अर्यः स्वामिवैश्ययोः) — The word अर्य is irregularly formed when meaning 'lord' and a वैश्य।",
    "Sūtra 3.1.104: upasaryaakaalyaaprajane (उपसर्या काल्या प्रजने) — The word उपसर्या is irregularly formed when meaning what has reached the time favourable to conception or ripe for fruition.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.105: ajaryamsamgatam (अजर्यं संगतम्) — The word अजर्यंम् 'imperishable' is irregularly formed when qualifying the word संगतम् 'friendship' expressed or understood.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.106: vadahasupikyapcha (वदः सुपि क्यप् च) — After the root वद् 'to speak', governing a case-inflected word as its उपपद and not having a preposition annexed to it, there comes the affix क्यप् also.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.107: bhuvobhaave (भुवो भावे) — After the root भू 'to be', in construction with a case-inflected word as its उपपद and when used without a preposition, the affix क्यप् is used to denote condition - भाव।",
    "Sūtra 3.1.108: hanastacha (हनस्त च) — After the root हनु 'to kill' when in construction with a case-inflected word as its उपपद and when used without a preposition comes the affix क्यप् in denoting condition and the letter त is the substitute of its final.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.109: etistushasvrudrujushahakyap (एतिस्तुशास्वृदृजुषः क्यप्) — After the verbs इ 'to go', स्तु 'to praise', शास् 'to govern', वृ 'to respect' and जुष् 'to please' comes the affix क्यप्।",
    "Sūtra 3.1.110: rudupadhaachchaakapichruteh (ऋदुपधाच्चाकॢपिचृतेः) — After the verbs having the penultimate short ऋ , the affix क्यप् is used, with the exception of the verbs कॢप् 'to be able' and वृत् 'to hurt'.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.111: eechakhanah (ई च खनः) — The affix क्यप् is used after the root खन 'to dig' and long ई is substituted for the final of the root.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.112: bhrunyosamjnyaayaam (भृञोऽसंज्ञायाम्) — The affix क्यप् is used after the root भृञ् 'to bear' when not used as a name.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.113: mrujervibhaashaa (मृजेर्विभाषा) — The affix क्यप् is optionally used after the verb सृज् 'to cleanse'.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.114: raajasooyasooryamrushodyaruchyakupyakrushtapachyaavyathyaah (राजसूयसूर्यमृषोद्यरुच्यकुप्यकृष्टपच्याव्यथ्याः) — The words राजसूय , सूर्य , मृषोद्य , रुच्य , कुप्य , कृष्ट , पच्य and अव्यथ्य irregularly formed by the addition of the affix क्यप्।",
    "Sūtra 3.1.115: bhidyoddhyaunade (भिद्योद्ध्यौ नदे) — The words भिद्य and उद्ध्यौ are irregularly formed by the affix क्यप् , when meaning 'river'.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.116: pushyasiddhyaunakshatre (पुष्यसिद्ध्यौ नक्षत्रे) — The words पुष्य and सिद्ध्य् are irregularly formed by the affix क्यप् , when used as names of asterisms.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.117: vipooyavineeyajityaamunyjakalkahalishu (विपूयविनीयजित्या मुञ्जकल्कहलिषु) — When the words विपूय , विनीय and जित्या are irregularly formed they mean 'the मुञ्ज grass', 'the sediment' and 'the plough', respectively.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.118: pratyapibhyaamgraheshchhandasi (प्रत्यपिभ्यां ग्रहेश्छन्दसि) — The word ग्रह 'to seize', preceded by the prepositions प्रति and अपि , takes the affix क्यप् in the छन्दस् (Vedas).",
    "Sūtra 3.1.119: padaasvairibaahyaapakshyeshucha (पदास्वैरिबाह्यापक्ष्येषु च) — The root ग्रह 'to seize' takes the affix क्यप् when it means a 'word', a 'dependent', 'outside' or a 'partisan'.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.120: vibhaashaakruvrushoh (विभाषा कृवृषोः) — After the verbs कृञ् 'to do' and वृष् 'to rain', the affix क्यप् is optionally used.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.121: yugyamchapattre (युग्यं च पत्रे) — The word युग्यम् is irregularly formed meaning 'a vehicle'.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.122: amaavasyadanyatarasyaam (अमावस्यदन्यतरस्याम्) — Optionally the word अमावस्या is irregular.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.123: chhandasinishtarkyadevahooyapraneeyonneeyochchhishyamaryastvaryaadhvaryakhanyakhaanyadevayajyapruchyapratisheevyabrahmavaadyabhaavyastaavyopachaayyaprudaani (छन्दसि निष्टर्क्यदेवहूयप्रणीयोन्नीयोच्छिष्यमर्यस्तर्याध्वर्यखन्यखान्यदेवयज्यापृच्छ्यप्रतिषीव्यब्रह्मवाद्यभाव्यस्ताव्योपचाय्यपृडानि) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas) the following words are found, which are formed irregularly - निष्टर्क्य , देवहूय , प्रणीय , उन्नीय , उच्छिष्य , मर्य , स्तर्या , ध्वर्य , खन्य , खान्य , देवयज्या , आपृच्छ्य , प्रतिषीव्य , ब्रह्मवाद्य , भाव्य , स्ताव्य , and पचाय्यपृड।",
    "Sūtra 3.1.124: ruhalornyat (ऋहलोर्ण्यत्) — The affix ण्यत् comes after a verb that ends in ऋ (long or short) or in a consonant.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.125: oraavashyake (ओरावश्यके) — The affix ण्यत् comes after a verb that ends in the letter उ - long or short, when the sense is that of 'necessity'.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.126: aasuyuvapirapilapitrapichamashcha (आसुयुवपिरपिलपित्रपिचमश्च) — The affix ण्यत् comes after the verbs आसु 'to distill', यु 'to join', वप 'to sow', रप् 'to speak distinctly', लप् 'to prate', अप् 'to be ashamed' and चम 'to drink'.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.127: aanaayyonitye (आनाय्योऽनित्ये) — The word आनाय्यः is irregularly formed when meaning 'impermanent'.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.128: pranaayyosammatau (प्रणाय्योऽसंमतौ) — The word प्रणाय्य is irregularly formed when meaning 'disapproved'.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.129: paayyasaannaayyanikaayyadhaayyaamaanahavirnivaasasaamidheneeshu (पाय्यसान्नाय्यनिकाय्यधाय्या मानहविर्निवाससामिधेनीषु) — The words पाय्य , सान्नाय्य , निकाय्य and धाय्या are irregularly formed meaning 'a measure', 'an oblation to fire', 'a dwelling' and 'a sacrificial prayer', respectively.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.130: krataukundapaayyasamchaayyau (क्रतौ कुण्डपाय्यसंचाय्यौ) — The words कुण्डपाय्यः and संचाय्यः are irregularly formed meaning 'a sacrifice'.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.131: agnauparichaayyopachaayyasamoohyaah (अग्नौ परिचाय्योपचाय्यसमूह्याः) — The words परिचाय्यः , पचाय्य and समूह्याः are irregularly formed when they are names of fire.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.132: chityaagnichityecha (चित्याग्निचित्ये च) — The words चित्य and ग्निचित्य are also irregularly formed.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.133: nvultruchau (ण्वुल्तृचौ) — The affixes ण्वुल् (अक्) and तृच् (तृ) are placed after all verbal roots, expressing the agent.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.134: nandigrahipachaadibhyolyuninyachah (नन्दिग्रहिपचादिभ्यो ल्युणिन्यचः) — After the verbs classed as नन्द 'to be happy', ग्रह 'to take' and पच् 'to cook' there are the affixes ल्यु (अन), णिनि (इन्) and अच (अ) respectively.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.135: igupadhajnyaapreekirahakah (इगुपधज्ञाप्रीकिरः कः) — After a verb ending in a consonant but preceded by इ , उ or ऋ -long or short, and after the verbs ज्ञा 'to know', श्री 'to please' and कॄ 'to scatter', comes the affix क (अ)। ",
    "Sūtra 3.1.136: aatashchopasarge (आतश्चोपसर्गे) — Also after a verb ending in long आ when there is a preposition along with it, the affix क is placed.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.137: paaghraadhmaadhetdrushahashah (पाघ्राध्माधेट्दृशः शः) — The affix श (अ) is used after the roots पा 'to drink', घ्रा 'to smell', ध्मा 'to blow' and धेट् 'to suck' and दृश् 'to see' when there is a preposition along with these roots.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.138: anupasargaallimpavindadhaaripaarivedyudejichetisaatisaahibhyashcha (अनुपसर्गाल्लिम्पविन्दधारिपारिवेद्युदेजिचेतिसातिसाहिभ्यश्च) — The affix श is used after the verbs - धारि , पारि , वेदि , उदेजि , चेति , साति and साहि , when used without a preposition.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.139: dadaatidadhaatyorvibhaashaa (ददातिदधात्योर्विभाषा) — The affix श is optionally used after the root दा 'to give' and धा 'to hold', when used without a preposition.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.140: jvalitikasantebhyonah (ज्वलितिकसन्तेभ्यो णः) — After the verbs beginning with ज्वल 'to shine' and ending with कस 'to go', when used without a preposition, the affix ण is optionally used.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.141: shyaadvyadhaasrusamsrvateenavasaavahrulihashlishashvasashcha (श्याद्व्यधास्रुसंस्र्वतीणवसाऽवहृलिहश्लिषश्वसश्च) — The affix ण is also used after the verbs - श्यै 'to go', verbs ending in a long भा , व्यद् 'to pierce', आस्रु 'to pain', संत्रु 'to flow', अतीण् 'to pass on', अवसा 'to complete', अवह 'to take away', लिह 'to lick', श्लिष 'to embrace' and श्वस 'to breathe'.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.142: dunyoranupasarge (दुन्योरनुपसर्गे) — The affix ण is used after the verbs दु 'to burn' and नी 'to lead', when used without a preposition.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.143: vibhaashaagraheh (विभाषा ग्रहः) — The affix ण is optionally used after the verb ग्रह 'to seize'.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.144: gehekah (गेहे कः) — The affix क is used after the verb ग्रह 'to seize' when the agent so expressed denotes a house.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.145: shilpinishvun (शिल्पिनि ष्वुन्) — The affix ष्वुन् (अक्) comes after a verb when the agent so expressed denotes an artist.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.146: gasthakan (गस्थकन्) — The affix थकन् (थक) comes after the verb गै 'to sing' when the agent so expressed, denotes an artist.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.147: nyutcha (ण्युट् च) — The affix ण्युट् is also used after the verb गै 'to sing' when the agent so expressed denotes an artist.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.148: hashchavreehikaalayoh (हश्च व्रीहिकालयोः) — After the verb हा , also the affix ण्युट् is used when the agent so expressed denotes 'rice' and 'time'.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.149: prusrulvahasamabhihaarevun (प्रुसृल्वः समभिहारे वुन्) — After the verbs प्रु 'to go', सृ 'to move', स्रु 'to flow' and लू 'to cut', the affix वुन् is used, when repitition is meant.",
    "Sūtra 3.1.150: aashishicha (आशिषि च) — The affix वुन् is applied after all verbs when Benediction is intended.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.1: karmanyan (कर्मण्यण्) — The affix अण् comes after a verbal root when the object (or whatever sort it may be), is in composition with it (an an उपपद).",
    "Sūtra 3.2.2: hvaavaamashcha (ह्वावामश्च) — The affix अण् comes after a root हूञ् 'to call' वेञ् 'to weave', माङ् 'to measure', when the object is in composition with it.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.3: aatonupasargekah (आतोऽनुपसर्गे कः) — The affix क comes after a verbal root that ends in long आ when there is no उपसर्ग preceding it and when the object is in composition with it.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.4: supisthah (सुपि स्थः) — The affix क comes after the root स्था when in composition with a word ending in a case-affix, as an उपपद ।",
    "Sūtra 3.2.5: tundashokayohaparimrujaapanudoh (तुन्दशोकयोः परिमृजापनुदोः) — The affix क comes after the verbs परिमृज् 'to wash out' and अपनुद् 'to drive away' when in composition with the words तुन्द 'navel' and शोक 'grief', as objects respectively.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.6: predaajnyah (प्रे दाज्ञः) — The affix क comes after the root दा 'to give' and ज्ञ 'to know', when taking the preposition प्र in composition with a word in the Accusative -2nd case.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.7: samikhyah (समि ख्यः) — The affix क comes after root ख्या 'to tell', when preceded by the preposition सम् and when the object is in compsition with it.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.8: gaaposhtak (गापोष्टक्) — The affix टक comes after the verbs गै 'to sing' and पा 'to drink' when used without a preposition and when the object is in composition with it.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.9: harateranudyamanech (हरतेरनुद्यमनेऽच्) — The affix अच् comes after the verb हृञ् when it does not mean 'to raise up', when the object is in composition with it.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.10: vayasicha (वयसि च) — The affix अच् comes after the verb हृञ् when the object is in composition with it and when the meaning of the word to be formed is descriptive of age.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.11: aangitaachchheelye (आङि ताच्छील्ये) — The affix अच् comes after the verb हृञ् (when the object is in composition with it) the root taking the preposition आञ् and the sense of the word to be formed in inclination or accustomed occupation.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.12: arhah (अर्हः) — The affix अच् comes after the verb अर्ह 'to respect', when the object is in composition with it.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.13: stambakarnayoharamijapoh (स्तम्बकर्णयो रमिजपोः) — The affix अच् comes after the verb रम् 'to sport' and जप् 'to whisper' when the case-inflected words स्तम्भ 'a clump of grass' and कर्ण 'ear' are in composition with them respectively.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.14: shamidhaatohasamjnyaayaam (शमि धातोः संज्ञायाम्) — The affix अच् is used after the verbal roots when शम् 'well' is in composition and the word to be formed denotes a name.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.15: adhikaranesheteh (अधिकरणे शेतेः) — The affix अच् comes after the verb शी 'to lie down' when in composition with a case-inflected word indicating location i.e. in the Locative -7th-case.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.16: chareshtah (चरेष्टः) — The affix ट comes after the verb चर् 'to go' when a case-inflected word in composition with it denotes a location.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.17: bhikshaasenaadaayeshucha (भिक्षासेनादायेषु च) — The affix ट is used after the verb चर् 'to go' when the words in composition with it भिक्षा 'alms', सेना 'army' and आदाय 'having taken'.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.18: purogratogreshusarteh (पुरोऽग्रतोऽग्रेषु सर्तेः) — The affix ट comes after the verb सृ 'to move' when the words in composition with it are पुरः , अग्रतः and अग्रे , all meaning 'in front or before'.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.19: poorvekartari (पूर्वे कर्तरि) — The affix ट comes after the verb सृ 'to go' when पूर्व in composition with it, denoting the agent.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.20: krunyohetutaachchheelyaanulomyeshu (कृञो हेतुताच्छील्यानुलोम्येषु) — The affix ट comes after the verb कृञ् 'to make' when the object is in composition with it denoting cause, habit and going with the grain (concession).",
    "Sūtra 3.2.21: divaavibhaanishaaprabhaabhaaskaraantaanantaadibahunaandeekimlipilibibalibhaktikartruchitrakshetrasamkhyaajangghaabaahvaharyattatdhanurarushshu (दिवाविभानिशाप्रभाभास्कारान्तानन्तादिबहुनान्दीकिम्लिपिलिबिबलिभक्तिकर्तृचित्रक्षेत्रसंख्याजङ्घाबाह्वहर्यत्तत्धनुररुष्षु) — The affix ट comes after the verb कृञ् 'to make' when the following words are in composition with it - 1. दिवा 'by day' 2. विभा 'light' 3. निशा 'night' 4. प्रभा 'splendour' 5. भाः 'light' 6. कार 'work' 7. अन्त 'end' 8. अनन्त 'endless' 9. आदि 'beginning' 10. बहु 'many' 11. नान्दी 'benediction' 12. किम् 'what' 13. लिपि 'writing' 14. लिबि 'writing' 15. बलि 'oblation' 16. भक्ति 'devotion' 17. कर्तृ 'agent' 18. चित्र 'painting' 19. क्षेत्र 'field' 20. संख्या - words denoting numerals 21. जङ्घा 'thigh' 22. बाहु 'hand' 23. अहः 'day' 24. यत् 'what' 25. तत् 'that' 26. धनुस् 'bow' 27. अरुस् 'wound'.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.22: karmanibhrutau (कर्मणि भृतौ) — The affix ट comes after the verb कृञ् 'to make' when the word कर्म is in composition with it and the sense of the word to be formed is that of wages.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.23: nashabdashlokakalahagaathaavairachaatusootramantrapadeshu (न शब्दश्लोककलहगाथावैरचाटुसूत्रमन्त्रपदेषु) — The affix ट does not come after the verb कृ 'to make' when the following words are in composition with it - 1. शब्द 'sound' 2. श्लोक 'verse' 3. कलह 'quarrel' 4. गाथा 'praise' 5. वैर 'enmity' 6. चाटु 'flattery' 7. सूत्र 'thread' 8. मन्त्र 'hymns' 9. पद 'word'.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.24: stambashakrutorin (स्तम्बशकृतोरिन्) — The affix इन् comes after the verb कृ when the objects in composition with it are the words स्तम्ब 'a sheaf' and शकृत् 'ordure'.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.25: haraterdrutinaathayohapashau (हरतेर्दृतिनाथयोः पशौ) — When the agent indicated is an animal, the affix इन् comes after the verb हृ 'to take', the object in composition with it being the words ददृति 'a leather bag' and नाथ 'a master'.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.26: phalegrahiraatmambharishcha (फलेग्रहिरात्मम्भरिश्च) — And the words फलेग्रहि and आत्मम्भरि are irregularly formed.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.27: chhandasivanasanarakshimathaam (छन्दसि वनसनरक्षिमथाम्) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas) the affix इन् comes after the verbs वन् 'to honour', सन् 'to worship', रक्ष् 'to protect' and अथ् 'to agitate', when the object is in composition.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.28: ejehakhash (एजेः खश्) — The affix खश् comes after the verb एजृ 'to tremble' when ending in शि and when the object is in composition with it.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.29: naasikaastanayordhmaadhetoh (नासिकास्तनयोर्ध्माधेटोः) — The affix खश् comes after the verbs ध्मा 'to blow' and धे 'to suck' when नासिका 'nose' and स्तन 'breast' are in composition with them as object.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.30: naadeemushtyoshcha (नाडीमुष्ट्योश्च) — And when the words नाडी 'a tube' and मुष्टि 'a fist' are objects in composition with the verbs ध्मा 'to blow' and धे 'to suck', the affix खश् is used.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.31: udikoolerujivahoh (उदि कूले रुजिवहोः) — The affix खश् comes after the verbs रुजि 'to break into pieces' and वह् 'to carry', when preceded by the उपसर्ग उत् and the word कूल 'bank' is in composition with them as the object.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.32: vahaabhrelihah (वहाभ्रे लिहः) — The affix खश् comes after the verb लिह 'to lick' when the object in composition with it, is the word वह 'the shoulder of an ox' or अभ्र 'a cloud'.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.33: parimaanepachah (परिमाणे पचः) — The affix खश् comes after the verb पच् 'to cook' when the object in composition with it denotes a measure.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.34: mitanakhecha (मितनखे च) — The affix खश् is used after the verb पच् 'to cook' when मित 'a measured partition' or नख 'a nail' is the word in composition with it as an object.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.35: vidhvarushostudah (विध्वरुषोस्तुदः) — The affix खश् comes after the verb तुद् 'to strike' when विधु 'the moon' or अरुस् 'a wound' is the word in composition with it as object.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.36: asooryalalaatayordrushitapoh (असूर्यललाटयोर्दृशितपोः) — The affix खश् comes after the verb दृश् 'to see' and तप् 'to heat' when असूर्य and ललाट are the words in composition with it as object.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.37: ugrampashyerammadapaanindhamaashcha (उग्रम्पश्येरम्मदपाणिन्धमाश्च) — The words उग्रम्पश्य , इरम्मद , पाणिन्धम are irregularly formed.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.38: priyavashevadahakhach (प्रियवशे वदः खच्) — The affix खच् comes after the verb वद् 'to speak' when प्रिय or वश is the word in composition with it as an object.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.39: dvishatparayostaapeh (द्विषत्परयोस्तापेः) — The affix खच् comes after the verb ताप् 'to heat' when द्विषत् or पर is the word in composition with it as an object.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.40: vaachiyamovrate (वाचि यमो व्रते) — The affix खच् comes after the verb यस् 'to curb' when the word वाक् 'speech' is in composition with it as an object and the sense indicated is that of a vow.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.41: poohasarvayordaarisahoh (पूःसर्वयोर्दारिसहोः) — The affix खच् comes after the verb दारि 'to split' and सह् 'to bear' when respectively in composition with the words पुर् 'a city' and सर्व 'all', as objects.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.42: sarvakoolaabhrakareesheshukashah (सर्वकूलाभ्रकरीषेषु कषः) — The affix खच् comes after the verb कष् 'to rub' when the words सर्व 'all', कूल 'bank', अभ्र 'cloud' and करीष 'a dry cow-dung' are in composition with it as objects.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.43: meghartibhayeshukrunyah (मेघर्तिभयेषु कृञः) — The affix खच् comes after the verb कृ 'to make' when the words मेघ 'cloud' अर्ति 'misfortune' and भय 'fear' are in composition as objects.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.44: kshemapriyamadrencha (क्षेमप्रियमद्रेऽण् च) — And the affix अण् as well as खच् come after the verb कृ 'to make' when the words क्षेम 'happiness', प्रिय 'pleasant' and भद्र 'joy' are in composition as objects.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.45: aashitebhuvahakaranabhaavayoh (आशिते भुवः करणभावयोः) — The affix खच् comes after the verb भू 'to be' when in composition with the case-inflected word आशित 'satisfied by eating' and the sense is that of instrument or condition.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.46: samjnyaayaambhrutruvrujidhaarisahitapidamah (संज्ञायां भृतॄवृजिधारिसहितपिदमः) — The affix खच् comes after the verbs - 1. भृ 'to bear' 2. तॄ 'to cross over' 3. वृ 'to choose' 4. जि 'to conquer' 5. धारि 'to hold' 6. सहि 'to bear' 7. तपि 'to heat' 8. दम 'to subdue'",
    "Sūtra 3.2.47: gamashcha (गमश्च) — And the affix खच् comes after the verb गम् 'to go' when in composition with a word ending in a case-affix and when the word to be formed denotes a name.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.48: antaatyantaadhvadoorapaarasarvaananteshudah (अन्तात्यन्ताध्वदूरपारसर्वानन्तेषु डः) — And the affix खच् comes after the verb गम् 'to go' when in composition with the verbs - 1. अन्त 'end' 2. अत्यन्त 'extreme' 3. अध्वम् 'road' 4. दूर 'far' 5. पार 'across' 6. सर्व 'all' 7. अनन्त 'endless'.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.49: aashishihanah (आशिषि हनः) — The affix ड comes after the verb हन् 'to kill' when the object is in composition with it and when benediction is intended.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.50: apekleshatamasoh (अपे क्लेशतमसोः) — The affix ड comes after the verb हन् 'to kill' when it is compounded with the preposition अप् and when the object in composition with it, is the word क्लेश 'pain' or तमस् 'darkness'.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.51: kumaarasheershayorninih (कुमारशीर्षयोर्णिनिः) — The affix णिनि comes after the verb हन् 'to kill' when the word in composition with it is कुमार 'a child' or शीर्ष 'head'.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.52: lakshanejaayaapatyoshtak (लक्षणे जायापत्योष्टक्) — The affix टक् comes after the verb हन् 'to kill' when it is in composition with the word जाया 'wife' or पति 'husband' as object and when the word so formed denotes the agent possessed of that attribute (or when the word so formed denotes a mark).",
    "Sūtra 3.2.53: amanushyakartrukecha (अमनुष्यकर्तृके च) — The affix टक् comes after the verb हन् 'to kill' when the object is in composition with it and when the word to be formed denotes an agent other than a human being.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.54: shaktauhastikapaatayoh (शक्तौ हस्तिकपाटयोः) — The affix टक् comes after the verb हन् 'to kill' when the object is in composition with it as its object is हस्ति 'elephant' or कपाट 'gate' and when the sense indicated is that of power.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.55: paanighataadaghaushilpini (पाणिघताडघौ शिल्पिनि) — The word पाणिघ and ताडघ are irregularly formed when denoting an artificier.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.56: aadhyasubhagasthoolapalitanagnaandhapriyeshuchvyrtheshvachvaukrunyahakaranekhyun (आढ्यसुभगस्थूलपलितनग्नान्धप्रियेषु च्व्यर्थेष्वच्वौ कृञः करणे ख्युन्) — The affix ख्युन् , when in the sense of the word to be formed is that of an instrumental agent, comes after the verb कृ 'to make', when the following words are in composition with it - 1. आढ्य 'rich' 2. सुभग 'fortunate' 3. स्थूल 'big' 4. पलित 'grey' 5. नग्न 'naked' 6. अन्ध 'blind' 7. प्रिय 'pleasant', provided these words formed by the affix च्वि though not actually ending in the affix च्वि।",
    "Sūtra 3.2.57: kartaribhuvahakhishnuchkhukanyau (कर्तरि भुवः खिष्णुच्खुकञौ) — The affixes खिष्णुच् and खकञ् , when the word to be formed denotes an agent comes after the verb भू 'to become', when it is in composition with the words formed by the affix च्वि though not actually ending in the affix च्वि।",
    "Sūtra 3.2.58: sprushonudakekvin (स्पृशोऽनुदके क्विन्) — The affix क्विन् comes after the verb स्पृश् 'to touch' when it is in composition with a case-inflected word other than उदक 'water'.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.59: rutvigdadhruksragdigushniganychuyujikrunychaamcha (ऋत्विग्दधृक्स्रग्दिगुष्णिगञ्चुयुजिक्रुञ्चां च) — The words - 1. ऋत्विक् 'a domestic priest' 2. दधृक् 'impudent' 3. स्रक् 'a garland' 4. दिक् 'direction' and 5. उष्णिक् 'a quatrain', are irregularly formed by adding the affix क्विन् and also after the verbs 6. अञ्चु 'to worship' 7. युजि 'to join' 8. क्रुञ्चु 'to approach', the affix क्विन् is used.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.60: tyadaadishudrushonaalochanekanycha (त्यदादिषु दृशोऽनालोचने कञ् च) — And the affix कञ् comes after the verb दृश् 'to see' when it is in composition with त्यद् etc. and does not signify perception.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.61: satsoodvishadruhaduhayujavidabhidachchhidajineeraajaamupasargepikvip (सत्सूद्विषद्रुहदुहयुजविदभिदच्छिदजिनीराजामुपसर्गेऽपि क्विप्) — The affix क्विप्comes after the following verbs when in composition with a word ending in a case-affix, though it may be an उपसर्ग viz. 1. सत् 'to sit' 2. सू 'to bring forth' 3. द्विष् 'to hate' 4. द्रुह् 'to bear malice' 5. दुह् 'to milk' 6. युज् 'to join' , 'to concentrate the mind' 7. विद् 'to know', 'to consider' 8. भिद् 'to divide' 9. च्छिद् 'to cut' 10. जि 'to conquer' 11. नी 'to lead 12. राज् 'to shine'.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.62: bhajonvih (भजो ण्विः) — The affix ण्वि comes after the verb भज् 'to share' when in composition with a word ending in a case-affix whether it be an उपसर्ग or not.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.63: chhandasisahah (छन्दसि सहः) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas) the affix णिव comes after the verb सह् 'to bear' when in composition with a word ending in a case-affix.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.64: vahashcha (वहश्च) — The affix णिव after the verb वह् 'to carry' in the छन्दस् (Vedas), when the word ending in case-affix is in composition with it.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.65: kavyapureeshapureeshyeshunyyut (कव्यपुरीषपुरीष्येषु ञ्युट्) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas) the affix ञ्युट् comes after the verb वह् 'to carry' when it is in composition with the words कव्य 'oblation of food to deceased ancestors', पुरीष 'faeces' and पुरीष्य 'water'.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.66: havyenantahapaadam (हव्येऽनन्तः पादम्) — The affix ञ्युट् comes in the छन्दस् (Vedas) after the verb वह् 'to carry' when it is in composition with the word हव्य 'an oblation to gods', provided that the word so formed does not occur in the middle of a पाद (4th part of a stanza).",
    "Sūtra 3.2.67: janasanakhanakramagamovit (जनसनखनक्रमगमो विट्) — The affix विट् (the whole of which is elided) comes in the छन्दस् (Vedas) after the verbs 1. जन् 'to be born' 2. सन् 'to bestow' 3. खन् 'to dig' 4. क्रम् 'to pace' 5. गम् 'to go' when a word ending in case-affix is in composition and the final nasals are changed into long आ।",
    "Sūtra 3.2.68: adonanne (अदोऽनन्ने) — The affix विट् comes after the verb अद् 'to eat' when in composition with a case-inflected word other than अन्न 'food'.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.69: kravyecha (क्रव्ये च) — The affix विट् comes after the verb अद् 'to eat' when the word क्रव्य is in composition with it.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.70: duhahakabghashcha (दुहः कब् घश्च) — The affix कप् comes after the verb दुह् 'to milk' when in composition with a word ending in a case-affix and the letter घ replaces the final.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.71: mantreshvetavahaukthashaspurodaashonvin (मन्त्रे श्वेतवहोक्थशस्पुरोडाशो ण्विन्) — In the मन्त्र literature,the affix णिवन् comes after the words 1. श्वेतवह 2.उक्थश 3. पुरोडाश् ।",
    "Sūtra 3.2.72: aveyajah (अवे यजः) — In the मन्त्र literature,the affix णिवन् comes after the verb यज् 'to sacrifice' when in composition the word अव्।",
    "Sūtra 3.2.73: vijupechhandasi (विजुपे छन्दसि) — The affix विच् comes after the verb यज् 'to sacrifice' when उप precedes it, in the छन्दस् (Vedas).",
    "Sūtra 3.2.74: aatomaninkvanipvanipashcha (आतो मनिन्क्वनिब्वनिपश्च) — The affixes मनिन् (मन्), वनिप् (वन्), विनय (वन्) and विच् come in the छन्दस् (Vedas) after the verbs which end in long आ , when used in a case-inflected word or उपसर्ग in in composition. ",
    "Sūtra 3.2.75: anyebhyopidrushyante (अन्येभ्योऽपि दृश्यन्ते) — These affixes i.e. - मनिन् (मन्), वनिप् (वन्), विनय (वन्) and विच् are seen after other verbs also besides those ending in long आ।",
    "Sūtra 3.2.76: kvipcha (क्विप् च) — And the affix क्विप् is also seen after all verbs, whether having an उपपद or not in the Vedic as well as in the modern Sanskrit.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.77: sthahakacha (स्थः क च) — The affixes क and क्विप् come after the verb स्था when in composition with a word ending in a case-affix or an उपसर्ग ।",
    "Sūtra 3.2.78: supyajaatauninistaachchhilye (सुप्यजातौ णिनिस्ताच्छील्ये) — When habit is to be expressed, the affix णिनि comes after a verb, provided the word with a case-affix in composition with it does not mean a genus.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.79: kartaryupamaane (कर्तर्युपमाने) — The affix णिनि comes after a verb when in composition with a word denoting an object of comparison, expressing the agent, the sense of the affix being 'doing something like that', that is to say, when the उपपद agent is the standard of comparison of the agent denoted by the word to which the sense of the affix refers.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.80: vrate (व्रते) — The affix णिनि comes after a verb, in composition with a word ending in a case-affix.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.81: bahulamaabheekshnye (बहुलमाभीक्ष्ण्ये) — The affix णिनि comes after a verb diversely when continued repitition of an action is to be expressed.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.82: manah (मनः) — The affix णिनि comes after the verb मन् 'to think' when there is a word with a case-affix in composition with it.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.83: aatmamaanekhashcha (आत्ममाने खश्च) — And the affix णिनि comes after the verb मन् 'to think' when the word in composition with it is a word with a case-affix and when it is used to signify thought, whereof the object is self (the sense of the affix being 'thinking himself as such').",
    "Sūtra 3.2.84: bhoote (भूते) — All the affixes to be treated of hereafter should be understood to come in the sense of past time.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.85: karaneyajah (करणे यजः) — The affix णिनि comes after the verb यज् 'to sacrifice' with the sense of past time, when the word in composition is the Instrumental -3rd case.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.86: karmanihanah (कर्मणि हनः) — The affix णिनि comes after the verb हन् 'to kill' with the sense of past time, when the word in composition is in the Accusative -2nd case.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.87: brahmabhroonavrutreshukvip (ब्रह्मभ्रूणवृत्रेषु क्विप्) — The affix क्विप्comes after the verb हन् 'to kill' with the sense of past time when the following words in the Accusative -2nd case ae in composition - 1. भ्रूण 'a foetus' 2. वृत्र ।",
    "Sūtra 3.2.88: bahulamchhandasi (बहुलं छन्दसि) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas) the affix क्विप्diversely comes after the verb हन् 'to kill' with the sense of past time,ending with the word even when the word in composition with it is other than those mentioned in the last sūtra.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.89: sukarmapaapamantrapunyeshukrunyah (सुकर्मपापमन्त्रपुण्येषु कृञः) — The affix क्विप्comes after the verb कृ 'to make' with the sense of past time, when the following words in the Accusative -2nd case are in composition - 1. सु 'action' 2. कर्म 'action' 3. पाप 'sin' 4. मन्त्र 'hymn' 5. पुण्य 'virtue'.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.90: somesunyah (सोमे सुञः) — The affix क्विप्comes after the verb सु 'to press out juice' with the sense of past time, when the word सोम , in the Accusative -2nd case, is in composition.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.91: agnaucheh (अग्नौ चेः) — The affix क्विप्comes after the verb चि 'to collect' with the sense of past time, when the word अग्नि , in the Accusative -2nd case, is in composition.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.92: karmanyagnyaakhyaayaam (कर्मण्यग्न्याख्यायाम्) — In expressing an object the affix क्विप्comes after the verb चि 'to collect' with the sense of past time when in composition with a word in the Accusative -2nd case, provided the word so formed is the name of fire.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.93: karmaneenirvikriyah (कर्मणीनिविक्रियः) — The affix इनि comes after the compound verb विकृ 'to sell' in the sense of past time, when in composition with a word in the Accusative -2nd case.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.94: drushehakvanip (दृशेः क्वनिप्) — The affix क्वनिप् comes after the verb दृश् 'to see' in the sense of past time, when in composition with a word in the Accusative -2nd case.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.95: raajaniyudhikrunyah (राजनि युधिकृञः) — The affix क्वनिप् comes after the verbs युध 'to fight' and कृ 'to make' with a past signification when the word राजन् 'king' is in composition, in the Accusative -2nd case.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.96: sahecha (सहे च) — The affix क्वनिप् comes after the verbs युध 'to fight' and कृ 'to make' with a past signification when the word सह 'with', is in composition.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.97: saptamyaamjanerdah (सप्तम्यां जनेर्डः) — The affix ड comes after the verb जन् 'to be produced', with a past signification, when the word, in composition with it is in the Locative -7th-case.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.98: panychamyaamajaatau (पञ्चम्यामजातौ) — The affix ड comes after the verb जन् 'to be produced', with a past signification, when the word, in composition with it is in the Ablative -5th case, which does not denote a genus.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.99: upasargechasamjnyaayaam (उपसर्गे च संज्ञायाम्) — The affix ड comes after the verb जन् 'to be produced', with a past signification, when an उपसर्ग is in composition and when the sense is simply appellative.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.100: anaukarmani (अनौ कर्मणि) — The affix ड comes after the verb जन् 'to be produced', with a past signification, when the root takes the preposition अनु and is compounded with a word in the Accusative -2nd case.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.101: anyeshvapidrushyate (अन्येष्वपि दृश्यते) — The affix ड is seen to come after the verb जन् 'to be produced', with a past signification,though it be in composition with other nouns, having cases other than those mentioned in the previous sūtras.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.102: nishthaa (निष्ठा) — The affixes called निष्ठा come after a verbal root used in the sense of past time.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.103: suyajorngvanip (सुयजोर्ङ्वनिप्) — The affix ङ्वनिप् comes after the verbs सु 'to press out or extract juice' and यज् 'to sacrifice', with a past signification.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.104: jeeryateratrun (जीर्यतेरतृन्) — The affix अतृन् comes after the verb जृ 'to grow old' with the sense of past time.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.105: chhandasilit (छन्दसि लिट्) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas), the affix लिट् (Perfect Tense) comes after a verb with a past signification.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.106: litahakaanajvaa (लिटः कानज्वा) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas), the affix लिट् (Perfect Tense) is optionally replaced by the affix कानच्।",
    "Sūtra 3.2.107: kvasushcha (क्वसुश्च) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas) the affix क्वसु is optionally the substitute for लिट् ।",
    "Sūtra 3.2.108: bhaashaayaamsadavasashruvah (भाषायां सदवसश्रुवः) — In modern Sanskrit the affix क्वसु optionally replaces लिट् (Perfect Tense) after the verbs सद् , वस् and श्रु with a past signification.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.109: upeyivaananaashvaananoochaanashcha (उपेयिवाननाश्वाननूचानश्च) — The forms उपेयिवान् , नाश्वान् , नूचान् are irregularly formed.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.110: lung (लुङ्) — The affix लुङ् (Aorist) comes after the verb in the sense of past time.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.111: anadyatanelang (अनद्यतने लङ्) — The affix लुङ् (Aorist) comes after a verbal root used in the sense of past before the commencement of the current day.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.112: abhijnyaavachanelrut (अभिज्ञावचने लृट्) — When a word implying 'recollection' is in connection with it, a verb takes the affix लृट् (2nd Future) in the sense of the past before the commencement of the present day.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.113: nayadi (न यदि) — The affix लृट् (2nd Future) is not applied in the sense of the past when the उपपद denoting recollection has in connection with it the particle यत्।",
    "Sūtra 3.2.114: vibhaashaasaakaangkshe (विभाषा साकाङ्क्षे) — The affix लृट् (2nd Future) is optionally applied in the sense of the past, when a word implying 'recollection' is in connection with it and whether such a word has the particle यत् or is used simply; provided that the two verbs, occurring in the same complex sentence, are also connected together, that each is necessary to the other , to complete the sense of the speaker.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.115: parokshelit (परोक्षे लिट्) — The affix लिट् (Perfect Tense) comes after the verb in the sense of the past before the commencement of the current day and unperceived by the narrator.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.116: hashashvatorlangcha (हशश्वतोर्लङ् च) — And the affix लङ् (Imperfect Tense) comes after the verb when the particles ह and शश्वत are in connection with it and when the verb denotes past action unperceived by the speaker and before the commencement of the current day.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.117: prashnechaasannakaale (प्रश्ने चासन्नकाले) — The affixes लङ् (Imperfect Tense) and लिट् (Perfect Tense) come after a verb (in expressing a past time not belonging to the current day and unperceived by the speaker) when the past referred to is recent and the sentence is interrogative.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.118: latsme (लट् स्मे) — The affix लट् (Present Tense) comes after a verb when the particle स्म is in connection with it (and denotes a past time not belonging to the current day and unperceived by the speaker). Note : This debars लिट् (Perfect Tense) .",
    "Sūtra 3.2.119: aparokshecha (अपरोक्षे च) — The affix लट् (Present Tense) comes after a verb when the particle स्म is in connection with it and denotes a past action not belonging to the current day and when the action is perceived by the agent.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.120: nanauprushtaprativachane (ननौ पृष्टप्रतिवचने) — The affix लट् (Present Tense) is used after a verb in denoting a past action when the word ननु is in connection with it and an answer is given to the question.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.121: nanvorvibhaashaa (नन्वोर्विभाषा) — The affix लट् (Present Tense) comes optionally after a verb in denoting past time, in reply to an interrogation, when the words न 'not' and नु 'what of that' are in connection with it.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.122: purilungchaasme (पुरि लुङ् चास्मे) — Optionally the affixes लुङ् (Aorist) and लट् (Present Tense) come after a verb in denoting past time not belonging to the current day, when the word पुरा is used in the sentence, provided that the word स्म is not used.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.123: vartamaanelat (वर्तमाने लट्) — The affix लट् (Present Tense) comes after a verb when denoting a present action.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.124: latahashatrushaanachaavaprathamaasamaanaadhikarane (लटः शतृशानचावप्रथमासमानाधिकरणे) — The affixes शतृ and शानच् are substitutes of लट् (Present Tense) when agreeing with what does not end with the 1st (Nominative Case) case-affix.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.125: sambodhanecha (सम्बोधने च) — The affixes शतृ and शानच् are substitutes of लट् (Present Tense) even when agreeing with what ends with a 1st (Nominative Case) case-affix, provided that it is in the Vocative Case.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.126: lakshanahetvohakriyaayaah (लक्षणहेत्वोः क्रियायाः) — The affixes शतृ and शानच् are substitutes of लट् (Present Tense) and come after a verb in expressing an attendant circumstance or characteristic and the cause of an action.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.127: tausat (तौ सत्) — These two - शतृ and शानच् are called सत्.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.128: poongyajohashaanan (पूङ्यजोः शानन्) — The affix शानन् comes after the verbs पू 'to purify' and यज् 'to sacrifice'.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.129: taachchheelyavayovachanashaktishuchaanash (ताच्छील्यवयोवचनशक्तिषु चानश्) — The affix चानश् comes after a verb in expressing 'habit', standard of age' and 'inability'.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.130: ingdhaaryohashatrakruchchhrini (इङ्धार्योः शत्रकृच्छ्रिणि) — The affix शतृ comes after the verb इङ् 'to go' and धारि 'to hold' in denoting that the agent does the action without trouble.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.131: dvishomitre (द्विषोऽमित्रे) — The affix शतृ comes after the verb द्विष् when the agent indicated means 'an enemy'.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.132: sunyoyajnyasamyoge (सुञो यज्ञसंयोगे) — The affix शतृ comes after the verb सु 'to press out or extract juice' when the sense is that of association with sacrifice.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.133: arhahapoojaayaam (अर्हः प्रशंसायाम्) — The affix शतृ comes after the verb अर्ह in expressing praise.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.134: aakvestachchheelataddharmatatsaadhukaarishu (आक्वेस्तच्छीलतद्धर्मतत्साधुकारिषु) — From this sūtra as far as क्विप् in sūtra [[3.4.177]] (inclusive), the affixes that we shall treat of, are to be understood in the sense of agents having such a habit or nature or having skill in such and such action.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.135: trun (तृन्) — The affix तृन् comes after all verbs in the sense of 'agents having such a habit etc.'.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.136: alamkrunyniraakrunyprajanotpachotpatonmadaruchyapatrapavrutuvrudhusahacharishnuch (अलंकृञ्निराकृञ्प्रजनोत्पचोत्पतोन्मदरुच्यपत्रपवृतुवृधुसहचर इष्णुच्) — The affix इष्णुच् comes after following verbs in the sense of 'agents having such a habit etc.' - 1. अलंकृ 'to adorn' 2. ञ्निराकृ 'to expel' 3. प्रजन् 'to be born' 4. उत्पच् 'to be ripe' 5. उत्पत् 'to fly' 6. उन्मद् 'to be mad' 7. रुच् 'to shine' 8. अपत्रप् 'to be ashamed' 9. वृत् 'to move' 10. वृध् 'to grow 12. सह 'to bear' 13. चर् 'to walk'.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.137: neshchhandasi (णेश्छन्दसि) — The affix इष्णुच् in the sense of 'the agent having such a habit etc.' comes in the छन्दस् (Vedas) after the verb that ends in the causative णि।",
    "Sūtra 3.2.138: bhuvashcha (भुवश्च) — The affix इष्णुच् in the sense of 'the agent having such a habit etc.' comes in the छन्दस् (Vedas) after the verb भू 'to be' etc.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.139: glaajisthashchaksnuh (ग्लाजिस्थश्च क्स्नुः) — The affix क्स्नु comes after the following verbs in the sense of 'the agent having such a habit etc.' viz. - 1. ग्ला 'to be weary' 2. जि 'to conquer' 3. स्था 'to stand', as well as after भू 'to be'.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.140: trasigrudhidhrushikshipehaknuh (त्रसिगृधिधृषिक्षिपेः क्नुः) — The affix क्नु comes after the verbs - 1. त्रस् 'to tremble' 2. गृध् 'to be greedy' 3. धृष् 'to be bold' 4. क्षिप् 'to throw' in the sense of 'agent having such a habit etc.'.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.141: shamityashtaabhyoghinun (शमित्यष्टाभ्यो घिनुण्) — The affix घिनुण् comes after the 8 verbs beginning with शम् 'to be calm' in the sense of 'the agent having such a habit etc.'.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.142: sampruchaanurudhaangyamaangyasaparisrusamsrujaparidevisamjvaraparikshipaparirataparivadaparidahaparimuhadushadvishadruhaduhayujaakreedavivichatyajarajabhajaaticharaapacharaamushaabhyaahanashcha (संपृचानुरुधाङ्यमाङ्यसपरिसृसंसृजपरिदेविसंज्वरपरिक्षिपपरिरटपरिवदपरिदहपरिमुहदुषद्विषद्रुहदुहयुजाक्रीडविविचत्यजरजभजातिचरापचरामुषाभ्याहनश्च) — The affix घिनुण् comes after the following verbs in the sense of 'the agent having such a habit etc.'. - 1. संपृच् 2. अनुरुध् 3. आङ्यम् 4. आङ्यस् 5. परिसृ 6. संसृज् 7. परिदेवि 8. संज्वर् 9. परिक्षिप् 10. परिरट् 11. परिवद् 12. परिदह् 13. परिमुह् 14. दुष् 15. द्विष् 16. द्रुह् 17. दुह् 18. युज् 19. आक्रीड् 20. विविच् 21. त्यज् 22. रज् 23. भज् 24 अतिचर् 25. अपचर् 26. आमुष् 27. अभ्याहन्।",
    "Sūtra 3.2.143: vaukashalasakatthasrambhah (वौ कषलसकत्थस्रम्भः) — The affix घिनुण् comes after the verbs कष् 'to injure', लस् 'to embrace and sport', कत्थ 'to praise' and स्रम्भ 'to believe', when these are in composition with the preposition वि।",
    "Sūtra 3.2.144: apechalashah (अपे च लषः) — The affix घिनुण् comes after the verb लष 'to wish' when compounded with the preposition अप and वि।",
    "Sūtra 3.2.145: prelapasrudrumathavadavasah (प्रे लपसृद्रुमथवदवसः) — The affix घिनुण् comes after the verbs 1. लप् 2. सृ 3. द्रु 4. मथ 5. वद् 6. वस् when compounded with the preposition वि।",
    "Sūtra 3.2.146: nindahimsaklishakhaadavinaashaparikshipaparirataparivaadivyaabhaashaasoonyovuny (निन्दहिंसक्लिशखादविनाशपरिक्षिपपरिरटपरिवादिव्याभाषासूञो वुञ्) — The affix वुञ् is added to the following verbs in the sense of 'the agent having such a habit etc.' - 1. निन्द् 2. हिंस् 3. क्लिश् 4. खाद् 5. विनाश् 6. परिक्षिप् 7. परिरट् 8. व्याभाष् and असूय।",
    "Sūtra 3.2.147: devikrushoshchopasarge (देविक्रुशोश्चोपसर्गे) — The affix वुञ् comes after the verbs देवि 'to lament' and क्रुश 'to cry' when an उपसर्ग is in composition with them.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.148: chalanashabdaarthaadakarmakaadyuch (चलनशब्दार्थादकर्मकाद्युच्) — The affix युच् comes, in the sense of 'the agent having such a habit etc.' after intransitive verbs denoting 'motion' or 'sound'.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.149: anudaattetashchahalaadeh (अनुदात्तेतश्च हलादेः) — The affix युच् comes, in the sense of 'the agent having such a habit etc.' after intransitive verbs as are आत्मनेपदि and begin with a consonant and are अनुदात्त i.e. have a gravely accented vowel as as indicatory.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.150: juchangkramyadandramyasrugrudhijvalashuchalashapatapadah (जुचङ्क्रम्यदन्द्रम्यसृगृधिज्वलशुचलषपतपदः) — The affix युच् comes after the following verbs in the sense of 'the agent having such a habit etc.' - 1. जु 2. चङ्क्रम्य 3. दन्द्रम्य 4. सृ 5. गृध 6.ज्वल 7. शुच 8. लष 9. पत 10. पद।",
    "Sūtra 3.2.151: krudhamandaarthebhyashcha (क्रुधमण्डार्थेभ्यश्च) — And after the verbs having the sense of क्रुध् 'to be angry' and मण्ड 'to adorn', the affix युच् is used. ",
    "Sūtra 3.2.152: nayah (न यः) — The affix युच् is not used after the verbs which end in the letter य।",
    "Sūtra 3.2.153: soodadeepadeekshashcha (सूददीपदीक्षश्च) — The affix युच् does not come after the verbs सूद् 'to strike', दीप् 'to shine' and दीक्ष् 'to initiate'.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.154: lashapatapadasthaabhoovrushahanakamagamashrubhyukany (लषपतपदस्थाभूवृषहनकमगमशॄभ्य उकञ्) — The affix उकञ् comes after the following verbs, in the sense of 'agent having such habit etc.' - 1. लष् 2. पत् 3. पद् 4. स्था 5. भू 6. वृष् 7. हन् 8. कम् 9. गम् 10. शॄ ।",
    "Sūtra 3.2.155: jalpabhikshakuttaluntavrungahashaakan (जल्पभिक्षकुट्टलुण्टवृङः षाकन्) — The affix षाकन् comes, in the sense of 'agent having such habit etc.' after the following verbs - 1. जल्प् 2. भिक्ष् 3. कुट्ट 4. लुण्ट 5.वृङ ।",
    "Sūtra 3.2.156: prajorinih (प्रजोरिनिः) — The affix इनि comes in the sense of 'agent having such habit etc.' after the verb प्रजु 'to hasten forward'.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.157: jidrukshivishreenvamaavyathaabhyamaparibhooprasoobhyashcha (जिदृक्षिविश्रीण्वमाव्यथाभ्यमपरिभूप्रसूभ्यश्च) — The affix इनि comes in the sense of 'agent having such habit etc.' after the verbs 1. जि 'to conquer' 2. दृ 'to respect' 3. क्षि 'to waste, to dwell, to go' 4. विश्रि 'to shelter' 5. इ 'to go' 6. वम् 'to vomit' 7. अव्यथ 'not to give pain' 8. अभ्यम 'to injure' 9. परिभू 'to humiliate' 10. प्रसू 'to beget'.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.158: spruhigruhipatidayinidraatandraashraddhaabhyaaluch (स्पृहिगृहिपतिदयिनिद्रातन्द्राश्रद्धाभ्य आलुच्) — The affix आलुच् comes in the sense of 'agent having such habit etc.' after the words - 1. स्पृह् 'to desire' 2. गृह् 'to seize' 3. पत् 'to go' 4. दय् 'to give, to go , to protect' 5. निद्रा 'to sleep' 6. तन्द्रा 'to be tired' 7. श्रद्धा 'to venerate'.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.159: daadhetsishadasadoruh (दाधेट्सिशदसदो रुः) — The affix रु comes after the verbs 1. दा 'to give' 2. धेट् 'to suck' 3. सि 'to bind' 4. शद 'to fall' 5. सद् 'to sit'.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.160: srughasyadahakmarach (सृघस्यदः क्मरच्) — The affix क्मरच् comes in the sense of 'agent having such a habit etc.' comes after the verbs 1. सृ 'to flow' 2. घसि 'to eat' 3. अद् 'to eat'.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.161: bhanyjabhaasamidoghurach (भञ्जभासमिदो घुरच्) — The affix घुरच् comes in the sense of 'agent having such a habit etc.' after the verbs 1. भञ्ज् 'to break' 2. भास् 'to shine' 3. भिद् 'to be fat'.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.162: vidibhidichchhidehakurach (विदिभिदिच्छिदेः कुरच्) — The affix कुरच् comes in the sense of 'agent having such a habit etc.' after the verbs 1. विद् 'to know' 2. भिद् 'to divide' 3. छिद् 'to pierce'.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.163: innashjisarttibhyahakvarap (इण्नश्जिसर्त्तिभ्यः क्वरप्) — The affix क्वरप् comes in the sense of 'agent having such a habit etc.' after the verbs 1. इ 'to go' 2. नश् 'to destroy' 3. जि 'to conquer' 4. सृ 'to flow'.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.164: gatvarashcha (गत्वरश्च) — And the word गत्वर is irregularly formed.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.165: jaagurookah (जागुरूकः) — The affix ऊक comes after the verb जागृ 'to be awake' in the sense of 'agent having such a habit'.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.166: yajajapadashaamyangah (यजजपदशां यङः) — The affix ऊक comes in the sense of 'agent having such a habit etc.' after the verbs 1. यज् 2. जप् 3. दश् when they end in the affix य्।",
    "Sūtra 3.2.167: namikampismyajasakamahimsadeeporah (नमिकम्पिस्म्यजसकमहिंसदीपो रः) — The affix र comes in the sense of 'agent having such a habit etc.' after the verbs 1. नम 'to bow' 2. क्मप् 'to shake' 3. स्मि 'to smile' 4. अजस् 'not to cease' 5. कम 'to desire' 6. हिंस 'to injure' 7. दीप 'to shine'.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.168: sanaashamsabhikshuh (सनाशंसभिक्ष उः) — The affix उ comes after the roots that have taken the affix सन् and after all the verbs आशंस् 'to wish' and भिक्ष 'to beg' in the sense of 'agent having such a habit etc.'.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.169: vindurichchhuh (विन्दुरिच्छुः) — The words विन्दु and इच्छु are irregularly formed by the addition of the affix उ , in the sense of 'agent having such a habit etc.'.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.170: kyaachchhandasi (क्याच्छन्दसि) — The affix उ comes in the छन्दस् (Vedas) after the roots that have taken the Denominative affix क्य in the sense of 'agent having such a habit etc.'.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.171: aadrugamahanajanahakikinaulitcha (आदृगमहनजनः किकिनौ लिट् च) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas), the affixes कि and किन् in the sense of 'agent having such a habit etc.' come after the verbs that end in long आ or long or short ऋ and after the verbs 1. गम् 'to go' 2. हन् 'to kill' 3. जन् 'to be produced' and these affixes operate like लिट् (Perfect Tense) causing reduplication of the root.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.172: svapitrushornajing (स्वपितृषोर्नजिङ्) — The affix नजिङ् comes, in the sense of 'agent having such a habit etc.' after the verbs स्वप् 'to sleep' and तृष् 'to be thirsty'.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.173: shruvandyoraaruh (शॄवन्द्योरारुः) — The affix आरु comes, in the sense of 'agent having such a habit etc.' after the verbs शॄ 'to to injure' and वन्द् 'to praise, to salute'.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.174: bhiyahakruklukanau (भियः क्रुक्लुकनौ) — The affixes क्रु and क्लुकन come in the sense of 'agent having such a habit etc.' after the verb भी 'to fear'.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.175: stheshabhaasapisakasovarach (स्थेशभासपिसकसो वरच्) — The affix वरच् comes, in the sense of 'agent having such a habit etc.' after the verbs 1. स्था 'to stand' 2. ईश 'to rule' 3. भास् 'to shine' 4. पिस् 'to go' 5. कस् 'to go'.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.176: yashchayangah (यश्च यङः) — The affix वरच् in the sense of 'agent having such a habit etc.' comes after the verb या when it ends with the affix यङ्।",
    "Sūtra 3.2.177: bhraajabhaasadhurvidyutorjiprujugraavastuvahakvip (भ्राजभासधुर्विद्युतोर्जिपॄजुग्रावस्तुवः क्विप्) — The affix क्विप् comes in the sense of 'agent having such a habit etc.' after the verbs 1. भ्राज 'to shine' 2. भास् 'to shine' 3. धुर्व 'to injure' 4. द्युत् 'to shine' 5. ऊर्ज 'to be strong' 6. पॄ 'to fill' 7. जु 'to move rapidly' 8. स्तु 'to praise', when preceded by the word ग्रवन् 'a stone'.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.178: anyebhyopidrushyate (अन्येभ्योऽपि दृश्यते) — The affix क्विप् comes in the sense of 'agent having such a habit etc.' after the verbs other than those seen above.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.179: bhuvahasamjnyaantarayoh (भुवः संज्ञाऽन्तरयोः) — The affix क्विप् comes after the verb भू 'to be' when the word so formed denotes a name or surety.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.180: viprasambhyodvasamjnyaayaam (विप्रसम्भ्यो ड्वसंज्ञायाम्) — The affix डु comes after the verb भू 'to be' when it is preceded by the उपसर्ग वि , प्र and सम् provided that the word to be formed does not mean an appellative.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.181: dhahakarmanishtran (धः कर्मणि ष्ट्रन्) — The affix ष्ट्रन् comes, in denoting the object after the verb धा 'to feed'.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.182: daamneeshasayuyujastutudasisichamihapatadashanahahakarane (दाम्नीशसयुयुजस्तुतुदसिसिचमिहपतदशनहः करणे) — The affix ष्ट्रन् with in the sense of instrument, comes after the verbs 1. दाप 'to cut' 2. नी 'to lead' 3. शस् 'to hurt' 4. यु 'to join' 5. युज् 'to join' 6. स्तु 'to praise' 7. तुद् 'to inflict pain' 8. सि 'to bind' 9. सिच् 'to sprinkle' 10. मिह् 'to urine' 11. पत् 'to fall' 12. दश् 'to bite' 13. नह् 'to bind'",
    "Sūtra 3.2.183: halasookarayohapuvah (हलसूकरयोः पुवः) — The affix ष्ट्रन् is used after the verb पू 'to purify' with the sense of instrument when denoting a member of the body of a plough or of a hog.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.184: artiloodhoosookhanasahacharitrah (अर्तिलूधूसूखनसहचर इत्रः) — The affix इत्र comes after the verbs 1. ऋ 'to go' 2. लू 'to cut' 3. धू 'to shake' 4. सू 'to bring forth' 5. खन् 'to dig' 6. सह् 'to bear' 7. चर् 'to go' , with the sense of instrument.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.185: puvahasamjnyaayaam (पुवः संज्ञायाम्) — The affix इत्र comes after the verb पू 'to purify' with the sense of the agent so expressed being the instrument when the sense of the complete word is simply appellative and not descriptive.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.186: kartaricharshidevatayoh (कर्तरि चर्षिदेवतयोः) — The affix इत्र comes after the verb पू 'to purify' with the sense of the agent or instrument when it is respectively used in connection with a sage or a deity.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.187: nyeetahaktah (ञीतः क्तः) — The verbal roots marked with an indicatory ञि , take the affix क्त , in denoting the present time.",
    "Sūtra 3.2.188: matibuddhipoojaarthebhyashcha (मतिबुद्धिपूजार्थेभ्यश्च) — And after the roots denoting inclination, understanding, or respect, the affix क्त is used with the force of the present",
    "Sūtra 3.3.1: unaadayobahulam (उणादयो बहुलम्) — The affixes उण् and the rest with the force of the present and with a sense simply appellative are attached diversely.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.2: bhootepidrushyante (भूतेऽपि दृश्यन्ते) — The उणादि affixes are seen also attached with the force of the past time.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.3: bhavishyatigamyaadayah (भविष्यति गम्यादयः) — The words गामि etc. are valid forms having the sense of the future time.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.4: yaavatpuraanipaatayorlat (यावत्पुरानिपातयोर्लट्) — The affix लट् (Present Tense) comes after a root with the force of futurity when it has in construction with it the particles यावत् and पुरा।",
    "Sūtra 3.3.5: vibhaashaakadaakarhyoh (विभाषा कदाकर्ह्योः) — The affix लट् (Present Tense) is optionally used after a root with the force of the futurity when it has in construction with it the adverbs कदा and कर्हि।",
    "Sūtra 3.3.6: kimvruttelipsaayaam (किंवृत्ते लिप्सायाम्) — When the word किम् or its derivatives are in construction with a verb, the affix लट् (Present Tense) is used optionally after a root, in denoting future time, provided that the sentences expresses a desire of gaining on the part of the speaker.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.7: lipsyamaanasiddhaucha (लिप्स्यमानसिद्धौ च) — And when the success, that would accrue to another by fulfilling the desire of the speaker, is indicated in a sentence, the present tense may optionally be used with the force of the futurity.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.8: lodarthalakshanecha (लोडर्थलक्षणे च) — The affix लट् (Present Tense) is optionally used with the force of futurity after that root, which is in a conditional sentence, is the condition precedent for the action indicated by another verb having the sense of the imperative mood.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.9: lingchordhvamauhoortike (लिङ् चोर्ध्वमौहूर्तिके) — The लट् (Present Tense) or the लिङ् (Potential) is used under similar conditions in denoting futurity, when the future time is future by a मूहूर्त (= 48 minutes).",
    "Sūtra 3.3.10: tumunnvulaukriyaayaamkriyaarthaayaam (तुमुन्ण्वुलौ क्रियायां क्रियार्थायाम्) — The affixes तुमुन् and ण्वुल् are placed after a verbal root with the force of the future when the word in construction therewith is another verb, denoting an action performed for the sake of the (future) action.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.11: bhaavavachanaashcha (भाववचनाश्च) — And the affixes that are ordained to come after a root with the force of denoting the mere action of the verb, such as धञ् etc. -- लोहितादिडाज्भ्यः क्यष् [[3.1.3]], have also the force of the future, when the word in construction therewith is another verb denoting an action performed for the sake of the future action.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.12: ankarmanicha (अण् कर्मणि च) — The affix अण् comes after a root with the force of the future when the word in construction with it is in the Accusative -2nd case and when the action is performed for the sake of another action.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.13: lrutsheshecha (लृट् शेषे च) — The affix लृट् (2nd Future) is used after a verb in the remaining cases where futurity pure and simple is indicated and also where there is construction with it another verb denoting an action performed for the sake of the future action.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.14: lrutahasadvaa (लृटः सद् वा) — The affixes called सत् i.e. शतृ and शानच् are optionally the substitutes of लृट् (2nd Future).",
    "Sūtra 3.3.15: anadyatanelut (अनद्यतने लुट्) — The affix लुट् (1st Future) comes after a verbal root in the sense of what will happen but not in the course of the current day.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.16: padarujavishasprushoghany (पदरुजविशस्पृशो घञ्) — The affix घञ् comes after the roots 1. पद् 'to pace' 2. रुज् 'to pain 3. विश् 'to enter' 4. स्पृश् 'to touch'.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.17: srusthire (सृ स्थिरे) — The affix घञ् comes after the verb शृ 'to move' when the agent is permanently fixed.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.18: bhaave (भावे) — The affix घञ् comes after a root when mere action is denoted.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.19: akartarichakaarakesamjnyaayaam (अकर्तरि च कारके संज्ञायाम्) — The affix घञ् comes after a root when the sense is that of an appellative, the word being related to the verb from which its name is deduced, but not as agent.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.20: parimaanaakhyaayaamsarvebhyah (परिमाणाख्यायां सर्वेभ्यः) — The affix घञ् comes after all roots when the word so formed is the name of a measure.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.21: ingashcha (इङश्च) — The affix घञ् comes after the root इङ् 'to study'.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.22: upasargeruvah (उपसर्गे रुवः) — The affix घञ् comes after the verb रू 'to roar' when it has an उपसर्ग in composition with it.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.23: samiyudruduvah (समि युद्रुदुवः) — The affix घञ् comes after the roots 1. यु 'to join' 2. द्रु 'to run' 3. दु 'to burn' when in composition with the preposition सम्।",
    "Sūtra 3.3.24: shrineebhuvonupasarge (श्रिणीभुवोऽनुपसर्गे) — The affix घञ् comes after the roots 1. शृ 'to go to' 2. नी 'to lead' 3. भू 'to be' when not in composition with an उपसर्ग ।",
    "Sūtra 3.3.25: vaukshushruvah (वौ क्षुश्रुवः) — The affix घञ् comes after the roots 1. क्षु 'to sneeze' 2. श्रु 'to move and hear' when the preposition वि is in composition.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.26: avodorniyah (अवोदोर्नियः) — The affix घञ् comes after the verb नी 'to lead' when the prepositions अव and उत् are in composition.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.27: predrustusruvah (प्रे द्रुस्तुस्रुवः) — The affix घञ् comes after the roots 1. द्रु 'to run' 2. स्तु 'to praise' 3. श्रु 'to move and hear' when the word in composition is प्र।",
    "Sūtra 3.3.28: nirabhyohapoolvoh (निरभ्योः पूल्वोः) — The affix घञ् comes after the roots 1. पू 'to purify' 2. लू 'to cut' when निर् and अभि are respectively in composition.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.29: unnyorgrah (उन्न्योर्ग्रः) — The affix घञ् comes after the root गॄ when the उपसर्ग-s उत् and नि are in composition.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.30: krudhaanye (कॄ धान्ये) — The affix घञ् comes after the verb कॄ when the prepositions उत् and नि are in composition and when the sense of the verb relates to grain.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.31: yajnyesamistuvah (यज्ञे समि स्तुवः) — The affix घञ् comes after the verb स्तु 'to praise' when it is preceded by the उपसर्ग सम् and the word refers to sacrificial subjects.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.32: prestroyajnye (प्रे स्त्रोऽयज्ञे) — The affix घञ् comes after the verb स्तॄ 'to cover' when preceded by the preposition प्र ; provided that the word so formed does not refer to sacrifice.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.33: prathanevaavashabde (प्रथने वावशब्दे) — The affix घञ् comes after the verb स्तॄ 'to cover' when the preposition वि is in composition with it when the sense is that of extension and when such spreading does not refer to words.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.34: chhandonaamnicha (छन्दोनाम्नि च) — The affix घञ् comes after the verb स्तॄ 'to cover' with the उपसर्ग वि when the word so formed is the name of a metre.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.35: udigrahah (उदि ग्रहः) — The affix घञ् comes after the verb ग्रह् 'to seize' when the preposition उत् is in composition.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.36: samimushtau (समि मुष्टौ) — The affix घञ् comes after the verb ग्रह् 'to seize' when in composition with preposition सम् when the sense of the root refers to fist.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.37: parinyorneenordyootaabhreshayoh (परिन्योर्नीणोर्द्यूताभ्रेषयोः) — The affix घञ् comes after the roots 1. नी 'to lead' 2. इ 'to go' when the prepositions परि and नि respectively in composition with them and when the words so formed respectively mean 'a game' and 'propriety or arrangement or law'.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.38: paraavanupaatyayinah (परावनुपात्यय इणः) — The affix घञ् comes after the root इ 'to go' in composition with the word परि when the sense is that of following in regular succession.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.39: vyupayohashetehaparyaaye (व्युपयोः शेतेः पर्याये) — The affix घञ् comes after the root सी 'to lie down' when the prepositions वि and उप are in composition with it and when the sense of the word so formed is that of 'regular succession'.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.40: hastaadaanecherasteye (हस्तादाने चेरस्तेये) — The affix घञ् comes after the root चि 'to collect' when the sense expressed is that of taking by hand provided it does not refer to stealing.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.41: nivaasachitishareeropasamaadhaaneshvaadeshchakah (निवासचितिशरीरोपसमाधानेष्वादेश्च कः) — The affix घञ् comes after the roots चि 'to collect' and क is the substitute of the initial च in these senses viz. - 1. 'a dwelling' 2. 'a fire on the funeral pile' 3. 'the body' 4. 'collection'.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.42: samghechaanauttaraadharye (संघे चानौत्तराधर्ये) — The affix घञ् comes after the roots चि 'to collect' and क is the substitute of the initial च in the sense of 'a multitude or assembly' (of living beings possessing some common characteristics) but not merely a confused crowd of men.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.43: karmavyatihaarenachstriyaam (कर्मव्यतिहारे णच् स्त्रियाम्) — The affix णच् comes after a root in denoting reciprocity of action and the word so formed is in the feminine gender.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.44: abhividhaubhaavinun (अभिविधौ भाव इनुण्) — The affix इनुण् comes after a root in denoting condition when co-extensiveness is meant.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.45: aakroshevanyorgrahah (आक्रोशेऽवन्योर्ग्रहः) — The affix घञ् comes after the root ग्रह् 'to seize' in composition with अव and नि when malediction is meant.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.46: prelipsaayaam (प्रे लिप्सायाम्) — The affix घञ् comes after the root ग्रह् 'to seize' when the word प्र is in composition and the sense denoted is the desire of acquisition.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.47: parauyajnye (परौ यज्ञे) — The affix घञ् comes after the root ग्रह् 'to seize' in composition with परि when it relates to sacrificial subjects.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.48: nauvrudhaanye (नौ वृ धान्ये) — The affix घञ् comes after the verb वृ preceded by नि when the sense is that of grain.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.49: udishrayatiyautipoodruvah (उदि श्रयतियौतिपूद्रुवः) — The affix घञ् comes after the verbs 1. श्रि 2. यु 'to join' 3. पू 'to purify' 4. द्रु 'to run' when the preposition उत् is in composition.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.50: vibhaashaangirupluvoh (विभाषाऽऽङि रुप्लुवोः) — The affix घञ् is optionally used after the verbs 1. रू 'to roar' 2. प्लु 'to float' when the preposition अङ् is in composition.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.51: avegrahovarshapratibandhe (अवे ग्रहो वर्षप्रतिबन्धे) — The affix घञ् is optionally used after the root ग्रह् 'to seize' when the word अव is in composition, the sense being 'withholding the rain'.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.52: prevanijaam (प्रे वणिजाम्) — The affix घञ् is optionally used after the root ग्रह् 'to seize' in composition with प्र when the word so formed relates to commerce.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.53: rashmaucha (रश्मौ च) — The affix घञ् is optionally used after the root ग्रह् 'to seize' in composition with प्र when the word so formed means 'a rein'.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.54: vrunoteraachchhaadane (वृणोतेराच्छादने) — The affix घञ् is optionally used after the verb वृ 'to choose' when प्र is in composition and the word so formed means 'a sort of covering'.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.55: paraubhuvovajnyaane (परौ भुवोऽवज्ञाने) — The affix घञ् is optionally used after the verb भू 'to be', the word परि being in construction and the sense of the word so formed being 'disregard'.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.56: erach (एरच्) — The affix अच् comes after a root ending in इ or ई (when mere action is denoted or when the sense is that of an appellative, the word being related to the verb from which its name is deduced, but not as an agent).",
    "Sūtra 3.3.57: rudorap (ॠदोरप्) — After a root ending in long ॠ , short उ or long ऊ , there is the affix अप्।",
    "Sūtra 3.3.58: grahavrudrunishchigamashcha (ग्रहवृदृनिश्चिगमश्च) — The affix अप् comes after the verbs 1. ग्रह् 'to seize' 2. वृ 'to choose' 3. दृ 4. निश्चि 5. गम् 'to go'.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.59: upasargedah (उपसर्गेऽदः) — The affix अप् comes after the verb अद् 'to eat' when an उपसर्ग is in composition.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.60: naunacha (नौ ण च) — And The affix ण as well as अप् come after the verb अद् 'to eat' when the उपसर्ग नि is in composition.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.61: vyadhajaporanupasarge (व्यधजपोरनुपसर्गे) — The affix अप् comes after the verbs 1. व्यध् 'to hurt or to pierce' 2. जप् 'to mutter' when no उपसर्ग is in composition with them.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.62: svanahasorvaa (स्वनहसोर्वा) — The affix अप् comes optionally after the verbs 1. स्वन् 2. हस् when no उपसर्ग is in composition with them.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.63: yamahasamupanivishucha (यमः समुपनिविषु च) — And The affix अप् comes optionally after the verb यम् 'to surround' when the उपसर्ग -s सम् , उप , नि and वि are in composition ; or even when it is without उपसर्ग -less.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.64: naugadanadapathasvanah (नौ गदनदपठस्वनः) — The affix अप् comes optionally after the verbs 1. गद् 'to speak' 2. नद् 'to sound' 3. पठ् 'to read' 4. स्वन् 'to sound' when the उपसर्ग नि is in composition with them.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.65: kvanoveenaayaamcha (क्वणो वीणायां च) — The affix अप् comes optionally after the verb क्वन् 'to jingle' when नि is in composition with it, as well as when it is without any उपसर्ग or when 'flute' is meant.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.66: nityampanahaparimaane (नित्यं पणः परिमाणे) — The affix अप् comes Invariably after the verb पण् 'to barter' when the sense is that of 'measure'.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.67: madonupasarge (मदोऽनुपसर्गे) — The affix अप् comes after the verb मद् when not in composition with an उपसर्ग ।",
    "Sūtra 3.3.68: pramadasammadauharshe (प्रमदसम्मदौ हर्षे) — The words प्रमद and सम्मद are irregularly formed, meaning 'joy'.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.69: samudorajahapashushu (समुदोरजः पशुषु) — The affix अप् comes after the verb अज् 'to go' when the preposition सम् and उत् are in composition and the word so formed refers to beasts.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.70: aksheshuglahah (अक्षेषु ग्लहः) — The word ग्लह is irregularly formed when the sense of the root refers to gambling.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.71: prajanesarteh (प्रजने सर्तेः) — The affix अप् comes after the verb श्रि 'to flow' in the sense of impregnating (the covering of cows etc.).",
    "Sūtra 3.3.72: hvahasamprasaaranamchanyabhyupavishu (ह्वः सम्प्रसारणं च न्यभ्युपविषु) — The affix अप् comes after the verb ह्वे 'to call' when the preposition नि , अभि , उप and वि are in composition with it and its semi-vowel is changed into the corresponding vowel.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.73: aangiyuddhe (आङि युद्धे) — The affix अप् comes after the verb ह्वे 'to call' when the word in composition is the उपसर्ग आण् and the semi-vowel of the root is changed into its corresponding vowel, when the word so formed means 'battle'.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.74: nipaanamaahaavah (निपानमाहावः) — The word आहाव is irregularly formed when meaning 'a trough'.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.75: bhaavenupasargasya (भावेऽनुपसर्गस्य) — The affix अप् comes after the verb ह्वे 'to call' and there is the change of the semi-vowel to its corresponding vowel, when the root is without an उपसर्ग and mere action is denoted.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.76: hanashchavadhah (हनश्च वधः) — The affix अप् comes after the verb हन् 'to kill' when without an उपसर्ग , in the sense of mere action and वध is the substitute of हन् 'to kill' before this affix.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.77: moortaughanah (मूर्तौ घनः) — The affix अप् comes after the verb हन् 'to kill' when the word so formed means 'solidity' and घन् is the substitute.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.78: antarghanodeshe (अन्तर्घनो देशे) — The verb हन् preceded by the word अन्तर् takes the affix अप् and घन् is the substitute of the word हन् when the word so formed means 'a country'.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.79: agaaraikadeshepraghanahapraghaanashcha (अगारैकदेशे प्रघणः प्रघाणश्च) — The words प्रघणः and प्रघाण are irregularly formed meaning 'a portion of a dwelling house'.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.80: udghanotyaadhaanam (उद्घनोऽत्याधानम्) — The word उद्घन is irregularly formed in the sense of 'bench'.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.81: apaghanonggam (अपघनोऽङ्गम्) — The word अपघन is irregularly formed meaning 'a member of the body'.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.82: karaneyovidrushu (करणेऽयोविद्रुषु) — The affix अप् comes after the verb हन् 'to kill' when the words अयस् , वि or द्रु are in composition with it, when the word so formed is related to the verb as an instrument and घन् is the substitute.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.83: stambekacha (स्तम्बे क च) — The affix क also comes after a root हन् 'to kill' when स्तम्ब 'a clump' is the word in composition and the relation of the word so formed to the verb is that of the instrument.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.84: paraughah (परौ घः) — The affix क also comes after a root हन् 'to kill' when the उपसर्ग परि is in composition and the relation between the word so formed and the verb is that of an instrument and घ replaces हन् ।",
    "Sūtra 3.3.85: upaghnaashraye (उपघ्न आश्रये) — The word उपघ्न is irregularly formed meaning 'an inclined place for leaning or support'.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.86: samghodghauganaprashamsayoh (संघोद्घौ गणप्रशंसयोः) — The words संघ and उद्घ are irregularly formed in the sense of 'a collection' and 'a praise' respectively.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.87: nighonimitam (निघो निमितम्) — The word निघ is irregularly formed in the sense of 'as high as broad'.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.88: dvitahaktrih (ड्वितः क्त्रिः) — The affix क्त्रि comes after the verb which has an indicatory डु when denoting mere action etc.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.89: tvitothuch (ट्वितोऽथुच्) — After that verb that has an indicatory टु , the affix अथुच् comes with the force of denoting mere action etc.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.90: yajayaachayatavichchhaprachchharakshonang (यजयाचयतविच्छप्रच्छरक्षो नङ्) — After the verbs 1. यज् 'to worship' 2. याच् 'to ask for' 3. यत् 'to strive' 4. विच्छ् 'to shine' 5. प्रच्छ् 'to ask' 6. रक्ष् 'to preserve', comes the affix नङ् with the force of denoting mere action etc.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.91: svaponan (स्वपो नन्) — The affix नन् comes under similar circumstances after the verb स्वप् 'to sleep'.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.92: upasargeghohakih (उपसर्गे घोः किः) — The affix कि comes under similar circumstances after a घु verb -- दाधा घ्वदाप् [[1.1.20]] when an उपसर्ग is in composition with it.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.93: karmanyadhikaranecha (कर्मण्यधिकरणे च) — The affix कि comes after a घु verb -- दाधा घ्वदाप् [[1.1.20]] when a word in the Accusative -2nd case is in composition with it and when the relation of the word so formed to its verb, is that of 'location.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.94: striyaamktin (स्त्रियां क्तिन्) — To express an action etc. by a word in the feminine gender, the affix क्तिन् is added to the root.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.95: sthaagaapaapachaambhaave (स्थागापापचो भावे) — After the roots 1. स्था 'to stand' 2. गा 'to sing' 3. पा 'to drink' 4. पच् 'to cook', the affix क्तिन् is used when a word in the feminine gender denoting a 'mere action' is to be expressed.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.96: mantrevrusheshapachamanavidabhooveeraaudaattah (मन्त्रे वृषेषपचमनविदभूवीरा उदात्तः) — In the मन्त्र literature, क्तिन् acutely accented comes after the following roots, forming words in feminine gender, denoting a 'mere action' 1. वृष् 'to rain' 2. इष् 'to wish 3. पच् 'to cook' 4. मन् 'to think' 5. विद् 'to know' 6. भू 'to be' 7. वि 'to go, to consume' 8. रा 'to give'.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.97: ootiyootijootisaatihetikeertayashcha (ऊतियूतिजूतिसातिहेतिकीर्तयश्च) — And these words viz. 1. ऊति 'preserving sport' 2. यूति 'joining' 3. जूति 'velocity' 4. साति 'destruction' 5. हेति 'a weapon' 6. कीर्ति 'fame', are anomalous forms, acutely accented (उदात्त).",
    "Sūtra 3.3.98: vrajayajorbhaavekyap (व्रजयजोर्भावे क्यप्) — The affix क्यप् comes after a roots 1. व्रज 'to go' 2. यज् 'to worship' acutely accented (उदात्त) in forming a word in the feminine denoting action.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.99: samjnyaayaamsamajanishadanipatamanavidashunysheengbhrunyinah (संज्ञायां समजनिषदनिपतमनविदषुञ्शीङ्भृञिणः) — The affix क्यप् comes after the following verbs in forming a word in the feminine denoting an 'appellative 'and is acutely accented (उदात्त) viz. 1. समज 2. निषद 3. निपत 4. मन 5. विद 6. षुञ् 7. शीङ् 8. भृञ् 9. इण्",
    "Sūtra 3.3.100: krunyahashacha (कृञः श च) — And after the root कृ comes the affix श in forming a feminine as well as the affix क्यप्।",
    "Sūtra 3.3.101: ichchhaa (इच्छा) — The form इच्छा 'desire' is irregular.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.102: apratyayaat (अ प्रत्ययात्) — After the verbs that end in an affix, there is the affix अ, the word being feminine.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.103: guroshchahalah (गुरोश्च हलः) — The affix अ comes after a verb which has a prosodially heavy vowel and ends in a consonant when the word to be formed is feminine.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.104: shidbhidaadibhyong (षिद्भिदादिभ्योऽङ्) — The affix अण् comes after those verbs that have an indicatory षि and after भिद् when the word to be formed is feminine.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.105: chintipoojikathikumbicharchashcha (चिन्तिपूजिकथिकुम्बिचर्चश्च) — The affix अण् as well as the affix युच् come after the following verbs, forming feminine words - 1. चिन्त् 'to think' 2. पूज् 'to worship' 3. कथ् 'to narrate' 4. कुम्ब् 'to cover' 5. चर्च् 'to learn'",
    "Sūtra 3.3.106: aatashchopasarge (आतश्चोपसर्गे) — The affix अण् comes after those verbs which end in long आ when an उपसर्ग is in composition and when the word to be formed is feminine.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.107: nyaasashranthoyuch (ण्यासश्रन्थो युच्) — After verbs ending in णि and after आस् 'to sit' and श्रन्थ् 'to loose', there is the affix युच् when the word to be formed is feminine.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.108: rogaakhyaayaamnvulbahulam (रोगाख्यायां ण्वुल् बहुलम्) — The affix ण्वुल् comes diversely after verbs when the word to be formed is feminine noun, being the name of 'diseases'.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.109: samjnyaayaam (संज्ञायाम्) — The affix ण्वुल् comes after the verbal roots, when the word to be formed is an appellative.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.110: vibhaashaakhyaanapariprashnayorinycha (विभाषाऽऽख्यानपरिप्रश्नयोरिञ् च) — And the affix इञ् comes optionally after a root when a question and answer is expressed (as well as ण्वुल् and other affixes ordained by other rules).",
    "Sūtra 3.3.111: paryaayaarharnotpattishunvuch (पर्यायार्हर्णोत्पत्तिषु ण्वुच्) — The affix ण्वुच् comes optionally after a root in the sense of succession, merit, debt or production.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.112: aakroshenanyyanih (आक्रोशे नञ्यनिः) — The affix अनि comes after a verb when the particle नञ् is in composition with it and the sense implied is that of 'cursing'.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.113: krutyalyutobahulam (कृत्यल्युटो बहुलम्) — The affixes called कृत्य -- कृत्याः प्राङ् ण्वुलः [[3.1.95]], and the affix ल्युट् , are diversely applicable and have other senses than those taught before.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.114: napumsakebhaavektah (नपुंसके भावे क्तः) — The affix क्त is added to the root when action is expressed, the word being in the neuter gender.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.115: lyutcha (ल्युट् च) — The affix ल्युट् is added to the root when the name of an action is expressed, in the neuter gender.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.116: karmanichayenasamsparshaatkartuhashareerasukham (कर्मणि च येन संस्पर्शात् कर्तुः शरीरसुखम्) — The affix ल्युट् is added to a root when the name of an action is expressed, in the neuter gender provided that the verb has in construction with it, such a word in the Accusative -2nd case, as indicates the thing, from the contact with which, there arises a pleasant sensation corporally to the agent.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.117: karanaadhikaranayoshcha (करणाधिकरणयोश्च) — The affix ल्युट् is added to a root when the relation of the word so formed to the verb is that of an instrument or location.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.118: pumsisamjnyaayaamghahapraayena (पुंसि संज्ञायां घः प्रायेण) — The affix घ generally comes in the sense of an instrument or location after a root, when the word to be formed is a name and is in the masculine gender.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.119: gocharasamcharavahavrajavyajaapananigamaashcha (गोचरसंचरवहव्रजव्यजापणनिगमाश्च) — And the words 1. गोचर 2. संचर 3. वह 4. व्रज 5. व्यज 6. आपण 7. निगम are anomalous.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.120: avetrustrorghany (अवे तॄस्त्रोर्घञ्) — The affix घञ् comes after the roots 1. तॄ 'to cross' 2. स्तॄ 'to spread, to cover', when the उपसर्ग अव is in composition with them and when the word so formed is an appellative related to the verb either as an instrument or as a location.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.121: halashcha (हलश्च) — And after a verb ending in a consonant, comes the affix घञ् (when the word to be formed is masculine and related to the verb as an instrument or a location and thereby the palatal is changed into guttural).",
    "Sūtra 3.3.122: adhyaayanyaayodyaavasamhaaraadhaaraavayaashcha (अध्यायन्यायोद्यावसंहाराधारावायाश्च) — And the words 1. अध्याय 2. न्याय 3. उद्याव 4. संहार 5. आधारा 6. आवयाः are anomalous.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.123: udangkonudake (उदङ्कोऽनुदके) — The word उदङ्क is anomalous when the sense of the root refers to subjects other than 'water'.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.124: jaalamaanaayah (जालमानायः) — The word आनाय is irregularly formed when the meaning is 'a net'.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.125: khanoghacha (खनो घ च) — The affix घ as well as घञ् come after the verb खन् 'to dig' when the word to be formed is an appellative related to the verb as an instrument or location.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.126: eeshadduhasushukruchchhraakruchchhraartheshukhal (ईषद्दुःसुषु कृच्छ्राकृच्छ्रार्थेषु खल्) — In the sense of 'hard and difficult' or 'light and easy' the affix खल् is added to a verb when ईषद् and दुर् and सु are combined with it as उपपद-s.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.127: kartrukarmanoshchabhookrunyoh (कर्तृकर्मणोश्च भूकृञोः) — The affix खल् comes after the verbs भू 'to be' and कृ when the उपपद-s in composition with them are 'agent' and 'object' respectively, preceded by the words ईषद् etc. in combination with them, meaning 'hard or light'.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.128: aatoyuch (आतो युच्) — The affix युच् comes after the roots ending in long आ (when ईषद् and दुर् and सु are combined as उपपद-sūtras, in the sense of easily or with difficulty).",
    "Sūtra 3.3.129: chhandasigatyarthebhyah (छन्दसि गत्यर्थेभ्यः) — The affix युच् comes in the छन्दस् (Vedas) after the roots having the sense of 'to go' when the word ईषद् etc. meaning 'lightly' or 'with difficulty' are in composition with such verbs.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.130: anyebhyopidrushyate (अन्येभ्योऽपि दृश्यते) — The affix युच् is seen to come number the छन्दस् (Vedas) after other verbs also, than those meaning 'to go'",
    "Sūtra 3.3.131: vartamaanasaameepyevartamaanavadvaa (वर्तमानसामीप्ये वर्तमानवद्वा) — The affixes which are used when the sense is that of present time, may, optionally in like manner, be used when the sense is that of past or future time not remote from the present.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.132: aashamsaayaambhootavachcha (आशंसायां भूतवच्च) — The affixes which are used when the sense is that of past time or of the present time, may, optionally, in like manner, be used after a root in denoting future time when hope is expressed.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.133: kshipravachanelrut (क्षिप्रवचने लृट्) — When the word क्षिप्र 'quickly' or its synonym is in construction with the verb, the future affix लृट् (2nd Future) is used after the root when 'hope' is expressed in a conditional form.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.134: aashamsaavachaneling (आशंसावचने लिङ्) — The affix of the Potential is used in denoting Futurity after a root, when the उपपद in composition with it is a word expressing 'hope'.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.135: naanadyatanavatkriyaaprabandhasaameepyayoh (नानद्यतनवत् क्रियाप्रबन्धसामीप्ययोः) — When constant continuance of action or a near Past or Future is meant, the Past and Future are not denoted as taught in अनद्यतने लङ् [[3.2.111]] and अनद्यतने लुट् [[3.3.15]], through the Imperfect and the II Future, but through the Aorist and the First Future.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.136: bhavishyatimaryaadaavachanevarasmin (भविष्यति मर्यादावचनेऽवरस्मिन्) — The Futurity is not expressed, as taught in अनद्यतने लुट् [[3.3.15]] through the II Future, but through the I Future, when a statement is made of a limit on this (अवर) side of another place.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.137: kaalavibhaagechaanahoraatraanaam (कालविभागे चानहोरात्राणाम्) — The II Future is used instead of the I Future in denoting Future time not belonging to the current day when the word अवर is used together with a word expressing division of time, but not when it is a word giving the sense of 'day' or 'night'.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.138: parasminvibhaashaa (परस्मिन् विभाषा) — Optionally so, when a declaration is made with regard to that side of a limit of time.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.139: lingnimittelrungkriyaatipattau (लिङ्निमित्ते लृङ् क्रियातिपत्तौ) — Where there is a reason for affixing लिङ् (Benedictive) the affix ऌङ् (Conditional Future) is used in the Future tense when the non-completion of the action is to be understood.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.140: bhootecha (भूते च) — And (where there is a reason for affixing लिङ् (Benedictive) , the affix ऌङ् (Conditional Future) is to be used, when the non-completion of the action is to be understood) if the sense is that of past time.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.141: votaapyoh (वोताप्योः) — From this point up to sūtra उताप्योः समर्थयोर्लिङ् [[3.3.152]] (the whole of the following sentence is to be taken as exerting a governing the influence on the sūtras that follow; where there is a reason for affix लिङ् (Benedictive) , the ऌङ् (Conditional Future) may be) optionally (used in denoting the past time, when the non-completion of the action is to be understood).",
    "Sūtra 3.3.142: garhaayaamladapijaatvoh (गर्हायां लडपिजात्वोः) — The affix लट् (Present Tense) is used after a root when it has in composition with it the wordsअपि or जातु , the sense implied by the sentence being that of 'censure'.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.143: vibhaashaakathamilingcha (विभाषा कथमि लिङ् च) — The affix लिङ् (Benedictive) as well as लट् (Present Tense) is optionally used after a root when the word कथम् is in construction with it and censure is implied.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.144: kimvruttelinglrutau (किंवृत्ते लिङ्लृटौ) — The affixes लिङ् (Benedictive) and लृट् (I Future) come after a verb when the interrogative words like किम् etc. are in composition with it and censure is implied.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.145: anavakaptyamarshayorakimvruttepi (अनवकॢप्त्यमर्षयोरकिंवृत्तेऽपि) — When it is to be expressed that somebody hold that something is not likely to take place or is not to be tolerated, the Potential and the I Future are used, even without the Interrogative Pronoun.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.146: kimkilaastyartheshulrut (किंकिलास्त्यर्थेषु लृट्) — The affix लृट् (I Future) is used after a root when the words किंकिल or those having the sense of अस्ति 'he is' are in construction with it (when the action is not likely to occur, or is not to be tolerated).",
    "Sūtra 3.3.147: jaatuyadorling (जातुयदोर्लिङ्) — The affix लिङ् (Benedictive) comes after a root, the words जातु and यत् being in construction with it, when the sense is that the action is not believed to be likely or is not to be tolerated.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.148: yachchayatrayoh (यच्चयत्रयोः) — The affix लिङ् (Benedictive) comes after a root in all tenses when the words यच्च and यत्र are in composition with it, provided that censure is implied.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.149: garhaayaamcha (गर्हायां च) — The affix लिङ् (Benedictive) comes in all tenses when the words यच्च and यत्र are in composition with it, provided that censure is implied.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.150: chitreekaranecha (चित्रीकरणे च) — The affix लिङ् (Benedictive) comes in all tenses when used with the words यच्च and यत्र and the sense implied is that of 'wonder'.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.151: sheshelrudayadau (शेषे लृडयदौ) — In all the cases when 'wonder' is implied by word other than यच्च and यत्र , the affix लृट् (I Future) is used after a root, except when the word यदि is used.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.152: utaapyohasamarthayorling (उताप्योः समर्थयोर्लिङ्) — The affix लिङ् (Benedictive) comes after a verb in all tenses when the words उत and अपि , both having the same meaning, are in composition. ",
    "Sūtra 3.3.153: kaamapravedanekachchiti (कामप्रवेदनेऽकच्चिति) — The affix लिङ् (Benedictive) comes after a root, in expressing or making known of a wish, except when the word कच्चित् is in composition with it.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.154: sambhavaanelamitichetsiddhaaprayoge (सम्भावनेऽलमिति चेत् सिद्धाप्रयोगे) — The affix लिङ् (Benedictive) is used after a root, when the expectation (of a person or thing being able or competent to do or suffer the action denoted by the verb is implied (or expressed by any other word used along with them) than 'alarm'.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.155: vibhaashaadhaatausambhaavanavachaneyadi (विभाषा धातौ सम्भावनवचनेऽयदि) — The affix लिङ् (Benedictive) is optionally used after a verb when it has another verb which expresses 'expectation' in construction with it, but not so when the word यत् is used.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.156: hetuhetumatorling (हेतुहेतुमतोर्लिङ्) — The affix लिङ् (Benedictive) is optionally used after those verbs which express the condition and its consequence.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.157: ichchhaartheshulinglotau (इच्छार्थेषु लिङ्लोटौ) — The affixes लिङ् (Benedictive) and लोट् (Imperative) are used after a root when another verb having the same sense of 'wishing' is in construction with it.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.158: samaanakartrukeshutumun (समानकर्तृकेषु तुमुन्) — The affix तुमुन् comes after a verb when another verb meaning 'to wish' is in construction, provided that the agent of both the verbs is the same.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.159: lingcha (लिङ् च) — The affix लिङ् (Benedictive) is used after a verb when the verbs meaning 'to wish' are in construction with it and the agent of both the verbs is the same.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.160: ichchhaarthebhyovibhaashaavartamaane (इच्छार्थेभ्यो विभाषा वर्तमाने) — After roots meaning 'to wish' the लिङ् (Benedictive) is optionally used denoting the present time.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.161: vidhinimantranaamantranaadheeshtasamprashnapraarthaneshuling (विधिनिमन्त्रणामन्त्रणाधीष्टसंप्रश्नप्रार्थनेषु लिङ्) — The affix लिङ् (Benedictive) comes after a verb when the agent either 1. commands 2. invites 3. permits 4. politely expresses a wish 6. asks questions or 7. prays.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.162: lotcha (लोट् च) — The affix लोट् (Imperative) is used after a root in the sense of commanding etc.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.163: praishaatisargapraaptakaaleshukrutyaashcha (प्रैषातिसर्गप्राप्तकालेषु कृत्याश्च) — The affixes called कृत्य and the affix लोट् (Imperative) come also after verbs, in the sense of direction, granting permission and proper (particular) time.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.164: lingchordhvamauhoortike (लिङ् चोर्ध्वमौहूर्तिके) — The affix लिङ् (Benedictive) (as well as कृत्य and लोट् (Imperative) ) is used (under similar circumstances in the sense of 1. direction 2. permission etc.) when the time is future by a मुहूर्त (48 minutes or an Indian hour); (or the Potential may be used as well when it signifies 'at this very moment').",
    "Sūtra 3.3.165: smelot (स्मे लोट्) — The affix लोट् (Imperative) comes after a verb when the word स्म is in composition (when the sense is that of 'direction', permission etc.) and referring to time by a मुहूर्त (48 minutes or an Indian hour).",
    "Sūtra 3.3.166: adheeshtecha (अधीष्टे च) — And when 'wish' is meant ( the लोट् (Imperative) may be used when the word स्म is in composition with the verb.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.167: kaalasamayavelaasutumun (कालसमयवेलासु तुमुन्) — The affix तुमुन् comes after a root when the words 1. काल 2. समय 3. वेला (all meaning time) are in composition.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.168: lingyadi (लिङ् यदि) — The affix लिङ् (Benedictive) comes after a root when the word यद् is in composition and the words 1. काल 2. समय 3. वेला occur in construction.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.169: arhekrutyatruchashcha (अर्हे कृत्यतृचश्च) — The affixes कृत्य and the affix तृच are added to a root when fitness as regards the agent is implied (as well as in the affix लिङ् (Benedictive) ).",
    "Sūtra 3.3.170: aavashyakaadhamarnyayorninih (आवश्यकाधमर्ण्ययोर्णिनिः) — The affix णिनि is added to the root in denoting agent, showing that there is some 'necessity' or 'indebtedness' or 'obligation' on the part of the agent in connection with the action denoted by the verb.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.171: krutyaashcha (कृत्याश्च) — The affixes called कृत्य also come after a root when the sense to be indicated is that of 'necessity' or 'obligation'.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.172: shakilingcha (शकि लिङ् च) — And the affix लिङ् (Benedictive) as well as the कृत्य affixes come after a verb when the sense is that of 'capability'.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.173: aashishilinglotau (आशिषि लिङ्लोटौ) — The affixes लिङ् (Benedictive) and लोट् (Imperative) come after a verb by which 'benediction' is intended.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.174: ktichktauchasamjnyaayaam (क्तिच्क्तौ च संज्ञायाम्) — The affixes क्तिच् and क्त are used after a root when benediction is intended, provided that the whole word so formed is an appellative.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.175: maangilung (माङि लुङ्) — The affixes लुङ् (Aorist) comes after a verb when the word माण् is used in connection with it.",
    "Sūtra 3.3.176: smottarelangcha (स्मोत्तरे लङ् च) — When the word मान is followed by स्म the affix लङ् (Imperfect Tense) as well as लुङ् (Aorist) may be used after a verbal root.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.1: dhaatusambandhepratyayaah (धातुसम्बन्धे प्रत्ययाः) — When there is a syntactical relation between the senses of the verbs, the affixes are valid, even in denoting time other than that for which they have been specifically enjoined.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.2: kriyaasamabhihaarelotlotohisvauvaachatadhvamoh (क्रियासमभिहारे लोट्; लोटो हिस्वौ; वा च तध्वमोः) — When the (frequency of) repetition of an action is indicated, the affix लोट् (Imperative) is added to the root and the verb is repeated. And the affixes हि and स्व or the affixes त and ध्वम् are the substitutes of लोट् (Imperative).",
    "Sūtra 3.4.3: samuchchayenyatarasyaam (समुच्चयेऽन्यतरस्याम्) — The affix लोट् (Imperative) is similarly added to the root optionally when several themes follow one after another.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.4: yathaavidhyanuprayogahapoorvasmin (यथाविध्यनुप्रयोगः पूर्वस्मिन्) — In the first case -- क्रियासमभिहारे लोट्, लोटो हिस्वौ, वा च तध्वमोः [[3.4.2]] the same verb must be used in the subsequent clause, as the verb which was put in the लोट् (Imperative Mood) .",
    "Sūtra 3.4.5: samuchchayesaamaanyavachanasya (समुच्चये सामान्यवचनस्य) — In the second case -- समुच्चयेऽन्यतरस्याम् [[3.4.3]], where many actions are spoken of together, the verb that is made to follow, should be such as has the sense common to all those verbs.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.6: chhandasilunglanglitah (छन्दसि लुङ्लङ्लिटः) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas), the लुङ् (Aorist), लङ् (Imperfect Tense) and लिट् (Perfect Tense) are optionally used in all tenses, in relation to verbs.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.7: lingarthelet (लिङर्थे लेट्) — The affix लेट् (Vedic Subjunctive) is optionally used the छन्दस् (Vedas) wherever the लिङ् (Benedictive) can be used.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.8: upasamvaadaashangkayoshcha (उपसंवादाशङ्कयोश्च) — Where a contingent promise (a reciprocal agreement) or apprehension is implied, the affix लेट् (Vedic Subjunctive) is used after a root in the छन्दस् (Vedas) Literature.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.9: tumarthesesenaseasenksekasenadhyaiadhyainkadhyaikadhyainshadhyaishadhyaintavaitavengtavenah (तुमर्थे सेसेनसेऽसेन्क्सेकसेनध्यैअध्यैन्कध्यैकध्यैन्शध्यैशध्यैन्तवैतवेङ्तवेनः) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas) the following affixes come after the roots with the force of the affix तुमुन् , viz. 1. से 2. सेन् 3. असे 4. असेन् 5. क्से 6. क्सेन् 7. अध्यै 8. अध्यैन् 9. कध्यै 10. कध्यैन् 11. शाध्यै 12. शाध्यैन् 13. तवै 14. तवै 15. तवैन् ।",
    "Sūtra 3.4.10: prayairohishyaiavyathishyai (प्रयै रोहिष्यै अव्यथिष्यै) — The words 1. प्रयै 2. रोहिष्यै 3. अव्यथिष्यै are irregularly formed Vedic Infinitives.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.11: drushevikhyecha (दृशे विख्ये च) — The words 1. दृशे 2. विख्ये are anomalous Vedic Infinitives.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.12: shakinamulkamulau (शकि णमुल्कमुलौ) — The affixes णमुल् and कमुल् are added to roots in the छन्दस् (Vedas) to form Infinitives, when they are governed by the verb शक् 'to be able'.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.13: eeshvaretosunkasunau (ईश्वरे तोसुन्कसुनौ) — The affixes तोसुन् and कसुन् are added to roots in the छन्दस् (Vedas) to form Infinitives, when the word ईश्वर is in composition.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.14: krutyaarthetavaikenkenyatvanah (कृत्यार्थे तवैकेन्केन्यत्वनः) — The affixes 1. तवै 2. केन् 3. केन्य 4. त्वन् are added to roots in the छन्दस् (Vedas), in the sense of कृत्य-affixes.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.15: avachakshecha (अवचक्षे च) — The word of अवचक्षे is an anomalous passive participle in the छन्दस् (Vedas).",
    "Sūtra 3.4.16: bhaavalakshanesthenkrunyvadicharihutamijanibhyastosun (भावलक्षणे स्थेण्कृञ्वदिचरिहुतमिजनिभ्यस्तोसुन्) — The affix तोसुन् comes in the छन्दस् (Vedas) after the following verbs, when mere name of the action is indicated viz. 1. स्था 'to stand' 2. इण् 'to go' 3. कृञ् 'to make' 4. वद् 'to speak' 5. चर् 'to go, to walk' 6. हु 'to sacrifice' 7. तम् 'to grow tired' 8. जन् 'to produce' ।",
    "Sūtra 3.4.17: srupitrudohakasun (सृपितृदोः कसुन्) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas), the affix कसुन् comes after the verbs 1. सृप् 'to creep' 2. तृद् 'to injure' , in the sense of Infinitives indicating name of action.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.18: alangkhalvohapratishedhayohapraachaamktvaa (अलङ्खल्वोः प्रतिषेधयोः प्राचां क्त्वा) — According to the opinion of the Eastern Grammarians, the affix क्त्वा comes after the verb, when there are in combination with it, the words अलम् and खलु expressing the sense of prohibition.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.19: udeechaammaangovyateehaare (उदीचां माङो व्यतीहारे) — According to the opinion of the Eastern Grammarians, the affix क्त्वा is added to the root मेन् 'to exchange' when the sense is that of interchange, (though the action denoted by the former word is not prior to the action denoted by the latter word).",
    "Sūtra 3.4.20: paraavarayogecha (परावरयोगे च) — The affix क्त्वा is added to a root, to denote what is situated on the side - पर or on this side of something - अवर।",
    "Sūtra 3.4.21: samaanakartrukayohapoorvakaale (समानकर्तृकयोः पूर्वकाले) — When two actions have the same agent, the affix क्त्वा comes after that verb which takes place in time anterior to that of the other (i.e. Absolutive in त्व refers to that action which precedes in time).",
    "Sūtra 3.4.22: aabheekshnyenamulcha (आभीक्ष्ण्ये णमुल् च) — The affixes णमुल् and क्त्वा come after a root when reiteration is to be expressed.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.23: nayadyanaakaangkshe (न यद्यनाकाङ्क्षे) — The affixes णमुल् and क्त्वा are not added to a root when the word यद् is used in a simple sentence which does not depend upon another to complete the sense.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.24: vibhaashaagreprathamapoorveshu (विभाषाऽग्रेप्रथमपूर्वेषु) — The affixes णमुल् and क्त्वा come optionally after that verb which denotes the prior action, when both verbs have the same agent, provided that the following words are in composition - 1. अग्रे 2. प्रथम 3. पूर्व।",
    "Sūtra 3.4.25: karmanyaakroshekrunyahakhamuny (कर्मण्याक्रोशे कृञः खमुञ्) — The affix खमुञ् is added to the verb कृ 'to make', when a word in the Accusative -2nd case is in construction with it, if the sense intended implies 'abuse'.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.26: svaaduminamul (स्वादुमि णमुल्) — (When the actions signified by the verbs कृ 'to make' and another have the same agent), the affix णमुल् is added to the verb कृ 'to make' which is concerned about a time anterior to that of the other), provided that a word signifying 'sweet' is in composition.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.27: anyathaivamkathamitthamsusiddhaaprayogashchet (अन्यथैवंकथमित्थंसु सिद्धाप्रयोगश्चेत्) — When the words 1. अन्यथा 'otherwise' 2. एवम् 'so' 3. कथम् 'how' 4. इत्थम् 'thus' are compounded with the verb, the णमुल् comes after कृ 'to make', if it be such that its omission would be unobjectionable.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.28: yathaatathayorasooyaaprativachane (यथातथयोरसूयाप्रतिवचने) — The affix णमुल् is added to the root कृ 'to make', the words 1. यथा 2. तथा being compounded with it when an angry reply is made (if the omission of कृञ् is unobjectionable).",
    "Sūtra 3.4.29: karmanidrushividohasaakalye (कर्मणि दृशिविदोः साकल्ये) — When the object is compounded with it, the verb दृश् 'to see' or विद् 'to know' takes the affix णमुल् to denote the total number of such objects.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.30: yaavativindajeevoh (यावति विन्दजीवोः) — The affix णमुल् comes after the verb विद् 'to know' and जीव् 'to live' when the word यावत् is combined with them.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.31: charmodarayohapooreh (चर्मोदरयोः पूरेः) — The affix णमुल् comes after the verb पुर् 'to fill' when the word चर्मन् and उदर् are compounded with it.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.32: varshapramaanoolopashchaasyaanyatarasyaam (वर्षप्रमाण ऊलोपश्चास्यान्यतरस्याम्) — The affix णमुल् comes after the verb पुर् 'to fill' when the word so formed expresses a measure of rainfall and optionally the long ऊ of this पुर् is elided.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.33: cheleknopeh (चेले क्नोपेः) — The affix णमुल् comes after the causative of the root क्नूय् 'to wet', when there is compounded with a noun denoting 'clothing', in the Accusative -2nd case, as an उपपद , if the whole word so formed expresses a measure of the rainfall.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.34: nimoolasamoolayohakashah (निमूलसमूलयोः कषः) — The affix णमुल् comes after the verb कष् 'to rub' when the words निमूल and समूल are compounded with it in the Accusative -2nd case.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.35: shushkachoornarooksheshupishah (शुष्कचूर्णरूक्षेषु पिषः) — The affix णमुल् comes after the verb पिष् 'to grind', when the words 1. शुष्क 'dry' 2. चूर्ण 'powder' 3. रूक्षे 'dry', in the Accusative -2nd case are compounded with it.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.36: samoolaakrutajeeveshuhankrunygrahah (समूलाकृतजीवेषु हन्कृञ्ग्रहः) — The affix णमुल् comes after the verbs 1. हन् 'to kill' 2. कृ 'to make' 3. ग्रह् 'to seize', when the words 1. समूल 2. आकृत 3. जीव in the Accusative -2nd case are respectively compounded with them.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.37: karanehanah (करणे हनः) — The affix णमुल् comes after the verb हन् 'to kill' when a word in the Instrumental -3rd case is in composition with it.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.38: snehanepishah (स्नेहने पिषः) — The affix णमुल् comes after the verb पिष् 'to grind' when a word in the Instrumental -3rd case denoting 'liquid' is in composition.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.39: hastevarttigrahoh (हस्ते वर्त्तिग्रहोः) — The affix णमुल् comes after the verbs वर्त्ति (the causative of वृत्) and ग्रह् 'to seize' when a word denoting 'hand' in the Instrumental -3rd case, is in composition.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.40: svepushah (स्वे पुषः) — The affix णमुल् comes after the verb पुष् 'to feed' when a word in the Instrumental -3rd case having the sense of स्व is in composition.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.41: adhikaranebandhah (अधिकरणे बन्धः) — The affix णमुल् comes after the बन्ध् 'to bind' when a word expressing location is in construction with it.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.42: samjnyaayaam (संज्ञायाम्) — The affix णमुल् comes after the बन्ध् 'to bind' when a word so formed denotes an appellative.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.43: kartrorjeevapurushayornashivahoh (कर्त्रोर्जीवपुरुषयोर्नशिवहोः) — The affix णमुल् comes after the roots नश् 'to destroy' and वह् 'to carry' when the words जीव 'life' and पुरुष 'person' expressing the agent of these verbs, are respectively in construction with them.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.44: oordhveshushipooroh (ऊर्ध्वे शुषिपूरोः) — The affix णमुल् comes after the roots शुष् 'to dry' and पूर् 'to fill' when the word ऊर्ध्व denoting an agent is in composition with them.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.45: upamaanekarmanicha (उपमाने कर्मणि च) — The affix णमुल् comes after a root when an object or an agent denoting similitude is in composition with it.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.46: kashaadishuyathaavidhyanuprayogah (कषादिषु यथाविध्यनुप्रयोगः) — The same verb should be used after the gerunds formed from the verbs कष् 'to rub' etc. as the verb from which the gerund is derived.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.47: upadamshastruteeyaayaam (उपदंशस्तृतीयायाम्) — The affix णमुल् comes after a root दंश् 'to bite' preceded by the preposition उप when a word ending with the Instrumental -3rd case is in composition with it..",
    "Sūtra 3.4.48: himsaarthaanaamchasamaanakarmakaanaam (हिंसार्थानां च समानकर्मकाणाम्) — The affix णमुल् comes after the roots having the sense of हिंस 'to injure, to strike' when the object of this gerund is the same as the object of the main verb and when the noun with which it is compounded ends with the Instrumental -3rd case-affix.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.49: saptamyaamchopapeedarudhakarshah (सप्तम्यां चोपपीडरुधकर्षः) — The affix णमुल् comes after the roots 1. पीड् 'to press' 2. रुद्ध् 'to obstruct' 3. कृष् 'to draw' when they are preceded by the preposition उप and when they are compounded with nouns ending with the Locative -7th case-affix.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.50: samaasattau (समासत्तौ) — (The affix णमुल् comes after a root when a word in the Locative -7th case or Instrumental -3rd case is in composition with it) and when immediate contiguity is intended i.e. 'to fall together by the ears'.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.51: pramaanecha (प्रमाणे च) — The affix णमुल् comes after a root when a noun in the Instrumental -3rd case or Locative -7th case is in composition with it and when measure of length is intended.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.52: apaadaanepareepsaayaam (अपादाने परीप्सायाम्) — The affix णमुल् is added to the root when a noun in the Ablative -5th case is in composition and when 'haste' is intended.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.53: dviteeyaayaamcha (द्वितीयायां च) — The affix णमुल् is added to the root when a word in the Accusative -2nd case is in composition and when 'haste' is intended.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.54: svaanggedhruve (स्वाङ्गेऽध्रुवे) — The affix णमुल् comes after a verb when a word in the Accusative -2nd case is in composition, signifying the limbs of one's own body, when the limb is such that its loss will not destroy life.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.55: pariklishyamaanecha (परिक्लिश्यमाने च) — The affix णमुल् comes after a root when a word in the Accusative -2nd case denoting a limb of one's own body, which is completely afflicted by the action, is in composition.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.56: vishipatipadiskandaamvyaapyamaanaasevyamaanayoh (विशिपतिपदिस्कन्दां व्याप्यमानासेव्यमानयोः) — The affix णमुल् comes after the verbs 1. विश् 'to enter' 2. पत् 'to fall' 3. पद् 'to pace, to go' 4. स्कन्द् 'to leap', when a word in Accusative -2nd case is in composition and when the sense denoted is that of complete pervasion and total absorption.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.57: asyatitrushohakriyaantarekaaleshu (अस्यतितृषोः क्रियाऽन्तरे कालेषु) — The affix णमुल् comes after the verbs 1. अस् 'to throw' 2. तृष् 'to be thirsty' when it is intended to express an intermission of the action denoted by the root, provided that a word in the Accusative -2nd case denoting time is in composition.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.58: naamnyaadishigrahoh (नाम्न्यादिशिग्रहोः) — The affix णमुल् comes after the verbs 1. आदिश् 2. ग्रह् 'to seize' when the word नामन् 'name' in the Accusative -2nd case is in composition.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.59: avyayeyathaabhipretaakhyaanekrunyahaktvaanamulau (अव्ययेऽयथाभिप्रेताख्याने कृञः क्त्वाणमुलौ) — The affixes क्तवा and णमुल् come after the root कृ 'to make' when an indeclinable word in composition with it and the meaning is the communication of anything in a disagreeable or undesired way.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.60: tiryachyapavarge (तिर्यच्यपवर्गे) — The affixes क्तवा and णमुल् come after the root कृ 'to make' when the word त्रियक् is in composition in the sense of 'carrying to the end'.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.61: svaanggetaspratyayekrubhvoh (स्वाङ्गे तस्प्रत्यये कृभ्वोः) — The affixes क्तवा and णमुल् are added to the roots कृ 'to make' and भू 'to be', in composition with a word denoting a member of one's own body when the affix तस् is joined thereto.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.62: naadhaarthapratyayechvyarthe (नाधाऽर्थप्रत्यये च्व्यर्थे) — The affixes क्तवा and णमुल् are added to the roots कृ 'to make' and भू 'to be', when a word ending in the affix ना -- विनञ्भ्यां नानाञौ नसह [[5.2.27]], or in an affix having the force of धा -- संख्याया विधाऽर्थे धा [[5.3.42]], or having the sense of the affix च्वि 'to make or to become something with it had not been before' -- अभूततद्भावे कृभ्वस्तियोगे सम्पद्यकर्तरि च्विः [[5.4.50]], is in composition.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.63: tooshneemibhuvah (तूष्णीमि भुवः) — The affixes क्तवा and णमुल् are added to the roots भू 'to be', when the word तूष्णीम् 'silently' is in composition.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.64: anvachyaanulomye (अन्वच्यानुलोम्ये) — The affixes क्तवा and णमुल् come after the root भू 'to be' when the word अन्वक् in the sense of being favourably disposed, is in composition.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.65: shakadhrushajnyaaglaaghatarabhalabhakramasahaarhaastyartheshutumun (शकधृषज्ञाग्लाघटरभलभक्रमसहार्हास्त्यर्थेषु तुमुन्) — The affix तुमुन् is added to every verb when another verb having the sense of 1. शक् 'to be able' 2. धृष् 'to make bold' 3. ज्ञा 'to know' 4. ग्लै 'to be weary' 5. घट् 'to strive' 6. रभ् 'to begin' 7. लभ् 'to get' 8. क्रम् 'to set about' 9. सह् 'to bear' 10. अर्ह् 'to be pleased or to condescend' 11. अस् 'to be'.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.66: paryaaptivachaneshvalamartheshu (पर्याप्तिवचनेष्वलमर्थेषु) — The affix तुमुन् comes after a verb having in composition with it अलम् and its synonyms when these words express to be capable of something.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.67: kartarikrut (कर्तरि कृत्) — The affixes called कृत् are used in the sense of an agent.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.68: bhavyageyapravachaneeyopasthaaneeyajanyaaplaavyaapaatyaavaa (भव्यगेयप्रवचनीयोपस्थानीयजन्याप्लाव्यापात्या वा) — The words 1. भव्य 2. गेय 3. प्रवचनीय 3. उपस्थानीय 4. जन्य 5. आप्लाव्य 6. आपात्य may be optionally be used to denote the agent.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.69: lahakarmanichabhaavechaakarmakebhyah (लः कर्मणि च भावे चाकर्मकेभ्यः) — The tense affixes called ल are used in denoting the object and the agent and after intransitive verbs, they denote the action as well as the agent.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.70: tayorevakrutyaktakhalarthaah (तयोरेव कृत्यक्तखलर्थाः) — The affixes called कृत्य and the affix called क्त and those that have the sense of खल् have only these last two senses, viz. an action and an object (भाव and कर्म).",
    "Sūtra 3.4.71: adikarmaniktahakartaricha (आदिकर्मणि क्तः कर्तरि च) — The affix क्त also denotes the agent when it expresses a beginning of an action.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.72: gatyarthaakarmakashlishasheengsthaasavasajanaruhajeeryatibhyashcha (गत्यर्थाकर्मकश्लिषशीङ्स्थाऽऽसवसजनरुहजीर्यतिभ्यश्च) — The affix क्त is used in denoting the agent as well as the act and the object after verbs implying motion after intransitive roots and after the verbs 1. श्लिष् 'to embrace' 2. शि 'to lie down' 3. स्था 'to stand' 4. आस् 'to sit' 5. वस् 'to dwell' 6. जन् 'to produce' 7. रुह् 'to mount' 8. जृ 'to grow old'.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.73: daashagoghnausampradaane (दाशगोघ्नौ सम्प्रदाने) — The word दाश and गोघ्न are irregularly formed and the affix in these denotes the idea of the Dative or Recipient.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.74: bheemaadayopaadaane (भीमादयोऽपादाने) — The words भीम etc. are irregularly formed and denote ablation.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.75: taabhyaamanyatronaadayah (ताभ्यामन्यत्रोणादयः) — The words formed by उणादि affixes denote other ideas other than these two - 1. Reciepient 2. Ablation.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.76: ktodhikaranechadhrauvyagatipratyavasaanaarthebhyah (क्तोऽधिकरणे च ध्रौव्यगतिप्रत्यवसानार्थेभ्यः) — The affix क्त which is ordained after roots denoting fixedness (to cling to a place), motion and taking gives the sense of location as well.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.77: lasya (लस्य) — In the place of ल will be substituted the affixes we shall announce hereafter.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.78: tiptasjhisipthasthamibvasmastaataamjhathaasaathaamdhvamidvahimahing (तिप्तस्झिसिप्थस्थमिब्वस्मस् तातांझथासाथांध्वमिड्वहिमहिङ्) — The following are the substitutes of ल - तिप् - तस् - झि - सिप् - थस् - थ - मिप् - वस् - मस् - त - आताम् - झ - थास् - आथाम् - ध्वम् - इट् - वहि - महिङ् ।",
    "Sūtra 3.4.79: titaatmanepadaanaamtere (टित आत्मनेपदानां टेरे) — The substitute ए replaces he last vowel, with the consonant that follows it, of the आत्मनेपद substitutes of that ल which has an indicatory ट्।",
    "Sūtra 3.4.80: thaasasse (थासस्से) — The word से is the substitute of थास् in those tenses that have an indicatory ट्।",
    "Sūtra 3.4.81: litastajhayoreshirech (लिटस्तझयोरेशिरेच्) — The words एश् and इरेच् are the substitutes of ट and झ respectively in the लिट् (Perfect Tense).",
    "Sūtra 3.4.82: parasmaipadaanaamnalatususthalathusanalvamaah (परस्मैपदानां णलतुसुस्थलथुसणल्वमाः) — In the room of the परस्मैपद affixes, the following are substituted in the लिट् (Perfect Tense). Singular - णल् (अ), थल् (थ), णल् (अ). Dual - अतुस् (अतुः), अथुस् (अथुः), व (व). Plural - उस् (उः) , अ (अ), म (म).",
    "Sūtra 3.4.83: vidolatovaa (विदो लटो वा) — The above nine affixes of the लिट् (Perfect Tense) are optionally added in the लट् (Present Tense) also after the verb विद् 'to know'.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.84: bruvahapanychaanaamaaditaahobruvah (ब्रुवः पञ्चानामादित आहो ब्रुवः) — Instead of the first 5 tense-affixes in the लट् (Present Tense) coming after the verb ब्रु 'to speak' there may optionally be the affixes of the लिट् (Perfect Tense) ; आह being at the same time the substitute in the room of ब्रु 'to speak'.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.85: lotolangvat (लोटो लङ्वत्) — The personal endings of the लोट् (Imperative Mood) are as those of the लङ् (Imperfect Tense).",
    "Sūtra 3.4.86: eruh (एरुः) — In the लोट् (Imperative Mood) उ is the substitute of इ।",
    "Sūtra 3.4.87: serhyapichcha (सेर्ह्यपिच्च) — In the लोट् (Imperative Mood) , हि is substituted for सि and this has not the indicatory प् of सिप् , i.e. it is acutely accented.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.88: vaachhandasi (वा छन्दसि) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas) the substitute of हि is optionally treated as not having an indicatory प्।",
    "Sūtra 3.4.89: mernih (मेर्निः) — In the लोट् (Imperative Mood) नि is substituted for the affix मि।",
    "Sūtra 3.4.90: aametah (आमेतः) — In the लोट् (Imperative Mood) आम् is substituted for what would have substituted otherwise ए by टित आत्मनेपदानां टेरे [[3.4.79]].",
    "Sūtra 3.4.91: savaabhyaamvaamau (सवाभ्यां वामौ) — For such an ए coming after स् , is substituted व् and for that coming after व् , is substituted अम् , in the (Imperative Mood).",
    "Sūtra 3.4.92: aaduttamasyapichcha (आडुत्तमस्य पिच्च) — In the लोट् (Imperative Mood) आट् is the augment of the affixes the first person and the termination is as if it had an indicatory प्।",
    "Sūtra 3.4.93: etai (एत ऐ) — The ऐ is substituted for ए forming part of the affixes of the first person of the लोट् (Imperative Mood).",
    "Sūtra 3.4.94: letodaatau (लेटोऽडाटौ) — The augments अट् and आट् are added to the तिङ् (Personal Endings) of the लेट् (Vedic Subjunctive).",
    "Sūtra 3.4.95: aatai (आत ऐ) — In the लेट् (Vedic Subjunctive) ऐ is the substitute of आ in the first and second person dual of the आत्मनेपद ।",
    "Sūtra 3.4.96: vaitonyatra (वैतोऽन्यत्र) — In the लेट् (Vedic Subjunctive) ऐ is optionally the substitute of ए in other places then those mentioned in the last sūtra.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.97: itashchalopahaparasmaipadeshu (इतश्च लोपः परस्मैपदेषु) — In the परस्मैपद affixes the इ is optionally elided in the लेट् (Vedic Subjunctive).",
    "Sūtra 3.4.98: suttamasya (स उत्तमस्य) — The स् of the first person is optionally elided in the लेट् (Vedic Subjunctive).",
    "Sūtra 3.4.99: nityamngitah (नित्यं ङितः) — There is always elision of the स् of the first person of the affixes that come in the room of that ल which has an indicatory ङ्।",
    "Sūtra 3.4.100: itashcha (इतश्च) — And there is elision of the इ of that परस्मैपद affix which is the substitute of a ल having an indicatory ङ्।",
    "Sūtra 3.4.101: tasthasthamipaamtaamtamtaamah (तस्थस्थमिपां तांतंतामः) — The affixes 1. ताम् 2. तम् 3. त 4. आम् are the substitutes of the four affixes तस् , थस् , थ and मिप् respectively of any ल which has an indicatory ङ् ।",
    "Sūtra 3.4.102: lingasseeyut (लिङस्सीयुट्) — The तिङ् (Personal Endings) of the लिङ् (Benedictive) and the Potential take the augment स्युत् ।",
    "Sūtra 3.4.103: yaasutparasmaipadeshoodaattongichcha (यासुट् परस्मैपदेषूदात्तो ङिच्च) — When the परस्मैपद affixes of the Potential follow, then यासुट् acutely accented, is their augment and the termination is regarded as having an indicatory ङ्।",
    "Sūtra 3.4.104: kidaashishi (किदाशिषि) — The augment यासुट् comes after that लिङ् (Benedictive) also which denotes benediction and it is acutely accented and the substitutes of this लिङ् (Benedictive) are as they had an indicatory क्।",
    "Sūtra 3.4.105: jhasyaran (झस्य रन्) — The affix रन् is the substitute of झ in the लिङ् (Potential and Benedictive).",
    "Sūtra 3.4.106: itot (इटोऽत्) — The short अ is the substitute of इ of the आत्मनेपद first person singular in the Potential and Benedictive.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.107: suttithoh (सुट् तिथोः) — The augment सुट् is added to the following affixes त and थ when part of the affixes of the Potential and Benedictive.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.108: jherjus (झेर्जुस्) — In the Potential and Benedictive जुस् is the substitute of झि , the ending of the first person plural परस्मैपद ।",
    "Sūtra 3.4.109: sijabhyastavidibhyahacha (सिजभ्यस्तविदिभ्यश्च) — (In those tenses which are marked with an indicatory ङ् ) जुस् is the substitute of झि when it comes after an लुङ् (Aorist) in सिच् or the लङ् (Imperfect Tense) of a reduplicated verb or the root विद् 'to know'.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.110: aatah (आतः) — When सिच् is elided जुस् is the substitute of झि after a लुङ् (Aorist) stem which ends in long आ।",
    "Sūtra 3.4.111: langahashaakataayanasyaiva (लङः शाकटायनस्यैव) — In the opinion of शाकटायन only जुस् is the substitute of झि , in the लङ् (Imperfect Tense) of the roots which end in a long आ।",
    "Sūtra 3.4.112: dvishashcha (द्विषश्च) — In the opinion of शाकटायन only जुस् is the substitute of झि , in the लङ् (Imperfect Tense) after the verb द्विष् 'to hate'.",
    "Sūtra 3.4.113: tingshitsaarvadhaatukam (तिङ्शित्सार्वधातुकम्) — All the personal endings -- तिप्तस्झिसिप्थस्थमिब्वस्मस्तातांझथासाथांध्वमिड्वहिमहिङ् [[3.4.78]], and all affixes with an indicatory श् are called सार्वधातुक ।",
    "Sūtra 3.4.114: aardhadhatukamsheshah (आर्धधातुकं शेषः) — The remainder i.e. the affixes other than तिङ् (Personal Endings) and those with an indicatory श् sub-joined to a verbal root are called आर्द्धधातुक।",
    "Sūtra 3.4.115: litcha (लिट् च) — The तिङ् (Personal Endings) of the लिट् (Perfect Tense) are also called आर्द्धधातुक ।",
    "Sūtra 3.4.116: lingaashishi (लिङाशिषि) — When the sense is that of Benediction, the substitutes of लिङ् (Benedictive) are called आर्द्धधातुक i.e. the तिङ् (Personal Endings) of the लिङ् (Benedictive) are आर्द्धधातुक ।",
    "Sūtra 3.4.117: chhandasyubhayathaa (छन्दस्युभयथा) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas) this distinction of सार्वधातुक and आर्द्धधातुक is not always maintained and the affixes are promiscuously used.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.1: ngyaappraatipadikaat (ङ्याप्प्रातिपदिकात्) — (From this point forward up to the end of the Fifth Chapter, whatever we shall treat of, should be understood to come) after what ends with the feminine affixes ङी or आप् or after a प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stem).",
    "Sūtra 4.1.2: svaujasamautchhashtaabhyaambhisngebhyaambhyasngasibhyaambhyasngasosaamngyossup (स्वौजसमौट्छष्टाभ्याम्भिस्ङेभ्याम्भ्यस्ङसिभ्याम्भ्यस्ङसोसाङ्ङ्योस्सुप्) — (After what ends with the feminine terminations ङी or आप् or after a प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stem), the following case-affixes ae used for declension) - 1st - सु (स), औ , जस् (अस्)। 2nd - अम् , औट् (औ), शस् (अस्)। 3rd - टा (आ), भ्याम् , भिस् । 4th - ङे (ए), भ्याम् , भ्यस्। 5th - ङसि (अस्), भ्याम् , भ्यस्। 6th - ङस् (अस्), ओस् , आम्। 7th - ङि (इ), ओस् , सुप् (सु)।",
    "Sūtra 4.1.3: striyaam (स्त्रियाम्) — When the feminine nature is to be indicated the affixes which we shall treat of hereinafter must be used.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.4: ajaadyatashtaap (अजाद्यतष्टाप्) — The affix टाप् is used to indicate feminine nature after the प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stem) अज etc. and after the stems ending in short अ।",
    "Sūtra 4.1.5: runnebhyongeep (ऋन्नेभ्यो ङीप्) — The affix ङीप् is used in forming the feminine after प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stem) ending in ऋ or न्।",
    "Sūtra 4.1.6: ugitashcha (उगितश्च) — And after what has an indicatory उक् (उ , ऋ or ऌ) the affix ङीप् is used denoting a feminine.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.7: vanoracha (वनो र च) — The affix ङीप् is added, in forming the feminine to the stems that end in the syllable वन् , and र् is the substitute of the final such syllable.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.8: paadonyatarasyaam (पादोऽन्यतरस्याम्) — The affix ङीप् is optionally used in the feminine after a प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stem) ending with the word पाद्।",
    "Sūtra 4.1.9: taabruchi (टाबृचि) — The affix ङीप् is used in the feminine after a प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stem) ending with the word पाद् when the word denotes a verse of the ऋग्वेद।",
    "Sūtra 4.1.10: nashatsvasraadibhyah (न षट्स्वस्रादिभ्यः) — The feminine affixes are not used after the stems called षद् -- ष्णान्ता षट् [[1.1.24]] and after स्वस्र etc.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.11: manah (मनः) — The affix ङीप् is not used after a प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stem) ending in the syllable मन्।",
    "Sūtra 4.1.12: anobahuvreeheh (अनो बहुव्रीहेः) — The affix ङीप् is not used to denote the feminine after a बहुव्रीहि समास ending in अन्।",
    "Sūtra 4.1.13: daabubhaabhyaamanyatarasyaam (डाबुभाभ्यामन्यतरस्याम्) — The affix डाप् comes optionally after both - 1. प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stem) ending in अन् 2. बहुव्रीहि समास ।",
    "Sūtra 4.1.14: anupasarjanaat (अनुपसर्जनात्) — The following rules apply to a प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stem) which is not a subordinate term in a compound.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.15: tiddhaananydvayasajdaghnanymaatrachtayapthakthanykanykvarapah (टिड्ढाणञ्द्वयसज्दघ्नञ्मात्रच्तयप्ठक्ठञ्कञ्क्वरपः) — The affix ङीप् is added in the feminine after the प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stems) ending in short अ , if the affix with which it ends has an indicatory ट् or if the affix be ढ or अण् or अञ् or द्वयसच् or दघ्नच् or मात्रच् or तयप् or ठक् or ठञ् or कञ् or क्वरप्।",
    "Sūtra 4.1.16: yanyashcha (यञश्च) — The affix ङीप् is used in denoting the feminine after a प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stem) ending in यञ् -- गर्गादिभ्यो यञ् [[4.1.105]].",
    "Sūtra 4.1.17: praachaamshphataddhitah (प्राचां ष्फ तद्धितः) — In the opinion of the Eastern Grammarians, the affix ष्फ is used after what ends with the affix यञ् and it is to be regarded as a तद्धित-affix.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.18: sarvatralohitaadikatantebhyah (सर्वत्र लोहितादिकतन्तेभ्यः) — The affix ष्फ is invariably added in the feminine after the words beginning with लोहित and ending with क्त when they take the affix यञ्।",
    "Sūtra 4.1.19: kauravyamaandookaabhyaamcha (कौरव्यमाण्डूकाभ्यां च) — The affix ष्फ is added in the feminine after the words 1. कौरव्य and 2. माण्डूक।",
    "Sūtra 4.1.20: vayasiprathame (वयसि प्रथमे) — The affix ङीप् is used in the feminine after a प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stem) ending in अ and denoting early age.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.21: dvigoh (द्विगोः) — The affix ङीप् come in the feminine after a प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stem) ending in अ , which is द्विगु समास (Numeral Determinative Compound). ",
    "Sūtra 4.1.22: aparimaanabistaachitakambalyebhyonataddhitaluki (अपरिमाणबिस्ताचितकम्बल्येभ्यो न तद्धितलुकि) — The affix ङीप् is not used when a तद्धित affix is elided after a द्विगु समास (Numeral Determinative Compound) ending in a word not denoting a mass or measure; or in 1. बिस्त 2. आचित or 3. कम्बल्य।",
    "Sūtra 4.1.23: kaandaantaatkshetre (काण्डान्तात् क्षेत्रे) — The affix ङीप् is not used after an adjectival द्विगु समास (Numeral Determinative Compound) ending with the word काण्ड where the तद्धित affix is elided when the compound means field.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.24: purushaatpramaanenyatarasyaam (पुरुषात् प्रमाणेऽन्यतरस्याम्) — The affix ङीप् is not optionally used after a द्विगु समास (Numeral Determinative Compound) where the तद्धित affix is elided when the compound ends in the word पुरुष , referring to 'measure'.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.25: bahuvreeheroodhasongeesh (बहुव्रीहेरूधसो ङीष्) — The affix ङीप् is used in the feminine after a बहुव्रीहि समास ending in the word ऊधस् 'an udder'.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.26: samkhyaavyayaaderngeep (संख्याव्ययादेर्ङीप्) — The affix ङीप् comes in the feminine after a बहुव्रीहि समास ending in the word ऊधस् 'an udder', beginning with a Numeral or indeclinable.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.27: daamahaayanaantaachcha (दामहायनान्ताच्च) — The affix ङीप् comes in the feminine after a बहुव्रीहि समास beginning with a Numeral and ending with the words 1. दामन् 'a rope' and 2. हायन 'a year'.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.28: anupadhaalopinonyatarasyaam (अन उपधालोपिनोन्यतरस्याम्) — The affix ङीप् comes after that बहुव्रीहि समास which ending in the syllable अन् loses its penultimate अ।",
    "Sūtra 4.1.29: nityamsamjnyaachhandasoh (नित्यं संज्ञाछन्दसोः) — The affix ङीप् necessarily comes in the छन्दस् (Vedas) and in forming Names after that बहुव्रीहि समास which ending in the syllable अन् loses its penultimate अ।",
    "Sūtra 4.1.30: kevalamaamakabhaagadheyapaapaaparasamaanaaryakrutasumanggalabheshajaachcha (केवलमामकभागधेयपापापरसमानार्यकृत-सुमङ्गलभेषजाच्च) — The affix ङीप् necessarily comes denoting the feminine after the following प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stems) when used to express a Name or in the छन्दस् (Vedas).",
    "Sūtra 4.1.31: raatreshchaajasau (रात्रेश्चाजसौ) — The affix ङीप् comes after the word रात्रि in the छन्दस् (Vedas) and in denoting a Name except the affix जस् (1st - Nominative Case Plural) is added.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.32: antarvatpativatornuk (अन्तर्वत्पतिवतोर्नुक्) — The augment नुक् is added to the words अन्तर्वत् and पतिवत् when the affix ङीप् is added to form the feminine.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.33: patyurnoyajnyasamyoge (पत्युर्नो यज्ञसंयोगे) — The substitute न् replaces the final इ of पति before the feminine affix ङीप् when the word so formed means 'a wife' who takes part in the sacrifices of her husband.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.34: vibhaashaasapoorvasya (विभाषा सपूर्वस्य) — In forming the feminine with the affix ङीप् , न् is optionally the substitute of the final इ of पति when the latter is preceded by another vowel.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.35: nityamsapatnyaadishu (नित्यं सपत्न्यादिषु) — In forming the feminine with the affix ङीप् the word पति always takes the substitute न् in the words like सपत्नि etc.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.36: pootakratoraicha (पूतक्रतोरै च) — In forming the feminine, the letter ऐ is the substitute of the final word पूतक्तु when the affix ङीप् is added.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.37: vrushaakapyagnikusitakuseedaanaamudaattah (वृषाकप्यग्निकुसितकुसिदानामुदात्तः) — In forming the feminine with the affix ङीप् the letter ऐ having उदात्त accent is the substitute of the finals 1. वृषाकपि 2. अग्नि 3. कुसति and 3. कुसीद ।",
    "Sūtra 4.1.38: manorauvaa (मनोरौ वा) — In forming the feminine with the affix ङीप् , औ is optionally the substitute of the final मनु (as well as the उदात्त ऐ).",
    "Sūtra 4.1.39: varnaadanudaattaattopadhaattonah (वर्णादनुदात्तात्तोपधात्तो नः) — The affix ङीप् is optionally used after a प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stem) expressive of colour ending with a gravely accented vowel and having the letter त् as its penultimate letter and the letter न् is substituted in the room of त्।",
    "Sūtra 4.1.40: anyatongeesh (अन्यतो ङीष्) — The affix ङीष् is used in the feminine after every other word expressive of colour and ending with an अनुदात्त accent.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.41: shidgauraadibhyashcha (षिद्गौरादिभ्यश्च) — The affix ङीष् is used in forming the feminine after the words ending with affixes which have an indicatory ष् and after the words गौर etc.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.42: jaanapadakundagonasthalabhaajanaagakaalaneelakushakaamukakabaraadvruttyamatraavapanaakrutrimaashraanaasthaulyavarnaanaachchhaadanaayovikaaramaithunechchhaakeshavesheshu (जानपदकुण्डगोणस्थलभाजनागकालनीलकुशकामुककबराद्वृत्त्यमत्रावपनाकृत्रिमाश्राणास्थौल्यवर्णानाच्छादनायोविकारमैथुनेच्छाकेशवेशेषु) — The affix ङीष् is used after the 11 words जानपद etc. in the sense of 'profession' etc. 1. जानप् 2. कुण्ड 3. गोण 4. स्थल 5. भाज 6. नाग 7. काल 8. नील 9. कुश् 10. कामुक and 11 कबर ; the affix ङीष् is employed when the sense is that of 1. 'profession or living' 2. 'a bowl' 3. 'a sack or vessel for keeping grain' 4. 'a natural spot of ground' 5. 'a cooked food or rice-gruel' 6. 'stout' 7. 'black-coloured' 8. 'blue-coloured other than cloth' 9. 'a plough-share' 10. 'a libidinous female' 11. 'a fillet or braid of hair', respectively.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.43: shonaatpraachaam (शोणात् प्राचाम्) — The affix ङीष् is used in the feminine according to the opinion of the Eastern Grammarians after the word शोण।",
    "Sūtra 4.1.44: votogunavachanaat (वोतो गुणवचनात्) — The affix ङीष् is optionally used in the feminine after a word ending in short अ and being expressive of quality.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.45: bahvaadibhyashcha (बह्वादिभ्यश्च) — And the affix ङीष् is optionally used in the feminine after the words बहु etc.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.46: nityamchhandasi (नित्यं छन्दसि) — The affix ङीष् is always used in the छन्दस् (Vedas) in forming the feminine of the words बहु etc.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.47: bhuvashcha (भुवश्च) — The affix ङीष् is always used in the छन्दस् (Vedas) in forming the feminine after the word भु।",
    "Sūtra 4.1.48: pumyogaadaakhyaayaam (पुंयोगादाख्यायाम्) — The feminine affix ङीष् comes after a word when it expresses the name of a wife in relation to her husband.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.49: indravarunabhavasharvarudramrudahimaaranyayavayavanamaatulaachaaryaanaamaanuk (इन्द्रवरुणभवशर्वरुद्रमृडहिमारण्ययवयवनमातुलाचार्याणामानुक्) — The augment आनुक् is added to the Proper Nouns 1. इन्द्र 2. वरुण 3. भव 4. शर्व 5. रुद्र and 6. मृड and to the words 1. हिम 'snow' 3. अरण्य 'forest' 4. यव 'barely' 5. यवन 'a Yavana' 6. मातुल 'a maternal uncle' and 7. आचार्य 'a perceptor', before the feminine affix ङीष्।",
    "Sūtra 4.1.50: kreetaatkaranapoorvaat (क्रीतात् करणपूर्वात्) — The affix ङीष् is used in the feminine after a compound word ending in क्रीत , the first member of the compound being the name of the means wherewith the thing is bought.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.51: ktaadalpaakhyaayaam (क्तादल्पाख्यायाम्) — The affix ङीष् is used after a compound प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stem) in which a name denoting the means herewith, is the first member and the second member is a word formed by the Particle क्त when the sense is that of 'a small quantity'. ",
    "Sūtra 4.1.52: bahuvreeheshchaantodaattaat (बहुव्रीहेश्चान्तोदात्तात्) — The affix ङीष् is used in the feminine after that बहुव्रीहि समास which ending with a word formed by the affix क्त has an acute accent on the last syllable.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.53: asvaanggapoorvapadaadvaa (अस्वाङ्गपूर्वपदाद्वा) — The affix ङीष् is optionally used in the feminine after a बहुव्रीहि समास ending with the word in क्त having acute accent on the final, the antecedent word not being a word denoting a part of the body.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.54: svaanggaachchopasarjanaadasamyogopadhaat (स्वाङ्गाच्चोपसर्जनादसंयोगोपधात्) — And the feminine affix ङीष् comes optionally after what ends with the name of a part of the body when the word is a subordinate member in compound and has not a conjunct for its penultimate letter (i.e. the final अ is not preceded by a double consonant).",
    "Sūtra 4.1.55: naasikodaraushthajangghaadantakarnashrunggaachcha (नासिकोदरौष्ठजङ्घादन्तकर्णशृङ्गाच्च) — And the feminine ङीष् comes optionally after compounds ending with 1. नासिका 'a nose' 2. उदर 'belly' 3. ओष्ठ 'lip' 4. जंघा 'leg' 5. दन्त 'tooth' 6. कर्ण 'ear' and 7. शृङ्ग 'horn'.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.56: nakrodaadibahvachah (न क्रोडादिबह्वचः) — The feminine affix ङीष् does not come after a प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stem) which denoting a part of the body, belongs to the class क्रोडा 'the flank' etc., of a horse', nor when the word is a stem of more than two syllables.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.57: sahananyvidyamaanapoorvaachcha (सहनञ्विद्यमानपूर्वाच्च) — The affix ङीष् does not come in the feminine after a प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stem) denoting a part of the body when the word is subordinate in a compound, preceded by the word 1. सह 'with' 2. नञ् 'not' or 3. विद्यमान 'having'.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.58: nakhamukhaatsamjnyaayaam (नखमुखात् संज्ञायाम्) — The feminine affix ङीष् is not used after 1. नख 2. मुख when (the word at the end of which they stand) is a Name.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.59: deerghajihveechachchhandasi (दीर्घजिह्वी च च्छन्दसि) — The form दीर्घजिह्वी 'long-tongued' is irregularly formed in the छन्दस् (Vedas).",
    "Sūtra 4.1.60: dikpoorvapadaanngeep (दिक्पूर्वपदान्ङीप्) — The feminine affix ङीप् comes after a प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stem) which is preceded by a word signifying direction.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.61: vaahah (वाहः) — The feminine affix ङीष् comes after a प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stem) ending with the word वाह्।",
    "Sūtra 4.1.62: sakhyashishveetibhaashaayaam (सख्यशिश्वीति भाषायाम्) — The forms सखी and अशिश्वी are irregular forms ending in ङीष् found in secular (or vernacular as opposed to Vedic) Sanskrit.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.63: jaaterastreevishayaadayopadhaat (जातेरस्त्रीविषयादयोपधात्) — The feminine affix ङीष् comes after a word denoting a जाति or species when it does not express in its original meaning a feminine and which moreover has not the letter य् for its penultimate.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.64: paakakarnaparnapushpaphalamoolavaalottarapadaachcha (पाककर्णपर्णपुष्पफलमूलवालोत्तरपदाच्च) — And the feminine affix ङीष् comes after the प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stem) expressive of जाति , followed by the following 1. पाक 'cooked' 2. कर्ण 'ear' 3. पुष्प 'flower' 4. फल 'fruit' 5. मूल 'root' 6. बाल 'youth'",
    "Sūtra 4.1.65: itomanushyajaateh (इतो मनुष्यजातेः) — The feminine affix ङीष् comes after a प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stem) ending in short इ denoting classes or races of men.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.66: oongutah (ऊङुतः) — After a प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stem) ending in short उ , not having the letter य् as its penultimate letter and being expressive of races of men, the affix in the feminine is ऊङ्।",
    "Sūtra 4.1.67: baahvantaatsamjnyaayaam (बाह्वन्तात् संज्ञायाम्) — The feminine affix ऊङ् comes in denoting a Name after a प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stem) ending with the word बाहु।",
    "Sūtra 4.1.68: panggoshcha (पङ्गोश्च) — The feminine affix ऊङ् comes after the word पंगु 'lame'.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.69: ooroottarapadaadaupamye (ऊरूत्तरपदादौपम्ये) — When the feminine affix ऊङ् comes after a stem ending in ऊरु when comparison with something (expressed by the first term) is meant.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.70: samhitashaphalakshanavaamaadeshcha (संहितशफलक्षणवामादेश्च) — The feminine affix ऊङ् comes in the छन्दस् (Vedas) after the word ऊरु when the words 1. संहित 'accompanied or joined' 2. शफ 'a hoof' 3. लक्षण 'a mark' 4. वाम 'handsome' precede it.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.71: kadrukamandalvoshchhandasi (कद्रुकमण्डल्वोश्छन्दसि) — The feminine affix ऊङ् comes in the छन्दस् (Vedas) after the words 1. कद्रु 'tawny' 2. कमण्डलु 'a water pot'.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.72: samjnyaayaam (संज्ञायाम्) — The feminine affix ऊङ् comes in denoting a Name after the words 1. कद्रु 'tawny' 2. कमण्डलु 'a water pot'.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.73: shaarnggaravaadyanyongeen (शार्ङ्गरवाद्यञो ङीन्) — The feminine affix ङीन् comes after the words शार्ङ्गरव etc. and that which ends with the affix अञ्।",
    "Sūtra 4.1.74: yangashchaap (यङश्चाप्) — The feminine affix चाप् comes after a stem which is formed by the affix ञ्यङ् or ष्यङ्।",
    "Sūtra 4.1.75: aavatyaachcha (आवट्याच्च) — And the feminine affix चाप् comes after the word आवट्य।",
    "Sūtra 4.1.76: taddhitaah (तद्धिताः) — The तद्धित-affixes are treated of here after.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.77: yoonastih (यूनस्तिः) — The feminine affix ति comes after the प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stem) युवन् and this affix gets the name तद्धित।",
    "Sūtra 4.1.78: aninyoranaarshayorguroopottamayohashyanggotre (अणिञोरनार्षयोर्गुरूपोत्तमयोः ष्यङ् गोत्रे) — In Patronymics used in narrower sense (counting first from the grand-child), which are formed the affixes अण् and इञ् , the feminine is formed by substituting य (ष्यङ्) for the अ and इ of those affixes and adding the long आ under -- यङश्चाप् [[4.1.74]], provided that they do not denote ऋषि clans and have prosodially long syllable preceding the last syllable.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.79: gotraavayavaat (गोत्रावयवात्) — After a word denoting a non-principal गोत्र , ष्यङ् is the substitute of अण् and इञ् , the feminine, even though the syllable preceding the final be not prosodially long.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.80: kraudyaadibhyashcha (क्रौड्यादिभ्यश्च) — The affix ष्यङ् comes in the feminine after the words क्रौडि etc.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.81: daivayajnyishauchivrukshisaatyamugrikaantheviddhibhyonyatarasyaam (दैवयज्ञिशौचिवृक्षिसात्यमुग्रिकाण्ठेविद्धिभ्योऽन्यतरस्याम्) — The affix ष्यङ् optionally comes after the words 1. दैवयज्ञि 2. शौचिवृक्षि 3. सात्यमुग्रि and 4. काण्ठेविद्धि ।",
    "Sūtra 4.1.82: samarthaanaamprathamaadvaa (समर्थानां प्रथमाद्वा) — The तद्धित affixes, on the alternative of their being used at all, comes after the word that is signified by the first of the words in construction in a sūtra.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.83: praagdeevyaton (प्राग्दीव्यतोऽण्) — The affix अण् should be understood to come after whatever we shall teach hereafter up to sūtra तेन दीव्यति खनति जयति जितम् [[4.4.2]] etc.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.84: ashvapatyaadibhyashcha (अश्वपत्यादिभ्यश्च) — The affix अण् comes after the प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stem) अश्वपति etc., in the various mentioned senses antecedently up to तेन दीव्यति खनति जयति जितम् [[4.4.2]].",
    "Sūtra 4.1.85: dityadityaadityapatyuttarapadaannyah (दित्यदित्यादित्यपत्युत्तरपदाण्ण्यः) — The affix ण्य comes, in the various senses taught here-in-after antecedently to तेन दीव्यति खनति जयति जितम् [[4.4.2]] etc. after the Proper Names - 1. दिति 2. अदिति 3. आदित्य and that which has the word पति as its final member.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.86: utsaadibhyony (उत्सादिभ्योऽञ्) — The affix अञ् comes after the word उत्स etc. in the various senses taught antecedently to तेन दीव्यति खनति जयति जितम् [[4.4.2]].",
    "Sūtra 4.1.87: streepumsaabhyaamnanysnanyaubhavanaat (स्त्रीपुंसाभ्यां नञ्स्नञौ भवनात्) — The affixes नञ् and स्नञ् come after the words स्त्री and पुंस respectively, in the senses specified in the sūtra reckoning from this one as far as sūtra धान्यानां भवने क्षेत्रे खञ् [[5.2.1]].",
    "Sūtra 4.1.88: dvigorluganapatye (द्विगोर्लुगनपत्ये) — A तद्धित affix ordained to come on account of the relation of the words being that of a द्विगु समास (Numeral Determinative Compound) is elided by लुक् when it has the sense of the various affixes taught antecedent to तेन दीव्यति खनति जयति जितम् [[4.4.2]] etc., but not so, the affix having the sense of a गोत्र (Patronymic).",
    "Sūtra 4.1.89: gotrelugachi (गोत्रेऽलुगचि) — The लुक् elision of गोत्र (Patronymic) affixes in plural, which have been enjoined by sūtras यस्कादिभ्यो गोत्रे [[2.4.63]] etc. and the rest is prohibited, when the affix has an initial vowel and it has the sense of the various affixes taught antecedent to तेन दीव्यति खनति जयति जितम् [[4.4.2]].",
    "Sūtra 4.1.90: yooniluk (यूनि लुक्) — There is लुक् elision of the युवन् गोत्र (Patronymic) forming affix -- जीवति तु वंश्ये युवा [[4.1.163]], when a प्राग्दीव्यतीय affix beginning with a vowel is to be added.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.91: phakphinyoranyatarasyaam (फक्फिञोरन्यतरस्याम्) — There is optionally लुक् elision of the युवन् affixes फक् and फिञ् when a प्राग्दीव्यतीय affix beginning with a vowel is to be added.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.92: tasyaapatyam (तस्यापत्यम्) — The affix अण् mentioned in प्राग्दीव्यतोऽण् [[4.1.83]] and those which follow it denote 'the descendant of someone'.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.93: ekogotre (एको गोत्रे) — The one and the same affix is used when a more distant descendant, how low-so-ever, is to be denoted.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.94: gotraadyoonyastriyaam (गोत्राद्यून्यस्त्रियाम्) — When a descendant of the description denoted by युवन् -- जीवति तु वंश्ये युवा [[4.1.163]], is intended to be expressed, a new affix is attached, only after that what already ends with an affix marking a descendant as low at least as a grandson (गोत्र): but in the feminine the word is not termed युवन् and no new affix is added.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.95: atainya (अत इञ्) — The affix affix इञ् after a प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stem) which ends in short अ , in denoting a descendant.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.96: baahvaadibhyashcha (बाह्वादिभ्यश्च) — The affix इञ् is added in the sense of a descendant after the words बहु etc.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.97: sudhaaturakangcha (सुधातुरकङ् च) — The affix इञ् is placed after the word सुधातृ in denoting the descendant and the ऋ of सुधातृ is replaced by the substitute अकङ् before this affix.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.98: gotrekunyjaadibhyashchphany (गोत्रे कुञ्जादिभ्यश्च्फञ्) — The affix च्फञ् comes after the words कुञ्च etc. when a remoter descendant (called गोत्र) is to be denoted.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.99: nadaadibhyahaphak (नडादिभ्यः फक्) — The affix फक् comes, in denoting a गोत्र descendant after the प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stems) नड etc.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.100: haritaadibhyonyah (हरितादिभ्योऽञः) — The affix फक् comes after the words हरित etc. when they end in the affix अञ् -- अनृष्यानन्तर्ये बिदादिभ्योऽञ् [[4.1.104]]",
    "Sūtra 4.1.101: yanyinyoshcha (यञिञोश्च) — The affix फक् is added in denoting a descendent after a प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stem) ending in the affixes यञ् or इञ्।",
    "Sūtra 4.1.102: sharadvachchhunakadarbhaadbhruguvatsaagraayaneshu (शरद्वच्छुनकदर्भाद्भृगुवत्साग्रायणेषु) — The affix फक् comes in denoting a गोत्र (Patronymic) descendant after the words 1. शरद्वत् 2. शुनक 3. दर्भा when they denote the descendants of भृगु , वत्स and अग्रायण , respectively. ",
    "Sūtra 4.1.103: dronaparvatajeevantaadanyatarayaam (द्रोणपर्वतजीवन्तादन्यतरस्याम्) — The affix फक् comes in the sense of a गोत्र (Patronymic) descendant, optionally after the words 1. द्रोण 2. पर्वत and 3. जीवन्त।",
    "Sūtra 4.1.104: anrushyaanantaryebidaadibhyony (अनृष्यानन्तर्ये बिदादिभ्योऽञ्) — The affix अञ् comes after the words बिद etc. in denoting a remote (गोत्र) descendant, but after those words of this class which are not the names of ancient sages, the affix अञ् has the force of denoting immediate descendant.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.105: gargaadibhyoyany (गर्गादिभ्यो यञ्) — The affix यञ् comes in the sense of a गोत्र (Patronymic) descendant after the words गर्ग etc.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.106: madhubabhrvorbraahmanakaushikayoh (मधुबभ्र्वोर्ब्राह्मणकौशिकयोः) — The affix यञ् comes, in the sense of a गोत्र (Patronymic) descendant after the words 1. मधु and 2. बभ्रु when the words so formed mean ब्राह्मण and कौशिक respectively.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.107: kapibodhaadaanggirase (कपिबोधादाङ्गिरसे) — The affix यञ् comes in the sense of a गोत्र (Patronymic) descendant after the words 1. कपिand 2. बोध when the special descendants of the family of अङ्गिरस are meant.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.108: vatandaachcha (वतण्डाच्च) — The affix यञ् comes in the sense of a गोत्र (Patronymic) descendant after the word वतण्ड when meaning a descendant of अङ्गिरस।",
    "Sūtra 4.1.109: lukstriyaam (लुक् स्त्रियाम्) — The affix यञ् is लुक् elided in the feminine after the word वतण्डी when meaning a female descendant of अङ्गिरस।",
    "Sūtra 4.1.110: ashvaadibhyahaphany (अश्वादिभ्यः फञ्) — The affix फञ् comes in the sense of a गोत्र (Patronymic) descendant after the words अश्व etc.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.111: bhargaattraigarte (भर्गात् त्रैगर्ते) — The affix फञ् comes in the sense of a गोत्र (Patronymic) descendant after the word भर्ग when the meaning is a त्रैगर्ते।",
    "Sūtra 4.1.112: shivaadibhyon (शिवादिभ्योऽण्) — The affix अण् comes in the sense of a descendant after the words शिव etc.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.113: avruddhaabhyonadeemaanusheebhyastannaamikaabhyah (अवृद्धाभ्यो नदीमानुषीभ्यस्तन्नामिकाभ्यः) — The affix अण् comes in the sense of descendant after the words are the names of rivers or women when such words are not वृद्धम् words and when they are used as names and not as adjectives.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.114: rushyandhakavrushnikurubhyashcha (ऋष्यन्धकवृष्णिकुरुभ्यश्च) — The affix अण् comes in the sense of descendant after प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stem) denoting the name of a ऋषि or the name of a person of the family of 1. अन्धक 2. वृष्णि 3. कुरु।",
    "Sūtra 4.1.115: maaturutsamkhyaasambhadrapoorvaayaah (मातुरुत् संख्यासम्भद्रपूर्वायाः) — The affix अण् comes in the sense of descendant after the word मातृ when it is preceded by a Numeral or by the words सम् or भद्र and the letter उ is substituted for the final ऋ of मातृ।",
    "Sūtra 4.1.116: kanyaayaahakaneenacha (कन्यायाः कनीन च) — The affix अण् comes in the sense of descendant after the word कन्या and when this affix is added, कनीन is the substitute of कन्या।",
    "Sūtra 4.1.117: vikarnashunggachchhagalaadvatsabharadvaajaatrishu (विकर्णशुङ्गच्छगलाद्वत्सभरद्वाजात्रिषु) — The affix अण् comes after the words 1. विकर्ण 2. शुङ्ग and 3. छगल when the sense is a descendant of the family of वत्स , भारद्वाज and अत्रि , respectively.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.118: peelaayaavaa (पीलाया वा) — The affix अण् comes optionally after the word पीला in denoting a descendant.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.119: dhakchamandookaat (ढक् च मण्डूकात्) — The affix ढक् comes optionally in the sense of a descendant after the word मण्डूक as well as the affix अण्।",
    "Sūtra 4.1.120: streebhyodhak (स्त्रीभ्यो ढक्) — Words ending in the feminine affixes take the affix ढक् in forming their गोत्र (Patronymic).",
    "Sūtra 4.1.121: dvyachah (द्व्यचः) — The affix ढक् comes in the sense of a descendant after a word ending in a feminine affix and consisting of two vowels.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.122: itashchaaninyah (इतश्चानिञः) — The affix ढक् comes in the sense of a descendant after a disyllabic प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stem) ending in short इ , but not, however after a word ending in the Patronymic affix इञ्।",
    "Sūtra 4.1.123: shubhraadibhyashcha (शुभ्रादिभ्यश्च) — The affix ढक् comes in the sense of a descendant after the stems शुभ्र etc.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.124: vikarnakusheetakaatkaashyape (विकर्णकुषीतकात् काश्यपे) — The affix ढक् comes after the words 1. विकर्ण and 2. कुषीत when they mean the descendants of काश्यप।",
    "Sūtra 4.1.125: bhruvovukcha (भ्रुवो वुक् च) — The affix ढक् comes in the sense of a descendant after the word भ्रू and the augment वुक् is added when this affix is to be applied.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.126: kalyaanyaadeenaaminang (कल्याण्यादीनामिनङ्) — The affix ढक् comes in the sense of a descendant after the words कल्याणी etc. and the substitute इनङ् takes the place of the final of these words before this affix.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.127: kulataayaavaa (कुलटाया वा) — The affix ढक् comes in the sense of a descendant after the word कुल्टा and इनङ् is optionally the substitute of the final before this affix.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.128: chatakaayaaairak (चटकाया ऐरक्) — The word चटका takes the affix ऐरक् in forming the Patronymic.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.129: godhaayaadhrak (गोधाया ढ्रक्) — The affix ढ्रक् comes in the sense of a descendant after the word गोधा।",
    "Sūtra 4.1.130: aaragudeechaam (आरगुदीचाम्) — The affix आरक् comes in the sense of a descendant after the word गोधा according to the opinion of Northern Grammarians.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.131: kshudraabhyovaa (क्षुद्राभ्यो वा) — The affix ढ्रक् comes optionally in the sense of descendant after the feminine words denoting mean objects.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.132: pitrushvasushchhan (पितृष्वसुश्छण्) — The affix छण् comes in the sense of a descendant after the word पितृष्वसृ।",
    "Sūtra 4.1.133: dhakilopah (ढकि लोपः) — The final vowel of पितृष्वसृ is elided when the affix ढक् , in the sense of a descendant, is added.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.134: maatrushvasushcha (मातृष्वसुश्च) — So also after the word मातृष्वसृ the affix छण् is added and the final is elided when ढक् follows in forming Patronymic.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.135: chatushpaadbhyodhany (चतुष्पाद्भ्यो ढञ्) — The affix ढञ् comes in the sense of a descendant after the bases denoting quadrupeds.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.136: grushtyaadibhyashcha (गृष्ट्यादिभ्यश्च) — The affix ढञ् comes in the sense of a descendant after the word गृष्टि etc.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.137: raajashvashuraadyat (राजश्वशुराद्यत्) — The affix यत् comes in the sense of the descendant after the words राजन् and श्वसुर।",
    "Sūtra 4.1.138: kshatraadghah (क्षत्राद्घः) — The affix घ comes in the sense of a descendant after the word क्षत्र।",
    "Sūtra 4.1.139: kulaatkhah (कुलात् खः) — The affix ख comes in the sense of a descendant after the प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stem) कुल and a compound word that ends in कुल।",
    "Sūtra 4.1.140: apoorvapadaadanyatarasyaamyaddhakanyau (अपूर्वपदादन्यतरस्यां यड्ढकञौ) — The affixes यत् and ढकञ् come optionally after the word कुल when it is not preceded by any other word which gets the designation of पद -- सुप्तिङन्तं पदम् [[1.4.14]].",
    "Sūtra 4.1.141: mahaakulaadanykhanyau (महाकुलादञ्खञौ) — The affixes अञ् and खञ् come optionally after the word महाकुल।",
    "Sūtra 4.1.142: dushkulaaddhak (दुष्कुलाड्ढक्) — The affix ढक् comes optionally in the sense of descendant after the word दुष्कुल।",
    "Sūtra 4.1.143: svasushchhah (स्वसुश्छः) — The affix छ comes in the sense of descendant after the word स्वसृ।",
    "Sūtra 4.1.144: bhraaturvyachcha (भ्रातुर्व्यच्च) — The affix व्यत् also comes in the sense of descendant after the word भ्रातृ।",
    "Sūtra 4.1.145: vyansapatne (व्यन् सपत्ने) — The affix व्यत् comes after the word भ्रातृ when the sense is that of 'an enemy'.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.146: revatyaadibhyashthak (रेवत्यादिभ्यष्ठक्) — The affix ठक् comes in the sense of descendant after the word रेवती etc.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.147: gotrastriyaahakutsanenacha (गोत्रस्त्रियाः कुत्सने ण च) — And when contempt is to be expressed, the affix ण comes in the sense of descendant after a feminine word denoting a गोत्र-descendant.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.148: vruddhaatthaksauveereshubahulam (वृद्धाट्ठक् सौवीरेषु बहुलम्) — When contempt is to be expressed, the affix ठक् is diversely added in the senses of a descendant after a वृद्ध word denoting सौवीर गोत्र-s.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.149: pheshchhacha (फेश्छ च) — When contempt is to be expressed, the affix छ (as well as the affix ठक्) comes in the sense of descendant after a प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stem) ending in the affix फिञ् and denoting a सौवीर गोत्र।",
    "Sūtra 4.1.150: phaantaahrutimimataabhyaamnaphinyau (फाण्टाहृतिमिमताभ्यां णफिञौ) — The affixes ण and फिञ् comes in the sense of descendant of a person belonging to सुविर country after the word फाण्टाहृति and मिमता।",
    "Sūtra 4.1.151: kurvaadibhyonyah (कुर्वादिभ्यो ण्यः) — The affix ण्य comes in the sense of descendant after the words कुरु etc.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.152: senaantalakshanakaaribhyashcha (सेनान्तलक्षणकारिभ्यश्च) — The affix ण्य comes in the sense of descendant after प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stem) ending in सेना after the word लक्षण and after words denoting artisans.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.153: udeechaaminy (उदीचामिञ्) — According to the opinion of Northern Grammarians, the affix इञ् comes in the sense of descendant after the words ending in सेना , the word लक्षण and words expressing artisans.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.154: tikaadibhyahaphiny (तिकादिभ्यः फिञ्) — The affix फिञ् comes in the sense of descendant after the words तिक etc.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.155: kausalyakaarmaaryaabhyaamcha (कौसल्यकार्मार्याभ्यां च) — The affix फिञ् comes in the sense of descendant after the words कौसल्य and कार्मार्या।",
    "Sūtra 4.1.156: anodvyachah (अणो द्व्यचः) — The affix फिञ् comes in the sense of descendant after a disyllabic word ending in the affix अण्।",
    "Sūtra 4.1.157: udeechaamvruddhaadagotraat (उदीचां वृद्धादगोत्रात्) — According to the opinion of Northern Grammarians after the words with वृद्धि in the first syllable when it is not a गोत्र -name, the affix फिञ् is used in the sense of a descendant.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.158: vaakinaadeenaamkukcha (वाकिनादीनां कुक् च) — The augment क् (कुक्) is added to the words वाकिन etc. when the Patronymic affix फिन् follows.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.159: putraantaadanyatarasyaam (पुत्रान्तादन्यतरस्याम्) — The augment कुक् optionally comes after a stem ending with the word पुत्र when the Patronymic affix फिन् follows.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.160: praachaamavruddhaatphinbahulam (प्राचामवृद्धात् फिन् बहुलम्) — According to the opinion of Eastern Grammarians after a stem not having वृद्धि vowel in the first syllable, the affix फिन् is diversely used in the sense of a descendant.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.161: manorjaataavanyyataushukcha (मनोर्जातावञ्यतौ षुक् च) — The affixes अञ् and यत् come after the word मनु and the augment षुक् is added when these affixes follow provided that the whole word so formed denotes a जाति (class name).",
    "Sūtra 4.1.162: apatyampautraprabhrutigotram (अपत्यं पौत्रप्रभृति गोत्रम्) — A descendant being a grandson or a still lower offspring is called गोत्र।",
    "Sūtra 4.1.163: jeevatituvamshyeyuvaa (जीवति तु वंश्ये युवा) — But when one in a line of descent beginning with a father (and reckoning upwards) is alive, the descendant of a grandson or still lower descendant is called युवन् only.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.164: bhraatarichajyaayasi (भ्रातरि च ज्यायसि) — When an elder brother is alive, the younger brother gets the title of युवन् , being the descendant of a grandson etc.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.165: vaanyasminsapindesthaviratarejeevati (वान्यस्मिन् सपिण्डे स्थविरतरे जीवति) — The living descendant of a grandson etc. is called optionally a युवन् when a more superior सपिण्ड other than a brother is alive.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.166: vruddhasyachapoojaayaam (वृद्धस्य च पूजायाम्) — The गोत्र is sometimes optionally regarded as युवन् when respectful reference to him is intended.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.167: yoonashchakutsaayaam (यूनश्च कुत्सायाम्) — The युवन् is optionally spoken of as गोत्र when contemptuous reference to him is intended.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.168: janapadashabdaatkshatriyaadany (जनपदशब्दात् क्षत्रियादञ्) — The affix अञ् comes in the sense of descendant after a word which while denoting a country, expresses also a tribe of क्षत्रिय-s.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.169: saalveyagaandhaaribhyaamcha (साल्वेयगान्धारिभ्यां च) — The affix अञ् comes in the sense of descendant after the words 1. साल्वेय and 2. गान्धारि ।",
    "Sūtra 4.1.170: dvyanymagadhakalinggasooramasaadan (द्व्यञ्मगधकलिङ्गसूरमसादण्) — The affix अण् comes in the sense of descendant after disyllabic words and the words 1. मगध 2. कलिङ्ग and 3. सूरमस when they are the names of countries as well as क्षत्रिय-s.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.171: vruddhetkosalaajaadaanynyyang (वृद्धेत्कोसलाजादाञ्ञ्यङ्) — The affix ञ्यङ् comes in the sense of descendant after a word having वृद्धि in the first syllable and after a word ending in short इ and after the words 1. कोसल and 2. अजाद when they are the names of countries and क्षत्रिय-s.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.172: kurunaadibhyonyah (कुरुनादिभ्यो ण्यः) — The affix ण्य comes after the word कुरु and a word beginning with न when these words denote a country being the name of a क्षत्रिय tribe also.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.173: saalvaavayavapratyagrathakalakootaashmakaadiny (साल्वावयवप्रत्यग्रथकलकूटाश्मकादिञ्) — The affix इञ् comes in the sense of descendant after a word which denotes any sub-division of the country साल्व and after the words 1. प्रत्यग्रथ 2. कलकूट and 3. अश्मक, when these are names of countries and of tribes.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.174: tetadraajaah (ते तद्राजाः) — These (viz. the affixes अञ् -- जनपदशब्दात् क्षत्रियादञ् [[4.1.168]] etc.) are called तद्राजा 'the king thereof' affixes.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.175: kambojaalluk (कम्बोजाल्लुक्) — After the word कम्बोज there is elision by लुक् of the तद्राजा affix.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.176: striyaamavantikuntikurubhyashcha (स्त्रियामवन्तिकुन्तिकुरुभ्यश्च) — In denoting a feminine name, the तद्राजा is elided after the words 1. अवन्ति 2. कुन्ति and 3. कुरु ।",
    "Sūtra 4.1.177: atashcha (अतश्च) — In forming the feminine of a word which ends in the masculine in the तद्राजा affix अ , the affix is लुक् elided.",
    "Sūtra 4.1.178: napraachyabhargaadiyaudheyaadibhyah (न प्राच्यभर्गादियौधेयादिभ्यः) — The तद्राजा affix is not elided in the feminine, if it forms the names of the क्षत्रिय-sūtras of the East or it comes after the word भर्ग etc. and यौधेय etc.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.1: tenaraktamraagaat (तेन रक्तं रागात्) — The affix अण् already ordained -- प्राग्दीव्यतोऽण् [[4.1.83]], comes after the name of a colour in the sense of 'coloured thereby'.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.2: laakshaarochanaashakalakardamaatthak (लाक्षारोचनाशकलकर्दमाट्ठक्) — The affix ठक् comes, in the sense of coloured thereby after the words 1. लाक्षा 2. रोचना 3. शकल 4. कर्दमा (which being names of colours, are in the Instrumental -3rd case in a sentence).",
    "Sūtra 4.2.3: nakshatrenayuktahakaalah (नक्षत्रेण युक्तः कालः) — The affix अण् already ordained -- प्राग्दीव्यतोऽण् [[4.1.83]], comes after a word in the Instrumental -3rd case in construction which is the name of a lunar mansion, to signify a time connected with the asterism.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.4: lubavisheshe (लुबविशेषे) — The affix above ordained is elided by लुप् when there is no specification.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.5: samjnyaayaamshravanaashvatthaabhyaam (संज्ञायां श्रवणाश्वत्थाभ्याम्) — The affix above ordained is elided by लुप् after the words 1. श्रवण and 2. अश्वथ when the whole word so formed is an appellation and there is specification of time.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.6: dvamdvaachchhah (द्वन्द्वाच्छः) — The affix छ comes after the द्वन्द compound of the names of lunar mansions, when it is in the Instrumental -3rd case in construction, to signify time connected with the asterism whether there be a specification or not.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.7: drushtamsaama (दृष्टं साम) — The affix अण् -- प्राग्दीव्यतोऽण् [[4.1.83]] comes after a word in construction in the Instrumental -3rd case, in the sense of seen - the thing seen by the one whose name is in the Instrumental -3rd case, being the साम वेद।",
    "Sūtra 4.2.8: kalerdhak (कलेर्ढक्) — The affix ढक् comes in the sense of साम वेद seen after the word कलि being in the Instrumental -3rd case.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.9: vaamadevaaddyaddyau (वामदेवाड्ड्यड्ड्यौ) — The affixes ड्यत् and ड्य come in the sense of the साम वेद seen after the word वामदेव , being in the Instrumental -3rd case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.10: parivrutorathah (परिवृतो रथः) — The affix अण् comes after a word in the Instrumental -3rd case in construction in the sense of 'surrounded' the thing so surrounded being 'a chariot'.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.11: paandukambalaadinih (पाण्डुकम्बलादिनिः) — The affix इनि comes after the word पाण्डुकम्बल etc. being in the Instrumental -3rd case in construction in the sense of 'surrounded' the thing so surrounded being 'a chariot'.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.12: dvaipavaiyaaghraadany (द्वैपवैयाघ्रादञ्) — The affix अञ् comes after the words द्वैप and वैयाघ्र being in the Instrumental -3rd case in construction in the sense of 'surrounded' the thing so surrounded being 'a chariot'.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.13: kaumaaraapoorvavachane (कौमारापूर्ववचने) — The word कौमार is irregularly formed by adding the affix अण् when meaning 'virginity'.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.14: tatroddhrutamamatrebhyah (तत्रोद्धृतममत्रेभ्यः) — The affix अञ् already ordained -- प्राग्दीव्यतोऽण् [[4.1.83]], comes in the sense of 'placed thereon' after words denoting vessels when such words are in the Locative -7th case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.15: sthandilaachchhayitarivrate (स्थण्डिलाच्छयितरि व्रते) — The affix अञ् already ordained -- प्राग्दीव्यतोऽण् [[4.1.83]], comes after the word स्थण्डिल being in the Locative -7th case in construction in the sense of 'a sleeper thereon' and the whole word so formed denotes 'a person performing a vow'.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.16: samskrutambhakshaah (संस्कृतं भक्षाः) — The affix अण् comes after a word ending in the Locative -7th case to denote 'what is prepared therein' -if that which is so prepared be 'granular food'.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.17: shoolokhaadyat (शूलोखाद्यत्) — The affix यत् comes in the sense of 'prepared food' after the words शूल and उखा ending in the Locative -7th case.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.18: dadhnashthak (दध्नष्ठक्) — The affix ठक्",
    "Sūtra 4.2.19: udashvitonyatarasyaam (उदश्वितोऽन्यतरस्याम्) — The affix ठक् comes in the sense of 'prepared food', optionally after the word उदश्वित ending in the Locative -7th case.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.20: ksheeraaddhany (क्षीराड्ढञ्) — The affix ढञ् comes in the sense of 'prepared food' after the word दधि ending in the Locative -7th case.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.21: saasminpaurnamaaseetisamjnyaayaam (सास्मिन् पौर्णमासीति संज्ञायाम्) — The affix अण् comes after the name of a full-moon-night to denote the division of time in which the night falls.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.22: aagrahaayanyashvatthaatthak (आग्रहायण्यश्वत्थाट्ठक्) — The affix ठक् comes in the sense of Locative -7th case after the words आग्रहायणी and अश्वत्थ ending in the 1st - Nominative Case-affix in construction and being the name of a full-moon night.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.23: vibhaashaaphaalguneeshravanaakaarttikeechaitreebhyah (विभाषा फाल्गुनीश्रवणाकार्त्तिकीचैत्रीभ्यः) — The affix ढक् optionally comes after the words 1. फाल्गुनी 2. कार्त्तिकी and 3. चैत्री being the names of full-moon nights, the whole word so formed being a Name denoting a division of time (a month, a fortnight or a year) in which the moon is full.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.24: saasyadevataa (सास्य देवता) — The affix अण् -- प्राग्दीव्यतोऽण् [[4.1.83]], is added to the name of a deity when something is to be spoken of as his.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.25: kasyet (कस्येत्) — The short इ is the substitute of the final अ of क when the affix is added.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.26: shukraadghan (शुक्राद्घन्) — The affix घन् comes in the sense of 'that its deity' after the word शुक्र।",
    "Sūtra 4.2.27: aponaptrapaannaptrubhyaamghah (अपोनप्त्रपान्नप्तृभ्यां घः) — The affix घ comes after the words 1. अपोनप्तृ and 2. अपन्नप्तृ in the sense of 'that its deity'.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.28: chhacha (छ च) — Also छ is added to the words 1. अपोनप्तृ and 2. अपन्नप्तृ in the sense of 'that its deity'.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.29: mahendraadghaanaucha (महेन्द्राद्घाणौ च) — The affixes घ and अण् and छ come after the name महेन्द्र in the sense of 'this its deity'.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.30: somaattyan (सोमाट्ट्यण्) — The affix ट्यण् comes after the name सोम in the sense of 'this its deity'.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.31: vaayvrutupitrushasoyat (वाय्वृतुपित्रुषसो यत्) — The affix यत् comes after the names 1. वायु 2. ऋतु 3. पितृ and 4. उषस् in the sense of 'this its deity'.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.32: dyaavaapruthiveeshunaaseeramarutvadagneeshomavaastoshpatigruhamedhaachchhacha (द्यावापृथिवीशुनासीरमरुत्वदग्नीषोमवास्तोष्पतिगृहमेधाच्छ च) — The affix छ also comes in the sense of 'this its deity' after the names 1. द्यावा 2. पृथिवी 3. शुनासीर 4. मरुत्वद् 5. अग्निषोम 6. वास्तोष्पति 7. गृहमेधा।",
    "Sūtra 4.2.33: agnerdhak (अग्नेर्ढक्) — The affix ढक् comes in the sense of 'this its deity' after the name अग्नि।",
    "Sūtra 4.2.34: kaalebhyobhavavat (कालेभ्यो भववत्) — After the words expressive of time, the affixes denoting 'who stays there' -- कालाट्ठञ् [[4.3.11]] to तत्र भवः [[4.3.53]], come also in the sense of 'this its deity'.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.35: mahaaraajaproshthapadaatthany (महाराजप्रोष्ठपदाट्ठञ्) — The affix ठञ् comes in the sense of 'this its deity' after the words 1. महाराज and 2. प्रोष्ठपद।",
    "Sūtra 4.2.36: pitruvyamaatulamaataamahapitaamahaah (पितृव्यमातुलमातामहपितामहाः) — The words 1. पितृव्य 'a father's brother' 2. मातुल 'a mother's brother' 3. मातामह 'a mother's father' 4. पितामह 'a father's father' are irregularly formed.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.37: tasyasamoohah (तस्य समूहः) — An affix is added to a word when the sense is 'a collection thereof'.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.38: bhikshaadibhyon (भिक्षादिभ्योऽण्) — The affix अण् comes the sense is 'a collection thereof' after the words भिक्षा etc.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.39: gotrokshoshtrorabhraraajaraajanyaraajaputravatsamanushyaajaadvuny (गोत्रोक्षोष्ट्रोरभ्रराजराजन्यराजपुत्रवत्समनुष्याजाद्वुञ्) — The affix वुञ् comes the sense is 'a collection thereof' after a word denoting a गोत्र (Patronymic) and after 1. उक्ष 2. उष्ट्र 3. उरभ्र 4. राजन 5. राजन्य 6. राजपुत्र 7. वत्स 8. मनुष्य and 9. अज।",
    "Sūtra 4.2.40: kedaaraadyanycha (केदाराद्यञ् च) — The affixes यञ् and वुञ् come after the word केदार in the sense of 'collection thereof'.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.41: thanykavachinashcha (ठञ् कवचिनश्च) — The affix ठञ् comes in the sense of 'collection thereof' after the word केदार and also after the word कवचिन ।",
    "Sūtra 4.2.42: braahmanamaanavavaadavaadyan (ब्राह्मणमाणववाडवाद्यन्) — The affix यन् is added in the sense of 'collection thereof' after the words 1. ब्राह्मण 2. माणव and वाडव ।",
    "Sūtra 4.2.43: graamajanabandhusahaayebhyahatal (ग्रामजनबन्धुसहायेभ्यः तल्) — The affix तल् comes in the sense of 'collection thereof' after the words 1. ग्राम 2. जन 3. बन्धु and 4. सहाय।",
    "Sūtra 4.2.44: anudaattaaderany (अनुदात्तादेरञ्) — The affix अञ् comes in the sense of 'collection thereof' after the words having अनुदात्त on the first syllable.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.45: khandikaadibhyashcha (खण्डिकादिभ्यश्च) — The affix अञ् comes in the sense of 'collection thereof' after the words खण्डिक etc.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.46: charanebhyodharmavat (चरणेभ्यो धर्मवत्) — After the name of a Vedic School, the affixes which denote the rule of that school, also come in the sense of 'collection thereof'.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.47: achittahastidhenoshthak (अचित्तहस्तिधेनोष्ठक्) — The affix ठक् comes in the sense of 'collection thereof' after the names of things without consciousness and after 1. हस्ति and 2. धेनु।",
    "Sūtra 4.2.48: keshaashvaabhyaamyanychhaavanyatarasyaam (केशाश्वाभ्यां यञ्छावन्यतरस्याम्) — The affixes यञ् and छ come optionally in the sense of 'collection thereof' after the words 1. केश and 2. अश्व , respectively.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.49: paashaadibhyoyah (पाशादिभ्यो यः) — The affix य comes in the sense of 'collection thereof' after the words पाश etc.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.50: khalagorathaat (खलगोरथात्) — The affix य comes in the sense of 'collection thereof' after the words 1. खल 2 गो and 3. रथ।",
    "Sūtra 4.2.51: initrakatyachashcha (इनित्रकट्यचश्च) — The affixes इनि , त्र and कट्यष्यच् come in the sense of 'collection thereof', respectively after the words 1. खल 2 गो and 3. रथ।",
    "Sūtra 4.2.52: vishayodeshe (विषयो देशे) — The affix अण् -- प्राग्दीव्यतोऽण् [[4.1.83]], comes after a word in the Genitive -6th-Case in construction in the sense of 'any body'sūtras sphere', if a country is indicated by such sphere.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.53: raajanyaadibhyovuny (राजन्यादिभ्यो वुञ्) — The affix वुञ् comes after the words राजन्य etc. in the same sense.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.54: bhaurikyaadyaishukaaryaadibhyovidhalbhaktalau (भौरिक्याद्यैषुकार्यादिभ्यो विधल्भक्तलौ) — The affixes विधल् and भक्तल् come respectively after the words बहौरिकि and ऐषुकारि etc. in the sense of 'sphere of country'.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.55: sosyaadiritichchhandasahapragaatheshu (सोऽस्यादिरिति च्छन्दसः प्रगाथेषु) — The affix अण् is added to the names of Meters, indicates a प्रगाथ beginning therewith.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.56: samgraameprayojanayoddhrubhyah (संग्रामे प्रयोजनयोद्धृभ्यः) — The affix अण् -- प्राग्दीव्यतोऽण् [[4.1.83]] when it is added to a word which denotes either the object of a battle or the warrior of a battle fought for that object or by that warrior as a leader.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.57: tadasyaampraharanamitikreedaayaamnah (तदस्यां प्रहरणमिति क्रीडायाम् णः) — The affix ण to the name of a weapon indicates a game played with that weapon.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.58: ghanyahasaasyaamkriyetinyah (घञः साऽस्यां क्रियेति ञः) — The affix ञ added to a noun of action ending in the affix घञ् denotes an action occurring in that.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.59: tadadheetetadveda (तदधीते तद्वेद) — The affix अण् -- प्राग्दीव्यतोऽण् [[4.1.83]] comes after a word denoting 'some subject of study' in the sense of 'who has studied that or who understands that'.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.60: kratookthaadisootraantaatthak (क्रतूक्थादिसूत्रान्ताट्ठक्) — The affix ठञ् comes in the sense of 'one who studies or one who understands' after the name of a sacrifice after उक्थ etc. and after a stem ending with the word सूत्र।",
    "Sūtra 4.2.61: kramaadibhyovun (क्रमादिभ्यो वुन्) — The affix वुन् comes in the sense of 'who studies or who knows' after the words क्रम etc.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.62: anubraahmanaadinih (अनुब्राह्मणादिनिः) — The affix इनि comes in the sense of 'who studies or who knows' after the word अनुब्राह्मण।",
    "Sūtra 4.2.63: vasantaadibhyashthak (वसन्तादिभ्यष्ठक्) — The affix ठक् comes in the sense of 'who studies or who knows' after the words वसन्त etc.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.64: proktaalluk (प्रोक्ताल्लुक्) — After the title of a work which is named after the Announcer thereof the affixes denoting 'who studies or who knows that' are elided by लुक् ।",
    "Sūtra 4.2.65: sootraachchakopadhaat (सूत्राच्च कोपधात्) — The affix denoting denoting 'who studies or who knows that' is elided by लुक् after the title of a sūtra work having क् as penultimate.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.66: chhandobraahmanaanichatadvishayaani (छन्दोब्राह्मणानि च तद्विषयाणि) — The affixes denoting the Announcer when added to छन्दस् (Vedas) and the ब्राह्मण-sūtras express this relation only.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.67: tadasminnasteetideshetannaamni (तदस्मिन्नस्तीति देशे तन्नाम्नि) — (An affix is placed after a word expressive of anything) in the sense of '- that thing is in this' - the place taking a name therefrom.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.68: tenanirvruttam (तेन निर्वृत्तम्) — After a word in the Instrumental -3rd case in construction an affix is added in the sense of 'completed by him' when the whole word so formed is the name of a country.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.69: tasyanivaasah (तस्य निवासः) — After a word in the Genitive -6th-Case in construction an affix is added in the sense of 'his dwelling-place' the whole word expressing the name of a country.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.70: adoorabhavashcha (अदूरभवश्च) — And lastly a place is named after whatever is found near it.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.71: orany (ओरञ्) — The affix अञ् comes after a stem ending in a उ or ऊ (in the four-fold senses given above).",
    "Sūtra 4.2.72: matoshchabahvajanggaat (मतोश्च बह्वजङ्गात्) — The affix अञ् comes in the quadruple sense after a word which ends in the affix मतुप् and whose stem is polysyllabic.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.73: bahvachahakoopeshu (बह्वचः कूपेषु) — The affix अञ् comes in the quadruple sense after a polysyllabic प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stem) when 'a well' is to be designated.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.74: udakchavipaashah (उदक् च विपाशः) — The affix अञ् comes in the quadruple sense after any polysyllabic प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stem) in denoting 'a well' situated on the Northern bank of the river विपाश।",
    "Sūtra 4.2.75: samkalaadibhyashcha (संकलादिभ्यश्च) — The affix अण् comes after the words संकल etc. in the above 4-fold sense.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.76: streeshusauveerasaalvapraakshu (स्त्रीषु सौवीरसाल्वप्राक्षु) — So also when the palace is situated in the lands of the सौवीर or साल्व or of the Eatern People and the word in these cases is always feminine.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.77: suvaastvaadibhyon (सुवास्त्वादिभ्योऽण्) — The affix अञ् comes after the words सुवास्तु etc. in the 4-fold sense.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.78: ronee (रोणी) — The affix अण् comes after राणो in the 4-fold sense.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.79: kopadhaachcha (कोपधाच्च) — The affix अण् comes in the 4-fold sense after a stem having क् for its penultimate.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.80: vunychhankathajilaseniradhanynyayaphakphinyinynyyakakthakoreehanakrushaashvarshyakumudakaashatrunaprekshaashmasakhisamkaashabalapakshakarnasutamgamapragadinvaraahakumudaadibhyah (वुञ्छण्कठजिलसेनिरढञ्ण्ययफक्फिञिञ्ञ्यकक्ठकोऽरीहणकृशाश्वर्श्यकुमुदकाशतृणप्रेक्षाऽश्मसखिसंकाशबलपक्षकर्णसुतंगमप्रगदिन्वराहकुमुदादिभ्यः) — In the above 4-senses are added the following 17-affixes after the following 17 classes of words respectively - ……………………………………………….",
    "Sūtra 4.2.81: janapadelup (जनपदे लुप्) — The name of a kingdom is formed by the लुप् elision of these affixes (when the name of the people without the change of number and gender, is at the same time the name of the kingdom).",
    "Sūtra 4.2.82: varanaadibhyashcha (वरणादिभ्यश्च) — Also after the word वरण etc. the affix denoting locality becomes elided but the number and gender are not changed.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.83: sharkaraayaavaa (शर्कराया वा) — Optionally after the word शर्करा the 4-fold significant affix is elided by लुप् ।",
    "Sūtra 4.2.84: thakchhaucha (ठक्छौ च) — The affixes ठक् and छ come after the word शर्करा in the 4-fold sense.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.85: nadyaammatup (नद्यां मतुप्) — The affix मतुप् is added denoting a river.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.86: madhvaadibhyashcha (मध्वादिभ्यश्च) — The affix मतुप् is added to the words मधु etc. in the four senses given above.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.87: kumudanadavetasebhyodmatup (कुमुदनडवेतसेभ्यो ड्मतुप्) — The affix ड्मतुप् comes after the words 1. कुमुद 2. नड and 3. वेतस in the above four senses and the final of these words is elided before this affix.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.88: nadashaadaaddvalach (नडशादाड्ड्वलच्) — The affix ड्वलच् comes after 1. नड and 2. शाद in the four senses given above, the final of the words being elided.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.89: shikhaayaavalach (शिखाया वलच्) — The affix वलच् comes after the word शिखा in the above four senses.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.90: utkaraadibhyashchhah (उत्करादिभ्यश्छः) — The affix छ comes after the words उत्कर etc. in the four senses.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.91: nadaadeenaamkukcha (नडादीनां कुक् च) — The augment कुक् comes after the words नड etc. when the affix छ follows in the above four senses.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.92: sheshe (शेषे) — The affixes taught hereafter have senses other than those mentioned above.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.93: raashtraavaarapaaraadghakhau (राष्ट्रावारपाराद्घखौ) — The affixes घ and ख are respectively added after the words 1. राष्ट् and 2. अवारपार।",
    "Sūtra 4.2.94: graamaadyakhanyau (ग्रामाद्यखञौ) — The affixes व and खञ् (ईन) come after the word ग्राम।",
    "Sūtra 4.2.95: kattryaadibhyodhakany (कत्र्यादिभ्यो ढकञ्) — The affix ढकञ् (एयक) comes after the words कत्रि etc.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.96: kulakukshigreevaabhyahashvaasyalamkaareshu (कुलकुक्षिग्रीवाभ्यः श्वास्यलंकारेषु) — The affix ढकञ् is added to the words 1. कुल 2. कुक्षि and 3. ग्रीवा when the whole words so formed mean respectively 'a dog', 'a sword' and 'an ornament'.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.97: nadyaadibhyodhak (नद्यादिभ्यो ढक्) — The affix ढक् comes after the words नदी etc. in the remaining senses i.e. तत्र जातः [[4.3.25]] etc.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.98: dakshinaapashchaatpurasastyak (दक्षिणापश्चात्पुरसस्त्यक्) — The words 1. दक्षिणा 2. पश्चात् and 3. पुरस् the affix त्यक् (त्य) is added in the remaining senses.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.99: kaapishyaahashphak (कापिश्याः ष्फक्) — After the word कापिशी , the affix ष्फक् is added in the remaining senses (the feminine being formed by ङीष् -- षिद्गौरादिभ्यश्च [[4.1.41]]).",
    "Sūtra 4.2.100: ramkoramanushyencha (रंकोरमनुष्येऽण् च) — After the word रंकु the affixes ष्फक् and अण् are added in the remaining senses when the meaning is a non-human being.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.101: dyupraagapaagudakprateechoyat (द्युप्रागपागुदक्प्रतीचो यत्) — After the words 1. दिव् 2. प्राच् 3. अपाच् 4. उदच् and 5. प्रत्यच् , the affix यत् is added in the remaining senses.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.102: kanthaayaashthak (कन्थायाष्ठक्) — After the word कन्था the affix is ठक् is added in the remaining senses.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.103: varnauvuk (वर्णौ वुक्) — To the same stem is added the affix वुक् when it treats about something which is to be found in the land of वर्णु (name of a river and also the country near it).",
    "Sūtra 4.2.104: avyayaattyap (अव्ययात्त्यप्) — The affix त्यप् comes after an indeclinable in the remaining senses.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.105: aishamohyahashvasonyatarasyaam (ऐषमोह्यःश्वसोऽन्यतरस्याम्) — The affix त्यप् is added optionally after the words 1. ऐषमस् 2. ह्यस् and 3. श्वस् , in the remaining senses.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.106: teeraroopyottarapadaadanynyau (तीररूप्योत्तरपदादञ्ञौ) — The affix अञ् comes after a word ending with तीर and the ञ् comes after a word ending with कप्य , in the remaining senses.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.107: dikpoorvapadaadasamjnyaayaamnyah (दिक्पूर्वपदादसंज्ञायां ञः) — The affix ञ comes in the remaining senses after a word preceded by another that signifies 'direction' provided the compound is not a name.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.108: madrebhyony (मद्रेभ्योऽञ्) — The affix अञ् is added to the word मद्र , preceded by a word denoting 'direction', in the remaining senses.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.109: udeechyagraamaachchabahvachontodaattaat (उदीच्यग्रामाच्च बह्वचोऽन्तोदात्तात्) — The affix अञ् comes in the remaining senses after a word consisting of more than two syllables having उदात्त accent on the final, being the name of a village of the people of the North.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.110: prasthottarapadapaladyaadikopadhaadan (प्रस्थोत्तरपदपलद्यादिकोपधादण्) — The affix अण् comes in the remaining senses after a word ending with प्रस्थ after the words पलदी etc. and after a word having a penultimate क , whether these words express villages of North folk or not.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.111: kanvaadibhyogotre (कण्वादिभ्यो गोत्रे) — The affix अण् comes after the Patronymics formed from कण्व etc.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.112: inyashcha (इञश्च) — After a family-name formed by इञ् the affix अण् is added in the remaining senses.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.113: nadvyachahapraachyabharateshu (न द्व्यचः प्राच्यभरतेषु) — The affix अण् is however not added to a word which though ending in the Patronymic affix इञ् consists of two syllables when it is the family name of Eastern People or of भरत।",
    "Sūtra 4.2.114: vruddhaachchhah (वृद्धाच्छः) — After the word वृद्ध , the affix छ is added in the remaining senses.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.115: bhavatashthakchhasau (भवतष्ठक्छसौ) — The affixes ठक् and छस् come after वृद्ध word भवत् , in the remaining senses.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.116: kaashyaadibhyashthanynyithau (काश्यादिभ्यष्ठञ्ञिठौ) — The affixes ठञ् and ञिठ् come in the remaining senses after the words काशि etc.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.117: vaaheekagraamebhyashcha (वाहीकग्रामेभ्यश्च) — The affixes ठञ् and ञिठ् come in the remaining senses after the वृद्ध words denoting the villages of वाहीक।",
    "Sūtra 4.2.118: vibhaashosheenareshu (विभाषोशीनरेषु) — The affixes ठञ् and ञिठ् come optionally in the remaining senses after the वृद्ध words denoting वाहीक villages situated in उशीनर।",
    "Sūtra 4.2.119: ordeshethany (ओर्देशे ठञ्) — The affixes ठञ् comes in the remaining senses after a प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stem) denoting a locality and ending in उ।",
    "Sūtra 4.2.120: vruddhaatpraachaam (वृद्धात् प्राचाम्) — The affixes ठञ् comes in the remaining senses after a वृद्ध word ending in उ and denoting a locality of East-folks.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.121: dhanvayopadhaadvuny (धन्वयोपधाद्वुञ्) — The affix वुञ् comes in the remaining senses after a वृद्ध word denoting a locality which has the letter य as its penultimate and after a वृद्ध place name denoting a waste or desert place.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.122: prasthapuravahaantaachcha (प्रस्थपुरवहान्ताच्च) — The affix वुञ् comes in the remaining senses after a वृद्ध word denoting a locality and ending with 1. प्रस्थ 2. पुर or वह।",
    "Sūtra 4.2.123: ropadhetohapraachaam (रोपधेतोः प्राचाम्) — The affix वुञ् comes in the remaining senses after a वृद्ध word denoting a locality of the East-folk, the word having penultimate र or ending in ई।",
    "Sūtra 4.2.124: janapadatadavadhyoshcha (जनपदतदवध्योश्च) — The affix वुञ् comes in the remaining senses after a वृद्ध word denoting an inhabited kingdom or a limit of such kingdom",
    "Sūtra 4.2.125: avruddhaadapibahuvachanavishayaat (अवृद्धादपि बहुवचनविषयात्) — The affix वुञ् comes in the remaining senses, even after a word which is not a वृद्ध which is always plural, when it denotes an inhabited country or a limit of such country, as well as after such वृद्ध words.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.126: kachchhaagnivaktragarttottarapadaat (कच्छाग्निवक्त्रवर्त्तोत्तरपदात्) — The affix वुञ् comes in the remaining senses after a word whether a वृद्ध or not, denoting a locality and having its second term the words 1. कच्छ 2. अग्नि 3. वक्त्र and 4. गर्त।",
    "Sūtra 4.2.127: dhoomaadibhyashcha (धूमादिभ्यश्च) — The affix वुञ् comes in the remaining senses after the words धूम etc. denoting country.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.128: nagaraatkutsanapraaveenyayoh (नगरात् कुत्सनप्रावीण्ययोः) — The affix वुञ् comes after the word नगर in the remaining senses, when censure or praise is implied.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.129: aranyaanmanushye (अरण्यान्मनुष्ये) — The affix वुञ् comes in the remaining senses after the word अरण्य , in the sense of 'a man'.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.130: vibhaashaakuruyugandharaabhyaam (विभाषा कुरुयुगन्धराभ्याम्) — The affix वुञ् comes optionally in the remaining senses after the words 1. कुरु and 2. युगन्धर।",
    "Sūtra 4.2.131: madravrujyohakan (मद्रवृज्योः कन्) — The affix कन् comes in the remaining senses after the words 1. मद्र and 2. वृजि।",
    "Sūtra 4.2.132: kopadhaadan (कोपधादण्) — The affix अण् comes in the remaining senses after a word denoting a place and having the letter क as its penultimate.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.133: kachchhaadibhyashcha (कच्छादिभ्यश्च) — The affix अण् comes in the remaining senses after the words कच्छ etc. denoting places.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.134: manushyatatsthayorvuny (मनुष्यतत्स्थयोर्वुञ्) — The affix वुञ् comes after the words कच्छ etc. in the senses of born etc. when the meaning is 'a man' or 'what exists in a man'.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.135: apadaatausaalvaat (अपदातौ साल्वात्) — The affix वुञ् comes after the word साल्व in the senses of being born etc. when denoting 'a man 'or 'what exists in a man', provided that it does not mean a foot-soldier.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.136: goyavaagvoshcha (गोयवाग्वोश्च) — The affix वुञ् comes in the remaining senses of being born etc. after the words साल्व etc. when the word signifies 'a cow' or 'a barley gruel'.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.137: gartottarapadaachchhah (गर्तोत्तरपदाच्छः) — The affix छ comes in the remaining senses after a प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stem) denoting a place and having the word गर्त as its second term.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.138: gahaadibhyashcha (गहादिभ्यश्च) — The affix छ comes in the remaining senses after the words गह etc.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.139: praachaamkataadeh (प्राचां कटादेः) — The affix छ comes in the remaining senses after the words beginning with कद denoting the places of the East-folk.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.140: raajnyahakacha (राज्ञः क च) — The letter क is the substitute of the final of the word राजन् , when छ is added.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.141: vruddhaadakekaantakhopadhaat (वृद्धादकेकान्तखोपधात्) — The affix छ comes in the remaining senses after a वृद्ध word denoting a place and ending with अक् or इक् or having ख as its penultimate.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.142: kanthaapaladanagaragraamahradottarapadaat (कन्थापलदनगरग्रामहृदोत्तरपदात्) — The affix छ comes in the remaining senses after a वृद्ध words, having the words 1. कन्था 2. पलद 3. नगर 4. ग्राम and 5. हृद , as second terms.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.143: parvataachcha (पर्वताच्च) — The affix छ comes after the word पर्वत in the remaining senses.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.144: vibhaashaamanushye (विभाषाऽमनुष्ये) — The affix छ optionally comes in the remaining senses after the word पर्वत when it does not denote 'a man'.",
    "Sūtra 4.2.145: krukanaparnaadbhaaradvaaje (कृकणपर्णाद्भारद्वाजे) — The affix छ comes in the remaining senses after कृकण and पर्ण when denoting the country भारद्वाच।",
    "Sūtra 4.3.1: yushmadasmadoranyatarasyaamkhanycha (युष्मदस्मदोरन्यतरस्यां खञ् च) — The affix खञ् also comes optionally in the remaining senses after the words 1. युष्मद् and 2. अस्मद्।",
    "Sūtra 4.3.2: tasminnanichayushmaakaasmaakau (तस्मिन्नणि च युष्माकास्माकौ) — When the affix खञ् is added and when अण् is added then 1. युष्माक and 2. अस्माक are the substitutes of युष्मद् and अस्मद्।",
    "Sūtra 4.3.3: tavakamamakaavekavachane (तवकममकावेकवचने) — In expressing one individual, तबक and ममक are the substitutes of युष्मद् and अस्मद् respectively when खञ् and अण् follow.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.4: ardhaadyat (अर्धाद्यत्) — The affix यत् comes after the word अर्द्ध in the remaining senses.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.5: paraavaraadhamottamapoorvaachcha (परावराधमोत्तमपूर्वाच्च) — The affix यत् comes in the remaining senses after the word अर्द्ध when preceded by 1. पर 2. अवर 3. अधम and 4. उत्तम।",
    "Sūtra 4.3.6: dikpoorvapadaatthanycha (दिक्पूर्वपदाट्ठञ् च) — And the affix ठञ् also (as well as यत्) comes in the remaining senses after the word अर्द्ध when the prior term denotes a direction.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.7: graamajanapadaikadeshaadanythanyau (ग्रामजनपदैकदेशादञ्ठञौ) — The affixes अञ् and ठञ् come in the remaining senses after the word अर्द्ध preceded by a word denoting direction when a particular portion of a village or an inhabited country.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.8: madhyaanmah (मध्यान्मः) — After the word मध्य there is the affix म in the remaining senses.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.9: asaampratike (अ साम्प्रतिके) — The affix अ comes in the remaining senses after the word मध्य , the meaning being 'fit' or 'proper'.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.10: dveepaadanusamudramyany (द्वीपादनुसमुद्रं यञ्) — The affix यञ् comes in the remaining senses after the word द्वीप , which is near the sea.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.11: kaalaatthany (कालाट्ठञ्) — The affix ठञ् comes in the remaining senses after the words denoting time.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.12: shraaddhesharadah (श्राद्धे शरदः) — The affix ठञ् comes in the remaining senses after the word शरद् when expressing श्राद्ध।",
    "Sūtra 4.3.13: vibhaashaarogaatapayoh (विभाषा रोगातपयोः) — The affix ठञ् comes optionally comes in the remaining senses after the word शरद् when expressing illness or heat.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.14: nishaapradoshaabhyaamcha (निशाप्रदोषाभ्यां च) — The affix ठञ् comes optionally comes in the remaining senses after the words 1. निशा and 2. प्रदोष ।",
    "Sūtra 4.3.15: shvasastutcha (श्वसस्तुट् च) — The affix ठञ् comes optionally comes in the remaining senses after the word श्वस् and it takes the augment तुट्।",
    "Sūtra 4.3.16: samdhivelaadyrutunakshatrebhyon (संधिवेलाद्यृतुनक्षत्रेभ्योऽण्) — The affix अण् comes in the remaining senses after the words संधिवेला etc. and the words expressing 'season' and 'asterism'.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.17: praavrushenyah (प्रावृष एण्यः) — The affix एण्य comes in the remaining senses after the word प्रावृष।",
    "Sūtra 4.3.18: varshaabhyashthak (वर्षाभ्यष्ठक्) — The affix ठक् comes in the remaining senses after the word वर्षा।",
    "Sūtra 4.3.19: chhandasithany (छन्दसि ठञ्) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas), the word वर्षा takes the affix ठञ् , in the remaining senses.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.20: vasantaachcha (वसन्ताच्च) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas), the affix ठञ् comes in the remaining senses after the word वसन्त।",
    "Sūtra 4.3.21: hemantaachcha (हेमन्ताच्च) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas), the affix ठञ् comes in the remaining senses after the word हेमन्त।",
    "Sūtra 4.3.22: sarvatraanchatalopashcha (सर्वत्राण् च तलोपश्च) — The affix अण् comes always after the word हेमन्त and (before this affix) the letter त of हेमन्त is elided.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.23: saayamchirampraahnepragevyayebhyashtyutyulaututcha (सायंचिरम्प्राह्णेप्रगेऽव्ययेभ्यष्ट्युट्युलौ तुट् च) — After the words 1. सायं 'at eve' 2. चिरम् 'for a long time' 3. प्राह्णे 'in the forenoon' 4. प्रगे 'at dawn' and after indeclinables expressing time, there are the affixes ट्यु and ट्युल् and their augment is तुट्।",
    "Sūtra 4.3.24: vibhaashaapoorvaahnaaparaahnaabhyaam (विभाषा पूर्वाह्णापराह्णाभ्याम्) — Optionally after the words 1. पूर्वाह्ण and 2. अपराह्ण there are the affixes ट्यु and ट्युल् and their augment is तुट्।",
    "Sūtra 4.3.25: tatrajaatah (तत्र जातः) — The affixes ordained above or hereafter come after a word in the Locative -7th case in construction in the sense of 'born or grown or originated there or then'.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.26: praavrushashthap (प्रावृषष्ठप्) — After the word प्रावृट् being in the Locative -7th case-affix, there is the affix ठप् in the sense of 'produced therein'.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.27: samjnyaayaamsharadovuny (संज्ञायां शरदो वुञ्) — The affix वुञ् comes after the word शरद in the Locative -7th case-affix in the sense of 'born therein', the whole word being a name.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.28: poorvaahnaaparaahnaardraamoolapradoshaavaskaraadvun (पूर्वाह्णापराह्णार्द्रामूलप्रदोषावस्कराद्वुन्) — The affix वुञ् comes in the sense of 'born therein' after the words 1. पूर्वाह्ण 2. अपराह्ण 3. आर्द्रा 4. मूला 5. प्रदोष and 6. अवस्कर , the whole being a name.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.29: pathahapanthacha (पथः पन्थ च) — The affix वुञ् comes after the word पथ , in the sense of 'produced therein' and thereby in the room of पथ , the substitute is पन्थ।",
    "Sūtra 4.3.30: amaavaasyaayaavaa (अमावास्याया वा) — The affix वुञ् comes optionally after the word अमावास्या in the sense of 'born therein'.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.31: acha (अ च) — The affix अ is also added to the word अमावास्या in the sense of 'born therein'.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.32: sindhvapakaraabhyaamkan (सिन्ध्वपकराभ्यां कन्) — After the words 1. सिन्धु and 2. अपकर there is the affix कन् in the sense of 'born therein'.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.33: ananyaucha (अणञौ च) — And the affixes अण् and अञ् come respectively after the words 1. सिन्धु and 2. अपकर।",
    "Sūtra 4.3.34: shravishthaaphalgunyanuraadhaasvaatitishyapunarvasuhastavishaakhaashaadhaabahulaalluk (श्रविष्ठाफल्गुन्यनुराधास्वातितिष्यपुनर्वसुहस्तविशाखाषाढाबहुलाल्लुक्) — The affix denoting 'born therein' is elided by लुक् after the words 1. श्रविष्ठ 2. फाल्गुनी 3. अनुराधा 4. स्वाति 5. तिष्य 6. पुनर्वसु 7. हस्त 8. विशाखा 9. अषाढा and 10. बहुला , all denoting asterisms.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.35: sthaanaantagoshaalakharashaalaachcha (स्थानान्तगोशालखरशालाच्च) — There is लुक् elision of the affix denoting 'born therein' after a word ending in स्थान and after the words 1. गोशाल and 2. खरशाल।",
    "Sūtra 4.3.36: vatsashaalaabhijidashvayukchhatabhishajovaa (वत्सशालाभिजिदश्वयुक्छतभिषजो वा) — There is optionally लुक् elision of the affix denoting 'born therein' after the words 1. वत्सशाला 2. अभिजित् 3. अश्वयुक् and 4. शतभित्।",
    "Sūtra 4.3.37: nakshatrebhyobahulam (नक्षत्रेभ्यो बहुलम्) — There is diversely लुक् elision of the affix denoting 'born therein' after an asterism.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.38: krutalabdhakreetakushalaah (कृतलब्धक्रीतकुशलाः) — An affix (one of those already taught) comes after a word in the Locative -7th case, in the sense of 'done there', 'obtained there', 'bought there' and 'dexterous therein'.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.39: praayabhavah (प्रायभवः) — After a word being in construction in the Locative -7th case, an affix (one of those ordained already) comes in the sense of 'generally found therein'.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.40: upajaanoopakarnopaneeveshthak (उपजानूपकर्णोपनीवेष्ठक्) — The affix ठक् comes in the sense of 'mostly to be found there' after the words 1. उपजानु 2. उपकरण and 3. उपोनीवि , being in the Locative -7th case.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.41: sambhoote (संभूते) — After a प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stem) or a word ending in the feminine affix ङि and आप् , being in the Locative -7th case in construction, an affix comes in the sense of 'adapted therein'. ",
    "Sūtra 4.3.42: koshaaddhany (कोशाड्ढञ्) — The affix ढञ् comes after the words कोश etc. in the sense of 'adapted to that'.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.43: kaalaatsaadhupushpyatpachyamaaneshu (कालात् साधुपुष्प्यत्पच्यमानेषु) — An affix comes after a word denoting time being in the Locative -7th case in construction, in the sense of 'being good', 'flowering' or 'ripening therein.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.44: uptecha (उप्ते च) — An affix comes after a word denoting 'time' being in the Locative -7th case in construction meaning 'sown therein'.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.45: aashvayujyaavuny (आश्वयुज्या वुञ्) — The affix वुञ् comes in the sense of 'sown' after the word आश्वयुजी।",
    "Sūtra 4.3.46: greeshmavasantaadanyatarasyaam (ग्रीष्मवसन्तादन्यतरस्याम्) — The affix वुञ् comes optionally after the words 1. ग्रीष्म and 2. वसन्त in the sense of 'sown'.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.47: deyamrune (देयमृणे) — After a प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stem) being in the Locative -7th case in construction denoting time, an affix comes in the sense of 'being then due'; provided that the thing due be 'debt'.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.48: kalaapyashvatthayavabusaadvun (कलाप्यश्वत्थयवबुसाद्वुन्) — The affix वुञ् comes in the sense of 'debt then due' after the words 1. कलापिन् 2. अश्वत्थ and 3. यवबुस् , denoting time and being in the Locative -7th case.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.49: greeshmaavarasamaadvuny (ग्रीष्मावरसमाद्वुञ्) — The affix वुञ् comes in the sense of 'debt due' after the words 1. ग्रीष्म and 2. अवरसम।",
    "Sūtra 4.3.50: samvatsaraagrahaayaneebhyaamthanycha (संवत्सराग्रहायणीभ्यां ठञ् च) — The affix ठञ् also (as well as वुञ् ) comes after the words 1. संवत्सरा 2. अग्राहायणी in the sense of 'debt due'.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.51: vyaaharatimrugah (व्याहरति मृगः) — An affix comes after a word in the Locative -7th case in construction denoting time, in the sense of 'who then wanders' and the word so formed refers to a wild beast.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.52: tadasyasodham (तदस्य सोढम्) — An affix comes after a word in the Nominative 1st-Case in construction denoting time in the sense of 'this is his habit or endurance'.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.53: tatrabhavah (तत्र भवः) — An affix comes after a word in the Locative -7th case in construction in the sense of 'who stays there'.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.54: digaadibhyoyat (दिगादिभ्यो यत्) — The affix यत् comes in the sense of 'who stays there' after the प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stems) दिक् etc.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.55: shareeraavayavaachcha (शरीरावयवाच्च) — The affix यत् comes in the sense of 'what stays there' after a word denoting a part of the body.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.56: drutikukshikalashivastyastyaherdhany (दृतिकुक्षिकलशिवस्त्यस्त्यहेर्ढञ्) — The affix ढञ् comes in the sense of 'what stays there' after the words 1. दृति 2. कुक्षि 3. कलशि 4. वस्ति 5. अस्ति and 6. अहि।",
    "Sūtra 4.3.57: greevaabhyoncha (ग्रीवाभ्योऽण् च) — The affix अण् also (as well as ढञ् ) comes after the word ग्रीवा in the sense of 'what stays there'.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.58: gambheeraanynyyah (गम्भीराञ्ञ्यः) — The affix ञ्य comes in the sense of 'who stays there' after the word गम्भीर।",
    "Sūtra 4.3.59: avyayeebhaavaachcha (अव्ययीभावाच्च) — After an अव्ययीभाव समास the affix ञ्य is used in the sense of 'who stays there'.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.60: antahapoorvapadaatthany (अन्तःपूर्वपदाट्ठञ्) — After an अव्ययीभाव समास having the word अन्तर as prior term, the affix ठञ् is used in the sense of 'who stays there'.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.61: graamaatparyanupoorvaat (ग्रामात् पर्यनुपूर्वात्) — After the word ग्राम preceded by परि or अनु (the whole being अव्ययीभाव समास ) there is the affix ठञ् in the sense of 'who stays there'.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.62: jihvaamoolaangguleshchhah (जिह्वामूलाङ्गुलेश्छः) — After the words 1. जिह्वामूल and 2. अङ्गुलि there is the affix छ in the sense of 'who stays there'.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.63: vargaantaachcha (वर्गान्ताच्च) — After a word ending with वर्ग the affix छ is used in the sense of 'who occurs there'.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.64: ashabdeyatkhaavanyatarasyaam (अशब्दे यत्खावन्यतरस्याम्) — After a word ending with वर्ग but not meaning a 'letter or word' the affixes यत् and ख are optionally used in the sense of 'who stays there'.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.65: karnalalaataatkanalamkaare (कर्णललाटात् कनलंकारे) — The affix कन् comes in the sense of 'what occurs there' after कर्ण and ललाट , the word denoting 'an ornament'. ",
    "Sūtra 4.3.66: tasyavyaakhyaanitichavyaakhyaatavyanaamnah (तस्य व्याख्यान इति च व्याख्यातव्यनाम्नः) — After the name of a subject of commentary an affix comes in the sense of 'its commentary', as well as in the sense of 'what occurs there'.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.67: bahvachontodaattaatthany (बह्वचोऽन्तोदात्ताट्ठञ्) — The affix ठञ् comes in the sense of 'staying' and 'a commentary' after a polysyllabic word having उदात्त on the final (the word being the name of a thing to be explained).",
    "Sūtra 4.3.68: kratuyajnyebhyashcha (क्रतुयज्ञेभ्यश्च) — The affix ठञ् comes in the sense of 'occurring' and 'a commentary' after the name of a work to be explained provided that such work relates to a क्रतु or a यज्ञ।",
    "Sūtra 4.3.69: adhyaayeshvevarsheh (अध्यायेष्वेवर्षेः) — The affix ठञ् comes after the name of an explainable work called after a ऋषि in the senses of 'occurring therein' or 'commentary thereon' when it refers to an अध्याय only.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.70: paurodaashapurodaashaatshthan (पौरोडाशपुरोडाशात् ष्ठन्) — The affix ष्ठन् comes in the sense of 'occurring therein' and 'commentary thereon' after the words 1. पौरोडाश and 2. पुरोडाश।",
    "Sūtra 4.3.71: chhandasoyadanau (छन्दसो यदणौ) — The affixes यत् and अण् comes in the sense of 'occurring therein' or 'commentary thereon' after the word छन्दस्।",
    "Sūtra 4.3.72: dvyajrudbraahmanarkprathamaadhvarapurashcharananaamaakhyaataatthak (द्व्यजृद्ब्राह्मणर्क्प्रथमाध्वरपुरश्चरणनामाख्याताट्ठक्) — The affix ठक् comes in the sense of 'occurring therein' or 'commentary thereon' after a word of two syllables and a word ending in short ऋ and the words 1. ब्राह्मण 2. ऋक् 3. प्रथम 4. पुरश्चरण 5. नाम 6. आख्यात and 7. नामाख्यात being the names of explainable works.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.73: anrugayanaadibhyah (अणृगयनादिभ्यः) — The affix अण् comes in the senses of 'occurring therein' and 'commentary thereon' after the words ऋगयन etc.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.74: tataagatah (तत आगतः) — The affix -- प्राग्दीव्यतोऽण् [[4.1.83]] etc. comes in the sense of 'what has come thence'.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.75: thagaayasthaanebhyah (ठगायस्थानेभ्यः) — After a word denoting sources of revenue there is the affix ठक् in the sense of 'come thence'.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.76: shundikaadibhyon (शुण्डिकादिभ्योऽण्) — The affix अण् comes in the sense of 'thence come' after the words शुण्डिक etc.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.77: vidyaayonisambandhebhyovuny (विद्यायोनिसंबन्धेभ्यो वुञ्) — The affix वुञ् comes in the sense of 'thence come' after a word denoting a person connected through the relationship or family origin.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.78: rutashthany (ऋतष्ठञ्) — The affix ठञ् comes in the sense of 'come thence' after a word ending in short ऋ and denoting a person related through learning or blood.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.79: pituryachcha (पितुर्यच्च) — The affix यत् and ठञ् comes in the sense of 'come thence' after the word पितृ।",
    "Sūtra 4.3.80: gotraadangkavat (गोत्रादङ्कवत्) — After a word ending with a Patronymic affix the rule of affix in the sense of 'thence come' is like that relating to the affix denoting its mark.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.81: hetumanushyebhyonyatarasyaamroopyah (हेतुमनुष्येभ्योऽन्यतरस्यां रूप्यः) — The affix रूप्य denotes that which from something has originated when it is added to a word denoting 'cause' or to the name of a man viewed as a cause.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.82: mayatcha (मयट् च) — After a word denoting a cause or a man viewed as a cause, there is the affix मयट् in the sense of 'come thence'.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.83: prabhavati (प्रभवति) — After a प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stem) which is the Ablative -5th case in construction, an affix (one of those already taught) comes in the sense of 'what appears for the first time'.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.84: vidooraanynyyah (विदूराञ्ञ्यः) — The affix य comes in the sense of 'what manifests itself there' after the word विदुर।",
    "Sūtra 4.3.85: tadgachchhatipathidootayoh (तद्गच्छति पथिदूतयोः) — An affix -- प्राग्दीव्यतोऽण् [[4.1.83]] etc. comes after a word in the Accusative -2nd case in construction in the sense of 'what goes thereto', provided that, which goes, is a road or a messenger.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.86: abhinishkraamatidvaaram (अभिनिष्क्रामति द्वारम्) — An affix -- प्राग्दीव्यतोऽण् [[4.1.83]] etc. comes after a word in the Accusative -2nd case in construction in the sense of 'a door which looks towards that'.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.87: adhikrutyakrutegranthe (अधिकृत्य कृते ग्रन्थे) — An affix comes after a word in the Accusative -2nd case in construction in the sense of 'made in relation to any subject' when the thing made is a 'book'.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.88: shishukrandayamasabhadvamdvendrajananaadibhyashchhah (शिशुक्रन्दयमसभद्वन्द्वेन्द्रजननादिभ्यश्छः) — The affix छ comes in the sense of 'a book made relating to a subject' after the following words in the Accusative -2nd case in construction viz. 1. शिशुक्रन्द 2. यमसभ , the द्वन्द समास and the words इन्द्रजनन etc.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.89: sosyanivaasah (सोऽस्य निवासः) — After a word in the Nominative 1st-Case in construction, an affix comes in the sense of 'this is his dwelling place'.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.90: abhijanashcha (अभिजनश्च) — After a word in the Nominative 1st-Case in construction, an affix comes in the sense of 'this is his mother-land'.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.91: aayudhajeevibhyashchhahaparvate (आयुधजीविभ्यश्छः पर्वते) — The affix छ comes after a word denoting 'mountain' in the sense of 'this is his mother-land', when it is a person who lives by arms.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.92: shandikaadibhyonyyah (शण्डिकादिभ्यो ञ्यः) — The affix ञ्य comes in the sense of 'this is his native-land' after the words शण्डिक etc.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.93: sindhutakshashilaadibhyonanyau (सिन्धुतक्षशिलादिभ्योऽणञौ) — The affixes अण् and अञ् come respectively after the words सिन्धु etc. and तक्षशिला etc. in the sense of 'this is his native land'.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.94: toodeeshalaaturavarmateekoochavaaraaddhakchhandhanyyakah (तूदीशलातुरवर्मतीकूचवाराड्ढक्छण्ढञ्यकः) — After the words 1. तूदी 2. शलातुर 3. वर्मती and 4. कूचवार come respectively the affixes 1. ढक् 2. छण् 3. ढञ् and 4. यक् in the sense of 'this is his native land'.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.95: bhaktih (भक्तिः) — An affix -- प्राग्दीव्यतोऽण् [[4.1.83]], comes after a word in the Nominative 1st-Case in construction in the sense of 'this is his object of veneration or love'.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.96: achittaadadeshakaalaatthak (अचित्ताददेशकालाट्ठक्) — After a word denoting a thing not having consciousness, but not being the name of a country or time, the affix ठक् is used in the sense of 'this is his object of devotion or love'.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.97: mahaaraajaatthany (महाराजाट्ठञ्) — The affix ठञ् comes in the sense of 'this is his object of veneration' after the word महाराज।",
    "Sūtra 4.3.98: vaasudevaarjunaabhyaamvun (वासुदेवार्जुनाभ्यां वुन्) — The affix वुञ् comes in the sense of 'this is his object of veneration' after the words 1. वासुदेव and अर्जुना।",
    "Sūtra 4.3.99: gotrakshatriyaakhyebhyobahulamvuny (गोत्रक्षत्रियाख्येभ्यो बहुलं वुञ्) — The affix वुञ् comes diversely in the sense of 'this is his object of veneration' after a word denoting गोत्र (Patronymic) or a क्षत्रिय।",
    "Sūtra 4.3.100: janapadinaamjanapadavatsarvamjanapadenasamaanashabdaanaambahuvachane (जनपदिनां जनपदवत् सर्वं जनपदेन समानशब्दानां बहुवचने) — Of words denoting Princes (literally - who are Lords of जनपद) the base and affix meaning 'this is his object of veneration' are the same, in every respect, like those of a word denoting kingdom, provided that, the Prince-denoting words have, in the plural, the same form as the Kingdom-denoting words.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.101: tenaproktam (तेन प्रोक्तम्) — After a word in the Instrumental -3rd case in construction, an affix -- प्राग्दीव्यतोऽण् [[4.1.83]] etc., comes in the sense of 'enounced by him'.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.102: tittirivaratantukhandikokhaachchhan (तित्तिरिवरतन्तुखण्डिकोखाच्छण्) — The affix छण् comes in the sense of 'enounced by him' after the words 1. तित्तिरि 2. वरतन्तु 3. खण्डिक and 4. उख।",
    "Sūtra 4.3.103: kaashyapakaushikaabhyaamrushibhyaamninih (काश्यपकौशिकाभ्यामृषिभ्यां णिनिः) — The affix णिनि comes in the sense of 'enounced by him' after the words 1. काश्यप and 2. कौशिक denoting ऋषि-s (Vedic Seers).",
    "Sūtra 4.3.104: kalaapivaishampaayanaantevaasibhyashcha (कलापिवैशम्पायनान्तेवासिभ्यश्च) — After the words denoting the pupils of कलापि and वैशम्पायन , the affix णिनि is used in the sense of 'enounced by him'.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.105: puraanaprokteshubraahmanakalpeshu (पुराणप्रोक्तेषु ब्राह्मणकल्पेषु) — The affix णिनि comes in the sense of 'enounced by him' after a word in the Instrumental -3rd case in construction when it denotes a ब्राह्मण or a कल्प-work enounced by ancient sages.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.106: shaunakaadibhyashchhandasi (शौनकादिभ्यश्छन्दसि) — The affix णिनि comes in the sense of 'enounced by him' after the words शौनक etc. in denoting छन्दस् (Vedas).",
    "Sūtra 4.3.107: kathacharakaalluk (कठचरकाल्लुक्) — The affix denoting 'enounced by him' is elided by लुक्-substitution after the words कठ and चरक।",
    "Sūtra 4.3.108: kalaapinon (कलापिनोऽण्) — The affix अण् comes in the sense of 'enounced by him' after the word कलापि।",
    "Sūtra 4.3.109: chhagalinodhinuk (छगलिनो ढिनुक्) — The affix ढिनुक् comes in the sense of 'enounced by him' after the word छगलिन।",
    "Sūtra 4.3.110: paaraasharyashilaalibhyaambhikshunatasootrayoh (पाराशर्यशिलालिभ्यां भिक्षुनटसूत्रयोः) — The affix णिनि comes in the sense of 'enounced by him' after the words 1. पाराशर्य and 2. शिलालिन् , the works enounced being भिक्षु-sūtra and नट-sūtra respectively.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.111: karmandakrushaashvaadinih (कर्मन्दकृशाश्वादिनिः) — The affix इनि comes in the sense of 'enounced by him' the thing enounced being भिक्षु-sūtra and नट-sūtra after the words 1. कर्मन्द 2. कृशाश्व।",
    "Sūtra 4.3.112: tenaikadik (तेनैकदिक्) — An affix -- प्राग्दीव्यतोऽण् [[4.1.83]] etc. comes after a word in the Instrumental -3rd case in construction in the sense of 'in the same direction with that'.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.113: tasishcha (तसिश्च) — The affix तसि comes in the sense of 'in the same direction with that'.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.114: urasoyachcha (उरसो यच्च) — The affixes यत् and तसि come in the sense of 'in the same direction with that' after the word उरस।",
    "Sūtra 4.3.115: upajnyaate (उपज्ञाते) — After a word in the Instrumental -3rd case in construction an affix is used in the sense 'discovered by him'.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.116: krutegranthe (कृते ग्रन्थे) — An affix comes after a word in the Instrumental -3rd case in construction in the sense of 'made', the thing made being 'a book'.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.117: samjnyaayaam (संज्ञायाम्) — An affix comes after a word in the Instrumental -3rd case in construction in the sense of 'made by him' when the whole word is a Name.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.118: kulaalaadibhyovuny (कुलालादिभ्यो वुञ्) — The affix वुञ् comes in the sense of 'made by him' after the words कुलाल etc. the whole word so formed being a Name.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.119: kshudraabhramaravatarapaadapaadany (क्षुद्राभ्रमरवटरपादपादञ्) — The affix अञ् comes after the words 1. क्षुद्रा 2. भ्रमर 3. वटर and 4. पादप in the sense of 'made by him', the whole word being a Name.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.120: tasyedam (तस्येदम्) — After a word in the Genitive -6th-Case in construction an affix -- प्राग्दीव्यतोऽण् [[4.1.83]] comes in the sense of 'this is his',",
    "Sūtra 4.3.121: rathaadyat (रथाद्यत्) — The affix यत् comes after रथ in the sense of 'this is his'.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.122: pattrapoorvaadany (पत्रपूर्वादञ्) — When preceded by a word denoting 'a draught animal', रथ takes the affix अञ् in the sense of 'this is his'.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.123: pattraadhvaryuparishadashcha (पत्राध्वर्युपरिषदश्च) — After a word denoting a draught-animal and after the words 1. अध्वर्यु and 2. परिषद् the affix अञ् is added.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.124: halaseeraatthak (हलसीराट्ठक्) — The affix ठक् comes in the sense of 'this is his' after the words 1. हल and 2. सीर।",
    "Sūtra 4.3.125: dvamdvaadvunvairamaithunikayoh (द्वन्द्वाद्वुन् वैरमैथुनिकयोः) — The affix वुञ् comes in the sense of 'this is his' after द्वन्द compound of words denoting 'mutual enmity' or 'matrimonial relationship'.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.126: gotracharanaadvuny (गोत्रचरणाद्वुञ्) — The affix वुञ् comes in the sense of 'this is his' after the words denoting गोत्र (Patronymic/Family-names) of Vedic schools.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.127: samghaangkalakshaneshvanyyanyinyaaman (संघाङ्कलक्षणेष्वञ्यञिञामण्) — The affix अण् comes in the sense of 'this is his' after a गोत्र (Patronymic) word ending with the affix अञ् or यञ् or इञ् , the words so formed expressing a multitude, a mark or a sign. ",
    "Sūtra 4.3.128: shaakalaadvaa (शाकलाद्वा) — The affix अण् optionally comes in the sense of 'this is his congregation, mark, sign or hamlet' after the word शाकल।",
    "Sūtra 4.3.129: chhandogaukthikayaajnyikabahvruchanataanynyyah (छन्दोगौक्थिकयाज्ञिकबह्वृचनटाञ्ञ्यः) — The affix ञ्य comes in the sense of 'this is his Law or Tradition' after the words 1. छान्दोग 2. औक्थिक 3. याज्ञिक 4. बह्वृच and 5. नट।",
    "Sūtra 4.3.130: nadandamaanavaantevaasishu (न दण्डमाणवान्तेवासिषु) — The affix वुञ् is not used after a Family-name when it denotes 'a beginner pupil' and 'a boarder pupil'.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.131: raivatikaadibhyashchhah (रैवतिकादिभ्यश्छः) — The affix छ comes in the sense of 'this is his' after the words रैवतिक etc.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.132: kaupinyjalahaastipadaadan (कौपिञ्जलहास्तिपदादण्) — The affix अण् comes in the sense of 'this is his' after the words 1. कौपिञ्जल 2. हास्तिपद।",
    "Sūtra 4.3.133: aatharvanikasyekalopashcha (आथर्वणिकस्येकलोपश्च) — The affix अण् comes in the sense of 'this is his' after the word आथर्वणिक and the penultimate इक् is elided.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.134: tasyavikaarah (तस्य विकारः) — An affix -- प्राग्दीव्यतोऽण् [[4.1.83]] etc., comes after a word in the Genitive -6th-Case in construction in the sense of 'a modification thereof'.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.135: avayavechapraanyoshadhivrukshebhyah (अवयवे च प्राण्योषधिवृक्षेभ्यः) — An affix comes after a word denoting an animal, a herb and a tree in Genitive -6th-Case in construction in the sense 'this is its part' (as well as 'this is its modification').",
    "Sūtra 4.3.136: bilvaadibhyon (बिल्वादिभ्योऽण्) — The affix अण् comes in the sense of 'its modification or its part' after the words बिल्व etc.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.137: kopadhaachcha (कोपधाच्च) — After a word having क् as its penultimate, the affix अण् comes in the sense of modification or a part or both, as appropriate.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.138: trapujatunohashuk (त्रपुजतुनोः षुक्) — The affix अण् with the augment षुक् comes in the sense of 'its modification' after the words त्रपुन् and जतुन्।",
    "Sūtra 4.3.139: orany (ओरञ्) — The affix अण् comes in the sense of 'modification or part' (provided that the word has not the अनुदात्त - grave accent on the first syllable).",
    "Sūtra 4.3.140: anudaattaadeshcha (अनुदात्तादेश्च) — The affix अञ् comes in the sense of 'modification or part' after a word having अनुदात्त - grave accent on the first syllable.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.141: palaashaadibhyovaa (पलाशादिभ्यो वा) — The affix अञ् comes optionally in the sense of 'modification or part' after the words पलाश etc.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.142: shamyaashtlany (शम्याष्ट्लञ्) — The affix ट्लञ् comes in the sense of 'modification or part' after the word शमी।",
    "Sūtra 4.3.143: mayadvaitayorbhaashaayaamabhakshyaachchhaadanayoh (मयड्वैतयोर्भाषायामभक्ष्याच्छादनयोः) — The affix मयट् comes optionally after any base, in these two meanings of 'product' and 'part' in secular language when neither food nor clothing is spoken of.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.144: nityamvruddhasharaadibhyah (नित्यं वृद्धशरादिभ्यः) — The affix मयट् comes in the sense of 'product' and 'part' when neither food nor clothing is spoken of, invariably after वृद्ध words and शर etc.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.145: goshchapureeshe (गोश्च पुरीषे) — The affix मयट् comes after the word गो in the sense of 'its dung'.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.146: pishtaachcha (पिष्टाच्च) — The affix मयट् invariably comes in the sense of 'its product or part' after the word पिष्ट।",
    "Sūtra 4.3.147: samjnyaayaamkan (संज्ञायां कन्) — The affix कन् comes in the sense of 'product' after the word पिष्ट , the whole word being a Name.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.148: vreehehapurodaashe (व्रीहेः पुरोडाशे) — The affix मयट् comes after the word व्रीहि in the sense of a पुरोडाश।",
    "Sūtra 4.3.149: asamjnyaayaamtilayavaabhyaam (असंज्ञायां तिलयवाभ्याम्) — The affix मयट् comes in the sense of 'product' after the words तिल and यवा - the whole not being a name.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.150: dvyachashchhandasi (द्व्यचश्छन्दसि) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas) after a disyllabic word the affix मयट् comes in the sense of 'product or part'.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.151: notvadvardhrabilvaat (नोत्वद्वर्ध्रबिल्वात्) — The affix मयट् does not come in the छन्दस् (Vedas) after the disyllabic words having a short vowel उ in them, nor after the words 1. वर्ध्र and 2. बिल्वा।",
    "Sūtra 4.3.152: taalaadibhyon (तालादिभ्योऽण्) — The affix अण् comes in the sense of 'its product or part' after the words ताला etc.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.153: jaataroopebhyahaparimaane (जातरूपेभ्यः परिमाणे) — The affix अण् comes after a word denoting 'gold' when the sense is a weight or measure.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.154: praanirajataadibhyony (प्राणिरजतादिभ्योऽञ्) — The affix अञ् comes in the sense of 'product or part' after the words expressing living beings and after रजत etc.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.155: nyitashchatatpratyayaat (ञितश्च तत्प्रत्ययात्) — The affix अञ् comes in the sense of 'product or part' after a word which ends in an affix having an indicatory ञ् , such affix denoting 'its product or part'.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.156: kreetavatparimaanaat (क्रीतवत् परिमाणात्) — After a word denoting 'a measure' the affix expressing 'its product or part' is the same as the affix having the sense of 'purchased'.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.157: ushtraadvuny (उष्ट्राद्वुञ्) — The affix वुञ् comes in the sense of 'product or part' after the word उष्ट्र।",
    "Sūtra 4.3.158: umornayorvaa (उमोर्णयोर्वा) — The affix वुञ् comes optionally in the sense of 'product or part' after the words 1. उमा and 2. ऊर्णा।",
    "Sūtra 4.3.159: enyaadhany (एण्या ढञ्) — The affix ढञ् comes optionally in the sense of 'product or part' after the feminine word एणी।",
    "Sūtra 4.3.160: gopayasoryat (गोपयसोर्यत्) — The affix यत् comes in the sense of 'product or part' after the words 1. गो and 2. पयस्।",
    "Sūtra 4.3.161: droshcha (द्रोश्च) — The affix यत् comes in the sense of 'product or part' after the word द्रु।",
    "Sūtra 4.3.162: maanevayah (माने वयः) — The affix वय comes in the sense of 'product' after the word द्रु , the word meaning 'a measure'.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.163: phaleluk (फले लुक्) — The affix denoting 'product or part' is लुक् elided when such a product or part is 'a fruit'.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.164: plakshaadibhyon (प्लक्षादिभ्योऽण्) — The affix अण् comes in the sense of 'product or part, it being a fruit' after the words प्लक्ष etc.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.165: jambvaavaa (जम्ब्वा वा) — The affix अण् optionally comes in denoting a fruit after the word जम्बु।",
    "Sūtra 4.3.166: lupcha (लुप् च) — The affix denoting 'fruit' is optionally elided by लुप् after the word जम्बु।",
    "Sūtra 4.3.167: hareetakyaadibhyashcha (हरीतक्यादिभ्यश्च) — The affix denoting 'fruit' is elided by लुप् after the words हरीतकी etc.",
    "Sūtra 4.3.168: kamseeyaparashavyayoryanyanyaulukcha (कंसीयपरशव्ययोर्यञञौ लुक् च) — The affixes यञ् and अञ् come respectively in the sense of 'its product' after the words 1. कंसीय and 2. परशव्य and there is लुक् elision (of the छ and यत् affixes of those words).",
    "Sūtra 4.4.1: praagvahateshthak (प्राग्वहतेष्ठक्) — The affix ठक् comes as a governing affix in the senses enumerated hereafter up to sūtra [[4.4.76]].",
    "Sūtra 4.4.2: tenadeevyatikhanatijayatijitam (तेन दीव्यति खनति जयति जितम्) — The affix ठक् comes after a word in the Instrumental -3rd case in construction in the sense of 'he plays', 'he digs', 'he conquers' or 'he is conquered'.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.3: samskrutam (संस्कृतम्) — The affix ठक् comes after a word in the Instrumental -3rd case in construction, in the sense of 'refined thereby'.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.4: kulatthakopadhaadan (कुलत्थकोपधादण्) — After the word कुलत्थ and after the words having a penultimate क् , the affix अण् is added in the sense of 'refined or prepared therewith'.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.5: tarati (तरति) — The affix ठक् comes after a word in the Instrumental -3rd case in construction, in the sense of 'he crosses thereby over the waters'.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.6: gopuchchhaatthany (गोपुच्छाट्ठञ्) — The affix ठञ् comes after the word गोपुच्छ in the sense of 'he crosses thereby'.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.7: naudvyachashthan (नौद्व्यचष्ठन्) — The affix ठञ् comes after the word नौ and after bases having two syllables in the sense of 'he crosses therewith'.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.8: charati (चरति) — After a word in the Instrumental -3rd case in construction comes the affix ठक् in the sense of 'he goes on by means thereof'.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.9: aakarshaatshthal (आकर्षात् ष्ठल्) — The affix ष्ठल् comes in the sense of 'he goes on by means thereof' after the word आकर्ष।",
    "Sūtra 4.4.10: parpaadibhyahashthan (पर्पादिभ्यः ष्ठन्) — The affix ष्ठन् comes in the sense of 'he goes on, by means thereof' after the words पर्प etc.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.11: shvaganaatthanycha (श्वगणाट्ठञ्च) — The affixes ठञ् and ष्ठन् , come after the word श्वगण , in the sense of 'he goes by means thereof'.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.12: vetanaadibhyojeevati (वेतनादिभ्यो जीवति) — The affix ठक् comes in the sense of 'he lives thereby' after the words वेतन etc. being in the Instrumental -3rd case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.13: vasnakrayavikrayaatthan (वस्नक्रयविक्रयाट्ठन्) — The affix ठन् comes in the sense of 'he lives thereby' after the words 1. वस्न 2. क्रय and 3. विक्रय being in the Instrumental -3rd case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.14: aayudhaachchhacha (आयुधाच्छ च) — The affixes छ and ठन् come in the sense of 'he conveys thereby' after the word आयुध।",
    "Sūtra 4.4.15: haratyutsanggaadibhyah (हरत्युत्सङ्गादिभ्यः) — The affix ठक् comes in the sense of 'he conveys thereby' after the words उत्सङ्ग etc. being in the Instrumental -3rd case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.16: bhastraadibhyahashthan (भस्त्रादिभ्यः ष्ठन्) — The affix ष्ठन् comes in the sense of 'he conveys' after the words भस्त्र etc. being in the Instrumental -3rd case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.17: vibhaashaavivadhaveevadhaat (विभाषा विवधवीवधात्) — The affix ष्ठन् optionally comes in the sense of 'he conveys' after the words 1. विवध and 2. वीवध being in the Instrumental -3rd case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.18: ankutilikaayaah (अण् कुटिलिकायाः) — The affix अण् comes in the sense of 'he conveys' after the word कुटिलिका in the Instrumental -3rd case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.19: nirvruttekshadyootaadibhyah (निर्वृत्तेऽक्षद्यूतादिभ्यः) — The affix ठक् comes in the sense of 'completed thereby' after the words अक्षद्यूत etc. being in the Instrumental -3rd case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.20: ktrermamnityam (क्त्रेर्मम् नित्यम्) — The affix मप् comes always after the words ending in the affix त्रि, in the sense of 'completed thereby'.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.21: apamityayaachitaabhyaamkakkanau (अपमित्ययाचिताभ्यां कक्कनौ) — The affixes कक् and कन् come respectively after the words 1. अपमित्य and 2. याचित when the sense is that of completion.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.22: samsrushte (संसृष्टे) — The affix ठक् comes after a word in the Instrumental -3rd case in construction when the sense is 'mixed therewith'.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.23: choornaadinih (चूर्णादिनिः) — The affix इनि comes after the word चूर्ण when the sense is 'mixed therewith'.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.24: lavanaalluk (लवणाल्लुक्) — The affix ठक् meaning 'mixed therewith' is लुक् elided after the word लवण।",
    "Sūtra 4.4.25: mudgaadan (मुद्गादण्) — The affix अण् comes after the word मुद्ग when the sense is 'mixed therewith'.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.26: vyanyjanairupasikte (व्यञ्जनैरुपसिक्ते) — The affix ठक् comes after a word denoting a condiment, being in the Instrumental -3rd case in construction when the sense is 'sprinkled therewith'.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.27: ojassahombhasaavartate (ओजस्सहोऽम्भसा वर्तते) — The affix ठक् comes in the sense of 'it exists' after the words 1. ओजस् 2. सहस् and 3. अभस् being in the Instrumental -3rd case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.28: tatpratyanupoorvameepalomakoolam (तत् प्रत्यनुपूर्वमीपलोमकूलम्) — The affix ठक् comes in the sense of 'it exists' after 1. ईप 2. लोम and 3. कूल preceded by अनु and प्रति ; the word being in the Accusative -2nd case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.29: parimukhamcha (परिमुखं च) — The affix ठक् comes in the sense of 'it exists' after the word परिमुख being it the Accusative -2nd case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.30: prayachchhatigarhyam (प्रयच्छति गर्ह्यम्) — The affix ठक् comes after a word in the Accusative -2nd case in construction when the sense is 'he gives', the motive being mean.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.31: kuseedadashaikaadashaatshthanshthachau (कुसीददशैकादशात् ष्ठन्ष्ठचौ) — The affixes ष्ठन् and ष्ठच् come respectively after the words कुसीद and दशैकादश when the sense is 'he gives for a mean motive'.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.32: unychhati (उञ्छति) — The affix ठक् comes after a word in the Accusative -2nd case in construction when the sense is 'who gleans that'.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.33: rakshati (रक्षति) — The affix ठक् comes after a word in the Accusative -2nd case in construction when the sense is 'he aids or protects that'.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.34: shabdadarduramkaroti (शब्ददर्दुरं करोति) — The affix ठक् comes after a word in the Accusative -2nd case in construction when the sense is 'who makes a sound or croaking'.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.35: pakshimatsyamrugaanhanti (पक्षिमत्स्यमृगान् हन्ति) — The affix ठक् comes after a word in the Accusative -2nd case in construction denoting birds, fishes or wild beasts, when the sense is 'who kills that'.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.36: paripanthamchatishthati (परिपन्थं च तिष्ठति) — The affix ठक् also comes in the sense of 'who stays' after the word परिपन्थ , the word being in the Accusative -2nd case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.37: maathottarapadapadavyanupadamdhaavati (माथोत्तरपदपदव्यनुपदं धावति) — The affix ठक् also comes in the sense of 'who runs' after a word having माथ as its second term and after the words पदवी and अनुपद।",
    "Sūtra 4.4.38: aakrandaatthanycha (आक्रन्दाट्ठञ्च) — The affixes ठञ् and ठक् come after the word आक्रन्द being in the Accusative -2nd case in construction in the sense of 'who runs'.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.39: padottarapadamgruhnaati (पदोत्तरपदं गृह्णाति) — The affix ठक् comes in the sense of 'who takes' after a word having पद as its second member, the word being in the Accusative -2nd case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.40: pratikanthaarthalalaamamcha (प्रतिकण्ठार्थललामं च) — The affix ठक् comes in the sense of 'who takes' after the words 1. प्रतिकण्ठा 2. अर्थ and 3. ललाम being in the Accusative -2nd case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.41: dharmamcharati (धर्मं चरति) — The affix ठक् comes after the word धर्मं being in the Accusative -2nd case in construction in the sense of 'who practices that'.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.42: pratipathametithamshcha (प्रतिपथमेति ठंश्च) — The affix ठन् and ठक् comes after the word प्रतिपथम् , in the Accusative -2nd case in construction in the sense of 'who goes'.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.43: samavaayaansamavaiti (समवायान् समवैति) — The affix ठन् and ठक् comes after the words in the Accusative -2nd case in construction denoting combination in the sense 'who assembles there'.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.44: parishadonyah (परिषदो ण्यः) — The affix ण्य comes after the word परिषद in the sense of 'who assembles there'.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.45: senaayaavaa (सेनाया वा) — The affix ण्य comes optionally after the word सेना in the sense of 'who assembles there'.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.46: samjnyaayaamlalaatakukkutyaupashyati (संज्ञायां ललाटकुक्कुट्यौ पश्यति) — The affix ठक् comes in the sense of 'who sees that' after the words 1. ललाट and 2. कुक्कुटी in the Accusative -2nd case in construction, the whole word being a Name.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.47: tasyadharmyam (तस्य धर्म्यम्) — The affix ठक् comes after a word in the Genitive -6th-Case in construction in the sense of 'its usage'.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.48: anmahishyaadibhyah (अण् महिष्यादिभ्यः) — The affix अण् comes in the sense of 'its law' after the word महिषी etc.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.49: rutony (ऋतोऽञ्) — The affix अञ् comes in the sense of 'its law' after a प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stem) ending ऋ।",
    "Sūtra 4.4.50: avakrayah (अवक्रयः) — The affix ठक् comes in the sense of 'its tax' after a word in the Genitive -6th-Case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.51: tadasyapanyam (तदस्य पण्यम्) — The affix ठक् comes in the sense of 'this is whose saleable commodity' after a word in the Nominative 1st-Case in construction denoting the thing to be sold.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.52: lavanaatthany (लवणाट्ठञ्) — The affix ठञ् comes in the sense of 'this is whose saleable commodity' after the word लवण।",
    "Sūtra 4.4.53: kisharaadibhyahashthan (किशरादिभ्यः ष्ठन्) — The affix ष्ठन् comes in the sense of 'this is whose saleable commodity' after the words किशर etc.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.54: shalaalunonyatarasyaam (शलालुनोऽन्यतरस्याम्) — The affix ष्ठन् comes in the sense of 'this is whose saleable commodity' after the word शलालुन।",
    "Sūtra 4.4.55: shilpam (शिल्पम्) — The affix ठक् comes in the sense of 'this is whose Art' after a word denoting Art in the Nominative 1st-Case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.56: maddukajharjharaadananyatarasyaam (मड्डुकझर्झरादणन्यतरस्याम्) — The affix अण् optionally comes in the sense of 'this is whose Art' after the words 1. मड्डुक and 2. झर्झर।",
    "Sūtra 4.4.57: praharanam (प्रहरणम्) — The affix ठक् comes in the sense of 'this is whose weapon' after a word denoting 'a weapon' and being in the Nominative 1st-Case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.58: parashvadhaatthanycha (परश्वधाट्ठञ्च) — The affixes ठञ् and ठक् come in the sense of 'this is whose weapon' after the word परश्वध।",
    "Sūtra 4.4.59: shaktiyashtyoreekak (शक्तियष्ट्योरीकक्) — The affix ईकक् comes in the sense of 'this is whose weapon' after the words 1. शक्ति and 2. यष्ट्यि।",
    "Sūtra 4.4.60: astinaastidishtammatih (अस्तिनास्तिदिष्टं मतिः) — The affix ठक् comes in the sense of 'this is whose belief' after the words 1. अस्ति 2. नास्ति and 3. दिष्ट।",
    "Sūtra 4.4.61: sheelam (शीलम्) — The affix ठक् comes in the sense of 'whose habit is this' after a word in the Nominative 1st-Case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.62: chhatraadibhyonah (छत्रादिभ्यो णः) — The affix ण comes in the sense of 'whose habit is this' after the words छत्र etc.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.63: karmaadhyayanevruttam (कर्माध्ययने वृत्तम्) — The affix ठक् comes in the sense of 'this is his act, occurring in study' after a word in the Nominative 1st-Case in construction, if such a word is an कर्म (act) which has वृत्तम् (occurred) अध्ययन in (study).",
    "Sūtra 4.4.64: bahvachpoorvapadaatthach (बह्वच्पूर्वपदाट्ठच्) — The affix ठच् comes in the sense of 'this is whose act occurring in study' after a compound having polysyllabic word as a prior member.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.65: hitambhakshaah (हितं भक्षाः) — The affix ठक् comes after a word expressing food, in the Nominative 1st-Case in construction, in the sense of 'this is wholesome diet for whom'.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.66: tadasmaideeyateniyuktam (तदस्मै दीयते नियुक्तम्) — The affix ठक् comes in the sense of 'to whom this is to be given rightfully' after a word expressing the thing to be given, in the Nominative 1st-Case (तद्) in construction, the force of the affix being that of a Dative -4th Case.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.67: shraanaamaamsaudanaattithan (श्राणामांसौदनाट्टिठन्) — The affix टिठन् comes in the sense of 'to whom this is given rightfully' after the words 1. श्राणा and 2. मांसौदन।",
    "Sūtra 4.4.68: bhaktaadananyatarasyaam (भक्तादणन्यतरस्याम्) — The affix अण् optionally comes after the word भक्त in the sense of 'to whom this is to be given rightfully'.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.69: tatraniyuktah (तत्र नियुक्तः) — The affix ठक् comes in the sense of 'appointed there' after a word in the Locative -7th case (तत्र) in construction.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.70: agaaraantaatthan (अगारान्ताट्ठन्) — The affix ठन् comes in the sense of 'appointed there' after a word ending with अगार।",
    "Sūtra 4.4.71: adhyaayinyadeshakaalaat (अध्यायिन्यदेशकालात्) — The affix ठक् comes in the sense of 'who studies there' after a word in the Locative -7th case in construction, denoting an improper place or time.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.72: kathinaantaprastaarasamsthaaneshuvyavaharati (कठिनान्तप्रस्तारसंस्थानेषु व्यवहरति) — The affix ठक् comes in the sense of 'who transacts business therein', after compounds ending in कठिन and after प्रस्तार, being in the Locative -7th case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.73: nikatevasati (निकटे वसति) — The affix ठक् comes in the sense of 'who dwells' after the Locative word निकट।",
    "Sūtra 4.4.74: aavasathaatshthal (आवसथात् ष्ठल्) — The affix ष्ठल् comes in the sense of 'who dwells there' after the word आवसथ in the Locative -7th case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.75: praagghitaadyat (प्राग्घिताद्यत्) — In each sūtra from this one forward to -- तस्मै हितम् [[5.1.5]], the affix यत् bears rule.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.76: tadvahatirathayugapraasanggam (तद्वहति रथयुगप्रासङ्गम्) — The affix यत् comes in the sense of 'what bears it' after the words 1. रथ 2. युग and 3. प्रासङ्ग being in the Accusative -2nd case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.77: dhuroyaddhakau (धुरो यड्ढकौ) — The affixes यत् and ढक् comes in the sense of 'what bears it' after the word धुर in the Accusative -2nd case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.78: khahasarvadhuraat (खः सर्वधुरात्) — The affix ख comes in the sense of 'what bears it' after the word सर्वधुरा being in Accusative -2nd case construction.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.79: ekadhuraallukcha (एकधुराल्लुक् च) — The affix ख comes in the sense of 'what bears it' after the word एकधुरा being in Accusative -2nd case construction, the affix is optionally elided too.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.80: shakataadan (शकटादण्) — The affix अण् comes in the sense of 'what bears it' after the word शकट being in Accusative -2nd case construction.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.81: halaseeraatthak (हलसीराट्ठक्) — The affix ठक् comes in the sense of 'what bears it' after the words 1. हल and 2. सीर in Accusative -2nd case construction.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.82: samjnyaayaamjanyaah (संज्ञायां जन्याः) — The affix यत् comes in the sense of 'what bears it' after the word जनी being in Accusative -2nd case construction, the whole word being a Name.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.83: vidhyatyadhanushaa (विध्यत्यधनुषा) — The affix यत् comes in the sense of 'what pierces it' after a word in the Accusative -2nd case in construction, provided that it is not a bow with which anything is pierced.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.84: dhanaganamlabdhaa (धनगणं लब्धा) — The affix यत् comes in the sense of 'who obtains it' after the words 1. धन and 2. गण being in the Accusative -2nd case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.85: annaannah (अन्नाण्णः) — The affix ण comes in the sense of 'who obtains it' after the word अन्न , in the Accusative -2nd case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.86: vashamgatah (वशं गतः) — The affix यत् comes in the sense of 'gone' after the word वश 'control', being in the Accusative -2nd case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.87: padamasmindrushyam (पदमस्मिन् दृश्यम्) — The affix यत् comes in the sense of 'in it is visible' after the word पद being in the Nominative 1st-Case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.88: moolamasyaabarhi (मूलमस्याबर्हि) — The affix यत् comes in the sense of 'whose root is eradicated' after the word मूल being in the Nominative 1st-Case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.89: samjnyaayaamdhenushyaa (संज्ञायां धेनुष्या) — The word धेनुष्या is irregularly formed being a Name.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.90: gruhapatinaasamyuktenyyah (गृहपतिना संयुक्ते ञ्यः) — The affix ञ्य comes in the sense of 'joined with' after the word गृहपति in the Instrumental -3rd case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.91: nauvayodharmavishamoolamoolaseetaatulaabhyastaaryatulyapraapyavadhyaanaamyasamasamitasammiteshu (नौवयोधर्मविषमूलमूलसीतातुलाभ्यस्तार्यतुल्यप्राप्यवध्यानाम्यसमसमितसम्मितेषु) — The affix यत् comes after the words 1. नौ 'a boat' 2. वयस् 'age' 3. धर्म 'merit' 4. विष 'poison' 5. मूल 'a root' 6. मूल 'a capital' 7. सीता 'a furrow' and 8. तुला 'a balance', in the senses respectively of 1. 'to be crossed' 2. 'like' 3. 'attainable' 4. 'to be put to death' 5. 'to be bent down' 6. 'equivalent to' 7. 'united with' and 8. 'equally measured'.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.92: dharmapathyarthanyaayaadanapete (धर्मपथ्यर्थन्यायादनपेते) — The affix यत् comes in the sense of 'not deviating there from' after the words 1. धर्म 2. पथिन् 3. अर्थ and 4. न्याय ।",
    "Sūtra 4.4.93: chhandasonirmite (छन्दसो निर्मिते) — The affix यत् comes in the sense of 'made' after the word छन्दस् being in the Instrumental -3rd case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.94: urasoncha (उरसोऽण् च) — The affixes अण् and यत् come in the sense of 'made' after उरस् in the Instrumental -3rd case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.95: hrudayasyapriyah (हृदयस्य प्रियः) — The affix यत् comes in the sense of 'loved' after the word हृदय being in the Genitive -6th-Case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.96: bandhanecharshau (बन्धने चर्षौ) — The affix यत् comes in the sense of 'a bond' after the word हृदय being in the Genitive -6th-Case construction, when the word denotes a 'hymn'.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.97: matajanahalaatkaranajalpakarsheshu (मतजनहलात् करणजल्पकर्षेषु) — The affix यत् comes after words 1. मत 2. जन and 3. हल in the senses respectively of 1. 'means 2. 'gossip' and 3. 'drawing', the words being in the Genitive -6th-Case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.98: tatrasaadhuh (तत्र साधुः) — The affix यत् comes in the sense of 'excellent in regard thereto' after a word in the Locative -7th case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.99: pratijanaadibhyahakhany (प्रतिजनादिभ्यः खञ्) — The affix खञ् comes in the sense of 'excellent in regard thereto' after the words प्रतिजन etc.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.100: bhaktaannah (भक्ताण्णः) — The affix ण comes in the sense of 'excellent with regard thereto' after the word भक्त।",
    "Sūtra 4.4.101: parishadonyah (परिषदो ण्यः) — The affix ण्य comes in the sense of 'excellent with regard thereto' after the word परिषद।",
    "Sūtra 4.4.102: kathaadibhyashthak (कथादिभ्यष्ठक्) — The affix ठक् comes in the sense of 'excellent with regard thereto' after the words कथ etc.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.103: gudaadibhyashthany (गुडादिभ्यष्ठञ्) — The affix ठञ् comes in the sense of 'excellent with regard thereto' after the words गुड etc.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.104: pathyatithivasatisvapaterdhany (पथ्यतिथिवसतिस्वपतेर्ढञ्) — The affix ठञ् comes in the sense of 'excellent with regard thereto' after the words 1. पथि 2. अतिथि 3. वसति and 4. स्वपति।",
    "Sūtra 4.4.105: sabhaayaayah (सभाया यः) — The affix यत् comes in the sense of 'excellent with regard thereto' after the word सभा ।",
    "Sūtra 4.4.106: dhashchhandasi (ढश्छन्दसि) — The affix ढ comes in the sense of 'excellent with regard thereto' after the word सभा in the छन्दस् (Vedas).",
    "Sūtra 4.4.107: samaanateerthevaasee (समानतीर्थे वासी) — The affix यत् comes in the sense of 'resident therein' after the word समानतीर्थ in the Locative -7th case construction.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.108: samaanodareshayitochodaattah (समानोदरे शयित ओ चोदात्तः) — The affix यत् comes in the sense of 'who sleeps' after the word समानोदर in the Locative -7th case construction and the उदात्त falls on the letter ओ।",
    "Sūtra 4.4.109: sodaraadyah (सोदराद्यः) — The affix य comes in the sense of 'who sleeps' after the word सोदर the word being in the Locative -7th case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.110: bhavechhandasi (भवे छन्दसि) — The affix यत् comes in the sense of 'what stays here' in the छन्दस् (Vedas) when in the Locative -7th case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.111: paathonadeebhyaamdyan (पाथोनदीभ्यां ड्यण्) — The affix ड्यण comes in the sense of 'what stays there' after the words 1. पाथस् and 2. नदी , in the छन्दस् (Vedas), whereby the last vowel with the consonant following is elided.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.112: veshantahimavadbhyaaman (वेशन्तहिमवद्भ्यामण्) — The affix अण् comes in the sense of 'what stays there' after the words 1. वेशन्त and 2. हिमवत् , in the छन्दस् (Vedas).",
    "Sūtra 4.4.113: srotasovibhaashaadyaddyau (स्रोतसो विभाषा ड्यड्ड्यौ) — The affixes ड्यत् and ड्य come in the sense of 'what stays there' after the word स्रोतस् and before these affixes the final syllable अस् of स्रोतस् is elided, in the छन्दस् (Vedas).",
    "Sūtra 4.4.114: sagarbhasayoothasanutaadyan (सगर्भसयूथसनुताद्यन्) — The affix यन् comes in the sense of 'what stays there' after the words 1. सगर्भ 2. सयूथ and 3. सनुत।",
    "Sūtra 4.4.115: tugraadghan (तुग्राद्घन्) — The affix धन् comes in the sense of 'what stays there' after the word तुग्र , in the छन्दस् (Vedas).",
    "Sūtra 4.4.116: agraadyat (अग्राद्यत्) — The affix यत् comes in the sense of 'what stays there' after the word अग्र , in the छन्दस् (Vedas).",
    "Sūtra 4.4.117: ghachchhaucha (घच्छौ च) — The affixes घच् and छ come in the sense of 'what stays there' after the word अग्र , in the छन्दस् (Vedas).",
    "Sūtra 4.4.118: samudraabhraadghah (समुद्राभ्राद्घः) — The affix घ comes in the sense of 'what stays there' after the words 1. समुद्र and 2. अभ्र , in the छन्दस् (Vedas).",
    "Sūtra 4.4.119: barhishidattam (बर्हिषि दत्तम्) — The affix यत् comes in the sense of 'given' after the word बर्हिष् in the Locative -7th case in construction, in the छन्दस् (Vedas).",
    "Sūtra 4.4.120: dootasyabhaagakarmanee (दूतस्य भागकर्मणी) — The affix यत् comes in the sense of 'its share' or 'its duty' after the word दूत in the Genitive -6th-Case in construction, in the छन्दस् (Vedas).",
    "Sūtra 4.4.121: rakshoyaatoonaamhananee (रक्षोयातूनां हननी) — The affix यत् comes in the sense of 'killer' after the words 1. रक्षा and 2. यातू in the Genitive -6th-Case in construction, in the छन्दस् (Vedas).",
    "Sūtra 4.4.122: revateejagateehavishyaabhyahaprashasye (रेवतीजगतीहविष्याभ्यः प्रशस्ये) — The affix यत् comes in the sense of 'praising' after the words 1. रेवती 2. जगतीand 3. हविष्य in the Genitive -6th-Case in construction, in the छन्दस् (Vedas).",
    "Sūtra 4.4.123: asurasyasvam (असुरस्य स्वम्) — The affix यत् comes in the sense of 'property' after the word असुर in the Genitive -6th-Case in construction, in the छन्दस् (Vedas).",
    "Sūtra 4.4.124: maayaayaaman (मायायामण्) — The affix अण् comes in the sense of 'glamour' after the word असुर in the Genitive 6th-Case in construction, in the छन्दस् (Vedas).",
    "Sūtra 4.4.125: tadvaanaasaamupadhaanomantriteeshtakaasulukchamatoh (तद्वानासामुपधानो मन्त्र इतीष्टकासु लुक् च मतोः) — The affix यत् comes in the छन्दस् (Vedas) after a प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stem) in the Nominative 1st-Case in construction, ending with the affix मतुप् when the sense is 'this is their मन्त्र of putting up' provided that the things put are bricks and the affix मतुप् is लुक् elided.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.126: ashvimaanan (अश्विमानण्) — The affix अण् comes in the छन्दस् (Vedas) after the words अश्विमान् to denote bricks put up with the मन्त्र containing the word अश्विन् and the affix मतुप् is लुक् elided.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.127: vayasyaasumoordhnomatup (वयस्यासु मूर्ध्नो मतुप्) — The affix मतुप् is added in the छन्दस् (Vedas) to the word मूर्धन्वत् in expressing bricks collected with the मन्त्र containing the word वयस्।",
    "Sūtra 4.4.128: matvarthemaasatanvoh (मत्वर्थे मासतन्वोः) — The affix यत् comes in the छन्दस् (Vedas) with the force of मतुप् after a word in the Nominative 1st-Case in construction, the word so formed meaning 'a month' or 'a body'.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.129: madhornyacha (मधोर्ञ च) — The affixes यत् and ष come with the force of मतुप् in the छन्दस् (Vedas) after the word मधु।",
    "Sūtra 4.4.130: ojasohaniyatkhau (ओजसोऽहनि यत्खौ) — The affixes यत् and ख come with the force of मतुप् after the word ओजस् when 'a day' is meant.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.131: veshoyashaaderbhagaadyal (वेशोयशआदेर्भगाद्यल्) — The affix थल् comes in the छन्दस् (Vedas) with the force of मतुप् after the word भग having the words 1. वेशस् or 2. यशस् in the beginning.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.132: khacha (ख च) — The affix ख comes after the words 1. वेशोभग and 2. यशोभग in the छन्दस् (Vedas) with the force of मतुप्।",
    "Sūtra 4.4.133: poorvaihikrutaminayaucha (पूर्वैः कृतमिनयौ च) — The affixes इन , ख and य come in the sense of 'made by them' after the word पूर्व 'fore-fathers' in the Instrumental -3rd case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.134: adbhihasamskrutam (अद्भिः संस्कृतम्) — The affix यत् comes in the sense of 'sanctified' after the word अपस् in the Instrumental -3rd case in construction, in the छन्दस् (Vedas).",
    "Sūtra 4.4.135: sahasrenasammitaughah (सहस्रेण संमितौ घः) — The affix घ comes in the sense of 'like' after the word सहस्र in the Instrumental -3rd case in construction, in the छन्दस् (Vedas).",
    "Sūtra 4.4.136: mataucha (मतौ च) — The affix घ comes in the छन्दस् (Vedas) with the force of मतुप् after the word सहस्र।",
    "Sūtra 4.4.137: somamarhatiyah (सोममर्हति यः) — The affix य comes in the sense of 'who deserves that' after the word सोम in the Accusative -2nd case in construction, in the छन्दस् (Vedas).",
    "Sūtra 4.4.138: mayecha (मये च) — The affix य comes in the छन्दस् (Vedas) after the word सोम with the force of मतुप्।",
    "Sūtra 4.4.139: madhoh (मधोः) — The affix यत् comes in the छन्दस् (Vedas) after the word मधु with the force of मतुप्।",
    "Sūtra 4.4.140: vasohasamoohecha (वसोः समूहे च) — The affix यत् comes in the sense of 'a collection' after the word वसु , as well as with the force of मतुप् , in the छन्दस् (Vedas).",
    "Sūtra 4.4.141: nakshatraadghah (नक्षत्राद्घः) — The affix घ comes in the छन्दस् (Vedas) after the word नक्षत्र without altering the meaning.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.142: sarvadevaattaatil (सर्वदेवात् तातिल्) — The affix तातिल् comes in the छन्दस् (Vedas) after the words 1. सर्व and 2. देव without altering the meaning.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.143: shivashamarishtasyakare (शिवशमरिष्टस्य करे) — The affix तातिल् comes in the छन्दस् (Vedas) after the words 1. शिव 2. शम् and 3. अरिष्ट in the Genitive 6th-Case in construction when the sense is 'he does'.",
    "Sūtra 4.4.144: bhaavecha (भावे च) — The affix तातिल् comes in the छन्दस् (Vedas) after the words 1. शिव 2. शम् and 3. अरिष्ट in the Genitive 6th-Case in construction, the sense being that of condition.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.1: praakkreetaachchhah (प्राक् क्रीताच्छः) — From this one forward to तेन कृतम् [[6.1.37]], the affix छ bears the rule.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.2: ugavaadibhyot (उगवादिभ्यो यत्) — The affix यत् comes after a प्रातिपदिक ending with उ (long or short), and after the words गो and the rest, the senses of the affix being those taught up to sutra [[5.1.37]]",
    "Sūtra 5.1.3: kambalaachchasamjnyaayaam (कम्बलाच्च संज्ञायाम्) — The affix यत् comes in the प्रक्क्रितीय senses after the word कम्बल, when a Name is meant.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.4: vibhaashaahavirapoopaadibhyah (विभाषा हविरपूपादिभ्यः) — The affix यत् comes optionally after the words denoting 'offering' and etc., in the sense of प्रक्क्रितीय।",
    "Sūtra 5.1.5: tasmaihitam (तस्मै हितम्) — An affix comes after a word in the fourth case in construction, in the sense of 'good for that'.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.6: shareeraavayavaadyat (शरीरावयवाद्यत्) — The affix यत् comes in the sense of 'good for that' after a word denoting a part of the body.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.7: khalayavamaashatilavrushabrahmanashcha (खलयवमाषतिलवृषब्रह्मणश्च) — The affix यत् comes in the sense of 'good for that' after the word खल, यव, माष, तिल, वृष and ब्रह्मण।",
    "Sūtra 5.1.8: ajaavibhyaamthyan (अजाविभ्यां थ्यन्) — The affix थ्यन् comes in the sense of 'good for that' after the words अज and अवि।",
    "Sūtra 5.1.9: aatmanvishvajanabhogottarapadaatkhah (आत्मन्विश्वजनभोगोत्तरपदात् खः) — The affix ख comes in the sense of 'good for that' after the words आत्मन् and विश्वजन and after the compounds having the word भोग as their second term",
    "Sūtra 5.1.10: sarvapurushaabhyaamnadhanyau (सर्वपुरुषाभ्यां णढञौ) — The affixes ण and ढञ् come in the sense of 'good for that' after the words सर्व and पुरुष।",
    "Sūtra 5.1.11: maanavacharakaabhyaamkhany (माणवचरकाभ्यां खञ्) — The affix खञ् comes in the sense of 'good for that' after the words माणव and चरक।",
    "Sūtra 5.1.12: tadarthamvikrutehaprakrutau (तदर्थं विकृतेः प्रकृतौ) — After the word being the name of a product, the above-mentioned affix comes, to denote a thing which is the primitive that is serviceable for that.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.13: chhadirupadhibalehadhany (छदिरुपधिबलेर्ढञ्) — The affix ढञ् (+/- एय) comes, in the sense of a primitive serviceable for a product after the words छदिस् , उपधि and बालि, denoting the product.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.14: rushabhopaanahornyyah (ऋषभोपानहोर्ञ्यः) — The affix ञ्य (+/- य) comes, in the sense of a primitive serviceable for a product after the words ऋषभ and उपानह्, denoting the products.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.15: charmmanony (चर्मणोऽञ्) — The affix अञ् (+/- अ) comes, in the sense of a primitive serviceable for a product after a word expressing the product of leather.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.16: tadasyatadasminsyaaditi (तदस्य तदस्मिन् स्यादिति) — The above mentioned affixes come after a word in the first case in construction, with the force of a genitive or locative, when the word in the first case is agent of the verb स्यत् ; in other words - the above-mentioned affixes have also the senses of 'very well sufficient there to' and 'very well sufficient to be made therein'.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.17: parikhaayaadhany (परिखाया ढञ्) — The affix ढञ् (+/- एय) comes after the word परिखा in the above senses of 'this is sufficient for that' and 'this is sufficient therein'.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.18: praagvateshthany (प्राग्वतेष्ठञ्) — Up to sutra [[5.1.115]] (excluding that) the affix ठञ् (+/- इक or +/- क) bears rule.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.19: aarhaadagopuchchhasamkhyaaparimaanaatthak (आर्हादगोपुच्छसंख्यापरिमाणाट्ठक्) — Up to sutra [[5.1.63]], inclusive, the affix ठक् (+/- इक or +/- क)",
    "Sūtra 5.1.20: asamaasenishkaadibhyah (असमासे निष्कादिभ्यः) — The affix ठक् comes after the words निष्क etc., when they are not parts of a compound, the sense of the affix being that taught in the subsequent sutras up to [[5.1.63]].",
    "Sūtra 5.1.21: shataachchathanyataavashate (शताच्च ठन्यतावशते) — The affixes ठन् (-/- इक) and यत् (-/य) come in the senses taught up to [[5.1.63]] after the word शत् , when it is not part of a compound and when it does not mean merely 'hundred'.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.22: samkhyaayaaatishadantaayaahakan (संख्याया अतिशदन्तायाः कन्) — The affix (-/- -क) comes after a Numeral, when it does not end with ति or शत् , in the sense of the affix being that taught hereafter up to [[5.1.63]]",
    "Sūtra 5.1.23: vatoridvaa (वतोरिड्वा) — The affix कन् coming after a Numeral ending with वत्, takes optionally the augment इद् , the sense of the affix being those given up to [[5.1.63]]",
    "Sūtra 5.1.24: vimshatitrimshadbhyaamdvunnasamjnyaayaam (विंशतित्रिंशद्भ्यां ड्वुन्नसंज्ञायाम्) — The affix डुवन् (-/- -अक) comes in the senses taught up to [[5.1.63]] after the words विंशति and त्रिंशत् , when it does not denote a Name: the ति and अत् of the base being dropped before this affix.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.25: kamsaattithan (कंसाट्टिठन्) — The affix टिठन् (-/- -इक) comes in the senses taught up to [[5.1.63]] after the word कंस।",
    "Sūtra 5.1.26: shoorpaadanyanyatarasyaam (शूर्पादञन्यतरस्याम्) — The affix अञ् (+/- अ) comes optionally in the senses taught up to [[5.1.63]] after the word शूर्पा।",
    "Sūtra 5.1.27: shatamaanavimshatikasahasravasanaadan (शतमानविंशतिकसहस्रवसनादण्) — The affix अण् (-/- -अ) comes in the senses taught up to [[5.1.63]] after the words शतमान , विंशतिक , सहस्र and वसन।",
    "Sūtra 5.1.28: adhyardhapoorvadvigorlugasamjnyaayaam (अध्यर्धपूर्वद्विगोर्लुगसंज्ञायाम्) — The affix having the senses taught up to [[5.1.63]], is elided by लुक् after a stem beginning with the word अध्यर्ध , and after a द्विगु compound, when it is not in a name.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.29: vibhaashaakaarshaapanasahasraabhyaam (विभाषा कार्षापणसहस्राभ्याम्) — The affix having the senses taught up to [[5.1.63]], is not always संख्या। Thus for the purpose of application of the affix कृत्वसूच् [[5.4.17]], this word is not a संख्या।",
    "Sūtra 5.1.30: dvitripoorvaannishkaat (द्वित्रिपूर्वान्निष्कात्) — The आर्हीय affix [[5.1.63]] is optionally elided after a द्विगु occasioning compound, of the word निष्क preceded by द्वि and त्रि।",
    "Sūtra 5.1.31: bistaachcha (बिस्ताच्च) — The आर्हीय affix [[5.1.37]]-63 occasioning a द्विगु compound, is optionally elided after the word बिस्त preceded by द्वि and त्रि।",
    "Sūtra 5.1.32: vimshatikaatkhah (विंशतिकात् खः) — The affix ख (ईन) comes in the आर्हीय senses [[5.1.37]]-63 after the word विंशतिक , when preceded by the word अध्यर्द्ध or a Numeral, occasioning a द्विगु।",
    "Sūtra 5.1.33: khaaryaaeekan (खार्या ईकन्) — The affix ईकन् (-/- -ईक) comes in the आर्हीय senses [[5.1.37]]-63 after the word खारी , when preceded by the word अध्यर्ध or a Numeral occasioning a द्विगु।",
    "Sūtra 5.1.34: panapaadamaashashataadat (पणपादमाषशताद्यत्) — The affix यत् (य) comes in the आर्हीय senses [[5.1.37]]-63 after the words पण, माष and शत , when preceded by the word अध्यर्ध or a Numeral occasioning a द्विगु।",
    "Sūtra 5.1.35: shaanaadvaa (शाणाद्वा) — The affix यत् comes optionally after the word शन, in the आर्हीय-senses [[5.1.63]], when it is preceded by the word अध्यर्ध or a Numeral occasioning a द्विगु।",
    "Sūtra 5.1.36: dvitripoorvaadancha (द्वित्रिपूर्वादण् च) — The affix अण् (-/- -अ) as well as यत् optionally also comes after the word शाण , in the आर्हीय-senses [[5.1.37]]-63, when preceded by the words द्वि and त्रि।",
    "Sūtra 5.1.37: tenakreetam (तेन क्रीतम्) — The thirteen affixes taught in [[5.1.18]]-36 have the sense of 'purchased with this price' and are added to a word in the third case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.38: tasyanimittamsamyogotpaatau (तस्य निमित्तं संयोगोत्पातौ) — The above affixes have further the sense of 'for its sake', when the meaning is a relation or an unwanted appearance.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.39: godvyachorasamkhyaaparimaanaashvaaderyat (गोद्व्यचोऽसंख्यापरिमाणाश्वादेर्यत्) — After the word गो and after a word having two syllables, with the exception of a Numeral, or a Measure of capacity or अश्व etc., the affix यत् (य) is added, in the above sense of 'a relation or a portent for the purpose of that'.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.40: putraachchhacha (पुत्राच्छ च) — After the word पुत्र the affix छ (ईय) also comes, as well as यत् (य), in the above sense of 'a relation or a portent for the purpose of that'.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.41: sarvabhoomipruthiveebhyaamananyau (सर्वभूमिपृथिवीभ्यामणञौ) — The affixes अण् (+/- -अ) and अञ् (+/- -अ) are respectively added to the words सार्वभूमि and पृथ्वी , in the above mentioned sense of 'a connection or a portent for its purpose'.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.42: tasyeshvarah (तस्येश्वरः) — To the same bases सार्वभूमि and पृथ्वी , are added the same affixes अण् and अञ् respectively, in the sense of 'lord thereof'.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.43: tatravidititicha (तत्र विदित इति च) — To the same bases सार्वभूमि and पृथ्वी , being in the 7th case in construction, are added the same affixes अण् and अञ् respectively, in the sense that of 'known therein'.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.44: lokasarvalokaatthany (लोकसर्वलोकाट्ठञ्) — The affix ठञ् (+/- इक) comes in the sense of 'known therein' after the words लोक and सर्वलोक , in the 7th case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.45: tasyavaapah (तस्य वापः) — The above mentioned affixes [[5.1.18]] etc. come after a word in the 6th-Case in construction, in the sense of 'sown with so much'.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.46: paatraatshthan (पात्रात् ष्ठन्) — The affix ष्ठान् (-/- इक) comes in the sense of 'sown with so much' after the word पात्र।",
    "Sūtra 5.1.47: tadasminvruddhyaayalaabhashulkopadaadeeyate (तदस्मिन् वृद्ध्यायलाभशुल्कोपदा दीयते) — The above mentioned affixes have also the sense of 'an interest, or a rent, or a profit, or a tax,or a bribe given thereby or in that'.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.48: pooranaardhaatthan (पूरणार्धाट्ठन्) — The affix ठञ् (+/- इक) comes in the same sense of 'an interest, or a rent, or a profit, or a tax,or a bribe given thereby or therein' after a word denoting an ordinal and after the word अर्ध।",
    "Sūtra 5.1.49: bhaagaadyachcha (भागाद्यच्च) — The affix यत् (य) comes after the word भाग in the sense of 'an interest, or a rent, or a profit, or a tax,or a bribe given thereby or therein'.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.50: taddharativahatyaavahatibhaaraadvamshaadibhyah (तद्धरति वहत्यावहति भाराद्वंशादिभ्यः) — The above mentioned affixes after the word भार preceded by the word वंश etc., have the sense of 'who carries away, or conveys or brings that'.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.51: vasnadravyaabhyaamthankanau (वस्नद्रव्याभ्यां ठन्कनौ) — The affix ठन् (-/- -इक्) and कन् (-/- क) come respectively after the words वसन and द्रव्य , in the 2nd case in construction, in the same sense of 'who carries etc.'.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.52: sambhavatyavaharatipachati (सम्भवत्यवहरति पचति) — The above mentioned affixes have also the sense of 'what is capable of holding that, or takes away that, or cooks that'.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.53: aadhakaachitapaatraatkhonyatarayaam (आढकाचितपात्रात् खोऽन्यतरस्याम्) — The affix ख (ईन) may optionally be added in the above sense of 'being capable of holding etc.' after the words आढक, आचित and पात्र।",
    "Sūtra 5.1.54: dvigoshthamshcha (द्विगोः ष्ठंश्च) — The affix ष्ठान् (-/- इक) as well as the affix affix ख (ईन) may optionally come after the same words आढक, आचित and पात्र being final of a द्विगु compound, the sense being that of 'what can hold etc.'.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.55: kulijaallukkhaucha (कुलिजाल्लुक्खौ च) — After the word कुलिज , being final of a द्विगु , there is optionally the elision of the above affixes, or the adding of the affix ख (इन), in the sense of 'what can hold that etc.'.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.56: sosyaamshavasnabhrutayah (सोऽस्यांशवस्नभृतयः) — The affixes taught in प्राग्वतेष्ठञ् [[5.1.18]] etc. have also the sense of 'this is his portion, price or pay'.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.57: tadasyaparimaanam (तदस्य परिमाणम्) — The affixes taught in प्राग्वतेष्ठञ् [[5.1.18]] etc. have the sense of 'this is its measure'.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.58: samkhyaayaahasamjnyaasamghasootraadhyayaneshu (संख्यायाः संज्ञासंघसूत्राध्ययनेषु) — The affixes प्राग्वतेष्ठञ् [[5.1.18]] etc. come after a word denoting a numeral in the sense of 'this is its measure when the word so formed means a Name, a Multitude, a Book or a fixed way and mode of study.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.59: pangktivimshatitrimshatchatvaarimshatpanychaashatshashtisaptatyasheetinavatishatam (पङ्क्तिविंशतित्रिंशत्चत्वारिंशत्पञ्चाशत्षष्टिसप्तत्यशीतिनवतिशतम्) — The following words are anomalous - 1. पङ्क्ति 'a verse' 2. विंशति 'twenty' 3. त्रिंशत् 'thirty' 4.चत्वारिंशत् 'forty' 5. पञ्चाशत् 'fifty' 6. षष्टि 'sixty' 7. सप्तति 'seventy' 8. अशीति 'eighty' 9. नवति 'ninety' 10. शतम् 'hundred'.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.60: panychaddashatauvargevaa (पञ्चद्दशतौ वर्गे वा) — The words 1. पञ्चत् and 2. दशत् in combination with वर्ग may be anomalously so formed, in the sense of 'this is its measure'.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.61: saptanonychhandasi (सप्तनोऽञ् छन्दसि) — The affix अञ् (+/- अ) comes after the word सप्तन् in the छन्दस् (Vedas) when the meaning is that of a वर्ग।",
    "Sūtra 5.1.62: trimshachchatvaarimshatorbraahmanesamjnyaayaamdan (त्रिंशच्चत्वारिंशतोर्ब्राह्मणे संज्ञायां डण्) — The affix अञ् (+/- अ) comes in the sense of 'this is its measure' after the words 1. त्रिंशत् and 2. चत्वारिशत् when it is a Name denoting a ब्राहमण-book.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.63: tadarhati (तद् अर्हति) — The affixes प्राग्वतेष्ठञ् [[5.1.18]] have also the sense of 'who deserves that'.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.64: chhedaadibhyonityam (छेदादिभ्यो नित्यम्) — After the words छेद etc. in the Accusative -2nd case in construction, the above mentioned affixes have the sense of 'who deserves that under all circumstances'.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.65: sheershachchhedaadyachcha (शीर्षच्छेदाद्यच्च) — The affix यत् as well as the above affixes come after the word शीर्षच्छेद in the Accusative -2nd case in the sense 'who deserves that under all circumstances'.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.66: dandaadibhyah (दण्डादिभ्यः) — After the words दण्ड etc. in the Accusative -2nd case the affix य comes in the sense of 'who deserves that'.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.67: chhandasicha (छन्दसि च) — The affix यत् (य) comes in the sense of 'deserving that' after a प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stem), in the छन्दस् (Vedas).",
    "Sūtra 5.1.68: paatraadghamshcha (पात्राद्घंश्च) — The affix घञ् (-/- इयं) together with यत् (यं) comes in the sense of 'deserving that' after the word पात्र।",
    "Sūtra 5.1.69: kadanggaradakshinaachchhacha (कडङ्करदक्षिणाच्छ च) — The affixes छ (ईयं) and यत् (यं) comes in the sense of 'deserving that' after the words 1. कडङ्गर and 2. दक्षिणा।",
    "Sūtra 5.1.70: sthaaleebilaat (स्थालीबिलात्) — The affixes छ (ईयं) and यत् (यं) comes in the sense of 'deserving that' after the word स्थालीबिल।",
    "Sūtra 5.1.71: yajnyartvigbhyaamghakhanyau (यज्ञर्त्विग्भ्यां घखञौ) — The affixes घ (इ य) and खञ् (+/- --ईन) come respectively after the words 1. यज्ञ and 2. ऋत्विज in the sense of 'deserving that'",
    "Sūtra 5.1.72: paaraayanaturaayanachaandraayanamvartayati (पारायणतुरायणचान्द्रायणं वर्तयति) — The affix ठञ् (+/- -- इक , प्राग्वतेष्ठञ् [[5.1.18]]) comes in the sense of 'who performs this' after the words 1. पारायण 2. तुरायण and 3. चान्द्रायण being in the Accusative -2nd case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.73: samshayamaapannah (संशयमापन्नः) — The affix ठञ् (+/- -- इक) comes in the sense of 'being fallen into this or thrown into it' after the word संशय in the Accusative -2nd case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.74: yojanamgachchhati (योजनं गच्छति) — The affix ठञ् comes in the sense of 'who goes' after the word योजन in the Accusative -2nd case construction.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.75: pathahashkan (पथः ष्कन्) — The affix ष्कन् comes in the sense of 'who goes there' after the word पथ being in the Accusative -2nd case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.76: panthonanityam (पन्थो ण नित्यम्) — The affix ण comes after the word पन्थ which becomes the substitute of पथिन्, the sense of the affix being 'who always goes'.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.77: uttarapathenaahrutamcha (उत्तरपथेनाहृतं च) — The affix ठञ् comes in the sense of 'who passes by that way' and 'what is conveyed by that way' after the word उत्तरपथ in the Instrumental -3rd case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.78: kaalaat (कालात्) — In the following sūtras the phrase 'after a word denoting time' should be supplied to complete the sense.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.79: tenanirvruttam (तेन निर्वृत्तम्) — The affix ठञ् comes after a word denoting time in the Instrumental -3rd case in construction in the sense of 'to be accomplished by that time'.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.80: tamadheeshtobhrutobhootobhaavee (तमधीष्टो भृतो भूतो भावी) — The above affixes come after a word expressing time in the Accusative -2nd case in construction in the senses of 'solicited to instruct for such a period or which will last so long'.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.81: maasaadvayasiyatkhanyau (मासाद्वयसि यत्खञौ) — The affixes यत् and खञ् come after the word मास in denoting 'age'.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.82: dvigoryap (द्विगोर्यप्) — The affix यप् comes after the word मास when forming a द्विगु समास (Numeral Determinative Compound) and meaning 'age'.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.83: shanmaasaannyachcha (षण्मासाण्ण्यच्च) — The affixes ण्त् , यप् and ठञ् comes in the sense of 'age' after the word षण्मास।",
    "Sūtra 5.1.84: avayasithamshcha (अवयसि ठंश्च) — The affix ठन् comes after the word षण्मास when 'age' is Not meant.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.85: samaayaahakhah (समायाः खः) — The affix ख (ईन) comes in the four-fold senses of 'solicited', 'hired', 'lasted' and 'will last', after the word समा।",
    "Sūtra 5.1.86: dvigorvaa (द्विगोर्वा) — The affix ख (ईन) comes optionally in the senses taught in पन्थो ण नित्यम् [[5.1.76]], तमधीष्टो भृतो भूतो भावी [[5.1.80]] after the word समा , forming a द्विगु समास (Numeral Determinative Compound).",
    "Sūtra 5.1.87: raatryahassamvatsaraachcha (रात्र्यहस्संवत्सराच्च) — The affix ख optionally in the senses taught in तेन निर्वृत्तम् [[5.1.79]], द्विगोर्यप् [[5.1.82]], after the words 1. रात्री 2. अहन् and 3. सम्वत्सर , occasioning a द्विगु समास (Numeral Determinative Compound).",
    "Sūtra 5.1.88: varshaallukcha (वर्षाल्लुक् च) — The above affixes and ख and ठिञ् may also be elided after a द्विगु समास (Numeral Determinative Compound) ending in वर्षा।",
    "Sūtra 5.1.89: chittavatinityam (चित्तवति नित्यम्) — The affixes meaning 'accomplished' etc. पन्थो ण नित्यम् [[5.1.76]], तमधीष्टो भृतो भूतो भावी [[5.1.80]] are necessarily elided after the word वर्षा forming a द्विगु समास (Numeral Determinative Compound) when it refers to being endowed with reason.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.90: shashtikaahashashtiraatrenapachyante (षष्टिकाः षष्टिरात्रेण पच्यन्ते) — The anomalously formed word षष्टिकाः has the meaning of 'what are matured in six nights'.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.91: vatsaraantaachchhashchhandasi (वत्सरान्ताच्छश्छन्दसि) — The affix छ comes in the छन्दस् (Vedas) in the five-fold senses taught in पन्थो ण नित्यम् [[5.1.76]], तमधीष्टो भृतो भूतो भावी [[5.1.80]], after a stem ending in वत्सर।",
    "Sūtra 5.1.92: samparipoorvaatkhacha (सम्परिपूर्वात् ख च) — When the affixes ख (ईन) and छ (ईय) come in the छन्दस् (Vedas) in the five-fold senses taught in पन्थो ण नित्यम् [[5.1.76]], तमधीष्टो भृतो भूतो भावी [[5.1.80]], after the word वत्सर , when preceded by सम् and परि।",
    "Sūtra 5.1.93: tenaparijayyalabhyakaaryasukaram (तेन परिजय्यलभ्यकार्यसुकरम्) — The affix ठञ् comes after a word denoting time in the Instrumental -3rd case in construction in the sense 'to be subdued, to be gained or attained, to be completed and to be easily completed in that time'.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.94: tadasyabrahmacharyam (तदस्य ब्रह्मचर्यम्) — The affix ठञ् comes after a word of time in the sense of 'an abstinence that lasts so long' or 'who practises abstinence so long'.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.95: tasyachadakshinaayajnyaakhyebhyah (तस्य च दक्षिणा यज्ञाख्येभ्यः) — The affix ठञ् comes after a word being the name of sacrifice, in the sense of 'the fee thereof'.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.96: tatrachadeeyatekaaryambhavavat (तत्र च दीयते कार्यं भववत्) — The affixes having the sense of भव तत्र भवः [[4.3.53]] , कालाट्ठञ् [[4.3.11]] , come after a time-denoting word in the sense of 'what is given in that, and what is done in that'.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.97: vyushtaadibhyon (व्युष्टादिभ्योऽण्) — The affix अण् comes after the words व्युष्ट etc. in the Locative -7th case in construction, the sense of 'being given therein or done therein'.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.98: tenayathaakathaachahastaabhyaamnayatau (तेन यथाकथाचहस्ताभ्यां णयतौ) — The affixes ण and यत् come respectively after the words यथा-कथा-च and हस्त being in the Instrumental -3rd case in construction having the sense of what is 'given or is done in this way'.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.99: sampaadini (सम्पादिनि) — The affix ठञ् comes after a word in the Instrumental -3rd case in construction in the sense of 'fitted for that'.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.100: karmaveshaadyat (कर्मवेषाद्यत्) — The affix यत् (यं) comes in the sense of 'being fitted with that', after the words 1. कर्म and 2. वेष being in the Instrumental -3rd case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.101: tasmaiprabhavatisamtaapaadibhyah (तस्मै प्रभवति संतापादिभ्यः) — The affix ठञ् comes after the words संताप etc. in the Dative -4th Case in construction in the sense of 'what is able to effect that'.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.102: yogaadyachcha (योगाद्यच्च) — The affix यत् (यं) is also added in the sense of 'able to effect that' after the word योग।",
    "Sūtra 5.1.103: karmanukany (कर्मण उकञ्) — The affix उकञ् comes after the word कर्मण in the same sense of 'able to effect that'.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.104: samayastadasyapraaptam (समयस्तदस्य प्राप्तम्) — The affix ठञ् comes in the sense of 'that has arrived for it' after the word समय in the Nominative 1st-Case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.105: kaalaadyat (ऋतोरण्) — The affix अण् comes in the sense of 'that has come for it' after the word ऋतु।",
    "Sūtra 5.1.106: chhandasighas (छन्दसि घस्) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas) the affix घस् (इय) comes in the sense of 'season has come for it' After the verbs the word ऋतु।",
    "Sūtra 5.1.107: kaalaadyat (कालाद्यत्) — The affix यत् (यं) comes in the same sense of 'time has come for it' after the word काल।",
    "Sūtra 5.1.108: prakrushtethany (प्रकृष्टे ठञ्) — The affix यत् (यं) comes in the sense of 'long standing' after the word काल being the Nominative 1st-Case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.109: prayojanam (प्रयोजनम्) — The affix ठञ् comes in the sense of 'that whose occasion or purpose is this' after a word in the Nominative 1st-Case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.110: vishaakhaashaadhaadanmanthadandayoh (विशाखाषाढादण् मन्थदण्डयोः) — The affix अण् comes in the sense of 'that whose purpose is this' after the words 1. विशाखा and 2. आषाढ when the derivative of the first is combined with मन्य and that of the second with दण्ड।",
    "Sūtra 5.1.111: anupravachanaadibhyashchhah (अनुप्रवचनादिभ्यश्छः) — The affix छ (ईय) comes in the same sense of 'that whose purpose is this' after The affix words अनुप्रवचन etc.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.112: samaapanaatsapoorvapadaat (समापनात् सपूर्वपदात्) — The affix छ (ईय) comes in the same sense of 'that whose purpose is this' after the word समापन when it has a word in composition preceding it.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.113: aikaagaarikatchaure (ऐकागारिकट् चौरे) — The word ऐकागारिकट् is irregularly formed in the sense of 'thief'.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.114: aakaalikadaadyantavachane (आकालिकडाद्यन्तवचने) — The word आकालिकट् is irregularly formed in the sense of 'what coincides with the beginning and the end i.e. what lasts only an instant'.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.115: tenatulyamkriyaachedvatih (तेन तुल्यं क्रिया चेद्वतिः) — The affix वति (वत्) comes after a word in the Instrumental -3rd case in construction, in the sense of 'like that' when the meaning is 'similarity of action'.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.116: tatratasyeva (तत्र तस्येव) — The affix वति (वत्) also comes in the sense of 'like what is therein or thereof'.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.117: tadarham (तदर्हम्) — The affix वति (वत्) comes after a word in the Accusative -2nd case in construction in the sense of 'befitting that or suited to that'.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.118: upasargaachchhandasidhaatvarthe (उपसर्गाच्छन्दसि धात्वर्थे) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas) the affix वति (वत्) is added to an उपसर्ग (Preposition) in the sense of a verbal root.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.119: tasyabhaavastvatalau (तस्य भावस्त्वतलौ) — The affixes त्व and तल् come in the sense of 'the nature thereof' after a word in the Genitive 6th-Case.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.120: aachatvaat (आ च त्वात्) — From this forward as far as the sūtra ब्रह्मणस्त्वः [[5.1.136]], the affixes त्व and तल् bear the rule.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.121: nananypoorvaattatpurushaadachaturasamgatalavanavatayudhakatarasalasebhyah (न नञ्पूर्वात्तत्पुरुषादचतुरसंगतलवणवटयुधकतरसलसेभ्यः) — The affixes denoting 'nature' taught hereafter do not come after a तत्-पुरुष compound formed by the negative particle नञ् with the exception of the the following - 1. चतुर 2. संगत 3. लवण 4. वट 5. बुध 6. कत 7. रस and 8. लस ।",
    "Sūtra 5.1.122: pruthvaadibhyimanijvaa (पृथ्वादिभ्य इमनिज्वा) — The affix इमनिच् (इमन्) comes optionally in the sense of 'nature thereof' after the words पृथु etc.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.123: varnadrudhaadibhyahashyanycha (वर्णदृढादिभ्यः ष्यञ् च) — The affixes ष्यञ् and इमनिच् come in the sense of 'nature thereof' after a word denoting colour and after the words दृढ etc.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.124: gunavachanabraahmanaadibhyahakarmanicha (गुणवचनब्राह्मणादिभ्यः कर्मणि च) — The affix ष्यञ् has after a word expressive of quality and after ब्राह्मण etc., the sense of the activity or occupation or something or someone.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.125: stenaadyannalopashcha (स्तेनाद्यन्नलोपश्च) — The affix यत् (यं) comes in the sense of 'nature thereof or action thereof' after the word स्तेन in the Genitive 6th-Case and न is elided before this affix.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.126: sakhyuryah (सख्युर्यः) — The affix य comes in the sense of 'nature or action thereof' after the word सखि।",
    "Sūtra 5.1.127: kapijnyaatyordhak (कपिज्ञात्योर्ढक्) — The affix ढक् comes in the sense of 'nature or action thereof' after the words 1. कपि and 2. ज्ञाति।",
    "Sūtra 5.1.128: patyantapurohitaadibhyoyak (पत्यन्तपुरोहितादिभ्यो यक्) — The affix यक् comes in the sense of 'nature or action thereof' after a compound ending with पति and after पुरोहित etc.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.129: praanabhrujjaativayovachanodgaatraadibhyony (प्राणभृज्जातिवयोवचनोद्गात्रादिभ्योऽञ्) — The affix अञ् comes in the sense of 'nature or action or thereof' after class names of animals and words expressing age as well as after उद्गात्रि etc.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.130: haayanaantayuvaadibhyon (हायनान्तयुवादिभ्योऽण्) — The affix अण् comes in the sense of 'nature or action thereof' after compounds ending in हायन and after युवन etc.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.131: igantaachchalaghupoorvaat (इगन्ताच्च लघुपूर्वात्) — The affix अण् comes in the sense of 'nature or action thereof' after a stem ending in इक् (इ ई उ ऊ ऋ or ऌ) when the preceding syllable is prosodially light.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.132: yopadhaadguroopottamaadvuny (योपधाद्गुरूपोत्तमाद्वुञ्) — The affix वुञ् comes in the sense of 'nature or action thereof' after a polysyllabic stem whose penultimate letter is य् and whose penultimate syllable is prosodially heavy.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.133: dvamdvamanojnyaadibhyashcha (द्वन्द्वमनोज्ञादिभ्यश्च) — The affix वुञ् comes in the sense of 'nature or action thereof' after a द्वन्द समास and after the words मनोज्ञ etc.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.134: gotracharanaachshlaaghaatyaakaaratadaveteshu (गोत्रचरणाच्श्लाघात्याकारतदवेतेषु) — The affix वुञ् comes in the sense of 'nature or action thereof' after a गोत्र (Patronymic/Family-name) and after the Name of a Vedic School when one boasts thereby or manifests his contempt thereby or when it means one who has attained that (or has come for an inspection or inquiring thereof).",
    "Sūtra 5.1.135: hotraabhyashchhah (होत्राभ्यश्छः) — The affix छ (ईय) comes in the sense of 'nature or action thereof' after words expressing होत्रा priests.",
    "Sūtra 5.1.136: brahmanastvah (ब्रह्मणस्त्वः) — The affix त्व comes in the sense of of 'nature or action thereof' after the word ब्रह्मण denoting a kind of होत्रा priest.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.1: dhaanyaanaambhavanekshetrekhany (धान्यानां भवने क्षेत्रे खञ्) — The affix खञ् comes in the sense of 'a place of growing when that place is a field' after the name of any particular corn being in the Genitive 6th-Case.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.2: vreehishaalyordhak (व्रीहिशाल्योर्ढक्) — The affix ढक् comes in the sense of 'a place of growing, when it is a field' after the words 1. व्रीहि and 2. शालि।",
    "Sūtra 5.2.3: yavayavakashashtikaadyat (यवयवकषष्टिकाद्यत्) — The affix यत् comes in the sense of 'a place of growing, when it is a field' after the words 1. यव 2. यवक and 3. षष्टिक।",
    "Sūtra 5.2.4: vibhaashaatilamaashomaabhanggaanubhyah (विभाषा तिलमाषोमाभङ्गाऽणुभ्यः) — The affix यत् comes in the sense of 'a place of growing, when it is a field' optionally after the words 1. तिल 2. माष3. उमा 4. भङ्गा and 5. अणु।",
    "Sūtra 5.2.5: sarvacharmanahakrutahakhakhanyau (सर्वचर्मणः कृतः खखञौ) — The affix ख (ईन) and खञ् comes in the sense of 'wholly made thereof' after the word सर्वचर्मन्।",
    "Sūtra 5.2.6: yathaamukhasammukhasyadarshanahakhah (यथामुखसंमुखस्य दर्शनः खः) — The affix ख (ईन) and खञ् comes in the sense of 'a mirror' after the words 1. यथामुख and 2. संमुख being in Genitive 6th-Case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.7: tatsarvaadehapathyanggakarmapatrapaatramvyaapnoti (तत्सर्वादेः पथ्यङ्गकर्मपत्रपात्रं व्याप्नोति) — After the words 1. पथि 2. अङ्ग 3. कर्मन् 4. पत्र or 5. पात्र , preceded by सर्व being in the Accusative -2nd case in construction, the affix ख (ईन) comes in the sense of 'what pervades or fills the whole of that'.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.8: aaprapadampraapnoti (आप्रपदं प्राप्नोति) — The affix ख (ईन) comes in the sense of 'reaching thereto' after the word आप्रपद।",
    "Sūtra 5.2.9: anupadasarvaannaayaanayambaddhaabhakshayatineyeshu (अनुपदसर्वान्नायानयं बद्धाभक्षयतिनेयेषु) — The affix ख (ईन) comes in the senses of 'so bound', 'eating that' and 'to carry thereto' after the words 1. अनुपद 2. सर्वान्न and 3. आयन।",
    "Sūtra 5.2.10: parovaraparamparaputrapautramanubhavati (परोवरपरम्परपुत्रपौत्रमनुभवति) — The affix ख (ईन) comes in the sense of 'who witnesses or experiences that' after the words 1. परोवर 2. परम्पर and 3. पुत्रपौत्र , in the Accusative -2nd case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.11: avaarapaaraatyantaanukaamamgaamee (अवारपारात्यन्तानुकामं गामी) — The affix ख (ईन) comes in the sense of 'who purposes to go' after the words 1. अवारपार 2. अत्यन्त and 3. अनुकाम being in the Accusative -2nd case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.12: samaamsamaamvijaayate (समांसमां विजायते) — The affix ख (ईन) comes in the sense of 'who bears in the womb' after the word समांसमाम्।",
    "Sūtra 5.2.13: adyashveenaavashtabdhe (अद्यश्वीनाऽवष्टब्धे) — The word अद्यश्वीन is anomalous meaning 'a female near delivery'.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.14: aagaveenah (आगवीनः) — The word आगवीन is irregularly formed.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.15: anugvalamgaamee (अनुग्वलंगामी) — The affix ख (ईन) comes in the sense of 'who is fit to follow' after the word अनुगु।",
    "Sūtra 5.2.16: adhvanoyatkhau (अध्वनो यत्खौ) — The affixes यत् (यं) and ख (ईन) come in the sense of 'who is fit or able to follow' after the word अध्वन्।",
    "Sūtra 5.2.17: abhyamitraachchhacha (अभ्यमित्राच्छ च) — The affixes छ (ईय), यत् (यं) and ख (ईन) come in the sense of 'who is able to go' after the word अभ्यमित्र।",
    "Sūtra 5.2.18: goshthaatkhanybhootapoorve (गोष्ठात् खञ् भूतपूर्वे) — The affix खञ् comes in the sense of 'it formerly had been' after the word गोष्ठ।",
    "Sūtra 5.2.19: ashvasyaikaahagamah (अश्वस्यैकाहगमः) — The affix खञ् comes in the sense of 'what is travelled over or traversed in one day' after the word अश्व being in the Genitive 6th-Case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.20: shaaleenakaupeeneadhrushtaakaaryayoh (शालीनकौपीने अधृष्टाकार्ययोः) — The words शालीन and कौपीन are anomalous when meaning 'modest' and 'a shameful action, respectively.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.21: vraatenajeevati (व्रातेन जीवति) — The affix खञ् comes in the sense of 'who leads this life' or 'who lives by this' after the word व्रात being in the Instrumental -3rd case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.22: saaptapadeenamsakhyam (साप्तपदीनं सख्यम्) — The word साप्तपदीन is anomalous when meaning 'friendship'.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.23: haiyamgaveenamsamjnyaayaam (हैयंगवीनं संज्ञायाम्) — The word हैयंगवीन is anomalous when it is a Name.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.24: tasyapaakamoolepeelvadikarnaadibhyahakunabjaahachau (तस्य पाकमूले पील्वादिकर्णादिभ्यः कुणब्जाहचौ) — The affixes कुणप् (कुण) and जाहच् (जाह) come in the senses of 'the fruiting-season of this' and 'the root of this'.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.25: pakshaattih (पक्षात्तिः) — The affix ति comes in the sense of 'the root of it' after the word पक्ष in the Genitive 6th-Case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.26: tenavittashchunychupchanapau (तेन वित्तश्चुञ्चुप्चणपौ) — The affixes चुञ्चुप् (चुञ्चु) and चणप् (चण) come in the sense of 'celebrated through this' after a word in the Instrumental -3rd case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.27: vinanybhyaamnaanaanyaunasaha (विनञ्भ्यां नानाञौ नसह) — The affixes ना and नाञ् comes in the sense of 'not being together' after the words 1. वि and 2. नञ् respectively.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.28: vehashaalachchhangkatachau (वेः शालच्छङ्कटचौ) — The affixes शालच् (शाल) and शङ्कटच् (शङ्कट) come after the preposition वि without changing the sense.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.29: samprodashchakatach (सम्प्रोदश्च कटच्) — The affix कटच् (कट) comes after the words 1. सम् 2. प्रद् 3. उद् and 4. वि।",
    "Sūtra 5.2.30: avaatkutaarachcha (अवात् कुटारच्च) — The affixes कुटारच् and कटच् come after the word अव।",
    "Sūtra 5.2.31: natenaasikaayaahasamjnyaayaamteetanynaatajbhratachah (नते नासिकायाः संज्ञायां टीटञ्नाटज्भ्रटचः) — The affixes टीटच् , नाटच् and भ्रटच् come in the sense of 'a hooked nose' after the word अव when the word so formed is a Name.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.32: nerbidajbireesachau (नेर्बिडज्बिरीसचौ) — The affixes बिडच् and बिरीसच् come in the sense of 'a hooked nose' after the word नि when the word so formed is a Name.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.33: inachpitachchikachicha (इनच्पिटच्चिकचि च) — The affixes इनच् and पिटच् come in the sense of 'a hooked nose' after the word नि ; and चिक् and चि are the substitutes of नि before those affixes respectively.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.34: upaadhibhyaamtyakannaasannaaroodhayoh (उपाधिभ्यां त्यकन्नासन्नारूढयोः) — The affix त्यकन् comes in the sense of 'nearness' and after the words 1. उप and 2. अधि , respectively, the words so formed being Names.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.35: karmanighatothach (कर्मणि घटोऽठच्) — The affix अठच् comes in the sense of 'employing oneself zealously in it' after the word कर्म in the Locative -7th case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.36: tadasyasamjaatamtaarakaadibhyitach (तदस्य संजातं तारकादिभ्य इतच्) — The affix इतच् comes in the sense of 'that whereof this is observed' after the words तारका etc. in the Nominative 1st-Case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.37: pramaanedvayasajdaghnanymaatrachah (प्रमाणे द्वयसज्दघ्नञ्मात्रचः) — The affixes द्वयसच् , दघ्नश्च and मात्रच् come in the sense of 'that whereof this is the lineal measure' after a word in Nominative 1st-Case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.38: purushahastibhyaamancha (पुरुषहस्तिभ्यामण् च) — The affix अण् , द्वयसच् , दघ्नश्च and मात्रच् come in the sense of 'that whereof this is the lineal measure' after the words 1. पुरुष and 2. हस्ति in the Nominative 1st-Case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.39: yadtadetebhyahaparimaanevatup (यद्तदेतेभ्यः परिमाणे वतुप्) — The affix वतुप् comes in the sense of 'that where of this is the measure of volume' after the words 1.यद् 2. तद् and 3. एतद् being in the Nominative 1st-Case of construction.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.40: kimidambhyaamvoghah (किमिदंभ्यां वो घः) — After the words किम् and इदम् , घ (इय्) is substituted for the व् of वतुप्।",
    "Sūtra 5.2.41: kimahasamkhyaaparimaanedaticha (किमः संख्यापरिमाणे डति च) — The affixes डति (अति with the elision of इम्) and वतुप् come in the sense of 'numerical quantity' after the word किम् in the Nominative 1st-Case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.42: samkhyaayaaavayavetayap (संख्याया अवयवे तयप्) — The affix तयप् comes in the sense of 'that whereof the parts are so many' after a numeral.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.43: dvitribhyaamtayasyaayajvaa (द्वित्रिभ्यां तयस्यायज्वा) — The affix अयच् is optionally the substitute of तयप् after the words 1. द्वि and 2. त्रि।",
    "Sūtra 5.2.44: ubhaadudaattonityam (उभादुदात्तो नित्यम्) — After the word उभ , अयच् is always the substitute for तयप् , having the उदात्त (acute accent) on its first syllable.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.45: tadasminnadhikamitidashaantaaddah (तदस्मिन्नधिकमिति दशान्ताड्डः) — The affix ड (अ with the elision of अन् of the base) comes in the sense of 'this is surplus in it' after a Numeral ending in दशन् being in the Nominative 1st-Case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.46: shadantavimshateshcha (शदन्तविंशतेश्च) — The affix ड comes in the sense of 'this is surplus in it' after a Numeral ending in शत् and after विंशति with the elision of अत् and अति।",
    "Sūtra 5.2.47: samkhyaayaagunasyanimaanemayat (संख्याया गुणस्य निमाने मयट्) — The affix मयट् (मथ with feminine in ङीप्) comes when denoting a thing given in exchange in the sense of 'containing so many times more of something' or 'the price of a portion of this is so many equal portion of the other' after a Numeral.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.48: tasyapooranedat (तस्य पूरणे डट्) — The affix डट् (अ causing the elision of the last vowel with the consonant following it) comes in the sense of 'making full this number' after a Numeral being the Genitive 6th-Case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.49: naantaadasamkhyaadermat (नान्तादसंख्यादेर्मट्) — The augment मट् comes before डट् in the sense of 'making full this number' after a Numeral which ends in न् when no other Numeral precedes it.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.50: thatchachchhandasi (थट् चच्छन्दसि) — The थट् is the augment of डट् in the छन्दस् (Vedas) after a Numeral ending in न् and not preceded by another Numeral as well as the augment मट्।",
    "Sūtra 5.2.51: shatkatikatipayachaturaamthuk (षट्कतिकतिपयचतुरां थुक्) — When डट् follows, थुक् is the augment of the words 1. षट् 2. कति 3. कतिपय and 4. चतुर्।",
    "Sūtra 5.2.52: bahupoogaganasamghasyatithuk (बहुपूगगणसंघस्य तिथुक्) — When डट् follows, तिथुक् is the augment of the words 1. बहु 2. पूग 3. गण and 4. सङ्गघ।",
    "Sūtra 5.2.53: vatorithuk (वतोरिथुक्) — When follows is the augment of a stem ending in वतु।",
    "Sūtra 5.2.54: dvesteeyah (द्वेस्तीयः) — The affix तीय comes in the sense of 'completer thereof' after the word द्वि।",
    "Sūtra 5.2.55: trehasamprasaaranamcha (त्रेः सम्प्रसारणं च) — The affix तीय comes in the sense of 'completer thereof' after the word त्रि and there is सम्प्रसारण (Vocalisation) of the stem.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.56: vimshatyaadibhyastamadanyatarasyaam (विंशत्यादिभ्यस्तमडन्यतरस्याम्) — After the words विंशति etc. तमट् (तम feminine in ङीप्) is optionally the augment of डट्।",
    "Sūtra 5.2.57: nityamshataadimaasaardhamaasasamvatsaraachcha (नित्यं शतादिमासार्धमाससंवत्सराच्च) — After the words शत etc. and after 1. मास 2. अर्धमास and 3. संवत्सर तमट् (तम feminine in ङीप्) is always the augment of डट्।",
    "Sūtra 5.2.58: shashtyaadeshchaasamkhyaadeh (षष्ट्यादेश्चासंख्यादेः) — After the words षष्ठी etc. when no other Numeral precedes them; तमट् is always the augment of डट्।",
    "Sūtra 5.2.59: matauchchhahasooktasaamnoh (मतौ छः सूक्तसाम्नोः) — When a सूक्त or साम्न् is to be expressed, the affix छ (ईय) comes after a प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stem) in the sense of the affix मतुप् -- तदस्यास्त्यस्मिन्निति मतुप् [[5.2.94]].",
    "Sūtra 5.2.60: adhyaayaanuvaakayorluk (अध्यायानुवाकयोर्लुक्) — When an अध्याय or अनुवाक is to be expressed there is लुक् elision of the affix छ (ईय) having the sense of मतुप् -- तदस्यास्त्यस्मिन्निति मतुप् [[5.2.94]].",
    "Sūtra 5.2.61: vimuktaadibhyon (विमुक्तादिभ्योऽण्) — The affix अण् comes in the sense of मतुप् when an अध्याय or अनुवाक is to be expressed, after the words विमुक्त etc.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.62: goshadaadibhyovun (गोषदादिभ्यो वुन्) — The affix वुन् comes in the sense of मतुप् when an अध्याय or अनुवाक is to be expressed",
    "Sūtra 5.2.63: tatrakushalahapathah (तत्र कुशलः पथः) — The affix वुन् comes in the sense of 'versed therein or skilled therein' after the word पथिन् being in the Locative -7th case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.64: aakarshaadibhyahakan (आकर्षादिभ्यः कन्) — The affix कन् comes in the sense of 'versed therein or skilled therein' after the प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stem) आकर्ष etc. being in the Locative -7th case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.65: dhanahiranyaatkaame (धनहिरण्यात् कामे) — The affix कन् comes in the sense of 'a desire thereafter' after the words 1. धन and 2. हिरण्य being in the Locative -7th case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.66: svaanggebhyahaprasite (स्वाङ्गेभ्यः प्रसिते) — The affix कन् comes in the sense of 'who takes care of it, who bestows care upon' after a word denoting a part of one's body.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.67: udaraatthagaadyoone (उदराट्ठगाद्यूने) — The affix ठक् comes in the sense of 'voracious' after the word उदर।",
    "Sūtra 5.2.68: sasyenaparijaatah (सस्येन परिजातः) — The affix कन् comes in the sense of 'to supply richly with it' after the word सस्य being in the Instrumental -3rd case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.69: amshamhaaree (अंशं हारी) — The affix कन् comes in the sense of 'who must take that' after the word अंश 'a share' being in the Accusative -2nd case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.70: tantraadachiraapahrute (तन्त्रादचिरापहृते) — The affix कन् comes in the sense of taken off there from not long ago or shortly before' after the word तन्त्र 'a loom'.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.71: braahmanakoshnikesamjnyaayaam (ब्राह्मणकोष्णिके संज्ञायाम्) — The words ब्राह्मण and उष्णिक are anomalous when they are a Name.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.72: sheetoshnaabhyaamkaarini (शीतोष्णाभ्यां कारिणि) — The affix कन् comes in the sense of 'who goes to work thus' after the words शीत and उष्ण।",
    "Sūtra 5.2.73: adhikam (अधिकम्) — The word अधिक is anomalous.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.74: anukaabhikaabheekahakamitaa (अनुकाभिकाभीकः कमिता) — The words 1. अनुक 2. अभिक and 3. अभीक are anomalous meaning 'being at liberty to do or being fond of'.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.75: paarshvenaanvichchhati (पार्श्वेनान्विच्छति) — The affix कन् comes in the sense of 'who strives to gain something by that' after the word पार्श्व in the Instrumental -3rd case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.76: ayahashooladandaajinaabhyaamthakthanyau (अयःशूलदण्डाजिनाभ्यां ठक्ठञौ) — The affixes ठक् and ठञ् come in the sense of 'who strives to gain something by that 'after the words 1. अयःशूल and 2. दण्डाजिन , respectively",
    "Sūtra 5.2.77: taavatithamgrahanamitilugvaa (तावतिथं ग्रहणमिति लुग्वा) — The affix कन् is added to an ordinal number in the sense of 'acquiring a subject after so many attempts' and there is optionally the elision of the affix denoting the ordinal number.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.78: seshaamgraamaneeh (स एषां ग्रामणीः) — The affix कन् comes in the sense of 'he is their leader' after a word in the Nominative 1st-Case with the force of Genitive 6th-Case.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.79: shrungkhalamasyabandhanamkarabhe (शृङ्खलमस्य बन्धनं करभे) — The affix कन् comes in the sense of 'clog is its fetter' after the word शृङ्खल 'a clog' when the whole word means 'a young camel'.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.80: utkunmanaah (उत्क उन्मनाः) — The word उत्क is anomalous meaning 'longing after, yearning'.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.81: kaalaprayojanaadroge (कालप्रयोजनाद्रोगे) — The affix कन् comes after a word expressing a time or a cause or effect (of the disease) when an illness is denoted.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.82: tadasminnannampraayesamjnyaayaam (तदस्मिन्नन्नं प्राये संज्ञायाम्) — The affix कन् comes in the sense of 'this is the principal food of this particular occasion' after a word denoting food in the Nominative 1st-Case in construction, when the whole word so formed is a Name.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.83: kulmaashaadany (कुल्माषादञ्) — The affix अण् comes in the sense of 'this is the principal food on this particular occasion' after the word कुल्माष when the whole word is a Name.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.84: shrotriyamshchhandodheete (श्रोत्रियंश्छन्दोऽधीते) — The word श्रोत्रिन् is irregularly formed meaning 'who has studied the छन्दस् (Vedas)'.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.85: shraaddhamanenabhuktaminithanau (श्राद्धमनेन भुक्तमिनिठनौ) — The affixes इनि (इन्) and ठन् come in the sense of 'this is eaten by him' after the word ।",
    "Sūtra 5.2.86: poorvaadinih (पूर्वादिनिः) — The affix इनि (इन्) comes in the sense of 'by whom something was done formerly' after the word पूर्व।",
    "Sūtra 5.2.87: sapoorvaachcha (सपूर्वाच्च) — The affix इनि (इन्) comes in the sense of 'by whom something is done' after the word पूर्व, also when another word precedes it.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.88: ishtaadibhyashcha (इष्टादिभ्यश्च) — The affix इनि (इन्) comes in the sense of 'by him' after इष्ट etc.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.89: chhandasiparipanthipariparinauparyavasthaatari (छन्दसि परिपन्थिपरिपरिणौ पर्यवस्थातरि) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas) the words 1. परिपन्थिन् and 2. परिपरिण् are anomalously formed by this affix and have the sense of 'an antagonist'.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.90: anupadyanveshtaa (अनुपद्यन्वेष्टा) — The word अनुपदिन् formed anomalously by इनि denotes 'who goes after, who searches'.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.91: saakshaaddrashtarisamjnyaayaam (साक्षाद्द्रष्टरि संज्ञायाम्) — The affix इनि comes in the sense of 'a spectator, looker on' after the word साक्षात् when the word so formed is a Name.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.92: kshetriyachparakshetrechikitsyah (क्षेत्रियच् परक्षेत्रे चिकित्स्यः) — The word क्षेत्रियच् (क्षेत्रिय) is anomalous meaning 'curable in another body' i.e. 'not curable in this life'.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.93: indriyamindralimgamindradrushtamindrasrushtamindrajushtamindradattamitivaa (इन्द्रियमिन्द्रलिंगमिन्द्रदृष्टमिन्द्रसृष्टमिन्द्रजुष्टमिन्द्रदत्तमिति वा) — The word इन्द्रियम् (having उदात्त (acute accent) on the last) is anomalous meaning 'an organ of sense' and so called either because it is 'the characteristic from which the existence of इन्द्र is inferred' or 'it is seen by इन्द्र ' or 'it is created by इन्द्र ' or it is wished by इन्द्र ' or 'it is given by इन्द्र '.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.94: tadasyaastyasminnitimatup (तदस्यास्त्यस्मिन्निति मतुप्) — The affix मतुप् comes in the sense of 'whose it is' or 'in whom it is' after a word in the Nominative 1st-Case in construction.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.95: rasaadibhyashcha (रसादिभ्यश्च) — The affix मतुप् comes in the sense of 'whose it is' or 'in whom it is' after the प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stem) रस etc.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.96: praanisthaadaatolajanyatarasyaam (प्राणिस्थादातो लजन्यतरस्याम्) — The affix लच् comes optionally in the sense of मतुप् after a stem ending in long आ the word expressing something which is found only in a living being.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.97: sidhmaadibhyashcha (सिध्मादिभ्यश्च) — The affix लच् comes in the sense of मतुप् after the words सिध्म etc. and optionally after मतुप् also.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.98: vatsaamsaabhyaamkaamabale (वत्सांसाभ्यां कामबले) — The affix लच् comes in the senses of 'love' and 'strength' respectively after the words वत्स and अंस।",
    "Sūtra 5.2.99: phenaadilachcha (फेनादिलच् च) — The affixes इलच् and लच् come in the sense of मतुप् after the word फेन and optionally after the affix मतुप् also.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.100: lomaadipaamaadipichchhaadibhyahashanelachah (लोमादिपामादिपिच्छादिभ्यः शनेलचः) — The three affixes श , न and इलच् come in the sense of मतुप् respectively after the words of the three classes i.e. 1. लोमदि 2. पामादि and 3. पिच्छादि and the affix मतुप् also comes in the alternative.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.101: prajnyaashraddhaarchaavruttibhyonah (प्रज्ञाश्रद्धार्चाभ्यो णः) — The affix ण् comes in the sense of मतुप् after the words 1. प्रज्ञा 2. श्रद्धा and 3. अर्चा as well as the affix मतुप् ।",
    "Sūtra 5.2.102: tapahasahasraabhyaamvineenee (तपःसहस्राभ्यां विनीनी) — The affixes विनि and इनि come with the force of मतुप् after the words तपस् and सहर respectively.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.103: ancha (अण् च) — And also अण् comes after तपस् and सहर।",
    "Sūtra 5.2.104: sikataasharkaraabhyaamcha (सिकताशर्कराभ्यां च) — The affix अण् comes in the sense of मतुप् after सिकता and शर्करा।",
    "Sūtra 5.2.105: deshelubilachaucha (देशे लुबिलचौ च) — When the sense if of 'locality' there may take place लुप् elision of the affixes denoting मतुप् (with the preservation of the gender and number of the word) or there may be the affixes इलच् , अण् and मतुप् after the words सिकता and शर्करा।",
    "Sūtra 5.2.106: dantunnaturach (दन्त उन्नत उरच्) — The affix उरच् comes in the sense of 'having projecting teeth' after the word दन्त।",
    "Sūtra 5.2.107: ooshasushimushkamadhorah (ऊषसुषिमुष्कमधो रः) — The affix र comes after the words 1. ऊष 2. सुषि 3. मुष्क and 4. मधु with the force of मतुप्।",
    "Sūtra 5.2.108: dyudrubhyaammah (द्युद्रुभ्यां मः) — The affix म comes in the sense of मतुप् after 1. द्यु and 2. द्रु ।",
    "Sūtra 5.2.109: keshaadvonyatarasyaam (केशाद्वोऽन्यतरस्याम्) — The affix व comes optionally with the force of मतुप् ।",
    "Sūtra 5.2.110: gaandyajagaatsamjnyaayaam (गाण्ड्यजगात् संज्ञायाम्) — The affix व comes in the sense of मतुप् after 1. गाण्डी and 2. अजग when the word is a Name.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.111: kaandaandaadeeranneerachau (काण्डाण्डादीरन्नीरचौ) — The affixes ईरन् and ईरच् come in the sense of मतुप् after the words 1. काण्ज and 2. अण्ड respectively.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.112: rajahakrushyaasutiparishadovalach (रजःकृष्यासुतिपरिषदो वलच्) — The affix वलच् comes in the sense of मतुप् after 1. रजस् 2. कृषि 3. आसुति and 3. परिषद्।",
    "Sūtra 5.2.113: dantashikhaatsamjnyaayaam (दन्तशिखात् संज्ञायाम्) — The affix वलच् comes in the sense of मतुप् after 1. दन्त and 2. शिखा when a Name is formed.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.114: jyotsnaatamisraashrungginojasvinnoorjasvalagominmalinamaleemasaah (ज्योत्स्नातमिस्राशृङ्गिणोर्जस्विन्नूर्जस्वलगोमिन्मलिनमलीमसाः) — The words 1. ज्योत्स्न 2. तमिस्रा 3. शृङ्गिण 4. ऊर्जस्विन् 5. ऊर्जस्वल 6. गोमिन् 7. मलिन and 8. मलीमस are irregularly formed in the sense of मतुप् and are Names.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.115: atinithanau (अत इनिठनौ) — The affixes इनि and ठन् come in the sense of मतुप् after the प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stems) ending in short अ and in the alternative मतुप् also comes.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.116: vreehyaadibhyashcha (व्रीह्यादिभ्यश्च) — The affixes इनि and ठन् come in the sense of मतुप् after the words व्रीहि etc. as well as the affix मतुप् ।",
    "Sūtra 5.2.117: tundaadibhyilachcha (तुन्दादिभ्य इलच् च) — The affix इलच् also comes in the sense of मतुप् after the प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stems) तुन्द etc.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.118: ekagopoorvaatthanynityam (एकगोपूर्वाट्ठञ् नित्यम्) — The affix ठञ् always comes in the sense of मतुप् after a stem which in composition is preceded by एक or गो।",
    "Sūtra 5.2.119: shatasahasraantaachchanishkaat (शतसहस्रान्ताच्च निष्कात्) — The affix ठञ् comes in the sense of मतुप् after the words 1. शत and 2. सहस्र when they follow after निष्क।",
    "Sūtra 5.2.120: roopaadaahataprashamsayorap (रूपादाहतप्रशंसयोर्यप्) — The affix यप् comes in the sense of मतुप् after the word रूप when 'stamping (coining)' or 'praise' is denoted.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.121: asmaayaamedhaasrajovinih (अस्मायामेधास्रजो विनिः) — After a stem ending in अस् and after माया , मेधा and स्रज् comes the affix विनि in the sense of मतुप्।",
    "Sūtra 5.2.122: bahulamchhandasi (बहुलं छन्दसि) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas) the affix विनि is added diversely in the sense of मतुप् ।",
    "Sūtra 5.2.123: oornaayaayus (ऊर्णाया युस्) — The affix युस् is added to ऊर्णा in the sense of मतुप् in the छन्दस् (Vedas).",
    "Sūtra 5.2.124: vaachogminih (वाचो ग्मिनिः) — The affix ग्मिनि come in the sense of मतुप् after the word वाच्।",
    "Sūtra 5.2.125: aalajaatachaubahubhaashini (आलजाटचौ बहुभाषिणि) — The affixes आलच् and आटच् come in the sense of मतुप् after वाच् , the word denoting 'a talkative'.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.126: svaaminnaishvarye (स्वामिन्नैश्वर्ये) — The irregularly formed word स्वामिन् denotes 'Sir or Lord'.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.127: arshaadibhyoch (अर्शआदिभ्योऽच्) — The affix अच् comes in the sense of मतुप् after the words अर्श etc.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.128: dvamdvopataapagarhyaatpraanisthaadinih (द्वन्द्वोपतापगर्ह्यात् प्राणिस्थादिनिः) — The affix इनि (इन्) comes in the sense of मतुप् after a द्वन्द compound after the name of a disease and after anything denoting fault when the thing is found in a living being.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.129: vaataatisaaraabhyaamkukcha (वातातिसाराभ्यां कुक् च) — The augment कुक् comes before इनि (इन्) after the words 1. वात and 2. अतिसार।",
    "Sūtra 5.2.130: vayasipooranaat (वयसि पूरणात्) — The affix इनि (इन्) comes in the sense of मतुप् after an ordinal numeral when age is denoted.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.131: sukhaadibhyashcha (सुखादिभ्यश्च) — The affix इनि (इन्) comes (to the exclusion of other affixes) in the sense of मतुप् after the words सुख etc.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.132: dharmasheelavarnaantaachcha (धर्मशीलवर्णान्ताच्च) — The affix इनि (इन्) comes in the sense of मतुप् (to the exclusion of others) after nominal steps ending in 1. धर्म 2. शील 3. वर्ण।",
    "Sūtra 5.2.133: hastaajjaatau (हस्ताज्जातौ) — The affix इनि (इन्) comes in the sense of मतुप् after the word हस्त when a genus is denoted by the word so formed.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.134: varnaadbrahmachaarini (वर्णाद्ब्रह्मचारिणि) — The affix इनि (इन्) comes in the sense of मतुप् after the word वर्ण when the word so formed means a ब्रह्मचारिण्।",
    "Sūtra 5.2.135: pushkaraadibhyodeshe (पुष्करादिभ्यो देशे) — The affix इनि (इन्) comes in the sense of मतुप् after the words पुष्कर etc. when the word so formed denotes a locality.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.136: balaadibhyomatubanyatarasyaam (बलादिभ्यो मतुबन्यतरस्याम्) — The affixes मतुप् and इनि come after the प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stems) बल etc.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.137: samjnyaayaammanmaabhyaamh (संज्ञायां मन्माभ्याम्) — The affix इनि (इन्) comes in the sense of मतुप् after a प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stem) ending in मन् or म when the whole word so formed means a Name.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.138: kamshambhyaambabhayustitutayasah (कंशंभ्यां बभयुस्तितुतयसः) — The seven affixes 1. ब 2. भ 3. युस् 4. ति 5. तु 6. त and 7. यस् comes in the sense of मतुप् after कम् 'water and happiness' and शम् 'happiness'.",
    "Sūtra 5.2.139: tundivalivaterbhah (तुन्दिवलिवटेर्भः) — The affix भ comes in the sense of मतुप् after 1. तुन्दि 2. वलि and 3. वटि।",
    "Sūtra 5.2.140: ahamshubhamoryus (अहंशुभमोर्युस्) — The affix युस् (यु) comes in the sense of मतुप् after the word अहम् and the indeclinable शुभम् 'good'.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.1: praagdishovibhaktih (प्राग्दिशो विभक्तिः) — The sūtra taught from this forward up to दिक्शब्देभ्यः सप्तमीपञ्चमीप्रथमाभ्यो दिग्देशकालेष्वस्तातिः [[5.3.27]] (exclusive) are called विभक्ति।",
    "Sūtra 5.3.2: kimsarvanaamabahubhyodvyaadibhyah (किंसर्वनामबहुभ्योऽद्व्यादिभ्यः) — These प्राग्दिशीय affixes come after the word किम् and after a stem called सर्वनाम and after बहु but not after द्वि etc.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.3: idamish (इदम इश्) — For इदम् there is the substitute इश् when a प्राग्दिशीय affix follows.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.4: etetaurathoh (एतेतौ रथोः) — The substitutes एत and इत come instead of इदम् when a प्राग्दिशीय affix beginning with र and थ respectively follows.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.5: etadosh (एतदोऽन्) — The substitute अश् comes in the place of एतद् when a प्राग्दिशीय affix follows.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.6: sarvasyasonyatarasyaamdi (सर्वस्य सोऽन्यतरस्यां दि) — The स is substituted for सर्व before a प्राग्दिशीय विभक्ति beginning with द।",
    "Sūtra 5.3.7: panychamyaastasil (पञ्चम्यास्तसिल्) — The affix तसिल् (तस्) comes after the word किम् , a सर्वनाम and बहु when ending in Ablative -5th case.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.8: taseshcha (तसेश्च) — The affix तसिल् (तस्) is substituted for तस् -- प्रतियोगे पञ्चम्यास्तसिः [[5.4.44]], अपादाने चाहीयरुहोः [[5.4.45]] when किम् a सर्वनाम and बहु follow.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.9: paryabhibhyaamcha (पर्यभिभ्यां च) — The affix तसिल् (तस्) comes after परि and अभि also.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.10: saptamyaastral (सप्तम्यास्त्रल्) — The affix त्रल् comes after किम् , सर्वनाम and बहु when ending in Locative -7th case.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.11: idamohah (इदमो हः) — The affix ह comes after इदम् ending in the Locative -7th case.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.12: kimot (किमोऽत्) — The affix अत् (अ) comes after किम् ending in the Locative -7th case.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.13: vaahachachchhandasi (वा ह च च्छन्दसि) — Optionally the affix ह also comes in the छन्दस् (Vedas) after the word किम् in the Locative -7th case as well as other affixes.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.14: itaraabhyopidrushyante (इतराभ्योऽपि दृश्यन्ते) — The above affixes are seen coming after किम् , a सर्वनाम and बहु ending with other case-affixes also besides the Locative -7th case and Ablative -5th case.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.15: sarvaikaanyakimyattadahakaaledaa (सर्वैकान्यकिंयत्तदः काले दा) — After 1. सर्व 'all' 2. एक 'one' 3. अन्य 'other' 4. किम् 'what' 5 यद् 'which' and 6. तद् 'that' when time is denoted comes the affix दा , the words being in the Locative -7th case.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.16: idamorhil (इदमो र्हिल्) — After इदम् 'this' ending in the Locative -7th case comes the affix र्हिल् when time is denoted.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.17: adhunaa (अधुना) — The word अधुना is anomalous having the same sense.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.18: daaneemcha (दानीं च) — The affix दानीम् also comes after इदम् ending in the Locative -7th case, denoting time.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.19: tadodaacha (तदो दा च) — After तद् ending in the Locative -7th case when time is denoted, comes the affixes दा and दानीम् ",
    "Sūtra 5.3.20: tayordaarhilauchachchhandasi (तयोर्दार्हिलौ च च्छन्दसि) — After the two प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stems) इदम् and तद् come respectively the affixes दा and र्हिल् in the छन्दस् (Vedas) and also other affixes.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.21: anadyatanerhilanyatarasyaam (अनद्यतने र्हिलन्यतरस्याम्) — The affix र्हिल् comes optionally in denoting time not of the current day after the words किम् , the सर्वनाम and बहु etc.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.22: sadyahaparutparaaryaishamahaparedyavyadyapoorvedyuranyedyuranyataredyuritaredyuraparedyuradharedyurubhayedyuruttaredyuh (सद्यःपरुत्परार्यैषमःपरेद्यव्यद्यपूर्वेद्युरन्येद्युरन्यतरेद्युरितरेद्युरपरेद्युरधरेद्युरुभयेद्युरुत्तरेद्युः) — The following words are anomalous - 1. सद्यः 2. परुत् 3. परारि 4. ऐषमस् 5. परेद्यवि 6. अद्य 7. पूर्वेद्युस् 8. अन्येद्युस् 9. अन्यतरेद्युस् 10. इतरेद्युस् 11. अपरेद्युस् 12. अधरेद्युस् 13. उभयेद्युस् and 14. उत्तरेद्युस्।",
    "Sūtra 5.3.23: prakaaravachanethaal (प्रकारवचने थाल्) — The affix थाल् comes after the words किम् etc. -- किंसर्वनामबहुभ्योऽद्व्यादिभ्यः [[5.3.2]] when we speak of a kind or manner of being.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.24: idamasthamuh (इदमस्थमुः) — After इदम् comes the affix थमु (थम्) in the same sense of a kind or manner of being.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.25: kimashcha (किमश्च) — Also after किम् comes the affix थमु in the sense of denoting a manner.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.26: thaahetauchachchhandasi (था हेतौ च च्छन्दसि) — The affix था comes in the sense of 'cause' after the word किम् in the छन्दस् (Vedas).",
    "Sūtra 5.3.27: dikshabdebhyahasaptameepanychameeprathamaabhyodigdeshakaaleshvastaatih (दिक्शब्देभ्यः सप्तमीपञ्चमीप्रथमाभ्यो दिग्देशकालेष्वस्तातिः) — The affix अस्ताति (अस्तात्) comes after the words of 'direction', 'locality' or 'time' ending in the Locative -7th case, Ablative -5th case, Nominative 1st-Case, without a change of sense.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.28: dakshinottaraabhyaamatasuch (दक्षिणोत्तराभ्यामतसुच्) — The affix अतसुच् (अतस्) comes in the sense of 'direction', 'locality' or 'time' after the words 1. दक्षिण and 2. उत्तर।",
    "Sūtra 5.3.29: vibhaashaaparaavaraabhyaam (विभाषा परावराभ्याम्) — The affix अतसुच् (अतस्) comes in the sense of अस्ताति (अस्तात्) after 1. पर and 2. अवर।",
    "Sūtra 5.3.30: anycherluk (अञ्चेर्लुक्) — After words of direction ending in अञ्च् there is लुक् elision of the affix अस्ताति।",
    "Sūtra 5.3.31: uparyuparishtaat (उपर्युपरिष्टात्) — The words 1. उपरि and 2. उपरिष्टात् are anomalous in the sense of अस्ताति।",
    "Sūtra 5.3.32: pashchaat (पश्चात्) — The word पश्चात् is anomalous in the sense of अस्ताति।",
    "Sūtra 5.3.33: pashchapashchaachachchhandasi (पश्च पश्चा च च्छन्दसि) — The words पश्च and पश्चा are anomalous in the छन्दस् (Vedas) having the force of अस्ताति।",
    "Sūtra 5.3.34: uttaraadharadakshinaadaatih (उत्तराधरदक्षिणादातिः) — The affix अति is added to the words 1. उत्तर and 2. दक्षिण in the sense of अस्ताति।",
    "Sūtra 5.3.35: enabanyatarasyaamadoorepanychamyaah (एनबन्यतरस्यामदूरेऽपञ्चम्याः) — The affix एनप् (एन) comes optionally after the words 1. उत्तर and 2. दक्षिण in the sense of अस्ताति, when the limit indicated is not remote and when it is not a substitute of the Ablative -5th case affix.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.36: dakshinaadaach (दक्षिणादाच्) — The affix आच् (आ) comes after the word दक्षिण in the sense of अस्ताति , but not as a substitute of the Ablative -5th case.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.37: aahichadoore (आहि च दूरे) — The affix आहि comes after the word दक्षिण in the sense of अस्ताति as well as आच् when the reference is to a distant limit.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.38: uttaraachcha (उत्तराच्च) — The affixes आच् (आ) and आहि come after उत्तरा come in the sense of अस्ताति when the reference is to a distant limit.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.39: poorvaadharaavaraanaamasipuradhavashchaishaam (पूर्वाधरावराणामसि पुरधवश्चैषाम्) — The affix असि (अस्) comes in the sense of अस्ताति after 1. पूर्व 2. अधर and 3. अवर ; and 1. पुर् 2. अध् and 3. अव are the respective substitutes before this affix.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.40: astaaticha (अस्ताति च) — The same substitution takes place when the affix अस्ताति follows.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.41: vibhaashaavarasya (विभाषावरस्य) — The substitution of अव् for अवर is optional when अस्ताति follows.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.42: sankhyaayaavidhaarthedhaa (संख्याया विधार्थे धा) — The affix धा comes after a प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stem) denoting a Numeral when it means the mode or manner of an action.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.43: adhikaranavichaalecha (अधिकरणविचाले च) — The affix धा comes after a Numeral when the sense is a change in the apportionment or distribution of substances.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.44: ekaaddhodhyamunyanyaarayaam (एकाद्धो ध्यमुञन्यतरस्याम्) — After the word एक the substitute comes optionally instead of धा।",
    "Sūtra 5.3.45: dvitryoshchadhamuny (द्वित्र्योश्च धमुञ्) — The substitute धमुञ् comes optionally in the place of धा after the words 1. द्वि and 2. त्रि।",
    "Sūtra 5.3.46: edhaachcha (एधाच्च) — The substitute एधाच् (एधा) comes optionally in the place of धा after 1. द्वि and 2. त्रि।",
    "Sūtra 5.3.47: yaapyepaashap (याप्ये पाशप्) — The affix पाशप् denotes something as insignificant.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.48: pooranaadbhaageteeyaadan (पूरणाद्भागे तीयादन्) — After a प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stem) an ordinal number ending in तीय , comes the affix अन् (the word retaining its denotation) when a 'part' is meant.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.49: praagekaadashabhyochchhandasi (प्रागेकादशभ्योऽच्छन्दसि) — After an ordinal numeral up to 11 exclusive, comes the affix अन् , the word retaining its denotation when a 'part' is meant, but not so in the छन्दस् (Vedas).",
    "Sūtra 5.3.50: shashthaashtamaabhyaamnyacha (षष्ठाष्टमाभ्यां ञ च) — The affixes ञ (अ) and अन् after 1. षष्ठ and 2. अष्ठम when a 'part' is meant, but not in the छन्दस् (Vedas).",
    "Sūtra 5.3.51: maanapashvanggayohakanlukaucha (मानपश्वङ्गयोः कन्लुकौ च) — After the words 1. षष्ठ and 2. अष्ठम there may come respectively कन् (क) and लुक् elision of the affix when the meaning is a division of a measure called मान or grain or the part of the body of a beast respectively.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.52: ekaadaakinichchaasahaaye (एकादाकिनिच्चासहाये) — After the word एक comes also the affix आकिनिच् (आकिन्) (the word retaining its denotation) when the sense is 'without a companion'.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.53: bhootapoorvecharat (भूतपूर्वे चरट्) — The affix चर (with the feminine in ङीप्) comes after a प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stem), the word retaining its detonation when the meaning is 'this had been before'.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.54: shashthyaaroopyacha (षष्ठ्या रूप्य च) — After a प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stem) ending in the Genitive 6th-Case comes the affix रूप्य and also चरट् in the sense of 'having belonged formerly to somebody'.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.55: atishaayanetamabishthanau (अतिशायने तमबिष्ठनौ) — When the sense is that of surpassing, there come the affixes तमप् (तम) and इष्ठन् (इष्ठ) after a प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stem) the word retaining its denotation.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.56: tingashcha (तिङश्च) — So also after a finite verb, comes the affix तमप् (तम) when 'surpassing' is meant",
    "Sūtra 5.3.57: dvivachanavibhajyopapadetarabeeyasunau (द्विवचनविभज्योपपदे तरबीयसुनौ) — The affixes तरप् (तर) and ईयसुन् (ईयस्) come in the sense of 'surpassing' after a प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stem) or a finite-verb when it expresses (comparison between) two things or when that which is added to it (उपपद) is to be distinguished from another.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.58: ajaadeegunavachanaadeva (अजादी गुणवचनादेव) — The two affixes beginning with a vowel i.e. ईयस् and इष्ठ are added only after words denoting attributes.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.59: tushchhandasi (तुश्छन्दसि) — The affixes इष्ठन् and इयसुन् come in the छन्दस् (Vedas) after a प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stem) ending in तृ।",
    "Sūtra 5.3.60: prashasyasyashrah (प्रशस्यस्य श्रः) — For प्रशस्य is substituted श्र when the affixes इष्ठन् and इयसुन् follow.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.61: jyacha (ज्य च) — For प्रशस्य is also substituted ज्य when the affixes इष्ठन् and इयसुन् follow.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.62: vruddhasyacha (वृद्धस्य च) — ज्य is also substituted for वृद्ध when the affixes इष्ठन् and इयसुन् follow.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.63: antikabaadhayornedasaadhau (अन्तिकबाढयोर्नेदसाधौ) — For अन्तिक is substituted नेद and for बाढ is साध when the affixes इष्ठन् and इयसुन् follow.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.64: yuvaalpayohakananyatarasyaam (युवाल्पयोः कनन्यतरस्याम्) — Before the affixes इष्ठन् and इयसुन् , कन् is optionally substituted for युवन् and अल्प।",
    "Sūtra 5.3.65: vinmatorluk (विन्मतोर्लुक्) — The affixes विन् and मत् are लुक् elided when इष्ठन् and इयसुन् follow.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.66: prashamsaayaamroopap (प्रशंसायां रूपप्) — The affix रूपप् comes without a change of connotation after a stem - nominal or verbal, denoting 'praise'.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.67: eeshadasamaaptaukalpabdeshyadesheeyarah (ईषदसमाप्तौ कल्पब्देश्यदेशीयरः) — The affixes कल्पप् (कल्प), देश्य and देशीयर् (देशीय) come after a nominal or verbal stem which connotes a slight incompleteness.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.68: vibhaashaasupobahuchpurastaattu (विभाषा सुपो बहुच् पुरस्तात्तु) — Optionally to a declined noun may be added the affix बहुच् (बहु) but it stands before, when the sense is slight incompleteness.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.69: prakaaravachanejaateeyar (प्रकारवचने जातीयर्) — The affix जातीयर् (जातीय) comes after a case-inflected word which expresses 'a speciality'.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.70: praagivaatkah (प्रागिवात्कः) — The affix क governs all sūtras as far as इवे प्रतिकृतौ [[5.3.96]].",
    "Sūtra 5.3.71: avyayasarvanaamnaamakachpraakteh (अव्ययसर्वनाम्नामकच् प्राक् टेः) — The affix अकच् (अक्) is added to an indeclinable and to a Pronominal before the last vowel of those words in the sense of प्राग्रीव affixes.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.72: kasyachadah (कस्य च दः) — The letter द is the substitute of the final क् of an indeclinable when the affix अकच् (अक्) is added.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.73: ajnyaate (अज्ञाते) — The affixes क -- प्रागिवात्कः [[5.3.70]], and अकच् (अक्) -- अव्ययसर्वनाम्नामकच् प्राक् टेः [[5.3.71]], come after a word, noun or verb, when something or somebody not known is spoken of.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.74: kutsite (कुत्सिते) — The affixes क -- प्रागिवात्कः [[5.3.70]], and अकच् (अक्) -- अव्ययसर्वनाम्नामकच् प्राक् टेः [[5.3.71]], come when the thing is spoken of as contemptible.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.75: samjnyaayaamkan (संज्ञायां कन्) — The affix कन् (क) comes in the above sense of contemptible when the whole word is a Name.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.76: anukampaayaam (अनुकम्पायाम्) — The above affixes come when compassion is denoted.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.77: neetauchatadyuktaat (नीतौ च तद्युक्तात्) — Also as an expression of courteousness, the above mentioned affix is added to that by which compassion is shown.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.78: bahvachomanushyanaamnashthajvaa (बह्वचो मनुष्यनाम्नष्ठज्वा) — The affix ठच् is optionally added to a word of more than two syllables being the name of a human being, as an expression of compassion or of courtesy joined with compassion.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.79: ghanilachaucha (घनिलचौ च) — Also the affixes घन् and इलच् come after a word of more than two syllables being the name of a human being when compassion or courtesy joined with compassion is expressed.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.80: praachaamupaaderadajvuchaucha (प्राचामुपादेरडज्वुचौ च) — According to the opinion of Eastern Grammarians the affixes अडच् and वुच् also come after a human name beginning with the word उप।",
    "Sūtra 5.3.81: jaatinaamnahakan (जातिनाम्नः कन्) — The affix कन् is added to a Name of a human being which expresses a special idea when compassion or courtesy is meant.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.82: ajinaantasyottarapadalopashcha (अजिनान्तस्योत्तरपदलोपश्च) — The affix कन् comes in the sense of compassion, after a man-name ending in अजिन and this second member is elided before the affix.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.83: thaajaadaavoordhvamdviteeyaadachah (ठाजादावूर्ध्वं द्वितीयादचः) — When ठ -- बह्वचो मनुष्यनाम्नष्ठज्वा [[5.3.78]], or one of the affixes beginning with a vowel -- घनिलचौ च [[5.3.79]], प्राचामुपादेरडज्वुचौ च [[5.3.80]], taught above, follows, there is elision of all that portion which comes after the second vowel of the name of a human being.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.84: shevalasuparivishaalavarunaaryamaadeenaamtruteeyaat (शेवलसुपरिविशालवरुणार्यमादीनां तृतीयात्) — There is elision of that portion of the word which follows the third vowel in the case of a man-name beginning with 1. शेवल 2. सुपरि 3. विशाल 4. वरुण 5. आर्यमान् when the above affixes ठ or those having initial vowel follow.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.85: alpe (अल्पे) — The above-mentioned affix क -- प्रागिवात्कः [[5.3.70]], and the rest come in expressing the small quantity or small number of anything.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.86: hrasve (ह्रस्वे) — The above-mentioned affixes क -- प्रागिवात्कः [[5.3.70]], come in expressing shortness of length or diminutive.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.87: samjnyaayaamkan (संज्ञायां कन्) — The affix कन् comes when the short thing is a Name.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.88: kuteeshameeshundaabhyorah (कुटीशमीशुण्डाभ्यो रः) — The affix र comes after the words 1. कुटी 2. शमी and 3. शुण्डा when expressing shortness of length.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.89: kutvaadupach (कुत्वा डुपच्) — The affix डुपच् (उप) comes in expressing diminution after the word कुतू 'a jar'.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.90: kaasoogoneebhyaamshtarach (कासूगोणीभ्यां ष्टरच्) — The affix ष्टरच् (तर with feminine -- अन्यतो ङीष् [[4.1.40]]) comes in expressing diminution after the words 1. कासू and 2. गोणी।",
    "Sūtra 5.3.91: vatsokshaashvarshabhebhyashchatanutve (वत्सोक्षाश्वर्षभेभ्यश्च तनुत्वे) — The affix ष्टरच् expresses slenderness after the words 1. वत्स 2. उक्षन् 3. अश्व and 4. ऋषव।",
    "Sūtra 5.3.92: kimyattadonirddhaaranedvayorekasyadatarach (किंयत्तदो निर्द्धारणे द्वयोरेकस्य डतरच्) — After the words किम् , यद् and तद् in determining of the one out of two, comes the affix डतरच् (अतर with the elision of the final इम् and अद्).",
    "Sūtra 5.3.93: vaabahoonaamjaatipariprashnedatamach (वा बहूनां जातिपरिप्रश्ने डतमच्) — The affix डतमच् (अतम with the elision of the last syllable) comes after किम् , यत् and तत् , optionally when the object is the determining of the one out of many, the question being that of caste. ",
    "Sūtra 5.3.94: ekaachchapraachaam (एकाच्च प्राचाम्) — After the word एक , according to the opinion of Eastern Grammarians, may be added the affixes डतरच् and डतमच् in the above senses.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.95: avakshepanekan (अवक्षेपणे कन्) — The affix कन् comes after a प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stem) in expressing scoffing.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.96: ivepratikrutau (इवे प्रतिकृतौ) — The affix कन् means also 'like this' when the imitation of a thing is to be expressed.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.97: samjnyaayaamcha (संज्ञायां च) — The affix कन् comes in the sense of 'like this' when the whole word so formed is a Name.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.98: lummanushye (लुम्मनुष्ये) — When in the same way a Man is denoted the affix is elided by लुप् , the word retaining its number and gender.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.99: jeevikaarthechaapanye (जीविकार्थे चापण्ये) — A similar elision of the affix कन् takes place then also, when the figure is made a means of livelihood, it being presumed, that no traffic is driven thereby.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.100: devapathaadibhyashcha (देवपथादिभ्यश्च) — After the words देवपथ etc. there is similar elision of the affix कन् -- इवे प्रतिकृतौ [[5.3.96]] and संज्ञायां च [[5.3.97]] expressing an image or a Name.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.101: vasterdhany (वस्तेर्ढञ्) — The affix ढञ् comes in the sense of 'like this' after वस्ति।",
    "Sūtra 5.3.102: shilaayaadhah (शिलाया ढः) — The affix ढ comes in the sense of 'like this' after शिला।",
    "Sūtra 5.3.103: shaakhaadibhyoyat (शाखादिभ्यो यत्) — The affix यत् comes in the sense of 'like this' after शाखा etc.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.104: dravyamchabhavye (द्रव्यं च भव्ये) — The word द्रव्य is anomalous meaning 'beautiful'.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.105: kushaagraachchhah (कुशाग्राच्छः) — The affix छ comes in the sense of 'like this' after the word कुशाग्र।",
    "Sūtra 5.3.106: samaasaachchatadvishayaat (समासाच्च तद्विषयात्) — The affix छ comes, also, only in the sense of 'like this' after a compound noun which contains in itself the force of 'like this'.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.107: sharkaraadibhyon (शर्करादिभ्योऽण्) — The affix अण् comes in the sense of 'like this' after the words शर्करा etc.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.108: anggulyaadibhyashthak (अङ्गुल्यादिभ्यष्ठक्) — The affix ठक् comes in the sense of 'like this' after the words अङ्गुली etc.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.109: ekashaalaayaashthajanyatarasyaam (एकशालायाष्ठजन्यतरस्याम्) — The affix ठच् also comes optionally after the word एकशाला with the force of 'like this'.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.110: karkalohitaadeekak (कर्कलोहितादीकक्) — The affix ईकक् (ईक) comes in the sense of 'like this' after 1. कर्क and 2. लोहित।",
    "Sūtra 5.3.111: pratnapoorvavishvemaatthaalchhandasi (प्रत्नपूर्वविश्वेमात्थाल् छन्दसि) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas), the affix थाल् comes in the sense of 'like this' after 1. प्रत्न 2. पूर्व 3. विश्व and 4. इम (इदम्).",
    "Sūtra 5.3.112: poogaanynyyograamaneepoorvaat (पूगाञ्ञ्योऽग्रामणीपूर्वात्) — The affix ञ्य is added without changing the connotation, to a word denoting a horde, but not when the word is derived from the name of their leader.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.113: vraatachphanyorastriyaam (व्रातच्फञोरस्त्रियाम्) — The affix ञ्य comes after the name of a wild band after a word ending in च्फाञ् -- गोत्रे कुञ्जादिभ्यश्च्फञ् [[4.1.98]], without change of sense, but not in the feminine.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.114: aayudhajeevisamghaanynyyadvaaheekeshvabraahmanaraajanyaat (आयुधजीविसंघाञ्ञ्यड्वाहीकेष्वब्राह्मणराजन्यात्) — To a name expressing multitude living by the trade of arms, is added the affix ञ्यट् when it is the name among वाहीक but not when it is the name of a ब्राह्मण , nor when the word is राजन्य।",
    "Sūtra 5.3.115: vrukaattenyan (वृकाट्टेण्यण्) — The affix टेण्यण् comes after the word वृक , a class of persons living by trade of arms.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.116: daamanyaaditrigartashashthaachchhah (दामन्यादित्रिगर्तषष्ठाच्छः) — The affix छ (ईय) comes without changing the sense after दामिनि etc. and after six warrior-stocks called त्रिगर्त षष्ठा।",
    "Sūtra 5.3.117: parshvaadiyaudheyaadibhyaamananyau (पर्श्वादियौधेयादिभ्यामणञौ) — The affix अण् comes after पर्शु etc. and the affix अञ् comes after यौधेय etc. without changing the sense when these words denote warrior classes.",
    "Sūtra 5.3.118: abhijidvidabhruchchhaalaavachchhikhaavachchhameevadoornaavachchhrumadanoyany (अभिजिद्विदभृच्छालावच्छिखावच्छमीवदूर्णावच्छ्रुमदणो यञ्) — The affix यण् comes without changing the sense, after the words 1. अभिजित् 2. बिदभृत् 3. शालावत् 4. शिखावत् 5. शामीवत् 6. ऊर्णावत् and 7. श्रुमत् when those words end in the Patronymic affix अण् ।",
    "Sūtra 5.3.119: nyyaadayastadraajaah (ञ्यादयस्तद्राजाः) — The affixes ञ्य etc. -- पूगाञ्ञ्योऽग्रामणीपूर्वात् [[5.3.112]], etc. are called तद्राजा।",
    "Sūtra 5.4.1: paadashatasyasamkhyaaderveepsaayaamvunlopashcha (पादशतस्य संख्यादेर्वीप्सायां वुन् लोपश्च) — The affix वुन् comes after the words 1. पाद and 2. शत when preceded by a numeral, the sense being that of distributive relation, and the final of the stem is elided.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.2: dandavyavasargayoshcha (दण्डव्यवसर्गयोश्च) — Also when the sense is of a punishment or a donation.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.3: sthoolaadibhyahaprakaaravachanekan (स्थूलादिभ्यः प्रकारवचने कन्) — The affix कन् comes in the sense of 'like that or speciality', after the words स्थूल etc.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.4: anatyantagatauktaat (अनत्यन्तगतौ क्तात्) — After a participle ending in क्त comes the affix कन् when the meaning is something not yet wholly completed.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.5: nasaamivachane (न सामिवचने) — Not so when a word in the sense of 'half' precedes such participle.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.6: bruhatyaaaachchhaadane (बृहत्या आच्छादने) — The affix कन् comes after the word बृहति when it means 'an article of dress'.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.7: ashadakshaashitanggvalamkarmaalampurushaadhyuttarapadaatkhah (अषडक्षाशितङ्ग्वलंकर्मालम्पुरुषाध्युत्तरपदात् खः) — The affix ख comes after the words 1. अषडक्ष 2. आशितङ्गु 3. अलंकर्म 4. अलम्पुरुष and after a stem ending in अधि।",
    "Sūtra 5.4.8: vibhaashaaanycheradikstriyaam (विभाषा अञ्चेरदिक्स्त्रियाम्) — The affix ख optionally may be added without change of sense to a stem ending in अञ्च् when it does not mean a point of the compass used in the feminine gender.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.9: jaatyantaachchhabandhuni (जात्यन्ताच्छ बन्धुनि) — The affix छ (ईय) is added without a change of sense to a stem ending in the word जाति when it means appropriateness.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.10: sthaanaantaadvibhaashaasasthaanenetichet (स्थानान्ताद्विभाषा सस्थानेनेति चेत्) — The affix छ (ईय) is optionally added to a stem ending in स्थान if it is compounded with something with which another is made to take an equal place.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.11: kimettingavyayaghaadaamvadravyaprakarshe (किमेत्तिङव्ययघादाम्वद्रव्यप्रकर्षे) — To the affixes तर and तम (घ -- तरप्तमपौ घः [[1.1.22]]) ordained to come after the word किम् -- अतिशायने तमबिष्ठनौ [[5.3.55]], or after a word ending in ए -- घकालतनेषु कालनाम्नः [[6.3.17]], or after a finite verb -- तिङश्च [[5.3.56]], द्विवचनविभज्योपपदे तरबीयसुनौ [[5.3.57]], or after an indeclinable, is added the affix आम् , but not if the excess belongs to a substance (and not to an action or quality)",
    "Sūtra 5.4.12: amuchachchhandasi (अमु च च्छन्दसि) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas) the affix अमु (अम्) also is added after the above, under similar circumstances.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.13: anugaadinashthak (अनुगादिनष्ठक्) — The affix ठक् comes after the word अनुगादिन , without changing its sense.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.14: nachahastriyaamany (णचः स्त्रियामञ्) — The affix अण् (अ) comes without changing the sense, after a word ending in the affix णच् (अ) when the word is feminine.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.15: aninunah (अणिनुणः) — The affix अण् (अ) comes without changing the sense, after a stem ending in the affix इणुन्।",
    "Sūtra 5.4.16: visaarinomatsye (विसारिणो मत्स्ये) — The affix अण् (अ) is added to the word विसारिन् when a word expressing 'fish' is to be made.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.17: samkhyaayaahakriyaabhyaavruttigananekrutvasuch (संख्यायाः क्रियाभ्यावृत्तिगणने कृत्वसुच्) — The affix कृत्वसुच् is added to a numeral when the repetition of such an action is to be counted.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.18: dvitrichaturbhyahasuch (द्वित्रिचतुर्भ्यः सुच्) — The affix सुच् (स्) is added to the numerals 1. द्वि 2. त्रि and 3. चतुर् in the sense of counting the repetition of an action.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.19: ekasyasakruchcha (एकस्य सकृच्च) — The word सकृत् is substituted for एक before the affix सुच् (स्) when an action is to be counted.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.20: vibhaashaabahordhaaviprakrushtakaale (विभाषा बहोर्धाविप्रकृष्टकाले) — The affix धा is optionally added to the numeral बहु to count the repetition of an action occurring in a not distant period of time.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.21: tatprakrutavachanemayat (तत्प्रकृतवचने मयट्) — The affix मयट् (मय with the feminine in grave ई) is added to a word in Nominative 1st-Case in construction when the sense is 'made thereof' or 'subsisting therein'.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.22: samoohavachchabahushu (समूहवच्च बहुषु) — When that, whereof something is made or subsists in, is a multitude, then the affixes expressing a great quantity -- तस्य समूहः [[4.2.37]] etc. may also be used to denote 'made thereof, subsisting therein'.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.23: anantaavasathetihabheshajaanynyyah (अनन्तावसथेतिहभेषजाञ्ञ्यः) — The affix ञ्य comes without changing sense, after the words 1. अनन्ता 2. आवसथ 3. इतिह and 4. भेषजा।",
    "Sūtra 5.4.24: devataantaattaadarthyeyat (देवतान्तात्तादर्थ्ये यत्) — After a stem ending in the word देवता being in the Dative -4th Case in construction comes the affix यत् (यं) in the sense of 'appointed for it'.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.25: paadaarghaabhyaamcha (पादार्घाभ्यां च) — The affix यत् (यं) comes after the words 1. पाद and 2. अर्घ being in the Dative -4th Case in construction when the meaning is 'for the purpose of that'.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.26: atithernyyah (अतिथेर्ञ्यः) — The affix ञ्य comes after अतिथि in the Dative -4th Case in construction, in the sense of 'for the purpose of that'.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.27: devaattal (देवात्तल्) — The affix तल् comes after देव without change of sense.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.28: avehakah (अवेः कः) — The affix क comes after अवि without change of sense.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.29: yaavaadibhyahakan (यावादिभ्यः कन्) — The affix कन् comes after the words याव etc. without changing their sense.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.30: lohitaanmanau (लोहितान्मणौ) — The affix कन् comes without changing the sense, after लोहित when it means a precious stone.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.31: varnechaanitye (वर्णे चानित्ये) — The affix कन् comes after लोहित when it means color which is not permanent.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.32: rakte (रक्ते) — The affix कन् comes after the word लोहित meaning a substance dyed red.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.33: kaalaachcha (कालाच्च) — The affix कन् is added to the word काल when it means a passing colour or dyed with colour.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.34: vinayaadibhyashthak (विनयादिभ्यष्ठक्) — The affix ठक् comes without changing the sense after the word विनय etc.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.35: vaachovyaahrutaarthaayaam (वाचो व्याहृतार्थायाम्) — The affix ठक् comes after वाच् when it means the purport of the message spoken by another.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.36: tadyuktaatkarmanon (तद्युक्तात् कर्मणोऽण्) — The affix अण् comes after the word कर्मन् 'occupation' when it occurs in connection therewith (i.e. when it is the result of an oral message or commission).",
    "Sūtra 5.4.37: oshadherajaatau (ओषधेरजातौ) — The affix अण् comes after ओषधि when it does not mean a species.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.38: prajnyaadibhyashcha (प्रज्ञादिभ्यश्च) — The affix अण् comes after the words प्रज्ञ etc. (the words retaining their sense).",
    "Sūtra 5.4.39: mrudastikan (मृदस्तिकन्) — The affix तिकन् comes after मृद् (the word retaining its sense).",
    "Sūtra 5.4.40: sasnauprashamsaayaam (सस्नौ प्रशंसायाम्) — The affixes स and स्नौ come after मृद् when it means 'excellence'.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.41: vrukajyeshthaabhyaamtiltaatilauchachchhandasi (वृकज्येष्ठाभ्यां तिल्तातिलौ च च्छन्दसि) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas) the affixes तिल् and तातिल् come after 1. वृक and 2. ज्येष्ठ when excellence is denoted.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.42: bahvalpaarthaachchhaskaarakaadanyatarasyaam (बह्वल्पार्थाच्छस् कारकादन्यतरस्याम्) — After a word signifying much or little, comes the affix शस् optionally when the word stands in agreement with a verb (as कारक)।",
    "Sūtra 5.4.43: samkhyaikavachanaachchaveepsaayaam (संख्यैकवचनाच्च वीप्सायाम्) — The affix शस् comes optionally after crude forms denoting numbers and words denoting units of a coin in the singular number when a distributive sense is to be expressed (and the word is a कारक).",
    "Sūtra 5.4.44: pratiyogepanychamyaastasih (प्रतियोगे पञ्चम्यास्तसिः) — The affix तसि comes after that Ablative -5th case which is ordained owing to the union with the कर्मप्रवचनीय word प्रति।",
    "Sūtra 5.4.45: apaadaanechaaheeyaruhoh (अपादाने चाहीयरुहोः) — The affix तसि comes after that Ablative -5th case which has the force of an अपादान कारक when this अपादान relation arises owing to the union with the verbs हीय (passive of हा) and रुह।",
    "Sūtra 5.4.46: atigrahaavyathanakshepeshvakartaritruteeyaayaah (अतिग्रहाव्यथनक्षेपेष्वकर्तरि तृतीयायाः) — The affix तसि comes after that Instrumental -3rd case which does not denote an agent and is governed by a verb having the sense of 'to excel', 'not to give away' and 'to blame'.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.47: heeyamaanapaapayogaachcha (हीयमानपापयोगाच्च) — And The affix तसि comes optionally after a word ending in the Instrumental -3rd case-affix when such a word is joined to the verb हीय or the noun पाप not denoting an agent.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.48: shashthyaavyaashraye (षष्ठ्या व्याश्रये) — The affix तसि comes optionally after a word ending in the Genitive 6th-Case when the sense is that of a party-name or function.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.49: rogaachchaapanayane (रोगाच्चापनयने) — The affix तसि comes optionally after a word denoting a disease ending in the Genitive 6th-Case when the healing of the same is denoted.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.50: abhootatadbhaavekrubhvastiyogesampadyakartarichvih (अभूततद्भावे कृभ्वस्तियोगे सम्पद्यकर्तरि च्विः) — The affix च्वि comes after a word when the agent has attained to the new state expressed by the word, what the thing previously was not and when the verbs कृ 'to make', भू 'to be' and अस् 'to be' are conjoined with it.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.51: arurmanashchakshushchetorahorajasaamlopashcha (अरुर्मनश्चक्षुश्चेतोरहोरजसां लोपश्च) — The affix च्वि comes after the words 1. अरुस् 2. मनस् 3. चक्षुस् 4. चेतस् 5. रहस् and 6. रजस् and there is elision of their final consonant.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.52: vibhaashaasaatikaartsnye (विभाषा साति कार्त्स्न्ये) — The affix साति may be used optionally in the sense of च्वि when something is changed in all its parts into something else.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.53: abhividhausampadaacha (अभिविधौ सम्पदा च) — The affix साति comes after a word in the sense of च्वि when it is in construction with the verb सम्पद् and the meaning is that all things of a kind are changed into something else, though partially.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.54: tadadheenavachane (तदधीनवचने) — The affix साति comes after a word expressing 'a master or lord' in the sense of 'dependent upon this' when it is in conjunction with the above verbs 1. कृ 'to make' 2. भू 'to be' 3. अस्ति 'to be' and 4. सम्पद्।",
    "Sūtra 5.4.55: deyetraacha (देये त्रा च) — The affix त्रा comes in the sense of 'to be given to that' as well as the affix साति , in conjunction with the above verbs 1. कृ 'to make' 2. भू 'to be' 3. अस्ति 'to be' and 4. सम्पद्।",
    "Sūtra 5.4.56: devamanushyapurushamartyebhyodviteeyaasaptamyorbahulam (देवमनुष्यपुरुषपुरुमर्त्येभ्यो द्वितीयासप्तम्योर्बहुलम्) — After the words 1. देव 2. मनुष्य 3. पुरुष 4. पुरु and 5. मर्त्ये ending in the Accusative -2nd case or Locative -7th case, the affix त्रा is diversely used, having the force of the Accusative -2nd case or Locative -7th case.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.57: avyaktaanukaranaaddvyajavaraardhaadanitaudaach (अव्यक्तानुकरणाद्द्व्यजवरार्धादनितौ डाच्) — The affix डाच् comes after the half of a word denoting an imitation of an inarticulate sound when such half consists of at least two syllables and when it is not followed by the quotation-mark इति।",
    "Sūtra 5.4.58: krunyodviteeyatruteeyashambabeejaatkrushau (कृञो द्वितीयतृतीयशम्बबीजात् कृषौ) — The affix डाच् comes after the word 1. द्वितीय 2. तृतीय 3. शम्ब and 4. बीज when connected with the verb कृ 'to make' and meaning 'to plough in such a way'.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.59: samkhyaayaashchagunaantaayaah (संख्यायाश्च गुणान्तायाः) — The affix डाच् comes after a numeral followed by the word गुण the sense being 'to plough so many times'.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.60: samayaachchayaapanaayaam (समयाच्च यापनायाम्) — The affix डाच् comes after the word समय when कृ 'to make' follows, when the sense is that of 'neglecting'.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.61: sapattranishpatraadativyathane (सपत्त्रनिष्पत्रादतिव्यथने) — The affix डाच् comes after the words 1. सपत्त्र and 2. निष्पत्र followed by the verb कृ 'to make' when the sense is that of causing intense pain.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.62: nishkulaannishkoshane (निष्कुलान्निष्कोषणे) — The affix डाच् comes after the word निष्कुल followed by the verb कृ 'to make' when the sense is 'to disembowel'.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.63: sukhapriyaadaanulomye (सुखप्रियादानुलोम्ये) — The affix डाच् comes after the words 1. सुख and 2. प्रिय followed by कृ 'to make' when the meaning is ('to concede', 'gratify') 'to go with the grain'.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.64: duhakhaatpraatilomye (दुःखात् प्रातिलोम्ये) — The affix डाच् comes after the word दुःख followed by कृ 'to make' when the sense is that of roasting.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.65: shoolaatpaake (शूलात् पाके) — The affix डाच् comes after the word शूल followed by कृ 'to make' when the sense is that of roasting.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.66: satyaadashapathe (सत्यादशपथे) — The affix डाच् comes after the word सत्य followed by कृ 'to make' when not meaning 'to swear'.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.67: madraatparivaapane (मद्रात् परिवापणे) — The affix डाच् comes after the word मद्र followed by कृ 'to make' in the sense of 'to shave'.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.68: samaasaantaah (समासान्ताः) — The following affixes are added to the ends of compounds without changing their sense.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.69: napoojanaat (न पूजनात्) — The समासान्त affixes are not applied to those words whose first member is a word expressing praise.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.70: kimahakshepe (किमः क्षेपे) — The समासान्त affix is not applied to a word preceded by किम् in the sense of reproach.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.71: nanyastatpurushaat (नञस्तत्पुरुषात्) — The समासान्त affix does not come after a तत्-पुरुष समास of words like राजन् etc. herein taught, when the negative particle न precedes them.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.72: pathovibhaashaa (पथो विभाषा) — The समासान्त affix does not optionally come after a तत्-पुरुष समास of the word पथिन् with नञ् ।",
    "Sūtra 5.4.73: bahuvreehausamkhyeyedajabahuganaat (बहुव्रीहौ संख्येये डजबहुगणात्) — The affix डाच् comes after a बहुव्रीहि समास denoting numeral except when the last term of such समास is बहु and गण।",
    "Sūtra 5.4.74: rukpoorapdhoohapathaamaanakshe (ऋक्पूरब्धूःपथामानक्षे) — The affix अ comes after 1. ऋक् 2. पुर् 3. अप् 4. धुर् and 5. पथिन् when finals is compound, but not so when धुर् is in conjunction with अक्ष।",
    "Sūtra 5.4.75: achpratyanvavapoorvaatsaamalomnah (अच् प्रत्यन्ववपूर्वात् सामलोम्नः) — The affix अच् comes after the words 1. सामन् and 2. लोमन् when 1. प्रति 2. अनु and 3. अव precede them.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.76: akshnodarshanaat (अक्ष्णोऽदर्शनात्) — The affix अच् comes after the word अक्षि when not meaning 'the eye'.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.77: achaturavichaturasuchaturastreepumsadhenvanaduharksaamavaangmanasaakshibhruvadaaragavorvashtheevapadashtheevanaktamdivaratrimdivaahardivasarajasanihashreyasapurushaayushadvyaayushatryaayushargyajushajaatokshamahokshavruddhokshopashunagoshthashvaah (अचतुरविचतुरसुचतुरस्त्रीपुंसधेन्वनडुहर्क्सामवाङ्मनसाक्षिभ्रुवदारगवोर्वष्ठीवपदष्ठीवनक्तंदिवरात्रिंदिवाहर्दिवसरजसनिःश्रेयसपुरुषायुषद्व्यायुषत्र्यायुषर्ग्यजुषजातोक्षमहोक्षवृद्धोक्षोपशुनगोष्ठश्वाः) — The following words are irregularly formed by adding the affix अच् - 1. अचतुर 2. विचतुर 3. सुचतुर 4. स्त्री-पुंसौ 5. धेन्वनडुहौ 6. ऋक्सामे 7. वाङ्मनसे 8. अक्षिभ्रुवम् 9. दार-गवम् 10. ऊर्वष्ठीवम् 11. पदष्ठीवम् 12. नक्तं-दिवम् 13. रत्रिंदिवम् 14. अहर्दिवम् 15. सरजसम् 16. निः-श्रेयसम् 17. पुरुषा-युषम् 18. द्व्यायुषम् 19. त्र्या-युषम् 20. ऋ-यजुषम् 21. जातोक्षः 22. महो-क्षः 23. वृद्धो-क्षः 24. उपशुनम् 25. गोष्ठश्वाः।",
    "Sūtra 5.4.78: brahmahastibhyaamvarchchasah (ब्रह्महस्तिभ्याम् वर्च्चसः) — The affix अच् comes after the word वर्चस् when preceded in a compound by the words ब्रह्म or हस्ति।",
    "Sūtra 5.4.79: avasamandhebhyastamasah (अवसमन्धेभ्यस्तमसः) — The affix अच् comes after the word तमस् when preceded by the words 1. अव 2. सम् 3. अन्ध in a compound.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.80: shvasovaseeyahashreyasah (श्वसो वसीयःश्रेयसः) — The affix अच् comes after the words 1. वसीयस् and 2. श्रेयस् when they follow the word श्वस् in a compound.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.81: anvavataptaadrahasah (अन्ववतप्ताद्रहसः) — The affix अच् comes after the word रहस् when it follows 1. अनु 2. अव and 3. तप्त in a compound.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.82: praterurasahasaptameesthaat (प्रतेरुरसः सप्तमीस्थात्) — The affix अच् comes after the word उरस् when it follows the word प्रति in a compound and has the sense of the Locative.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.83: anugavamaayaame (अनुगवमायामे) — The word अनुगव is irregularly formed by adding the affix अच् and has the sense of 'suited to the length of the cows'.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.84: dvistaavaatristaavaavedih (द्विस्तावा त्रिस्तावा वेदिः) — The words 1. द्विस्तावा and 2.त्रिस्तावा are irregularly formed meaning a वेदि 'altar'.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.85: upasargaadadhvanah (उपसर्गादध्वनः) — The affix अच् comes after the word अर्धवन् preceded by an उपसर्ग (Preposition) in a compound.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.86: tatpurushasyaanggulehasamkhyaavyayaadeh (तत्पुरुषस्याङ्गुलेः संख्याव्ययादेः) — The affix अच् comes after a तत्-पुरुष समास ending in the word अङ्गुलि when a numeral or an indeclinable precedes it.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.87: ahassarvaikadeshasamkhyaatapunyaachcharaatreh (अहस्सर्वैकदेशसंख्यातपुण्याच्च रात्रेः) — The affix अच् comes after the word रात्रि when preceded by अहन् or सर्व or a word denoting a portion of night, or संख्यात or पुण्य when the compound is a तत्-पुरुष as well as when a numeral or an indeclinable precedes रात्रि।",
    "Sūtra 5.4.88: ahnohnetebhyah (अह्नोऽह्न एतेभ्यः) — For अहन् is substituted अह्न when preceded by the above words (अहन् or सर्व or a word denoting a portion of night, or संख्यात or पुण्य) (and taking the affix टच् to be mentioned in राजाऽहस्सखिभ्यष्टच् [[5.4.91]]).",
    "Sūtra 5.4.89: nasamkhyaadehasamaahaare (न संख्यादेः समाहारे) — This substitution of अह्न for अहन् does not take place after a numeral when it forms a collective noun meaning a number of days taken as a unity.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.90: uttamaikaabhyaamcha (उत्तमैकाभ्यां च) — And also after the word that stands last in the above list (i.e. पुण्य) and एक this substitution does not take place.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.91: raajaahassakhibhyashtach (राजाहस्सखिभ्यष्टच्) — The affix टच् is added to the words 1. राजन् 2. अहन् and 3. सखि when standing at the end of a तत्-पुरुष समास ।",
    "Sūtra 5.4.92: gorataddhitaluki (गोरतद्धितलुकि) — The affix टच् comes after गो standing at the end of a तत्-पुरुष समास when no elision of a तद्धित-affix has taken place in forming such a समास ।",
    "Sūtra 5.4.93: agraakhyaayaamurasah (अग्राख्यायामुरसः) — The affix टच् comes after the word उरस् standing at the end of a तत्-पुरुष समास when it has the sense of 'the most excellent of its kind'.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.94: anoshmaayassarasaamjaatisamjnyayoh (अनोऽश्मायस्सरसाम् जातिसंज्ञयोः) — The affix टच् comes after 1. अनस् 2. अश्मन् 3. अयस् and 4. सरस् when at the end of a तत्-पुरुष समास it denotes a genus or a name.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.95: graamakautaabhyaamchatakshnah (ग्रामकौटाभ्यां च तक्ष्णः) — The affix टच् comes after तक्ष when preceded by 1. ग्राम and 2. कौट in a तत्-पुरुष समास ।",
    "Sūtra 5.4.96: atehashunah (अतेः शुनः) — The affix टच् comes after the word श्वन् preceded by अति in a तत्-पुरुष समास ।",
    "Sūtra 5.4.97: upamaanaadapraanishu (उपमानादप्राणिषु) — The affix टच् comes after the word श्वन् ending in a तत्-पुरुष समास when another thing not being a living object is compared with it.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.98: uttaramrugapoorvaachchasakthnah (उत्तरमृगपूर्वाच्च सक्थ्नः) — The affix टच् comes after सक्थि when preceded by 1. उत्तर 2. मृग 3. पूर्व in a तत्-पुरुष समास as well as when a thing is compared with it.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.99: naavodvigoh (नावो द्विगोः) — The affix टच् comes after the word नौ when at the end of a द्विगु समास (Numeral Determinative Compound).",
    "Sūtra 5.4.100: ardhaachcha (अर्धाच्च) — The affix टच् comes after the word नौ when preceded by the word अर्ध in a तत्-पुरुष समास ।",
    "Sūtra 5.4.101: khaaryaahapraachaam (खार्याः प्राचाम्) — To the word खारी , at the end of a द्विगु समास (Numeral Determinative Compound) and to the same, when preceded by the word अर्ध in a तत्-पुरुष समास the affix टच् is added, according to the opinion of the Eastern Grammarians.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.102: dvitribhyaamanyjaleh (द्वित्रिभ्यामञ्जलेः) — The affix टच् is added to the word अञ्जलि when preceded by 1. द्वि or 2. त्रि in a द्विगु तत्-पुरुष समास (Numeral Determinative Compound).",
    "Sūtra 5.4.103: anasantaannapumsakaachchhandasi (अनसन्तान्नपुंसकाच्छन्दसि) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas) the affix टच् comes after a तत्-पुरुष समास in Neuter Gender ending in अन् or अस्।",
    "Sūtra 5.4.104: brahmanojaanapadaakhyaayaam (ब्रह्मणो जानपदाख्यायाम्) — The affix टच् comes after the word ब्रह्मण in a तत्-पुरुष समास when the compound denotes a person belonging to a certain country.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.105: kumahadbhyaamanyatarasyaam (कुमहद्भ्यामन्यतरस्याम्) — The affix टच् comes optionally after the word ब्रह्मण preceded by the words 1. कु and 2. महत् in a तत्-पुरुष समास ।",
    "Sūtra 5.4.106: dvamdvaachchudashahaantaatsamaahaare (द्वन्द्वाच्चुदषहान्तात् समाहारे) — The affix टच् comes after a द्वन्द समास denoting in a palatal or a द् or ष् or ह् when the compound is a समाहार द्वन्द (collective noun taken as a unity).",
    "Sūtra 5.4.107: avyayeebhaavesharatprabhrutibhyah (अव्ययीभावे शरत्प्रभृतिभ्यः) — The affix टच् comes after the words शरत् etc. when forming an अव्ययीभाव समास ।",
    "Sūtra 5.4.108: anashcha (अनश्च) — The affix टच् comes after an अव्ययीभाव समास ending in अम् as the final of a compound.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.109: napumsakaadanyatarasyaam (नपुंसकादन्यतरस्याम्) — The affix टच् comes optionally after an अव्ययीभाव समास ending with a neuter word whose final syllable is अऩ्।",
    "Sūtra 5.4.110: nadeepaurnamaasyaagrahaayaneebhyah (नदीपौर्णमास्याग्रहायणीभ्यः) — The affix टच् comes optionally after an अव्ययीभाव समास ending in 1. नदी 2. पौर्णमासी and 3. आग्रहायणि।",
    "Sūtra 5.4.111: jhayah (झयः) — The affix टच् comes optionally after an अव्ययीभाव समास ending in a letter of झय् class (a mute letter).",
    "Sūtra 5.4.112: gireshchasenakasya (गिरेश्च सेनकस्य) — The affix टच् comes after an अव्ययीभाव समास ending in गिरि according to the opinion of the Grammarian सेनक।",
    "Sūtra 5.4.113: bahuvreehausakthyakshnohasvaanggaatshach (बहुव्रीहौ सक्थ्यक्ष्णोः स्वाङ्गात् षच्) — The affix षच् comes after the words 1. सक्थि and 2. अक्षि , final in a बहुव्रीहि समास and denoting a portion of one's body.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.114: anggulerdaaruni (अङ्गुलेर्दारुणि) — The affix षच् comes after a बहुव्रीहि समास ending in the word अङ्गुलि when the compound means 'a piece of wood'.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.115: dvitribhyaamshamoordhnah (द्वित्रिभ्यां ष मूर्ध्नः) — The affix ष comes after a बहुव्रीहि समास ending in मूर्ध्न् and preceded by 1. द्वि and 2. त्रि।",
    "Sūtra 5.4.116: appooraneepramaanyoh (अप् पूरणीप्रमाण्योः) — The affix अप् comes after a बहुव्रीहि समास ending in a feminine ordinal numeral or in the word प्रमाणी।",
    "Sūtra 5.4.117: antarbahirbhyaamchalomnah (अन्तर्बहिर्भ्यां च लोम्नः) — The affix अप् comes after a बहुव्रीहि समास ending in लोमन् and preceded by 1. अन्तर and 2. बहिस्।",
    "Sūtra 5.4.118: anynaasikaayaahasamjnyaayaamnasamchaasthoolaat (अञ्नासिकायाः संज्ञायां नसं चास्थूलात्) — The affix अच् is added to the word नासिका final in a बहुव्रीहि समास when it expresses a name whereby नस् is substituted for नासिका , but not so when the word स्थूल precedes the word नासिका।",
    "Sūtra 5.4.119: upasargaachcha (उपसर्गाच्च) — The affix अच् comes after the word नासिका final in a बहुव्रीहि समास when an उपसर्ग (Preposition) precedes it and नस् is substituted for नासिका।",
    "Sūtra 5.4.120: supraatasushvasudivashaarikukshachaturashraineepadaajapadaproshthapadaah (सुप्रातसुश्वसुदिवशारिकुक्षचतुरश्रैणीपदाजपदप्रोष्ठपदाः) — The following बहुव्रीहि-s are irregularly formed by adding अच् - 1. सु-प्रात 2. सु-श्व 3. सु-दिव 4. शारिकुक्ष 5. चतुरश्र 6. एणी-पद 7. अज-पद and 8. प्रोष्ठ-पद।",
    "Sūtra 5.4.121: nanyduhasubhyohalisakthyoranyatarasyaam (नञ्दुःसुभ्यो हलिसक्थ्योरन्यतरस्याम्) — The affix अच् comes optionally after the words 1. हलि and 2. सक्थि final in a बहुव्रीहि समास when preceded by a negative particle or by the words 1. दुस् and 2. सु।",
    "Sūtra 5.4.122: nityamasichprajaamedhayoh (नित्यमसिच् प्रजामेधयोः) — The affix असिच् (अस्) comes invariably after 1. प्रजा and 2. मेधा final in a बहुव्रीहि समास when the above particles 1. नञ् 2. दुस् and 3. सु precede them.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.123: bahuprajaashchhandasi (बहुप्रजाश्छन्दसि) — The form बहुप्रजास् is valid in the Vedas.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.124: dharmaadanichkevalaat (धर्मादनिच् केवलात्) — The affix अनिच् (अन्) comes after the word धर्म when it is the last member of a बहुव्रीहि समास and is itself the only word without any other word joined with it or when the first member is a single word.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.125: jambhaasuharitatrunasomebhyah (जम्भा सुहरिततृणसोमेभ्यः) — The word जम्भन् stands at the ending of a बहुव्रीहि समास when preceded by 1. सु 2. हरित 3. तृण and 4. सोम।",
    "Sūtra 5.4.126: dakshinermaalubdhayoge (दक्षिणेर्मा लुब्धयोगे) — The form दक्षिणेर्मन् is an irregularly formed बहुव्रीहि समास when used in conjunction with a hunter.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.127: ichkarmavyatihaare (इच् कर्मव्यतिहारे) — The affix इच् comes after a बहुव्रीहि समास when the compound denotes the reciprocity of an action.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.128: dvidandyaadibhyashcha (द्विदण्ड्यादिभ्यश्च) — The words द्विदण्डि etc. are valid forms of इच्।",
    "Sūtra 5.4.129: prasambhyaamjaanunorjnyuh (प्रसम्भ्यां जानुनोर्ज्ञुः) — After the words प्र and सम् there is the substitution of ज्ञु for जानु when forming the बहुव्रीहि समास ।",
    "Sūtra 5.4.130: oordhvaadvibhaashaa (ऊर्ध्वाद्विभाषा) — The substitution of ज्ञु for जानु when the word ऊर्धव precedes it.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.131: oodhasonang (ऊधसोऽनङ्) — The syllable अनङ् is the substitute of the final ऊधस् in a बहुव्रीहि समास ।",
    "Sūtra 5.4.132: dhanushashcha (धनुषश्च) — The अनङ् is the substitute of the final of धनुस् in a बहुव्रीहि समास ।",
    "Sūtra 5.4.133: vaasamjnyaayaam (वा संज्ञायाम्) — The substitution of अनङ् does not optionally take place when the बहुव्रीहि समास is a name.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.134: jaayaayaaning (जायाया निङ्) — For the final of जाया is substituted निङ् in a बहुव्रीहि समास ।",
    "Sūtra 5.4.135: gandhasyedutpootisusurabhibhyah (गन्धस्येदुत्पूतिसुसुरभिभ्यः) — For the final of गन्ध is substituted इ when preceded by 1. उत् 2. पूति 3. सु and 4. सुरभि in a बहुव्रीहि समास ।",
    "Sūtra 5.4.136: alpaakhyaayaam (अल्पाख्यायाम्) — The इ is substituted for the final अ of गन्ध at the end of a बहुव्रीहि समास when गन्ध means 'a little'.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.137: upamaanaachcha (उपमानाच्च) — The इ is substituted for the final अ of गन्ध at the end of a बहुव्रीहि समास when preceded by a word denoting a thing with which it is compared.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.138: paadasyalopohastyaadibhyah (पादस्य लोपोऽहस्त्यादिभ्यः) — The final अ of पाद is elided when it is at the end of a बहुव्रीहि समास preceded by a word denoting a thing with which it is compared but not so when such word is हस्ति etc.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.139: kumbhapadeeshucha (कुम्भपदीषु च) — The words कुम्भपदी etc. have been formed by the similar elision of the अ of पाद।",
    "Sūtra 5.4.140: samkhyaasupoorvasya (संख्यासुपूर्वस्य) — The final अ of पाद is elided also when a numeral or the word सु precedes it in a बहुव्रीहि समास ।",
    "Sūtra 5.4.141: vayasidantasyadatru (वयसि दन्तस्य दतृ) — For दन्त is substituted दत् in a बहुव्रीहि समास when a numeral or सु precedes it and the whole word expresses a stage of life i.e. an age.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.142: chhandasicha (छन्दसि च) — For दन्त is substituted दत् in the छन्दस् (Vedas) when final in a बहुव्रीहि समास ।",
    "Sūtra 5.4.143: striyaamsamjnyaayaam (स्त्रियां संज्ञायाम्) — For दन्त is substituted दत् when in the feminine gender denoting a name.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.144: vibhaashaashyaavaarokaabhyaam (विभाषा श्यावारोकाभ्याम्) — Optionally दत् is substituted for दन्त in a बहुव्रीहि समास when it is preceded by the words श्याव and अरोक।",
    "Sūtra 5.4.145: agraantashuddhashubhravrushavaraahebhyashcha (अग्रान्तशुद्धशुभ्रवृषवराहेभ्यश्च) — The substitution of दत् for दन्त is optional in a बहुव्रीहि समास when it is preceded by a word ending in 1. अग्र or by 2. शुद्ध 3. शुभ्र and 4. वराह।",
    "Sūtra 5.4.146: kakudasyaavasthaayaamlopah (ककुदस्यावस्थायां लोपः) — The final letter of ककुद is dropped in a बहुव्रीहि समास when it denotes age or condition of animals.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.147: trikakutparvate (त्रिककुत् पर्वते) — The बहुव्रीहि word त्रिककुद् formed by the elision of the final अ of ककुद is the name of a mountain.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.148: udvibhyaamkaakudasya (उद्विभ्यां काकुदस्य) — After उत् and वि the final of काकुद is elided in a बहुव्रीहि समास ।",
    "Sūtra 5.4.149: poornaadvibhaashaa (पूर्णाद्विभाषा) — After पूर्ण the final of काकुद is optionally elided in a बहुव्रीहि समास ।",
    "Sūtra 5.4.150: suhruddurhrudaumitraamitrayoh (सुहृद्दुर्हृदौ मित्रामित्रयोः) — The words सुहृत् and दुहृत् are irregularly formed बहुव्रीहि समास denoting 'a friend' and 'a foe' respectively.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.151: urahaprabhrutibhyahakap (उरःप्रभृतिभ्यः कप्) — The affix कप् comes after उरस् etc. final in a बहुव्रीहि समास ।",
    "Sūtra 5.4.152: inahastriyaam (इनः स्त्रियाम्) — The affix कप् is added to a बहुव्रीहि समास the last member of which ends in इन् when a feminine word is denoted",
    "Sūtra 5.4.153: nadyrutashcha (नद्यृतश्च) — The affix कप् is added to a बहुव्रीहि समास the last member of which is a feminine word ending in long ई or ऊ defined as नदी words or which ends in a short ऋ।",
    "Sūtra 5.4.154: sheshaadvibhaashaa (शेषाद्विभाषा) — After all other बहुव्रीहि समास not covered by the foregoing rules, may optionally be added the affix कप्।",
    "Sūtra 5.4.155: nasamjnyaayaam (न संज्ञायाम्) — The affix कप् does not come after a बहुव्रीहि समास when a name is meant.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.156: eeyasashcha (ईयसश्च) — The affix कप् does not come after a बहुव्रीहि समास the last member of which ends in the affix ईयस्।",
    "Sūtra 5.4.157: vanditebhraatuh (वन्दिते भ्रातुः) — The affix कप् does not come after a बहुव्रीहि समास ending in the word भ्रातृ when it means 'praised'.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.158: rutashchhandasi (ऋतश्छन्दसि) — The affix कप् does not come after a बहुव्रीहि समास ending in short ऋ in the छन्दस् (Vedas).",
    "Sūtra 5.4.159: naadeetantryohasvaangge (नाडीतन्त्र्योः स्वाङ्गे) — The affix कप् does not come after the words नाडी and तन्त्री final in a बहुव्रीहि समास when they mean organs of the body.",
    "Sūtra 5.4.160: nishpravaanishcha (निष्प्रवाणिश्च) — The word निष्प्रवाणि is irregularly formed without adding the affix कप् though the last word is a नदी word.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.1: ekaachodveprathamasya (एकाचो द्वे प्रथमस्य) — In the room of the first portion, containing a single vowel, there are two.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.2: ajaaderdviteeyasya (अजादेर्द्वितीयस्य) — Of that whose first syllable begins with a vowel, there are two in the room of the second portion containing a single vowel.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.3: nandraahasamyogaadayah (न न्द्राः संयोगादयः) — The letters न् , द् , and र् being the first letter of a compound consonant and being part of the second syllable, are not reduplicated.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.4: poorvobhyaasah (पूर्वोऽभ्यासः) — The first of the two is called अभ्यास or Reduplicate.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.5: ubheabhyastam (उभे अभ्यस्तम्) — The both are collectively called अभ्यस्त।",
    "Sūtra 6.1.6: jakshityaadayahashat (जक्षित्यादयः षट्) — So also the six roots beginning with जक्षि are called अभ्यस्त।",
    "Sūtra 6.1.7: tujaadeenaamdeerghobhyaasasya (तुजादीनां दीर्घोऽभ्यासस्य) — In the room of a short vowel of the Reduplicate of the the roots तुज् etc., a long is substituted.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.8: litidhaatoranabhyaasasya (लिटि धातोरनभ्यासस्य) — When the tense-affixes of the Perfect follow, there is reduplication of the root, which is not already reduplicated.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.9: sanyangoh (सन्यङोः) — Of a non-reduplicate root ending in सन् (Desiderative) or यङ् (Intensive) affixes, there is reduplication.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.10: shlau (श्लौ) — Of a non-reduplicate root there is reduplication when the विकरण श्लु follows.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.11: changi (चङि) — Of a non-reduplicate root there is reduplication when the affix चङ् of the Aorist follows.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.12: daashvaansaahvaanmeedhvaamshcha (दाश्वान् साह्वान् मीढ्वांश्च) — The participles दाश्वाम् , साह्वान् , and मीढ्वान् are irregularly formed without reduplication.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.13: shyangahasamprasaaranamputrapatyostatpurushe (ष्यङः सम्प्रसारणं पुत्रपत्योस्तत्पुरुषे) — There is vocalisation of the semi-vowel य् of the affix ष्यङ् [[4.1.78]] when followed in a तत्-पुरुष compound, by the words पुत्र and पति।",
    "Sūtra 6.1.14: bandhunibahuvreehau (बन्धुनि बहुव्रीहौ) — There is vocalisation of the affix ष्यङ् [[4.1.78]] when the word बन्धु follows in a बहुव्रीही compound.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.15: vachisvapiyajaadeenaamkiti (वचिस्वपियजादीनां किति) — The semi-vowels of the roots वच् , स्वप् , and यजादि verbs are vocalised when followed by an affix having an indicatory क।",
    "Sūtra 6.1.16: grahijyaavayivyadhivashtivichativrushchatipruchchhatibhrujjateenaamngiticha (ग्रहिज्यावयिव्यधिवष्टिविचतिवृश्चतिपृच्छतिभृज्जतीनां ङिति च) — There is vocalisation of the semi-vowels of the following verbs, when an affix having an indicatory क् or ङ् follows - ग्रह 'to take', ज्या 'to become old', वेञ् 'to weave', व्यध 'to strike', वश 'to shine', व्यच 'to deceive', व्रश्च 'to cut', प्रच्छ 'to ask' and भ्रस्ज 'to cook, to fry'.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.17: lityabhyaasasyobhayeshaam (लिट्यभ्यासस्योभयेषाम्) — There takes place a vocalisation of the semi-vowels of the reduplicate (अभ्यास) of both वाच्यादि [[6.1.15]] and ग्रहादि [[6.1.16]] words, when affixes of लिट् follow.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.18: svaapeshchangi (स्वापेश्चङि) — Of the causative verb स्वपि 'to cause one to sleep', there is vocalisation of the semi-vowel, when the affix चङ् of the Reduplicated Aorist follows.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.19: svapisyamivyenyaamyangi (स्वपिस्यमिव्येञां यङि) — There is vocalisation of the semi-vowel, of the verbs स्वप् 'to sleep', स्यम् 'to shout' and व्ये 'to cover', when followed by the affix यङ् of the Intensive.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.20: navashah (न वशः) — There is not vocalisation of the semi-vowel of वश्, when the affix यङ् follows.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.21: chaayahakee (चायः की) — The verb की is substituted for the verb चायृ 'to worship, to observe', when the Intensive affix यङ् follows.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.22: sphaayahaspheenishthaayaam (स्फायः स्फी निष्ठायाम्) — The स्फी is the substitute of स्फाय 'to swell', the निष्ठा affixes follow.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.23: styahprapoorvasya (स्त्यः प्रपूर्वस्य) — The verb स्त्या (स्त्यै and ष्ठ्यै) when preceded by प्र changes its semi-vowel to a vowel, when a निष्ठ affix follows.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.24: dravamoortisparshayohashyah (द्रवमूर्तिस्पर्शयोः श्यः) — There is vocalisation of the semi-vowel of the root श्या (श्यै) 'to go' when the निष्ठा affix follows, when the sense is 'coagulation' or 'cold to touch'.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.25: prateshcha (प्रतेश्च) — There is vocalisation of श्या preceded by the उपसर्ग प्रति , when the निष्ठा affixes follow.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.26: vibhaashaabhyavapoorvasya (विभाषाऽभ्यवपूर्वस्य) — There is optionally the vocalisation of the श्या followed by निष्ठा affixes, when the उपसर्गs अभि and अव precede it.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.27: shrutampaake (शृतं पाके) — Optionally शृत is formed in the sense of 'cooked', by the vocalisation of the semi-vowel of आ before the निष्ठा affix क्त।",
    "Sūtra 6.1.28: pyaayahapee (प्यायः पी) — पी is optionally the substitute of the root प्याय् 'to increase' before the निष्ठा affixes.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.29: lidyangoshcha (लिड्यङोश्च) — There is substitution of पी for प्याय् when the affixes of the Perfect (लिट्) and the Intensive (यङ्) follow.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.30: vibhaashaashveh (विभाषा श्वेः) — There is optionally the vocalisation of the semi-vowel श्वि before the affixes of the Perfect and the Intensive.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.31: nauchasamshchangoh (णौ च संश्चङोः) — There is optionally the vocalisation of the semi-vowel, in the causative of श्वि , when followed by the Desiderative सन् and the Aorist चङ् affix.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.32: hvahasamprasaaranam (ह्वः सम्प्रसारणम्) — There is the vocalisation of the semi-vowel of the causative of ह्वे before the Desiderative and the Reduplicated Aorist affixes.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.33: abhyastasyacha (अभ्यस्तस्य च) — There is vocalisation of the semi-vowel of ह्वा in the reduplicated form, in both the syllables.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.34: bahulamchhandasi (बहुलं छन्दसि) — In the छन्दस् , the semi-vowel of this root is diversely vocalised.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.35: chaayahakee (चायः की) — For चाय् is diversely substituted की in the छन्दस्।",
    "Sūtra 6.1.36: apasprudhethaamaanruchuraanruhushchichyushetityaajashraataahashritamaasheeraasheerttah (अपस्पृधेथामानृचुरानृहुश्चिच्युषेतित्याजश्राताःश्रितमाशीराशीर्त्ताः) — In the छन्दस् the following irregular forms are met with - अस्पृधेथाम् , आनृचुः , आनृहुः , चिच्युषे , तित्याज , श्राताः , श्रितम् , आशीः , आशीर्त्तः।",
    "Sūtra 6.1.37: nasamprasaaranesamprasaaranam (न सम्प्रसारणे सम्प्रसारणम्) — When a semi-vowel base has been vocalised, there is no vocalisation of the other semi-vowel that may precede it in the same word.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.38: litivayoyah (लिटि वयो यः) — In the substituted root वय [[2.4.41]], the य in the Perfect is not vocalised.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.39: vashchaasyaanyatarasyaamkiti (वश्चास्यान्यतरस्याम् किति) — Before the tense-affixes of the Perfect that have an indicatory क [[1.2.5]], for the य् of वय् may optionally be substituted a व्।",
    "Sūtra 6.1.40: venyah (वेञः) — The semi-vowel of वे 'to weave' is not vocalised in the Perfect.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.41: lyapicha (ल्यपि च) — The semi-vowel of वे 'to weave' is not vocalised in the Participial affix ल्यप् follows.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.42: jyashcha (ज्यश्च) — The semi-vowel of ज्या 'to grow old' is not vocalised when the affix ल्यप् follows.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.43: vyashcha (व्यश्च) — The semi-vowel of व्या (व्ये) 'to cover' is not vocalised when the affix ल्यप् follows.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.44: vibhaashaapareh (विभाषा परेः) — The vocalisation may optionally take place when व्ये preceded by परि takes the affix ल्यप्।",
    "Sūtra 6.1.45: aadechupadesheshiti (आदेच उपदेशेऽशिति) — In a root, which in the system of grammatical instruction (i.e. the धातुपाठ), ends with a diphthong (ए , ऐ , ओ, औ), there is the substitution of आ for the diphthong, provided that no affix with an indicatory श् follows it.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.46: navyoliti (न व्यो लिटि) — There is not the substitution of आ for the diphthong of the root व्ये when the affixes of the Perfect follow.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.47: sphuratisphulatyorghanyi (स्फुरतिस्फुलत्योर्घञि) — In the roots स्फुर् and स्फुल् 'to move', there is the substitution of the आ for the diphthong when the affix घञ् follows.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.48: kreengjeenaamnau (क्रीङ्जीनां णौ) — The substitution of आ for the diphthong takes place in the causatives of the roots क्री 'to buy, to purchase', इ 'to study' and जि 'to conquer'.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.49: sidhyaterapaaralaukike (सिध्यतेरपारलौकिके) — The substitution of आ takes for the diphthong in the causative of सिध् , when it does not refer to the next life.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.50: meenaatiminotideengaamlyapicha (मीनातिमिनोतिदीङां ल्यपि च) — And there is substitution of आ for the finals of मी 'to hurt', मि 'to scatter' and दी 'to decay' when the affix ल्यप् follows, as well as before those affixes which demand this substitution for the diphthong.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.51: vibhaashaaleeyateh (विभाषा लीयतेः) — There is optionally the substitution of आ for the final of ली 'to adhere', in the धातुपाठ , when the affix ल्यप् follows or such an affix as would demand this substitution of the diphthong.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.52: khideshchhandasi (खिदेश्छन्दसि) — There is optionally the substitution of आ in the room of the diphthong of the verb खिद् 'to suffer pain', in the छन्दस्।",
    "Sūtra 6.1.53: apaguronamuli (अपगुरो णमुलि) — There is optionally the substitution of आ in the room of the diphthong of the root गुर् 'to exert' when preceded by the preposition अप and taking the affix णमुल्।",
    "Sūtra 6.1.54: chisphurornau (चिस्फुरोर्णौ) — There is optionally the substitution of आ in the room of the diphthong of the roots चि and स्फुर् when in the Causative.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.55: prajaneveeyateh (प्रजने वीयतेः) — There is optionally the substitution of आ in the room of the diphthong of the root वी in the causative, when meaning 'to conceive an embryo'.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.56: bibheterhetubhaye (बिभेतेर्हेतुभये) — There is optionally the substitution of आ in the room of the diphthong of the root भी 'to fear' in the causative, when the fear is produced directly through the agent of the causative.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.57: nityamsmayateh (नित्यं स्मयतेः) — There is invariably the substitution of आ for the diphthong of the root स्मि 'to smile' in the causative, when the astonishment is produced directly through the agent of the causative.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.58: srujidrushorjhalyamakiti (सृजिदृशोर्झल्यमकिति) — The augment अम् (अ) comes after the ऋ or सृज् 'to create' and दृश् 'to see', when an affix beginning with a झल् letter (the Mute and the Sibilant) follows: provided that it has no indicatory क।",
    "Sūtra 6.1.59: anudaattasyachardupadhasyaanyatarasyaam (अनुदात्तस्य चर्दुपधस्यान्यतरस्याम्) — The augment अम् (अ) augment comes optionally after the ऋ of those roots which are exhibited in the धातुपाठ as अनुदात्त , when such roots end in a consonant having a ऋ has penultimate and are followed by an affix beginning with a mute or sibilant and not having an indicatory क।",
    "Sūtra 6.1.60: sheershamshchhandasi (शीर्षंश्छन्दसि) — The word शीर्षन् 'head', is found in छन्दस्।",
    "Sūtra 6.1.61: yechataddhite (ये च तद्धिते) — There is the substitution of this stem शीर्षन् for शिरस् when a तद्धित-affix beginning with य follows.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.62: achisheershah (अचि शीर्षः) — There is the substitution of शीर्ष for शीरस् when a तद्धित-affix beginning with a vowel follows.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.63: paddannomaashrunnishasanyooshandoshanyakanychhakannudannaasanychhasprabhrutishu (पद्दन्नोमास्हृन्निशसन्यूषन्दोषन्यकञ्छकन्नुदन्नासञ्छस्प्रभृतिषु) — In the weak cases (beginning with the accusative plural) the following stems are substituted: पद for पाद , दत् for दन्त , नस् for नासिका , मास् for मास , हृद् for हृदय , निश for निशा , असन् for असृज् , यूषन् for यूष , दोषन् for दास् , यकन् for यकृत् , शकन् for शकृत् , उदन् for उदक and आसन् for आस्य।",
    "Sūtra 6.1.64: dhaatvaadehashahasah (धात्वादेः षः सः) — There is the substitution of स in the room of the ष् being the initial of a verbal root as enunciated in the धातुपाठ।",
    "Sūtra 6.1.65: nonah (णो नः) — There is the substitution of न् for the initial ण् of the root in the धातुपाठ।",
    "Sūtra 6.1.66: lopovyorvali (लोपो व्योर्वलि) — There is लोप-substitution (elision) of the व् and य् when followed by any consonant except य्।",
    "Sūtra 6.1.67: verapruktasya (वेरपृक्तस्य) — There is the elision of the affix वि when reduced to the single letter व्।",
    "Sūtra 6.1.68: halngyaabbhyodeerghaatsutisyapruktamhal (हल्ङ्याब्भ्यो दीर्घात् सुतिस्यपृक्तं हल्) — After a consonant there is the elision of the nominative affix स् and the tense-affix ति and सि (when reduced to the form of त् and स् ) being consonants; and so also after the long vowels ई and आ of the feminine (affix ङी and आप् ), there is the elision of the nominative affix स्।",
    "Sūtra 6.1.69: enghrasvaatsambuddheh (एङ्ह्रस्वात् सम्बुद्धेः) — The consonant of the nominative-affix (सु and its substitute अम् ) is elided in the Vocative singular after a nominal-stem ending in ए or ओ or a short vowel.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.70: sheshchhandasibahulam (शेश्छन्दसि बहुलम्) — In the छन्दस् , the elision of the case-ending इ (शि) of the nominative and accusative plural neuter, is optional.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.71: hrasvasyapitikrutituk (ह्रस्वस्य पिति कृति तुक्) — To a root ending in a short vowel is added the augment त् (तुक्) when a कृत्-affix having an indicatory ए follows.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.72: samhitaayaam (संहितायाम्) — In the following sutras up to [[6.1.157]] inclusive, the words संहितायाम् 'in an unbroken flow of speech', should be supplied.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.73: chhecha (छे च) — The augment त् is added to a preceding short vowel also when छ follows an in an uninterrupted speech.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.74: aangmaangoshcha (आङ्माङोश्च) — The augment त् is added to the particle आ and the prohibitive particle मा , when छ follows an in a continuous text.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.75: deerghaat (दीर्घात्) — The augment त् is added to a long vowel, when followed by छ in a continuous text.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.76: padaantaadvaa (पदान्ताद्वा) — The augment त् is added optionally to a long vowel final in a full word (पद) when followed by छ।",
    "Sūtra 6.1.77: ikoyanachi (इको यणचि) — The semi-vowels य् व् र् ल् are the substitutes of the corresponding vowels इ उ ऋ and ऌ (long and short), when followed by a vowel.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.78: echoyavaayaavah (एचोऽयवायावः) — For the vowels ए ऐ ओ and औ are respectively substituted अय् आय् अव् and आव् when a vowel follows.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.79: vaantoyipratyaye (वान्तो यि प्रत्यये) — The substitution of अव् and आव् for ओ and औ also takes place before an affix beginning with य।",
    "Sūtra 6.1.80: dhaatostannimittasyaiva (धातोस्तन्निमित्तस्यैव) — For the final dipthongs ओ and औ of a root, are substituted अव् and आव् respectively, before an affix beginning with य् , then only when such diphthong has been itself first evolved by that affix.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.81: kshayyajayyaushakyaarthe (क्षय्यजय्यौ शक्यार्थे) — In क्षय्य and जय्य there is substitution of अय् for ए only then when the sense is that of 'to be possible to do'.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.82: krayyastadarthe (क्रय्यस्तदर्थे) — In the क्रय्य there is substitution of अय् for ए when the sense is that of 'exposed or put out for sale, saleable'.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.83: bhayyapravayyechachchhandasi (भय्यप्रवय्ये च च्छन्दसि) — The forms भय्य and प्रवय्य are found in the छन्दस",
    "Sūtra 6.1.84: ekahapoorvaparayoh (एकः पूर्वपरयोः) — From here up to [[6.1.111]] inclusive is always to be supplied the phrase 'for the preceding and the following is substituted'.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.85: antaadivachcha (अन्तादिवच्च) — And this single substitute is considered as the final of the preceding (form) and the initial of the succeeding (form).",
    "Sūtra 6.1.86: shatvatukorasiddhah (षत्वतुकोरसिद्धः) — The substitution of the final आदेश is to be considered as to have not taken effect, when otherwise स would have changed to ष , or when the augment त् (तुक्) is to be added.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.87: aadgunah (आद्गुणः) — The गुण is the single substitute of the final अ or आ of a preceding word and the simple vowel of the succeeding (अ or आ + a vowel = गुण)।",
    "Sūtra 6.1.88: vruddhirechi (वृद्धिरेचि) — The वृद्धि is the single substitute of अ or आ of a preceding word and the initial diphthong of the succeeding (अ or आ + diphthong = वृद्धि)।",
    "Sūtra 6.1.89: etyedhatyoothsu (एत्येधत्यूठ्सु) — The वृद्धि is the single substitute of अ or आ + ए of एति (root इ) and एधति (root एध), and for अ or आ + ऊ of उठ (the substitute of वा in वाह by [[6.4.132]]).",
    "Sūtra 6.1.90: aatashcha (आटश्च) — The वृद्धि is the single substitute when the augment आट् is followed by any vowel.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.91: upasargaadrutidhaatau (उपसर्गादृति धातौ) — The वृद्धि is the single substitute when the अ or आ of a preposition (उपसर्ग) is followed by the short ऋ of a verb.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.92: vaasupyaapishaleh (वा सुप्यापिशलेः) — According to the opinion of आपिशलि, the वृद्धि is optionally the single substitute, when the अ or आ of a preposition is followed by a Denominative Verb beginning with ऋ।",
    "Sūtra 6.1.93: automshasoh (औतोऽम्शसोः) — For the ओ of a nominal stem + अ of the Accusative case-ending अम् and अस् the single substitute is आ।",
    "Sūtra 6.1.94: engipararoopam (एङि पररूपम्) — For the अ or आ of the Preposition + ए or ओ of a verbal root, the second vowel is the single substitute.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.95: omaangoshcha (ओमाङोश्च) — For the अ or आ of ओम् or + the vowel of the Preposition आङ् , the second vowel is the single substitute.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.96: usyapadaantaat (उस्यपदान्तात्) — For the अ or आ (not standing at the end of a पद or full word) + उ of उस the Tense-affix, the second vowel is the single substitute.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.97: atogune (अतो गुणे) — Also when the short अ , not being final in a पद , is followed by a गुण letter, then in the room of both the precedent and the subsequent - the single substitute is the form of the subsequent i.e. the गुण।",
    "Sūtra 6.1.98: avyaktaanukaranasyaatitau (अव्यक्तानुकरणस्यात इतौ) — The इ of इति is the single substitute for the अत् (of a word denoting imitation of an inarticulate sound) + इति।",
    "Sūtra 6.1.99: naamreditasyaantyasyatuvaa (नाम्रेडितस्यान्त्यस्य तु वा) — This substitution does not take place when a sound-imitation word is doubled, here, however, for the final त् + इ , the single substitute is optionally इ (the second vowel).",
    "Sūtra 6.1.100: nityamaamreditedaachi (नित्यमाम्रेडिते डाचि) — Of such a doubled sound-imitation word, to which the affix आ is added which causes elision of the final अत् , for the final त् of the first member and the initial consonant of the second member, such subsequent consonant is always the single substitute.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.101: akahasavarnedeerghah (अकः सवर्णे दीर्घः) — When a single vowel is followed by a homogenous vowel, the corresponding long vowel is the single substitute for both the precedent and the subsequent vowels.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.102: prathamayohapoorvasavarnah (प्रथमयोः पूर्वसवर्णः) — For the simple vowel of a nominal-stem and for the vowel of the case-affixes of the Nominative and the Accusative in all numbers, there is the single substitution of a long vowel corresponding to the first vowel.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.103: tasmaachchhasonahapumsi (तस्माच्छसो नः पुंसि) — After such a long vowel homogenous with the first, न् is substituted for the स् of the Acccusative case affix शस् in the masculine.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.104: naadichi (नादिचि) — The substitution of a long vowel homogenous with the first, does not take place when अ or आ is followed by a vowel (other than अ) of the case-affixes of the Nominative and the Accusative.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.105: deerghaajjasicha (दीर्घाज्जसि च) — The substitution of a long vowel homogenous with the first, does not take place when a long vowel is followed by a nominative or accusative case-affix beginning with a vowel (other than अ) or by the Nominative Plural affix अस्।",
    "Sūtra 6.1.106: vaachhandasi (वा छन्दसि) — In the Vedas, the long vowel may optionally be the single substitute of both vowels in these cases last mentioned.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.107: amipoorvah (अमि पूर्वः) — There is the single substitution of the first vowel, when a simple vowel is followed by the अ of the case ending अम्।",
    "Sūtra 6.1.108: samprasaaranaachcha (सम्प्रसारणाच्च) — There is the single substitution of the first vowel for the vocalised semi-vowel and the subsequent vowel.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.109: engahapadaantaadati (एङः पदान्तादति) — In the room of ए or ओ final in a पद , and the short अ , which follows it, is substituted the single vowel of the form of the first (ए or ओ)।",
    "Sūtra 6.1.110: ngasingasoshcha (ङसिङसोश्च) — In the room of ए or ओ (in the body of a word), + अ of the case-affix अस् of the Ablative and Genitive Singular, the single substitute is the form of the precedent.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.111: rutut (ऋत उत्) — In the room of ऋ + अ of the case-affix अस् of the Ablative and Genitive singular, the single substitute is the letter short उ।",
    "Sūtra 6.1.112: khyatyaatparasya (ख्यत्यात् परस्य) — There is the substitution of उ for the अ of अस् of the Ablative and Genitive Singular after सखि and पति , when for the इ of those two stems य् is substituted.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.113: atororaplutaadaplute (अतो रोरप्लुतादप्लुते) — The उ is the substitute of रु (the र् substitute of a final स् [[8.2.66]]) when an अ , which is not a प्लुत, both precedes and follows it.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.114: hashicha (हशि च) — The उ is the substitute of रु (the र् substitute of a final स् [[8.2.66]]) when it is followed by a soft consonant and preceded by an अप्लुत short अ।",
    "Sūtra 6.1.115: prakrutyaantahapaadamavyapare (प्रकृत्याऽन्तःपादमव्यपरे) — The final ए or ओ and the following अ when occurring in the middle half of a foot of a Vedic verse, retain their original forms, except when the अ is followed by ख् or य्।",
    "Sūtra 6.1.116: avyaadavadyaadavakramuravrataayamavantvavasyushucha (अव्यादवद्यादवक्रमुरव्रतायमवन्त्ववस्युषु च) — The ए or ओ retain their original form in the middle of a Vedic verse, when the following words come after them (though the अ in these has a व् and य् following it) - अव्यात् , अवद्यात् , अवक्रमुः , अव्रत , अवन्तु , अवस्यु।",
    "Sūtra 6.1.117: yajushyurah (यजुष्युरः) — In the यजुर्वेद , the word उरस् when changed to उरो , retains it original form when followed by a short अ which is also retained.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.118: aapojushaanovrushnovarshishthembembaalembikepoorve (आपोजुषाणोवृष्णोवर्षिष्ठेऽम्बेऽम्बालेऽम्बिकेपूर्वे) — In the यजुर्वेद , the short अ is retained after आपो , जुषाणो , वृष्णो , वर्षिष्ठे and also in and after अम्बे or अम्बाले when they stand before अम्बिके। ",
    "Sūtra 6.1.119: anggityaadaucha (अङ्ग इत्यादौ च) — In the यजुर्वेद , when the word अङ्गे is followed by अङ्गे , the subsequent short अ is retained, as well as the preceding ए or ओ।",
    "Sūtra 6.1.120: anudaattechakudhapare (अनुदात्ते च कुधपरे) — In the यजुर्वेद , when an अनुदात्त अ is followed by a Guttural or a ध, the antecedent ए or ओ retains it s form, as well as this subsequent अ।",
    "Sūtra 6.1.121: avapathaasicha (अवपथासि च) — In the यजुर्वेद , when the gravely accented अ of अवपथास् follows ए or ओ , the vowels retain their original form.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.122: sarvatravibhaashaagoh (सर्वत्र विभाषा गोः) — After गो the subsequent अ may optionally be retained everywhere, in the Vedas as well as in the secular literature.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.123: avangsphotaayanasya (अवङ् स्फोटायनस्य) — According to the opinion of स्फोटायन , there is the substitution of अवङ् for the ओ of गो when it is followed by any vowel.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.124: indrecha (इन्द्रे च) — The substitution of अव for the ओ of गो is compulsory when a vowel to be found in the word इन्द्र follows it.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.125: plutapragruhyaaachinityam (प्लुतप्रगृह्या अचि नित्यम्) — The प्लुत ([[8.2.82]] etc.) and प्रगृह्य ([[1.1.11]] etc.) vowels remain unaltered when followed by a vowel (so far as the operation of that vowel is concerned).",
    "Sūtra 6.1.126: aangonunaasikashchhandasi (आङोऽनुनासिकश्छन्दसि) — For the adverb आ , is substituted in the छन्दस् the nasalised आँ , when a vowel follows it, and it retains its original form.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.127: ikosavarneshaakalyasyahrasvashcha (इकोऽसवर्णे शाकल्यस्य ह्रस्वश्च) — According to the opinion of शाकल्य , the simple vowels with the exception of अ , when followed by a non-homogenous vowel, retain their original forms; and if the vowel is long, it is shortened.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.128: rutyakah (ऋत्यकः) — According to the opinion of शाकल्य , the simple vowel followed by ऋ retains its original form, and if the vowel is long, it is shortened.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.129: aplutavadupasthite (अप्लुतवदुपस्थिते) — Before the word इति in the पदपाठ , a प्लुत vowel is treated like an ordinary अप्लुत vowel.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.130: eechaakravarmanasya (ई३ चाक्रवर्मणस्य) — According to the opinion of चाक्रवर्मण , the प्लुत ई3 followed by a vowel is treated like an ordinary vowel.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.131: divaut (दिव उत्) — For the final of the nominal-stem दिव् , there is the substitution of उ , when it is a पद ([[1.4.14]] etc.).",
    "Sūtra 6.1.132: etattadohasulopokorananysamaasehali (एतत्तदोः सुलोपोऽकोरनञ्समासे हलि) — After एतद् and तद् there is elision of the case-affix स् (of the Nominative Singular), when a consonant follows it, when these words are not combined with क ([[5.3.71]]) and have not the Negative Particle in composition.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.133: syashchhandasibahulam (स्यश्छन्दसि बहुलम्) — In the छन्दस् , the case-affix of the nominative singular is diversely elided after स्य , when a consonant follows it.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.134: sochilopechetpaadapooranam (सोऽचि लोपे चेत् पादपूरणम्) — The case affix of सस् 'he', is elided before a vowel, if by such elision the meter of the foot becomes complete.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.135: sutkaatpoorvah (सुट् कात् पूर्वः) — Up to [[6.1.157]] inclusive, the following sentence is to be supplied in every aphorism - 'before क is added स्'.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.136: adabhyaasavyavaayepi (अडभ्यासव्यवायेऽपि) — The augment सुट् is placed before क even when the augment अट् [[6.4.71]] or the Reduplicate intervenes (between the preposition and the verb).",
    "Sūtra 6.1.137: samparyupebhyahakarotaubhooshane (सम्पर्युपेभ्यः करोतौ भूषणे) — The augment सुट् is placed before क when सम् , परि , and उप are followed by the verb कृ and the sense is that of ornamenting.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.138: samavaayecha (समवाये च) — The augment सुट् is placed before क even when सम् , परि , and उप are followed by the verb कृ and the sense being that of combining.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.139: upaatpratiyatnavaikrutavaakyaadhyaahaareshu (उपात् प्रतियत्नवैकृतवाक्याध्याहारेषु) — The augment सुट् is placed before क , when the verb कृ comes after उप , and the sense is that of 'to take pains for something, to prepare, and to supply and ellipses in a discourse'.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.140: kirataulavane (किरतौ लवने) — The augment सुट् is placed before क , when the verb कृ comes after उप , and the sense is that of 'to cut or to split'.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.141: himsaayaamprateshcha (हिंसायां प्रतेश्च) — The augment सुट् is placed before क , when the verb कृ comes after उप and प्रति and the sense 'to cause suffering'.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.142: apaachchatushpaachchhakunishvaalekhane (अपाच्चतुष्पाच्छकुनिष्वालेखने) — The augment सुट् is placed before क , when the verb कृ comes after अप and the sense is 'the scraping of earth by four-footed animals or birds'.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.143: kustumburoonijaatih (कुस्तुम्बुरूणि जातिः) — The word कुस्तुम्बुरु is irregularly, formed with the augment सुट् and means 'a species of herb'.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.144: aparasparaahakriyaasaatatye (अपरस्पराः क्रियासातत्ये) — The word अपस्पराः is formed by the augment सुट् when the sense is that of 'uninterrupted action'.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.145: goshpadamsevitaasevitapramaaneshu (गोष्पदं सेवितासेवितप्रमाणेषु) — The word गोष्पद is formed by सुट् , when meaning a locality visited or not visited by cows, or when it means quantity.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.146: aaspadampratishthaayaam (आस्पदं प्रतिष्ठायाम्) — The word आस्पद is formed by सुट् when meaning 'a place or position'.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.147: aashcharyamanitye (आश्चर्यमनित्ये) — The word आशचर्य is formed by सुट् when meaning something 'unusual'.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.148: varchaskevaskarah (वर्चस्केऽवस्करः) — The word अवस्कर is formed by सुट् meaning 'excrement'.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.149: apaskarorathaanggam (अपस्करो रथाङ्गम्) — The word अपस्कर is formed by सुट् meaning 'the part of a chariot'.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.150: vishkirahashakunauvaa (विष्किरः शकुनौ वा) — The word विषिकर is formed with सुट् optionally when denoting a kind of bird, the other form being विकार।",
    "Sūtra 6.1.151: hrasvaachchandrottarapademantre (ह्रस्वाच्चन्द्रोत्तरपदे मन्त्रे) — In a मन्त्र , the सुट् is added to चन्द्र when it is second member in a compound and is preceded by a short vowel.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.152: pratishkashashchakasheh (प्रतिष्कशश्च कशेः) — To the root कश् 'to go, to punish', is added the augment सुट् , when preceded by the preposition प्रति , the form being प्रतिष्कशः।",
    "Sūtra 6.1.153: praskanvaharishchandraavrushee (प्रस्कण्वहरिश्चन्द्रावृषी) — The words प्रस्कण्व and हरिश्चन्द्र are formed by सुट् meaning the two Rishis of that name.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.154: maskaramaskarinauvenuparivraajakayoh (मस्करमस्करिणौ वेणुपरिव्राजकयोः) — The word मस्कर means 'a bamboo', and मस्करिन् means 'a medicant monk'.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.155: kaasteeraajastundenagare (कास्तीराजस्तुन्दे नगरे) — The words कास्तर and अजस्तुन्द are names of cities.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.156: kaaraskarovrukshah (कारस्करो वृक्षः) — The word कारस्कर means 'a tree'.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.157: paaraskaraprabhruteenichasamjnyaayaam (पारस्करप्रभृतीनि च संज्ञायाम्) — The words पारस्कर etc. are Names.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.158: anudaattampadamekavarjam (अनुदात्तं पदमेकवर्जम्) — A word is, with the exception of one syllable, unaccented.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.159: karshaatvatoghanyontudaattah (कर्षात्वतो घञोऽन्त उदात्तः) — A stem formed with the कृत-affix घञ् has the acute accent on the end-syllable, if it is formed from the root कृष् (कर्षति) or has a long आ in it.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.160: unychhaadeenaamcha (उञ्छादीनां च) — The words उच्छ etc. have acute accent on the last syllable.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.161: anudaattasyachayatrodaattalopah (अनुदात्तस्य च यत्रोदात्तलोपः) — An unaccented vowel gets also the acute accent, when on account of it preceding acute is elided.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.162: dhaatoh (धातोः) — A root has the acute on the end syllable.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.163: chitah (चितः) — A stem (formed by an affix or an augment or substitute) having an indicatory च् gets acute on the end syllable.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.164: taddhitasya (तद्धितस्य) — A stem formed with a तद्धित-affix having an indicatory च् , has acute on the end syllable.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.165: kitah (कितः) — A stem formed by a तद्धित-affix having an indicatory क , has acute accent on the end syllable.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.166: tisrubhyojasah (तिसृभ्यो जसः) — The Nominative Plural (जस्) of तिस् has acute accent on the last syllable.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.167: chaturahashasi (चतुरः शसि) — The word चतुर् , followed by the Accusative Plural, has acute accent on the last syllable.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.168: saavekaachastruteeyaadivibhaktih (सावेकाचस्तृतीयादिर्विभक्तिः) — The case affixes of the Instrumental and of the cases that follow it have the acute accent, if the stem in the Locative Plural is monosyllabic.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.169: antodattaaduttarapadaadanyatarasyaamanityasamaase (अन्तोदात्तादुत्तरपदादन्यतरस्यामनित्यसमासे) — The same case endings may optionally have the acute accent, if the monosyllabic word stands at the end of a compound, and has acute accent on the final, when the compound can be easily unloosened.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.170: anycheshchhandasyasarvanaamasthaanam (अञ्चेश्छन्दस्यसर्वनामस्थानम्) — In the छन्दस् , the case-endings other than the सर्वनामस्थान , get the acute accent when coming after अञ्चि।",
    "Sūtra 6.1.171: oodidampadaadyappumraidyubhyah (ऊडिदम्पदाद्यप्पुम्रैद्युभ्यः) — The same (असर्वनामस्थान) case-endings have the acute accent, when the stem ends in वाह् , also after इदम् after पद् etc. (up to [[6.1.63]]) after अप , पुंस् , रै and दिव्।",
    "Sūtra 6.1.172: ashtanodeerghaat (अष्टनो दीर्घात्) — The असर्वनामस्थान case-endings after अष्टन् 'eight', have acute accent, when it gets the form अष्टा।",
    "Sūtra 6.1.173: shaturanumonadyajaadee (शतुरनुमो नद्यजादी) — After an oxytone Particle in अत् the feminine suffix ई , (नदि) and the case endings beginning with vowels (with the exception of strong cases) have acute accent, when the participial affix has not the augment न् (i.e. is not अन्त).",
    "Sūtra 6.1.174: udaattayanohalpoorvaat (उदात्तयणो हल्पूर्वात्) — The same endings have the acute accent, when for the acutely accented final vowel of the stem, a semi-vowel is substituted, and which is preceded by a consonant.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.175: nongdhaatvoh (नोङ्धात्वोः) — But not so, when the vowel is of the feminine affix ऊ [[4.1.66]], or the final of a root.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.176: hrasvanudbhyaammatup (ह्रस्वनुड्भ्यां मतुप्) — The otherwise unaccented मत् (वत्) takes the acute accent, when an oxytoned stem ends in a light vowel, or the affix has before it the augment न् [[8.2.16]].",
    "Sūtra 6.1.177: naamanyatarasyaam (नामन्यतरस्याम्) — After an oxytoned stem which ends in a light vowel, the genitive ending नाम् has optionally the acute accent.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.178: ngyaashchhandasibahulam (ङ्याश्छन्दसि बहुलम्) — In the छन्दस , the ending नाम् has diversely the acute accent after the feminine affix ई।",
    "Sūtra 6.1.179: shattrichaturbhyohalaadih (षट्त्रिचतुर्भ्यो हलादिः) — The case-endings beginning with a consonant, have the acute accent after the Numerals called षट् [[1.1.24]], as well as after त्रि and चतुर् ।",
    "Sūtra 6.1.180: jhalyupottamam (झल्युपोत्तमम्) — The above numerals, when taking a case-affix beginning with a भस् or स् , get the acute accent on the penultimate syllable, when the said numerals assume a form consisting of three or more syllables.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.181: vibhaashaabhaashaayaam (विभाषा भाषायाम्) — In the Secular language this is optional.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.182: nagoshvantsaavavarnaraadangkrungkrudbhyah (न गोश्वन्त्साववर्णराडङ्क्रुङ्कृद्भ्यः) — The foregoing rules from [[6.1.168]] downwards have no applicability after गो , and श्वन् and words ending in them; nor after a stem which before the case ending of the Nominative Singular has अ or आ , nor after रज् , or after a stem ending in अञ्च् , nor as well as after कुञ्च् and कृत्।",
    "Sūtra 6.1.183: divojhal (दिवो झल्) — After दिव् a case-ending beginning with भ or स is unaccented.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.184: nruchaanyatarasyaam (नृ चान्यतरस्याम्) — After नृ , a case-ending beginning with भ or स is optionally unaccented.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.185: titsvaritam (तित्स्वरितम्) — An affix having an indicatory त् , is स्वरित i.e. has circumflex accent.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.186: taasyanudaattenngidadupadeshaallasaarvadhaatukamanudaattamahanvingoh (तास्यनुदात्तेन्ङिददुपदेशाल्लसार्वधातुकमनुदात्तमह्न्विङोः) — The Personal-endings and their substitutes [[3.2.124]]-126 are, when they are सार्वधातुक [[3.4.113]] etc., unaccented after the characteristic of the Periphrastic Future (तासि) after a root which in the धातुपाठ has an unaccented vowel or a ङ् (with the exception of ह्नुङ् and इङ्) as indicatory letter, as well as after what has a final अ in the Grammatical System of Instruction (उपदेश)।",
    "Sūtra 6.1.187: aadihasichonyatarasyaam (आदिः सिचोऽन्यतरस्याम्) — The सिच् Aorist, the first syllable may optionally have the acute accent.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.188: svapaadirhimsaamachyaniti (स्वपादिहिंसामच्यनिटि) — The acute accent is optionally on the first syllable when a Personal-ending, being सार्वधातुक tense affix beginning with a vowel, provided that the vowel is not the augment इट् , follows after स्वप् etc., or after हिंस्।",
    "Sūtra 6.1.189: abhyastaanaamaadih (अभ्यस्तानामादिः) — The acute accent falls on the first syllable of the reduplicate verbs when followed by an affix beginning with a vowel (the vowel being not नुट्) and being a सार्वधातुक Personal-ending.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.190: anudaattecha (अनुदात्ते च) — Also when the unaccented endings of the three persons in the singular follow, the first syllable of the reduplicate has the acute.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.191: sarvasyasupi (सर्वस्य सुपि) — The acute is on the first syllable of सर्व when the case-endings follow.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.192: bheehreebhruhumadajanadhanadaridraajaagaraampratyayaatpoorvampiti (भीह्रीभृहुमदजनधनदरिद्राजागरां प्रत्ययात् पूर्वम् पिति) — In भी , ह्री , भृ , हु , मद् , जन् , धन् , दरिद्रा and जागृ , and in their reduplicates, the acute accent is, before the सार्वधातुक unaccented endings of the three persons in singular, (पित्), on the syllable which precedes the affix.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.193: liti (लिति) — The acute accent falls on the syllable immediately preceding the affix that has an indicatory ल्।",
    "Sūtra 6.1.194: aadirnamulyanyatarasyaam (आदिर्णमुल्यन्यतरस्याम्) — The first syllable may be optionally acute when the absolutive affix णमुल् follows.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.195: achahakartruyaki (अचः कर्तृयकि) — The roots which are exhibited in धातुपाठ with a final vowel, may be optionally have the acute on the first syllable, before the affixes of the Passive (यक्), when the sense of the verb is Reflexive.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.196: thalichaseteedantovaa (थलि च सेटीडन्तो वा) — Before the ending थ of the Perfect, Second Person Singular, when this ending takes the augment इ ; the acute accent falls either on the first syllable, or on this इ , or on the personal ending.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.197: nynityaadirnityam (ञ्नित्यादिर्नित्यम्) — Whatever is derived with an affix having an indicatory ञ् or न् , has the acute accent invariably on the first syllable.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.198: aamantritasyacha (आमन्त्रितस्य च) — The first syllable of a Vocative gets the acute accent.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.199: pathimathohasarvanaamasthaane (पथिमथोः सर्वनामस्थाने) — The acute accent is on the first syllable of पथिन् and मथिन् when followed by a strong case-ending.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.200: antashchatavaiyugapat (अन्तश्च तवै युगपत्) — The Infinitive in तवै has the acute on the first syllable and on the last syllable at one and the same time.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.201: kshayonivaase (क्षयो निवासे) — The word क्षय has the acute on the first syllable and on the last syllable at one and the same time.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.202: jayahakaranam (जयः करणम्) — The acute accent falls on the first syllable of जय , in the sense of 'whereby one attains victory'.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.203: vrushaadeenaamcha (वृषादीनां च) — The words वृष etc. have the acute on the first syllable.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.204: samjnyaayaamupamaanam (संज्ञायामुपमानम्) — The acute accent falls on the first syllable of that word with which something is likened, provided that it is a name.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.205: nishthaachadvyajanaat (निष्ठा च द्व्यजनात्) — A disyllabic Participle in त (निष्ठा) when a Name has the acute on the first syllable, but not if the first syllable has an आ।",
    "Sūtra 6.1.206: shushkadhrushtau (शुष्कधृष्टौ) — Also शुष्क and धृष्ट have acute on the first syllable.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.207: aashitahakartaa (आशितः कर्ता) — The word आशित meaning 'having eaten' has acute on the first syllable.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.208: riktevibhaashaa (रिक्ते विभाषा) — The word रिक्त may have optionally the acute on the first syllable.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.209: jushtaarpitechachhandasi (जुष्टार्पिते च छन्दसि) — In the छन्दस , the words जुष्ट and अर्पित have optionally the acute on the first syllable.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.210: nityammantre (नित्यं मन्त्रे) — In the मन्त्राः , these words जुष्ट and अर्पित have always the acute on the first syllable.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.211: yushmadasmadorngasi (युष्मदस्मदोर्ङसि) — The acute accent is on the first syllable of युष्मद् and अस्मद् in the Genitive Singular.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.212: ngayicha (ङयि च) — The acute accent is on the first syllable of युष्मद् and अस्मद् in the Dative Singular.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.213: yatonaavah (यतोऽनावः) — Whatever is formed by the affix यत् , has, if it is a disyllabic word, the acute on the first syllable, with the exception of नाव्यः from नौ।",
    "Sūtra 6.1.214: eedavandavrushamsaduhaamnyatah (ईडवन्दवृशंसदुहां ण्यतः) — The acute accent is on the first syllable of ईड् , वन्द , वृ , शंस् and दुह् , when they are followed by the affix ण्यत्।",
    "Sūtra 6.1.215: vibhaashaavenvindhaanayoh (विभाषा वेण्विन्धानयोः) — The acute accent is optionally on the first syllable of वेणु and इन्धान।",
    "Sūtra 6.1.216: tyaagaraagahaasakuhashvathakrathaanaam (त्यागरागहासकुहश्वठक्रथानाम्) — The acute accent is optionally on the first syllables of त्याग , राग , हास , कुह , श्वठ , and क्रथ।",
    "Sūtra 6.1.217: upottamamriti (उपोत्तमं रिति) — What is formed by an affix having an indicatory र , has acute on the penultimate syllable, the full word consisting of more than two syllables.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.218: changyanyatarasyaam (चङ्यन्यतरस्याम्) — The acute accent may be optionally on the penultimate syllable of the reduplicated Aorist in चङ् , the word consisting of more than two syllables.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.219: matohapoorvamaatsamjnyaayaamstriyaam (मतोः पूर्वमात् संज्ञायां स्त्रियाम्) — The आ before the affix मत् has the acute accent, when the word is a name in the Feminine Gender.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.220: antovatyaah (अन्तोऽवत्याः) — The Names ending in अवति have the acute accent on the last syllable.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.221: eevatyaah (ईवत्याः) — The Names ending in ईवति have the acute on the last syllable.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.222: chau (चौ) — In compound words ending in अञ्च् , the final vowel of the preceding word has the acute accent in the weak cases in which only च् of अञ्च् remains.",
    "Sūtra 6.1.223: samaasasya (समासस्य) — A compound word has the acute on the last syllable.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.1: bahuvreehauprakrutyaapoorvapadam (बहुव्रीहौ प्रकृत्या पूर्वपदम्) — In a बहुव्रीहि समास the first member preserves its own original accent.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.2: tatpurushetulyaarthatruteeyaasaptamyupamaanaavyayadviteeyaakrutyaah (तत्पुरुषे तुल्यार्थतृतीयासप्तम्युपमानाव्ययद्वितीयाकृत्याः) — In a तत्-पुरुष समास the first member preserves its original accent when it is a word - 1. meaning 'a resemblance' or 2. an Instrumental or 3. a Locative or 4. a word with which the second member is compared or 5. an indeclinable or 6. an Accusative or 7. a Future Passive Participle",
    "Sūtra 6.2.3: varnahavarneshvanete (वर्णो वर्णेष्वनेते) — The first member of a तत्-पुरुष समास preserves its original accent when a word denoting colour is compounded with another colour denoting word but not so when it is the word एत।",
    "Sūtra 6.2.4: gaadhalavanayohapramaane (गाधलवणयोः प्रमाणे) — The first member of a तत्-पुरुष समास preserves its original accent when the second term is गाध or लवण and the compound expresses 'a measure or mass'.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.5: daayaadyamdaayaade (दायाद्यं दायादे) — In a तत्-पुरुष समास having the word दायद् as its second member, the first member denoting inheritance preserves its original accent.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.6: pratibandhichirakruchchhrayoh (प्रतिबन्धि चिरकृच्छ्रयोः) — In a तत्-पुरुष समास having the words चिर or कृच्छ्र as its second member, the first member, when it denotes that which experiences an obstacle, preserves its original accent.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.7: padepadeshe (पदेऽपदेशे) — The first member of a तत्-पुरुष समास preserves its original accent when the second member is the word पद denoting 'a pretext'.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.8: nivaatevaatatraane (निवाते वातत्राणे) — The first member of a तत्-पुरुष समास preserves its original accent when the second member is the word निवात in the sense of 'a protection from wind'.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.9: shaaradeanaartave (शारदेऽनार्तवे) — The first member of a तत्-पुरुष समास preserves its original accent when the second member is the word शारद having any other sense than that of 'autumnal'.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.10: adhvaryukashaayayorjaatau (अध्वर्युकषाययोर्जातौ) — The first member of a तत्-पुरुष समास preserves its original accent when the second member is the word अध्वर्यु or कषाय denoting a genus.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.11: sadrushapratiroopayohasaadrushye (सदृशप्रतिरूपयोः सादृश्ये) — The first member of a तत्-पुरुष समास preserves its original accent when the second member is the word सदृश or प्रतिरूप expressing resemblance with someone or something.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.12: dvigaupramaane (द्विगौ प्रमाणे) — The first member of a तत्-पुरुष समास preserves its original accent when the second member is a द्विगु समास (Numeral Determinative Compound) denoting 'measure or quantity'.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.13: gantavyapanyamvaanije (गन्तव्यपण्यं वाणिजे) — Before the word वाणिज 'a trader' the first member of a तत्-पुरुष समास preserves its accent when it is a word specifying the place wither one has to go or the ware in which one deals.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.14: maatropajnyopakramachchhaayenapumsake (मात्रोपज्ञोपक्रमच्छाये नपुंसके) — The first member of a तत्-पुरुष समास preserves its original accent when the words 1. मात्रा 2. उपज्ञा 3. उपक्रम and 4. छाया when these words appear as neuter.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.15: sukhapriyayorhite (सुखप्रिययोर्हिते) — The first member of a तत्-पुरुष समास preserves its original accent when its second term is सुख or प्रिय and the sense is 'to feel delight' or 'is good'.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.16: preetaucha (प्रीतौ च) — The first member of a तत्-पुरुष समास preserves its original accent when its second term is सुख or प्रिय and the sense is 'agreeable to one' or 'desired'.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.17: svamsvaamini (स्वं स्वामिनि) — The first member of a तत्-पुरुष समास preserves its original accent when it denotes a thing possessed and when its second term is स्वामिन्।",
    "Sūtra 6.2.18: patyaavaishvarye (पत्यावैश्वर्ये) — The first member of a तत्-पुरुष समास preserves its original accent when it ends in पति and means 'master' or 'lord'.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.19: nabhoovaakchiddidhishu (न भूवाक्चिद्दिधिषु) — The words भू , वाक् , चित् and दिधिषू however do not preserve their original accent in तत्-पुरुष समास when coming before the word पति denoting 'master' or 'lord'.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.20: vaabhuvanam (वा भुवनम्) — The word भुवन may optionally keep its accent in a तत्-पुरुष समास before the word पति denoting 'master' or 'lord'.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.21: aashangkaabaadhanedeeyassusambhaavane (आशङ्काबाधनेदीयस्सु संभावने) — The first member of a तत्-पुरुष समास preserves its original accent before words आशङ्क , आबाध and नेदीयस् , when it treats about a supposition.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.22: poorvebhootapoorve (पूर्वे भूतपूर्वे) — The first member of a तत्-पुरुष समास preserves its original accent when the second member is the word पूर्व and the sense is 'this had been lately…'.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.23: savidhasaneedasamaryaadasaveshasadesheshusaameepye (सविधसनीडसमर्यादसवेशसदेशेषु सामीप्ये) — The first member of a तत्-पुरुष समास preserves its original accent when the second member is 1. सविध 2. सनीड 3. समर्याद 4. सवेश and 5. सदेश in the sense of 'what can be found in the vicinity thereof'.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.24: vispashtaadeenigunavachaneshu (विस्पष्टादीनि गुणवचनेषु) — The words विस्पष्ट etc. preserve their accent when followed by an adjective word in a compound.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.25: shrajyaavamakanpaapavatsubhaavekarmadhaaraye (श्रज्याऽवमकन्पापवत्सु भावे कर्मधारये) — In a कर्मधारय समास the first member consisting of a भाव (verbal noun) preserves its original accent before the adjective forms built from श्र -- प्रशस्यस्य श्रः [[5.3.60]], ज्य -- ज्य च [[5.3.61]], अवम and कन् -- युवाल्पयोः कनन्यतरस्याम् [[5.3.64]], and before a form built from the word पाप।",
    "Sūtra 6.2.26: kumaarashcha (कुमारश्च) — In a कर्मधारय समास the first member consisting of the word कुमार preserves it original accent.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.27: aadihapratyenasi (आदिः प्रत्येनसि) — In a कर्मधारय समास of कुमार followed by प्रत्येनस् the acutely accented (उदात्त) falls on the first syllable of कुमार।",
    "Sūtra 6.2.28: poogeshvanyatarasyaam (पूगेष्वन्यतरस्याम्) — The first syllable of कुमार is optionally acutely accented (उदात्त) when the second member is a word denoting 'the name of a horde'.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.29: igantakaalakapaalabhagaalasharaaveshudvigau (इगन्तकालकपालभगालशरावेषु द्विगौ) — In a द्विगु समास (Numeral Determinative Compound) the first member preserves its original accent before a stem ending in a simple vowel with the exception of अ (इक्) before a word denoting time, as well as before 1. कपाल 2. भगाल and 3. शराव।",
    "Sūtra 6.2.30: bahvanyatarasyaam (बह्वन्यतरस्याम्) — In a द्विगु समास (Numeral Determinative Compound) the word बहु may optionally preserve its accent when followed by an इक्-ending stem or by a time-word or by 1. कपाल 2. भगाल and 3. शराव।",
    "Sūtra 6.2.31: dishtivitastyoshcha (दिष्टिवितस्त्योश्च) — In a द्विगु समास (Numeral Determinative Compound) the first member may optionally preserve its accent when followed by the words दिष्टि and वितस्ति।as its second members.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.32: saptameesiddhashushkapakvabandheshvakaalaat (सप्तमी सिद्धशुष्कपक्वबन्धेष्वकालात्) — When a word ending in the Locative -7th case does not denote time preserves its original accent when followed by 1. सिद्ध 2. शुष्क 3. पक्व and 4. बन्ध in a compound.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.33: paripratyupaapaavarjyamaanaahoraatraavayaveshu (परिप्रत्युपापा वर्ज्यमानाहोरात्रावयवेषु) — The particles 1. परि 2. प्रति 3. उप and 4. अप preserve their accent before that word which specifies an exclusion or a portion of day and night (in an अव्ययीभाव समास also).",
    "Sūtra 6.2.34: raajanyabahuvachanadvamdvendhakavrushnishu (राजन्यबहुवचनद्वन्द्वेऽन्धकवृष्णिषु) — The first member of a द्वन्द समास formed of names denoting the क्षत्रिय (warrior) clans in the plural number retains its original accent when the warrior belongs to the clan of अन्धक or वृष्णि।",
    "Sūtra 6.2.35: samkhyaa (संख्या) — The numeral word standing as the first member of a द्वन्द समास , preserves its accent.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.36: aachaaryopasarjanashchaantevaasee (आचार्योपसर्जनश्चान्तेवासी) — When words denoting scholars are named after their teachers and are compounded into a द्वन्द समास the first member retains its accent.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.37: kaartakaujapaadayashcha (कार्तकौजपादयश्च) — Also in the द्वन्द समास-s कार्तकौजप etc. the first members retain their accent.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.38: mahaanvreehyaparaahnagrushteeshvaasajaabaalabhaarabhaaratahailihilarauravapravruddheshu (महान् व्रीह्यपराह्णगृष्टीष्वासजाबालभारभारतहैलिहिलरौरवप्रवृद्धेषु) — The word महत् (महा) retains its accent before the following - 1. व्रीहि 2. अपराह्ण 3. गृष्टि 4. इष्वास 5. जाबाल 6. भार 7. भारत 8. हैलिहिल 9. रौरव and 10. प्रवृद्धे।",
    "Sūtra 6.2.39: kshullakashchavaishvadeve (क्षुल्लकश्च वैश्वदेवे) — The words महत् and क्षुल्लक retain their accent before the word वैश्वदेव।",
    "Sūtra 6.2.40: ushtrahasaadivaamyoh (उष्ट्रः सादिवाम्योः) — The word उष्ट्र retains its accent before सादि and वामि।",
    "Sūtra 6.2.41: gauhasaadasaadisaarathishu (गौः सादसादिसारथिषु) — The word गो retains its accent before 1. साद 2. सादि and 3. सारथि।",
    "Sūtra 6.2.42: kurugaarhapatariktagurvasootajaratyashleeladrudharoopaapaarevadavaataitilakadroohapanyakambalodaaseebhaaraanaamcha (कुरुगार्हपतरिक्तगुर्वसूतजरत्यश्लीलदृढरूपापारेवडवातैतिलकद्रूःपण्यकम्बलो दासीभाराणां च) — The first member retains its accent in the following - 1. कुरु-गार्हपत 2. रिक्त-गुरु 3. असूत-जरती 4. अश्लील-दृढ-रूपा 5. पारे-वडवा 6. तैतिल-कद्रूः 7. पण्य-कम्बलः and 8. दासीभार etc.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.43: chaturtheetadarthe (चतुर्थी तदर्थे) — A word in the Dative -4th Case as the first member retains its accent when the second member expresses that which is suited to become the former.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.44: arthe (अर्थे) — Before the word अर्थ the first member in the Dative -4th Case retains its accent.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.45: ktecha (क्ते च) — The first member in the Dative -4th Case retains its accent before a Past Participle in क्त।",
    "Sūtra 6.2.46: karmadhaarayenishthaa (कर्मधारयेऽनिष्ठा) — Before the Past Participle in क्त the first member when it itself is not a Past Participle, retains its original accent in a कर्मधारय समास ।",
    "Sūtra 6.2.47: aheenedviteeyaa (अहीने द्वितीया) — Before the Past Participle in क्त , a word ending in the Accusative -2nd case retains its accent when it does not mean a separation.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.48: truteeyaakarmani (तृतीया कर्मणि) — A word ending in the Instrumental -3rd case retains its accent before the Past Participle in क्त when it has a Passive meaning.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.49: gatiranantarah (गतिरनन्तरः) — A word called गति -- गतिश्च [[1.4.60]], when standing immediately before a Participle in क्त having a Passive significance, retains its accent.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.50: taadauchanitikrutyatau (तादौ च निति कृत्यतौ) — An immediately preceding गति -- गतिश्च [[1.4.60]], retains its original accent before (a word formed by) a कृत्-affix beginning with त् which as an indicatory न् but before तु।",
    "Sūtra 6.2.51: tavaichaantashchayugapat (तवै चान्तश्च युगपत्) — An immediately preceding गति -- गतिश्च [[1.4.60]], retains its original accent before an Infinitive in तवै -- कृत्यार्थे तवैकेन्केन्यत्वनः [[3.4.14]], but whereby simultaneously the final has the acute as well.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.52: anigantonychatauvapratyaye (अनिगन्तोऽञ्चतौ वप्रत्यये) — An immediately preceding गति -- गतिश्च [[1.4.60]], not ending in इ or उ retains its accent before an affix having a व् follows.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.53: nyadheecha (न्यधी च) — The गति-s नि and अधि however retain their original accent before अञ्च् when the affix व् follows.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.54: eeshadanyatarasyaam (ईषदन्यतरस्याम्) — The word ईषत् when the first member of a compound may optionally preserve its original accent.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.55: hiranyaparimaanamdhane (हिरण्यपरिमाणं धने) — The first member denoting the quantity of gold retains optionally its original accent before the word धन।",
    "Sūtra 6.2.56: prathamochiropasampattau (प्रथमोऽचिरोपसम्पत्तौ) — The word प्रथम when first in a compound optionally retains its original accent when meaning 'a novice'.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.57: katarakatamaukarmadhaaraye (कतरकतमौ कर्मधारये) — The words कतर and कतम when as first member of a compound optionally retain their original accent in a कर्मधारय समास।",
    "Sūtra 6.2.58: aaryobraahmanakumaarayoh (आर्यो ब्राह्मणकुमारयोः) — The word आर्य optionally retains its original accent in a कर्मधारय समास before the words ब्राह्मण and कुमार।",
    "Sūtra 6.2.59: raajaacha (राजा च) — The word राजन् optionally retains its original accent in a कर्मधारय समास before the words ब्राह्मण and कुमार।",
    "Sūtra 6.2.60: shashtheepratyenasi (षष्ठी प्रत्येनसि) — The word राजन् ending in Genitive 6th-Case optionally retains its original accent before the word प्रत्येनस्।",
    "Sūtra 6.2.61: ktenityaarthe (क्ते नित्यार्थे) — A word having the sense of 'always' optionally retains its original accent before a Past Participle in क्त ।",
    "Sūtra 6.2.62: graamahashilpini (ग्रामः शिल्पिनि) — The word ग्राम when first member of a compound optionally retains its original accent before a word denoting 'a professional man or artisan'.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.63: raajaachaprashamsaayaam (राजा च प्रशंसायाम्) — The word राजन् optionally retains its original accent after a profession-denoting noun when praise is expressed.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.64: aadirudaattah (आदिरुदात्तः) — In the following up to -- न भूताधिकसंजीवमद्राश्मकज्जलम् [[6.2.91]], inclusive, the phrase 'the first syllable in -(the word standing in the Nominative 1st-Case) has the acute accent (उदात्त)' is always to be supplied.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.65: saptameehaarinaudharmyeharane (सप्तमीहारिणौ धर्म्येऽहरणे) — If the first member of a compound is in the Locative -7th case or denoting the name of the Receiver of Tax, has acutely accented (उदात्त) first syllable, when the second member is a word denoting 'what is lawful', but not when it is हरण।",
    "Sūtra 6.2.66: yuktecha (युक्ते च) — The first member of a compound has acute on the first syllable when the second member denotes that by whom the things denoted by the first are regulated or kept in order.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.67: vibhaashaadhyakshe (विभाषाऽध्यक्षे) — The acute accent (उदात्त) on the first syllable is optional when the word अध्यक्ष follows.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.68: paapamchashilpini (पापं च शिल्पिनि) — The word पाप is optionally acutely accented (उदात्त) on the first syllable when followed by a word denoting a professional man.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.69: gotraantevaasimaanavabraahmaneshukshepe (गोत्रान्तेवासिमाणवब्राह्मणेषु क्षेपे) — The first syllable of the first member of a compound is acutely accented (उदात्त) before a गोत्र (Patronymic) name or a Scholar-name and also before माणव and ब्राह्मण when a reproach is meant.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.70: anggaanimaireye (अङ्गानि मैरेये) — The first syllable of the word preceding मैरेय gets the acute accent (उदात्त) when it denotes the ingredient of the same.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.71: bhaktaakhyaastadartheshu (भक्ताख्यास्तदर्थेषु) — A word denoting food gets the acute accent (उदात्त) on the first syllable when before a word which denotes a repository suited to contain that.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.72: gobidaalasimhasaindhaveshoopamaane (गोबिडालसिंहसैन्धवेषूपमाने) — A word denoting the object of comparison gets the acute accent (उदात्त) on the first syllable when standing before गो , बिडाल , सिंह and सैन्धव।",
    "Sūtra 6.2.73: akejeevikaarthe (अके जीविकाऽर्थे) — A word denoting the object of comparison gets the acute accent (उदात्त) on the first syllable when the second member is a word ending in the affix अक and the compound expresses a calling by which one gets his living.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.74: praachaamkreedaayaam (प्राचां क्रीडायाम्) — A compound, the second member of which is a word ending in affix अक and which denotes the sport of the Eastern people, gets the acute accent (उदात्त) on the first syllable.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.75: aniniyukte (अणि नियुक्ते) — A compound, the second member of which is a word ending in the कृत् -affix अण् and which denotes a functionary, gets the acute accent (उदात्त) on the first syllable.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.76: shilpinichaakrunyah (शिल्पिनि चाकृञः) — And when such a compound ending in अण् -affix denotes the name of a professional man, but not when the second term कार(derived from कृञ्), the acute accent (उदात्त) is on the first syllable of the first word.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.77: samjnyaayaamcha (संज्ञायां च) — Also when such an उपपद compound ending in अण् -affix denotes a Name, the acute accent (उदात्त) falls on the first syllable but not when the second term is कार।",
    "Sūtra 6.2.78: gotantiyavampaale (गोतन्तियवं पाले) — The words 1. गो 2. तन्ति and 3. यव get the acute accent (उदात्त) on the first syllable when followed by पाल।",
    "Sūtra 6.2.79: nini (णिनि) — A compound ending in कृत् -affix णिनि (इन्) has the acute accent (उदात्त) on the first syllable of the first member.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.80: upamaanamshabdaarthaprakrutaaveva (उपमानं शब्दार्थप्रकृतावेव) — When the first member of a compound expresses that with which resemblance is denoted then it has acute accent (उदात्त) on the first syllable before a word formed by णिनि (इन्) affix, only then, when such latter word is radical without any preposition and means 'giving out a definite sound like so and so'.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.81: yuktaarohyaadayashcha (युक्तारोह्यादयश्च) — The compounds युक्तारोहिन् etc. have acute accent (उदात्त) on the first syllable.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.82: deerghakaashatushabhraashtravatamje (दीर्घकाशतुषभ्राष्ट्रवटं जे) — When the first member is a word ending in a long vowel or is 1. काश 2. तुष 3. भ्राष्ट्र 4. वट and is followed by ज , the acutely accented (उदात्त) falls on the first syllable.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.83: antyaatpoorvambahvachah (अन्त्यात् पूर्वं बह्वचः) — In a word consisting of more than two syllables followed by ज , the acute accent (उदात्त) falls on the syllable before the last.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.84: graamenivasantah (ग्रामेऽनिवसन्तः) — Before ग्राम the first syllable of the first member as acute accent (उदात्त) when thereby inhabitants are not meant.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.85: ghoshaadishu (घोषादिषु च) — The first member has acute accent (उदात्त) on the first syllable when followed by घोषा etc.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.86: chhaatryaadayahashaalaayaam (छात्र्यादयः शालायाम्) — The words छात्रि etc. get acute accent (उदात्त) on the first syllable when followed by the word शाला।",
    "Sūtra 6.2.87: prasthevruddhamakarkyaadeenaam (प्रस्थेऽवृद्धमकर्क्यादीनाम्) — The first member which has not a वृद्धि in the first syllable or which is not कर्की etc. gets the acute accent (उदात्त) on the first syllable before प्रस्थ।",
    "Sūtra 6.2.88: maalaadeenaamcha (मालादीनां च) — The first syllable of माला etc. gets the acute accent (उदात्त) when प्रस्थ follows.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.89: amahannavamnagarenudeechaam (अमहन्नवं नगरेऽनुदीचाम्) — The first member has an acute accent (उदात्त) on the first syllable before the word नगर but not when it is the word महत् or नव , nor when it refers to a city in the lands of the Northern People.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.90: armechaavarnamdvyachtryach (अर्मे चावर्णं द्व्यच्त्र्यच्) — A word of two or three syllables ending in a अ or आ (with the exception of महा and नव) standing before the word अर्म has acute accent (उदात्त) on the first syllable.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.91: nabhootaadhikasamjeevamadraashmakajjalam (न भूताधिकसंजीवमद्राश्मकज्जलम्) — The following words do not get acute accent (उदात्त) on the first syllable when standing before अर्म etc. - 1. भूत 2. अधिक 3. संजीव 4. मद्र 5. अश्मन् and 6. कञ्जल।",
    "Sūtra 6.2.92: antah (अन्तः) — In the following sūtras up to निष्ठोपसर्गपूर्वमन्यतरस्याम् [[6.2.110]], inclusive, is to be supplied the phrase 'the last syllable in a word standing in the Nominative 1st-Case has the acute accent (उदात्त)'.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.93: sarvamgunakaartsnye (सर्वं गुणकार्त्स्न्ये) — The acute accent (उदात्त) is on the final of the word सर्व standing as the first member before an attributive word in the sense 'whole, through and through'.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.94: samjnyaayaamgirinikaayayoh (संज्ञायां गिरिनिकाययोः) — The last syllable of the first member before गिरि and निकाय has the acute accent (उदात्त) when the compound is a Name.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.95: kumaaryaamvayasi (कुमार्यां वयसि) — The last syllable of the first member get the acute accent (उदात्त) when the word कुमारी follows, the compound denoting age.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.96: udakekevale (उदकेऽकेवले) — Before the word उदक when the compound denotes a mixture, the last syllable of the first member has the acute accent (उदात्त).",
    "Sūtra 6.2.97: dvigaukratau (द्विगौ क्रतौ) — Before a द्विगु समास (Numeral Determinative Compound), when the compound denotes a sacrifice, the last syllable of the first member has the acute accent (उदात्त).",
    "Sūtra 6.2.98: sabhaayaamnapumsake (सभायां नपुंसके) — Before the word सभा when it is exhibited as Neuter, the first member of the compound gets the acute accent (उदात्त) on the last syllable.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.99: purepraachaam (पुरे प्राचाम्) — Before the word पुर , when the compound denotes a city of the Eastern People, the final of the final of the first member as the acute accent (उदात्त).",
    "Sūtra 6.2.100: arishtagaudapoorvecha (अरिष्टगौडपूर्वे च) — When the words अरिष्ट and गौड stand first, the first member has the acute accent (उदात्त) on the final before the word पुर।",
    "Sūtra 6.2.101: nahaastinaphalakamaardeyaah (न हास्तिनफलकमार्देयाः) — But when the words 1. हास्तिन 2. फलक and 3. मार्देय precede पुर , the acute accent (उदात्त) does not fall on their final.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.102: kusoolakoopakumbhashaalambile (कुसूलकूपकुम्भशालं बिले) — The words 1. कुसूल 2. कूप 3. कुम्भ and 4. शाला have the acute accent (उदात्त) on the last syllable before the word बिल।",
    "Sūtra 6.2.103: dikshabdaagraamajanapadaakhyaanachaanaraateshu (दिक्शब्दा ग्रामजनपदाख्यानचानराटेषु) — Words expressing (in space of time) have acute accent (उदात्त) on the last syllable when followed by a word denoting a village or a country or a narrative before the word चानराट।",
    "Sūtra 6.2.104: aachaaryopasarjanashchaantevaasini (आचार्योपसर्जनश्चान्तेवासिनि) — The direction denoting words have acute accent (उदात्त) on the final, before the names of scholars when such names derived from those of their teachers.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.105: uttarapadavruddhausarvamcha (उत्तरपदवृद्धौ सर्वं च) — Words denoting direction and the word सर्व have acute accent (उदात्त) on the final before a word which takes वृद्धि in the first syllable of the second term by सुसर्वार्धाज्जनपदस्य [[7.3.12]].",
    "Sūtra 6.2.106: bahuvreehauvishvamsamjnyayaam (बहुव्रीहौ विश्वं संज्ञायाम्) — The word विश्व has acute accent (उदात्त) on the final, being first member in a बहुव्रीहि समास , when it is a Name.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.107: udaraashveshushu (उदराश्वेषुषु) — The first member in a बहुव्रीहि समास , before the words 1. उदर 2. अश्व and 3. इषु , gets acute accent (उदात्त) on the final syllable when the compound denotes a Name.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.108: kshepe (क्षेपे) — A word before 1. उदर 2. अश्व and 3. इषु in a बहुव्रीहि समास gets the acute accent (उदात्त) on the final, when reproach is meant.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.109: nadeebandhuni (नदी बन्धुनि) — In a बहुव्रीहि समास having the word बन्धु as its second member, the first member ending in the feminine affix ई (नदी word) has the ac on its final syllable.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.110: nishthopasargapoorvamanyatarasyaam (निष्ठोपसर्गपूर्वमन्यतरस्याम्) — In a बहुव्रीहि समास a Participle in a क्त preceded by a preposition, standing as the first member of the compound has optionally acute accent (उदात्त) on the last syllable.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.111: uttarapadaadih (उत्तरपदादिः) — In the following sūtras up to कुण्डं वनम् [[6.2.136]], inclusive, should always be supplied the phrase 'the first syllable of the second member has the acute accent (उदात्त)'.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.112: karnovarnalakshanaat (कर्णो वर्णलक्षणात्) — In a बहुव्रीहि समास the word कर्ण standing as second member has acute accent (उदात्त) on the first syllable when it is preceded by a word denoting colour or mark.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.113: samjnyaupamyayoshcha (संज्ञौपम्ययोश्च) — In a बहुव्रीहि समास the second member कर्ण has acute accent (उदात्त) on the first syllable when the compound denotes a Name or Resemblance.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.114: kanthaprushthagreevaajamghamcha (कण्ठपृष्ठग्रीवाजंघं च) — In a बहुव्रीहि समास expressing a Name or comparison the second members 1. कण्ठ 2. पृष्ठ 3. ग्रीवा and 4. जङ्घा have acute accent (उदात्त) on the first syllable.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.115: shrunggamavasthaayaamcha (शृङ्गमवस्थायां च) — In a बहुव्रीहि समास denoting age (as well as a Name or a Resemblance), the second member शृङ्ग gets acute accent (उदात्त) on the first syllable.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.116: nanyojaramaramitramrutaah (नञो जरमरमित्रमृताः) — After a Negative Particle, in a बहुव्रीहि समास the acute accent (उदात्त) falls on the first syllable of 1. जर 2. मर 3. मित्र and 4. मृत।",
    "Sūtra 6.2.117: sormanaseealomoshasee (सोर्मनसी अलोमोषसी) — After the adjective सु in a बहुव्रीहि समास a stem ending in मन् and अस् with the exception of लोमन् and उषस् has acute accent (उदात्त) on the first syllable.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.118: kratvaadayashcha (क्रत्वादयश्च) — After the adjective सु in a बहुव्रीहि समास the acute accent (उदात्त) falls on the first syllable of क्रतु etc.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.119: aadyudaattamdvyachchhandasi (आद्युदात्तं द्व्यच् छन्दसि) — In a बहुव्रीहि समास in the छन्दस् (Vedas) a word of two syllables with acute accent (उदात्त) on the first syllable when preceded by सु gets acute accent (उदात्त) on the first syllable.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.120: veeraveeryaucha (वीरवीर्यौ च) — In a बहुव्रीहि समास in the छन्दस् (Vedas) after सु the words वीर and वीर्य have acute accent (उदात्त) on the first syllable.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.121: koolateeratoolamoolashaalaakshasamamavyayeebhaave (कूलतीरतूलमूलशालाऽक्षसममव्ययीभावे) — In an अव्ययीभाव समास the following second terms have acute accent (उदात्त) on their first syllable - 1. कूल 2. तीर 3. तूल 4. मूल 5. शाला 6. अक्ष and 7. सम।",
    "Sūtra 6.2.122: kamsamanthashoorpapaayyakaandamdvigau (कंसमन्थशूर्पपाय्यकाण्डं द्विगौ) — In a द्विगु समास (Numeral Determinative Compound) the following second members get acute accent (उदात्त) on their first syllable - 1. कंस 2. मन्थ 3. शूर्प 3. पाय्य and 4. काण्ड।",
    "Sūtra 6.2.123: tatpurusheshaalaayaamnapumsake (तत्पुरुषे शालायां नपुंसके) — The word शाला at the end of a तत्-पुरुष समास when exhibited in the Neuter has acute on the first syllable.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.124: kanthaacha (कन्था च) — In a Neuter तत्-पुरुष समास ending in कन्था the acute accent (उदात्त) falls on the first syllable of the second member.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.125: aadishchihanaadeenaam (आदिश्चिहणादीनाम्) — In a Neuter तत्-पुरुष समास ending in कन्था the first syllable of चिहण etc. have the acute accent (उदात्त).",
    "Sūtra 6.2.126: chelakhetakatukakaandamgarhaayaam (चेलखेटकटुककाण्डं गर्हायाम्) — The words 1. चेल 2. खेट 3. कटुक and 4. काण्ड at the end of a तत्-पुरुष समास have acute accent (उदात्त) on the first syllable when a reproach is meant.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.127: cheeramupamaanam (चीरमुपमानम्) — The word चीर at the end of a तत्-पुरुष समास has acute accent (उदात्त) on the first syllable when something is compared with it.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.128: palalasoopashaakammishre (पललसूपशाकं मिश्रे) — In a तत्-पुरुष समास ending in 1. पलल 2. सूप and 3. शाक the acute accent (उदात्त) falls on the first syllable of these when the compound denotes a food mixed or seasoned with something.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.129: koolasoodasthalakarshaahasamjnyaayaam (कूलसूदस्थलकर्षाः संज्ञायाम्) — The words 1. कूल 2. सूद 3. स्थल and 4. कर्ष have acute accent (उदात्त) on their first syllable when at the end of a तत्-पुरुष समास denoting a Name.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.130: akarmadhaarayeraajyam (अकर्मधारये राज्यम्) — The word राज्यम् has acute accent (उदात्त) on the first syllable when at the end of a तत्-पुरुष समास which is not a कर्मधारय समास ।",
    "Sūtra 6.2.131: vargyaadayashcha (वर्ग्यादयश्च) — At the end of a non-कर्मधारय तत्-पुरुष समास the words वर्ग्य etc. have acute accent (उदात्त) on the first syllable.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.132: putrahapumbhyah (पुत्रः पुंभ्यः) — The word पुत्र coming after a Masculine noun in a तत्-पुरुष समास has a acute accent (उदात्त) on the first syllable.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.133: naachaaryaraajartviksamyuktajnyaatyaakhyebhyah (नाचार्यराजर्त्विक्संयुक्तज्ञात्याख्येभ्यः) — The word पुत्र does not have an acute accent (उदात्त) on the first syllable when preceded by a word which falls under the category of teachers, kings, priests, wife's relations and agnates and cognates.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.134: choornaadeenyapraanishashthyaah (चूर्णादीन्यप्राणिषष्ठ्याः) — The words चूर्ण etc. in a तत्-पुरुष समास have acute accent (उदात्त) on the first syllable when preceding word ends in a Genitive 6th-Case and does not denote a living being.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.135: shatchakaandaadeeni (षट् च काण्डादीनि) — The six words - 1. काण्ड 2. चीर 3. पलल 4. सूप 5. शाक and 6. कूल of sūtras [[6.2.126]]-129 preceded by a non-living Genitive 6th-Case word have acute accent (उदात्त) on the first syllable.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.136: kundamvanam (कुण्डं वनम्) — The word कुण्ड at the end of a तत्-पुरुष समास denoting 'a wood or forest' has acute accent (उदात्त) on the first syllable.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.137: prakrutyaabhagaalam (प्रकृत्या भगालम्) — The word भगाल at the end of a तत्-पुरुष समास preserves its original accent.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.138: shiternityaabahvajbahuvreehaavabhasat (शितेर्नित्याबह्वज्बहुव्रीहावभसत्) — After शिति , a word retains in a बहुव्रीहि समास its original accent when it is always of not more than two syllables with the exception of भसद्.।",
    "Sūtra 6.2.139: gatikaarakopapadaatkrut (गतिकारकोपपदात् कृत्) — In a तत्-पुरुष समास a word ending in a कृत् affix preserves its original accent when preceded by an indeclinable called गति -- गतिश्च [[1.4.60]], or a noun standing in intimate relation to a verb (कारक) or any word which gives occasion for compounding (उपपद -- तत्रोपपदं सप्तमीस्थम् [[3.1.92]])",
    "Sūtra 6.2.140: ubhevanaspatyaadishuyugapat (उभे वनस्पत्यादिषु युगपत्) — In वनस्पति etc. both members of the compound preserve their original accent simultaneously.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.141: devataadvamdvecha (देवताद्वन्द्वे च) — In a द्वन्द compound of the Names of Divinities, both the members retain their original accent.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.142: nottarapadenudaattaadaavapruthiveerudrapooshamanthishu (नोत्तरपदेऽनुदात्तादावपृथिवीरुद्रपूषमन्थिषु) — In a द्वन्द compound of the Names of Divinities, both members of the compound simultaneously do not retain their accent when the first syllable of the second word is अनुदात्त with the exception of 1.पृथिवी 2. रुद्र 3. पूष and 4. मन्थिन्।",
    "Sūtra 6.2.143: antah (अन्तः) — In the following sūtras up to the end of this chapter should always be supplied the phrase 'the last syllable of the second member has the acute accent (उदात्त)'.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.144: thaathaghanyktaajabitrakaanaam (थाथघञ्क्ताजबित्रकाणाम्) — The last syllable of the second member has the acute accent (उदात्त) in the verbal nouns ending in 1. थ 2. अथ 3. घञ् 4. क्त 5. अच् 6. अप् 7. इत्र and 8. क when preceded by a गति , a कारक or an उपपद -- गतिकारकोपपदात् कृत् [[6.2.139]]",
    "Sūtra 6.2.145: soopamaanaatktah (सूपमानात् क्तः) — The Participle in क्त has acute accent (उदात्त) on the final when it is preceded by सु or by a word with which the second member is compared.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.146: samjnyaayaamanaachitaadeenaam (संज्ञायामनाचितादीनाम्) — The Participle in क्त has acute accent (उदात्त) on the last syllable when preceded by a गति or a कारक or an उपपद if the compound denotes a Name, but not in आचित etc.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.147: pravruddhaadeenaamcha (प्रवृद्धादीनां च) — The word प्रवृद्ध etc. ending in क्त have acute accent (उदात्त) on the final.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.148: kaarakaaddattashrutayorevaashishi (कारकाद्दत्तश्रुतयोरेवाशिषि) — The final of Part Participles दत्त and श्रुत alone have the acute accent (उदात्त) in a compound denoting a Name and a Benediction, the preceding word being a word standing in close relation to an action (कारक)।",
    "Sūtra 6.2.149: itthambhootenakrutamiticha (इत्थम्भूतेन कृतमिति च) — The Participle in क्त has acute accent (उदात्त) on the final when the compound denotes 'done by one in such a condition'.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.150: anobhaavakarmavachanah (अनो भावकर्मवचनः) — After a कारक as mentioned in कारकाद्दत्तश्रुतयोरेवाशिषि [[6.2.148]], the second member ending in the affix अन and denoting an action in the Abstract or the object (i.e. having the senses of Passive Adjective), has the acute accent (उदात्त) on the final.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.151: manktinvyaakhyaanashayanaasanasthaanayaajakaadikreetaah (मन्क्तिन्व्याख्यानशयनासनस्थानयाजकादिक्रीताः) — The words ending in मन् or क्तिन् affixes and the words 1. व्याख्यान 2. शयन 3. आसन 4. स्थान and 5. क्रीत as well as याजक etc. have acute accent (उदात्त) on the final when at the end of a compound preceded by कारक word.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.152: saptamyaahapunyam (सप्तम्याः पुण्यम्) — The word पुण्य has acute accent (उदात्त) on the final when preceded by a Noun in the Locative -7th case.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.153: oonaarthakalahamtruteeyaayaah (ऊनार्थकलहं तृतीयायाः) — The acute accent (उदात्त) falls on the final of words having the sense of ऊन and of कलह when they are second members in a compound, preceded by a term in the Instrumental -3rd case.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.154: mishramchaanupasargamasamdhau (मिश्रं चानुपसर्गमसंधौ) — The word मिश्र has acute accent (उदात्त) on the final after an Instrumental -3rd case when it is not joined with any Preposition and does not mean a 'compact or alliance'.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.155: nanyogunapratishedhesampaadyarhahitaalamarthaastaddhitaah (नञो गुणप्रतिषेधे सम्पाद्यर्हहितालमर्थास्तद्धिताः) — The words formed with the तद्धित affixes denoting 'fitted for that' -- सम्पादिनि [[5.1.99]], 'deserving that' -- तद् अर्हति [[5.1.63]], 'good for that' -- तस्मै हितम् [[5.1.5]], 'capable to effect that' -- तस्मै प्रभवति संतापादिभ्यः [[5.1.101]], have acute accent (उदात्त) on the final when preceded by the Negative Particle नञ् , when it makes a negation with regard to the above mentioned attributes.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.156: yayatoshchaatadarthe (ययतोश्चातदर्थे) — The words formed with the तद्धित affixes य and यत् when not denoting 'useful for that' have acute accent (उदात्त) on the last syllable after the particle नञ् negating the attribute.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.157: achkaavashaktau (अच्कावशक्तौ) — A word formed with the कृत् affixes अच् and क preceded by the particle नञ् has the acute accent (उदात्त) on the final when the meaning is 'not capable'.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.158: aakroshecha (आक्रोशे च) — A word formed by the कृत् affixes अच् and क preceded by a Negative Particle have an acute accent (उदात्त) on the final when one abuses somebody by that word.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.159: samjnyaayaam (संज्ञायाम्) — When abuse is meant, a word preceded by नञ् has acute accent (उदात्त) on the final in denoting a Name.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.160: krutyokeshnuchchaarvaadayashcha (कृत्योकेष्णुच्चार्वादयश्च) — After the Negative Particle, the words formed by the कृत्य affixes -- कृत्याः प्राङ् ण्वुलः [[3.1.95]], by उक and इष्णुच् and the words चारु etc. have acute accent (उदात्त) on the final.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.161: vibhaashaatrunnannateekshnashuchishu (विभाषा तृन्नन्नतीक्ष्णशुचिषु) — After the negative particle, the final of the following is optionally acute accent (उदात्त) - a word formed with the affix तृन् and the words 1. अन्न 2. तीक्ष्ण and 3. शुचि।",
    "Sūtra 6.2.162: bahuvreehaavidametattadbhyahaprathamapooranayohakriyaaganane (बहुव्रीहाविदमेतत्तद्भ्यः प्रथमपूरणयोः क्रियागणने) — In a बहुव्रीहि समास , after the words इदम् , एतद् and तद् the last syllable of प्रथम and of a proper ordinal numeral as the acute accent (उदात्त) when the number of times of an action is meant.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.163: samkhyaayaahastanah (संख्यायाः स्तनः) — In a बहुव्रीहि समास , after a numeral the word स्तन has acute accent (उदात्त) on the final.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.164: vibhaashaachhandasi (विभाषा छन्दसि) — Optionally so, in the छन्दस् (Vedas), the स्तन after a numeral has acute accent (उदात्त) on the final.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.165: samjnyaayaammitraajinayoh (संज्ञायां मित्राजिनयोः) — In a बहुव्रीहि समास ending in मित्र and अजिन the acute accent (उदात्त) falls on the last syllable when the compound denotes a Name.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.166: vyavaayinontaram (व्यवायिनोऽन्तरम्) — In a बहुव्रीहि समास ending in अन्तर the acute accent (उदात्त) is on the final after a word which denotes 'that which lies between'.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.167: mukhamsvaanggam (मुखं स्वाङ्गम्) — In a बहुव्रीहि समास the acute accent (उदात्त) is on the final when the second member is मुख 'mouth' i.e. the actual bodily part of an animal and not used metaphorically.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.168: naavyayadikshabdagomahatsthoolamushtipruthuvatsebhyah (नाव्ययदिक्शब्दगोमहत्स्थूलमुष्टिपृथुवत्सेभ्यः) — In a बहुव्रीहि समास the acute accent (उदात्त) does not fall on such मुख 'mouth' denoting a real mouth when it comes after an indeclinable and a name of a direction or after 1. गो 2. महत् 3. स्थूल 4. मुष्टि 5. पृथु and 6. वत्स।",
    "Sūtra 6.2.169: nishthopamaanaadanyatarasyaam (निष्ठोपमानादन्यतरस्याम्) — In a बहुव्रीहि समास the word मुख denoting 'an actual mouth' has optionally the acute accent (उदात्त) on the final when preceded by a participle in त or by that wherewith something is compared.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.170: jaatikaalasukhaadibhyonaachchhaadanaatktokrutamitapratipannaah (जातिकालसुखादिभ्योऽनाच्छादनात् क्तोऽकृतमितप्रतिपन्नाः) — After a word denoting a species (with the exception of a word for 'garment or covering') and after a time-denoting word as well as after सुख etc. the Participle in the क्त has acute accent (उदात्त) on the final in a बहुव्रीहि समास but not so when the participles are 1. कृत 2. मित 3. प्रतिपन्न।",
    "Sūtra 6.2.171: vaajaate (वा जाते) — After a species (with the exception of a word for 'garment or covering') or a time-denoting word or after सुख etc. in a बहुव्रीहि समास the word जात has optionally acute accent (उदात्त) on the final.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.172: nanysubhyaam (नञ्सुभ्याम्) — In a बहुव्रीहि समास formed by the negative particle नञ् or by सु has the acute accent (उदात्त) on the last syllable of the compound.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.173: kapipoorvam (कपि पूर्वम्) — In a बहुव्रीहि समास formed by the negative particle नञ् or by सु and ending in the affix कप् -- नद्यृतश्च [[5.4.153]], has acute accent (उदात्त) on the syllable preceding the affix.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.174: hrasvaantentyaatpoorvam (ह्रस्वान्तेऽन्त्यात् पूर्वम्) — When the compound ends in a light vowel the acute accent (उदात्त) falls on the syllable before such last, in a बहुव्रीहि समास preceded by नञ् and सु to which the affix कप् -- नद्यृतश्च [[5.4.153]], is added.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.175: bahornanyvaduttarapadabhoomni (बहोर्नञ्वदुत्तरपदभूम्नि) — A बहुव्रीहि समास with बहु has the same accent as नञ् when it denotes muchness of the object expressed by the second member.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.176: nagunaadayovayavaah (न गुणादयोऽवयवाः) — In a बहुव्रीहि समास , after बहु the acute accent (उदात्त) does not fall on the final of गुण etc. when they appear in the compound as ingredient of something else.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.177: upasargaatsvaanggamdhruvamaparshu (उपसर्गात् स्वाङ्गं ध्रुवमपर्शु) — A word denoting a part of the body which is constant (and indispensable) with the exception of पर्शु has after a preposition in a बहुव्रीहि समास the acute accent (उदात्त) on the last syllable.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.178: vanamsamaase (वनं समासे) — After a preposition वन has acute accent (उदात्त) on the final in compounds of every kind.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.179: antah (अन्तः) — After अन्तर् the acute accent (उदात्त) falls on the final of वन।",
    "Sūtra 6.2.180: antashcha (अन्तश्च) — The word अन्तर् has acute accent (उदात्त) on the final when preceded by a preposition.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.181: nanivibhyaam (न निविभ्याम्) — The word अन्तर् does not have acute accent (उदात्त) on the final after the prepositions नि and वि।",
    "Sūtra 6.2.182: parerabhitobhaavimandalam (परेरभितोभाविमण्डलम्) — After परि a word which expresses something which has both this side and that side, as well as the word मण्डल has acute accent (उदात्त) on the final.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.183: praadasvaanggamsamjnyaayaam (प्रादस्वाङ्गं संज्ञायाम्) — After प्र a, a word which does not denote a part of the body has acute accent (उदात्त) on the final when the compound is a name.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.184: nirudakaadeenicha (निरुदकादीनि च) — The words निरुदकetc. Have acute accent (उदात्त) on the final.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.185: abhermukham (अभेर्मुखम्) — The word मुख has acute accent (उदात्त) on the final when preceded by अभि।",
    "Sūtra 6.2.186: apaachcha (अपाच्च) — The word मुख has acute accent (उदात्त) on the final after the preposition अप्।",
    "Sūtra 6.2.187: sphigapootaveenaanyjodhvakukshiseeranaamanaamacha (स्फिगपूतवीणाऽञ्जोऽध्वकुक्षिसीरनामनाम च) — The words 1. स्फिग 2. पूत 3. वीणा 4. अञ्जस् 5. अध्वम् 6. कुक्षि 6. नामन् and a word denoting 'a plough' have acute accent (उदात्त) on the final when preceded by the preposition अप्।",
    "Sūtra 6.2.188: adheruparistham (अधेरुपरिस्थम्) — After अधि that word which denotes that thing which overlaps or stands upon has the acute accent (उदात्त) on the final.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.189: anorapradhaanakaneeyasee (अनोरप्रधानकनीयसी) — After अनु a word which is not the Principal as well as कनीयस् has acute accent (उदात्त) on the final.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.190: purushashchaanvaadishtah (पुरुषश्चान्वादिष्टः) — After अनु the acute accent (उदात्त) falls on the final of पुरुष when it means a man of whom mention was already made.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.191: aterakrutpade (अतेरकृत्पदे) — After अति , a word not formed by a कृत् affix and the word पद have acute accent (उदात्त) on the last syllable.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.192: neranidhaane (नेरनिधाने) — After नि the second member has the acute accent (उदात्त) on the last syllable when the sense is of 'not laying down'.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.193: prateramshvaadayastatpurushe (प्रतेरंश्वादयस्तत्पुरुषे) — In a तत्-पुरुष समास the words अंशु etc. have acute accent (उदात्त) on the final when preceded by प्रति।",
    "Sūtra 6.2.194: upaaddvyajajinamagauraadayah (उपाद् द्व्यजजिनमगौरादयः) — In a तत्-पुरुष समास the words of two syllables and अजिन् have acute accent (उदात्त) on the final when preceded by उप but not when they are गौर etc.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.195: soravakshepane (सोरवक्षेपणे) — After सु the second member has acute accent (उदात्त) on the final in a तत्-पुरुष समास when reproach is meant, in spite of the addition of सु which denotes praise.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.196: vibhaashotpuchchhe (विभाषोत्पुच्छे) — In a तत्-पुरुष समास the word उत्पुच्छ may optionally have acute accent (उदात्त) on the final.",
    "Sūtra 6.2.197: dvitribhyaampaaddanmoordhasubahuvreehau (द्वित्रिभ्यां पाद्दन्मूर्धसु बहुव्रीहौ) — In a बहुव्रीहि समास the words 1. पाद् 2. दत् and 3. मूर्धन् have optionally acute accent (उदात्त) on the final after द्वि and त्रि।",
    "Sūtra 6.2.198: sakthamchaakraantaat (सक्थं चाक्रान्तात्) — The word सक्थ has acute accent (उदात्त) on the final optionally when preceded by any word other than what ends in क्र।",
    "Sūtra 6.2.199: paraadishchhandasibahulam (परादिश्छन्दसि बहुलम्) — The first syllable of the second member is diversely acutely accented (उदात्त) in the छन्दस् (Vedas).",
    "Sūtra 6.3.1: aluguttarapade (अलुगुत्तरपदे) — In the following sūtras up to विभाषा स्वसृपत्योः [[6.3.24]], inclusive, is always to be supplied the phrase 'the elision does not take place before the second member of the compound'.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.2: panychamyaahastokaadibhyah (पञ्चम्याः स्तोकादिभ्यः) — The Ablative -5th case-ending after स्तोक etc. is not elided before the second member of a compound.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.3: ojahasahombhastamasahatruteeyaayaah (ओजःसहोऽम्भस्तमसः तृतीयायाः) — The Instrumental -3rd case endings after 1. ओजस् 2. सहस् 3. अम्भस् and 4. तमस् are not elided before the second member of a compound.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.4: manasahasamjnyaayaam (मनसः संज्ञायाम्) — After मनस् when the compound is a Name, the Instrumental -3rd case endings are not elided before the second member.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.5: aajnyaayinicha (आज्ञायिनि च) — Also before आज्ञायिन् the Instrumental -3rd case endings of मनस् are not elided.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.6: aatmanashchapoorane (आत्मनश्च पूरणे) — The Instrumental -3rd case endings after आत्मान् are not elided when an Ordinal Numeral follows.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.7: vaiyaakaranaakhyaayaamchaturthyaah (वैयाकरणाख्यायां चतुर्थ्याः) — The Dative -4th Case ending is not elided after आत्मान् when the compound is the name of a technical term in grammar.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.8: parasyacha (परस्य च) — The Dative -4th Case endings is not elided after पर when the compound is the name of a technical term in grammar.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.9: haladantaatsaptamyaahasamjnyaayaam (हलदन्तात् सप्तम्याः संज्ञायाम्) — The Locative -7th case ending is not elided after a stem ending in a consonant or a short अ when the compound is a Name.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.10: kaaranaamnichapraachaamhalaadau (कारनाम्नि च प्राचां हलादौ) — The Locative -7th case affix is not elided after a stem ending in a consonant or a short अ in the name of atax of the Eastern People when the second member begins with a consonant.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.11: madhyaadgurau (मध्याद्गुरौ) — The Locative -7th case-affix is not elided after मध्य when गुरु follows.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.12: amoordhamastakaatsvaanggaadakaame (अमूर्धमस्तकात् स्वाङ्गादकामे) — is not elided after a word denoting a part of the body (with the exception of मूर्धन् and मस्तक) before every word other than काम।",
    "Sūtra 6.3.13: bandhechavibhaashaa (बन्धे च विभाषा) — The Locative -7th case-affix is optionally not elided after a word ending in a consonant or अ before बन्ध।",
    "Sūtra 6.3.14: tatpurushekrutibahulam (तत्पुरुषे कृति बहुलम्) — In a तत्-पुरुष समास when the second member is a word formed with a कृत् affix the Locative -7th case ending is optionally preserved.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.15: praavrutsharatkaaladivaamje (प्रावृट्शरत्कालदिवां जे) — The Locative -7th case-affix ending is retained after 1. प्रावट् 2. काल and 3. दिव् when ज follows.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.16: vibhaashaavarshaksharasharavaraat (विभाषा वर्षक्षरशरवरात्) — The Locative -7th case-affix ending is optionally retained after 1. वर्ष 2. क्षर 3. शर and 4. वर when ज follows.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.17: ghakaalataneshukaalanaamnah (घकालतनेषु कालनाम्नः) — The Locative -7th case-affix ending is optionally retained after a word denoting time ending in a consonant or अ when तरप् or तमप् or the word काल or the affix तन follow.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.18: shayavaasavaasishvakaalaat (शयवासवासिष्वकालात्) — The Locative -7th case-affix ending is optionally retained after the words 1. शय 2. वास and 3. वासिन् when the preceding word does not denote time and ends in a consonant or a short अ।",
    "Sūtra 6.3.19: nensiddhabadhnaatishu (नेन्सिद्धबध्नातिषु) — The Locative -7th case ending is not preserved before a stem ending in इन् before he word सिद्ध and before a word derived from बन्ध् ।",
    "Sūtra 6.3.20: sthechabhaashaayaam (स्थे च भाषायाम्) — The Locative -7th case ending is not preserved before स्थ in the spoken language.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.21: shashthyaaaakroshe (षष्ठ्या आक्रोशे) — The Genitive 6th-Case-affix is retained when the compound expresses an 'affront or insult'.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.22: putrenyatarasyaam (पुत्रेऽन्यतरस्याम्) — The Genitive 6th-Case-affix is optionally retained when insult is meant when पुत्र follows.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.23: rutovidyaayonisambandhebhyah (ऋतो विद्यायोनिसम्बन्धेभ्यः) — The Genitive 6th-Case-affix is retained after a word ending in ऋ and expressing a relationship through study or blood.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.24: vibhaashaasvasrupatyoh (विभाषा स्वसृपत्योः) — The Genitive 6th-Case-affix is optionally elided after a stem ending in ऋ when 1. स्वसृ and 2. पितृ follow.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.25: aanangrutodvandve (आनङ् ऋतो द्वन्द्वे) — In a द्वन्द समास of words ending in the short ऋ and expressing relationship through study or blood, the आनङ् is the substitute of ऋ of the first member.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.26: devataadvandvecha (देवताद्वन्द्वे च) — The आनङ् is the substitute for the final of the first member in a द्वन्द समास of the names of the देवता-s.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.27: eedagnehasomavarunayoh (ईदग्नेः सोमवरुणयोः) — For the final of अग्नि is substituted the long ई when 1. सोम or 2. वरुण follow.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.28: idvruddhau (इद्वृद्धौ) — The short इ is the substitute of the final of the अग्नि in such a द्वन्द समास in which both the members take the वृद्धि।",
    "Sūtra 6.3.29: divodyaavaa (दिवो द्यावा) — For दिव् is substituted द्यावा in a द्वन्द समास of names of देवता-s.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.30: divasashchapruthivyaam (दिवसश्च पृथिव्याम्) — For दिव् is also substituted दिवस् (as well as a द्यावा) when पृथिवी follows in a द्वन्द समास of names of देवता-s.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.31: ushaasoshasah (उषासोषसः) — For उषस् is substituted उषासा in a देवता - द्वन्द समास।",
    "Sūtra 6.3.32: maatarapitaraavudeechaam (मातरपितरावुदीचाम्) — According to Northern Grammarians मातरपितरौ is a valid form.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.33: pitaraamaataraachachchhandasi (पितरामातरा च च्छन्दसि) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas) the form पितरामातरा is a valid form.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.34: striyaahapumvadbhaashitapumskaadanoongsamaanaadhikaranestriyaamapooraneepriyaadishu (स्त्रियाः पुंवद्भाषितपुंस्कादनूङ् समानाधिकरणे स्त्रियामपूरणीप्रियाऽऽदिषु) — In the room of a feminine word there is substituted an equivalent and uniform masculine form when it is a word which has an actual corresponding masculine and does not end in the feminine affix ऊङ् and is followed by another feminine word in the relation of apposition with it, but not when such subsequent word is an ordinal numeral, nor प्रिय etc.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.35: tasilaadishvaakrutvasuchah (तसिलादिष्वाकृत्वसुचः) — A feminine word not ending in the affix ऊङ् and having an equivalent and uniform masculine is changed into such masculine form, before the affixes beginning with तसिल् etc. -- पञ्चम्यास्तसिल् [[5.3.7]], and ending with कृत्वसुच् -- संख्यायाः क्रियाऽभ्यावृत्तिगणने कृत्वसुच् [[5.4.17]].",
    "Sūtra 6.3.36: kyangmaaninoshcha (क्यङ्मानिनोश्च) — A feminine word not ending in ऊङ् and having an equivalent and uniform masculine is changed into masculine before the Denominative कयङ् and the affix मानिन्।",
    "Sūtra 6.3.37: nakopadhaayaah (न कोपधायाः) — A feminine word having a penultimate क् does not assume the masculine form.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.38: samjnyaapooranyoshcha (संज्ञापूरण्योश्च) — The feminine is not changed to masculine when it is a Name or an Ordinal Numeral.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.39: vruddhinimittasyachataddhitasyaaraktavikaare (वृद्धिनिमित्तस्य च तद्धितस्यारक्तविकारे) — The feminine is not changed into masculine when it is formed by such a तद्धित affix which causes the वृद्धि of the first syllable with exception however of तद्धित-substitute meaning 'coloured therewith' and 'made thereof'.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.40: svaanggaachchetomaanini (स्वाङ्गाच्चेतोऽमानिनि) — A feminine in ई ending in the name of a part of body does not become masculine except the word मानिन् follows.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.41: jaateshcha (जातेश्च) — A feminine noun expressing a class of kind does not become masculine.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.42: pumvatkarmadhaarayajaateeyadesheeyeshu (पुंवत् कर्मधारयजातीयदेशीयेषु) — The feminine (unless it ends in ऊ) having an equivalent and uniform masculine becomes masculine in a कर्मधारय समास and before 1. जातीय and 2. देशीय।",
    "Sūtra 6.3.43: gharoopakalpacheladbruvagotramatahateshungyonekaachohrasvah (घरूपकल्पचेलड्ब्रुवगोत्रमतहतेषु ङ्योऽनेकाचो ह्रस्वः) — Before the affixes 1. तर 2. तम 3. रूप 4. कल्प 5. चेल (with the feminine affix ई) 6. ब्रुव 7. गोत्र 8 मत and 9. हत a word ending in the feminine affix ङी becomes short when the feminine consists of two or more syllables and has an equivalent and uniform masculine.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.44: nadyaahasheshasyaanyatarasyaam (नद्याः शेषस्यान्यतरस्याम्) — In all the remaining feminine words called नदी -- यू स्त्र्याख्यौ नदी [[1.4.3]] and नेयङुवङ्स्थानावस्त्री [[1.4.4]], the substitution of short vowel under the preceding circumstances is optional.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.45: ugitashcha (उगितश्च) — The feminine ङी (ई) added to a word formed by a तद्धित affix having an indicatory उ or ऋ is optionally shortened before the घ etc. -- घरूपकल्पचेलड्ब्रुवगोत्रमतहतेषु ङ्योऽनेकाचो ह्रस्वः [[6.3.43]].",
    "Sūtra 6.3.46: aanmahatahasamaanaadhikaranajaateeyayoh (आन्महतः समानाधिकरणजातीययोः) — For the final महत् of is substituted आत् (आ) before a word which is in apposition with it and before जातीय।",
    "Sūtra 6.3.47: dvyashtanahasamkhyaayaamabahuvreehyasheetyoh (द्व्यष्टनः संख्यायामबहुव्रीह्यशीत्योः) — आत् (आ) is substituted for the final of द्वि and अष्टन् when another numeral follows but not in a बहुव्रीहि समास or before आशीतिः।",
    "Sūtra 6.3.48: trestrayah (त्रेस्त्रयः) — For त्रि is substituted त्रयस् when another numeral follows but not in a बहुव्रीहि समास or before आशीतिः।",
    "Sūtra 6.3.49: vibhaashaachatvaarimshatprabhrutausarveshaam (विभाषा चत्वारिंशत्प्रभृतौ सर्वेषाम्) — The above substitution is the case of all (द्वि , त्रि and अष्टन्) is optional when the word चत्वारिंशत् and the numerals which follow it are the second member.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.50: hrudayasyahrullekhayadanlaaseshu (हृदयस्य हृल्लेखयदण्लासेषु) — हृद् is substituted for हृदय before लेख and the affixes यत् and अण् and before लास।",
    "Sūtra 6.3.51: vaashokashyanyrogeshu (वा शोकष्यञ्रोगेषु) — हृद् is optionally substituted for हृदय before the words शोक and रोग or the affix ष्यङ् follow.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.52: paadasyapadaajyaatigopahateshu (पादस्य पदाज्यातिगोपहतेषु) — पद् is substituted for पाद before 1. आजि 2. आति 3. ग and 4. उपहत।",
    "Sūtra 6.3.53: padyatyatadarthe (पद् यत्यतदर्थे) — पद् is substituted for पाद before the affix यत् used in any sense other than that of 'suited there to'.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.54: himakaashihatishucha (हिमकाषिहतिषु च) — पद् is substituted for पाद before 1. हिम 2. काषिन् and 3. हति।",
    "Sūtra 6.3.55: ruchahashe (ऋचः शे) — पद् is substituted for पाद before the affix शस् when the meaning is that of a ऋक् (Hymn).",
    "Sūtra 6.3.56: vaaghoshamishrashabdeshu (वा घोषमिश्रशब्देषु) — पद् is optionally substituted for पाद before 1. घोष 2. मिश्र and 3. शब्द।",
    "Sūtra 6.3.57: udakasyodahasamjnyaayaam (उदकस्योदः संज्ञायाम्) — उद is substituted for उदक when the compound is a Name.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.58: peshamvaasavaahanadhishucha (पेषंवासवाहनधिषु च) — उद is substituted for उदक before 1. पेषं 2. वास 3. वाह and 4. धि।",
    "Sūtra 6.3.59: ekahalaadaupoorayitavyenyatarasyaam (एकहलादौ पूरयितव्येऽन्यतरस्याम्) — उद is optionally substituted for उदक before a word beginning with a single consonant and which expresses that which is filled with water.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.60: manthaudanasaktubinduvajrabhaarahaaraveevadhagaaheshucha (मन्थौदनसक्तुबिन्दुवज्रभारहारवीवधगाहेषु च) — उद is optionally substituted for उदक before 1. मन्थ 2. ओदन 3. सक्तु 4. बिन्दु 5. वज्र 5. भार 6. हार 7. वीवध and 8. गाह।",
    "Sūtra 6.3.61: ikohrasvongyogaalavasya (इको ह्रस्वोऽङ्यो गालवस्य) — According to the opinion of गालव a short vowel is substituted in a compound before the second member for the long इक् vowels (ई , ऊ , ॠ) unless it is the long vowel of the feminine affix ई (ङी).",
    "Sūtra 6.3.62: ekataddhitecha (एक तद्धिते च) — The short is substituted for the long एका before a तद्धित affix and when a second member follows.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.63: ngyaapohasamjnyaachhandasorbahulam (ङ्यापोः संज्ञाछन्दसोर्बहुलम्) — The short is diversely substituted for the feminine affixes ई and आ (ङी and आप्) in a Name and in the छन्दस् (Vedas).",
    "Sūtra 6.3.64: tvecha (त्वे च) — The feminine affixes ई and आ (ङी and आप्) diversely become short before the affix त्व।",
    "Sūtra 6.3.65: ishtakesheekaamaalaanaamchitatoolabhaarishu (इष्टकेषीकामालानां चिततूलभारिषु) — For the long vowel a short is substituted in इष्टका before चित in इषीका before तूल and in माला before भारिन्।",
    "Sūtra 6.3.66: khityanavyayasya (खित्यनव्ययस्य) — A short is always substituted for the final of the first member when the second member is a word formed by an affix having an indicatory ख but not when the first member is an indeclinable.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.67: arurdvishadajantasyamum (अरुर्द्विषदजन्तस्य मुम्) — मुम् is the augment added immediately after the final vowel of अरुस , द्विषत् and of a stem ending in a vowel unless it is an indeclinable, when the word formed by a खित् affix follows.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.68: ichekaachompratyayavachcha (इच एकाचोऽम्प्रत्ययवच्च) — A monosyllabic word ending in any vowel other than अ when followed by a word formed by a खित् affix receives the augment अम् which is added in the same way as the affix अम् of the Accusative -2nd case singular.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.69: vaachamyamapuramdaraucha (वाचंयमपुरंदरौ च) — वाचंयम and पुरंदर are irregularly formed.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.70: kaaresatyaagadasya (कारे सत्यागदस्य) — मुम् is the augment of सत्य and अगद when the word कार follows.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.71: shyenatilasyapaatenye (श्येनतिलस्य पाते ञे) — मुम् is the augment of the words श्येन and तिल before पात when the affix ञ् follows.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.72: raatrehakrutivibhaashaa (रात्रेः कृति विभाषा) — The word रात्रि optionally takes मुम् augment before a word formed by कृत् affix.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.73: naloponanyah (नलोपो नञः) — The न of the Negative Particle नञ् is elided when it is the first member of a compound.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.74: tasmaannudachi (तस्मान्नुडचि) — After the above न-elided of the Negative Particle नञ् (i.e. after अ) is added the augment नुट् to a word beginning with a vowel.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.75: nabhraannapaannavedaanaasatyaanamuchinakulanakhanapumsakanakshatranakranaakeshuprakrutyaa (नभ्राण्नपान्नवेदानासत्यानमुचिनकुलनखनपुंसकनक्षत्रनक्रनाकेषु प्रकृत्या) — The Negative Particle remains unchanged in - 1. नभ्राज् 2. नपात् 3. नवेदस् 4. नासत्या (dual) 5. नमुचि 6. नकुल 7. नख 8. नपुंसक 9. नक्षत्र 10. नक्र and 11. नाक।",
    "Sūtra 6.3.76: ekaadishchaikasyachaaduk (एकादिश्चैकस्य चादुक्) — The Negative Particle remains unchanged in a word which begins with एक and of this एक there is the augment अदुक् (अद्)।",
    "Sūtra 6.3.77: nagopraanishvanyatarasyaam (नगोऽप्राणिष्वन्यतरस्याम्) — The Negative Particle is optionally retained unchanged in नगो when it does not mean a living animate being.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.78: sahasyasahasamjnyaayaam (सहस्य सः संज्ञायाम्) — स is substituted for सह , in a Name.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.79: granthaantaadhikecha (ग्रन्थान्ताधिके च) — स is substituted for सह when it has the sense of 'up to the end'.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.80: dviteeyechaanupaakhye (द्वितीये चानुपाख्ये) — स is substituted for सह when it is in connection with a word which refers to a second object which latter however is not directly perceived.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.81: avyayeebhaavechaakaale (अव्ययीभावे चाकाले) — स is substituted for सह in an अव्ययीभाव समास when the second member is not a word denoting time.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.82: vopasarjanasya (वोपसर्जनस्य) — स is optionally substituted for सह when the compound is a बहुव्रीहि समास।",
    "Sūtra 6.3.83: prakrutyaashishyagovatsahaleshu (प्रकृत्याऽऽशिष्यगोवत्सहलेषु) — The word सह retains its original form when the sentence denotes benediction, except when it is गो , वत्स or हल।",
    "Sūtra 6.3.84: samaanasyachhandasyamoordhaprabhrutyudarkeshu (समानस्य छन्दस्यमूर्धप्रभृत्युदर्केषु) — स is substituted for समान् in the छन्दस् (Vedas), but not before 1. मूर्धन् 2. प्रभृति and 3. उदर्क।",
    "Sūtra 6.3.85: jyotirjanapadaraatrinaabhinaamagotraroopasthaanavarnavayovachanabandhushu (ज्योतिर्जनपदरात्रिनाभिनामगोत्ररूपस्थानवर्णवयोवचनबन्धुषु) — This substitution of स for समान् takes place before 1. ज्योतिस् 2. जनपद 3. रात्रि 4. गोत्र 5. रूप 6. स्थान 7. वर्ण 8. वयस् 9. वचन and 10. बन्धु in the common language also.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.86: charanebrahmachaarini (चरणे ब्रह्मचारिणि) — स is substituted for समान् before ब्रह्मचारिन् when it denotes persons engaged in fulfilling a common vow of studying the Vedas.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.87: teertheye (तीर्थे ये) — स is substituted for समान् before तीर्थ when the affix यत् is added to it.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.88: vibhaashodare (विभाषोदरे) — स is optionally substituted for समान् before उदर when the affix यत् is added to it.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.89: drugdrushavatushu (दृग्दृशवतुषु) — स is substituted for समान् before 1. दृग् 2. दृश and the affix वत्।",
    "Sūtra 6.3.90: idangkimoreeshkee (इदङ्किमोरीश्की) — ई is substituted for इदम् and की for किम् before the words 1. दृग् 2. दृश and the affix वत्।",
    "Sūtra 6.3.91: aasarvanaamnah (आ सर्वनाम्नः) — आ is substituted for the final of the pronouns - सर्वादीनि सर्वनामानि [[1.1.27]], before the words 1. दृग् 2. दृश and the affix वत्।",
    "Sūtra 6.3.92: vishvagdevayoshchateradryanychatauvapratyaye (विष्वग्देवयोश्च टेरद्र्यञ्चतावप्रत्यये) — In the room of the last consonant that follows it, of a pronoun and of the words विषवक् and देव is substituted अद्रि when अञ्च् with the affix व follows.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.93: samahasami (समः समि) — समि is substituted for सम् before this अञ्च् when no affix (or व affix) follows.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.94: tirasastiryalope (तिरसस्तिर्यलोपे) — तिरि is substituted for तिरस् before this अञ्च् when no affix (or व affix) follows, provided that the अ of अञ्च् is not elided.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.95: sahasyasadhrih (सहस्य सध्रिः) — सघ्रि is the substitute of सह before अञ्च् when no affix (or व affix) follows.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.96: sadhamaadasthayoshchhandasi (सध मादस्थयोश्छन्दसि) — सध is substituted for सह in the छन्दस् (Vedas) when माद and स्थ follow.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.97: dvyantarupasargebhyopeet (द्व्यन्तरुपसर्गेभ्योऽप ईत्) — After 1. द्वि 2. अन्तर and prepositions, long ई is the substitute of अप्।",
    "Sūtra 6.3.98: oodanordeshe (ऊदनोर्देशे) — After अनु , ऊ is substituted for (the अ of) अप् when the sense is that of a locality.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.99: ashashthyatruteeyaasthasyaanyasyadugaasheeraashaasthaasthitotsukotikaarakaraagachchheshu (अषष्ठ्यतृतीयास्थस्यान्यस्य दुगाशीराशाऽऽस्थाऽऽस्थितोत्सुकोतिकारकरागच्छेषु) — अन्य when not used in the Genitive 6th-Case or the Instrumental -3rd case gets the augment दुक् (द्) before 1. आशिस् 2. आशा 3. आस्था 4. उत्सुक 5. कारक and 6. राग as well as before the affix छ (ईय).",
    "Sūtra 6.3.100: arthevibhaashaa (अर्थे विभाषा) — दुक् (द्) is optionally the augment of अन्य when अर्थ follows.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.101: kohakattatpurushechi (कोः कत् तत्पुरुषेऽचि) — कत् is substituted for कु in a तत्-पुरुष समास when a word beginning with a vowel follows as the second member.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.102: rathavadayoshcha (रथवदयोश्च) — कत् is substituted for कु before रथ and वद।",
    "Sūtra 6.3.103: trunechajaatau (तृणे च जातौ) — कत् is substituted for कु when तृण follows denoting a species.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.104: kaapathyakshayoh (का पथ्यक्षयोः) — का is the substitute of कु before पथिन् and अक्ष।",
    "Sūtra 6.3.105: eeshadarthe (ईषदर्थे) — का is the substitute of कु when the meaning is 'a small'.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.106: vibhaashaapurushe (विभाषा पुरुषे) — का is optionally the substitute of कु when the word पुरुष follows.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.107: kavamchoshne (कवं चोष्णे) — का and कवङ् are optionally the substitutes of कु when उष्ण follows.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.108: pathichachchhandasi (पथि च च्छन्दसि) — This substitution of का and कव for कु takes place in the छन्दस् (Vedas) before पथ।",
    "Sūtra 6.3.109: prushodaraadeeniyathopadishtam (पृषोदरादीनि यथोपदिष्टम्) — The elision, augment and mutation of letters to be seen in पृषोदर etc. though not found taught in the treatises of Grammar, are valid to that extent and in the mode, as taught by the usage of the sages.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.110: samkhyaavisaayapoorvasyaahnasyaahannanyatarasyaamngau (संख्याविसायपूर्वस्याह्नस्याहन्नन्यतरस्यां ङौ) — अहन् may optionally be substituted for अह्न in the Locative -7th case singular when a numeral or वि or साय precede it.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.111: dhralopepoorvasyadeerghonah (ढ्रलोपे पूर्वस्य दीर्घोऽणः) — When ढ् or र् is elided for the preceding अ , इ and उ a corresponding long vowel is substituted.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.112: sahivahorodavarnasya (सहिवहोरोदवर्णस्य) — When ढ् or र् are elided, there is the substitution of ओ or आ of the verbs सह् and वह्।",
    "Sūtra 6.3.113: saadhyaisaadhvaasaadhetinigame (साढ्यै साढ्वा साढेति निगमे) — 1. साढ्यै 2. साढ्वा and 3. साढा are irregularly formed in the छन्दस् (Vedas).",
    "Sūtra 6.3.114: samhitaayaam (संहितायाम्) — In the following sūtras up to the end of the पाद are to be supplied the words 'in an uninterrupted flow of speech'.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.115: karnelakshanasyaavishtaashtapanychamanibhinnachhinnachhidrasruvasvastikasya (कर्णे लक्षणस्याविष्टाष्टपञ्चमणिभिन्नछिन्नछिद्रस्रुवस्वस्तिकस्य) — Before कर्ण there is the substitution of a long vowel for the final of the preceding word when it denotes a proprietorship mark or the ears of cattle, but not when the words 1. विष्ट 2. अष्टन् 3. पञ्चन् 4. मणि 5. भिन्न 6. छिन्न 7. छिद्र 8. स्रुव and 9. स्वस्तिक।",
    "Sūtra 6.3.116: nahivrutivrushivyadhiruchisahitanishukvau (नहिवृतिवृषिव्यधिरुचिसहितनिषु क्वौ) — A long vowel is substituted for the final vowel of the preceding word, before the verbs 1. नह् 2. वृत् 3. वृष् 4. व्यध् 5. रुच् 6. सह् and 7. तन् when these roots take the affix क्वि।",
    "Sūtra 6.3.117: vanagiryohasamjnyaayaamkotarakimshulakaadeenaam (वनगिर्योः संज्ञायां कोटरकिंशुलकादीनाम्) — For the final vowel of कोटर etc. a long vowel is substituted before वन and also of किंशुलक etc. before गिरि when the compound is a name.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.118: vale (वले) — The final of the preceding word is lengthened before the affix वल।",
    "Sūtra 6.3.119: mataubahvachonajiraadeenaam (मतौ बह्वचोऽनजिरादीनाम्) — The final vowel of a word consisting of more than two syllables in lengthened before the affix मत् when it is a name, but not of the words अजिर् etc.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.120: sharaadeenaamcha (शरादीनां च) — The final vowel of शर etc. is lengthened before मत् when it is a name.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.121: ikahavahepeeloh (इकः वहेऽपीलोः) — The final इ and the उ of a word with the exception of पीलु are lengthened before वह।",
    "Sūtra 6.3.122: upasargasyaghanyyamanushyebahulam (उपसर्गस्य घञ्यमनुष्ये बहुलम्) — The final vowel of a preposition is diversely lengthened before a word formed by the कृत् affix घञ् but not when the compound denotes a human being.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.123: ikahakaashe (इकः काशे) — A preposition ending in इ or उ lengthens its final before काश।",
    "Sūtra 6.3.124: dasti (दस्ति) — A preposition ending in इ or उ lengthens its final before the verb दा when the latter is changed to त।",
    "Sūtra 6.3.125: ashtanahasamjnyaayaam (अष्टनः संज्ञायाम्) — A long vowel is substituted for the final of अष्टन् before a second member, when the compound is a Name.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.126: chhandasicha (छन्दसि च) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas) also, the long vowel is substituted for the final of अष्टन् before a second member.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.127: chitehakapi (चितेः कपि) — The final word of चिति is lengthened before the affix कप्।",
    "Sūtra 6.3.128: vishvasyavasuraatoh (विश्वस्य वसुराटोः) — The final vowel of विश्व is lengthened before वसु and राट् (the form assumed by राज्).",
    "Sūtra 6.3.129: naresamjnyaayaam (नरे संज्ञायाम्) — The final vowel of विश्व is lengthened before नर when the compound is a Name.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.130: mitrecharshau (मित्रे चर्षौ) — The final vowel of विश्व is lengthened before मित्र when it is the name of a ऋषि।",
    "Sūtra 6.3.131: mantresomaashvendriyavishvadevyasyamatau (मन्त्रे सोमाश्वेन्द्रियविश्वदेव्यस्य मतौ) — In a मन्त्र the final vowels of 1. सोम 2. अश्व 3. इन्द्रिय and 4. विश्वदेव्य are lengthened when the affix मतुप् follows.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.132: oshadheshchavibhaktaavaprathamaayaam (ओषधेश्च विभक्तावप्रथमायाम्) — In a मन्त्र the final of ओषधि is lengthened before the case-endings but not in the Nominative 1st-Case.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.133: ruchitunughamakshutangkutrorushyaanaam (ऋचि तुनुघमक्षुतङ्कुत्रोरुष्याणाम्) — In the ऋग्वेद the finals of the particles 1. तु 2. नु 3. घ 4. मक्षु , the tense-affix तङ् , कु the ending त्र and the word उरुष्य are lengthened.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.134: ikahasunyi (इकः सुञि) — In a मन्त्र the finals of the preceding member ending in इ or उ are lengthened before the particle सु।",
    "Sūtra 6.3.135: dvyachotastingah (द्व्यचोऽतस्तिङः) — A tense affix ending in अ is lengthened in the ऋग्वेद when the verb consists of two syllables.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.136: nipaatasyacha (निपातस्य च) — In the ऋग्वेद the final of a particle is lengthened.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.137: anyeshaamapidrushyate (अन्येषामपि दृश्यते) — The elongation of the final is to be found in other words also.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.138: chau (चौ) — The final vowel of the preceding member is lengthened before अञ्च when it assumes the form च having lost its nasal and the vowel.",
    "Sūtra 6.3.139: samprasaaranasya (सम्प्रसारणस्य) — The vowel substituted for a semi-vowel is lengthened when it stands as the first member of a compound.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.1: anggasya (अङ्गस्य) — Whatever will be taught here after up to the end of the 7th अध्याय is consequent upon the अङ्ग (stem).",
    "Sūtra 6.4.2: halah (हलः) — The long vowel is substituted for a vocalised half-vowel अ , इ and उ at the end of a अङ्ग (stem), when it is preceded by a consonant which is a portion of the stem.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.3: naami (नामि) — The long vowel is substituted for the final of the stem before the Genitive 6th-Case plural affix नाम् (having the augment नुट्).",
    "Sūtra 6.4.4: natisruchatasru (न तिसृचतसृ) — The finals of तिसृ and चतसृ are not lengthened before नाम् (having the augment नुट्).",
    "Sūtra 6.4.5: chhandasyubhayathaa (छन्दस्युभयथा) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas) the finals of तिसृ and चतसृ are found in both ways, before the Genitive 6th-Case plural नाम्।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.6: nrucha (नृ च) — So also नृ before the Genitive 6th-Case plural नाम् is optionally lengthened.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.7: nopadhaayaah (नोपधायाः) — In a अङ्ग (stem) ending in न् the preceding vowel is lengthened before the affix नाम् ।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.8: sarvanaamasthaanechaasambuddhau (सर्वनामस्थाने चासम्बुद्धौ) — In a अङ्ग (stem) ending in न् the preceding vowel is lengthened in strong cases with the exception of the Vocative Case singular.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.9: vaashapoorvasyanigame (वा षपूर्वस्य निगमे) — The lengthening of the penultimate vowel of a अङ्ग (stem) ending in न् , before the affixes of the strong-case, is optional in the छन्दस् (Vedas) when ष precedes such a vowel.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.10: saantamahatahasamyogasya (सान्तमहतः संयोगस्य) — In the strong cases with the exception of Vocative Case singular, the penultimate vowel is lengthened in the case of a अङ्ग (stem) ending in स् with a Nasal consonant preceding it, and of महत्।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.11: aptruntruchsvasrunaptruneshtrutvashtrukshattruhotrupotruprashaastrunaam (अप्तृन्तृच्स्वसृनप्तृनेष्टृत्वष्टृक्षत्तृहोतृपोतृप्रशास्तॄणाम्) — In the strong cases, with the exception of the Vocative Case singular, the penultimate vowel is lengthened in अप् in stems formed by तृन् and तृच् affixes and in 1. स्वसृ 2. नप्तृ 3. नेष्टृ 4. त्वष्टृ 5. क्षत्तृ 6. होतृ 7. पोतृ and 9. प्रशास्तॄ।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.12: inhanpooshaaryamnaamshau (इन्हन्पूषार्यम्णां शौ) — The penultimate vowel is lengthened before the affix शि (Nominative 1st-Case and Accusative -2nd case plural) when the अङ्ग (stem) ends in इन् or हन् or पूषन् or अर्यमन्।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.13: saucha (सौ च) — The penultimate vowels of a अङ्ग (stem) ending in इन् , हन् , पूषन् or अर्यमन् are lengthened before the सु of the Nominative 1st-Case singular but not in Vocative Case singular.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.14: atvasantasyachaadhaatoh (अत्वसन्तस्य चाधातोः) — In the Nominative 1st-Case singular (with the exception of the Vocative Case singular) the penultimate vowel is lengthened in a अङ्ग (stem) ending in अतु and अस् when the consonant (अस्) does not belong to a root.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.15: anunaasikasyakvijhalohakngiti (अनुनासिकस्य क्विझलोः क्ङिति) — The penultimate vowel of a अङ्ग (stem) ending in a nasal is lengthened before the affix क्वि and before an affix having an indicatory क् or ङ् which begins with a consonant other than a semi-vowel or a nasal.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.16: ajjhanagamaamsani (अज्झनगमां सनि) — The lengthening of the vowel takes place in the case of a अङ्ग (stem) ending in a vowel, as well as of हन् and गम् when the Desiderative affix सन् being झलादि (i.e. not taking the augment इट्) follows.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.17: tanotervibhaashaa (तनोतेर्विभाषा) — the lengthened of the अङ्ग (stem) of तन् is optional before the Desiderative सन् when it does not take the augment इट्।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.18: kramashchaktvi (क्रमश्च क्त्वि) — The penultimate of क्रम is optionally lengthened before the affix क्त्वा when it is without the augment इट्।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.19: chchhvohashoodanunaasikecha (च्छ्वोः शूडनुनासिके च) — For च्छ (including the augment तुक्) is substituted श् and for व् is substituted ऊठ् before an affix beginning with a nasal as well as before क्वि and झलादि ङित् and कित् affixes -- अनुनासिकस्य क्विझलोः क्ङिति [[6.4.15]].",
    "Sūtra 6.4.20: jvaratvarasrivyavimavaamupadhaayaashcha (ज्वरत्वरस्रिव्यविमवामुपधायाश्च) — In 1. ज्वर 2. त्वर् 3. श्रिव् 4. अव and 5. मव् before the above mentioned affixes (क्वि and झलादि ङित् and कित् affixes -- अनुनासिकस्य क्विझलोः क्ङिति [[6.4.15]]) there is the single substitution of ऊठ् for the and the vowel preceding the final consonant.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.21: raallopah (राल्लोपः) — After र् there is the elision of छ् and व् before क्वि and झलादि ङित् and कित् affixes -- अनुनासिकस्य क्विझलोः क्ङिति [[6.4.15]].",
    "Sūtra 6.4.22: asiddhavadatraabhaat (असिद्धवदत्राभात्) — The change which is a अङ्ग (stem) will undergo by the application of any of the rules from this sūtra up to भस्य [[6.4.129]], is to be considered as not to have taken effect when we have to apply any other rule of this very section [[6.4.23]] to [[6.4.129]].",
    "Sūtra 6.4.23: shnaannalopah (श्नान्नलोपः) — After न which is added to the roots of the रुधादिगणः (7th Conjugation) as a गणविकरण - श्नम् (characteristic), there is the elision of the following न।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.24: aniditaamhalupadhaayaahakngiti (अनिदितां हल उपधायाः क्ङिति) — In a root-अङ्ग (stem) ending in a consonant preceded by न् - this न not being added to the root owing to its having an indicatory इ -- इदितो नुम् धातोः [[7.1.58]], the न् is elided when an affix having an indicatory क् or ङ् follows.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.25: danshasanyjasvanyjaamshapi (दंशसञ्जस्वञ्जां शपि) — The nasal of 1. दंश् 2. संज् and 3. स्वञ्ज is elided before the गणविकरण शप् of the roots of the भ्वादिगणः (1st Conjugation).",
    "Sūtra 6.4.26: ranyjeshcha (रञ्जेश्च) — The nasal of रञ्ज् is also elided before the गणविकरण शप्।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.27: ghanyichabhaavakaranayoh (घञि च भावकरणयोः) — The penultimate nasal of रञ्ज् is elided before घञ् when the word formed with it expresses a state or an instrument.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.28: syadojave (स्यदो जवे) — The word स्यद् is formed by घञ् in the sense of 'speed'.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.29: avodaidhaudmaprashrathahimashrathaah (अवोदैधौद्मप्रश्रथहिमश्रथाः) — 1. अवोद 2. एध 3. ओद्म 4. प्रश्रथ and 5. हिमश्रथ are irregularly formed by the elision.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.30: naanychehapoojaayaam (नाञ्चेः पूजायाम्) — The nasal of अञ्च् is not elided when meaning is to honour.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.31: ktviskandisyandoh (क्त्वि स्कन्दिस्यन्दोः) — स्कन्दि and स्यन्द retain their nasal before the affix क्त।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.32: jaantanashaamvibhaashaa (जान्तनशां विभाषा) — The nasal may be optionally elided before क्त्वा in a root ending in ज् and in नश्।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.33: bhanyjeshchachini (भञ्जेश्च चिणि) — The nasal may be optionally elided in भञ्ज before the 3rd person passive of the Aorist in चिण् (ई).",
    "Sūtra 6.4.34: shaasidanghaloh (शास इदङ्हलोः) — Before the Aorist in अङ् and before an affix beginning with a consonant having an indicatory क् or ङ् there is the substitution of ई for the vowel of शास्।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.35: shaahau (शा हौ) — Before the Imperative affix हि , शा is substituted for शास्।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.36: hanterjah (हन्तेर्जः) — ज is substituted for हन् before the Imperative affix हि।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.37: anudaattopadeshavanatitanotyaadeenaamanunaasikalopojhalikngiti (अनुदात्तोपदेशवनतितनोत्यादीनामनुनासिक लोपो झलि क्ङिति) — The final nasal of those roots which in the धातुपाठ have an accented root-vowel, as well as of वन , तन etc. (तनादिगणः -8th Conjugation) is elided before an affix beginning with a consonant (except a semi-vowel or nasal) when these have an indicatory क् or ङ्।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.38: vaalyapi (वा ल्यपि) — The nasal above the roots (i.e. अनुदात्त ending in a nasal and वन and तनादि) is optionally elided before the Absolutive affix ल्यप्।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.39: naktichideerghashcha (न क्तिचि दीर्घश्च) — Before the affix क्तिच् the above roots (वन and तनादि) neither drop their nasal nor lengthen their root-vowel.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.40: gamahakvau (गमः क्वौ) — The nasal of गम् is always elided before क्वि।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.41: vidvanoranunaasikasyaat (विड्वनोरनुनासिकस्यात्) — A stem ending in a nasal and followed by the affix विट् or वन् always substitutes for long आ for its nasal.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.42: janasanakhanaamsanyjhaloh (जनसनखनां सञ्झलोः) — The long आ is substituted for the final of जन् , सन् and खन् before the consonant beginning Desiderative affix सन् and before any other affix beginning with a इल् consonant which has an indicatory क् or ङ्।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.43: yevibhaashaa (ये विभाषा) — There is optionally the substitution of long आ for the finals of जन् , सन् and खन् before the affix beginning with य and marked with an indicatory क् or ङ्।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.44: tanoteryaki (तनोतेर्यकि) — The long आ is optionally substituted for the final of तन् before the Passive characteristic यक्।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.45: sanahaktichilopashchaasyaanyatarasyaam (सनः क्तिचि लोपश्चास्यान्यतरस्याम्) — The long आ is optionally substituted for the final of सन् before the affix क्तिच् and there is also optional elision of the nasal.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.46: aardhadhaatuke (आर्धधातुके) — From this up to युप्लुवोर्दीर्घश्छन्दसि [[6.4.68]], inclusive, is always to be supplied the words ' before an affix called आर्धधातुक -- आर्द्धधातुकं शेषः [[3.4.114]] etc.'",
    "Sūtra 6.4.47: bhrasjoropadhayoharamanyatarasyaam (भ्रस्जो रोपधयोः रमन्यतरस्याम्) — In the room of र् and the penultimate letter स् of the root भ्रस्ज , there is optionally the substitute रम् when an आर्धधातुक affix follows.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.48: atolopah (अतो लोपः) — The अ standing at the end of a अङ्ग (stem) is elided before an आर्धधातुक affix.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.49: yasyahalah (यस्य हलः) — When a consonant precedes the final य in a verbal अङ्ग (stem) this य is also elided before an आर्धधातुक affix.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.50: kyasyavibhaashaa (क्यस्य विभाषा) — The elision of य of he Denominative अङ्ग (stem) (क्य) is optional when preceded by a consonant and followed by an आर्धधातुक affix.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.51: neraniti (णेरनिटि) — The इ of the verbal अङ्ग (stem) formed with the affix णि is elided before an आर्धधातुक affix which does not take the augment इट् ।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.52: nishthaayaamseti (निष्ठायां सेटि) — The affix णि is elided before the affixes क्त and क्तवतु when these take the augment इट् ।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.53: janitaamantre (जनिता मन्त्रे) — In a मन्त्र the word जनिता is formed irregularly by the elision of णि before the affix तृ with the augment इट् ।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.54: shamitaayajnye (शमिता यज्ञे) — शमिता is formed irregularly by the elision of णि before an इट् augmented affix when meaning a sacrificial act.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.55: ayaamantaalvaayyetnvishnushu (अयामन्ताल्वाय्येत्न्विष्णुषु) — अय् is substituted for the इ of णि before the affixes 1. आम् 2. अन्त 3. आलु 4. आय्य 5. इत्नु and 6. इष्णु।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.56: lyapilaghupoorvaat (ल्यपि लघुपूर्वात्) — अय् is substituted for the इ of णि before the Absolutive affix ल्यप् when the vowel preceding the इ is light.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.57: vibhaashaapah (विभाषापः) — अय् is optionally substituted for the इ of णि before the Absolutive affix ल्यप् , after the verb आप्।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.58: yupluvordeerghashchhandasi (युप्लुवोर्दीर्घश्छन्दसि) — In यु and प्लु , long is substituted for उ in the छन्दस् (Vedas).",
    "Sūtra 6.4.59: kshiyah (क्षियः) — A long is substituted for the इ of क्षि before the Absolutive affix ल्यप्।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.60: nishthaayaamanyadarthe (निष्ठायामण्यदर्थे) — A long is substituted for the इ in क्षि before the Past Participle in क्त when it is not in the sense of the future Passive Participle in ण्यत्।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.61: vaakroshadainyayoh (वाक्रोशदैन्ययोः) — The long is optionally substituted for the इ in क्षि before the Past Participle in क्त when it is not in the sense of the future Passive Participle in ण्यत् when the word means 'imprecation' or 'a miserable plight'.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.62: syasichseeyuttaasishubhaavakarmanorupadeshejjhanagrahadrushaamvaachinvaditcha (स्यसिच्सीयुट्तासिषु भावकर्मणोरुपदेशेऽज्झनग्रहदृशां वा चिण्वदिट् च) — Before the affixes 1. स्य (First future and Conditional) 2. सिच् (S-Aorist) 3. सीयुद् (Benedictive) and 4. तासि (Periphrastic Future), when they are used in the भाव (Impersonal) and कर्म (Passive) voices 1. the verbal stems ending in a vowel in the Grammatical system of instruction (उपदेश), as well as the verbs 2. हन् 'to kill' 3. ग्रह् 'to seize' and 4. दृश् 'to see' are treated optionally in the same way as in the 3rd Person of the Passive Aorist in चिण् and when so treated, they have the augment इट् ।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.63: deengoyudachikngiti (दीङो युडचि क्ङिति) — युट् is the augment of दीङ् of an आर्धधातुक affix beginning with a vowel and having an indicatory क् or ङ्।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.64: aatolopiticha (आतो लोप इटि च) — The final आ of a root is elided before an आर्धधातुक affix with the augment इट् as well as when it begins with a vowel and has an indicatory क् or ङ्।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.65: eedyati (ईद्यति) — The final आ of a अङ्ग (stem) is changed into ई before the कृत् affix यत्।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.66: ghumaasthaagaapaajahaatisaamhali (घुमास्थागापाजहातिसां हलि) — For the final of the roots of the form of दा and घा (घु), as well as for that of the roots 1. मा 2. स्था 3. गा 4. पा 5. हा (जुहाति) and 6. सा (सो), there is substituted ई before an आर्धधातुक affix beginning with a consonant which has an indicatory क् or ङ्।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.67: erlingi (एर्लिङि) — ए is substituted for the आ of the above roots (1. मा 2. स्था 3. गा 4. पा 5. हा (जुहाति) and 6. सा (सो)) in the Benedictive Mood Active.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.68: vaanyasyasamyogaadeh (वाऽन्यस्य संयोगादेः) — For the final आ of any other root than those mentioned in घुमास्थागापाजहातिसां हलि [[6.4.66]], ए may optionally be substituted in the Benedictive active, when the root begins with a conjunct consonant.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.69: nalyapi (न ल्यपि) — The ई substitution for आ under sūtra घुमास्थागापाजहातिसां हलि [[6.4.66]] does not apply when the absolutive affix ल्यप् follows 1. मा 2. स्था 3. गा 4. पा 5. हा (जुहाति) 6. सा and 7. घु।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.70: mayateridanyatarasyaam (मयतेरिदन्यतरस्याम्) — इ may optionally be substituted for the आ of मा (मयति) before ल्यप् ।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.71: lunglanglrungkshvadudaattah (लुङ्लङ्लृङ्क्ष्वडुदात्तः) — अट् acutely accented (उदात्त) is the augment of the verbal अङ्ग (stem) in the Aorist, Imperfect and the Conditional.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.72: aadajaadeenaam (आडजादीनाम्) — आट् acutely accented (उदात्त) is the augment of a verbal अङ्ग (stem) beginning with a vowel in the Aorist, Imperfect and the Conditional.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.73: chhandasyapidrushyate (छन्दस्यपि दृश्यते) — The आट् augment is found in the छन्दस् (Vedas) also.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.74: namaangyoge (न माङ्योगे) — In connection with the prohibitive particle मा the augment अट् or आट् is not added in the Aorist, Imperfect and the Conditional.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.75: bahulamchhandasyamaangyogepi (बहुलं छन्दस्यमाङ्योगेऽपि) — There is diversity in the छन्दस् (Vedas) : the augment अट् or आट् is added even with मा and sometimes not added even there is no मा।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.76: irayore (इरयो रे) — रे is diversely substituted for इरे in the छन्दस् (Vedas).",
    "Sūtra 6.4.77: achishnudhaatubhruvaamyvoriyanguvangau (अचि श्नुधातुभ्रुवां य्वोरियङुवङौ) — Before an affix beginning with a vowel there are substituted for उ of नु , the characteristic of the roots of the स्वादिगणः (5th Conjugation) for the final इ , ई , उ and ऊ of a root, as well as for ऊ of भ्रू , the इय् (for इ or ई) and उव् (for उ or ऊ).",
    "Sūtra 6.4.78: abhyaasasyaasavarne (अभ्यासस्यासवर्णे) — इवङ् and उवङ् are substituted for the इ and उ of a reduplicate, before a non-homogeneous vowel.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.79: striyaah (स्त्रियाः) — इवङ् is substituted for the ई of स्त्री before an affix beginning with a vowel.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.80: vaamshasoh (वाऽम्शसोः) — The substitution of इवङ् for the ई of स्त्री is optional before the Accusative -2nd case-endings अम् and शस् (अस्).",
    "Sūtra 6.4.81: inoyan (इणो यण्) — For the इ of the root इण् (एति) is substituted a semi-vowel (य) before the affix beginning with a vowel.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.82: eranekaachosamyogapoorvasya (एरनेकाचोऽसंयोगपूर्वस्य) — A semi-vowel is substituted before an affix beginning with a vowel for the final of इ or ई of a root, not preceded by a conjunct consonant forming part of the root, when the अङ्ग (stem) is mono-syllabic.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.83: ohosupi (ओः सुपि) — When a case-affix beginning with a vowel follows, then the semi-vowel व् is substituted for the final ऊ of a अङ्ग (stem) containing more than one syllable if the अङ्ग (stem) ends with a verbal root ending in ऊ not preceded by a conjunct consonant forming part of the root.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.84: varshaabhvashcha (वर्षाभ्वश्च) — The semi-vowel व् is substituted for the ऊ of वर्षाभू also when a case-affix beginning with a vowel follows.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.85: nabhoosudhiyoh (न भूसुधियोः) — The semi-vowel substitution does not take place in the case of अङ्ग (stems) ending in भू or the word सुधी before affixes beginning with a vowel.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.86: chhandasyubhayathaa (छन्दस्युभयथा) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas), in the case of a अङ्ग (stem) in भू or the word सुधी , are found sometimes the इवङ् and उवङ् and sometimes the semi-vowel substitution.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.87: hushnuvohasaarvadhaatuke (हुश्नुवोः सार्वधातुके) — The semi-vowel व् is substituted for the उ of हु and for that of नु (the characteristic of स्वादिगणः (5th Conjugation), before a सार्वधातुक affix -- तिङ्शित्सार्वधातुकम् [[3.4.113]], beginning with a vowel when the अङ्ग (stem) consists of more than one syllable and the उ is not preceded by a conjunct consonant.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.88: bhuvovuglunglitoh (भुवो वुग्लुङ्लिटोः) — भू gets the augment व् (वुक्) before the tense-affixes of the Aorist and the Perfect, when beginning with a vowel.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.89: oodupadhaayaagohah (ऊदुपधाया गोहः) — For the penultimate ओ of the गुण-ated अङ्ग (stem) गोह् (from गुह्) there is the substituted ऊ before an affix beginning with a vowel.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.90: doshonau (दोषो णौ) — The ओ of दोष् is replaced by ऊ before the causative णि।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.91: vaachittaviraage (वा चित्तविरागे) — The ओ of दोष् is optionally replaced by ऊ when the sense is that of the disturbing of the mind.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.92: mitaamhrasvah (मितां ह्रस्वः) — The roots having an indicatory म् retain their penultimate short vowel before the causative णि।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.93: chinnamulordeerghonyatarasyaam (चिण्णमुलोर्दीर्घोऽन्यतरस्याम्) — Optionally a long may be substituted for the penultimate of the causative of मित् roots, before the third person of the Passive Aorist in चिण् (इ) and before the Absolutive affix णमुल् (अम्).",
    "Sūtra 6.4.94: khachihrasvah (खचि ह्रस्वः) — The penultimate of the Causative अङ्ग (stem) is shortened before the affix खच्।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.95: hlaadonishthaayaam (ह्लादो निष्ठायाम्) — The penultimate of the Causative of ह्लद् (ह्लादि) is shortened before the Participle affixes क्त and क्तवतु।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.96: chhaaderghedvyupasargasya (छादेर्घेऽद्व्युपसर्गस्य) — The penultimate of चुरादि (10th Conjugation) - छद् is shortened before the affix घ -- पुंसि संज्ञायां घः प्रायेण [[3.3.118]], when not preceded by two prepositions (or more).",
    "Sūtra 6.4.97: ismantrankvishucha (इस्मन्त्रन्क्विषु च) — The penultimate of छादि is shortened before the affixes 1. इस् 2. मन् 3. त्रन् and 4. क्वि।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.98: gamahanajanakhanaghasaamlopahakngityanangi (गमहनजनखनघसां लोपः क्ङित्यनङि) — The root-vowel of 1. गम् 2. जन् 3. खन् and 4. घस् is elided before an affix beginning with a vowel when it has an indicatory क् or ङ् ; but not before the Aorist affix अङ्।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.99: tanipatyoshchhandasi (तनिपत्योश्छन्दसि) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas) the root-vowel of तन् and पत् is elided before an affix beginning with a vowel, when it has an indicatory क् or ङ् ।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.100: ghasibhasorhalicha (घसिभसोर्हलि च) — The root-vowel of घस् and भस् is elided in the छन्दस् (Vedas) before any affix whether beginning with a vowel or a consonant which has an indicatory क् or ङ् ।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.101: hujhalbhyoherdhih (हुझल्भ्यो हेर्धिः) — After हु and after a consonant (with the exception of semi-vowels and nasals), धि is substituted for the Imperative affix हि when the latter does not take the augment इट् ।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.102: shrushrunuprukruvrubhyashchhandasi (श्रुशृणुपॄकृवृभ्यश्छन्दसि) — धि is substituted for the Imperative affix हि in the छन्दस् (Vedas) after 1. श्रु 2. शृणु 3. पॄ 4. कृ and 5. वृ।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.103: angitashcha (अङितश्च) — धि is substituted for the Imperative affix हि when the tense-affix is not ङित्।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.104: chinoluk (चिणो लुक्) — The personal endings are elided after चिण् , the 3rd person singular Passive of Aorist.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.105: atoheh (अतो हेः) — The Imperative affix हि is elided after a अङ्ग (stem) ending in short अ।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.106: utashchapratyayaadasamyogapoorvaat (उतश्च प्रत्ययादसंयोगपूर्वात्) — The Imperative affix हि is elided after the उ of an affix in the विकरण with which the Present-अङ्ग (stem) (special conjugation) is made, provided that the उ is not preceded by a conjunct consonant.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.107: lopashchaasyaanyatarasyaammvoh (लोपश्चास्यान्यतरस्यां म्वोः) — The पु of the विकरण उ and श्नु when not preceded by a conjunct consonant, may be elided optionally before a personal affix beginning with म् or व्।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.108: nityamkaroteh (नित्यं करोतेः) — The elision of उ is invariable before व् and म् in the case of कृ 'to make' (करोति).",
    "Sūtra 6.4.109: yecha (ये च) — The affix उ of the अङ्ग (stem) कुरु is always elided before a personal ending beginning with a य्।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.110: atutsaarvadhaatuke (अत उत् सार्वधातुके) — Before a सार्वधातुक affix with an indicatory क् or ङ् , short उ is substituted for the अ if कृ 'to make' (कर् + उ) when गुण-ated.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.111: shnasorallopah (श्नसोरल्लोपः) — Before a सार्वधातुक कित् or ङित् affix, the अ of श्न and अस् is elided.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.112: shnaabhyastayoraatah (श्नाऽभ्यस्तयोरातः) — Before a सार्वधातुक कित् or ङित् affix beginning with a vowel, the long आ of श्ना (the विकरण of the क्र्यादिगणः (9th Conjugation)) and of the reduplicate अङ्ग (stems) is elided.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.113: eehalyaghoh (ई हल्यघोः) — Before a सार्वधातुक कित् or ङित् affix beginning with a consonant, the आ of श्ना (the विकरण of the क्र्यादिगणः (9th Conjugation)) and of the reduplicate अङ्ग (stems) is replaced by ई except when the root is दा 'to give' or धा (धु).",
    "Sūtra 6.4.114: iddaridrasya (इद्दरिद्रस्य) — इ is substituted for the आ of दरिद्रा before a सार्वधातुक कित् or ङित् affix beginning with a consonant.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.115: bhiyonyatarasyaam (भियोऽन्यतरस्याम्) — इ is substituted for the ई of भी before a सार्वधातुक affix beginning with a consonant and having an indicatory क् or ङ्।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.116: jahaateshcha (जहातेश्च) — इ is optionally substituted for the आ of हा (जुहोत्यादिगणः (3rd Conjugation)) before a सार्वधातुक affix कित् or ङित् beginning with a consonant.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.117: aachahau (आ च हौ) — आ and इ are optionally substituted for the final of the अङ्ग (stem) of हा (जुहोत्यादिगणः (3rd Conjugation)) before the Imperative ending हि।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.118: lopoyi (लोपो यि) — The final of the अङ्ग (stem) of हा (जुहोत्यादिगणः (3rd Conjugation)) is elided before an affix beginning with य् being a सार्वधातुक कित् or ङित् affix.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.119: ghvasoreddhaavabhyaasalopashcha (घ्वसोरेद्धावभ्यासलोपश्च) — For the final vowel of the roots दा and धा (धु) and for the स् of अस् , is substituted ए before the Imperative ending हि and thereby the reduplicated syllable of दा and धा (धु) is elided.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.120: ataekahalmadhyenaadeshaaderliti (अत एकहल्मध्येऽनादेशादेर्लिटि) — ए is substituted for the short अ standing between two simple consonants of a verbal अङ्ग (stem), before the personal endings of the लिट् (Perfect Tense) which have an indicatory क् -- असंयोगाल्लिट् कित् [[1.2.5]], provided that, at the beginning of the root, in the reduplication, no other consonant has been substituted and when this ए is substituted, the reduplicate is elided.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.121: thalichaseti (थलि च सेटि) — ए is substituted for अ of a verbal अङ्ग (stem) standing between two simple consonants, the अङ्ग (stem) not having any different letter substituted in the reduplicate when the ending थल् of the लिट् (Perfect Tense) having the augment इट् follows and thereby the reduplicate is elided.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.122: truphalabhajatrapashcha (तॄफलभजत्रपश्च) — ए is substituted for अ of 1. तॄ 2. फल 3. भज and 4. त्रप and the reduplicate is elided when the affixes of the लिट् (Perfect Tense) having an indicatory क् (or ङ्) follow, as well as when थल् of the लिट् (Perfect Tense) having the augment इट् follows.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.123: raadhohimsaayaam (राधो हिंसायाम्) — ए is substituted for आ of राध when meaning 'to hurt someone' and the reduplicate is elided before the affixes क् (or ङ्) or as well as before थल् of the लिट् (Perfect Tense) having the augment इट्।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.124: vaajrubhramutrasaam (वा जॄभ्रमुत्रसाम्) — ए is optionally substituted for अ of the अङ्ग (stems) 1. जर् (जॄ) 2. भ्रम and 3. त्रस् and the reduplicate is thereby elided before the affixes of the लिट् (Perfect Tense) having an indicatory क् (or ङ्)",
    "Sūtra 6.4.125: phanaamchasaptaanaam (फणां च सप्तानाम्) — ए is optionally substituted for अ and आ of the seven roots 1. फण् 2. राज् 3. भ्राज् 4. भ्राश् 5. श्लाश् 6. स्याम् and 7. स्वन् and the reduplicate is elided thereby, before the affixes of the लिट् (Perfect Tense) having an indicatory क् (or ङ्) as well as before थल् of the लिट् (Perfect Tense) having the augment इट्।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.126: nashasadadavaadigunaanaam (न शसददवादिगुणानाम्) — ए is not substituted for अ of शस् , दद् or of roots beginning with a व् or of such verbal अङ्ग (stems) in which the अ results through the substitution being कित् or ङित् follow, of the सेट् थल् of the लिट् (Perfect Tense) nor is the reduplicate elided.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.127: arvanastrasaavananyah (अर्वणस्त्रसावनञः) — तृ (which is changed to न्त् in the strong cases and forms the feminine in ई unaccented) is substituted for the final of the अङ्ग (stem) अर्वन् , except in the Nominative 1st-Case singular or when the word is joined with the Negative particle.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.128: maghavaabahulam (मघवा बहुलम्) — तृ is diversely substituted for the final of मघवन्।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.129: bhasya (भस्य) — Whatever will be taught in the following up to the end of this अध्याय should be understood to apply to the nominal stems called भ -- यचि भम् [[1.4.18]], तसौ मत्वर्थे [[1.4.19]].",
    "Sūtra 6.4.130: paadahapat (पादः पत्) — For पाद is substituted पद् when the former is भ।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.131: vasohasamprasaaranam (वसोः सम्प्रसारणम्) — The semi-vowel of the affix वस् (वंस्) is vocalised to उ in a भ अङ्ग (stem).",
    "Sūtra 6.4.132: vaahooth (वाह ऊठ्) — The व is vocalised to ऊ (ऊठ्) when the compound अङ्ग (stem) is भ।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.133: shvayuvamaghonaamataddhite (श्वयुवमघोनामतद्धिते) — The व of 1. श्वन् 2. युवन् and 3. मधवन् becomes vocalised, but not before a तद्धित affix.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.134: alloponah (अल्लोपोऽनः) — Of a भ अङ्ग (stem) ending in अन् , the अ is elided.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.135: shapoorvahandhrutaraajnyaamani (षपूर्वहन्धृतराज्ञामणि) — Of a भ अङ्ग (stem) ending in अन् with a preceding ष as well as of हन् and धृतराजन् , the अ is elided before the affix अण् ।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.136: vibhaashaangishyoh (विभाषा ङिश्योः) — In a अङ्ग (stem) ending in अन् , the अ is optionally elided before the Locative -7th case ending इ before the ending शी (ई) of the Nominative 1st-Case and Accusative-2nd case dual Neuter.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.137: nasamyogaadvamantaat (न संयोगाद्वमन्तात्) — The अ in अन् is not elided when the भ अङ्ग (stem) ends in वन् or मन् with a consonant preceding व् or म्।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.138: achah (अचः) — The अ of अच् (अञ्च् ) is elided at the end of a भ अङ्ग (stem).",
    "Sūtra 6.4.139: udeet (उद ईत्) — The long ई is substituted for the अ of अच् (अञ्च् ) after the word उत् when the अङ्ग (stem) is भ।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.140: aatodhaatoh (आतो धातोः) — The final आ of a भ अङ्ग (stem) is elided when it ends in a root.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.141: mantreshvaangyaaderaatmanah (मन्त्रेष्वाङ्यादेरात्मनः) — In the मन्त्र-s , the beginning of आत्मन् is elided when the affix of the Instrumental -3rd case singular follows.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.142: tivimshaterditi (ति विंशतेर्डिति) — Of the भ अङ्ग (stem) विंशति , before an affix having an indicatory ड् the ति is elided.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.143: teh (टेः) — Before an affix having an indicatory ड् , the last vowel, with the consonant, if any, that follows it, is elided.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.144: nastaddhite (नस्तद्धिते) — Of the भ अङ्ग (stem) the final न् with the vowel that precedes it, is elided before a तद्धित affix.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.145: ahnashtakhoreva (अह्नष्टखोरेव) — The अ of अहन् is elided only before the affixes ट and ख।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.146: orgunah (ओर्गुणः) — For उ of ऊ of a भ अङ्ग (stem) there is substituted गुण before a तद्धित affix.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.147: dhelopokadrvaah (ढे लोपोऽकद्र्वाः) — For उ of ऊ of a भ अङ्ग (stem) is elided before the affix एय (ढ) but not of the अङ्ग (stem) कट्रू",
    "Sūtra 6.4.148: yasyeticha (यस्येति च) — The final अ and इ (both long and short) of a भ अङ्ग (stem) are elided before a तद्धित affix.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.149: sooryatishyaagastyamatsyaanaamyupadhaayaah (सूर्यतिष्यागस्त्यमत्स्यानां य उपधायाः) — Of the भ अङ्ग (stems) 1. सूर्य 2. तिष्य 3. अगस्त्य and 4. मत्स्य (and their derivatives when they are भ) the penultimate य् is also is also elided before a तद्धित affix.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.150: halastaddhitasya (हलस्तद्धितस्य) — The य् of a तद्धित affix when preceded by a consonant and penultimate in a अङ्ग (stem), is elided before the feminine ई।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.151: aapatyasyachataddhitenaati (आपत्यस्य च तद्धितेऽनाति) — The य् of a Patronymic affix, preceded by a consonant, is elided before a तद्धित when it does not begin with an आ।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.152: kyachvyoshcha (क्यच्व्योश्च) — The य् of a Patronymic affix, preceded by a consonant, is elided before the Denominative affix क्य and the adverbial affix च्वि।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.153: bilvakaadibhyashchhasyaluk (बिल्वकादिभ्यश्छस्य लुक्) — The affix छ of the भ अङ्ग (stems) बिल्वक etc. is elided before a तद्धित affix.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.154: turishthemeyassu (तुरिष्ठेमेयस्सु) — The affix तृ is elided before the affixes 1. इष्ठन् 2. इमनिव् and 3. ईयसुन्।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.155: teh (टेः) — The last vowel, with the consonant, if any, that follows it, is elided when the affixes 1. इष्ठ 2. इमन् and ईयस् follow.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.156: sthooladoorayuvahrasvakshiprakshudraanaamyanaadiparampoorvasyachagunah (स्थूलदूरयुवह्रस्वक्षिप्रक्षुद्राणां यणादिपरं पूर्वस्य च गुणः) — Before the affixes 1. इष्ठ 2. इमन् and 3. ईयस् the last semi-vowel is elided with that which follows it and for the first vowel, a गुण is substituted in 1. स्थूल 2. दूर 3. युवन् 4. ह्रस्व 5. क्षिप्र and 6. क्षुद्र।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.157: priyasthirasphirorubahulaguruvruddhatrupradeerghavrundaarakaanaamprasthasphavarbamhigarvarshitrabdraaghivrundaah (प्रियस्थिरस्फिरोरुबहुलगुरुवृद्धतृप्रदीर्घवृन्दारकाणां प्रस्थस्फवर्बंहिगर्वर्षित्रब्द्राघिवृन्दाः) — Before the affixes 1. इष्ठ 2. इमन् and ईयस् the following substitutions take place 1. प्र for प्रिय 2. स्थ for स्थिर 3. स्फ for स्फिर 4. वर् for उरु 5. बह for बहुल 6. गर् for गुरु 7. वर्ष for वृद्ध 8. त्रप् for तृप् 9. द्राघ for दीर्घ and 10. वृन्द for वृन्दारक।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.158: bahorlopobhoochabahoh (बहोर्लोपो भू च बहोः) — The इ and ई of these affixes (इमन् and ईयस्) are elided after बहु , and for बहु is substituted भू।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.159: ishthasyayitcha (इष्ठस्य यिट् च) — After बहु , the augment यिट् is added to इष्ठ and भू is the substitute of बहु।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.160: jyaadaadeeyasah (ज्यादादीयसः) — आ is substituted for the first letter of ईयस् after ज्य।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.161: rrutohalaaderlaghoh (र ऋतो हलादेर्लघोः) — Before the affixes 1. इष्ठ 2. इमन् and 3. ईयस् , र् is substituted for ऋ in a अङ्ग (stem), when this ऋ is preceded by a consonant and is not prosodially long (on account of being followed by a double consonant).",
    "Sūtra 6.4.162: vibhaasharjoshchhandasi (विभाषर्जोश्छन्दसि) — Before the affixes 1. इष्ठ 2. इमन् and 3. ईयस् , the ऋ of ऋजु may optionally be changed to र् , in the छन्दस् (Vedas).",
    "Sūtra 6.4.163: prakrutyaikaach (प्रकृत्यैकाच्) — A monosyllabic भ अङ्ग (stem) retains its original form without undergoing any change before the affixes 1. इष्ठ 2. इमन् and 3. ईयस् ।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.164: inanyanapatye (इनण्यनपत्ये) — The final इन् of a भ अङ्ग (stem) remains unaltered before the non-Patronymic अण् affix.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.165: gaathividathikeshiganipaninashcha (गाथिविदथिकेशिगणिपणिनश्च) — 1. गाथिन् 2. विदथिन् 3. केशिन् 4. गणिन् and 5. पणिन् remain unchanged before the Patronymic also.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.166: samyogaadishcha (संयोगादिश्च) — The syllable इन् of a अङ्ग (stem) ending in इन् remains unchanged before अण् when a conjunct consonant precedes it.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.167: an (अन्) — The syllable अन् of a अङ्ग (stem) ending in अन् remains unchanged before अण् affix whether Patronymic or otherwise.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.168: yechaabhaavakarmanoh (ये चाभावकर्मणोः) — The syllable अन् of a अङ्ग (stem) ending in अन् remains unchanged before a तद्धित affix beginning with य् when it does not denote existence in abstract of the avocation of someone.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.169: aatmaadhvaanaukhe (आत्माध्वानौ खे) — The finals of the अङ्ग (stems) आत्मन् and अध्वन् remain unchanged before the affix ख।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.170: namapoorvopatyevarmanah (न मपूर्वोऽपत्येऽवर्मणः) — In a अङ्ग (stem) in अन् with a preceding म् with the exception of वर्मन् , the ending अन् does not remain unchanged before the Patronymic affix अण् ।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.171: braahmoajaatau (ब्राह्मोऽजातौ) — ब्राह्म is irregularly formed from ब्रह्मन् when not meaning 'a kind of जाति'.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.172: kaarmastaachchheelye (कार्मस्ताच्छील्ये) — कार्म is irregularly formed from कर्मन् by the elision of the final अन् when the sense is 'accustomed to such occupation or prompt therein'.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.173: aukshamanapatye (औक्षमनपत्ये) — From उक्षन् is formed औक्ष when not meaning a descendant.",
    "Sūtra 6.4.174: daandinaayanahaastinaayanaatharvanikajaihmaashineyavaashinaayanibhraunahatyadhaivatyasaaravaikshvaakamaitreyahiranmayaani (दाण्डिनायनहास्तिनायनाथर्वणिकजैह्माशिनेयवाशिनायनिभ्रौणहत्यधैवत्यसारवैक्ष्वाकमैत्रेयहिरण्मयानि) — The following are irregularly formed - 1. दाण्डिनायन 2. हास्तिनायन 3. अथर्वणिक 4. जैह्माशिनेय 5. वाशिनायनि 6. भ्रौणहत्य 7. धैवत्य 8. सरवै 9. अक्ष्वाक 10. मैत्रेय and 11. हिरण्मया।",
    "Sūtra 6.4.175: rutvyavaastvyavaastvamaadhveehiranyayaanichchhandasi (ऋत्व्यवास्त्व्यवास्त्वमाध्वीहिरण्ययानि च्छन्दसि) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas) the following are irregularly formed 1. ऋत्व्य 2. वास्त्व्य 3. 4. वास्त्व 5. माध्वी and 6. हिरण्यय।",
    "Sūtra 7.1.1: yuvoranaakau (युवोरनाकौ) — For यु and वु (nasalized) in an affix, are substituted, respectively, अन and अक।",
    "Sūtra 7.1.2: aayaneyeeneeyiyahaphadhakhachchhaghaampratyayaadeenaam (आयनेयीनीयियः फढखच्छघां प्रत्ययादीनाम्) — आयन् for 1. फ् 2. एय् for ढ् 3. ईन् for ख् 4. ईय् for छ् and इय् for घ are substituted when these consonants stand in the beginning of an affix.",
    "Sūtra 7.1.3: jhontah (झोऽन्तः) — अन्त् is substituted for झ of an affix.",
    "Sūtra 7.1.4: adabhyastaat (अदभ्यस्तात्) — अत् is the substitute of झ after a reduplicated verbal अङ्ग (stem).",
    "Sūtra 7.1.5: aatmanepadeshvanatah (आत्मनेपदेष्वनतः) — अत् is always the substitute of झ in the आत्मनेपद when it is not preceded by a verbal अङ्ग (stem) ending in अ।",
    "Sūtra 7.1.6: sheengorut (शीङो रुट्) — The अत् substitute of झ gets the रुट् augment after the root शी।",
    "Sūtra 7.1.7: vettervibhaashaa (वेत्तेर्विभाषा) — The अत् substitute of झ optionally gets the रुट् augment after the verbal अङ्ग (stem) विद् (वेत्ति).",
    "Sūtra 7.1.8: bahulamchhandasi (बहुलं छन्दसि) — The augment रुट् is diversely applied in the छन्दस् (Vedas).",
    "Sūtra 7.1.9: atobhisais (अतो भिस ऐस्) — After a nominal अङ्ग (stem) ending in अ, ऐस् is substituted for the case-ending भिस्।",
    "Sūtra 7.1.10: bahulamchhandasi (बहुलं छन्दसि) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas) the substitution takes place diversely.",
    "Sūtra 7.1.11: nedamadasorakoh (नेदमदसोरकोः) — This substitution of ऐस् does not take place after 1. इदम् and 2. अदस् except when they end in क।",
    "Sūtra 7.1.12: taangasingasaaminaatsyaah (टाङसिङसामिनात्स्याः) — After a अङ्ग (stem) ending in अ are substituted इन् for the Instrumental -3rd case ending; आ (आत्) for the Ablative -5th case ending अस् and स्य for the Genitive 6th-Case ending अस्।",
    "Sūtra 7.1.13: ngeryah (ङेर्यः) — After a अङ्ग (stem) ending in अ are substituted there is substituted य for the Dative -4th Case ending ए।",
    "Sūtra 7.1.14: sarvanaamnahasmai (सर्वनाम्नः स्मै) — After a Pronominal अङ्ग (stem) ending in अ , स्मै is substituted for the Dative -4th Case ending ए।",
    "Sūtra 7.1.15: ngasingyohasmaatsminau (ङसिङ्योः स्मात्स्मिनौ) — After a Pronominal अङ्ग (stem) ending in अ , स्मात् is substituted for the Dative -4th Case ending अस् and स्मिन् for the Locative -7th case ending इ।",
    "Sūtra 7.1.16: poorvaadibhyonavabhyovaa (पूर्वादिभ्यो नवभ्यो वा) — स्मात् and स्मिन् are optionally substituted for the Ablative -5th case and Locative -7th case endings after पूर्व and the eight that follow it -- पूर्वपरावरदक्षिणोत्तरापराधराणि व्यवस्थायामसंज्ञायाम् [[1.1.34]].",
    "Sūtra 7.1.17: jasahashee (जसः शी) — After a Pronominal अङ्ग (stem) ending in अ , ई is substituted for the Nominative 1st-Case plural अस्।",
    "Sūtra 7.1.18: aungaapah (औङ आपः) — After a अङ्ग (stem) ending in the feminine affix आ , ई is substituted for the dual endings औ of Nominative 1st-Case and Accusative -2nd case.",
    "Sūtra 7.1.19: napumsakaachcha (नपुंसकाच्च) — After a neutral अङ्ग (stem), ई is substituted for the dual endings औ of Nominative 1st-Case and Accusative -2nd case.",
    "Sūtra 7.1.20: jashshasohashih (जश्शसोः शिः) — After a neutral अङ्ग (stem), इ is substituted for the endings (जस् and शस्) of Nominative 1st-Case and Accusative -2nd case.",
    "Sūtra 7.1.21: ashtaabhyaush (अष्टाभ्य औश्) — After the अङ्ग (stem) अष्टा (the form assumed by अष्टन् -- अष्टन आ विभक्तौ [[7.2.84]]), औश् is substituted for the endings of the Nominative 1st-Case and Accusative -2nd case.",
    "Sūtra 7.1.22: shadbhyoluk (षड्भ्यो लुक्) — The Nominative 1st-Case and Accusative -2nd case plural endings are elided after the numerals calls षष् -- ष्णान्ता षट् [[1.1.24]].",
    "Sūtra 7.1.23: svamornapumsakaat (स्वमोर्नपुंसकात्) — The Nominative 1st-Case and Accusative -2nd case endings सु and अम् are elided after a neutral अङ्ग (stem).",
    "Sūtra 7.1.24: atom (अतोऽम्) — After a neutral अङ्ग (stem) अ , अम् is substituted for सु and अम् , the Nominative 1st-Case and Accusative -2nd case endings.",
    "Sūtra 7.1.25: adddataraadibhyahapanychabhyah (अद्ड् डतरादिभ्यः पञ्चभ्यः) — अद्ड् is substituted for the Nominative 1st-Case and Accusative -2nd case singular endings after the Pronouns डतर etc. (i.e. the अङ्ग (stems) formed with the affixes 1. डतर and 2. डतम, and the अङ्ग (stems) 2. इतर 4. अन्य and 5. अन्यतर।",
    "Sūtra 7.1.26: netaraachchhandasi (नेतराच्छन्दसि) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas) अत् (or अद्) is not the substitute of सु and अम् Nominative 1st-Case and Accusative -2nd case endings after इतर।",
    "Sūtra 7.1.27: yushmadasmadbhyaamngasosh (युष्मदस्मद्भ्यां ङसोऽश्) — अश् -- अनेकाल्शित्सर्वस्य [[1.1.55]], is substituted for the Genitive 6th-Case ending अस् after the अङ्ग (stems) युष्मद् and अस्मद्।",
    "Sūtra 7.1.28: ngeprathamayoram (ङे प्रथमयोरम्) — अम् is substituted for the Dative -4th Case ending ए and for the endings of the Nominative 1st-Case and Accusative -2nd case in all numbers after the अङ्ग (stems) युष्मद् and अस्मद्।",
    "Sūtra 7.1.29: shasona (शसो न) — न् is substituted for स् of अस् the affix of the Accusative -2nd case plural after the अङ्ग (stems) युष्मद् and अस्मद्।",
    "Sūtra 7.1.30: bhyasobhyam (भ्यसो भ्यम्) — अभ्यम् is substituted for the Dative -4th Case ending भ्यस् after the अङ्ग (stems) युष्मद् and अस्मद्।",
    "Sūtra 7.1.31: panychamyaaat (पञ्चम्या अत्) — अत् is substituted for the Ablative -5th case ending भ्यस् after the अङ्ग (stems) युष्मद् and अस्मद्।",
    "Sūtra 7.1.32: ekavachanasyacha (एकवचनस्य च) — This substitution of अत् is made in the singular number also in the Ablative -5th case after the अङ्ग (stems) युष्मद् and अस्मद्।",
    "Sūtra 7.1.33: saamaakam (साम आकम्) — आकम् is substituted for the Genitive 6th-Case plural affix साम् -- आमि सर्वनाम्नः सुट् [[7.1.52]], after the अङ्ग (stems) युष्मद् and अस्मद्।",
    "Sūtra 7.1.34: aataunalah (आत औ णलः) — औ is substituted for णल् , the affix of the 1st and 3rd person singular of the लिट् (Perfect Tense), after the roots ending in long आ।",
    "Sūtra 7.1.35: tuhyostaatangaashishyanyatarasyaam (तुह्योस्तातङ्ङाशिष्यन्यतरस्याम्) — तातङ् is optionally substituted for the affixes तु and हि of the Imperative, when Benediction is meant.",
    "Sūtra 7.1.36: videhashaturvasuh (विदेः शतुर्वसुः) — वसु is substituted for the Present Participle affix शतृ after the root विद् 'to know'.",
    "Sūtra 7.1.37: samaasenanypoorvektvolyap (समासेऽनञ्पूर्वे क्त्वो ल्यप्) — In a compound, the first member of which is an indeclinable but not नञ् ; ल्यप् is substituted for क्त्वा।",
    "Sūtra 7.1.38: ktvaapichhandasi (क्त्वाऽपि छन्दसि) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas) the क्त्वा also, as well as ल्यप् is substituted for क्त्वा after an indeclinable compound, other than one preceded by the Negative नञ् ।",
    "Sūtra 7.1.39: supaamsulukpoorvasavarnaachchheyaadaadyaayaajaalah (सुपां सुलुक्पूर्वसवर्णाऽऽच्छेयाडाड्यायाजालः) — The following irregularly endings are substituted for the various case endings in the छन्दस् (Vedas) 1. स् of the Nominative 1st-Case singular for अस् of the plural 2. the लुक् elision of the case-endings 3. the single substitution of the homogeneous long vowel of the अङ्ग (stem) 4. आ 5. आत् 6. ए (शे) for the ending of the Nominative 1st-Case plural 7. या 8. आ (डा) with the elision of the last vowel and the consonant, if any, that follows it in the अङ्ग (stem) 9. या (ड्या) with a similar shortening of the अङ्ग (stem) 10. या (याच्) and आ (accent of ल).",
    "Sūtra 7.1.40: amomash (अमो मश्) — For the personal ending अम् of the 1st person singular (in the Aorist) म -- अनेकाल्शित्सर्वस्य [[1.1.55]] is substituted in the छन्दस् (Vedas).",
    "Sūtra 7.1.41: lopastaatmanepadeshu (लोपस्त आत्मनेपदेषु) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas) the त of the आत्मनेपद personal ending is elided.",
    "Sūtra 7.1.42: dhvamodhvaat (ध्वमो ध्वात्) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas) ध्वात् is substituted for the personal ending ध्वम्।",
    "Sūtra 7.1.43: yajadhvainamiticha (यजध्वैनमिति च) — यजध्वैनम् is irregularly formed in the छन्दस् (Vedas) for यजध्वनमेनम्।",
    "Sūtra 7.1.44: tasyataat (तस्य तात्) — For the ending त of the 2nd person plural Imperative is substituted तात् in the छन्दस् (Vedas).",
    "Sūtra 7.1.45: taptanaptanathanaashcha (तप्तनप्तनथनाश्च) — Also त and तन (before both, on account of the indicatory प् the preceding vowel of the verbal अङ्ग (stem) is strengthened or if weak not shortened) तन and थन are substituted for the त of the 2nd person plural Imperative in the छन्दस् (Vedas).",
    "Sūtra 7.1.46: idantomasi (इदन्तो मसि) — The personal ending मस् becomes in the छन्दस् (Vedas) मसि ending with a इ।",
    "Sūtra 7.1.47: ktvoyak (क्त्वो यक्) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas) the Absolutive affix क्त्वा gets at the end the augment य।",
    "Sūtra 7.1.48: ishtveenamiticha (इष्ट्वीनमिति च) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas) the Absolutive इष्ट्वीनम् is irregularly formed for इष्ट्वा।",
    "Sūtra 7.1.49: snaatvyaadayashcha (स्नात्व्यादयश्च) — स्नात्व्यी etc. are irregularly formed in the छन्दस् (Vedas).",
    "Sūtra 7.1.50: aajjaserasuk (आज्जसेरसुक्) — After a अङ्ग (stem) ending in अ or आ the affix अस् of the Nominative 1st-Case plural gets, in the छन्दस् (Vedas), the augment अस् (असुक्) at the end.",
    "Sūtra 7.1.51: ashvaksheeravrushalavanaanaamaatmapreetaukyachi (अश्वक्षीरवृषलवणानामात्मप्रीतौ क्यचि) — The same augment अस् (असुक्) is added after the words 1. अश्व 2. क्षीर 3. वृष and 4. लवण before the Denominative affix क्यचि when the delight of the subject in these things is to be expressed.",
    "Sūtra 7.1.52: aamisarvanaamnahasut (आमि सर्वनाम्नः सुट्) — After a Pronominal अङ्ग (stem) ending in a अ or आ the affix आम् of the Genitive 6th-Case plural gets the augment स् at the beginning.",
    "Sūtra 7.1.53: trestrayah (त्रेस्त्रयः) — त्रय is substituted for त्रि before the Genitive 6th-Case plural affix.",
    "Sūtra 7.1.54: hrasvanadyaaponut (ह्रस्वनद्यापो नुट्) — The augment न् is added before the Genitive 6th-Case plural ending आम् after the अङ्ग (stems) ending in a short vowel after अङ्ग (stems) called नदी -- यू स्त्र्याख्यौ नदी [[1.4.3]] etc., and after the अङ्ग (stems) ending in the feminine affix आ।",
    "Sūtra 7.1.55: shatchaturbhyashcha (षट्चतुर्भ्यश्च) — The augment न् is added before the Genitive 6th-Case plural ending आम् after the numerals called षष् and after चतुर्।",
    "Sūtra 7.1.56: shreegraamanyoshchhandasi (श्रीग्रामण्योश्छन्दसि) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas) after the words श्री and ग्रामणी the Genitive 6th-Case plural आम् gets the augment न्।",
    "Sūtra 7.1.57: gohapaadaante (गोः पादान्ते) — After गो when standing at the end of a ऋक् verse, the augment न् comes before the Genitive 6th-Case plural आम् ।",
    "Sūtra 7.1.58: iditonumdhaatoh (इदितो नुम् धातोः) — न् is added after the vowel of a root in a root which has an indicatory इ in the धातुपाठ।",
    "Sūtra 7.1.59: shemuchaadeenaam (शे मुचादीनाम्) — In मुच् etc. Before the characteristic श of the तुदादिगणः (6th Conjugation) the न् is added after the vowel of the root.",
    "Sūtra 7.1.60: masjinashorjhali (मस्जिनशोर्झलि) — The augment नुम् is added after the vowel of the roots मस्ज् and नश् before an affix beginning with any consonant other than a semi-vowel or a nasal.",
    "Sūtra 7.1.61: radhijabhorachi (रधिजभोरचि) — The augment नुम् is added after the root-vowel in रध् and जभ् before affixes beginning with a consonant.",
    "Sūtra 7.1.62: netyalitiradheh (नेट्यलिटि रधेः) — The augment नुम् is not added to रध् before an affix beginning with the augment इट् , except in the लिट् (Perfect Tense).",
    "Sūtra 7.1.63: rabherashablitoh (रभेरशब्लिटोः) — The augment नुम् is added after the vowel of the root रभ् 'to begin' before an affix beginning with a vowel but not before the विकरण शप् or the affixes of the लिट् (Perfect Tense).",
    "Sūtra 7.1.64: labheshcha (लभेश्च) — So also लभ् 'to get' before an affix beginning with a vowel with the exception of शप् and लिट् , there is no augment नुम् ।",
    "Sūtra 7.1.65: aangoyi (आङो यि) — The augment नुम् is added to लभ् 'to get' preceded by आ before an affix beginning with य।",
    "Sūtra 7.1.66: upaatprashamsaayaam (उपात् प्रशंसायाम्) — The augment नुम् is added to लभ् 'to get' preceded by उप before य when the reference is to something praise-worthy.",
    "Sūtra 7.1.67: upasargaatkhalghanyoh (उपसर्गात् खल्घञोः) — The augment नुम् is added to लभ् 'to get' preceded by a Preposition before the affixes खल् -- ईषद्दुःसुषु कृच्छ्राकृच्छ्रार्थेषु खल् [[3.3.126]], and घञ्।",
    "Sūtra 7.1.68: nasudurbhyaamkevalaabhyaam (न सुदुर्भ्यां केवलाभ्याम्) — The augment नुम् is added to लभ् 'to get' preceded by a Preposition before the affixes खल् -- ईषद्दुःसुषु कृच्छ्राकृच्छ्रार्थेषु खल् [[3.3.126]], and घञ् when सु or दुः alone (without another Preposition along with them) precede the root.",
    "Sūtra 7.1.69: vibhaashaachinnamuloh (विभाषा चिण्णमुलोः) — The augment नुम् is optionally added to लभ् 'to get' not preceded by a Preposition before the चिण् Aorist and the Absolutive णमुल्।",
    "Sūtra 7.1.70: ugidachaamsarvanaamasthaanedhaatoh (उगिदचां सर्वनामस्थानेऽधातोः) — Whatever has an indicatory उ , ऋ and ऌ (with the exception of a root) and the अङ्ग (stem) अच् (अञ्चि) get the augment नुम् in the strong cases.",
    "Sūtra 7.1.71: yujerasamaase (युजेरसमासे) — The प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stem) युज् before the strong cases gets the augment (नुम्) न् when it does not stand in a compound.",
    "Sūtra 7.1.72: napumsakasyajhalachah (नपुंसकस्य झलचः) — The augment (नुम्) न् is added in the strong cases to a Neuter अङ्ग (stem) ending in a consonant (other than a nasal or a semi-vowel) or ending in a vowel.",
    "Sūtra 7.1.73: ikochivibhaktau (इकोऽचि विभक्तौ) — The augment (नुम्) न् is added to a Neuter अङ्ग (stem) ending in a simple vowel, except अ , before a case-affix beginning with a vowel.",
    "Sūtra 7.1.74: truteeyaadishubhaashitapumskampumvadgaalavasya (तृतीयादिषु भाषितपुंस्कं पुंवद्गालवस्य) — A Neuter अङ्ग (stem) ending in a vowel except अ , of which there exists an equivalent, uniform masculine, is treated like the masculine, in the opinion of गावल before the vowel beginning affixes of the Instrumental -3rd case and the cases that follow it.",
    "Sūtra 7.1.75: asthidadhisakthyakshnaamanangudaattah (अस्थिदधिसक्थ्यक्ष्णामनङुदात्तः) — The acutely accented (उदात्त) अन् (अनङ्) is substituted for the finals of 1. अस्थि 2. दधि 3. सक्थि and 4. अक्षि, before the affixes of the Instrumental -3rd case and the cases that follow it, which begin with a vowel.",
    "Sūtra 7.1.76: chhandasyapidrushyate (छन्दस्यपि दृश्यते) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas) also, the अङ्ग (stems) 1. अस्थि 2. दधि 3. सक्थि and 4. अक्षि are found to take the substitute अन् (अनङ्) before the endings other than those mentioned above.",
    "Sūtra 7.1.77: eechadvivachane (ई च द्विवचने) — The acutely accented (उदात्त) ई is substituted for the final of 1. अस्थि 2. दधि 3. सक्थि and 4. अक्षि in the छन्दस् (Vedas) when the case-affixes of the dual follow.",
    "Sūtra 7.1.78: naabhyastaachchhatuh (नाभ्यस्ताच्छतुः) — The participle affix शतृ (अत्-अन्त्) does not take the augment नुम् after a reduplicate अङ्ग (stem).",
    "Sūtra 7.1.79: vaanapumsakasya (वा नपुंसकस्य) — The participle affix शतृ (अत्-अन्त्) optionally takes the augment नुम् after a reduplicate अङ्ग (stem) in Neuter nouns.",
    "Sūtra 7.1.80: aachchheenadyornum (आच्छीनद्योर्नुम्) — When the affix शतृ (अत्-अन्त्) comes after a verbal अङ्ग (stem) ending in अ or आ, it may optionally take the augment नुम् before the Neutral case-ending शी and before the feminine affix ई।",
    "Sūtra 7.1.81: shapshyanornityam (शप्श्यनोर्नित्यम्) — When the affix शतृ (अत्-अन्त्) comes after a verbal अङ्ग (stem) ending in विकरण-s शप् and श्यन् it invariably takes the augment नुम् before the Neutral शी (ई) and the feminine ending ई (नदी).",
    "Sūtra 7.1.82: saavanaduhah (सावनडुहः) — अनडुह् gets the augment नुम् before the ending सु of the Nominative 1st-Case singular (and Vocative Case).",
    "Sūtra 7.1.83: druksvavassvatavasaamchhandasi (दृक्स्ववस्स्वतवसां छन्दसि) — 1. दृक् 2. स्वस् and 3. स्वतवस् take the augment नुम् before the affix सु (Nominative 1st-Case and Vocative Case singular) in the छन्दस् (Vedas).",
    "Sūtra 7.1.84: divaut (दिव औत्) — औ is substituted for the final of दिव् before the affix सु (Nominative 1st-Case and Vocative Case singular).",
    "Sūtra 7.1.85: pathimathyrubhukshaamaat (पथिमथ्यृभुक्षामात्) — आत् (आ) is substituted for the final of 1. पथिन् 2. मथिन् and 3. ऋभुक्षिन् before the ending  सु (Nominative 1st-Case and Vocative Case singular).",
    "Sūtra 7.1.86: itotsarvanaamasthaane (इतोऽत् सर्वनामस्थाने) — अ is substituted for the इ of 1. पथिन् 2. मथिन् and 3. ऋभुक्षिन् in the strong cases.",
    "Sūtra 7.1.87: thonthah (थो न्थः) — न्थ् is substituted for the थ् of 1. पथिन् and 2. मथिन् in the strong cases.",
    "Sūtra 7.1.88: bhasyaterlopah (भस्य टेर्लोपः) — The last vowel, with the consonant that follows it, is dropped in . पथिन् 2. मथिन् and 3. ऋभुक्षिन् before a weak case-ending beginning with a vowel (before which the अङ्ग (stem) is called भ -- यचि भम् [[1.4.18]].",
    "Sūtra 7.1.89: pumsosung (पुंसोऽसुङ्) — असुङ् (अस्) is substituted for the final of पुंस् in the strong cases.",
    "Sūtra 7.1.90: gotonit (गोतो णित्) — The endings of the strong cases are णित् after गो।",
    "Sūtra 7.1.91: naluttamovaa (णलुत्तमो वा) — The ending of the 1st person singular in the लिट् (Perfect Tense) optionally acts as णित्।",
    "Sūtra 7.1.92: sakhyurasambuddhau (सख्युरसम्बुद्धौ) — After सखि, the endings of the strong cases, with the exception of the Vocative Case singular are णित्।",
    "Sūtra 7.1.93: anangsau (अनङ् सौ) — अनङ् (अन्) is substituted for the इ of सखि before सु of the Nominative 1st-Case singular (but not in the Vocative Case singular).",
    "Sūtra 7.1.94: rudushanaspurudamsonehasaamcha (ऋदुशनस्पुरुदंसोऽनेहसां च) — अनङ् (अन्) is substituted for the final of the अङ्ग (stems) ending in ऋ as well as for the final of 1. उशनस् 2. पुरुदंशस् and 3. अनेहस् in the Nominative 1st-Case singular (but not in the Vocative Case singular).",
    "Sūtra 7.1.95: trujvatkroshtuh (तृज्वत् क्रोष्टुः) — The word क्रोष्टु 'a jackal' is treated in the strong cases (with the exception of Vocative Case singular) as if it ended in तृच् (तृ).",
    "Sūtra 7.1.96: striyaamcha (स्त्रियां च) — The word क्रोष्टु 'a jackal' is treated as if it ended in तृच् (तृ), in the feminine, before all case-endings.",
    "Sūtra 7.1.97: vibhaashaatruteeyaadishvachi (विभाषा तृतीयादिष्वचि) — क्रोष्टु 'a jackal' may be treated as क्रोष्टृ before the endings beginning with a vowel, in the Instrumental -3rd case and the cases that follow it.",
    "Sūtra 7.1.98: chaturanaduhoraamudaattah (चतुरनडुहोरामुदात्तः) — चतुर् and अनडुह् get the acutely accented (उदात्त) augment आ (आम्) after the उ in the strong cases.",
    "Sūtra 7.1.99: amsambuddhau (अम् सम्बुद्धौ) — चतुर् and अनडुह् get the augment अ after the उ in the Vocative Case singular.",
    "Sūtra 7.1.100: tiddhaatoh (ॠत इद्धातोः) — For the final long ॠ of a root, there is substituted इर् -- उरण् रपरः [[1.1.51]].",
    "Sūtra 7.1.101: upadhaayaashcha (उपधायाश्च) — इर् is also substituted for the penultimate long ॠ of a root.",
    "Sūtra 7.1.102: udoshthyapoorvasya (उदोष्ठ्यपूर्वस्य) — उर् is substituted for the long ॠ of a root when it is preceded by a labial consonant belonging to the root.",
    "Sūtra 7.1.103: bahulamchhandasi (बहुलं छन्दसि) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas), the उर् substitution for ॠ of a root-stem is diverse.",
    "Sūtra 7.2.1: sichivruddhihaparasmaipadeshu (सिचि वृद्धिः परस्मैपदेषु) — Before the Aorist-characteristic स् (सिच्), वृद्धि is substituted in the परस्मैपद for the final of a अङ्ग (stem) ending in इ , उ , ऋ (long or short -- इको गुणवृद्धी [[1.1.3]]).",
    "Sūtra 7.2.2: atorlaantasya (अतो ल्रान्तस्य) — वृद्धि is substituted for the short अ when it is immediately followed by the final र् or ल् of a root, before the परस्मैपद s-Aorist.",
    "Sūtra 7.2.3: vadavrajahalantasyaachah (वदव्रजहलन्तस्याचः) — In the परस्मैपद s-Aorist there is वृद्धि of the अ of वद , व्रज् and of any vowel, without distinction, of the अङ्ग (stems) ending in a consonant.",
    "Sūtra 7.2.4: neti (नेटि) — The vowel of a अङ्ग (stem) ending in a consonant does not get वृद्धि when the स् (सिच्) takes the augment इट् ।",
    "Sūtra 7.2.5: hmyantakshanashvasajaagrunishvyeditaam (ह्म्यन्तक्षणश्वसजागृणिश्व्येदिताम्) — The वृद्धि of the vowel of the following अङ्ग (stems), does not take place before the इट् augment s-Aorist in the परस्मैपद ; namely - the अङ्ग (stems) ending in 1. ह् 2. म् or 3. य् , the roots 1. क्षण् 2. श्वस् 3. जागृ , a stem formed with णि, the root श्वि and the roots having an indicatory ए in the धातुपाठ।",
    "Sūtra 7.2.6: oornotervibhaashaa (ऊर्णोतेर्विभाषा) — Before an इट् beginning substituted-Aorist of the परस्मैपद there is optional वृद्धि of the vowel of ऊर्णु।",
    "Sūtra 7.2.7: atohalaaderlaghoh (अतो हलादेर्लघोः) — Before the इट् beginning s-Aorist of the परस्मैपद the short अ of the root gets optionally वृद्धि when the अङ्ग (stem) begins with a consonant and the अ is prosodially short by being followed by a simple consonant.",
    "Sūtra 7.2.8: nedvashikruti (नेड् वशि कृति) — The augment इट् is not added to a कृत् affix beginning with a sonant consonant (वश् प्रत्यहार).",
    "Sūtra 7.2.9: titutratathasisusarakaseshucha (तितुत्रतथसिसुसरकसेषु च) — The इट् augment is not taken by the following कृत् affixes - 1. ति 2. तु 3. त्र 4. त 5. थ 6. सि 7. सु 8. सर 9. क and 10. स।",
    "Sūtra 7.2.10: ekaachupadeshenudaattaat (एकाच उपदेशेऽनुदात्तात्) — The augment इट् is not added to that affix which is joined to a root, which in the Grammatical system of Instruction (i.e. in the धातुपाठ) is one syllable and is without accent (अनुदात्त). ",
    "Sūtra 7.2.11: shryukahakiti (श्र्युकः किति) — The augment इट् is not added to an affix having an indicatory फ् when it comes after the root श्रि or after a mono-syllabic root ending in 1. उ 2. ऊ 3. ऋ or 4. ॠ in the धातुपाठ।",
    "Sūtra 7.2.12: sanigrahaguhoshcha (सनि ग्रहगुहोश्च) — The Desiderative affix सन् does not get the augment इट् , not only after roots ending in 1. उ 2. ऊ 3. ऋ and 4. ॠ but also after ग्रह and गुह।",
    "Sūtra 7.2.13: krusrubhruvrustudrusrushruvoliti (कृसृभृवृस्तुद्रुस्रुश्रुवो लिटि) — The personal endings of the लिट् (Perfect Tense) do not get the augment इट् after 1 कृ 2. सृ 3. भृ 4. वृ 5. स्तु 6. द्रु 7. स्रु 8.श्रु।",
    "Sūtra 7.2.14: shveeditonishthaayaam (श्वीदितो निष्ठायाम्) — The participial affixes त and तथत् (क्त and क्तवतु) do not get the इट् augment after श्वि and after the root which has an indicatory ई।",
    "Sūtra 7.2.15: yasyavibhaashaa (यस्य विभाषा) — The participial affixes do not take the इट् augment after those roots, to which another suffix can optionally be added, with or without this augment इ।",
    "Sūtra 7.2.16: aaditashcha (आदितश्च) — The participial affixes do not take the इट् augment after a root which has an indicatory आ।",
    "Sūtra 7.2.17: vibhaashaabhaavaadikarmanoh (विभाषा भावादिकर्मणोः) — The participial affixes optionally take the इट् augment after roots having an indicatory आ when the affixes have an Impersonal sense or denote the beginning of an action.",
    "Sūtra 7.2.18: kshubdhasvaantadhvaantalagnamlishtaviribdhaphaantabaadhaanimanthamanastamahasaktaavispashtasvaraanaayaasabhrusheshu (क्षुब्धस्वान्तध्वान्तलग्नम्लिष्टविरिब्धफाण्टबाढानि मन्थमनस्तमःसक्ताविस्पष्टस्वरानायासभृशेषु) — The following words are made without the इट् augment in the senses given against them - 1. क्षुब्ध 'a churning stick' 2. स्वान्तः 'the mind' 3. ध्वान्तः 'darkness' 4. लग्नः 'attached' 5. म्लिष्टः 'indistinct or unintelligible' 6. विरिब्धः 'a note or a tone' 7. फाण्टः 'made without an effort or by an easy process' and 8. बाढः 'excessive'.",
    "Sūtra 7.2.19: dhrushishaseevaiyaatye (धृषिशसी वैयात्ये) — The participial affix does not get इट् augment after the roots 1. धृष् and 2. शस् when meaning 'bold, impudent and arrogant'.",
    "Sūtra 7.2.20: drudhahasthoolabalayoh (दृढः स्थूलबलयोः) — The irregularly formed Past Participle दृढ means 'stout' and 'strong'.",
    "Sūtra 7.2.21: prabhauparivrudhah (प्रभौ परिवृढः) — The irregularly formed परिवृढ means 'Lord'.",
    "Sūtra 7.2.22: kruchchhragahanayohakashah (कृच्छ्रगहनयोः कषः) — The participial affix does not take the augment इट् after the root कष् when the participle means 'difficult' and 'impenetrable'.",
    "Sūtra 7.2.23: ghushiravishabdane (घुषिरविशब्दने) — The participial affix does not take the augment इट् after the root घुष् in any sense other than that of 'proclaimed'.",
    "Sūtra 7.2.24: ardehasamnivibhyah (अर्देः संनिविभ्यः) — The participial affix does not take the augment इट् after the root अर्द when it is preceded by 1. सं 2. नि or 3. वि।",
    "Sūtra 7.2.25: abheshchaavidoorye (अभेश्चाविदूर्ये) — The participial affix does not take the augment इट् after the root अर्द when it is preceded by अभि, when the meaning is that of 'near'.",
    "Sūtra 7.2.26: neradhyayanevruttam (णेरध्ययने वृत्तम्) — The word वृत्त is formed from the causative of वृत् in the sense of 'studied through or read'.",
    "Sūtra 7.2.27: vaadaantashaantapoornadastaspashtachchhannajnyaptaah (वा दान्तशान्तपूर्णदस्तस्पष्टच्छन्नज्ञप्ताः) — The following irregularly formed participles from the causative roots may optionally take इट् - 1. दान्त 2. शान्त 3. पूर्ण 4. दस्त 5. स्पष्ट 6. छन्न and 7. ज्ञप्त।",
    "Sūtra 7.2.28: rushyamatvarasamghushaasvanaam (रुष्यमत्वरसंघुषास्वनाम्) — The participial affix may optionally get इट् augment after 1. रुष् 2. अम् 3. त्वर 4. संघुष् and 5. आस्वन्।",
    "Sūtra 7.2.29: hrusherlomasu (हृषेर्लोमसु) — The participial affix may optionally get इट् augment after हृष् when the word लोमन् or its synonym is in construction with it.",
    "Sūtra 7.2.30: apachitashcha (अपचितश्च) — And after अपचित has also a second form with the augment इ ।",
    "Sūtra 7.2.31: hruhvareshchhandasi (ह्रु ह्वरेश्छन्दसि) — ह्रु is substituted for ह्वर् in the छन्दस् (Vedas) before the Participial-affix.",
    "Sūtra 7.2.32: aparihvrutaashcha (अपरिह्वृताश्च) — The word अपरिह्वृता is irregularly formed in the छन्दस् (Vedas).",
    "Sūtra 7.2.33: somehvaritah (सोमे ह्वरितः) — ह्वरित् is irregularly formed from ह्वृ in the छन्दस् (Vedas) by गुण substitution and इट् augment when it refers to सोम।",
    "Sūtra 7.2.34: grasitaskabhitastabhitottabhitachattavikastavishastrushamstrushaastrutarutrutarootruvarutruvarootruvarutreerujjvalitiksharitikshamitivamityamiteeticha (ग्रसितस्कभितस्तभितोत्तभितचत्तविकस्ताविशस्तृशंस्तृशास्तृतरुतृतरूतृवरुतृवरूतृवरूत्रीरुज्ज्वलितिक्षरितिक्षमितिवमित्यमितीति च) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas), the following irregular forms are found, some with and some without the augment इट् 1. ग्रसित 2. स्कभित 3. स्तभित 4. उत्तभित 5. चत्त 6. विकस्त 7. विशस्तॄ 8. शंस्तृ 9. शास्तृ 10. तरुतृ 11. तरूतृ 12. वरुतृ 13. वरूतृ 14. वरुत्रीः 15. उज्ज्वलिति 16. क्षरिति 17. क्षमिति 18. वमिति and 19. अमिति।",
    "Sūtra 7.2.35: aardhadhaatukasyedvalaadeh (आर्धधातुकस्येड् वलादेः) — An आर्धधातुक affix -- आर्द्धधातुकं शेषः [[3.4.114]] etc., beginning with a consonant (except य) gets the augment इट् (in these rules).",
    "Sūtra 7.2.36: snukramoranaatmanepadanimitte (स्नुक्रमोरनात्मनेपदनिमित्ते) — The augment इट् is added to a आर्धधातुक वलादि affixes after स्नु and क्रम् only then they do not occasion the taking of the personal endings of the आत्मनेपद ।",
    "Sūtra 7.2.37: graholitideerghah (ग्रहोऽलिटि दीर्घः) — The augment इट् added to वलादि आर्धधातुक affixes, becomes lengthened, except in the personal endings of the लिट् (Perfect Tense), after the root ग्रह।",
    "Sūtra 7.2.38: vrutovaa (वॄतो वा) — The इट् augment is optionally lengthened after वॄ , वृञ् and after roots ending in long ॠ, except in the लिट् (Perfect Tense).",
    "Sūtra 7.2.39: nalingi (न लिङि) — The इट् is not lengthened after वॄ , वृञ् and after roots ending in long ॠ in the endings of the Benedictive.",
    "Sūtra 7.2.40: sichichaparasmaipadeshu (सिचि च परस्मैपदेषु) — The इट् is not lengthened after वॄ , वृञ् and after roots ending in long ॠ in the s-Aorist of the परस्मैपद ।",
    "Sūtra 7.2.41: itsanivaa (इट् सनि वा) — The Desiderative स् may optionally take इट् (which is optionally lengthened also) after the said after वृ and ॠ ending roots.",
    "Sūtra 7.2.42: lingsichoraatmanepadeshu (लिङ्सिचोरात्मनेपदेषु) — The इट् is optionally added to endings of the आत्मनेपद Benedictive and s-Aorist, after वृ and ॠ ending roots.",
    "Sūtra 7.2.43: rutashchasamyogaadeh (ऋतश्च संयोगादेः) — The इट् is optionally added to endings of the आत्मनेपद Benedictive and s-Aorist, after a root which ends in short ऋ which is preceded by a conjunct consonant.",
    "Sūtra 7.2.44: svaratisootisooyatidhoonyooditovaa (स्वरतिसूतिसूयतिधूञूदितो वा) — A वलादि आर्धधातुक affix optionally takes इट् after स्वृ , after the two roots सू (सूति and सूयति) after धूञ् and after a root which has an indicatory long ऊ।",
    "Sūtra 7.2.45: radhaadibhyashcha (रधादिभ्यश्च) — A वलादि आर्धधातुक affix optionally takes इट् after रध् and the seven roots that follow it (दिवादिगणः (4th Conjugation) 94 to 91).",
    "Sūtra 7.2.46: nirahakushah (निरः कुषः) — A वलादि आर्धधातुक affix optionally takes इट् after कुष् when it is preceded by निर्।",
    "Sūtra 7.2.47: innishthaayaam (इण्निष्ठायाम्) — The augment इट् is added to the Participial affixes त and तवत् after कुष् when it is preceded by निर्।",
    "Sūtra 7.2.48: teeshasahalubharusharishah (तीषसहलुभरुषरिषः) — An आर्धधातुक affix beginning with a त may optionally take the इट् affix after the roots 1. इष् 2. सह् 3. लुभ् 4. रुष् and 5. रिष्।",
    "Sūtra 7.2.49: saneevantardhabhrasjadambhushrisvruyoornubharajnyapisanaam (सनीवन्तर्धभ्रस्जदम्भुश्रिस्वृयूर्णुभरज्ञपिसनाम्) — The Desiderative स् may optionally take the इट् augment after a root ending in इव् and after 1. ऋधु 2. भ्रस्ज 3. दम्भु 4. श्रि 5. स्वृ 6. यु 7. ऊर्णु 8. भृ 9. ज्ञप् and 10. सन्।",
    "Sūtra 7.2.50: klishahaktvaanishthayoh (क्लिशः क्त्वानिष्ठयोः) — The affixes क्त्वा , क्त and क्त्वातु optionally get the इट् augment after क्लिश्।",
    "Sūtra 7.2.51: poongashcha (पूङश्च) — The affixes क्त्वा , क्त and क्त्वातु optionally get the इट् augment after पू।",
    "Sūtra 7.2.52: vasatikshudhorit (वसतिक्षुधोरिट्) — The affixes क्त्वा , क्त and क्त्वातु always get the इट् augment after वस् 'to dwell' and क्षुध्।",
    "Sūtra 7.2.53: anychehapoojaayaam (अञ्चेः पूजायाम्) — The affixes क्त्वा , क्त and क्त्वातु get the इट् augment after the root अञ्च् when meaning 'to honour or do something to show honour'.",
    "Sūtra 7.2.54: lubhovimochane (लुभो विमोहने) — The affixes क्त्वा , क्त and क्त्वातु get the इट् augment after the root लुभ् (तुदादिगणः (6th Conjugation)) when meaning 'entangled of confused'.",
    "Sūtra 7.2.55: jruvrashchyohaktvi (जॄव्रश्च्योः क्त्वि) — The affix क्त्वा gets the इट् augment after जॄ and जॄव्रश्च्।",
    "Sūtra 7.2.56: uditovaa (उदितो वा) — The affix क्त्वा optionally gets the इट् augment after a root which has an indicatory short उ।",
    "Sūtra 7.2.57: sesichikrutachrutachchhrudatrudanrutah (सेऽसिचि कृतचृतच्छृदतृदनृतः) — An आर्धधातुक affix beginning with a स् (except सिच् the characteristic of s-Aorist) may optionally take the इट् augment after the verbs 1. कृत् (तुदादिगणः (6th Conjugation) and रुधादिगणः (7th Conjugation) 2. चृत् - तुदादिगणः (6th Conjugation) 3. छृद् - रुधादिगणः (7th Conjugation) 4. तृद् -- तुदादिगणः (6th Conjugation) and 5. नृत् -- दिवादिगणः (4th Conjugation).",
    "Sūtra 7.2.58: gameritparasmaipadeshu (गमेरिट् परस्मैपदेषु) — An आर्धधातुक affix beginning with स् gets the इट् augment after गम् 'to go' in the परस्मैपद ।",
    "Sūtra 7.2.59: navrudbhyashchaturbhyah (न वृद्भ्यश्चतुर्भ्यः) — The परस्मैपद आर्धधातुक affixes beginning with स् do not get the इट् augment after वृत् and the three roots (वृध् , शृध् and स्यन्द्) that follow it.",
    "Sūtra 7.2.60: taasichakapah (तासि च कॢपः) — The परस्मैपद आर्धधातुक affixes beginning with स् and the affix तास् (the sign of the Periphrastic Future) do not get the इट् augment after the root कॢप्।",
    "Sūtra 7.2.61: achastaasvatthalyanitonityam (अचस्तास्वत् थल्यनिटो नित्यम्) — After a root which ends in a vowel and after the Periphrastic Future affix तासि is always devoid of the इट् augment (after such a root) थल् the personal ending of the लिट् (Perfect Tense) तास्, does not also get the augment इट् ।",
    "Sūtra 7.2.62: upadeshetvatah (उपदेशेऽत्वतः) — After a root which possesses a short अ as its root-vowel in the original enunciation (the धातुपाठ) and after which the Periphrastic Future तास् is always devoid of the augment इट् , थल् the personal-ending of the लिट् (Perfect Tense), like तास् does not get the augment इट् ।",
    "Sūtra 7.2.63: rutobhaaradvaajasya (ऋतो भारद्वाजस्य) — In the opinion of भारद्वाज , it is only after a root which ends in short ऋ and after which the Periphrastic Future तास् is always devoid of the augment इट् , थल् the personal-ending of the लिट् (Perfect Tense), like तास् does not get the augment इट् ।",
    "Sūtra 7.2.64: babhoothaatatanthajagrumbhavavarthetinigame (बभूथाततन्थजगृम्भववर्थेति निगमे) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas) are found the irregular forms 1. बभूथ 2. आततन्थ 3. जगृम्भ 4. and 5. ववर्थ।",
    "Sūtra 7.2.65: vibhaashaasrujidrushoh (विभाषा सृजिदृशोः) — थल् the personal-ending of the लिट् (Perfect Tense) gets the augment इट् after सृज् and दृश्।",
    "Sūtra 7.2.66: idattyartivyayateenaam (इडत्त्यर्तिव्ययतीनाम्) — थल् the personal-ending of the लिट् (Perfect Tense) gets the augment इट् after 1. अद् 2. ॠ and 3. व्यय्।",
    "Sūtra 7.2.67: vasvekaajaadghasaam (वस्वेकाजाद्घसाम्) — The Participial affix वस् gets the augment इट् only then the reduplicated root before it consists of one syllable or when it comes after a root ending in long आ and after घस्।",
    "Sūtra 7.2.68: vibhaashaagamahanavidavishaam (विभाषा गमहनविदविशाम्) — The affix वस् optionally takes इट् after 1. गम् 'to go' 2. हन् 'to kill' 3. विद् 'to know' and 4. विश् 'to enter'.",
    "Sūtra 7.2.69: sanimsasanivaamsam (सनिंससनिवांसम्) — The form सनिवांसम् with सनि is irregularly formed.",
    "Sūtra 7.2.70: ruddhanohasye (ऋद्धनोः स्ये) — स्य the sign of Future and Conditional gets the augment इट् after a root ending in short ऋ and after हन् 'to kill'.",
    "Sūtra 7.2.71: anyjehasichi (अञ्जेः सिचि) — The स् of the s-Aorist always takes the इट् augment after अञ्ज् - रुधादिगणः (7th Conjugation).",
    "Sūtra 7.2.72: stusudhoonybhyahaparasmaipadeshu (स्तुसुधूञ्भ्यः परस्मैपदेषु) — The सिच् of the Aorist in परस्मैपद takes the augment इट् after the roots 1. स्तु 2. सु and 3. धूञ्।",
    "Sūtra 7.2.73: yamaramanamaataamsakcha (यमरमनमातां सक् च) — The सिच् of the Aorist in परस्मैपद takes the augment इट् after the roots 1. यम् 2. रम् 3. नम् and roots ending in the long आ and स् (सक्) is added at the end of these अङ्ग (stems).",
    "Sūtra 7.2.74: smipoongranyjvashaamsani (स्मिपूङ्रञ्ज्वशां सनि) — The Desiderative सन् gets the augment इट् after the roots 1. स्मिङ् 2. पूङ् 3. ऋ 4. अञ्जू and 5. अशू।",
    "Sūtra 7.2.75: kirashchapanychabhyah (किरश्च पञ्चभ्यः) — The Desiderative सन् gets the augment इट् after the root कॄ - तुदादिगणः (6th Conjugation) and the four roots that follow it.",
    "Sūtra 7.2.76: rudaadibhyahasaarvadhaatuke (रुदादिभ्यः सार्वधातुके) — A सार्वधातुक affix beginning with a consonant other than य gets the augment इट् after the root रुद् - रुधादिगणः (7th Conjugation) and the four that follow it.",
    "Sūtra 7.2.77: eeshahase (ईशः से) — The सार्वधातुक affix से (the ending of the 2nd person Present and Imperative आत्मनेपदि) get the augment इट् after the root ईश - अदादिगणः (2nd Conjugation).",
    "Sūtra 7.2.78: eedajanordhvecha (ईडजनोर्ध्वे च) — The सार्वधातुक affixes से and ध्वे (the endings of the Present and Imperative आत्मनेपदि) get the augment इट् after the roots ईड् - अदादिगणः (2nd Conjugation) and जन् 'to produce'.",
    "Sūtra 7.2.79: lingahasaloponantyasya (लिङः सलोपोऽनन्त्यस्य) — In the सार्वधातुक लिङ् (Potential) the स् which is not final (i.e. the स् of the augments यास् and सीय् ) is elided.",
    "Sūtra 7.2.80: atoyeyah (अतो येयः) — After a Present अङ्ग (stem) ending in a short अ , इय् is substituted for the सार्वधातुक या (i.e. for the या of the augment यास् of the लिङ् (Potential)).",
    "Sūtra 7.2.81: aatongitah (आतो ङितः) — For the आ being a portion of a सार्वधातुक personal-ending which is ङित् (i.e. आते , आथे and आताम् and आथाम्), coming after a verbal अङ्ग (stem) ending in a short अ , there is substituted इय् ।",
    "Sūtra 7.2.82: aanemuk (आने मुक्) — Before the participial ending आन , a verbal अङ्ग (stem) ending in shot अ , gets the augment मुक्।",
    "Sūtra 7.2.83: eedaasah (ईदासः) — ई is substituted for the आ of आन after आस्।",
    "Sūtra 7.2.84: ashtanaavibhaktau (अष्टन आ विभक्तौ) — आ is substituted for the final of अष्टन् before a case-ending.",
    "Sūtra 7.2.85: raayohali (रायो हलि) — Before a case-ending beginning with a consonant, आ is substituted for the final of रै।",
    "Sūtra 7.2.86: yushmadasmadoranaadeshe (युष्मदस्मदोरनादेशे) — आ is substituted for the final of युष्मद् and अस्मद् before a case-ending.",
    "Sūtra 7.2.87: dviteeyaayaamcha (द्वितीयायां च) — आ is substituted for the final of युष्मद् and अस्मद् before the case-ending of the Accusative -2nd case.",
    "Sūtra 7.2.88: prathamaayaashchadvivachanebhaashaayaam (प्रथमायाश्च द्विवचने भाषायाम्) — आ is substituted for the final of युष्मद् and अस्मद् before the case-ending of the Nominative 1st-Case dual in the secular literature.",
    "Sūtra 7.2.89: yochi (योऽचि) — य is substituted for the final of युष्मद् and अस्मद् before a case-ending which is not a substitute and which begins with a vowel.",
    "Sūtra 7.2.90: sheshelopah (शेषे लोपः) — In the remaining cases where (आ or य is not substituted) there is elision of the final युष्मद् and अस्मद्।",
    "Sūtra 7.2.91: maparyantasya (मपर्यन्तस्य) — The substitutions taught hereafter up to प्रतयोत्तरपदयोश्च [[7.2.98]] take effect with regard to the portions of युष्मद् and अस्मद् up to म् i.e. the substitutes replace युष्म् and अस्म्।",
    "Sūtra 7.2.92: yuvaavaudvivachane (युवावौ द्विवचने) — In the dual, युव is substituted for युष्म् and आव for अस्म्।",
    "Sūtra 7.2.93: yooyavayaujasi (यूयवयौ जसि) — In the Nominative 1st-Case plural यूय is substituted for युष्म् and वय for अस्म्।",
    "Sūtra 7.2.94: tvaahausau (त्वाहौ सौ) — In the Nominative 1st-Case singular त्व is substituted for युष्म् and अह for अस्म्।",
    "Sūtra 7.2.95: tubhyamahyaungayi (तुभ्यमह्यौ ङयि) — In the Dative -4th Case singular तुभ्य is substituted for युष्म् and मह्य for अस्म्।",
    "Sūtra 7.2.96: tavamamaungasi (तवममौ ङसि) — In the Genitive 6th-Case singular तव is substituted for युष्म् and मम for अस्म्।",
    "Sūtra 7.2.97: tvamaavekavachane (त्वमावेकवचने) — In the remaining cases of the singular त्व is substituted for युष्म् and म for अस्म्।",
    "Sūtra 7.2.98: pratayottarapadayoshcha (प्रत्ययोत्तरपदयोश्च) — त्व is substituted for युष्म् and म for अस्म् when they signify a single individual, even when an affix follows or a word is in composition.",
    "Sūtra 7.2.99: trichaturohastriyaamtisruchatasru (त्रिचतुरोः स्त्रियां तिसृचतसृ) — तिसृ is substituted for त्रि and चतसृ for चतुर् in the feminine when a case-ending follows.",
    "Sūtra 7.2.100: achirrutah (अचि र ऋतः) — र् is substituted for ऋ of तिसृ and चतसृ before the case-affixes beginning with a vowel.",
    "Sūtra 7.2.101: jaraayaajarasanyatarasyaam (जराया जरसन्यतरस्याम्) — जरस् may be substituted for जरा , optionally before a case-affix beginning with a vowel.",
    "Sūtra 7.2.102: tyadaadeenaamah (त्यदादीनामः) — For the final of त्यद् etc. there is substituted अ when an affix called विभक्ति follows.",
    "Sūtra 7.2.103: kimahakah (किमः कः) — क is substituted for किम् before a विभक्ति affix.",
    "Sūtra 7.2.104: kutihoh (कु तिहोः) — कु is substituted for किम् before a विभक्ति affix beginning with a त or ह।",
    "Sūtra 7.2.105: kvaati (क्वाति) — कु is substituted for किम् before the विभक्ति अत् ।",
    "Sūtra 7.2.106: tadohasahasaavanantyayoh (तदोः सः सावनन्त्ययोः) — For the non-final त् and द् of त्यद् etc. there is substituted स् in the Nominative 1st-Case singular.",
    "Sūtra 7.2.107: adasausulopashcha (अदस औ सुलोपश्च) — For the स् of अदस् there is substituted औ whereby the Nominative 1st-Case singular affix सु is elided.",
    "Sūtra 7.2.108: idamomah (इदमो मः) — म् is substituted for the final म् of इदम् in the Nominative 1st-Case singular.",
    "Sūtra 7.2.109: dashcha (दश्च) — म् is substituted for the द् of इदम् before a विभक्ति affix.",
    "Sūtra 7.2.110: yahasau (यः सौ) — म् is substituted for the द् of इदम् before a विभक्ति affix.",
    "Sūtra 7.2.111: idoypumsi (इदोऽय् पुंसि) — अय् is substituted for the इद् of इदम् in the Nominative 1st-Case singular masculine.",
    "Sūtra 7.2.112: anaapyakah (अनाप्यकः) — अन is substituted for the इद् of इदम् in the Instrumental -3rd case singular and the cases that follow, provided that the augment अकच् is not added.",
    "Sūtra 7.2.113: halilopah (हलि लोपः) — The इद् of इदम् is elided before a विभक्ति affix beginning with a consonant.",
    "Sūtra 7.2.114: mrujervruddhih (मृजेर्वृद्धिः) — The वृद्धि (आर्) is substituted for the root vowel (ऋ) of the अङ्ग (stem) मृज् before an affix.",
    "Sūtra 7.2.115: achonyniti (अचो ञ्णिति) — Before the affixes having an indicatory ञ् or ण् , वृद्धि is substituted for the end-vowel of a अङ्ग (stem).",
    "Sūtra 7.2.116: ataupadhaayaah (अत उपधायाः) — In a अङ्ग (stem) ending in a consonant with an अ immediately preceding it, the वृद्धि is substituted for such अ when followed by an indicatory ञ् or ण्।",
    "Sūtra 7.2.117: taddhiteshvachaamaadeh (तद्धितेष्वचामादेः) — The वृद्धि is substituted for the first vowel of the अङ्ग (stem) when a तद्धित affix having an indicatory ञ् or ण् follows.",
    "Sūtra 7.2.118: kiticha (किति च) — The वृद्धि is substituted for the first vowel of the अङ्ग (stem) when a तद्धित affix with an indicatory क् follows.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.1: devikaashimshapaadityavaaddeerghasatrashreyasaamaat (देविकाशिंशपादित्यवाड्दीर्घसत्रश्रेयसामात्) — When a तद्धित affix having an indicatory ञ् , ण् or क् follows, आ is substituted instead of वृद्धि for the first vowels of the following - 1. देविका 2. शिंशपा 3. दित्यवाट् 4. दीर्घसत्र and 5. श्रेयस।",
    "Sūtra 7.3.2: kekayamittrayupralayaanaamyaaderiyah (केकयमित्त्रयुप्रलयानां यादेरियः) — Before a तद्धित affix having an indicatory ञ् , ण् or क् the वृद्धि is not substituted for the first vowel in a compound when it follows a word ending in य् or व् but ऐ and औ are respectively placed before the semi-vowels.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.3: nayvaabhyaampadaantaabhyaampoorvaututaabhyaamaich (न य्वाभ्यां पदान्ताभ्याम् पूर्वौ तु ताभ्यामैच्) — Before a तद्धित affix with an indicatory ञ् , ण् or क् the वृद्धि is not substituted for the first vowel in a compound when it follows a word ending in य् or व् but ऐ and औ are respectively placed before the semi-vowels.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.4: dvaaraadeenaamcha (द्वारादीनां च) — Before a तद्धित affix with an indicatory ञ् , ण् or क् the वृद्धि is not substituted for the first vowel after य् or व् but ऐ and औ are respectively placed before the semi-vowels in द्वार etc.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.5: nyagrodhasyachakevalasya (न्यग्रोधस्य च केवलस्य) — ऐ is placed before the य् of न्यग्रोध instead of वृद्धि when the word stands alone and is not a member of a compound and is followed by a तद्धित affix with the indicatory ञ् , ण् or क् ।",
    "Sūtra 7.3.6: nakarmavyatihaare (न कर्मव्यतिहारे) — The prohibition and the augment ordained by न य्वाभ्यां पदान्ताभ्याम् पूर्वौ तु ताभ्यामैच् [[7.3.3]], do not apply to a word which expresses the reciprocity of an action.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.7: svaagataadeenaamcha (स्वागतादीनां च) — The prohibition and the augment ordained by न य्वाभ्यां पदान्ताभ्याम् पूर्वौ तु ताभ्यामैच् [[7.3.3]], do not apply also to स्वागत etc.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.8: shvaaderinyi (श्वादेरिञि) — A compound beginning with श्वन् and followed by the तद्धित affix इञ् is not governed by the prohibition nor takes the augment taught in द्वारादीनां च [[7.3.4]].",
    "Sūtra 7.3.9: padaantasyaanyatarasyaam (पदान्तस्यान्यतरस्याम्) — The sūtra द्वारादीनां च [[7.3.4]] is optionally applied to श्वन् followed by पद।",
    "Sūtra 7.3.10: uttarapadasya (उत्तरपदस्य) — Up to यथातथयथापुरयोः पर्यायेण [[7.3.31]] inclusive, the substitution of वृद्धि will take place for the first vowel of the second member in a compound.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.11: avayavaadrutoh (अवयवादृतोः) — Before a तद्धित affix having an indicatory ञ् , ण् or क् वृद्धि is substituted for the first vowel of a word denoting season when it is preceded by a word denoting a part.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.12: susarvaardhaajjanapadasya (सुसर्वार्धाज्जनपदस्य) — After 1. सु 2. सर्व and 3. अर्ध the first vowel of the name of a country gets the वृद्धि when a तद्धित affix with an indicatory ञ् , ण् or क् follows.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.13: dishomadraanaam (दिशोऽमद्राणाम्) — After a word denoting direction, the first vowel of the name of a country with the exception of मद्र gets वृद्धि before a तद्धित affix having an indicatory ञ् , ण् or क् ।",
    "Sūtra 7.3.14: praachaamgraamanagaraanaam (प्राचां ग्रामनगराणाम्) — After a word denoting direction, the first vowel of the name of a village or city in the land of the Eastern people, gets the वृद्धि before a तद्धित affix having an indicatory ञ् , ण् or क् ।",
    "Sūtra 7.3.15: samkhyaayaahasamvatsarasamkhyasyacha (संख्यायाः संवत्सरसंख्यस्य च) — After a numeral, the first vowel of संवत्सर and of a numeral, gets वृद्धि before a तद्धित affix having an indicatory ञ् , ण् or क् ।",
    "Sūtra 7.3.16: varshasyaabhavishyati (वर्षस्याभविष्यति) — After a numeral, the first vowel of वर्ष gets वृद्धि before a तद्धित affix having an indicatory ञ् , ण् or क् when the affix does not refer to a Future time.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.17: parimaanaantasyaasamjnyaashaanayoh (परिमाणान्तस्यासंज्ञाशाणयोः) — After a numeral, the first vowel of a word denoting mass in its widest sense (with the exception of शाण) gets the वृद्धि before a तद्धित affix having an indicatory ञ् , ण् or क् when the word so formed does not mean a Name.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.18: jeproshthapadaanaam (जे प्रोष्ठपदानाम्) — In प्रोष्ठपद and its synonyms, the first vowel of the second member gets the वृद्धि before a तद्धित affix meaning 'born in that time' and having an indicatory ञ् , ण् or क् ।",
    "Sūtra 7.3.19: hrudbhagasindhvantepoorvapadasyacha (हृद्भगसिन्ध्वन्ते पूर्वपदस्य च) — The वृद्धि is substituted for the first vowels of both (the first and second) members in a compound ending with 1. हृद् 2. भग and 3. सिन्धु before a तद्धित affix having an indicatory ञ् , ण् or क् ।",
    "Sūtra 7.3.20: anushatikaadeenaamcha (अनुशतिकादीनां च) — Before a तद्धित affix having an indicatory ञ् , ण् or क् , the वृद्धि is substituted for the first vowel of both members of the compounds अनुशतिका etc.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.21: devataadvamdvecha (देवताद्वन्द्वे च) — Before a तद्धित affix having an indicatory ञ् , ण् or क् , the वृद्धि is substituted for the first vowels of both members of द्वन्द समास of the names of देवता-s।",
    "Sūtra 7.3.22: nendrasyaparasya (नेन्द्रस्य परस्य) — But the वृद्धि of the first vowel of इन्द्र when it stands as the second member of a द्वन्द समास , does not take place before a तद्धित affix having an indicatory ञ् , ण् or क् ।",
    "Sūtra 7.3.23: deerghaachchavarunasya (दीर्घाच्च वरुणस्य) — Before a तद्धित affix having an indicatory ञ् , ण् or क् in a द्वन्द समास of god-names, the वृद्धि is not substituted for the first vowel of वरुण when a long vowel precedes it.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.24: praachaamnagaraante (प्राचां नगरान्ते) — Before a तद्धित affix having an indicatory ञ् , ण् or क् the वृद्धि is substituted for the first vowels of both members of the compound which is the name of a city of the Eastern people and which ends in the word नगर।",
    "Sūtra 7.3.25: janggaladhenuvalajaantasyavibhaashitamuttaram (जङ्गलधेनुवलजान्तस्य विभाषितमुत्तरम्) — Before a तद्धित affix having an indicatory ञ् , ण् or क् the वृद्धि is substituted for the first vowel of the compound ending in 1. जङ्गल 2. धेनु and 3. बलज and optionally for the first vowel of these second members also.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.26: ardhaatparimaanasyapoorvasyatuvaa (अर्धात् परिमाणस्य पूर्वस्य तु वा) — Before a तद्धित affix having an indicatory ञ् , ण् or क् the वृद्धि is substituted for the first vowel of the second member, denoting a mass in its widest sense when the word अर्ध precedes it, but optionally for the first vowel of अर्ध।",
    "Sūtra 7.3.27: naatahaparasya (नातः परस्य) — When the first vowel of the second member preceded by अर्ध and denoting mass is short अ before a तद्धित affix having an indicatory ञ् , ण् or क् and optionally so for the first vowel of the first member (i.e. अर्ध).",
    "Sūtra 7.3.28: pravaahanasyadhe (प्रवाहणस्य ढे) — Before the affix ढ (एय), the वृद्धि is substituted for the first vowel of the second member of प्रवाहण but optionally so for the first member (i.e. प्र).",
    "Sūtra 7.3.29: tatpratyayasyacha (तत्प्रत्ययस्य च) — Even so from a new derivative from this stem ending in ढ, formed with a तद्धित affix having an indicatory ञ् , ण् or क् there is वृद्धि substitution for the first vowel of the second member and optionally for the first vowel of the first member in प्रवाहणेय and प्रावाहणेय।",
    "Sūtra 7.3.30: nanyahashucheeshvarakshetrajnyakushalanipunaanaam (नञः शुचीश्वरक्षेत्रज्ञकुशलनिपुणानाम्) — Before a तद्धित affix having an indicatory ञ् , ण् or क् , the वृद्धि is always substituted for the first vowel of 1. शुचि 2. ईश्वर 3. क्षेत्रज्ञ 4. कुशल and 4. निपुण when preceded by the Negative particle, but this substitution is optional for the vowel of the Negative particles.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.31: yathaatathayathaapurayohaparyaayena (यथातथयथापुरयोः पर्यायेण) — Before a तद्धित affix having an indicatory ञ् , ण् or क् , the words यथातथ and यथापुर may have वृद्धि of the first vowel of their first member or that of the second member, in alteration.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.32: hanastochinnaloh (हनस्तोऽचिण्णलोः) — त् is substituted for the न् of the root हन् 'to kill' before an affix with a indicatory ञ् or ण् which also causes वृद्धि of the penultimate अ , but the augment is not added before the Aorist sign nor before the Personal ending णल् of the लिट् (Perfect Tense).",
    "Sūtra 7.3.33: aatoyukchinkrutoh (आतो युक् चिण्कृतोः) — A root-अङ्ग (stem) ending in आ gets the augment युक् (य्) before the Aorist sign चिण् which causes also the वृद्धि of the root-vowel.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.34: nodaattopadeshasyamaantasyaanaachameh (नोदात्तोपदेशस्य मान्तस्यानाचमेः) — The वृद्धि is not substituted before the Aorist sign चिण् or a कृत् affix with an indicatory ञ् or ण् for the vowel of that root which ends in म and is acutely accented (उदात्त) in its original enunciation (धातुपाठ), but not so in चम् after आ।",
    "Sūtra 7.3.35: janivadhyoshcha (जनिवध्योश्च) — The वृद्धि is not substituted for the vowels of जन् 'to produce' and वधे before the Aorist sign चिण् and the कृत् affixes with an indicatory ञ् or ण् ।",
    "Sūtra 7.3.36: arttihreebleereeknooyeekshmaayyaataampungnau (अर्तिह्रीव्लीरीक्नूयीक्ष्माय्यातां पुङ्णौ) — The augment पुक् (प्) is added to the roots 1. ऋ 2. ह्री 3. व्ली 4. री 5. क्नुय् 6. क्ष्माय and to a root ending in long आ when the affix णि (the Causative) follows.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.37: shaachchhaasaahvaavyaavepaamyuk (शाच्छासाह्वाव्यावेपां युक्) — The augment युक् (य्) is added to the verbal stems 1. शा 2. छा 3. सा 4. ह्वा 5. वे and 6. पा before the affix णि (Causative).",
    "Sūtra 7.3.38: vovidhoonanejuk (वो विधूनने जुक्) — वा gets the augment जुक् (ज्) before the affix णि when the Causative has the sense of 'shaking'.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.39: leelornuglukaavanyatarasyaamsnehavipaatane (लीलोर्नुग्लुकावन्यतरस्यां स्नेहविपातने) — The roots ली and ला optionally get नुक् and लुक् augment respectively before the affix णि when the Causative means 'the melting of a fatty substance'.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.40: bhiyohetubhayeshuk (भियो हेतुभये षुक्) — The augment षुक् is added to the root भी before the affix णि when fear is caused immediately owing to the agent of the Causative.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.41: sphaayovah (स्फायो वः) — For the final of the stem स्फाय् is substituted व् in the Causative.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.42: shaderagatautah (शदेरगतौ तः) — For the final of शद् is substituted त् in the Causative, when it does not mean 'to drive'.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.43: ruhahaponyatarasyaam (रुहः पोऽन्यतरस्याम्) — प् may optionally be substituted for the final of रुह् 'to mount' in the Causative.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.44: pratyayasthaatkaatpoorvasyaatidaapyasupah (प्रत्ययस्थात् कात् पूर्वस्यात इदाप्यसुपः) — इ is substituted for the अ which stands before the क् belonging to an affix when the feminine ending आ follows, provided that, it does not come after a case-affix (i.e. when such a word in अक does not stand at the end of a बहुव्रीहि समास).",
    "Sūtra 7.3.45: nayaasayoh (न यासयोः) — The इ is not substituted for the अ of य् and स् with the augment क् when the feminine आ follows.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.46: udeechaamaatahasthaaneyakapoorvaayaah (उदीचामातः स्थाने यकपूर्वायाः) — According to the opinion of Northern Grammarians इ is not substituted for that अ which is obtained by shortening the long आ of the feminine (under sūtra केऽणः [[7.4.13]] before the affix क) which is preceded by य् or a क्।",
    "Sūtra 7.3.47: bhastraishaajaajnyaadvaasvaananypoorvaanaamapi (भस्त्रैषाऽजाज्ञाद्वास्वानञ्पूर्वाणामपि) — According to the opinion of Northern Grammarians इ is not substituted for that अ which is obtained by shortening the long आ of the feminine (under sūtra केऽणः [[7.4.13]]) of 1. भस्त्रा 2. एषा 3. अजा 4. ज्ञा 5. द्वा -- त्यदादीनामः [[7.2.102]], and 6. स्वा even not then when the negative particle precedes them.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.48: abhaashitapumskaachcha (अभाषितपुंस्काच्च) — According to the opinion of Northern Grammarians इ is not substituted for that अ which is obtained by shortening the long आ of the feminine (under sūtra केऽणः [[7.4.13]]) when to the feminine in long आ there is no equivalent masculine, even when the negative particle precedes.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.49: aadaachaaryaanaam (आदाचार्याणाम्) — According to the opinion of other Teachers, आ is substituted for the which is obtained by shortening the long आ of the feminine (under sūtra केऽणः [[7.4.13]]) of a word which has no corresponding masculine form.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.50: thasyekah (ठस्येकः) — For ठ at the beginning of a तद्धित affix there is substituted इक्।",
    "Sūtra 7.3.51: isusuktaantaatkah (इसुसुक्तान्तात् कः) — क is substituted for ठ after a अङ्ग (stem) ending in 1. इस् 2. उस् 3. उ or ऊ 4. ॠ and 5. त्।",
    "Sūtra 7.3.52: chajohakughinnyatoh (चजोः कु घिण्ण्यतोः) — For the final च् or ज् of a root, there is substituted a corresponding guttural, before an affix having an indicatory ध् and before ण्यत्। ",
    "Sūtra 7.3.53: nyangkvaadeenaamcha (न्यङ्क्वादीनां च) — The guttural is substituted in न्यङ्क्वु etc..",
    "Sūtra 7.3.54: hohanternyninneshu (हो हन्तेर्ञ्णिन्नेषु) — A guttural is substituted for the ह् in हन् 'to kill' before an affix having an indicatory ञ् or ण् and before न्।",
    "Sūtra 7.3.55: abhyaasaachcha (अभ्यासाच्च) — A guttural is substituted for the ह् in हन् 'to kill' after reduplication also.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.56: herachangi (हेरचङि) — A guttural is substituted for the ह् of हि (हिनोति) after a reduplication, but not in the reduplicated Aorist.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.57: sanlitorjeh (सन्लिटोर्जेः) — ज् in जि 'to conquer' after a reduplication before the Desiderative affix सन् and in the लिट् (Perfect Tense).",
    "Sūtra 7.3.58: vibhaashaacheh (विभाषा चेः) — A guttural is optionally substituted for the च् of चि 'to collect' after a reduplication in Desiderative and लिट् (Perfect Tense).",
    "Sūtra 7.3.59: nakvaadeh (न क्वादेः) — A guttural is not substituted for the final च् or ज् of a root which begins with a guttural, before the affix having an indicatory ध् and before ण्यत्।",
    "Sūtra 7.3.60: ajivrajyoshcha (अजिव्रज्योश्च) — A guttural is not substituted for the final ज् of अज् and व्रज् before an affix having an indicatory ध् and before ण्यत्।",
    "Sūtra 7.3.61: bhujanyubjaupaanyupataapayoh (भुजन्युब्जौ पाण्युपतापयोः) — भुज 'an arm' and न्युब्ज 'a kind of bodily disease' are irregularly formed without any change of their ज् before घञ्।",
    "Sūtra 7.3.62: prayaajaanuyaajauyajnyaangge (प्रयाजानुयाजौ यज्ञाङ्गे) — प्रयाज and अनुयाज are irregularly formed with घञ् when meaning 'a portion of a sacrificial offering'.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.63: vanychergatau (वञ्चेर्गतौ) — A guttural is not substituted for the palatal of वञ्च् in the sense of 'going'.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.64: okuchahake (ओक उचः के) — ओक is irregularly formed from the root उच् with the affix क (अ).",
    "Sūtra 7.3.65: nyaavashyake (ण्य आवश्यके) — A guttural is not substituted for the palatal before the affix ण्य when it means 'to do as absolute necessity'.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.66: yajayaacharuchapravacharchashcha (यजयाचरुचप्रवचर्चश्च) — A guttural is not substituted for the final palatals of 1. यज् 2. याच् 3. रुच् 4. प्र-वच् and 5. ऋच् before the affix ण्यत्।",
    "Sūtra 7.3.67: vachoshabdasamjnyaayaam (वचोऽशब्दसंज्ञायाम्) — A guttural is not substituted for the final of वच् before ण्यत् when it does not mean 'a word or speech'.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.68: prayojyaniyojyaushakyaarthe (प्रयोज्यनियोज्यौ शक्यार्थे) — प्रयोज्य and नियोज्य preserve their palatal in the sense of 'capable to do this'.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.69: bhojyambhakshye (भोज्यं भक्ष्ये) — भोज्य preserves its palatal in the sense of 'eatable'.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.70: ghorlopoletivaa (घोर्लोपो लेटि वा) — The final of दा and धा (धु roots) may optionally be elided in the लेट् (Vedic Subjunctive).",
    "Sūtra 7.3.71: otahashyani (ओतः श्यनि) — A अङ्ग (stem) ending in ओ loses its final before the Present characteristic श्यन् of the दिवादिगणः (4th Conjugation).",
    "Sūtra 7.3.72: ksasyaachi (क्सस्याचि) — The अ of the Aorist characteristic कस् is elided before an affix beginning with a vowel.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.73: lugvaaduhadihalihaguhaamaatmanepadedantye (लुग्वा दुहदिहलिहगुहामात्मनेपदे दन्त्ये) — The whole of the affix कस् is optionally elided before the personal endings of आत्मनेपद beginning with a dental, after 1. दुह् 2. दिह् 3. लिह् and 4. गुह्।",
    "Sūtra 7.3.74: shamaamashtaanaamdeerghahashyani (शमामष्टानां दीर्घः श्यनि) — Before the Present characteristic श्यन् , a long is substituted for the root-vowel in शम् and the seven roots that follow it.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.75: shthivuklamuchamaamshiti (ष्ठिवुक्लमुचमां शिति) — Before any other Present character (शित्) the root vowel of 1. ष्ठिव् 2. क्लम् and 3.आ-चम् is lengthened.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.76: kramahaparasmaipadeshu (क्रमः परस्मैपदेषु) — The long is substituted in क्रम् before a शित् affix, in the परस्मैपद ।",
    "Sūtra 7.3.77: ishugamiyamaamchhah (इषुगमियमां छः) — छ् is substituted for the final of 1. इष् 2. गम् and 3. यम् before a Present-character (शित्).",
    "Sūtra 7.3.78: paaghraadhmaasthaamnaadaandrushyarttisarttishadasadaampibajighradhamatishthamanayachchhapashyarchchhadhausheeyaseedaah (पाघ्राध्मास्थाम्नादाण्दृश्यर्त्तिसर्त्तिशदसदां पिबजिघ्रधमतिष्ठमनयच्छपश्यर्च्छधौशीयसीदाः) — Before a Present-character (शित्) the following substitutions take place - 1. पिब् for पा 2. जिघ्र for घ्रा 3. धम् for ध्मा 4. तिष्ठ् for स्था 5. मन् for म्ना 6. यछ् for दा (दाण्) 7. पश्य for दृश् 8. ऋच्छ् for ऋ 9. धौ for सृ 10. शीय् for शद् and 11. सीद् for सद्।",
    "Sūtra 7.3.79: jnyaajanorjaa (ज्ञाजनोर्जा) — Before a शित् affix, जा is substituted for ज्ञा and जन्।",
    "Sūtra 7.3.80: pvaadeenaamhrasvah (प्वादीनां ह्रस्वः) — A short is substituted for पू etc. before a शित् affix.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.81: meenaaternigame (मीनातेर्निगमे) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas) मी is shortened before a शित् affix.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.82: midergunah (मिदेर्गुणः) — For इ in मिद् there is substituted a गुण before a शित् affix.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.83: jusicha (जुसि च) — Before a personal ending जुस् (उस्) of the Imperfect, गुण is substituted for the final 1. इ 2. ई 3. उ. 4. ऊ 5. ऋ 6. ॠ and 7. ऌ।",
    "Sūtra 7.3.84: saarvadhaatukaardhadhaatukayoh (सार्वधातुकार्धधातुकयोः) — The गुण is substituted for the final इक् vowel of a अङ्ग (stem) before the affixes called सार्वधातुक and आर्धधातुक -- तिङ्शित्सार्वधातुकम् [[3.4.113]] etc.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.85: jaagrovichinnalngitsu (जाग्रोऽविचिण्णल्ङित्सु) — The गुण is substituted for the ऋ of the अङ्ग (stem) जागृ , except before the affix वि , before the Aorist character (चिण्) before the personal ending णल् of the लिट् (Perfect Tense) and before an affix with an indicatory ङ्।",
    "Sūtra 7.3.86: pugantalaghoopadhasyacha (पुगन्तलघूपधस्य च) — गुण is substituted before a सार्वधातुक and an आर्धधातुक affix for the इक् vowels of the Causative अङ्ग (stems) which take the augment प् -- अर्त्तिह्रीब्लीरीक्नूयीक्ष्माय्यातां पुङ्णौ [[7.3.36]], and for the short penultimate vowel of a root which ends in a single consonant.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.87: naabhyastasyaachipitisaarvadhaatuke (नाभ्यस्तस्याचि पिति सार्वधातुके) — The गुण is not substituted for the penultimate light इक् vowel in the reduplicated form of a root, before a सार्वधातुक affix beginning with a vowel and having an indicatory प्।",
    "Sūtra 7.3.88: bhoosuvostingi (भूसुवोस्तिङि) — भू and सु get not गुण before an immediately following personal ending which is सार्वधातुक ।",
    "Sūtra 7.3.89: utovruddhirlukihali (उतो वृद्धिर्लुकि हलि) — A root ending in short उ , which has no Present characteristic (i.e. the विकरण is dropped by लुक् elision) gets वृद्धि before a पित् सार्वधातुक affix beginning with a consonant, but not if the अङ्ग (stem) is reduplicated.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.90: oornotervibhaashaa (ऊर्णोतेर्विभाषा) — Before a पित् सार्वधातुक affix beginning with a consonant, the final उ of ऊर्णु optionally gets वृद्धि ।",
    "Sūtra 7.3.91: gunoprukte (गुणोऽपृक्ते) — Before a पित् सार्वधातुक affix which is a single consonant, गुण is substituted for the final of ऊर्णु ।",
    "Sūtra 7.3.92: trunahim (तृणह इम्) — Before a पित् सार्वधातुक affix beginning with a consonant, इ is added after अ of the verbal stem तृणह्।",
    "Sūtra 7.3.93: bruveet (ब्रुव ईट्) — Before a पित् सार्वधातुक affix beginning with a consonant, the augment इट् is placed after ब्रू।",
    "Sūtra 7.3.94: yangovaa (यङो वा) — The पित् सार्वधातुक affix beginning with a consonant, optionally get the augment इट् in the Intensive.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.95: turustushamyamahasaarvadhaatuke (तुरुस्तुशम्यमः सार्वधातुके) — A सार्वधातुक affix beginning with a consonant, optionally get the augment इट् after the roots 1. तु 2. रु 3. स्तु 4. शम् and 5. अम्।",
    "Sūtra 7.3.96: astisichoprukte (अस्तिसिचोऽपृक्ते) — A single consonantal सार्वधातुक affix gets the augment ईट् after अस् (अस्ति) and after the Aorist character सिच् ।",
    "Sūtra 7.3.97: bahulamchhandasi (बहुलं छन्दसि) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas), a single consonantal सार्वधातुक affix gets diversely the augment after अस् (अस्ति) and after the Aorist character सिच् ।",
    "Sūtra 7.3.98: rudashchapanychabhyah (रुदश्च पञ्चभ्यः) — After रुद् and the four roots that follow it, comes the augment ईट् consisting of a single consonant.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.99: adgaargyagaalavayoh (अड्गार्ग्यगालवयोः) — According to the opinion of गार्ग्य and गालाव , the augment अट् comes before a सार्वधातुक affix consisting of single consonant, after the above five roots रुद् etc.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.100: adahasarveshaam (अदः सर्वेषाम्) — After अद् 'to eat' , comes the augment अट् before a सार्वधातुक affix consisting of a single consonant, according to the opinion of all grammarians.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.101: atodeerghoyanyi (अतो दीर्घो यञि) — The long आ is substituted for the final अ of a tense अङ्ग (stem) before a सार्वधातुक affix beginning with a व् or म् (literally a consonant of यञ् प्रत्यहार).",
    "Sūtra 7.3.102: supicha (सुपि च) — Before a case-ending beginning with य् or भ् (literally a consonant of the यञ् प्रत्यहार) the final of a Nominal-stem is lengthened.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.103: bahuvachanejhalyet (बहुवचने झल्येत्) — Before a case-ending beginning with भ् or स् (literally a consonant of the झल् प्रत्यहार) in the plural, ए is substituted for the final अ of Nominal-stem.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.104: osicha (ओसि च) — Before the case-ending ओस् , ए is substituted for the final अ of Nominal-stem.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.105: aangichaapah (आङि चापः) — Before the case-ending ओस् and before आ of the Instrumental -3rd case, ए is substituted for the final आ of the feminine affix.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.106: sambuddhaucha (सम्बुद्धौ च) — ए is substituted for the final आ of the feminine affix, in the Vocative Case singular.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.107: ambaarthanadyorhrasvah (अम्बाऽर्थनद्योर्ह्रस्वः) — A short vowel is substituted in the Vocative Case singular for the final आ of the feminine affix, in the sense of 'mother, mother-dear' and also for the long vowel of the feminines called नदी -- यू स्त्र्याख्यौ नदी [[1.4.3]] etc.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.108: hrasvasyagunah (ह्रस्वस्य गुणः) — For the short इ and उ final in a nominal-stem, a गुण is substituted in the Vocative Case singular.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.109: jasicha (जसि च) — Before the affix अस् of the Nominative 1st-Case plural गुण is substituted for the final short vowel of a Nominal-stem.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.110: rutongisarvanaamasthaanayoh (ऋतो ङिसर्वनामस्थानयोः) — गुण is substituted for the final ऋ of a अङ्ग (stem) in the Locative -7th case singular and in the strong cases.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.111: gherngiti (घेर्ङिति) — For the इ and उ of the stems called घि -- यू स्त्र्याख्यौ नदी [[1.4.3]], गुण is substituted in the Dative -4th Case, Ablative -5th case and Genitive 6th-Case singular.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.112: aannadyaah (आण्नद्याः) — The augment आट् is added to the case-endings of the Dative -4th Case, Ablative -5th case and Genitive 6th-Case singular after the stem called नदी -- यू स्त्र्याख्यौ नदी [[1.4.3]] etc.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.113: yaadaapah (याडापः) — The augment याट् is added to the case-endings of the Dative -4th Case, Ablative -5th case and Genitive 6th-Case singular after a feminine अङ्ग (stem) ending in आ।",
    "Sūtra 7.3.114: sarvanaamnahasyaaddhrasvashcha (सर्वनाम्नः स्याड्ढ्रस्वश्च) — After a Pronominal अङ्ग (stem) ending in long आ of the feminine, the Dative -4th Case, Ablative -5th case and Genitive 6th-Case singular get the augment स्याट् and the आ of the अङ्ग (stem) is shortened.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.115: vibhaashaadviteeyaatruteeyaabhyaam (विभाषा द्वितीयातृतीयाभ्याम्) — After द्वितीया and तृतीया the Dative -4th Case, Ablative -5th case and Genitive 6th-Case singular may optionally get the augment स्याट् before which the आ of the अङ्ग (stem) is shortened.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.116: ngeraamnadyaamneebhyah (ङेराम्नद्याम्नीभ्यः) — For the ending इ of the Locative -7th case singular there is substituted आम् after a अङ्ग (stem) called नदी -- यू स्त्र्याख्यौ नदी [[1.4.3]] etc., after the feminines in आ and after नी।",
    "Sūtra 7.3.117: idudbhyaam (इदुद्भ्याम्) — After all the feminine नदी -- यू स्त्र्याख्यौ नदी [[1.4.3]] etc., words ending in a short इ and उ , आम् is substituted for the इ of the Locative -7th case singular.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.118: aut (औत्) — After a अङ्ग (stem) ending in short इ and उ and which is not नदी -- यू स्त्र्याख्यौ नदी [[1.4.3]] or घि -- शेषो घ्यसखि [[1.4.7]], औ is substituted for the इ of the Locative -7th case singular.",
    "Sūtra 7.3.119: achchagheh (अच्च घेः) — After a घि -- शेषो घ्यसखि [[1.4.7]], अङ्ग (stem) ending in short इ or उ , औ is substituted for the इ of the Locative -7th case singular and अ is substituted for the final of such a घि अङ्ग (stem).",
    "Sūtra 7.3.120: aangonaastriyaam (आङो नाऽस्त्रियाम्) — ना is substituted for the ending आ of the Instrumental -3rd case singular, after the घि अङ्ग (stems) when they are not feminine.",
    "Sūtra 7.4.1: nauchangyupadhaayaahrasvah (णौ चङ्युपधाया ह्रस्वः) — A short is substituted for the vowel, standing in a penultimate position, the Causative अङ्ग (stem), when the affix चङ् (sign of the Reduplicate Aorist of the Causatives) follows.",
    "Sūtra 7.4.2: naaglopishaasvruditaam (नाग्लोपिशास्वृदिताम्) — The shortening of the penultimate of the stem, before the causative affix in the reduplicated Aorist, does not take place, when it is a (Denominative) अङ्ग (stem), which has lost a simple (end vowel of the Nominal stem) before the Causative sign and also not, when it is the verb शास् , or a root which has an indicatory ऋ।",
    "Sūtra 7.4.3: bhraajabhaasabhaashadeepajeevameelapeedaamanyatarasyaam (भ्राजभासभाषदीपजीवमीलपीडामन्यतरस्याम्) — The shortening of the penultimate of the Causative अङ्ग (stem) in the reduplicated Aorist, is optional in the following - 1. भ्राज् 2. भास् 3. भाष् 4. दीप् 5. जीव् 6. मील् and 7. पीड् ।",
    "Sūtra 7.4.4: lopahapibatereechchaabhyaasasya (लोपः पिबतेरीच्चाभ्यासस्य) — The penultimate vowel in the Causative अङ्ग (stem) पा 'to drink' is elided in the Aorist and for the vowel of the reduplicate there is substituted long ई।",
    "Sūtra 7.4.5: tishthaterit (तिष्ठतेरित्) — Short इ is substituted for the penultimate vowel of the Causative अङ्ग (stem) स्था in the Aorist.",
    "Sūtra 7.4.6: jighratervaa (जिघ्रतेर्वा) — Short इ is optionally substituted for the penultimate vowel of the Causative अङ्ग (stem) of घ्रा in the Aorist.",
    "Sūtra 7.4.7: urrut (उर्ऋत्) — Short ऋ is optionally substituted for the penultimate ऋ and ॠ of a Causative अङ्ग (stem) in the reduplicated Aorist.",
    "Sūtra 7.4.8: nityamchhandasi (नित्यं छन्दसि) — Short ऋ is invariably substituted in the छन्दस् (Vedas) for the penultimate ऋ or ॠ of a Causative अङ्ग (stem) in the reduplicated Aorist.",
    "Sūtra 7.4.9: dayaterdigiliti (दयतेर्दिगि लिटि) — दिगि is substituted for दे (दयते) in the लिट् (Perfect Tense).",
    "Sūtra 7.4.10: rutashchasamyogaadergunah (ऋतश्च संयोगादेर्गुणः) — A root ending in short ऋ and preceded by a conjunct consonant gets गुण in the लिट् (Perfect Tense).",
    "Sūtra 7.4.11: ruchchhatyrutaam (ऋच्छत्यॄताम्) — There is गुण in the लिट् (Perfect Tense) of 1. ऋच्छ् 2. ॠ and roots ending in long ॠ।",
    "Sūtra 7.4.12: shrudrupraamhrasvovaa (शॄदॄप्रां ह्रस्वो वा) — In 1. शॄ 'to injure' 2. दॄ 'to tear' and 3. पॄ 'to protect'-- all belonging to क्र्यादिगणः (9th Conjugation), the vowel may be optionally shortened in the लिट् (Perfect Tense).",
    "Sūtra 7.4.13: kenah (केऽणः) — Before the affix क the preceding आ , ई and ऊ are shortened.",
    "Sūtra 7.4.14: nakapi (न कपि) — But before the समासान्त affix कप् coming after बहुव्रीहि समास , the अण् vowels are not shortened.",
    "Sūtra 7.4.15: aaponyatarasyaam (आपोऽन्यतरस्याम्) — Optionally the feminine अङ्ग (stem) in आ is not shortened before the affix कप्।",
    "Sūtra 7.4.16: rudrushongigunah (ऋदृशोऽङि गुणः) — गुण is substituted for the vowel of the root before the affix अङ् in the roots ending in ऋ or ॠ as well as दृश् 'to see'.",
    "Sūtra 7.4.17: asyatesthuk (अस्यतेस्थुक्) — The अङ्ग (stem) अस् 'to be' (अस्यते) gets the augment थुक् before this Aorist अङ्।",
    "Sūtra 7.4.18: shvayaterah (श्वयतेरः) — The अ is substituted for the final of श्वि in the Aorist अङ्।",
    "Sūtra 7.4.19: patahapum (पतः पुम्) — The augment प् is added after the vowel of a root पत् 'to fall' in the Aorist अङ्।",
    "Sūtra 7.4.20: vachum (वच उम्) — The augment उ is added after the अ of वच् in the Aorist अङ्।",
    "Sūtra 7.4.21: sheengahasaarvadhaatukegunah (शीङः सार्वधातुके गुणः) — For the vowel of शी there is substituted गुण when a सार्वधातुक affix follows.",
    "Sūtra 7.4.22: ayangyikngiti (अयङ् यि क्ङिति) — Before an affix beginning with a य् and having an indicatory क् or ङ् there is substituted अय् for the ई of शी।",
    "Sūtra 7.4.23: upasargaaddhrasvoohateh (उपसर्गाद्ध्रस्व ऊहतेः) — The short is substituted for the ऊ of ऊह् when a preposition precedes it and an affix beginning with य् with an indicatory क् or ङ् follows.",
    "Sūtra 7.4.24: eterlingi (एतेर्लिङि) — The short is substituted for the vowel of the अङ्ग (stem) इ (एति) before the augment यास् in the Benedictive, when a preposition precedes it.",
    "Sūtra 7.4.25: akrutsaarvadhaatukayordeerghah (अकृत्सार्वधातुकयोर्दीर्घः) — A long is substituted for the final vowel of the अङ्ग (stem) before an affix beginning with य् having an indicatory क् or ङ् , when it is not a कृत् or a सार्वधातुक affix.",
    "Sūtra 7.4.26: chvaucha (च्वौ च) — A long is substituted for the final vowel of the अङ्ग (stem) before the Adverbial affix च्वि -- अभूततद्भावे कृभ्वस्तियोगे सम्पद्यकर्तरि च्विः [[5.4.50]].",
    "Sūtra 7.4.27: reengrutah (रीङ् ऋतः) — री is substituted for the final short ऋ of a अङ्ग (stem) before an affix beginning with य् when it is not a कृत् or a सार्वधातुक affix and the Adverbial affix च्वि -- अभूततद्भावे कृभ्वस्तियोगे सम्पद्यकर्तरि च्विः [[5.4.50]].",
    "Sūtra 7.4.28: ringshayaglingkshu (रिङ् शयग्लिङ्क्षु) — For the final short ऋ of a root, there is substituted रि before the present character अ (श) before the Passive character य् and before the augment यास् in the Benedictive.",
    "Sūtra 7.4.29: gunortisamyogaadyoh (गुणोऽर्तिसंयोगाद्योः) — गुण is substituted for the final ऋ in the root ऋ (अर्ति) and in those roots ending in ऋ in which the vowel is preceded by a conjunct consonant, when the Passive character यक् or the Benedictive augment यास् follows.",
    "Sūtra 7.4.30: yangicha (यङि च) — गुण is substituted for the final ऋ in those roots ending in ऋ in which the vowel is preceded by a conjunct consonant, when the Intensive character यङ् follows.",
    "Sūtra 7.4.31: eeghraadhmoh (ई घ्राध्मोः) — Long ई is substituted for the vowel of the roots 1. घ्रा and 2. ध्मा in the Intensive.",
    "Sūtra 7.4.32: asyachvau (अस्य च्वौ) — Long ई is substituted for the final of अ or आ of a Nominal stem, before the Adverbial affix च्वि -- अभूततद्भावे कृभ्वस्तियोगे सम्पद्यकर्तरि च्विः [[5.4.50]]।",
    "Sūtra 7.4.33: kyachicha (क्यचि च) — Long ई is substituted for the final of अ or आ of a Nominal stem, before the Denominative affix क्यच् ।",
    "Sūtra 7.4.34: ashanaayodanyadhanaayaabubhukshaapipaasaagarddheshu (अशनायोदन्यधनाया बुभुक्षापिपासागर्द्धेषु) — The Denominative roots 1. अशनाय 2. उदन्य and 3. धनाय are irregularly formed when they respectively mean 1. 'to be hungry' 2. 'to be thirsty' and 3. 'to be greedy'.",
    "Sūtra 7.4.35: nachchhandasyaputrasya (न च्छन्दस्यपुत्रस्य) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas) the above rules causing lengthening or the substitution of long ई for the final vowel of the अङ्ग (stem), do not apply, except in the case of पुत्र।",
    "Sūtra 7.4.36: durasyurdravinasyurvrushanyatirishanyati (दुरस्युर्द्रविणस्युर्वृषण्यतिरिषण्यति) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas) 1. दुरस्यु 2. द्रविणस्यु 3. वृषण्यति and 4. रिषण्यति are irregularly formed",
    "Sūtra 7.4.37: ashvaaghasyaat (अश्वाघस्यात्) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas) long आ is substituted for the final of 1. अश्व and 2. अघ before the Denominative क्यच् ।",
    "Sūtra 7.4.38: devasumnayoryajushikaathake (देवसुम्नयोर्यजुषि काठके) — Long आ is substituted for the final of देव and सुम्न before the Denominative क्यच् in यजुष काठक।",
    "Sūtra 7.4.39: kavyadhvaraprutanasyarchilopah (कव्यध्वरपृतनस्यर्चि लोपः) — In the ऋग् वेद the final of 1. कवि 2. अध्वर and 3. पृतना is dropped before the Denominative affix क्यच् ।",
    "Sūtra 7.4.40: dyatisyatimaasthaamittikiti (द्यतिस्यतिमास्थामित्ति किति) — Short इ is substituted for the final of 1. दो 2. सो 3. मा and 4. स्था before an affix beginning with त् and having an indicatory क् ।",
    "Sūtra 7.4.41: shaachhoranyatarasyaam (शाच्छोरन्यतरस्याम्) — Short इ is optionally substituted for the final of 1. शा (शो) and 2. छा (छो) before an affix beginning with त् and having an indicatory क् ।",
    "Sūtra 7.4.42: dadhaaterhih (दधातेर्हिः) — हि is optionally substituted for धा (दधाति) before an affix beginning with त् and having an indicatory क् ।",
    "Sūtra 7.4.43: jahaateshchaktvi (जहातेश्च क्त्वि) — हि is optionally substituted for हा (जहाति) before क्त्वा।",
    "Sūtra 7.4.44: vibhaashaachhandasi (विभाषा छन्दसि) — हि is optionally substituted for हा (जहाति) before क्त्वा in the छन्दस् (Vedas).",
    "Sūtra 7.4.45: sudhitavasudhitanemadhitadhishvadhisheeyacha (सुधितवसुधितनेमधितधिष्वधिषीय च) — These five Vedic forms are irregularly formed - 1. सुधित 2. वसुधित 3. नेमधित 4. धिष्व and 3. धिषीय।",
    "Sūtra 7.4.46: dodadghoh (दो दद् घोः) — For दा , when it is a घु - दाधा घ्वदाप् [[1.1.20]], there is substituted दद् before a कित् affix beginning with त् ।",
    "Sūtra 7.4.47: achupasargaattah (अच उपसर्गात्तः) — त् is substituted for the घु - दाधा घ्वदाप् [[1.1.20]], before a कित् affix beginning with त when a preposition ending in a vowel preceded it.",
    "Sūtra 7.4.48: apobhi (अपो भि) — त् is substituted for the final of the अङ्ग (stem) अप् before a case-ending beginning with भ्।",
    "Sūtra 7.4.49: sahasyaarddhadhaatuke (सः स्यार्द्धधातुके) — त् is substituted for the final स् of a root before an आर्द्धधातुक affix beginning with a स्।",
    "Sūtra 7.4.50: taasastyorlopah (तासस्त्योर्लोपः) — The final स् of तास् (the character of the second future) and अस् 'to be' is elided before an affix beginning with स् ।",
    "Sūtra 7.4.51: richa (रि च) — The final स् of तास् (the character of the second future) and अस् 'to be' is elided before an affix beginning with र्।",
    "Sūtra 7.4.52: heti (ह एति) — The स् of तास् (the character of the second future) and अस् 'to be' is substituted ह् before the personal-ending ए।",
    "Sūtra 7.4.53: yeevarnayordeedheevevyoh (यीवर्णयोर्दीधीवेव्योः) — The final of दीधी and वेवी falls before an affix beginning with य् , इ or ई।",
    "Sūtra 7.4.54: sanimeemaaghurabhalabhashakapatapadaamachis (सनि मीमाघुरभलभशकपतपदामच इस्) — इस् is substituted for the root-vowel of 1. मी 2. मा 3. धा (घु) 4. रभ् 5. लभ् 6. शक् 7. पत् 8. पद् and 9. दा when the Desiderative सन् follows beginning with स् (i.e. not taking the augment इ) follows.",
    "Sūtra 7.4.55: aapjnyapyrudhaameet (आप्ज्ञप्यृधामीत्) — For the vowel of the roots 1. आप् 2. ज्ञपि and 3. ऋध् there is substituted long ई before सन् of the Desiderative when it begins with स्।",
    "Sūtra 7.4.56: dambhichcha (दम्भ इच्च) — For the vowel of the root दम्भ् there is substituted इ as well as ई before सन् of the Desiderative when it begins with स्।",
    "Sūtra 7.4.57: muchokarmakasyagunovaa (मुचोऽकर्मकस्य गुणो वा) — When मुच् has an Intransitive signification गुण is optionally substituted for its vowel before the अनिट् सन् of the Desiderative.",
    "Sūtra 7.4.58: atralopobhyaasasya (अत्र लोपोऽभ्यासस्य) — The reduplicate is elided under the circumstances mentioned in the foregoing sūtras सनि मीमाघुरभलभशकपतपदामच इस् [[7.4.54]] to मुचोऽकर्मकस्य गुणो वा [[7.4.57]].",
    "Sūtra 7.4.59: hrasvah (ह्रस्वः) — A short is substituted for the long vowel of the reduplicate.",
    "Sūtra 7.4.60: halaadihasheshah (हलादिः शेषः) — Of the consonants of the reduplicate, only the first is retained, the remainders are elided.",
    "Sūtra 7.4.61: sharpoorvaahakhayah (शर्पूर्वाः खयः) — Of a reduplicate, the hard compound (aspirate and un-aspirate) when preceded by a sibilant, are only retained, the other consonants are elided.",
    "Sūtra 7.4.62: kuhoshchuh (कुहोश्चुः) — For the guttural and ह् of a reduplicate there is substituted a Platal.",
    "Sūtra 7.4.63: nakavateryangi (न कवतेर्यङि) — The Palatal is not substituted for the Guttural of the reduplicate of कु (कवते) in the intensive.",
    "Sūtra 7.4.64: krusheshchhandasi (कृषेश्छन्दसि) — The Palatal is not substituted for the Guttural of the reduplicate of कृष् 'to draw' in the छन्दस् (Vedas) when in the Intensive.",
    "Sūtra 7.4.65: daadhartidardhartidardharshibobhootutetiktelarshyaapaneephanatsamsanishyadatkarikratkanikradadbharibhraddavidhvatodavidyutattaritratahasareesrupatamvareevrujanmarmrujyaaganeeganteeticha (दाधर्तिदर्धर्तिदर्धर्षिबोभूतुतेतिक्तेऽलर्ष्यापनीफणत्संसनिष्यदत्करिक्रत्कनिक्रदद्भरिभ्रद्दविध्वतोदविद्युतत्तरित्रतःसरीसृपतंवरीवृजन्मर्मृज्यागनीगन्तीति च) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas) are found the following eighteen irregularly reduplicated forms - 1. दाधर्ति 2. दर्धर्ति 3. दर्धर्षि 4. बोभूतु 5. तेतिक्ते 6. अलर्षि 7. आपनीफणत् 8. संसनिष्यदत् 9. करिक्रत् 10. कनिक्रदत् 11.भरिभ्रत् 12. द्दविध्वतः 13. दविद्युतत् 14. तरित्रतः 15. सरीसृपतम् 16. वरीवृजत् 17. मर्मृज्य and 18. आगनीगन्ति।",
    "Sūtra 7.4.66: urat (उरत्) — अर् -- उरण् रपरः [[1.1.51]] is substituted for the ऋ or ॠ of the reduplicate.",
    "Sūtra 7.4.67: dyutisvaapyohasamprasaaranam (द्युतिस्वाप्योः सम्प्रसारणम्) — There is vocalisation of the half-vowel of the reduplicate of द्युत् and स्वापि (Causative of स्वप्).",
    "Sūtra 7.4.68: vyatholiti (व्यथो लिटि) — There is vocalisation of the half-vowel of the reduplicate of व्यथ् in the लिट् (Perfect Tense).",
    "Sūtra 7.4.69: deerghinahakiti (दीर्घ इणः किति) — A long vowel is substituted in the reduplicate of the root इ (एति) before a personal ending of the लिट् (Perfect Tense), which has an indicatory क्।",
    "Sūtra 7.4.70: ataadeh (अत आदेः) — A long vowel is substituted in the लिट् (Perfect Tense) for the initial अ of the reduplicate.",
    "Sūtra 7.4.71: tasmaannuddvihalah (तस्मान्नुड् द्विहलः) — After such a lengthened आ of the reduplicate there is added the augment नुट् (न्) to the short अ of the root which ends in a double consonant.",
    "Sūtra 7.4.72: ashnoteshcha (अश्नोतेश्च) — After the lengthened आ of the reduplicate of अश् (अश्नोति) comes the augment नुट् (न्) before the short अ in the लिट् (Perfect Tense).",
    "Sūtra 7.4.73: bhavaterah (भवतेरः) — अ is substituted for the vowel of the reduplicate of भू 'to be' in the लिट् (Perfect Tense).",
    "Sūtra 7.4.74: sasoovetinigame (ससूवेति निगमे) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas) ससूव is irregularly formed in the लिट् (Perfect Tense).",
    "Sūtra 7.4.75: nijaamtrayaanaamgunahashlau (निजां त्रयाणां गुणः श्लौ) — गुण is substituted for the vowel of the reduplicate in the Reduplicated Present form (श्लु) of निज् , विज् and विष्।",
    "Sūtra 7.4.76: bhrunyaamit (भृञामित्) — In the Reduplicated Present form (श्लु) of the three roots 1. भृ 2. मा (माङ्) and 3. हा (ओहाङ्), इ is substituted for the vowel of the reduplicate. ",
    "Sūtra 7.4.77: artipipartyoshcha (अर्तिपिपर्त्योश्च) — इ is substituted for the vowel of the reduplicate of ऋ and पृ in the reduplicated Present form.",
    "Sūtra 7.4.78: bahulamchhandasi (बहुलं छन्दसि) — इ is diversely substituted in the छन्दस् (Vedas) for the vowel of the reduplicate, in the Reduplicated Present-form.",
    "Sūtra 7.4.79: sanyatah (सन्यतः) — इ is substituted for the final short अ of the reduplicate in the Desiderative.",
    "Sūtra 7.4.80: ohapuyanjyapare (ओः पुयण्ज्यपरे) — इ is substituted for the final उ or ऊ of a reduplicate before a labial, a semi-vowel and before ज् when अ or आ follows these consonants, in the Desiderative.",
    "Sūtra 7.4.81: sravatishrunotidravatipravatiplavatichyavateenaamvaa (स्रवतिशृणोतिद्रवतिप्रवतिप्लवतिच्यवतीनां वा) — इ is optionally substituted for the final उ of a reduplicate of 1. स्रु 2. श्रु 3. द्रु 4. प्रु 5. प्लु and 6. च्यु when the semi-vowel is followed by a अ or आ in the Desiderative.",
    "Sūtra 7.4.82: gunoyanglukoh (गुणो यङ्लुकोः) — गुण is substituted for the final of इ and उ (with their long) of a reduplicate when the Intensive character यङ् follows and also when it is elided.",
    "Sūtra 7.4.83: deerghokitah (दीर्घोऽकितः) — A long vowel is substituted for the अ of the reduplicate in the Intensive (with expressed or elided यङ्) when the reduplicate receives no augment having an indicatory क् ।",
    "Sūtra 7.4.84: neegvanychusramsudhvamsubhramsukasapatapadaskandaam (नीग्वञ्चुस्रंसुध्वंसुभ्रंसुकसपतपदस्कन्दाम्) — The augment नीक् is added to the reduplicate of the Intensive (with expressed or elided यङ्) in the following - 1. वञ्च् 2. संस्र 3. ध्वंस् 3. भ्रंश् 4. कस् 5. पत् 6. पद् and 7. स्कन्द्।",
    "Sūtra 7.4.85: nugatonunaasikaantasya (नुगतोऽनुनासिकान्तस्य) — The augment नुक् (न्) is added after the short अ of a reduplicate in the Intensive (with expressed or elided यङ्) when the root ends in a nasal.",
    "Sūtra 7.4.86: japajabhadahadashabhanyjapashaamcha (जपजभदहदशभञ्जपशां च) — The augment नुक् (न्) comes after the reduplicates of 1. जप 2. जभ 3. दह 4. दश 5. भञ्ज and 6. पश in the Intensive (with expressed or elided यङ्).",
    "Sūtra 7.4.87: charaphaloshcha (चरफलोश्च) — The augment नुक् (न्) comes after the reduplicates of चर् and फल् in the Intensive (with expressed or elided यङ्).",
    "Sūtra 7.4.88: utparasyaatah (उत् परस्यातः) — For the subsequent अ (i.e. for the अ of the root and not of the reduplicate), there is substituted उ in the Intensive (with expressed or elided यङ्).",
    "Sūtra 7.4.89: ticha (ति च) — उ is substituted for the vowel of चर् and फल् before an affix beginning with त्।",
    "Sūtra 7.4.90: reegrudupadhasyacha (रीगृदुपधस्य च) — The reduplicate of a root which has ऋ at the penultimate position, gets the augment री in the Intensive (with expressed or elided यङ्).",
    "Sūtra 7.4.91: rugrikauchaluki (रुग्रिकौ च लुकि) — The augments come after the reduplicate of a root which has ऋ at the penultimate position, only when the यङ् of the Intensive is elided.",
    "Sūtra 7.4.92: rutashcha (ऋतश्च) — The reduplicate of a root which ends in short ऋ gets, in the Intensive without यङ् the above augments (1. रीक् 2. रुक् and 3. रिक्), 1. रि 2. र् and 3. रि।",
    "Sūtra 7.4.93: sanvallaghunichangparenaglope (सन्वल्लघुनि चङ्परेऽनग्लोपे) — In the reduplicated Aorist of the Causative, the reduplicate adapts itself to that of the Desiderative when the vowel of the root is light and the root has not lost its end-vowel before the Causative affix.",
    "Sūtra 7.4.94: deergholaghoh (दीर्घो लघोः) — In the reduplicative syllable, a prosodially short vowel is lengthened in the reduplicated Aorist of the Causative when the vowel of the root is light and the root has not lost its end-vowel before the Causative णि।",
    "Sūtra 7.4.95: atsmrudrutvaraprathamradastruspashaam (अत् स्मृदॄत्वरप्रथम्रदस्तॄस्पशाम्) — Short अ is substituted for the vowel of the reduplicate in the reduplicated Aorist of the Causative of the roots 1. स्मृ 2. दॄ 3. त्वर 4. प्रथ 5. म्रद 6. स्तॄ and 7. स्पश्।",
    "Sūtra 7.4.96: vibhaashaaveshticheshtyoh (विभाषा वेष्टिचेष्ट्योः) — Short अ is optionally substituted for the vowel of the reduplicate in the reduplicated Aorist of the Causative of वेष्ट् and चेष्ट्।",
    "Sūtra 7.4.97: eechaganah (ई च गणः) — In the reduplicated Aorist of the Causative, ई is substituted optionally for the vowel of the reduplicate in गण्।",
    "Sūtra 8.1.1: sarvasyadve (सर्वस्य द्वे) — From here up to यथास्वे यथायथम् [[8.1.15]], inclusive, is to be supplied always the phrase 'the whole word is repeated'.",
    "Sūtra 8.1.2: tasyaparamaamreditam (तस्य परमाम्रेडितम्) — Of that which is twice uttered, the latter form is called अम्रेडित (repeated).",
    "Sūtra 8.1.3: anudaattamcha (अनुदात्तं च) — That which is called अम्रेडित (repeated) is gravely accented.",
    "Sūtra 8.1.4: nityaveepsayoh (नित्यवीप्सयोः) — The whole word is अम्रेडित (repeated) when the sense is of 'always' and 'each'.",
    "Sūtra 8.1.5: parervarjane (परेर्वर्जने) — The word परि is repeated when used in the sense of 'with the exception or exclusion of''.",
    "Sūtra 8.1.6: prasamupodahapaadapoorane (प्रसमुपोदः पादपूरणे) — 1. प्र 2. सम् 3. उ and 4. उत् are repeated when by so doubling, the foot of a verse is completed.",
    "Sūtra 8.1.7: uparyadhyadhasahasaameepye (उपर्यध्यधसः सामीप्ये) — 1. उपरि 2. अधि and 3. अधस् are repeated when it expresses uninterrupted nearness.",
    "Sūtra 8.1.8: vaakyaaderaamantritasyaasooyaasammatikopakutsanabhartsaneshu (वाक्यादेरामन्त्रितस्यासूयासम्मतिकोपकुत्सनभर्त्सनेषु) — A Vocative, at the beginning of a sentence, is repeated, when envy, praise, anger, blame, or threat is meant by the speaker.",
    "Sūtra 8.1.9: ekambahuvreehivat (एकं बहुव्रीहिवत्) — When एक is repeated, it is treated like a member of a बहुव्रीहि समास ।",
    "Sūtra 8.1.10: aabaadhecha (आबाधे च) — A word is repeated and is treated like a member of a बहुव्रीहि समास when a mental distress over something is expressed.",
    "Sūtra 8.1.11: karmadhaarayavatuttareshu (कर्मधारयवत् उत्तरेषु) — In the following rules, the double-word is treated like a कर्मधारय समास ।",
    "Sūtra 8.1.12: prakaaregunavachanasya (प्रकारे गुणवचनस्य) — An adjective is repeated, when it is meant to express that the said attribute belongs to a thing only to a limited degree and the double word is treated like a कर्मधारय समास ।",
    "Sūtra 8.1.13: akruchchhrepriyasukhayoranyatarasyaam (अकृच्छ्रे प्रियसुखयोरन्यतरस्याम्) — The words प्रिय and सुख are repeated optionally when they mean 'easily, without any difficulty'.",
    "Sūtra 8.1.14: yathaasveyathaayatham (यथास्वे यथायथम्) — The word यथायथम् is irregularly formed in the sense of 'respectively, fitly, properly'.",
    "Sūtra 8.1.15: dvandvamrahasyamaryaadaavachanavyutkramanayajnyapaatraprayogaabhivyaktishu (द्वन्द्वं रहस्यमर्यादावचनव्युत्क्रमणयज्ञपात्रप्रयोगाभिव्यक्तिषु) — The word द्वन्द्वम् is irregularly formed in the sense of 'secret' and when it expresses a 'limit', 'a separation', 'employing in a sacrificial vessel' and 'manifestation'.",
    "Sūtra 8.1.16: padasya (पदस्य) — Up to इडाया वा [[8.3.54]], inclusive, should be always supplied in every subsequent sūtra the phrase 'of a word' or 'to the whole of a word'.",
    "Sūtra 8.1.17: padaat (पदात्) — Up to सगतिरपि तिङ् [[8.1.68]], inclusive, should always be supplied the phrase 'after a पद'.",
    "Sūtra 8.1.18: anudaattamsarvamapaadaadau (अनुदात्तं सर्वमपादादौ) — Up to (सामान्यवचनं) विभाषितं विशेषवचने (बहुवचनम्) [[8.1.74]], inclusive, should always be supplied the phrase 'the whole is unaccented, if it does not stand at the beginning of the foot of a verse'.",
    "Sūtra 8.1.19: aamantritasyacha (आमन्त्रितस्य च) — All the syllables of the Vocative Case are unaccented when a word precedes them and they do not stand at the beginning of a hemistich.",
    "Sūtra 8.1.20: yushmadasmadohashashtheechaturtheedviteeyaasthayorvaannaavau (युष्मदस्मदोः षष्ठीचतुर्थीद्वितीयास्थयोर्वान्नावौ) — dual of युष्मद् and अस्मद् are substituted वाम and नौ respectively ।",
    "Sūtra 8.1.21: bahuvachanevasnasau (बहुवचनस्य वस्नसौ) — For (the Genitive 6th-Case, Dative -4th Case and Accusative -2nd case) plural of युष्मद् and अस्मद् are substituted वस् and नस् respectively (when a word precedes and these substitutes are अनुदात्त).",
    "Sūtra 8.1.22: temayaavekavachanasya (तेमयावेकवचनस्य) — For the Genitive 6th-Case and Dative -4th Case singular (of युष्मद् and अस्मद् are substituted) ते and मे respectively (when a word precedes and these substitutes are अनुदात्त).",
    "Sūtra 8.1.23: tvaamaudviteeyaayaah (त्वामौ द्वितीयायाः) — For the Accusative -2nd case singular of युष्मद् and अस्मद् are substituted त्वा and मा respectively (when a word precedes and these substitutes are अनुदात्त).",
    "Sūtra 8.1.24: nachavaahaahaivayukte (न चवाहाहैवयुक्ते) — when there is in connection with the सर्वनाम any of these - 1. च 'and' 2. वा 'or' 3. ह 'Oh!' 4. अह 'wonderful' or 5. एव 'only'.",
    "Sūtra 8.1.25: pashyaarthaishchaanaalochane (पश्यार्थैश्चानालोचने) — The above substitutions do not take place also in connection with verbs having the sense of 'seeing' when physical seeing is not denoted.",
    "Sūtra 8.1.26: sapoorvaayaahaprathamaayaavibhaashaa (सपूर्वायाः प्रथमाया विभाषा) — When the सर्वनाम follows a Nominative 1st-Case, which itself is preceded by another word, then the above substitutions may take place optionally.",
    "Sūtra 8.1.27: tingogotraadeenikutsanaabheekshnyayoh (तिङो गोत्रादीनि कुत्सनाभीक्ष्ण्ययोः) — The words गोत्र etc. become unaccented after a finite verb when a contempt or a repetition in intended.",
    "Sūtra 8.1.28: tingngatingah (तिङ्ङतिङः) — A finite verb is unaccented when a word precedes it which is not a finite verb.",
    "Sūtra 8.1.29: nalut (न लुट्) — By the लुट् (Periphrastic Future) is not unaccented when it is preceded by a word which is not a finite verb.",
    "Sūtra 8.1.30: nipaatairyadyadihantakuvinnechchechchankachchidyatrayuktam (निपातैर्यद्यदिहन्तकुविन्नेच्चेच्चण्कच्चिद्यत्रयुक्तम्) — The finite verb retains its accent in connection with the particles 1. यत् 'that', 'because' 2. यदि 'if' 3. हन्त 'also', 'O!' 4. कुवित् 'well' 5. नेत् 'not' 6. चेत् 'if' 7. च 'if' 8. कच्चित् (interrogative particle implying 'I hope' or 'I hope not') and 9. यत्र 'where'. ",
    "Sūtra 8.1.31: nahapratyaarambhe (नह प्रत्यारम्भे) — The finite verb retains its accent in connection with नह when used in the sense of forbidding.",
    "Sūtra 8.1.32: satyamprashne (सत्यं प्रश्ने) — The finite verb retains its accent in connection with सत्य when used in asking a question.",
    "Sūtra 8.1.33: anggaapraatilomye (अङ्गाप्रातिलोम्ये) — The finite verb retains its accent in connection with अङ्ग when used in a friendly assertion.",
    "Sūtra 8.1.34: hicha (हि च) — The finite verb retains its accent in connection with हि when used in a friendly assertion.",
    "Sūtra 8.1.35: chhandasyanekamapisaakaangksham (छन्दस्यनेकमपि साकाङ्क्षम्) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas), the finite verb retains its accent (but not always) in connection with हि when it stands in correlation to another verb, even more than one.",
    "Sūtra 8.1.36: yaavadyathaabhyaam (यावद्यथाभ्याम्) — The finite verb retains its accent in connection with यावत् and यथा।",
    "Sūtra 8.1.37: poojaayaamnaanantaram (पूजायां नानन्तरम्) — But not so when these particles यावत् and यथा immediately precede the verb an denote 'praise'.",
    "Sūtra 8.1.38: upasargavyapetamcha (उपसर्गव्यपेतं च) — A finite verb loses its accent when it denotes 'praise' and is joined immediately with यावत् and यथा through the intervention of an उपसर्ग (verbal Preposition).",
    "Sūtra 8.1.39: tupashyapashyataahaihapoojaayaam (तुपश्यपश्यताहैः पूजायाम्) — The finite verb retains its accent in connection with 1. तु 2. पश्य 3. पश्यत and 4. अह when meaning 'praise'.",
    "Sūtra 8.1.40: ahocha (अहो च) — The finite verb retains its accent in connection with अहो when meaning 'praise'.",
    "Sūtra 8.1.41: sheshevibhaashaa (शेषे विभाषा) — The finite verb optionally retains its accent in connection with अहो in the remaining cases (i.e. where it does not mean 'praise').",
    "Sūtra 8.1.42: puraachapareepsaayaam (पुरा च परीप्सायाम्) — The finite verb optionally retains its accent in connection with पुरा when it means 'haste' (i.e. when पुरा means 'before').",
    "Sūtra 8.1.43: nanvityanujnyaishanaayaam (नन्वित्यनुज्ञैषणायाम्) — The finite verb optionally retains its accent in connection with ननु when with this particle, permission is asked.",
    "Sūtra 8.1.44: kimkriyaaprashnenupasargamapratishiddham (किं क्रियाप्रश्नेऽनुपसर्गमप्रतिषिद्धम्) — The finite verb optionally retains its accent in connection with किम् when with this is asked a question relating to an action and when the verb is not preceded by a preposition or a negation.",
    "Sūtra 8.1.45: lopevibhaashaa (लोपे विभाषा) — When however किम् is not added in asking such a question, the finite verb may optionally retain its accent.",
    "Sūtra 8.1.46: ehimanyeprahaaselrut (एहिमन्ये प्रहासे लृट्) — In connection with एहिमन्ये used diversely in the लृट् (I Future) that follows it, retains its accent.",
    "Sūtra 8.1.47: jaatvapoorvam (जात्वपूर्वम्) — The finite verb optionally retains its accent after जातु when this जातु is not preceded by another word.",
    "Sūtra 8.1.48: kimvruttamchachiduttaram (किम्वृत्तं च चिदुत्तरम्) — Also after a form of किम् when the particle चित् follows it and when no other word precedes such form of किम् the finite verb retains its accent.",
    "Sūtra 8.1.49: aahoutaahochaanantaram (आहो उताहो चानन्तरम्) — Also after an immediately preceding आहो and उताहो when these follow, no other word, the verb retains its accent.",
    "Sūtra 8.1.50: sheshevibhaashaa (शेषे विभाषा) — When the above mentioned particles आहो and उताहो do not immediately precede the verb, the verb may optionally retain its accent.",
    "Sūtra 8.1.51: gatyarthalotaalrunnachetkaarakamsarvaanyat (गत्यर्थलोटा लृण्न चेत् कारकं सर्वान्यत्) — The लृट् (I Future) retains its accent in connection with the Imperative of a verb denoting 'motion' ('to go', 'to come', 'to start' etc.) but only in that case, when the subject and object of both the verbs are not wholly different one from another.",
    "Sūtra 8.1.52: lotcha (लोट् च) — Also an लोट् (Imperative Mood), following after an Imperative of verbs of 'motion' retains its accent when the subject or object of both the verbs is not wholly different.",
    "Sūtra 8.1.53: vibhaashitamsopasargamanuttamam (विभाषितं सोपसर्गमनुत्तमम्) — An Imperative preceded by a preposition and not in the 1st person, following an Imperative of verbs of 'motion', may optionally retain its accent when the कारक is not wholly different.",
    "Sūtra 8.1.54: hantacha (हन्त च) — An Imperative with a preposition preceding it, may optionally retain its accent, in connection with हन्त , but not in the 1st person.",
    "Sūtra 8.1.55: aamekaantaramaamantritamanantike (आम एकान्तरमामन्त्रितमनन्तिके) — After आम् , but separated from it by not more than one word, the Vocative retains its accent when the person addressed is not near.",
    "Sūtra 8.1.56: yaddhituparamchhandasi (यद्धितुपरं छन्दसि) — A finite verb followed by यत् or हि or तु retains its accent in the छन्दस् (Vedas).",
    "Sūtra 8.1.57: chanachidivagotraaditaddhitaamrediteshvagateh (चनचिदिवगोत्रादितद्धिताम्रेडितेष्वगतेः) — A finite verb retains its accent when it is not preceded by a गति Particle -- गतिश्च [[1.4.60]] etc., and when it is followed by 1. चन 2. चिद् 3. इव 4. गोत्र etc., a तद्धित affix, or by its own doubled form.",
    "Sūtra 8.1.58: chaadishucha (चादिषु च) — A finite verb, not preceded by a गति , retains its accent before the particles च (1. वा 2. ह 3. अह and 4. एव -- न चवाहाहैवयुक्ते [[8.1.24]]).",
    "Sūtra 8.1.59: chavaayogeprathamaa (चवायोगे प्रथमा) — The first finite verb only retains its accent in connection with च and वा।",
    "Sūtra 8.1.60: hetikshiyaayaam (हेति क्षियायाम्) — In connection with ह , the first finite verb retains its accent when an offence against custom is reprimanded.",
    "Sūtra 8.1.61: ahetiviniyogecha (अहेति विनियोगे च) — In connection with अह , the first finite verb retains its accent when it refers to various commissions (as well as when a breach of good manners is condemned).",
    "Sūtra 8.1.62: chaahalopevetyavadhaaranam (चाहलोप एवेत्यवधारणम्) — When च and अह are elided, the first finite verb still retains its accent when एव with the force of limitation, takes their place.",
    "Sūtra 8.1.63: chaadilopevibhaashaa (चादिलोपे विभाषा) — When च (1. वा 2. ह 3. अह and 4. एव -- न चवाहाहैवयुक्ते [[8.1.24]]) are elided the first verb optionally retains its accent.",
    "Sūtra 8.1.64: vaivaavetichachchhandasi (वैवावेति च च्छन्दसि) — Also in connection with वै and वाव , may optionally, in the छन्दस् (Vedas), the first verb retains its accent.",
    "Sūtra 8.1.65: ekaanyaabhyaamsamarthaabhyaam (एकान्याभ्यां समर्थाभ्याम्) — Also in connection with एक and अन्य , optionally in the छन्दस् (Vedas), the first verb retains its accent, when these word have the same meaning ('the one - the other').",
    "Sūtra 8.1.66: yadvruttaannityam (यद्वृत्तान्नित्यम्) — In connection with यद् in all its forms, the verb retains its accent always.",
    "Sūtra 8.1.67: poojanaatpoojitamanudaattamkaashthaadibhyah (पूजनात् पूजितमनुदात्तं काष्ठादिभ्यः) — After a word denoting praise belonging to काष्ठादि class the word whose praise is denoted, becomes अनुदात्त ।",
    "Sūtra 8.1.68: sagatirapiting (सगतिरपि तिङ्) — (After such words denoting praise) the finite verb (which is praised) becomes अनुदात्त even along with the गति , if any, that may precede it.",
    "Sūtra 8.1.69: kutsanechasupyagotraadau (कुत्सने च सुप्यगोत्रादौ) — A finite verb along with its preceding गति , if any, become अनुदात्त when a noun denoting the fault of the action follows, with the exception of गोत्र etc.",
    "Sūtra 8.1.70: gatirgatau (गतिर्गतौ) — A गति becomes unaccented when followed by another गति .",
    "Sūtra 8.1.71: tingichodaattavati (तिङि चोदात्तवति) — A गति becomes अनुदात्त when followed by an accented finite verb.",
    "Sūtra 8.1.72: aamantritampoorvamavidyamaanavat (आमन्त्रितं पूर्वमविद्यमानवत्) — A preceding Vocative is considered as non-existent (for the purposes of the accent of the following word and the enclitic forms of युष्मद् and अस्मद्).",
    "Sūtra 8.1.73: naamantritesamaanaadhikaranesaamaanyavachanam (नामन्त्रिते समानाधिकरणे सामान्यवचनम्) — A preceding Vocative, when it conveys a general idea, is not to be considered as if non-existent for the purposes of the subsequent Vocative, which stands in apposition with the former.",
    "Sūtra 8.1.74: vibhaashitamvisheshavachanebahuvachanam (विभाषितं विशेषवचने बहुवचनम्) — When the preceding Vocative is in the plural number, it is optionally considered as non-existent, if the subsequent Vocative, in apposition with it, is a specific term.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.1: poorvatraasiddham (पूर्वत्रासिद्धम्) — Whatever will be taught hereafter, up to the end of the work, is to be considered as not taken effect, in relation to the application of a preceding rule.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.2: nalopahasupsvarasamjnyaatugvidhishukruti (नलोपः सुप्स्वरसंज्ञातुग्विधिषु कृति) — The elision of a final न् -- नलोपः प्रातिपदिकान्तस्य [[8.2.7]], is considered as if not to have taken effect, in applying the following rules - 1. rules regarding case-endings 2. rules regarding accents 3. rules regarding any technical term of Grammar and 4. rules regarding the augment त् before a कृत् affix.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.3: namune (न मु ने) — The sūtra अदसोऽसेर्दादु दो मः [[8.2.80]], teaching the substitution of मु for the दस् of the pronoun अदस् is however not treated as असिद्ध in relation to the case-ending ना।",
    "Sūtra 8.2.4: udaattasvaritayoryanahasvaritonudaattasya (उदात्तस्वरितयोर्यणः स्वरितोऽनुदात्तस्य) — A स्वरित vowel is the substitute of an अनुदात्त vowel when the latter follows after such a semi-vowel which has replaced an उदात्त (acute accent) or a स्वरित vowel.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.5: ekaadeshudaattenodaattah (एकादेश उदात्तेनोदात्तः) — The single substitute of an unaccented with an उदात्त (acute accent) vowel is उदात्त।",
    "Sūtra 8.2.6: svaritovaanudaattepadaadau (स्वरितो वाऽनुदात्ते पदादौ) — The single substitute of an unaccented vowel standing at the beginning of a word, with an उदात्त (acute accent) vowel may optionally be a स्वरित or उदात्त (acute accent).",
    "Sūtra 8.2.7: nalopahapraatipadikaantasya (नलोपः प्रातिपदिकान्तस्य) — The न् at the end of a nominal-stem, which is a पद -- शेषो घ्यसखि [[1.4.7]], is elided.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.8: nangisambuddhyoh (न ङिसम्बुद्ध्योः) — (But such न्) is not elided in the Locative -7th case and Vocative Case singular.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.9: maadupadhaayaashchamatorvoyavaadibhyah (मादुपधायाश्च मतोर्वोऽयवादिभ्यः) — For the म् of the affix मत् is substituted व if the अङ्ग (stem) ends in म् or अ ( and आ) or if these are in the penultimate position; but not after यव etc.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.10: jhayah (झयः) — The व् is substituted for the म् of मत् after a अङ्ग (stem) ending in a mute consonant.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.11: samjnyaayaam (संज्ञायाम्) — The व् is substituted for the म् of मत् when the word so formed is a Name.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.12: aasandeevadashtheevachchakreevatkaksheevadrumanvachcharmanvatee (आसन्दीवदष्ठीवच्चक्रीवत्कक्षीवद्रुमण्वच्चर्मण्वती) — The following names are irregularly formed 1. आसन्दीवत् 2. अष्ठीवत् 3. चक्रीवत् 4. कक्षीवत् 5. रुमण्वत् and 6. चर्मण्वती। (Reference श्लोक - आसन्दीवति धान्यादं रुक्मिणं हरितस्रजम्। अश्वं बबन्ध सारङ्गं देवेभ्यो अनमेजयः।)",
    "Sūtra 8.2.13: udanvaanudadhaucha (उदन्वानुदधौ च) — The word उदन्वान् is irregularly formed in the sense of 'a sea'.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.14: raajanvaansauraajye (राजन्वान् सौराज्ये) — Also राजन्वान् when the sense is of a good government.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.15: chhandaseerah (छन्दसीरः) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas) व् is substituted for the म् of मत् after a अङ्ग (stem) ending in इ (or ई) or र्।",
    "Sūtra 8.2.16: anonut (अनो नुट्) — The affix मत् gets the augment नुट् in the छन्दस् (Vedas) after a अङ्ग (stem) ending in अन्।",
    "Sūtra 8.2.17: naadghasya (नाद्घस्य) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas) the affixes तर and तम get the augment नुट् after a stem in न्।",
    "Sūtra 8.2.18: kruporolah (कृपो रो लः) — For the र् of the root कृप् there is substituted ल्।",
    "Sūtra 8.2.19: upasargasyaayatau (उपसर्गस्यायतौ) — ल् is substituted for the र् of a preposition when अयते follows.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.20: groyangi (ग्रो यङि) — ल् is substituted for the र् of गॄ in the intensive.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.21: achivibhaashaa (अचि विभाषा) — र् is optionally changed to ल् before an affix beginning with a vowel.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.22: pareshchaghaangkayoh (परेश्च घाङ्कयोः) — The र् of परि is changed to ल् before घ and अङ्क।",
    "Sūtra 8.2.23: samyogaantasyalopah (संयोगान्तस्य लोपः) — When a word ends in a double consonant the last consonant is dropped.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.24: raatsasya (रात्सस्य) — Of a word ending in a conjunct consonant, only स् is elided if it comes after र् (but any other consonant coming after र् is not elided).",
    "Sūtra 8.2.25: dhicha (धि च) — The स् is elided before an affix beginning with ध।",
    "Sūtra 8.2.26: jhalojhali (झलो झलि) — The स् is elided when it is preceded by a झल् consonant (all consonant except semi-vowels and nasals) and is followed by an affix beginning with a झल् consonant.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.27: hrasvaadanggaat (ह्रस्वादङ्गात्) — The स् is elided before an affix beginning with झल् consonant (all consonant except semi-vowels and nasals) when it is preceded by a अङ्ग (stem) ending in a short vowel.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.28: iteeti (इट ईटि) — The स् is elided after the augment इट् if after this स् the augment ईट् follows.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.29: skohasamyogaadyorantecha (स्कोः संयोगाद्योरन्ते च) — The स् or क् , when initial in a conjunct consonant, are elided before a झल् (all consonant except semi-vowels and nasals) affix and at the end of a word.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.30: chohakuh (चोः कुः) — A Guttural is substituted for a palatal before a झल् (all consonant except semi-vowels and nasals) affix or at the end of a word.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.31: hodhah (हो ढः) — ढ is substituted for ह before a झल् (all consonant except semi-vowels and nasals) letter and at the end of a word.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.32: daaderdhaatorghah (दादेर्धातोर्घः) — Of a root beginning with द , the ध is substituted for ह before a झल् (all consonant except semi-vowels and nasals) letter or at the end of a word.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.33: vaadruhamuhashnuhashnihaam (वा द्रुहमुहष्णुहष्णिहाम्) — The ह of 1. द्रुह् 2. मुह् 3.ष्णुह् and 4. ष्णिह् is optionally changed to ध before a झल् (all consonant except semi-vowels and nasals) letter or at the end of a word.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.34: nahodhah (नहो धः) — The ह of नह् is changed to ध before a before a झल् (all consonant except semi-vowels and nasals) letter or at the end of a word.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.35: aahasthah (आहस्थः) — For the ह of the root आह् there is substituted थ before a झल् (all consonant except semi-vowels and nasals) letter.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.36: vrashchabhrasjasrujamrujayajaraajabhraajachchhashaamshah (व्रश्चभ्रस्जसृजमृजयजराजभ्राजच्छशां षः) — For the final consonants of 1. व्रश्च् 2. भ्रस्ज् 3. सृज् 4. मृज् 5. यज् 6. राज् and 7. भ्राज् and for the final छ and श , there is substituted ष् or at the end of a word.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.37: ekaachobashobhashjhashantasyasdhvoh (एकाचो बशो भष् झषन्तस्य स्ध्वोः) — For the letters 1. ब 2. ग 3. ड or 4. द in the beginning of a mono-syllable and belonging to a root, and which ends in 1. झ 2. भ 3. घ 4. ढ or 5. ध there is substituted 1. भ 2. घ 3. ढ or 4. ध respectively before स् or ध्व or at the end of a word.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.38: dadhastathoshcha (दधस्तथोश्च) — For the द of दध (the reduplicated form of धा) is substituted ध before the affixes beginning with त, थ, स and before ध्वम्।",
    "Sūtra 8.2.39: jhalaamjashonte (झलां जशोऽन्ते) — A corresponding ज, ब, ग, ड or द is substituted for all consonants (with the exception of semi-vowels and nasals) at the end of a word.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.40: jhashastathordhodhah (झषस्तथोर्धोऽधः) — ध is substituted for त or थ coming after झष् (झ, भ, घ, ढ, ध) but not after the root धा (दध).",
    "Sūtra 8.2.41: shadhohakahasi (षढोः कः सि) — क is substituted for ष or ढ before स।",
    "Sūtra 8.2.42: radaabhyaamnishthaatonahapoorvasyachadah (रदाभ्यां निष्ठातो नः पूर्वस्य च दः) — After र and द for the त of the Participial suffix त and तवत् there is substituted न and the same substitution takes place also for the preceding द।",
    "Sūtra 8.2.43: samyogaaderaatodhaatoryanvatah (संयोगादेरातो धातोर्यण्वतः) — For the त of the निष्ठा there is substituted न after a root ending in आ and commencing with a conjunct consonant, if the latter contains a semi-vowel.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.44: lvaadibhyah (ल्वादिभ्यः) — For the त of the निष्ठा there is substituted न after the roots लू and those that follow it.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.45: oditashcha (ओदितश्च) — For the त of the निष्ठा there is substituted न after a root which has an indicatory ओ in the धातुपाठ।",
    "Sūtra 8.2.46: kshiyodeerghaat (क्षियो दीर्घात्) — For the त of the निष्ठा there is substituted न after क्षि when the root-vowel is lengthened.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.47: shyosparshe (श्योऽस्पर्शे) — The निष्ठा त is changed to न after श्यै but not when the participle denotes 'cold'.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.48: anychonapaadaane (अञ्चोऽनपादाने) — The निष्ठा त is changed to न after अञ्च् but not when it is in connection with an Ablative -5th case.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.49: divovijigeeshaayaam (दिवोऽविजिगीषायाम्) — The निष्ठा त is changed to न after दिव् when the sense is not that of 'play'.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.50: nirvaanovaate (निर्वाणोऽवाते) — The word निर्वाण is irregularly formed by changing the निष्ठा त is changed to न when the sense is not that of 'wind'.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.51: shushahakah (शुषः कः) — क is substituted for the निष्ठा त after the root शुष्।",
    "Sūtra 8.2.52: pachovah (पचो वः) — व is substituted for the निष्ठा त after the root पच् 'to cook' ।",
    "Sūtra 8.2.53: kshaayomah (क्षायो मः) — म is substituted for the निष्ठा त after the root क्षै।",
    "Sūtra 8.2.54: prastyonyatarasyaam (प्रस्त्योऽन्यतरस्याम्) — म is optionally substituted for the निष्ठा त after the root स्तयै preceded by प्र।",
    "Sūtra 8.2.55: anupasargaatphullaksheebakrushollaaghaah (अनुपसर्गात् फुल्लक्षीबकृशोल्लाघाः) — The irregular participles 1. फुल्ल 2. क्षीब 3. कृश and 4. उल्लाघ are formed then only, when no preposition precedes them.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.56: nudavidondatraaghraahreebhyonyatarasyaam (नुदविदोन्दत्राघ्राह्रीभ्योऽन्यतरस्याम्) — The निष्ठा त is optionally changed to न after 1. नुद 2. विद 3. उन्द 4. त्रा 5. घ्रा and 6. ह्री।",
    "Sūtra 8.2.57: nadhyaakhyaaprumoorchhimadaam (न ध्याख्यापॄमूर्छिमदाम्) — The निष्ठा त is not changed to न after 1. ध्या 2. ख्या 3. पॄ 4. मूर्छि and 5. मद।",
    "Sūtra 8.2.58: vittobhogapratyayayoh (वित्तो भोगप्रत्यययोः) — The irregularly formed participle वित्त denotes 'possessions' and 'renowned'.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.59: bhittamshakalam (भित्तं शकलम्) — The word भित्त is irregularly formed in the sense of 'a fragment, a portion'.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.60: runamaadhamarnye (ऋणमाधमर्ण्ये) — The word ऋण is irregularly formed in the sense of 'debt.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.61: nasattanishattaanuttapratoortasoortagoortaanichhandasi (नसत्तनिषत्तानुत्तप्रतूर्तसूर्तगूर्तानि छन्दसि) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas) we have the following irregular participles - 1. नसत्त 2. निषत्त 3. अनुत्त 4. प्रतूर्त 5. सूर्त्त and 6. गूर्त्त।",
    "Sūtra 8.2.62: kvinpratyayasyakuh (क्विन्प्रत्ययस्य कुः) — A अङ्ग (stem) formed with the affix क्विन् under स्पृशोऽनुदके क्विन् [[3.2.58]] etc. substitutes, at the end of a word, a guttural for the final consonant.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.63: nashervaa (नशेर्वा) — The final नश् at the end of a word is optionally changed to guttural.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.64: monodhaatoh (मो नो धातोः) — न is substituted, at the end of a word, for the final म of a root.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.65: mvoshcha (म्वोश्च) — न is substituted for the म of a root before the affixes beginning with म and व।",
    "Sūtra 8.2.66: sasajushoruh (ससजुषो रुः) — For the final स् and for the ष् of ससजुष् is substituted रु , at the end of a word.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.67: avayaahashvetavaahapurodaashcha (अवयाःश्वेतवाःपुरोडाश्च) — The same substitution takes place for the final Nominatives of 1. अवयाः 2. श्वेतवाः and 3. पुरोडाः।",
    "Sūtra 8.2.68: ahan (अहन्) — रु is also substituted for the न् of अहन् at the end of a word.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.69: rosupi (रोऽसुपि) — When no case-ending follows (i.e. at the end of a word, in the narrower sense), र् is substituted for the न् of अहन्।",
    "Sūtra 8.2.70: amnaroodharavarityubhayathaachhandasi (अम्नरूधरवरित्युभयथा छन्दसि) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas), both रु and र् are substituted for the final 1. अमनस् 2. ऊधस् and 3. अवस्।",
    "Sūtra 8.2.71: bhuvashchamahaavyaahruteh (भुवश्च महाव्याहृतेः) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas), both रु and र् may replace the final of the word भुवस् when used as a महाव्याहृति।",
    "Sūtra 8.2.72: vasusramsudhvamsvanaduhaamdah (वसुस्रंसुध्वंस्वनडुहां दः) — द is substituted for the final स् of a word ending in the affix वस् and for the final of 1. स्रंस् 2. ध्वंस् and 3. अनडुह् at the end of a word (in the wider sense निपात एकाजनाङ् [[1.1.14]], उञः [[1.1.17]]).",
    "Sūtra 8.2.73: tipyanasteh (तिप्यनस्तेः) — द is substituted for the final स् of a root with the exception of अस् 'to be' , before the personal ending ति (त्) when it stands at the end of a word.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.74: sipidhaatorurvaa (सिपि धातो रुर्वा) —  द् or रु may optionally be substituted for the स् of a root, , before the personal ending सि (स्) when such स् stands at the end of a word.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.75: dashcha (दश्च) — द् or रु may optionally be substituted for the द् of a root, , before the personal ending सि (स्) when such द् stands at the end of a word.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.76: rvorupadhaayaadeerghikah (र्वोरुपधाया दीर्घ इकः) — A penultimate इ or उ is lengthened, when the र् or व् of a root can stand at the end of a word.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.77: halicha (हलि च) — Of a root ending in र् or व् , the penultimate इ or उ is lengthened before a consonantal beginning affix.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.78: upadhaayaamcha (उपधायां च) — The short इ or उ is lengthened, when the verb has र् or व् as its penultimate letter and is followed by a consonant.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.79: nabhakurchhuraam (न भकुर्छुराम्) — The lengthening of a vowel does not take place under हलि च [[8.2.77]] when the nominal अङ्ग (stem) ending in र् or व् is called भ (i.e. when a य् follows) and also not in कुर् and छुर्।",
    "Sūtra 8.2.80: adasoserdaadudomah (अदसोऽसेर्दादु दो मः) — When the सर्वनाम अदस् does not end in स् then there is substituted उ or ऊ for the vowel after द् , and म् for द्।",
    "Sūtra 8.2.81: eteedbahuvachane (एत ईद्बहुवचने) — For the ए coming after the द् of अदस् , there is substituted ई , and द् is changed to म् when plurality is to be expressed.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.82: vaakyasyatehaplutudaattah (वाक्यस्य टेः प्लुत उदात्तः) — Up to the close of this chapter (पाद), is always to be supplied the words 'the last vowel of a sentence is प्लुत and has the acute'.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.83: pratyabhivaadeshoodre (प्रत्यभिवादेऽशूद्रे) — In answer to a salutation, but not when it refers to शुद्र , the last vowel of a sentence becomes प्लुत and gets an acute accent (उदात्त).",
    "Sūtra 8.2.84: dooraaddhootecha (दूराद्धूते च) — The final vowel of a sentence becomes प्लुत and acutely accented (उदात्त) when used in calling a person from a distance.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.85: haiheprayogehaihayoh (हैहेप्रयोगे हैहयोः) — When the words है and हे are used in addressing a person from a distance, there the है and हे alone get the प्लुत and the accent.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.86: guroranrutonantyasyaapyekaikasyapraachaam (गुरोरनृतोऽनन्त्यस्याप्येकैकस्य प्राचाम्) — In the room of a prosodially long vowel (with the exception of ऋ) though it may not stand at the end, there is substituted a प्लुत for one at a time, under the above circumstances -- प्रत्यभिवादेशूद्रे [[8.2.83]] & दूराद्धूते च [[8.2.84]], in the opinion of Eastern Grammarians.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.87: omabhyaadaane (ओमभ्यादाने) — The vowel in ओम् is प्लुत in the beginning of a sacred text.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.88: yeyajnyakarmani (ये यज्ञकर्मणि) — The vowel of ये becomes प्लुत in a sacred text when it is used in a sacrificial work.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.89: pranavashteh (प्रणवष्टेः) — In a sacrificial work ओ3म् is substituted for the final vowel with the consonant, if any, that may follow it, in a sentence.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.90: yaajyaantah (याज्याऽन्तः) — The last vowel at the end of मन्त्र-s called याज्य , when used in sacrificial works is प्लुत and has the acute accent (उदात्त).",
    "Sūtra 8.2.91: broohipresyashraushadvaushadaavahaanaamaadeh (ब्रूहिप्रेष्यश्रौषड्वौषडावहानामादेः) — In a sacrificial work, the first syllable of 1. ब्रूहि 2. प्रेष्य 3. श्रौषट् and 4.आवह is प्लुत।",
    "Sūtra 8.2.92: agneetpreshaneparasyacha (अग्नीत्प्रेषणे परस्य च) — In an order given to अग्नीध्र priest, the first syllable as well as the succeeding syllable is प्लुत.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.93: vibhaashaaprushtaprativachaneheh (विभाषा पृष्टप्रतिवचने हेः) — हि at the end of an answer to a question may optionally be प्लुत।",
    "Sūtra 8.2.94: nigruhyaanuyogecha (निगृह्यानुयोगे च) — The end syllable of that sentence is optionally प्लुत when it asserts something which has been refuted and is used by the victor by way of censure.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.95: aamreditambhartsane (आम्रेडितं भर्त्सने) — The end syllable of an आम्रेडित Vocative Case is प्लुत when threat is expressed.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.96: anggayuktamtingaakaangksham (अङ्गयुक्तं तिङ् आकाङ्क्षम्) — The final syllable of a finite verb used as a threat becomes प्लुत when the word अङ्ग is joined with it and it demands another sentence to complete the conclusion.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.97: vichaaryamaanaanaam (विचार्यमाणानाम्) — The end syllable of those sentences is प्लुत which denote acts of reflection (or balancing between two alternatives).",
    "Sūtra 8.2.98: poorvamtubhaashaayaam (पूर्वं तु भाषायाम्) — In the common speech, the end vowel of the first alternative is only प्लुत।",
    "Sūtra 8.2.99: pratishravanecha (प्रतिश्रवणे च) — The end syllable of the sentence which expresses assent or promise or listening to, is प्लुत।",
    "Sūtra 8.2.100: anudaattamprashnaantaabhipoojitayoh (अनुदात्तं प्रश्नान्ताभिपूजितयोः) — The end vowel at the end of a question or of a praise is प्लुत, but unaccented.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.101: chiditichopamaartheprayujyamaane (चिदिति चोपमाऽर्थे प्रयुज्यमाने) — The end vowel at the end of a sentence becomes अनुदात्त and प्लुत when the particle चित् is used, denoting comparison.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.102: uparisvidaaseediticha (उपरिस्विदासीदिति च) — In 1. उपरि 2. स्विद् and 3. आसीद् the end vowel is अनुदात्त and प्लुत।",
    "Sūtra 8.2.103: svaritamaamreditesooyaasammatikopakutsaneshu (स्वरितमाम्रेडितेऽसूयासम्मतिकोपकुत्सनेषु) — Of the two Vocatives of the same form standing at the beginning of a sentence, the end vowel of the first becomes प्लुत and स्वरित when envy, praise, anger or blame is expressed.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.104: kshiyaasheehapraisheshutingaakaangksham (क्षियाऽऽशीःप्रैषेषु तिङ् आकाङ्क्षम्) — When an error against polite usage is censured or when a benediction or a bidding is intended, the end syllable of a finite verb becomes प्लुत and स्वरित , if this requires another sentence to complete the sense.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.105: anantyasyaapiprashnaakhyaanayoh (अनन्त्यस्यापि प्रश्नाख्यानयोः) — In a question or narration, the end vowel of a word, though not final in a sentence, becomes प्लुत and स्वरित , as well as the word which is final in a sentence.",
    "Sūtra 8.2.106: plutaavaichidutau (प्लुतावैच इदुतौ) — In forming the प्लुत of the diphthongs s ए and ओ , their last element इ and उ get the प्लुत।",
    "Sūtra 8.2.107: echopragruhyasyaadooraaddhootepoorvasyaardhasyaaduttarasyedutau (एचोऽप्रगृह्यस्यादूराद्धूते पूर्वस्यार्धस्यादुत्तरस्येदुतौ) — In the diphthongs which are not प्रगृह्य -- ईदूदेद्द्विवचनं प्रगृह्यम् [[1.1.11]] etc. and which become प्लुत under the circumstances mentioned in प्रत्यभिवादेशूद्रे [[8.2.83]] etc., but not when that circumstance is a call from a distance -- दूराद्धूते च [[8.2.84]]; for the first half, there is substituted the prolated आ and for the second portion इ or उ।",
    "Sūtra 8.2.108: tayoryvaavachisamhitaayaam (तयोर्य्वावचि संहितायाम्) — For these vowels इ or उ are substituted य् and व् when a vowel follows them in a संहिता (in an unbroken flow of speech).",
    "Sūtra 8.3.1: matuvasorusambuddhauchhandasi (मतुवसो रु सम्बुद्धौ छन्दसि) — For the final affixes मत् and वस् there is substituted रु in the Vocative Case singular, in the छन्दस् (Vedas).",
    "Sūtra 8.3.2: atraanunaasikahapoorvasyatuvaa (अत्रानुनासिकः पूर्वस्य तु वा) — In the following sūtras up to कानाम्रेडिते [[8.3.12]], this always to be supplied - 'But here a nasal vowel after which रु has been ordained'.",
    "Sūtra 8.3.3: aatotinityam (आतोऽटि नित्यम्) — A nasal vowel is ALWAYS substituted for आ before रु when it is followed by a letter of अट् प्रत्यहार (i.e. when it is followed by a vowel or ह , य , व or र).",
    "Sūtra 8.3.4: anunaasikaatparonusvaarah (अनुनासिकात् परोऽनुस्वारः) — After what precedes रु , if we omit to substitute the nasal, then अनुस्वार shall be the augment.",
    "Sūtra 8.3.5: samahasuti (समः सुटि) — रु is substituted for the म् of स्म् (and thereby अँ or अं is substituted for अ) when the augment स् follows in a संहिता ।",
    "Sūtra 8.3.6: pumahakhayyampare (पुमः खय्यम्परे) — रु is substituted for the म् of पुम् (whereby the उ is changed to उँ or उं) before a surd mute (खय्) which is followed by a vowel, semi-vowel or a nasal (अम् प्रत्यहार).",
    "Sūtra 8.3.7: nashchhavyaprashaan (नश्छव्यप्रशान्) — रु is substituted for the final न् of a word, with the exception of न् of प्रशान् before a छव् letter (छ ठ थ च ट त) which is followed by an अम् letter (vowel, semi-vowel and nasal).",
    "Sūtra 8.3.8: ubhayatharkshu (उभयथर्क्षु) — In both ways in the ऋग् verses.",
    "Sūtra 8.3.9: deerghaadatisamaanapade (दीर्घादटि समानपादे) — रु is optionally substituted for that final न् of a word which is preceded by a long vowel and is followed by a letter of the अट् प्रत्यहार (vowel or semi-vowel with the exception of ल्) when these (न् and अट्) come in contact with each other in the same stanza of the ऋग्वेद।",
    "Sūtra 8.3.10: nrunpe (नॄन् पे) — रु is optionally substituted for the न् of नॄन् before प्।",
    "Sūtra 8.3.11: svatavaanpaayau (स्वतवान् पायौ) — रु is substituted for the न् of स्वतवान् before पायु।",
    "Sūtra 8.3.12: kaanaamredite (कानाम्रेडिते) — रु is substituted for the न् of कान् when it is followed by another कान् which is an अम्रेडित (repeated).",
    "Sūtra 8.3.13: dhodhelopah (ढो ढे लोपः) — There is elision of ढ् when ढ् follows.",
    "Sūtra 8.3.14: rori (रो रि) — There is elision of र् when र् follows.",
    "Sūtra 8.3.15: kharavasaanayorvisarjaneeyah (खरवसानयोर्विसर्जनीयः) — The विसर्जनीय is substituted for र् before a खर् consonant or when there is a Pause.",
    "Sūtra 8.3.16: rohasupi (रोः सुपि) — The विसर्जनीय is substituted for रु called र (and not any other र) before the Locative -7th case plural case-affix सु।",
    "Sūtra 8.3.17: bhobhagoaghoapurvasyayoshi (भोभगोअघोअपूर्वस्य योऽशि) — य् is substituted for the रु called र (and not any other र) when it is preceded by 1. भो 2. भगो 3. अघो 4. अ or 5. आ before an अश् letter (vowels and soft-consonants).",
    "Sūtra 8.3.18: vyorlaghuprayatnatarahashaakataayanasya (व्योर्लघुप्रयत्नतरः शाकटायनस्य) — व् and य् (in भगोय् etc. and after अ or आ , at the end of a पद) are pronounced with a lighter articulation before an अश् letter (vowels and soft-consonants) according the opinion of शाकटायन।",
    "Sūtra 8.3.19: lopahashaakalyasya (लोपः शाकल्यस्य) — व् and य् preceded by अ or आ and the end of a पद are elided before an अश् letter (vowels and soft-consonants) according the opinion of शाकल्य।",
    "Sūtra 8.3.20: otogaargyasya (ओतो गार्ग्यस्य) — य् preceded by ओ is elided before an अश् letter (vowels and soft-consonants) according the opinion of गार्ग्य ।",
    "Sūtra 8.3.21: unyichapade (उञि च पदे) — व् and य् (preceded by अ or आ and the end of a पद) and followed by उ , when it is a word, are elided necessarily.",
    "Sūtra 8.3.22: halisarveshaam (हलि सर्वेषाम्) — (The य् when preceded by 1. भो 2. भगो 3. अघो 4. अ or 5. आ , is elided) before a consonant according to the opinion of all आचार्रचा-s.",
    "Sūtra 8.3.23: monusvaarah (मोऽनुस्वारः) — The अनुस्वार is substituted for म् at the end of a word, before a consonant.",
    "Sūtra 8.3.24: nashchaapadaantasyajhali (नश्चापदान्तस्य झलि) — The अनुस्वार is substituted for न् and not म् final in a word, before all consonants, with the exception",
    "Sūtra 8.3.25: moraajisamahakvau (मो राजि समः क्वौ) — म् is substituted for म् of स्म् before the word राज् ending with the affix क्विप्।",
    "Sūtra 8.3.26: hemaparevaa (हे मपरे वा) — म् is optionally substituted for म् before ह which itself is followed by म्।",
    "Sūtra 8.3.27: naparenah (नपरे नः) — न् is optionally substituted for म् when it is followed by ह which has a न after it.",
    "Sūtra 8.3.28: ngnohakuktukshari (ङ्णोः कुक्टुक् शरि) — The augment क् is added to a final ङ् and the augment ट् to a final ण् before a sibilant, optionally.",
    "Sūtra 8.3.29: dahasidhut (डः सि धुट्) — After a word ending in ड् there may optionally be added the augment ध् to a word beginning with स्।",
    "Sūtra 8.3.30: nashcha (नश्च) — After a word ending in न् , धुट् is optionally the augment to a word beginning with स्।",
    "Sūtra 8.3.31: shituk (शि तुक्) — The augment त् may optionally be added to a word ending in न् , when a word beginning with श् follows.",
    "Sūtra 8.3.32: ngamohrasvaadachingamunnityam (ङमो ह्रस्वादचि ङमुण्नित्यम्) — After a word ending in ङ् ण् or न् which is preceded by a light vowel, the same consonant ङ् ण् or न् is added invariably at the beginning of the next word, which commences with a vowel.",
    "Sūtra 8.3.33: mayunyovovaa (मय उञो वो वा) — व् is optionally the substitute of the Particle उ when it is preceded by मय् consonant (all consonants with the exception of the semi-vowels, sibilants, ह and ञ) and is followed by a vowel.",
    "Sūtra 8.3.34: visarjaneeyasyasah (विसर्जनीयस्य सः) — स् is the substitute of a विसर्ग when it is followed by a hard consonant (खर्) which itself is followed by a sibilant (शर्).",
    "Sūtra 8.3.35: sharparevisarjaneeyah (शर्परे विसर्जनीयः) — The विसर्ग is the substitute when it is followed by a hard consonant (खर्) which itself is followed by a sibilant (शर्).",
    "Sūtra 8.3.36: vaashari (वा शरि) — The विसर्ग is optionally the substitute of विसर्ग when followed by a sibilant (शर्).",
    "Sūtra 8.3.37: kupvohakapaucha (कुप्वोः ≍क≍पौ च) — Xक and Xप are optionally substituted for the विसर्ग when followed by a hard Guttural or a hard labial.",
    "Sūtra 8.3.38: sopadaadau (सोऽपदादौ) — स् is the substitute of a विसर्ग before an affix beginning with a hard guttural or labial.",
    "Sūtra 8.3.39: inahashah (इणः षः) — ष् is the substitute of a विसर्ग when is preceded by इ or उ and is followed by an affix beginning with a hard guttural or a labial.",
    "Sūtra 8.3.40: namaspurasorgatyoh (नमस्पुरसोर्गत्योः) — For the विसर्ग of नमस् and पुरस् there is substituted स् before a hard guttural or a labial when these words are गति -- पुरोऽव्ययम् [[1.4.67]] and साक्षात्प्रभृतीनि च [[1.4.74]].",
    "Sūtra 8.3.41: idudupadhasyachaapratyayasya (इदुदुपधस्य चाप्रत्ययस्य) — ष् is substituted before a hard guttural or a labial for the विसर्ग which is preceded इ or उ and not part of an affix.",
    "Sūtra 8.3.42: tirasonyatarasyaam (तिरसोऽन्यतरस्याम्) — The विसर्ग of गति तिरस् is optionally changed to स् before a hard guttural or a labial.",
    "Sūtra 8.3.43: dvistrishchaturitikrutvorthe (द्विस्त्रिश्चतुरिति कृत्वोऽर्थे) — ष् is optionally the substitute of the विसर्ग of 1. द्विस् 2. त्रिस् and 3. चतुर् when they are used as numeral adverbs (before a hard guttural or a labial).",
    "Sūtra 8.3.44: isusohasaamarthye (इसुसोः सामर्थ्ये) — For the विसर्ग of words ending in इस् and उस् before a hard guttural or a labial, there is optionally substituted ष् when the two words stand in correlation with one another.",
    "Sūtra 8.3.45: nityamsamaasenuttarapadasthasya (नित्यं समासेऽनुत्तरपदस्थस्य) — The विसर्ग of इस् or उस् ending word which is not preceded by any other word is invariably changed to ष् in a compound when followed by a hard consonant or a labial.",
    "Sūtra 8.3.46: atahakrukamikamsakumbhapaatrakushaakarneeshvanavyayasya (अतः कृकमिकंसकुम्भपात्रकुशाकर्णीष्वनव्ययस्य) — For the विसर्ग of a word ending in अस् with the exception of an indeclinable, स् is substituted in a compound when a form of कृ and कम् or the words 1. कंस 2. कुम्भ 3. पात्र 4. कुशा and 5. कर्णी follow and the first word is not preceded by another word.",
    "Sūtra 8.3.47: adhahashiraseepade (अधःशिरसी पदे) — For the विसर्ग of अधस् or शिरस् when not preceded by another word and followed by the word पद in composition with it, there is substituted स्।",
    "Sūtra 8.3.48: kaskaadishucha (कस्कादिषु च) — स् or ष् is substituted for the विसर्ग before a hard guttural or a labial in the words कस्क etc.",
    "Sūtra 8.3.49: chhandasivaapraamreditayoh (छन्दसि वाऽप्राम्रेडितयोः) — स् may optionally be substituted for the विसर्ग before a hard guttural or a labial in the छन्दस् (Vedas); but neither before प्र , nor before a doubled word.",
    "Sūtra 8.3.50: kahakaratkaratikrudhikruteshvanaditeh (कःकरत्करतिकृधिकृतेष्वनदितेः) — The विसर्ग is changed to स् in the छन्दस् (Vedas) before 1. कः 2. करत् 3. करति 4. कृधि and 5. कृतः but not so in the विसर्ग of अदितिः।",
    "Sūtra 8.3.51: panychamyaahaparaavadhyarthe (पञ्चम्याः परावध्यर्थे) — The विसर्ग of the Ablative -5th case is changed to स् before परि meaning 'over'.",
    "Sūtra 8.3.52: paatauchabahulam (पातौ च बहुलम्) — स् may diversely be substituted for the विसर्ग of the Ablative -5th case before the verb पातु in the छन्दस् (Vedas).",
    "Sūtra 8.3.53: shashthyaahapatiputraprushthapaarapadapayasposheshu (षष्ठ्याः पतिपुत्रपृष्ठपारपदपयस्पोषेषु) — For the विसर्ग  of the Genitive 6th-Case there is substituted स् in the छन्दस् (Vedas) before 1. पति 2. पुत्र 3. पृष्ठ 4. पार 5. पद 6. पयस्  and 7. पोष।",
    "Sūtra 8.3.54: idaayaavaa (इडाया वा) — स् is optionally substituted for the विसर्ग of इडाया before पति etc. -- षष्ठ्याः पतिपुत्रपृष्ठपारपदपयस्पोषेषु [[8.3.53]], in the छन्दस् (Vedas).",
    "Sūtra 8.3.55: apadaantasyamoordhanyah (अपदान्तस्य मूर्धन्यः) — Up to the end of the पद , is throughout to be supplied the following - 'A cerebral letter substituted always in the room of …, when this letter does not stand at the end of a word'.",
    "Sūtra 8.3.56: sahehasaadahasah (सहेः साडः सः) — ष् is substituted for the स् in साह when this occurs in the form of साड (साट्).",
    "Sūtra 8.3.57: inkoh (इण्कोः) — From this, up to the end of the chapter should be supplied, in every sūtra, the following - 'when a vowel (with the exception of अ or आ) or a र् or a guttural precedes'.",
    "Sūtra 8.3.58: numvisarjaneeyasharvyavaayepi (नुम्विसर्जनीयशर्व्यवायेऽपि) — The substitution of for स् takes place then also, when the augment नुम् (न्) the विसर्जनीय or a sibilant occurs between the said इण् and कु letters or the स्।",
    "Sūtra 8.3.59: aadeshapratyayayoh (आदेशप्रत्यययोः) — ष् is substituted for that स् which is a substitute (of the ष् of a root in the धातुपाठ by धात्वादेः षः सः [[6.1.64]]) or which is (the portion of) an affix, under the above mentioned conditions -- इण्कोः [[8.3.57]], नुम्विसर्जनीयशर्व्यवायेऽपि [[8.3.58]], of being preceded by an इण् vowel or a guttural.",
    "Sūtra 8.3.60: shaasivasighaseenaamcha (शासिवसिघसीनां च) — ष् is substituted for the स् of 1. शास् 2. वस् 'to dwell' and 3. घस् when it is preceded by an इण् vowel or a guttural.",
    "Sūtra 8.3.61: stautinyorevashanyabhyaasaat (स्तौतिण्योरेव षण्यभ्यासात्) — ष् is substituted for the स् after इ or उ in the reduplication of a Desiderative, if the स् of सन् is changed to ष् but only in स्तु and in Causative of roots which in the धातुपाठ begin with ष्।",
    "Sūtra 8.3.62: sahasvidisvadisaheenaamcha (सः स्विदिस्वदिसहीनां च) — स is substituted for the स् after the reduplicate of षण् Desiderative of the Causatives of 1. स्विद् 2. स्वद्  and 3. सह्।",
    "Sūtra 8.3.63: praaksitaadadvyavaayepi (प्राक्सितादड्व्यवायेऽपि) — (The substitution of ष् for स् to be taught hereafter, will take place) for all roots up to सित्  exclusive in परिनिविभ्यः सेवसितसयसिवुसहसुट्स्तुस्वञ्जाम् [[8.3.70]], even when the augment अट् intervenes (between the स and the efficient letter).",
    "Sūtra 8.3.64: sthaadishvabhyaasenachaabhyaasaya (स्थाऽऽदिष्वभ्यासेन चाभ्यासस्य) — In स्था etc. up to सित् exclusive -- उपसर्गात् सुनोतिसुवतिस्यतिस्तौतिस्तोभतिस्थासेनय सेधसिचसञ्जस्वञ्जाम् [[8.3.65]] to परिनिविभ्यः सेवसितसयसिवुसहसुट्स्तुस्वञ्जाम् [[8.3.70]], this substitution of ष् takes place then also, when the reduplicate intervenes and the स of the reduplicate is also changed to ष।",
    "Sūtra 8.3.65: upasargaatsunotisuvatisyatistautistobhatisthaasenayasedhasichasanyjasvanyjaam (उपसर्गात् सुनोतिसुवतिस्यतिस्तौतिस्तोभतिस्थासेनयसेधसिचसञ्जस्वञ्जाम्) — ष् is substituted for स् after an इ and उ of an उपसर्ग (Preposition) in the following verbs - 1. सू (सुनोति) 2. सू (सवति) 3. सो (स्यति -- ओतः श्यनि [[7.3.71]]) 5. स्तु (स्तौति - उतो वृद्धिर्लुकि हलि [[7.3.89]]) 6. स्तुभ (स्तोभते) 7. स्था 8. सेनय (Denominative) 9. सिध् (सेधति) 10.  सिच् 11. सञ्ज्  and 12. स्वञ्ज्।",
    "Sūtra 8.3.66: sadiraprateh (सदिरप्रतेः) — The  स् of सद् is changed to ष after an उपसर्ग (Preposition) having an इ or उ , but not after प्रति।",
    "Sūtra 8.3.67: stambheh (स्तम्भेः) — having an इ or उ।",
    "Sūtra 8.3.68: avaachchaalambanaavidooryayoh (अवाच्चालम्बनाविदूर्ययोः) — The  स् of स्तम्भ् is changed into to ष after the उपसर्ग (Preposition) अव in the sense of 'support' and 'contiguity'.",
    "Sūtra 8.3.69: veshchasvanobhojane (वेश्च स्वनो भोजने) — The ष् is substituted for the स् of स्वन् after वि  and अव when the sense is 'to smack while eating'.",
    "Sūtra 8.3.70: parinivibhyahasevasitasayasivusahasutstusvanyjaam (परिनिविभ्यः सेवसितसयसिवुसहसुट्स्तुस्वञ्जाम्) — ष् is substituted for the स् of 1. सेव् 2. सित 3. सय 4. सिव् 5. सह 6. the augment सुट् 7.  स्तु  and 8. स्वज् after the उपसर्ग (Prepositions)  परि , नि  and वि।",
    "Sūtra 8.3.71: sivaadeenaamvaadvyavaayepi (सिवादीनां वाऽड्व्यवायेऽपि) — The ष् change may take place optionally in the सिव् and the rest (of the last sūtra) even when the augment अ intervenes between the उपसर्ग (Prepositions)  परि , नि  and वि and the verb.",
    "Sūtra 8.3.72: anuviparyabhinibhyahasyandaterapraanishu (अनुविपर्यभिनिभ्यः स्यन्दतेरप्राणिषु) — ष् is optionally the substitute of the स् of स्यन्द् after the उपसर्ग (Prepositions) अनु , वि , परि , अभि  and वि when the subject is not a living being.",
    "Sūtra 8.3.73: vehaskanderanishthaayaam (वेः स्कन्देरनिष्ठायाम्) — ष् is optionally the substitute of the स् of स्कन्द् after the उपसर्ग (Preposition) वि but not in the participles in त and तवत।",
    "Sūtra 8.3.74: pareshcha (परेश्च) — ष् is optionally the substitute of the स् of स्कन्द् after the उपसर्ग (Preposition) परि everywhere.",
    "Sūtra 8.3.75: pariskandahapraachyabharateshu (परिस्कन्दः प्राच्यभरतेषु) — The word परिस्कन्द is used without the cerebral change in the country of Eastern Bharata.",
    "Sūtra 8.3.76: sphuratisphulatyornirnivibhyah (स्फुरतिस्फुलत्योर्निर्निविभ्यः) — ष् is optionally the substitute of the स् of स्फुर् and स्फुल् after the उपसर्ग (Prepositions) निस् , नि  and वि।",
    "Sūtra 8.3.77: vehaskabhnaaternityam (वेः स्कभ्नातेर्नित्यम्) — ष् is always the substitute of the स् of स्कम्भ after the उपसर्ग (Preposition) वि।",
    "Sūtra 8.3.78: inahasheedhvamlunglitaamdhonggaat (इणः षीध्वंलुङ्लिटां धोऽङ्गात्) — The cerebral sound is substituted in the room of ध् of षीध्वम्  and of the personal-endings of the Aorist and the लिट् (Perfect Tense), after a अङ्ग (stem) ending in इण् (a vowel other than अ).",
    "Sūtra 8.3.79: vibhaashetah (विभाषेटः) — The cerebral sound is optionally substituted for the ध् of षीध्वम्  and of the Aorist and the लिट् (Perfect Tense) after the augment इट् when the stem ends in inn",
    "Sūtra 8.3.80: samaasenggulehasanggah (समासेऽङ्गुलेः सङ्गः) — ष् is substituted for the स् of सङ्ग after the word अङ्गुलि in a compound.",
    "Sūtra 8.3.81: bheerohasthaanam (भीरोः स्थानम्) — ष् is substituted for the स् of स्थानम् when preceded by भीरु in a compound.",
    "Sūtra 8.3.82: agnehastutstomasomaah (अग्नेः स्तुत्स्तोमसोमाः) — ष् is substituted for the स् of 1. स्तुत 2. स्तोम  and 3. सोम when preceded by अग्नि in a compound.",
    "Sūtra 8.3.83: jyotiraayushahastomah (ज्योतिरायुषः स्तोमः) — ष् is substituted for the स् of स्तोम after ज्योतिस्  and  आयुस् in a compound.",
    "Sūtra 8.3.84: maatrupitrubhyaamsvasaa (मातृपितृभ्यां स्वसा) — ष् is optionally substituted for the स् of स्वसृ after मातृ  and पितृ in a compound.",
    "Sūtra 8.3.85: maatuhapiturbhyaamanyatarasyaam (मातुःपितुर्भ्यामन्यतरस्याम्) — ष् is optionally substituted for the स् of स्वसृ after मातुर्  and पितुर् in a compound.",
    "Sūtra 8.3.86: abhinisahastanahashabdasamjnyaayaam (अभिनिसः स्तनः शब्दसंज्ञायाम्) — ष् is optionally substituted for the स् of स्तन् after the double उपसर्ग (Preposition) अभि निस् when the word so formed is the name of a particular letter (विसर्ग).",
    "Sūtra 8.3.87: upasargapraadurbhyaamastiryachparah (उपसर्गप्रादुर्भ्यामस्तिर्यच्परः) — ष् is substituted for the स् of the verb अस् 'to be' when it is followed by a vowel or य् and is preceded by प्रादुः or an उपसर्ग (Preposition) इ or उ having in it.",
    "Sūtra 8.3.88: suvinirdurbhyahasupisootisamaah (सुविनिर्दुर्भ्यः सुपिसूतिसमाः) — ष् is substituted for the स् of स्वप् , सूति  and सम after सु , वि , निर्  and दुर्।",
    "Sūtra 8.3.89: ninadeebhyaamsnaatehakaushale (निनदीभ्यां स्नातेः कौशले) — ष् is substituted for the स् of स्ना after नि and नदी when the word so formed denotes 'dexterous'.",
    "Sūtra 8.3.90: sootrampratishnaatam (सूत्रं प्रतिष्णातम्) — The word प्रतिष्णात is irregularly formed when meaning 'sūtra'.",
    "Sūtra 8.3.91: kapishthalogotre (कपिष्ठलो गोत्रे) — The word कपिष्ठल is irregularly formed denoting the founder of a गोत्र (Patronymic) of that name.",
    "Sūtra 8.3.92: prashthogragaamini (प्रष्ठोऽग्रगामिनि) — The word प्रष्ठ is irregularly formed when denoting 'a chief' or 'one who goes in front'.",
    "Sūtra 8.3.93: vrukshaasanayorvishtarah (वृक्षासनयोर्विष्टरः) — The word विष्टर is irregularly formed in the sense of 'tree' and 'seat'.",
    "Sūtra 8.3.94: chhandonaamnicha (छन्दोनाम्नि च) — Also when it is the name of a meter, the irregular form विष्टर is used.",
    "Sūtra 8.3.95: gaviyudhibhyaamsthirah (गवियुधिभ्यां स्थिरः) — ष् is substituted for the स् of स्थिरः after the words गवि  and  युधि।",
    "Sūtra 8.3.96: vikushamiparibhyahasthalam (विकुशमिपरिभ्यः स्थलम्) — ष् is substituted for the स् of स्थल after वि , कु , शमि  and परि।",
    "Sūtra 8.3.97: ambaambagobhoomisavyaapadvitrikushekushangkvanggumanyjipunyjiparamebarhirdivyagnibhyahasthah (अम्बाम्बगोभूमिसव्यापद्वित्रिकुशेकुशङ्क्वङ्गुमञ्जिपुञ्जिपरमेबर्हिर्दिव्यग्निभ्यः स्थः) — ष् is substituted for the स् of स्थ after 1. अम्ब 2. आम्ब 3. गो 4. भूमि 5. सव्य 6. अप 7. द्वि 8. त्रि 9. कु 10. शेकु 11. शङ्क्वु 12. अङ्गु 13. मञ्जि 14. पुञ्जि 15. परमे 16. बर्हिस् 17. दिवि  and 18 अग्नि।",
    "Sūtra 8.3.98: sushaamaadishucha (सुषामादिषु च) — ष् is substituted for the स् of the words सुषामान् etc.",
    "Sūtra 8.3.99: etisamjnyaayaamagaat (एति संज्ञायामगात्) — ष् is substituted for the स् when followed by ए and preceded by इण् or कु , when the word is a name and when the स् is not preceded by ग्।",
    "Sūtra 8.3.100: nakshatraadvaa (नक्षत्राद्वा) — ष् is optionally substituted for the स् when the preceding word is the name of a Lunar mansion.",
    "Sūtra 8.3.101: hrasvaattaadautaddhite (ह्रस्वात् तादौ तद्धिते) — ष् is substituted for the final स् preceded by a उ before a तद्धित affix beginning with त।",
    "Sūtra 8.3.102: nisastapataavanaasevane (निसस्तपतावनासेवने) — ष् is substituted for the स् of निस् before the verb तप् when meaning is not that of 'repeatedly making red hot'.",
    "Sūtra 8.3.103: yushmattattatakshuhashvantahapaadam (युष्मत्तत्ततक्षुःष्वन्तःपादम्) — The स् standing in the inner half of a stanza is changed to ष्  before the त of त्वम् etc. and युष्मद्।",
    "Sūtra 8.3.104: yajushyekeshaam (यजुष्येकेषाम्) — In the opinion of some, the above change takes place in the यजुर्वेद also.",
    "Sūtra 8.3.105: stutastomayoshchhandasi (स्तुतस्तोमयोश्छन्दसि) — ष् is substituted for the स् of स्तुत in the छन्दस् (Vedas), in the opinion of some.",
    "Sūtra 8.3.106: poorvapadaat (पूर्वपदात्) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas), ष् is substituted for the स् when it stands in the beginning of a second word, preceded by a word ending in इ etc.",
    "Sūtra 8.3.107: sunyah (सुञः) — In the छन्दस् (Vedas),  ष् is substituted for the स् of the particle सु when preceded by a word having in it the change-effecting letter इ etc.",
    "Sūtra 8.3.108: sanoteranah (सनोतेरनः) — The स of the verb सन् , when it loses its न् is changed to ष , under the same circumstances.",
    "Sūtra 8.3.109: sahehaprutanartaabhyaamcha (सहेः पृतनर्ताभ्यां च) — ष् is substituted for the स् of सह after पृतना  and ऋत।",
    "Sūtra 8.3.110: naraparasrupisrujisprushispruhisavanaadeenaam (न रपरसृपिसृजिस्पृशिस्पृहिसवनादीनाम्) — The ष् substitution does not take place if र् follows the स् as well as in 1. सृप 2. सृज 3. स्पृश 4. स्पृह  and 5. सवन etc.",
    "Sūtra 8.3.111: saatpadaadyoh (सात्पदाद्योः) — The ष् substitution does not take place in the affix सात् and for that स् which stands at the beginning of a word.",
    "Sūtra 8.3.112: sichoyangi (सिचो यङि) — The ष् substitution does not take place in the स् of सिच् of the Intensive.",
    "Sūtra 8.3.113: sedhatergatau (सेधतेर्गतौ) — The ष् substitution does not take place in the स् of the verb सेध when the meaning is that of moving.",
    "Sūtra 8.3.114: pratistabdhanistabdhaucha (प्रतिस्तब्धनिस्तब्धौ च) — The words प्रतिस्तब्ध and निस्तब्ध are anomalous.",
    "Sūtra 8.3.115: sodhah (सोढः) — The ष् substitution does not take place in the स् of सोढ form of the root सह।",
    "Sūtra 8.3.116: stambhusivusahaamchangi (स्तम्भुसिवुसहां चङि) — The ष् substitution does not take place in the reduplicated Aorist of the roots 1. स्तम्भ् 2. सिव्  and 3. सह।",
    "Sūtra 8.3.117: sunotehasyasanoh (सुनोतेः स्यसनोः) — The ष् substitution does not take place in the स् of सु (सुनोति) in the Future, Conditional and Desiderative.",
    "Sūtra 8.3.118: sadishvanyjohaparasyaliti (सदेः परस्य लिटि) — The ष् substitution does not take place in the स् of सद्  and ष्वञ्ज् after the reduplicate in the लिट् (Perfect Tense).",
    "Sūtra 8.3.119: nivyabhibhyodvyaavayevaachhandasi (निव्यभिभ्योऽड्व्यवाये वा छन्दसि) — The ष् is optionally substituted in the छन्दस् (Vedas) after the उपसर्ग (Prepositions) नि , वि  and अभि when the augment अट् intervenes.",
    "Sūtra 8.4.1: rashaabhyaamnonahasamaanapade (रषाभ्यां नो णः समानपदे) — After न् and ष् , the ण् is the substitute of न् , when they occur as component letters in the same word.",
    "Sūtra 8.4.2: atkupvaangnumvyavaayepi (अट्कुप्वाङ्नुम्व्यवायेऽपि) — The substitute ण् takes the place of न् , even when a vowel or य् , व् , ह् or a guttural, or a labial, or the preposition आ , or the augment नुम् intervenes, causing separation.",
    "Sūtra 8.4.3: poorvapadaatsamjnyaayaamagah (पूर्वपदात् संज्ञायामगः) — So also, न् is replaced by ण् , when the letter occasioning the substitution, occurs in the first member of a compound, and the whole compound is a Name, provided that the first member does not end with the letter ग।",
    "Sūtra 8.4.4: vanampuragaamishrakaasidhrakaashaarikaakotaraagrebhyah (वनं पुरगामिश्रकासिध्रकाशारिकाकोटराऽग्रेभ्यः) — The न of वन , is changed into ण , when preceded by the words पुरगा , मिश्रका , सिध्रका , शारिका , कोटरा and अग्रे , as first members of the compound, and the whole compound is a name.",
    "Sūtra 8.4.5: pranirantahasharekshuplakshaamrakaarshyakhadirapiiyookshaabhyosamjnyaayaamapi (प्रनिरन्तःशरेक्षुप्लक्षाम्रकार्ष्यखदिरपीयूक्षाभ्योऽसंज्ञायामपि) — The न of वन , is replaced by ण , even when the compound is not a Name, when it is preceded by the words प्र , निर् , अन्तर , शर , इक्षु , प्लक्ष , आम्र , कार्ष्य , खदिर and पीयूक्षा।",
    "Sūtra 8.4.6: vibhaashaushadhivanaspatibhyah (विभाषौषधिवनस्पतिभ्यः) — The न of वन , is optionally replaced by ण , when the cause of change occurs in the first member of the compound and which denotes a perennial herb or forest tree.",
    "Sūtra 8.4.7: ahnodantaat (अह्नोऽदन्तात्) — The ण is the substitute of न of अहन् , when it is preceded by a word ending in अ , having in it a letter capable of producing a change.",
    "Sūtra 8.4.8: vaahanamaahitaat (वाहनमाहितात्) — The न of वाहन is changed into ण , when the letter producing the change, occurs in the first member of a compound, denoting the thing carried.",
    "Sūtra 8.4.9: paanamdeshe (पानं देशे) — The न of पान is changed into ण , when occurs as the second member of a compound, the first member of which contains a letter causing change; and the whole compound denotes a country or people.",
    "Sūtra 8.4.10: vaabhaavakaranayoh (वा भावकरणयोः) — Optionally when the compound denotes a condition or an instrument, the न् of पान is changed to ण , when it is a second member, the cause of change occurring in the first member in a compound.",
    "Sūtra 8.4.11: praatipadikaantanumvibhaktishucha (प्रातिपदिकान्तनुम्विभक्तिषु च) — Optionally ण is substituted for न when it stands at the end of a Nominal-stem (प्रातिपदिक) or is the augment नुम् or is न of a case-affix, (when the cause of change occurs in the first member of the compound).",
    "Sūtra 8.4.12: ekaajuttarapadenah (एकाजुत्तरपदे णः) — In a compound, the second member of which is a monosyllable, there is ण in the room of न of the second member, provided that the न is at the end of a प्रातिपदिक , or is the augment नुम् , or occurs in a विभक्ति; and when the first member contains a cause of change.",
    "Sūtra 8.4.13: kumaticha (कुमति च) — In a compound, the second member of which contains a guttural, there is ण in the room of न , that follows anything which standing in the prior member is qualified to cause the change, provided the न be at the end of a प्रातिपदिक , or be the augment नुम् , or occur in a विभक्ति।",
    "Sūtra 8.4.14: upasargaadasamaasepinopadeshasya (उपसर्गादसमासेऽपि णोपदेशस्य) — Of a root which has ण in its original enunciation, when it comes after a cause of such change standing in an उपसर्ग , even though the word be not a समास , the न is changed to ण।",
    "Sūtra 8.4.15: hinumeenaa (हिनुमीना) — The न of हिनु and मीना is changed to ण , when coming after an उपसर्ग containing in it a cause of change.",
    "Sūtra 8.4.16: aanilot (आनि लोट्) — The न of आनि , the affix of the Imperative, First Person, is changed into ण when it follows a letter competent to cause such a change standing in an उपसर्ग।",
    "Sūtra 8.4.17: nergadanadapatapadaghumaasyatihantiyaativaatidraatipsaativapativahatishaamyatichinotidegdhishucha (नेर्गदनदपतपदघुमास्यतिहन्तियातिवातिद्रातिप्सातिवपतिवहतिशाम्यतिचिनोतिदेग्धिषु च) — The ण is the substitute of न् of the prefix नि , following a cause for such change standing in an उपसर्ग when these words follow - गद 'to speak', नद 'to be happy', पत 'to fall', पद 'to go'; the घु verbs - मा 'to measure', शो 'to destroy', हन् 'to kill', या 'to go', वा 'to blow', द्रा 'to flee', प्शा 'to eat', वप् 'to weave', वह् 'to bear', शम् 'to be tranquil', चि 'to collect', and दिह् 'to anoint'.",
    "Sūtra 8.4.18: sheshevibhaashaakakhaadaavashaantupadeshe (शेषे विभाषाऽकखादावषान्त उपदेशे) — In the remaining verbs, optionally the न of नि is replaced by ण , when it is preceded by an उपसर्ग competent to cause the change; provided that, in the original enunciation, the verb has not an initial क or ख , nor ends with ष।",
    "Sūtra 8.4.19: aniteh (अनितेः) — The न of the verb अन् 'to breathe', is changed to ण , when preceded by an उपसर्ग competent to produce the change.",
    "Sūtra 8.4.20: antah (अन्तः) — The न of the verb अन् 'to breathe', is changed to ण , when preceded by an उपसर्ग competent to produce the change, provided it occurs at the end of a पद।",
    "Sūtra 8.4.21: ubhausaabhyaasasya (उभौ साभ्यासस्य) — Both the न-s are changed into ण in the reduplicated forms of the verb अन् , when preceded by an उपसर्ग competent to cause the change.",
    "Sūtra 8.4.22: hanteratpoorvasya (हन्तेरत्पूर्वस्य) — The न , when preceded by अ , in the root हन् , is changed to ण , when the verb is preceded by a preposition competent to cause the change.",
    "Sūtra 8.4.23: vamorvaa (वमोर्वा) — Optionally when व or म follow, the न of हन् is changed to ण , when preceded by an उपसर्ग competent to cause the change.",
    "Sūtra 8.4.24: antaradeshe (अन्तरदेशे) — The न preceded by short अ of the root हन् is changed into ण , when the root follows the उपसर्ग - अन्तर and the word does not mean 'a country'.",
    "Sūtra 8.4.25: ayanamcha (अयनं च) — The न of अयन is changed to ण , when preceded by the word अन्तर् and the word does not denote a country.",
    "Sūtra 8.4.26: chhandasyrudavagrahaat (छन्दस्यृदवग्रहात्) — In the छन्दस् , न of a second term is changed into ण , when prior term ends with a short ऋ even when there is an अवग्रह or hiatus between the two terms.",
    "Sūtra 8.4.27: nashchadhaatusthorushubhyah (नश्च धातुस्थोरुषुभ्यः) — In the छन्दस् , the न of (the Pronoun) नस् is changed into ण , when it comes after a root having a र or ष or after the words उरु and षु (सु)।",
    "Sūtra 8.4.28: upasargaadbahulam (उपसर्गाद् बहुलम्) — The न of नस् is changed diversely into ण , when it comes after an उपसर्ग having a cause of change.",
    "Sūtra 8.4.29: krutyachah (कृत्यचः) — The न of कृत् affix, preceded by a vowel, is changed into ण , when it follows an उपसर्ग having the cause of change.",
    "Sūtra 8.4.30: nervibhaashaa (णेर्विभाषा) — The न of कृत् affix ordained after a causative verb (णयन्त), is optionally changed into ण , when it comes after an उपसर्ग having a cause of change.",
    "Sūtra 8.4.31: halashchijupadhaat (हलश्च इजुपधात्) — The कृत् affix, coming after a verb, which begins with a consonant and has a penultimate इच् vowel, changes optionally its न् , which is preceded by a vowel, into ण् , when it comes after उपसर्ग having a cause of change.",
    "Sūtra 8.4.32: ijaadehasanumah (इजादेः सनुमः) — A कृत् affix ordained after a verb beginning with an इच् vowel, having the augment नुम् in it, and ending with a consonant, changes it s न् into ण् , when preceded by an उपसर्ग having in it the cause of change.",
    "Sūtra 8.4.33: vaanimsanikshanindaam (वा निंसनिक्षनिन्दाम्) — The न् of निस् , निक्ष and निन्द is changed to a ण optionally, when preceded by an उपसर्ग having in it a cause of change.",
    "Sūtra 8.4.34: nabhaabhoopookamigamipyaayeevepaam (न भाभूपूकमिगमिप्यायीवेपाम्) — The न of a कृत् affix is not changed to ण , though preceded by an उपसर्ग having in it a cause of change, when the affix is added to the following verbs - भा 'to shine', भू 'to be', पू 'to purify', कमि 'to be brilliant', गमि 'to go', प्यायि 'to increase', वेप 'to shake'.",
    "Sūtra 8.4.35: shaatpadaantaat (षात् पदान्तात्) — After a ष् final in a पद , the न् is not changed to ण।",
    "Sūtra 8.4.36: nashehashaantasya (नशेः षान्तस्य) — ण् is not the substitute of the verb नश 'to destroy', when ending in ष्।",
    "Sūtra 8.4.37: padaantasya (पदान्तस्य) — Of a न् final in a पद , ण् is not the substitute.",
    "Sūtra 8.4.38: padavyavaayepi (पदव्यवायेऽपि) — The न् is not changed to ण् when a पद intervenes between the cause of the change and the word containing the न्।",
    "Sūtra 8.4.39: kshubhnaadishucha (क्षुभ्नाऽऽदिषु च) — The ण् is not the substitute of न् in the words क्षुभ्ना etc.",
    "Sūtra 8.4.40: stohashchunaashchuh (स्तोः श्चुना श्चुः) — The letters स् and the dentals when coming in contact with श् and the palatals, are changed to श् and palatals respectively.",
    "Sūtra 8.4.41: shtunaashtuh (ष्टुना ष्टुः) — The letters स् and the dentals when coming in contact with ष् and the cerebrals, are changed to ष् and cerebrals respectively.",
    "Sūtra 8.4.42: napadaantaattoranaam (न पदान्ताट्टोरनाम्) — After टु final in a पद , the change of a dental (स्तु) to a cerebral (ष्टु), does not take place, except in the case of the affix नाम्।",
    "Sūtra 8.4.43: tohashi (तोः षि) — In the room of तु there is not a cerebral substitute, when ष् follows.",
    "Sūtra 8.4.44: shaat (शात्) — In the room of तु there is not a palatal substitute, when श् precedes.",
    "Sūtra 8.4.45: yaronunaasikenunaasikovaa (यरोऽनुनासिकेऽनुनासिको वा) — In the room of a यर् letter (every consonant except ह final) in a पद , when Nasal follows, there is optionally a Nasal substitute.",
    "Sūtra 8.4.46: achorahaabhyaamdve (अचो रहाभ्यां द्वे) — There is reduplication of यर् , i.e. all the consonants except ह after the letters र् and ह् following a vowel.",
    "Sūtra 8.4.47: anachicha (अनचि च) — When a vowel does not follow, there is reduplication of यर् (all consonants except ह) after a vowel.",
    "Sūtra 8.4.48: naadinyaakrosheputrasya (नादिन्याक्रोशे पुत्रस्य) — There is not reduplication of the letters of पुत्र , when the word आदिनी follows, the sense being that of reviling or cursing.",
    "Sūtra 8.4.49: sharochi (शरोऽचि) — There are not two in the room of a sibilant (शर्), when a vowel follows.",
    "Sūtra 8.4.50: triprabhrutishushaakataayanasya (त्रिप्रभृतिषु शाकटायनस्य) — According to the option of शाकटायन , the doubling does not take place when the conjunct consonants are three or more in number.",
    "Sūtra 8.4.51: sarvatrashaakalyasya (सर्वत्र शाकल्यस्य) — According to the opinion of शाकल्य , there is reduplication no where.",
    "Sūtra 8.4.52: deerghaadaacharyaanaam (दीर्घादाचार्याणाम्) — According to the opinion of all the Teachers, there is no doubling after a long vowel.",
    "Sūtra 8.4.53: jhalaamjashjhashi (झलां जश् झशि) — In the room of झल् letters, there is substitution of जश् letters, when झश् letters follow.",
    "Sūtra 8.4.54: abhyaasecharchcha (अभ्यासे चर्च) — The चर् is also substitute of झल् letters occurring in a reduplicate syllable, as well as जश्।",
    "Sūtra 8.4.55: kharicha (खरि च) — In the room of झल् , there is the substitute चर् , when खर् follows.",
    "Sūtra 8.4.56: vaavasaane (वाऽवसाने) — The चर् is optionally the substitute of a झल् that occurs in a Pause.",
    "Sūtra 8.4.57: anopragruhyasyaanunaasikah (अणोऽप्रगृह्यस्यानुनासिकः) — The अनुनासिका is optionally the substitute of an अण् vowel which occurs in a Pause, and is not a परिगृह्य।",
    "Sūtra 8.4.58: anusvaarasyayayiparasavarnah (अनुस्वारस्य ययि परसवर्णः) — In the room of अनुस्वारा, when यय् follows, a letter homogenous with the latter is substituted.",
    "Sūtra 8.4.59: vaapadaantasya (वा पदान्तस्य) — In the room of अनुस्वारा, final in a पद, the substitution of a letter homogenous with the latter is optional.",
    "Sūtra 8.4.60: torli (तोर्लि) — In the room of तु (a dental) when the letter ल follows, one homogenous with the latter is substituted.",
    "Sūtra 8.4.61: udahasthaastambhohapoorvasya (उदः स्थास्तम्भोः पूर्वस्य) — After उद्, in the room of the स of स्था or स्तम्भ, the substitute is a letter belonging to the class of the prior (i.e. a dental is substituted for this स). ",
    "Sūtra 8.4.62: jhayohonyatarasyaam (झयो होऽन्यतरस्याम्) — In the room of ह after (a sonant Mute) there is optionally a letter homogenous with the prior.",
    "Sūtra 8.4.63: shashchhoti (शश्छोऽटि) — in the room of श preceded by a surd Mute, there is optionally the letter छ् when a vowel or य, व or र follows such श।",
    "Sūtra 8.4.64: haloyamaamyamilopah (हलो यमां यमि लोपः) — After a consonant, the following semi-vowel or a nasal is elided optionally, when the same letters follow it",
    "Sūtra 8.4.65: jharojharisavarne (झरो झरि सवर्णे) — The mute of sibilant (झर्) preceded by a consonant and followed by a homogenous mute of sibilant, is optionally elided",
    "Sūtra 8.4.66: udaattaadanudaattasyasvaritah (उदात्तादनुदात्तस्य स्वरितः) — The स्वरित is the substitute of an अनुदात्त vowel which follows an उदात्त vowel.",
    "Sūtra 8.4.67: nodaattasvaritodayamagaargyakaashyapagaalavaanaam (नोदात्तस्वरितोदयमगार्ग्यकाश्यपगालवानाम्) — All prohibit the above substitution of स्वरित, except the आचार्याः - गार्ग्य, काश्यप and गाल्व; when an उदात्त or a स्वरित follows.",
    "Sūtra 8.4.68: aaiti (अ अ) — The अ which was considered to be open (विवृत) in all the preceding operations of the Grammar, is now made contracted (संवृत)",
]

def get_sutras() -> list:
    return CORE_SUTRAS
